# BOOK	001	GEN	Genesis	Genesis
001	GEN	001	001	In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.
001	GEN	001	002	And the earth was waste and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep: and the spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.
001	GEN	001	003	And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.
001	GEN	001	004	And God saw the light, that it was good: and God divided the light from the darkness.
001	GEN	001	005	And God called the light Day, and the darkness he called Night. And there was evening and there was morning, one day.
001	GEN	001	006	And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.
001	GEN	001	007	And God made the firmament, and divided the waters which were under the firmament from the waters which were above the firmament: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	008	And God called the firmament Heaven. And there was evening and there was morning, a second day.
001	GEN	001	009	And God said, Let the waters under the heaven be gathered together unto one place, and let the dry land appear: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	010	And God called the dry land Earth; and the gathering together of the waters called he Seas: and God saw that it was good.
001	GEN	001	011	And God said, Let the earth put forth grass, herb yielding seed, [and] fruit tree bearing fruit after its kind, wherein is the seed thereof, upon the earth: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	012	And the earth brought forth grass, herb yielding seed after its kind, and tree bearing fruit, wherein is the seed thereof, after its kind: and God saw that it was good.
001	GEN	001	013	And there was evening and there was morning, a third day.
001	GEN	001	014	And God said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days and years:
001	GEN	001	015	and let them be for lights in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	016	And God made the two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: [he made] the stars also.
001	GEN	001	017	And God set them in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth,
001	GEN	001	018	and to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness: and God saw that it was good.
001	GEN	001	019	And there was evening and there was morning, a fourth day.
001	GEN	001	020	And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and let fowl fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven.
001	GEN	001	021	And God created the great sea-monsters, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kinds, and every winged fowl after its kind: and God saw that it was good.
001	GEN	001	022	And God blessed them, saying, Be fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let fowl multiply in the earth.
001	GEN	001	023	And there was evening and there was morning, a fifth day.
001	GEN	001	024	And God said, Let the earth bring forth the living creature after its kind, cattle, and creeping thing, and beast of the earth after its kind: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	025	And God made the beast of the earth after its kind, and the cattle after their kind, and every thing that creepeth upon the ground after its kind: and God saw that it was good.
001	GEN	001	026	And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.
001	GEN	001	027	And God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.
001	GEN	001	028	And God blessed them: and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it; and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.
