001	GEN	001	030	and to every beast of the earth, and to every fowl of the air, and to every thing that creepeth upon the earth, wherein there is life, [I have given] every green herb for meat: and it was so.
001	GEN	001	031	And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And there was evening and there was morning, the sixth day.
001	GEN	002	001	And the heaven and the earth were finished, and all the host of them.
001	GEN	002	002	And on the seventh day God finished his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.
001	GEN	002	003	And God blessed the seventh day, and hallowed it: because that in it he rested from all his work which God had created and made.
001	GEN	002	004	These are the generations of the heaven and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made earth and heaven.
001	GEN	002	005	And no plant of the field was yet in the earth, and no herb of the field had yet sprung up: for the LORD God had not caused it to rain upon the earth, and there was not a man to till the ground;
001	GEN	002	006	but there went up a mist from the earth, and watered the whole face of the ground.
001	GEN	002	007	And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.
001	GEN	002	008	And the LORD God planted a garden eastward, in Eden; and there he put the man whom he had formed.
001	GEN	002	009	And out of the ground made the LORD God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.
001	GEN	002	010	And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became four heads.
001	GEN	002	011	The name of the first is Pishon: that is it which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;
001	GEN	002	012	and the gold of that land is good: there is bdellium and the onyx stone.
001	GEN	002	013	And the name of the second river is Gihon: the same is it that compasseth the whole land of Cush.
001	GEN	002	014	And the name of the third river is Hiddekel: that is it which goeth in front of Assyria. And the fourth river is Euphrates.
001	GEN	002	015	And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.
001	GEN	002	016	And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:
001	GEN	002	017	but of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die.
001	GEN	002	018	And the LORD God said, It is not good that the man should be alone; I will make him an help meet for him.
001	GEN	002	019	And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air; and brought them unto the man to see what he would call them: and whatsoever the man called every living creature, that was the name thereof.
001	GEN	002	020	And the man gave names to all cattle, and to the fowl of the air, and to every beast of the field; but for man there was not found an help meet for him.
001	GEN	002	021	And the LORD God caused a deep sleep to fall upon the man, and he slept; and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof:
001	GEN	002	022	and the rib, which the LORD God had taken from the man, made he a woman, and brought her unto the man.
001	GEN	002	023	And the man said, This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.
