001	GEN	050	011	And when the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, saw the mourning in the floor of Atad, they said, This is a grievous mourning to the Egyptians: wherefore the name of it was called Abel-mizraim, which is beyond Jordan.
001	GEN	050	012	And his sons did unto him according as he commanded them:
001	GEN	050	013	for his sons carried him into the land of Canaan, and buried him in the cave of the field of Machpelah, which Abraham bought with the field, for a possession of a buryingplace, of Ephron the Hittite, before Mamre.
001	GEN	050	014	And Joseph returned into Egypt, he, and his brethren, and all that went up with him to bury his father, after he had buried his father.
001	GEN	050	015	And when Joseph’s brethren saw that their father was dead, they said, It may be that Joseph will hate us, and will fully requite us all the evil which we did unto him.
001	GEN	050	016	And they sent a message unto Joseph, saying, Thy father did command before he died, saying,
001	GEN	050	017	So shall ye say unto Joseph, Forgive, I pray thee now, the transgression of thy brethren, and their sin, for that they did unto thee evil: and now, we pray thee, forgive the transgression of the servants of the God of thy father. And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.
001	GEN	050	018	And his brethren also went and fell down before his face; and they said, Behold, we be thy servants.
001	GEN	050	019	And Joseph said unto them, Fear not: for am I in the place of God?
001	GEN	050	020	And as for you, ye meant evil against me; but God meant it for good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.
001	GEN	050	021	Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.
001	GEN	050	022	And Joseph dwelt in Egypt, he, and his father’s house: and Joseph lived an hundred and ten years.
001	GEN	050	023	And Joseph saw Ephraim’s children of the third generation: the children also of Machir the son of Manasseh were born upon Joseph’s knees.
001	GEN	050	024	And Joseph said unto his brethren, I die: but God will surely visit you, and bring you up out of this land unto the land which he sware to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.
001	GEN	050	025	And Joseph took an oath of the children of Israel, saying, God will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.
001	GEN	050	026	So Joseph died, being an hundred and ten years old: and they embalmed him, and he was put in a coffin in Egypt.
