002	EXO	019	010	And the LORD said unto Moses, Go unto the people, and sanctify them today and tomorrow, and let them wash their garments,
002	EXO	019	011	and be ready against the third day: for the third day the LORD will come down in the sight of all the people upon mount Sinai.
002	EXO	019	012	And thou shalt set bounds unto the people round about, saying, Take heed to yourselves, that ye go not up into the mount, or touch the border of it: whosoever toucheth the mount shall be surely put to death:
002	EXO	019	013	no hand shall touch him, but he shall surely be stoned, or shot through; whether it be beast or man, it shall not live: when the trumpet soundeth long, they shall come up to the mount.
002	EXO	019	014	And Moses went down from the mount unto the people, and sanctified the people; and they washed their garments.
002	EXO	019	015	And he said unto the people, Be ready against the third day: come not near a woman.
002	EXO	019	016	And it came to pass on the third day, when it was morning, that there were thunders and lightnings, and a thick cloud upon the mount, and the voice of a trumpet exceeding loud; and all the people that were in the camp trembled.
002	EXO	019	017	And Moses brought forth the people out of the camp to meet God; and they stood at the nether part of the mount.
002	EXO	019	018	And mount Sinai was altogether on smoke, because the LORD descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.
002	EXO	019	019	And when the voice of the trumpet waxed louder and louder, Moses spake, and God answered him by a voice.
002	EXO	019	020	And the LORD came down upon mount Sinai, to the top of the mount: and the LORD called Moses to the top of the mount; and Moses went up.
002	EXO	019	021	And the LORD said unto Moses, Go down, charge the people, lest they break through unto the LORD to gaze, and many of them perish.
002	EXO	019	022	And let the priests also, which come near to the LORD, sanctify themselves, lest the LORD break forth upon them.
002	EXO	019	023	And Moses said unto the LORD, The people cannot come up to mount Sinai: for thou didst charge us, saying, Set bounds about the mount, and sanctify it.
002	EXO	019	024	And the LORD said unto him, Go, get thee down; and thou shalt come up, thou, and Aaron with thee: but let not the priests and the people break through to come up unto the LORD, lest he break forth upon them.
002	EXO	019	025	So Moses went down unto the people, and told them.
002	EXO	020	001	And God spake all these words, saying,
002	EXO	020	002	I am the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage.
002	EXO	020	003	Thou shalt have none other gods before me.
002	EXO	020	004	Thou shalt not make unto thee a graven image, nor [the likeness of] any form that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth:
002	EXO	020	005	thou shalt not bow down thyself unto them, nor serve them: for I the LORD thy God am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, upon the third and upon the fourth generation of them that hate me;
002	EXO	020	006	and shewing mercy unto thousands, of them that love me and keep my commandments.
002	EXO	020	007	Thou shalt not take the name of the LORD thy God in vain; for the LORD will not hold him guiltless that taketh his name in vain.
002	EXO	020	008	Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy.
002	EXO	020	009	Six days shalt thou labour, and do all thy work:
002	EXO	020	010	but the seventh day is a sabbath unto the LORD thy God: [in it] thou shalt not do any work, thou, nor thy son, nor thy daughter, thy manservant, nor thy maidservant, nor thy cattle, nor thy stranger that is within thy gates:
002	EXO	020	011	for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is, and rested the seventh day: wherefore the LORD blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it.
002	EXO	020	012	Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.
002	EXO	020	013	Thou shalt do no murder.
002	EXO	020	014	Thou shalt not commit adultery.
002	EXO	020	015	Thou shalt not steal.
002	EXO	020	016	Thou shalt not bear false witness against thy neighbour.
002	EXO	020	017	Thou shalt not covet thy neighbour’s house, thou shalt not covet thy neighbour’s wife, nor his manservant, nor his maidservant, nor his ox, nor his ass, nor any thing that is thy neighbour’s.
002	EXO	020	018	And all the people saw the thunderings, and the lightnings, and the voice of the trumpet, and the mountain smoking: and when the people saw it, they trembled, and stood afar off.
002	EXO	020	019	And they said unto Moses, Speak thou with us, and we will hear: but let not God speak with us, lest we die.
002	EXO	020	020	And Moses said unto the people, Fear not: for God is come to prove you, and that his fear may be before you, that ye sin not.
002	EXO	020	021	And the people stood afar off, and Moses drew near unto the thick darkness where God was.
002	EXO	020	022	And the LORD said unto Moses, Thus thou shalt say unto the children of Israel, Ye yourselves have seen that I have talked with you from heaven.
002	EXO	020	023	Ye shall not make [other gods] with me; gods of silver, or gods of gold, ye shall not make unto you.
002	EXO	020	024	An altar of earth thou shalt make unto me, and shalt sacrifice thereon thy burnt offerings, and thy peace offerings, thy sheep, and thine oxen: in every place where I record my name I will come unto thee and I will bless thee.
002	EXO	020	025	And if thou make me an altar of stone, thou shalt not build it of hewn stones: for if thou lift up thy tool upon it, thou hast polluted it.
002	EXO	020	026	Neither shalt thou go up by steps unto mine altar, that thy nakedness be not discovered thereon.
002	EXO	021	001	Now these are the judgments which thou shalt set before them.
002	EXO	021	002	If thou buy an Hebrew servant, six years he shall serve: and in the seventh he shall go out free for nothing.
002	EXO	021	003	If he come in by himself, he shall go out by himself: if he be married, then his wife shall go out with him.
002	EXO	021	004	If his master give him a wife, and she bear him sons or daughters; the wife and her children shall be her master’s, and he shall go out by himself.
002	EXO	021	005	But if the servant shall plainly say, I love my master, my wife, and my children; I will not go out free:
002	EXO	021	006	then his master shall bring him unto God, and shall bring him to the door, or unto the door post; and his master shall bore his ear through with an awl; and he shall serve him for ever.
002	EXO	021	007	And if a man sell his daughter to be a maidservant, she shall not go out as the menservants do.
002	EXO	021	008	If she please not her master, who hath espoused her to himself, then shall he let her be redeemed: to sell her unto a strange people he shall have no power, seeing he hath dealt deceitfully with her.
002	EXO	021	009	And if he espouse her unto his son, he shall deal with her after the manner of daughters.
002	EXO	021	010	If he take him another [wife]; her food, her raiment, and her duty of marriage, shall he not diminish.
002	EXO	021	011	And if he do not these three unto her, then shall she go out for nothing, without money.
002	EXO	021	012	He that smiteth a man, so that he die, shall surely be put to death.
002	EXO	021	013	And if a man lie not in wait, but God deliver [him] into his hand; then I will appoint thee a place whither he shall flee.
002	EXO	021	014	And if a man come presumptuously upon his neighbour, to slay him with guile; thou shalt take him from mine altar, that he may die.
002	EXO	021	015	And he that smiteth his father, or his mother, shall be surely put to death.
002	EXO	021	016	And he that stealeth a man, and selleth him, or if he be found in his hand, he shall surely be put to death.
002	EXO	021	017	And he that curseth his father, or his mother, shall surely be put to death.
002	EXO	021	018	And if men contend, and one smiteth the other with a stone, or with his fist, and he die not, but keep his bed:
002	EXO	021	019	if he rise again, and walk abroad upon his staff, then shall he that smote him be quit: only he shall pay for the loss of his time, and shall cause him to be thoroughly healed.
002	EXO	021	020	And if a man smite his servant, or his maid, with a rod, and he die under his hand; he shall surely be punished.
002	EXO	021	021	Notwithstanding, if he continue a day or two, he shall not be punished: for he is his money.
002	EXO	021	022	And if men strive together, and hurt a woman with child, so that her fruit depart, and yet no mischief follow: he shall be surely fined, according as the woman’s husband shall lay upon him; and he shall pay as the judges determine.
002	EXO	021	023	But if any mischief follow, then thou shalt give life for life,
002	EXO	021	024	eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot,
002	EXO	021	025	burning for burning, wound for wound, stripe for stripe.
002	EXO	021	026	And if a man smite the eye of his servant, or the eye of his maid, and destroy it; he shall let him go free for his eye’s sake.
002	EXO	021	027	And if he smite out his manservant’s tooth, or his maidservant’s tooth; he shall let him go free for his tooth’s sake.
002	EXO	021	028	And if an ox gore a man or a woman, that they die, the ox shall be surely stoned, and his flesh shall not be eaten; but the owner of the ox shall be quit.
002	EXO	021	029	But if the ox were wont to gore in time past, and it hath been testified to his owner, and he hath not kept him in, but that he hath killed a man or a woman; the ox shall be stoned, and his owner also shall be put to death.
002	EXO	021	030	If there be laid on him a ransom, then he shall give for the redemption of his life whatsoever is laid upon him.
002	EXO	021	031	Whether he have gored a son, or have gored a daughter, according to this judgment shall it be done unto him.
002	EXO	021	032	If the ox gore a manservant or a maidservant; he shall give unto their master thirty shekels of silver, and the ox shall be stoned.
002	EXO	021	033	And if a man shall open a pit, or if a man shall dig a pit and not cover it, and an ox or an ass fall therein,
002	EXO	021	034	the owner of the pit shall make it good; he shall give money unto the owner of them, and the dead [beast] shall be his.
002	EXO	021	035	And if one man’s ox hurt another’s, that he die; then they shall sell the live ox, and divide the price of it; and the dead also they shall divide.
002	EXO	021	036	Or if it be known that the ox was wont to gore in time past, and his owner hath not kept him in; he shall surely pay ox for ox, and the dead [beast] shall be his own.
002	EXO	022	001	If a man shall steal an ox, or a sheep, and kill it, or sell it; he shall pay five oxen for an ox, and four sheep for a sheep.
002	EXO	022	002	If the thief be found breaking in, and be smitten that he die, there shall be no bloodguiltiness for him.
002	EXO	022	003	If the sun be risen upon him, there shall be bloodguiltiness for him: he should make restitution; if he have nothing, then he shall be sold for his theft.
002	EXO	022	004	If the theft be found in his hand alive, whether it be ox, or ass, or sheep; he shall pay double.
002	EXO	022	005	If a man shall cause a field or vineyard to be eaten, and shall let his beast loose, and it feed in another man’s field; of the best of his own field, and of the best of his own vineyard, shall he make restitution.
002	EXO	022	006	If fire break out, and catch in thorns, so that the shocks of corn, or the standing corn, or the field, be consumed; he that kindled the fire shall surely make restitution.
002	EXO	022	007	If a man shall deliver unto his neighbour money or stuff to keep, and it be stolen out of the man’s house; if the thief be found, he shall pay double.
002	EXO	022	008	If the thief be not found, then the master of the house shall come near unto God, [to see] whether he have not put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods.
002	EXO	022	009	For every matter of trespass, whether it be for ox, for ass, for sheep, for raiment, [or] for any manner of lost thing, whereof one saith, This is it, the cause of both parties shall come before God; he whom God shall condemn shall pay double unto his neighbour.
002	EXO	022	010	If a man deliver unto his neighbour an ass, or an ox, or a sheep, or any beast, to keep; and it die, or be hurt, or driven away, no man seeing it:
002	EXO	022	011	the oath of the LORD shall be between them both, whether he hath not put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods; and the owner thereof shall accept it, and he shall not make restitution.
002	EXO	022	012	But if it be stolen from him, he shall make restitution unto the owner thereof.
002	EXO	022	013	If it be torn in pieces, let him bring it for witness; he shall not make good that which was torn.
002	EXO	022	014	And if a man borrow aught of his neighbour, and it be hurt, or die, the owner thereof not being with it, he shall surely make restitution.
002	EXO	022	015	If the owner thereof be with it, he shall not make it good: if it be an hired thing, it came for its hire.
002	EXO	022	016	And if a man entice a virgin that is not betrothed, and lie with her, he shall surely pay a dowry for her to be his wife.
002	EXO	022	017	If her father utterly refuse to give her unto him, he shall pay money according to the dowry of virgins.
002	EXO	022	018	Thou shalt not suffer a sorceress to live.
002	EXO	022	019	Whosoever lieth with a beast shall surely be put to death.
002	EXO	022	020	He that sacrificeth unto any god, save unto the LORD only, shall be utterly destroyed.
002	EXO	022	021	And a stranger shalt thou not wrong, neither shalt thou oppress him: for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.
002	EXO	022	022	Ye shall not afflict any widow, or fatherless child.
002	EXO	022	023	If thou afflict them in any wise, and they cry at all unto me, I will surely hear their cry;
002	EXO	022	024	and my wrath shall wax hot, and I will kill you with the sword; and your wives shall be widows, and your children fatherless.
002	EXO	022	025	If thou lend money to any of my people with thee that is poor, thou shalt not be to him as a creditor; neither shall ye lay upon him usury.
002	EXO	022	026	If thou at all take thy neighbour’s garment to pledge, thou shalt restore it unto him by that the sun goeth down:
002	EXO	022	027	for that is his only covering, it is his garment for his skin: wherein shall he sleep? and it shall come to pass, when he crieth unto me, that I will hear; for I am gracious.
002	EXO	022	028	Thou shalt not revile God, nor curse a ruler of thy people.
002	EXO	022	029	Thou shalt not delay to offer of the abundance of thy fruits, and of thy liquors. The firstborn of thy sons shalt thou give unto me.
002	EXO	022	030	Likewise shalt thou do with thine oxen, [and] with thy sheep: seven days it shall be with its dam; on the eighth day thou shalt give it me.
002	EXO	022	031	And ye shall be holy men unto me: therefore ye shall not eat any flesh that is torn of beasts in the field; ye shall cast it to the dogs.
002	EXO	023	001	Thou shalt not take up a false report: put not thine hand with the wicked to be an unrighteous witness.
002	EXO	023	002	Thou shalt not follow a multitude to do evil; neither shalt thou speak in a cause to turn aside after a multitude to wrest [judgment]:
002	EXO	023	003	neither shalt thou favour a poor man in his cause.
002	EXO	023	004	If thou meet thine enemy’s ox or his ass going astray, thou shalt surely bring it back to him again.
002	EXO	023	005	If thou see the ass of him that hateth thee lying under his burden, and wouldest forbear to help him, thou shalt surely help with him.
002	EXO	023	006	Thou shalt not wrest the judgment of thy poor in his cause.
002	EXO	023	007	Keep thee far from a false matter; and the innocent and righteous slay thou not: for I will not justify the wicked.
002	EXO	023	008	And thou shalt take no gift: for a gift blindeth them that have sight, and perverteth the words of the righteous.
002	EXO	023	009	And a stranger shalt thou not oppress: for ye know the heart of a stranger, seeing ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.
002	EXO	023	010	And six years thou shalt sow thy land, and shalt gather in the increase thereof:
002	EXO	023	011	but the seventh year thou shalt let it rest and lie fallow; that the poor of thy people may eat: and what they leave the beast of the field shall eat. In like manner thou shalt deal with thy vineyard, [and] with thy oliveyard.
002	EXO	023	012	Six days thou shalt do thy work, and on the seventh day thou shalt rest: that thine ox and thine ass may have rest, and the son of thy handmaid, and the stranger, may be refreshed.
002	EXO	023	013	And in all things that I have said unto you take ye heed: and make no mention of the name of other gods, neither let it be heard out of thy mouth.
002	EXO	023	014	Three times thou shalt keep a feast unto me in the year.
002	EXO	023	015	The feast of unleavened bread shalt thou keep: seven days thou shalt eat unleavened bread, as I commanded thee, at the time appointed in the month Abib (for in it thou camest out from Egypt); and none shall appear before me empty:
002	EXO	023	016	and the feast of harvest, the firstfruits of thy labours, which thou sowest in the field: and the feast of ingathering, at the end of the year, when thou gatherest in thy labours out of the field.
002	EXO	023	017	Three times in the year all thy males shall appear before the Lord GOD.
002	EXO	023	018	Thou shalt not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leavened bread; neither shall the fat of my feast remain all night until the morning.
002	EXO	023	019	The first of the firstfruits of thy ground thou shalt bring into the house of the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not seethe a kid in its mother’s milk.
002	EXO	023	020	Behold, I send an angel before thee, to keep thee by the way, and to bring thee into the place which I have prepared.
002	EXO	023	021	Take ye heed of him, and hearken unto his voice; provoke him not: for he will not pardon your transgression; for my name is in him.
002	EXO	023	022	But if thou shalt indeed hearken unto his voice, and do all that I speak; then I will be an enemy unto thine enemies, and an adversary unto thine adversaries.
002	EXO	023	023	For mine angel shall go before thee, and bring thee in unto the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Canaanite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite: and I will cut them off.
002	EXO	023	024	Thou shalt not bow down to their gods, nor serve them, nor do after their works: but thou shalt utterly overthrow them, and break in pieces their pillars.
002	EXO	023	025	And ye shall serve the LORD your God, and he shall bless thy bread, and thy water; and I will take sickness away from the midst of thee.
002	EXO	023	026	There shall none cast her young, nor be barren, in thy land: the number of thy days I will fulfill.
002	EXO	023	027	I will send my terror before thee, and will discomfit all the people to whom thou shalt come, and I will make all thine enemies turn their backs unto thee.
002	EXO	023	028	And I will send the hornet before thee, which shall drive out the Hivite, the Canaanite, and the Hittite, from before thee.
002	EXO	023	029	I will not drive them out from before thee in one year; lest the land become desolate, and the beast of the field multiply against thee.
002	EXO	023	030	By little and little I will drive them out from before thee, until thou be increased, and inherit the land.
002	EXO	023	031	And I will set thy border from the Red Sea even unto the sea of the Philistines, and from the wilderness unto the River: for I will deliver the inhabitants of the land into your hand; and thou shalt drive them out before thee.
002	EXO	023	032	Thou shalt make no covenant with them, nor with their gods.
002	EXO	023	033	They shall not dwell in thy land, lest they make thee sin against me: for if thou serve their gods, it will surely be a snare unto thee.
002	EXO	024	001	And he said unto Moses, Come up unto the LORD, thou, and Aaron, Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel; and worship ye afar off:
002	EXO	024	002	and Moses alone shall come near unto the LORD; but they shall not come near; neither shall the people go up with him.
002	EXO	024	003	And Moses came and told the people all the words of the LORD, and all the judgments: and all the people answered with one voice, and said, All the words which the LORD hath spoken will we do.
002	EXO	024	004	And Moses wrote all the words of the LORD, and rose up early in the morning, and builded an altar under the mount, and twelve pillars, according to the twelve tribes of Israel.
002	EXO	024	005	And he sent young men of the children of Israel, which offered burnt offerings, and sacrificed peace offerings of oxen unto the LORD.
002	EXO	024	006	And Moses took half of the blood, and put it in basons; and half of the blood he sprinkled on the altar.
002	EXO	024	007	And he took the book of the covenant, and read in the audience of the people: and they said, All that the LORD hath spoken will we do, and be obedient.
002	EXO	024	008	And Moses took the blood, and sprinkled it on the people, and said, Behold the blood of the covenant, which the LORD hath made with you concerning all these words.
002	EXO	024	009	Then went up Moses, and Aaron, Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel:
002	EXO	024	010	and they saw the God of Israel; and there was under his feet as it were a paved work of sapphire stone, and as it were the very heaven for clearness.
002	EXO	024	011	And upon the nobles of the children of Israel he laid not his hand: and they beheld God, and did eat and drink.
002	EXO	024	012	And the LORD said unto Moses, Come up to me into the mount, and be there: and I will give thee the tables of stone, and the law and the commandment, which I have written, that thou mayest teach them.
002	EXO	024	013	And Moses rose up, and Joshua his minister: and Moses went up into the mount of God.
002	EXO	024	014	And he said unto the elders, Tarry ye here for us, until we come again unto you: and, behold, Aaron and Hur are with you: whosoever hath a cause, let him come near unto them.
002	EXO	024	015	And Moses went up into the mount, and the cloud covered the mount.
002	EXO	024	016	And the glory of the LORD abode upon mount Sinai, and the cloud covered it six days: and the seventh day he called unto Moses out of the midst of the cloud.
002	EXO	024	017	And the appearance of the glory of the LORD was like devouring fire on the top of the mount in the eyes of the children of Israel.
002	EXO	024	018	And Moses entered into the midst of the cloud, and went up into the mount: and Moses was in the mount forty days and forty nights.
002	EXO	025	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	025	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, that they take for me an offering: of every man whose heart maketh him willing ye shall take my offering.
002	EXO	025	003	And this is the offering which ye shall take of them; gold, and silver, and brass;
002	EXO	025	004	and blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ [hair];
002	EXO	025	005	and rams’ skins dyed red, and sealskins, and acacia wood;
002	EXO	025	006	oil for the light, spices for the anointing oil, and for the sweet incense;
002	EXO	025	007	onyx stones, and stones to be set, for the ephod, and for the breastplate.
002	EXO	025	008	And let them make me a sanctuary; that I may dwell among them.
002	EXO	025	009	According to all that I shew thee, the pattern of the tabernacle, and the pattern of all the furniture thereof, even so shall ye make it.
002	EXO	025	010	And they shall make an ark of acacia wood: two cubits and a half shall be the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.
002	EXO	025	011	And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, within and without shalt thou overlay it, and shalt make upon it a crown of gold round about.
002	EXO	025	012	And thou shalt cast four rings of gold for it, and put them in the four feet thereof; and two rings shall be on the one side of it, and two rings on the other side of it.
002	EXO	025	013	And thou shalt make staves of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold.
002	EXO	025	014	And thou shalt put the staves into the rings on the sides of the ark, to bear the ark withal.
002	EXO	025	015	The staves shall be in the rings of the ark: they shall not be taken from it.
002	EXO	025	016	And thou shalt put into the ark the testimony which I shall give thee.
002	EXO	025	017	And thou shalt make a mercy-seat of pure gold: two cubits and a half [shall be] the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof.
002	EXO	025	018	And thou shalt make two cherubim of gold; of beaten work shalt thou make them, at the two ends of the mercy-seat.
002	EXO	025	019	And make one cherub at the one end, and one cherub at the other end: of one piece with the mercy-seat shall ye make the cherubim on the two ends thereof.
002	EXO	025	020	And the cherubim shall spread out their wings on high, covering the mercy-seat with their wings, with their faces one to another; toward the mercy-seat shall the faces of the cherubim be.
002	EXO	025	021	And thou shalt put the mercy-seat above upon the ark; and in the ark thou shalt put the testimony that I shall give thee.
002	EXO	025	022	And there I will meet with thee, and I will commune with thee from above the mercy-seat, from between the two cherubim which are upon the ark of the testimony, of all things which I will give thee in commandment unto the children of Israel.
002	EXO	025	023	And thou shalt make a table of acacia wood: two cubits [shall be] the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.
002	EXO	025	024	And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, and make thereto a crown of gold round about.
002	EXO	025	025	And thou shalt make unto it a border of an handbreadth round about, and thou shalt make a golden crown to the border thereof round about.
002	EXO	025	026	And thou shalt make for it four rings of gold, and put the rings in the four corners that are on the four feet thereof.
002	EXO	025	027	Close by the border shall the rings be, for places for the staves to bear the table.
002	EXO	025	028	And thou shalt make the staves of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold, that the table may be borne with them.
002	EXO	025	029	And thou shalt make the dishes thereof, and the spoons thereof, and the flagons thereof, and the bowls thereof, to pour out withal: of pure gold shalt thou make them.
002	EXO	025	030	And thou shalt set upon the table shewbread before me alway.
002	EXO	025	031	And thou shalt make a candlestick of pure gold: of beaten work shall the candlestick be made, even its base, and its shaft; its cups, its knops, and its flowers, shall be of one piece with it:
002	EXO	025	032	and there shall be six branches going out of the sides thereof; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side thereof, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side thereof:
002	EXO	025	033	three cups made like almond-blossoms in one branch, a knop and a flower; and three cups made like almond-blossoms in the other branch, a knop and a flower: so for the six branches going out of the candlestick:
002	EXO	025	034	and in the candlestick four cups made like almond-blossoms, the knops thereof, and the flowers thereof:
002	EXO	025	035	and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, for the six branches going out of the candlestick.
002	EXO	025	036	Their knops and their branches shall be of one piece with it: the whole of it one beaten work of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	037	And thou shalt make the lamps thereof, seven: and they shall light the lamps thereof, to give light over against it.
002	EXO	025	038	And the tongs thereof, and the snuffdishes thereof, shall be of pure gold.
002	EXO	025	039	Of a talent of pure gold shall it be made, with all these vessels.
002	EXO	025	040	And see that thou make them after their pattern, which hath been shewed thee in the mount.
002	EXO	026	001	Moreover thou shalt make the tabernacle with ten curtains; of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, with cherubim the work of the cunning workman shalt thou make them.
002	EXO	026	002	The length of each curtain shall be eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of each curtain four cubits: all the curtains shall have one measure.
002	EXO	026	003	Five curtains shall be coupled together one to another; and [the other] five curtains shall be coupled one to another.
002	EXO	026	004	And thou shalt make loops of blue upon the edge of the one curtain from the selvedge in the coupling; and likewise shalt thou make in the edge of the curtain that is outmost in the second coupling.
002	EXO	026	005	Fifty loops shalt thou make in the one curtain, and fifty loops shalt thou make in the edge of the curtain that is in the second coupling; the loops shall be opposite one to another.
002	EXO	026	006	And thou shalt make fifty clasps of gold, and couple the curtains one to another with the clasps: and the tabernacle shall be one.
002	EXO	026	007	And thou shalt make curtains of goats’ [hair] for a tent over the tabernacle: eleven curtains shalt thou make them.
002	EXO	026	008	The length of each curtain shall be thirty cubits, and the breadth of each curtain four cubits: the eleven curtains shall have one measure.
002	EXO	026	009	And thou shalt couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shalt double over the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tent.
002	EXO	026	010	And thou shalt make fifty loops on the edge of the one curtain that is outmost in the coupling, and fifty loops upon the edge of the curtain which is [outmost in] the second coupling.
002	EXO	026	011	And thou shalt make fifty clasps of brass, and put the clasps into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one.
002	EXO	026	012	And the overhanging part that remaineth of the curtains of the tent, the half curtain that remaineth, shall hang over the back of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	013	And the cubit on the one side, and the cubit on the other side, of that which remaineth in the length of the curtains of the tent, shall hang over the sides of the tabernacle on this side and on that side, to cover it.
002	EXO	026	014	And thou shalt make a covering for the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering of sealskins above.
002	EXO	026	015	And thou shalt make the boards for the tabernacle of acacia wood, standing up.
002	EXO	026	016	Ten cubits shall be the length of a board, and a cubit and a half the breadth of each board.
002	EXO	026	017	Two tenons shall there be in each board, joined one to another: thus shalt thou make for all the boards of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	018	And thou shalt make the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards for the south side southward.
002	EXO	026	019	And thou shalt make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for its two tenons, and two sockets under another board for its two tenons:
002	EXO	026	020	and for the second side of the tabernacle, on the north side, twenty boards:
002	EXO	026	021	and their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.
002	EXO	026	022	And for the hinder part of the tabernacle westward thou shalt make six boards.
002	EXO	026	023	And two boards shalt thou make for the corners of the tabernacle in the hinder part.
002	EXO	026	024	And they shall be double beneath, and in like manner they shall be entire unto the top thereof unto one ring: thus shall it be for them both; they shall be for the two corners.
002	EXO	026	025	And there shall be eight boards, and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.
002	EXO	026	026	And thou shalt make bars of acacia wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	026	027	and five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the side of the tabernacle, for the hinder part westward.
002	EXO	026	028	And the middle bar in the midst of the boards shall pass through from end to end.
002	EXO	026	029	And thou shalt overlay the boards with gold, and make their rings of gold for places for the bars: and thou shalt overlay the bars with gold.
002	EXO	026	030	And thou shalt rear up the tabernacle according to the fashion thereof which hath been shewed thee in the mount.
002	EXO	026	031	And thou shalt make a veil of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: with cherubim the work of the cunning workman shall it be made:
002	EXO	026	032	and thou shalt hang it upon four pillars of acacia overlaid with gold, their hooks [shall be] of gold, upon four sockets of silver.
002	EXO	026	033	And thou shalt hang up the veil under the clasps, and shalt bring in thither within the veil the ark of the testimony: and the veil shall divide unto you between the holy place and the most holy.
002	EXO	026	034	And thou shalt put the mercy-seat upon the ark of the testimony in the most holy place.
002	EXO	026	035	And thou shalt set the table without the veil, and the candlestick over against the table on the side of the tabernacle toward the south: and thou shalt put the table on the north side.
002	EXO	026	036	And thou shalt make a screen for the door of the Tent, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the embroiderer.
002	EXO	026	037	And thou shalt make for the screen five pillars of acacia, and overlay them with gold; their hooks shall be of gold: and thou shalt cast five sockets of brass for them.
002	EXO	027	001	And thou shalt make the altar of acacia wood, five cubits long, and five cubits broad; the altar shall be foursquare: and the height thereof shall be three cubits.
002	EXO	027	002	And thou shalt make the horns of it upon the four corners thereof: the horns thereof shall be of one piece with it: and thou shalt overlay it with brass.
002	EXO	027	003	And thou shalt make its pots to take away its ashes, and its shovels, and its basons, and its fleshhooks, and its firepans: all the vessels thereof thou shalt make of brass.
002	EXO	027	004	And thou shalt make for it a grating of network of brass; and upon the net shalt thou make four brasen rings in the four corners thereof.
002	EXO	027	005	And thou shalt put it under the ledge round the altar beneath, that the net may reach halfway up the altar.
002	EXO	027	006	And thou shalt make staves for the altar, staves of acacia wood, and overlay them with brass.
002	EXO	027	007	And the staves thereof shall be put into the rings, and the staves shall be upon the two sides of the altar, in bearing it.
002	EXO	027	008	Hollow with planks shalt thou make it: as it hath been shewed thee in the mount, so shall they make it.
002	EXO	027	009	And thou shalt make the court of the tabernacle: for the south side southward there shall be hangings for the court of fine twined linen an hundred cubits long for one side:
002	EXO	027	010	and the pillars thereof shall be twenty, and their sockets twenty, of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets [shall be] of silver.
002	EXO	027	011	And likewise for the north side in length there shall be hangings an hundred cubits long, and the pillars thereof twenty, and their sockets twenty, of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets of silver.
002	EXO	027	012	And for the breadth of the court on the west side shall be hangings of fifty cubits: their pillars ten, and their sockets ten.
002	EXO	027	013	And the breadth of the court on the east side eastward shall be fifty cubits.
002	EXO	027	014	The hangings for the one side [of the gate] shall be fifteen cubits: their pillars three, and their sockets three.
002	EXO	027	015	And for the other side shall be hangings of fifteen cubits: their pillars three, and their sockets three.
002	EXO	027	016	And for the gate of the court shall be a screen of twenty cubits, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the embroiderer: their pillars four, and their sockets four.
002	EXO	027	017	All the pillars of the court round about shall be filleted with silver; their hooks of silver, and their sockets of brass.
002	EXO	027	018	The length of the court shall be an hundred cubits, and the breadth fifty every where, and the height five cubits, of fine twined linen, and their sockets of brass.
002	EXO	027	019	All the instruments of the tabernacle in all the service thereof, and all the pins thereof, and all the pins of the court, shall be of brass.
002	EXO	027	020	And thou shalt command the children of Israel, that they bring unto thee pure olive oil beaten for the light, to cause a lamp to burn continually.
002	EXO	027	021	In the tent of meeting, without the veil which is before the testimony, Aaron and his sons shall order it from evening to morning before the LORD: it shall be a statute for ever throughout their generations on the behalf of the children of Israel.
002	EXO	028	001	And bring thou near unto thee Aaron thy brother, and his sons with him, from among the children of Israel, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office, even Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar, Aaron’s sons.
002	EXO	028	002	And thou shalt make holy garments for Aaron thy brother, for glory and for beauty.
002	EXO	028	003	And thou shalt speak unto all that are wise hearted, whom I have filled with the spirit of wisdom, that they make Aaron’s garments to sanctify him, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	028	004	And these are the garments which they shall make; a breastplate, and an ephod, and a robe, and a coat of chequer work, a mitre, and a girdle: and they shall make holy garments for Aaron thy brother, and his sons, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	028	005	And they shall take the gold, and the blue, and the purple, and the scarlet, and the fine linen.
002	EXO	028	006	And they shall make the ephod of gold, of blue, and purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the cunning workman.
002	EXO	028	007	It shall have two shoulderpieces joined to the two ends thereof; that it may be joined together.
002	EXO	028	008	And the cunningly woven band, which is upon it, to gird it on withal, shall be like the work thereof [and] of the same piece; of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.
002	EXO	028	009	And thou shalt take two onyx stones, and grave on them the names of the children of Israel:
002	EXO	028	010	six of their names on the one stone, and the names of the six that remain on the other stone, according to their birth.
002	EXO	028	011	With the work of an engraver in stone, like the engravings of a signet, shalt thou engrave the two stones, according to the names of the children of Israel: thou shalt make them to be enclosed in ouches of gold.
002	EXO	028	012	And thou shalt put the two stones upon the shoulderpieces of the ephod, to be stones of memorial for the children of Israel: and Aaron shall bear their names before the LORD upon his two shoulders for a memorial.
002	EXO	028	013	And thou shalt make ouches of gold:
002	EXO	028	014	and two chains of pure gold; like cords shalt thou make them, of wreathen work: and thou shalt put the wreathen chains on the ouches.
002	EXO	028	015	And thou shalt make a breastplate of judgment, the work of the cunning workman; like the work of the ephod thou shalt make it; of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, shalt thou make it.
002	EXO	028	016	Foursquare it shall be [and] double; a span shall be the length thereof, and a span the breadth thereof.
002	EXO	028	017	And thou shalt set in it settings of stones, four rows of stones: a row of sardius, topaz, and carbuncle shall be the first row;
002	EXO	028	018	and the second row an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond;
002	EXO	028	019	and the third row a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst;
002	EXO	028	020	and the fourth row a beryl, and an onyx, and a jasper: they shall be enclosed in gold in their settings.
002	EXO	028	021	And the stones shall be according to the names of the children of Israel, twelve, according to their names; like the engravings of a signet, every one according to his name, they shall be for the twelve tribes.
002	EXO	028	022	And thou shalt make upon the breastplate chains like cords, of wreathen work of pure gold.
002	EXO	028	023	And thou shalt make upon the breastplate two rings of gold, and shalt put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate.
002	EXO	028	024	And thou shalt put the two wreathen chains of gold on the two rings at the ends of the breastplate.
002	EXO	028	025	And the [other] two ends of the two wreathen chains thou shalt put on the two ouches, and put them on the shoulderpieces of the ephod, in the forepart thereof.
002	EXO	028	026	And thou shalt make two rings of gold, and thou shalt put them upon the two ends of the breastplate, upon the edge thereof, which is toward the side of the ephod inward.
002	EXO	028	027	And thou shalt make two rings of gold, and shalt put them on the two shoulderpieces of the ephod underneath, in the forepart thereof, close by the coupling thereof, above the cunningly woven band of the ephod.
002	EXO	028	028	And they shall bind the breastplate by the rings thereof unto the rings of the ephod with a lace of blue, that it may be upon the cunningly woven band of the ephod, and that the breastplate be not loosed from the ephod.
002	EXO	028	029	And Aaron shall bear the names of the children of Israel in the breastplate of judgment upon his heart, when he goeth in unto the holy place, for a memorial before the LORD continually.
002	EXO	028	030	And thou shalt put in the breastplate of judgment the Urim and the Thummim; and they shall be upon Aaron’s heart, when he goeth in before the LORD: and Aaron shall bear the judgment of the children of Israel upon his heart before the LORD continually.
002	EXO	028	031	And thou shalt make the robe of the ephod all of blue.
002	EXO	028	032	And it shall have a hole for the head in the midst thereof: it shall have a binding of woven work round about the hole of it, as it were the hole of a coat of mail, that it be not rent.
002	EXO	028	033	And upon the skirts of it thou shalt make pomegranates of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, round about the skirts thereof; and bells of gold between them round about:
002	EXO	028	034	a golden bell and a pomegranate, a golden bell and a pomegranate, upon the skirts of the robe round about.
002	EXO	028	035	And it shall be upon Aaron to minister: and the sound thereof shall be heard when he goeth in unto the holy place before the LORD, and when he cometh out, that he die not.
002	EXO	028	036	And thou shalt make a plate of pure gold, and grave upon it, like the engravings of a signet, HOLY TO THE LORD.
002	EXO	028	037	And thou shalt put it on a lace of blue, and it shall be upon the mitre; upon the forefront of the mitre it shall be.
002	EXO	028	038	And it shall be upon Aaron’s forehead, and Aaron shall bear the iniquity of the holy things, which the children of Israel shall hallow in all their holy gifts; and it shall be always upon his forehead, that they may be accepted before the LORD.
002	EXO	028	039	And thou shalt weave the coat in chequer work of fine linen, and thou shalt make a mitre of fine linen, and thou shalt make a girdle, the work of the embroiderer.
002	EXO	028	040	And for Aaron’s sons thou shalt make coats, and thou shalt make for them girdles, and headtires shalt thou make for them, for glory and for beauty.
002	EXO	028	041	And thou shalt put them upon Aaron thy brother, and upon his sons with him; and shalt anoint them, and consecrate them, and sanctify them, that they may minister unto me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	028	042	And thou shalt make them linen breeches to cover the flesh of their nakedness; from the loins even unto the thighs they shall reach:
002	EXO	028	043	and they shall be upon Aaron, and upon his sons, when they go in unto the tent of meeting, or when they come near unto the altar to minister in the holy place; that they bear not iniquity, and die: it shall be a statute for ever unto him and unto his seed after him.
002	EXO	029	001	And this is the thing that thou shalt do unto them to hallow them, to minister unto me in the priest’s office: take one young bullock and two rams without blemish,
002	EXO	029	002	and unleavened bread, and cakes unleavened mingled with oil, and wafers unleavened anointed with oil: of fine wheaten flour shalt thou make them.
002	EXO	029	003	And thou shalt put them into one basket, and bring them in the basket, with the bullock and the two rams.
002	EXO	029	004	And Aaron and his sons thou shalt bring unto the door of the tent of meeting, and shalt wash them with water.
002	EXO	029	005	And thou shalt take the garments, and put upon Aaron the coat, and the robe of the ephod, and the ephod, and the breastplate, and gird him with the cunningly woven band of the ephod:
002	EXO	029	006	and thou shalt set the mitre upon his head, and put the holy crown upon the mitre.
002	EXO	029	007	Then shalt thou take the anointing oil, and pour it upon his head, and anoint him.
002	EXO	029	008	And thou shalt bring his sons, and put coats upon them.
002	EXO	029	009	And thou shalt gird them with girdles, Aaron and his sons, and bind headtires on them: and they shall have the priesthood by a perpetual statute: and thou shalt consecrate Aaron and his sons.
002	EXO	029	010	And thou shalt bring the bullock before the tent of meeting: and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands upon the head of the bullock.
002	EXO	029	011	And thou shalt kill the bullock before the LORD, at the door of the tent of meeting.
002	EXO	029	012	And thou shalt take of the blood of the bullock, and put it upon the horns of the altar with thy finger; and thou shalt pour out all the blood at the base of the altar.
002	EXO	029	013	And thou shalt take all the fat that covereth the inwards, and the caul upon the liver, and the two kidneys, and the fat that is upon them, and burn them upon the altar.
002	EXO	029	014	But the flesh of the bullock, and its skin, and its dung, shalt thou burn with fire without the camp: it is a sin offering.
002	EXO	029	015	Thou shalt also take the one ram; and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands upon the head of the ram.
002	EXO	029	016	And thou shalt slay the ram, and thou shalt take its blood, and sprinkle it round about upon the altar.
002	EXO	029	017	And thou shalt cut the ram into its pieces, and wash its inwards, and its legs, and put them with its pieces, and with its head.
002	EXO	029	018	And thou shalt burn the whole ram upon the altar: it is a burnt offering unto the LORD: it is a sweet savour, an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
002	EXO	029	019	And thou shalt take the other ram; and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands upon the head of the ram.
002	EXO	029	020	Then shalt thou kill the ram, and take of its blood, and put it upon the tip of the right ear of Aaron, and upon the tip of the right ear of his sons, and upon the thumb of their right hand, and upon the great toe of their right foot, and sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.
002	EXO	029	021	And thou shalt take of the blood that is upon the altar, and of the anointing oil, and sprinkle it upon Aaron, and upon his garments, and upon his sons, and upon the garments of his sons with him: and he shall be hallowed, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons’ garments with him.
002	EXO	029	022	Also thou shalt take of the ram the fat, and the fat tail, and the fat that covereth the inwards, and the caul of the liver, and the two kidneys, and the fat that is upon them, and the right thigh; for it is a ram of consecration:
002	EXO	029	023	and one loaf of bread, and one cake of oiled bread, and one wafer, out of the basket of unleavened bread that is before the LORD:
002	EXO	029	024	and thou shalt put the whole upon the hands of Aaron, and upon the hands of his sons; and shalt wave them for a wave offering before the LORD.
002	EXO	029	025	And thou shalt take them from their hands, and burn them on the altar upon the burnt offering, for a sweet savour before the LORD: it is an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
002	EXO	029	026	And thou shalt take the breast of Aaron’s ram of consecration, and wave it for a wave offering before the LORD: and it shall be thy portion.
002	EXO	029	027	And thou shalt sanctify the breast of the wave offering, and the thigh of the heave offering, which is waved, and which is heaved up, of the ram of consecration, even of that which is for Aaron, and of that which is for his sons:
002	EXO	029	028	and it shall be for Aaron and his sons as a due for ever from the children of Israel: for it is an heave offering: and it shall be an heave offering from the children of Israel of the sacrifices of their peace offerings, even their heave offering unto the LORD.
002	EXO	029	029	And the holy garments of Aaron shall be for his sons after him, to be anointed in them, and to be consecrated in them.
002	EXO	029	030	Seven days shall the son that is priest in his stead put them on, when he cometh into the tent of meeting to minister in the holy place.
002	EXO	029	031	And thou shalt take the ram of consecration, and seethe its flesh in a holy place.
002	EXO	029	032	And Aaron and his sons shall eat the flesh of the ram, and the bread that is in the basket, at the door of the tent of meeting.
002	EXO	029	033	And they shall eat those things wherewith atonement was made, to consecrate [and] to sanctify them: but a stranger shall not eat thereof, because they are holy.
002	EXO	029	034	And if aught of the flesh of the consecration, or of the bread, remain unto the morning, then thou shalt burn the remainder with fire: it shall not be eaten, because it is holy.
002	EXO	029	035	And thus shalt thou do unto Aaron, and to his sons, according to all that I have commanded thee: seven days shalt thou consecrate them.
002	EXO	029	036	And every day shalt thou offer the bullock of sin offering for atonement: and thou shalt cleanse the altar, when thou makest atonement for it; and thou shalt anoint it, to sanctify it.
002	EXO	029	037	Seven days thou shalt make atonement for the altar, and sanctify it: and the altar shall be most holy; whatsoever toucheth the altar shall be holy.
002	EXO	029	038	Now this is that which thou shalt offer upon the altar; two lambs of the first year day by day continually.
002	EXO	029	039	The one lamb thou shalt offer in the morning; and the other lamb thou shalt offer at even:
002	EXO	029	040	and with the one lamb a tenth part [of an ephah] of fine flour mingled with the fourth part of an hin of beaten oil; and the fourth part of an hin of wine for a drink offering.
002	EXO	029	041	And the other lamb thou shalt offer at even, and shalt do thereto according to the meal offering of the morning, and according to the drink offering thereof, for a sweet savour, an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
002	EXO	029	042	It shall be a continual burnt offering throughout your generations at the door of the tent of meeting before the LORD: where I will meet with you, to speak there unto thee.
002	EXO	029	043	And there I will meet with the children of Israel; and [the Tent] shall be sanctified by my glory.
002	EXO	029	044	And I will sanctify the tent of meeting, and the altar: Aaron also and his sons will I sanctify, to minister to me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	029	045	And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will be their God.
002	EXO	029	046	And they shall know that I am the LORD their God, that brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, that I may dwell among them: I am the LORD their God.
002	EXO	030	001	And thou shalt make an altar to burn incense upon: of acacia wood shalt thou make it.
002	EXO	030	002	A cubit shall be the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof; foursquare shall it be: and two cubits shall be the height thereof: the horns thereof shall be of one piece with it.
002	EXO	030	003	And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, the top thereof, and the sides thereof round about, and the horns thereof; and thou shalt make unto it a crown of gold round about.
002	EXO	030	004	And two golden rings shalt thou make for it under the crown thereof, upon the two ribs thereof, upon the two sides of it shalt thou make them; and they shall be for places for staves to bear it withal.
002	EXO	030	005	And thou shalt make the staves of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold.
002	EXO	030	006	And thou shalt put it before the veil that is by the ark of the testimony, before the mercy-seat that is over the testimony, where I will meet with thee.
002	EXO	030	007	And Aaron shall burn thereon incense of sweet spices: every morning, when he dresseth the lamps, he shall burn it.
002	EXO	030	008	And when Aaron lighteth the lamps at even, he shall burn it, a perpetual incense before the LORD throughout your generations.
002	EXO	030	009	Ye shall offer no strange incense thereon, nor burnt offering, nor meal offering; and ye shall pour no drink offering thereon.
002	EXO	030	010	And Aaron shall make atonement upon the horns of it once in the year: with the blood of the sin offering of atonement once in the year shall he make atonement for it throughout your generations: it is most holy unto the LORD.
002	EXO	030	011	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	030	012	When thou takest the sum of the children of Israel, according to those that are numbered of them, then shall they give every man a ransom for his soul unto the LORD, when thou numberest them; that there be no plague among them, when thou numberest them.
002	EXO	030	013	This they shall give, every one that passeth over unto them that are numbered, half a shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary: (the shekel is twenty gerahs:) half a shekel for an offering to the LORD.
002	EXO	030	014	Every one that passeth over unto them that are numbered, from twenty years old and upward, shall give the offering of the LORD.
002	EXO	030	015	The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less, than the half shekel, when they give the offering of the LORD, to make atonement for your souls.
002	EXO	030	016	And thou shalt take the atonement money from the children of Israel, and shalt appoint it for the service of the tent of meeting; that it may be a memorial for the children of Israel before the LORD, to make atonement for your souls.
002	EXO	030	017	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	030	018	Thou shalt also make a laver of brass, and the base thereof of brass, to wash withal: and thou shalt put it between the tent of meeting and the altar, and thou shalt put water therein.
002	EXO	030	019	And Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and their feet thereat:
002	EXO	030	020	when they go into the tent of meeting, they shall wash with water, that they die not; or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn an offering made by fire unto the LORD:
002	EXO	030	021	so they shall wash their hands and their feet, that they die not: and it shall be a statute for ever to them, even to him and to his seed throughout their generations.
002	EXO	030	022	Moreover the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	030	023	Take thou also unto thee the chief spices, of flowing myrrh five hundred [shekels], and of sweet cinnamon half so much, even two hundred and fifty, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty,
002	EXO	030	024	and of cassia five hundred, after the shekel of the sanctuary, and of olive oil an hin:
002	EXO	030	025	and thou shalt make it an holy anointing oil, a perfume compounded after the art of the perfumer: it shall be an holy anointing oil.
002	EXO	030	026	And thou shalt anoint therewith the tent of meeting, and the ark of the testimony,
002	EXO	030	027	and the table and all the vessels thereof, and the candlestick and the vessels thereof, and the altar of incense,
002	EXO	030	028	and the altar of burnt offering with all the vessels thereof, and the laver and the base thereof.
002	EXO	030	029	And thou shalt sanctify them, that they may be most holy: whatsoever toucheth them shall be holy.
002	EXO	030	030	And thou shalt anoint Aaron and his sons, and sanctify them, that they may minister unto me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	030	031	And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, This shall be an holy anointing oil unto me throughout your generations.
002	EXO	030	032	Upon the flesh of man shall it not be poured, neither shall ye make any like it, according to the composition thereof: it is holy, [and] it shall be holy unto you.
002	EXO	030	033	Whosoever compoundeth any like it, or whosoever putteth any of it upon a stranger, he shall be cut off from his people.
002	EXO	030	034	And the LORD said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight;
002	EXO	030	035	and thou shalt make of it incense, a perfume after the art of the perfumer, seasoned with salt, pure [and] holy:
002	EXO	030	036	and thou shalt beat some of it very small, and put of it before the testimony in the tent of meeting, where I will meet with thee: it shall be unto you most holy.
002	EXO	030	037	And the incense which thou shalt make, according to the composition thereof ye shall not make for yourselves: it shall be unto thee holy for the LORD.
002	EXO	030	038	Whosoever shall make like unto that, to smell thereto, he shall be cut off from his people.
002	EXO	031	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	031	002	See, I have called by name Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah:
002	EXO	031	003	and I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,
002	EXO	031	004	to devise cunning works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,
002	EXO	031	005	and in cutting of stones for setting, and in carving of wood, to work in all manner of workmanship.
002	EXO	031	006	And I, behold, I have appointed with him Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan; and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded thee:
002	EXO	031	007	the tent of meeting, and the ark of the testimony, and the mercy-seat that is thereupon, and all the furniture of the Tent;
002	EXO	031	008	and the table and its vessels, and the pure candlestick with all its vessels, and the altar of incense;
002	EXO	031	009	and the altar of burnt offering with all its vessels, and the laver and its base;
002	EXO	031	010	and the finely wrought garments, and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office;
002	EXO	031	011	and the anointing oil, and the incense of sweet spices for the holy place: according to all that I have commanded thee shall they do.
002	EXO	031	012	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	031	013	Speak thou also unto the children of Israel, saying, Verily ye shall keep my sabbaths: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that ye may know that I am the LORD which sanctify you.
002	EXO	031	014	Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it is holy unto you: every one that profaneth it shall surely be put to death: for whosoever doeth any work therein, that soul shall be cut off from among his people.
002	EXO	031	015	Six days shall work be done; but on the seventh day is a sabbath of solemn rest, holy to the LORD: whosoever doeth any work in the sabbath day, he shall surely be put to death.
002	EXO	031	016	Wherefore the children of Israel shall keep the sabbath, to observe the sabbath throughout their generations, for a perpetual covenant.
002	EXO	031	017	It is a sign between me and the children of Israel for ever: for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.
002	EXO	031	018	And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, the two tables of the testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God.
002	EXO	032	001	And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down from the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we know not what is become of him.
002	EXO	032	002	And Aaron said unto them, Break off the golden rings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them unto me.
002	EXO	032	003	And all the people brake off the golden rings which were in their ears, and brought them unto Aaron.
002	EXO	032	004	And he received it at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, and made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.
002	EXO	032	005	And when Aaron saw [this], he built an altar before it; and Aaron made proclamation, and said, Tomorrow shall be a feast to the LORD.
