002	EXO	036	016	And he coupled five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves.
002	EXO	036	017	And he made fifty loops on the edge of the curtain that was outmost in the coupling, and fifty loops made he upon the edge of the curtain which was [outmost in] the second coupling.
002	EXO	036	018	And he made fifty clasps of brass to couple the tent together, that it might be one.
002	EXO	036	019	And he made a covering for the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering of sealskins above.
002	EXO	036	020	And he made the boards for the tabernacle of acacia wood, standing up.
002	EXO	036	021	Ten cubits was the length of a board, and a cubit and a half the breadth of each board.
002	EXO	036	022	Each board had two tenons, joined one to another: thus did he make for all the boards of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	036	023	And he made the boards for the tabernacle; twenty boards for the south side southward:
002	EXO	036	024	and he made forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for its two tenons, and two sockets under another board for its two tenons.
002	EXO	036	025	And for the second side of the tabernacle, on the north side, he made twenty boards,
002	EXO	036	026	and their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.
002	EXO	036	027	And for the hinder part of the tabernacle westward he made six boards.
002	EXO	036	028	And two boards made he for the corners of the tabernacle in the hinder part.
002	EXO	036	029	And they were double beneath, and in like manner they were entire unto the top thereof unto one ring: thus he did to both of them in the two corners.
002	EXO	036	030	And there were eight boards, and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets; under every board two sockets.
002	EXO	036	031	And he made bars of acacia wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	036	032	and five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the tabernacle for the hinder part westward.
002	EXO	036	033	And he made the middle bar to pass through in the midst of the boards from the one end to the other.
002	EXO	036	034	And he overlaid the boards with gold, and made their rings of gold for places for the bars, and overlaid the bars with gold.
002	EXO	036	035	And he made the veil of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: with cherubim the work of the cunning workman made he it.
002	EXO	036	036	And he made thereunto four pillars of acacia, and overlaid them with gold: their hooks were of gold; and he cast for them four sockets of silver.
002	EXO	036	037	And he made a screen for the door of the Tent, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the embroiderer;
002	EXO	036	038	and the five pillars of it with their hooks: and he overlaid their chapiters and their fillets with gold: and their five sockets were of brass.
002	EXO	037	001	And Bezalel made the ark of acacia wood: two cubits and a half was the length of it, and a cubit and a half the breadth of it, and a cubit and a half the height of it:
002	EXO	037	002	and he overlaid it with pure gold within and without, and made a crown of gold to it round about.
002	EXO	037	003	And he cast for it four rings of gold, in the four feet thereof; even two rings on the one side of it, and two rings on the other side of it.
002	EXO	037	004	And he made staves of acacia wood, and overlaid them with gold.
002	EXO	037	005	And he put the staves into the rings on the sides of the ark, to bear the ark.
002	EXO	037	006	And he made a mercy-seat of pure gold: two cubits and a half [was] the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof.
002	EXO	037	007	And he made two cherubim of gold; of beaten work made he them, at the two ends of the mercy-seat;
002	EXO	037	008	one cherub at the one end, and one cherub at the other end: of one piece with the mercy-seat made he the cherubim at the two ends thereof.
002	EXO	037	009	And the cherubim spread out their wings on high, covering the mercy-seat with their wings, with their faces one to another; toward the mercy-seat were the faces of the cherubim.
002	EXO	037	010	And he made the table of acacia wood: two cubits [was] the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof:
002	EXO	037	011	and he overlaid it with pure gold, and made thereto a crown of gold round about.
002	EXO	037	012	And he made unto it a border of an handbreadth round about, and made a golden crown to the border thereof round about.
002	EXO	037	013	And he cast for it four rings of gold, and put the rings in the four corners that were on the four feet thereof.
002	EXO	037	014	Close by the border were the rings, the places for the staves to bear the table.
002	EXO	037	015	And he made the staves of acacia wood, and overlaid them with gold, to bear the table.
002	EXO	037	016	And he made the vessels which were upon the table, the dishes thereof, and the spoons thereof, and the bowls thereof, and the flagons thereof, to pour out withal, of pure gold.
002	EXO	037	017	And he made the candlestick of pure gold: of beaten work made he the candlestick, even its base, and its shaft; its cups, its knops, and its flowers, were of one piece with it:
002	EXO	037	018	and there were six branches going out of the sides thereof; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side thereof, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side thereof:
002	EXO	037	019	three cups made like almond-blossoms in one branch, a knop and a flower; and three cups made like almond-blossoms in the other branch, a knop and a flower: so for the six branches going out of the candlestick.
002	EXO	037	020	And in the candlestick were four cups made like almond-blossoms, the knops thereof, and the flowers thereof:
002	EXO	037	021	and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, and a knop under two branches of one piece with it, for the six branches going out of it.
002	EXO	037	022	Their knops and their branches were of one piece with it: the whole of it was one beaten work of pure gold.
002	EXO	037	023	And he made the lamps thereof, seven, and the tongs thereof, and the snuffdishes thereof, of pure gold.
002	EXO	037	024	Of a talent of pure gold made he it, and all the vessels thereof.
002	EXO	037	025	And he made the altar of incense of acacia wood: a cubit was the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, foursquare; and two cubits was the height thereof; the horns thereof were of one piece with it.
002	EXO	037	026	And he overlaid it with pure gold, the top thereof, and the sides thereof round about, and the horns of it: and he made unto it a crown of gold round about.
002	EXO	037	027	And he made for it two golden rings under the crown thereof, upon the two ribs thereof, upon the two sides of it, for places for staves to bear it withal.
002	EXO	037	028	And he made the staves of acacia wood, and overlaid them with gold.
002	EXO	037	029	And he made the holy anointing oil, and the pure incense of sweet spices, after the art of the perfumer.
002	EXO	038	001	And he made the altar of burnt offering of acacia wood: five cubits was the length thereof, and five cubits the breadth thereof, foursquare; and three cubits the height thereof.
002	EXO	038	002	And he made the horns thereof upon the four corners of it; the horns thereof were of one piece with it: and he overlaid it with brass.
002	EXO	038	003	And he made all the vessels of the altar, the pots, and the shovels, and the basons, the fleshhooks, and the firepans: all the vessels thereof made he of brass.
002	EXO	038	004	And he made for the altar a grating of network of brass, under the ledge round it beneath, reaching halfway up.
002	EXO	038	005	And he cast four rings for the four ends of the grating of brass, to be places for the staves.
002	EXO	038	006	And he made the staves of acacia wood, and overlaid them with brass.
002	EXO	038	007	And he put the staves into the rings on the sides of the altar, to bear it withal; he made it hollow with planks.
002	EXO	038	008	And he made the laver of brass, and the base thereof of brass, of the mirrors of the serving women which served at the door of the tent of meeting.
002	EXO	038	009	And he made the court: for the south side southward the hangings of the court were of fine twined linen, an hundred cubits:
002	EXO	038	010	their pillars were twenty, and their sockets twenty, of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets were of silver.
002	EXO	038	011	And for the north side an hundred cubits, their pillars twenty, and their sockets twenty, of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets of silver.
002	EXO	038	012	And for the west side were hangings of fifty cubits, their pillars ten, and their sockets ten; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets of silver.
002	EXO	038	013	And for the east side eastward fifty cubits.
002	EXO	038	014	The hangings for the one side [of the gate] were fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three;
002	EXO	038	015	and so for the other side: on this hand and that hand by the gate of the court were hangings of fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three.
002	EXO	038	016	All the hangings of the court round about were of fine twined linen.
002	EXO	038	017	And the sockets for the pillars were of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets of silver; and the overlaying of their chapiters of silver; and all the pillars of the court were filleted with silver.
002	EXO	038	018	And the screen for the gate of the court was the work of the embroiderer, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: and twenty cubits was the length, and the height in the breadth was five cubits, answerable to the hangings of the court.
002	EXO	038	019	And their pillars were four, and their sockets four, of brass; their hooks of silver, and the overlaying of their chapiters and their fillets of silver.
002	EXO	038	020	And all the pins of the tabernacle, and of the court round about, were of brass.
002	EXO	038	021	This is the sum of [the things for] the tabernacle, even the tabernacle of the testimony, as they were counted, according to the commandment of Moses, for the service of the Levites, by the hand of Ithamar, the son of Aaron the priest.
002	EXO	038	022	And Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made all that the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	038	023	And with him was Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan, an engraver, and a cunning workman, and an embroiderer in blue, and in purple, and in scarlet, and fine linen.
002	EXO	038	024	All the gold that was used for the work in all the work of the sanctuary, even the gold of the offering, was twenty and nine talents, and seven hundred and thirty shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary.
002	EXO	038	025	And the silver of them that were numbered of the congregation was an hundred talents, and a thousand seven hundred and threescore and fifteen shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary:
002	EXO	038	026	a beka a head, [that is], half a shekel, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for every one that passed over to them that were numbered, from twenty years old and upward, for six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty men.
002	EXO	038	027	And the hundred talents of silver were for casting the sockets of the sanctuary, and the sockets of the veil; an hundred sockets for the hundred talents, a talent for a socket.
002	EXO	038	028	And of the thousand seven hundred seventy and five [shekels] he made hooks for the pillars, and overlaid their chapiters, and made fillets for them.
002	EXO	038	029	And the brass of the offering was seventy talents, and two thousand and four hundred shekels.
002	EXO	038	030	And therewith he made the sockets to the door of the tent of meeting, and the brasen altar, and the brasen grating for it, and all the vessels of the altar,
002	EXO	038	031	and the sockets of the court round about, and the sockets of the gate of the court, and all the pins of the tabernacle, and all the pins of the court round about.
002	EXO	039	001	And of the blue, and purple, and scarlet, they made finely wrought garments, for ministering in the holy place, and made the holy garments for Aaron; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	002	And he made the ephod of gold, blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.
002	EXO	039	003	And they did beat the gold into thin plates, and cut it into wires, to work it in the blue, and in the purple, and in the scarlet, and in the fine linen, the work of the cunning workman.
002	EXO	039	004	They made shoulderpieces for it, joined together: at the two ends was it joined together.
002	EXO	039	005	And the cunningly woven band, that was upon it, to gird it on withal, was of the same piece [and] like the work thereof; of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	006	And they wrought the onyx stones, enclosed in ouches of gold, graven with the engravings of a signet, according to the names of the children of Israel.
002	EXO	039	007	And he put them on the shoulderpieces of the ephod, to be stones of memorial for the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	008	And he made the breastplate, the work of the cunning workman, like the work of the ephod; of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.
002	EXO	039	009	It was foursquare; they made the breastplate double: a span was the length thereof, and a span the breadth thereof, being double.
002	EXO	039	010	And they set in it four rows of stones: a row of sardius, topaz, and carbuncle was the first row.
002	EXO	039	011	And the second row, an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond.
002	EXO	039	012	And the third row, a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst.
002	EXO	039	013	And the fourth row, a beryl, an onyx, and a jasper: they were enclosed in ouches of gold in their settings.
002	EXO	039	014	And the stones were according to the names of the children of Israel, twelve, according to their names; like the engravings of a signet, every one according to his name, for the twelve tribes.
002	EXO	039	015	And they made upon the breastplate chains like cords, of wreathen work of pure gold.
002	EXO	039	016	And they made two ouches of gold, and two gold rings; and put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate.
002	EXO	039	017	And they put the two wreathen chains of gold on the two rings at the ends of the breastplate.
002	EXO	039	018	And the [other] two ends of the two wreathen chains they put on the two ouches, and put them on the shoulderpieces of the ephod, in the forepart thereof.
002	EXO	039	019	And they made two rings of gold, and put them upon the two ends of the breastplate, upon the edge thereof, which was toward the side of the ephod inward.
002	EXO	039	020	And they made two rings of gold, and put them on the two shoulderpieces of the ephod underneath, in the forepart thereof, close by the coupling thereof, above the cunningly woven band of the ephod.
002	EXO	039	021	And they did bind the breastplate by the rings thereof unto the rings of the ephod with a lace of blue, that it might be upon the cunningly woven band of the ephod, and that the breastplate might not be loosed from the ephod; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	022	And he made the robe of the ephod of woven work, all of blue;
002	EXO	039	023	and the hole of the robe in the midst thereof, as the hole of a coat of mail, with a binding round about the hole of it, that it should not be rent.
002	EXO	039	024	And they made upon the skirts of the robe pomegranates of blue, and purple, and scarlet, [and] twined [linen].
002	EXO	039	025	And they made bells of pure gold, and put the bells between the pomegranates upon the skirts of the robe round about, between the pomegranates;
002	EXO	039	026	a bell and a pomegranate, a bell and a pomegranate, upon the skirts of the robe round about, to minister in; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	027	And they made the coats of fine linen of woven work for Aaron, and for his sons,
002	EXO	039	028	and the mitre of fine linen, and the goodly headtires of fine linen, and the linen breeches of fine twined linen,
002	EXO	039	029	and the girdle of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, the work of the embroiderer; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	030	And they made the plate of the holy crown of pure gold, and wrote upon it a writing, like the engravings of a signet, HOLY TO THE LORD.
002	EXO	039	031	And they tied unto it a lace of blue, to fasten it upon the mitre above; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	039	032	Thus was finished all the work of the tabernacle of the tent of meeting: and the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they.
002	EXO	039	033	And they brought the tabernacle unto Moses, the Tent, and all its furniture, its clasps, its boards, its bars, and its pillars, and its sockets;
002	EXO	039	034	and the covering of rams’ skins dyed red, and the covering of sealskins, and the veil of the screen;
002	EXO	039	035	the ark of the testimony, and the staves thereof, and the mercy-seat;
002	EXO	039	036	the table, all the vessels thereof, and the shewbread;
002	EXO	039	037	the pure candlestick, the lamps thereof, even the lamps to be set in order, and all the vessels thereof, and the oil for the light;
002	EXO	039	038	and the golden altar, and the anointing oil, and the sweet incense, and the screen for the door of the Tent;
002	EXO	039	039	the brasen altar, and its grating of brass, its staves, and all its vessels, the laver and its base;
002	EXO	039	040	the hangings of the court, its pillars, and its sockets, and the screen for the gate of the court, the cords thereof, and the pins thereof, and all the instruments of the service of the tabernacle, for the tent of meeting;
002	EXO	039	041	the finely wrought garments for ministering in the holy place, and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	039	042	According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel did all the work.
002	EXO	039	043	And Moses saw all the work, and, behold, they had done it; as the LORD had commanded, even so had they done it: and Moses blessed them.
002	EXO	040	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
002	EXO	040	002	On the first day of the first month shalt thou rear up the tabernacle of the tent of meeting.
002	EXO	040	003	And thou shalt put therein the ark of the testimony, and thou shalt screen the ark with the veil.
002	EXO	040	004	And thou shalt bring in the table, and set in order the things that are upon it; and thou shalt bring in the candlestick, and light the lamps thereof.
002	EXO	040	005	And thou shalt set the golden altar for incense before the ark of the testimony, and put the screen of the door to the tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	006	And thou shalt set the altar of burnt offering before the door of the tabernacle of the tent of meeting.
002	EXO	040	007	And thou shalt set the laver between the tent of meeting and the altar, and shalt put water therein.
002	EXO	040	008	And thou shalt set up the court round about, and hang up the screen of the gate of the court.
002	EXO	040	009	And thou shalt take the anointing oil, and anoint the tabernacle, and all that is therein, and shalt hallow it, and all the furniture thereof: and it shall be holy.
002	EXO	040	010	And thou shalt anoint the altar of burnt offering, and all its vessels, and sanctify the altar: and the altar shall be most holy.
002	EXO	040	011	And thou shalt anoint the laver and its base, and sanctify it.
002	EXO	040	012	And thou shalt bring Aaron and his sons unto the door of the tent of meeting, and shalt wash them with water.
002	EXO	040	013	And thou shalt put upon Aaron the holy garments; and thou shalt anoint him, and sanctify him, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.
002	EXO	040	014	And thou shalt bring his sons, and put coats upon them:
002	EXO	040	015	and thou shalt anoint them, as thou didst anoint their father, that they may minister unto me in the priest’s office: and their anointing shall be to them for an everlasting priesthood throughout their generations.
002	EXO	040	016	Thus did Moses: according to all that the LORD commanded him, so did he.
002	EXO	040	017	And it came to pass in the first month in the second year, on the first day of the month, that the tabernacle was reared up.
002	EXO	040	018	And Moses reared up the tabernacle, and laid its sockets, and set up the boards thereof, and put in the bars thereof, and reared up its pillars.
002	EXO	040	019	And he spread the tent over the tabernacle, and put the covering of the tent above upon it; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	020	And he took and put the testimony into the ark, and set the staves on the ark, and put the mercy-seat above upon the ark:
002	EXO	040	021	and he brought the ark into the tabernacle, and set up the veil of the screen, and screened the ark of the testimony; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	022	And he put the table in the tent of meeting, upon the side of the tabernacle northward, without the veil.
002	EXO	040	023	And he set the bread in order upon it before the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	024	And he put the candlestick in the tent of meeting, over against the table, on the side of the tabernacle southward.
002	EXO	040	025	And he lighted the lamps before the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	026	And he put the golden altar in the tent of meeting before the veil:
002	EXO	040	027	and he burnt thereon incense of sweet spices; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	028	And he put the screen of the door to the tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	029	And he set the altar of burnt offering at the door of the tabernacle of the tent of meeting, and offered upon it the burnt offering and the meal offering; as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	030	And he set the laver between the tent of meeting and the altar, and put water therein, to wash withal.
002	EXO	040	031	And Moses and Aaron and his sons washed their hands and their feet thereat;
002	EXO	040	032	when they went into the tent of meeting, and when they came near unto the altar, they washed: as the LORD commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	033	And he reared up the court round about the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the screen of the gate of the court. So Moses finished the work.
002	EXO	040	034	Then the cloud covered the tent of meeting, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	035	And Moses was not able to enter into the tent of meeting, because the cloud abode thereon, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.
002	EXO	040	036	And when the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward, throughout all their journeys:
002	EXO	040	037	but if the cloud were not taken up, then they journeyed not till the day that it was taken up.
002	EXO	040	038	For the cloud of the LORD was upon the tabernacle by day, and there was fire therein by night, in the sight of all the house of Israel, throughout all their journeys.
#
# BOOK	003	LEV	Leviticus	Leviticus
003	LEV	001	001	And the LORD called unto Moses, and spake unto him out of the tent of meeting, saying,
003	LEV	001	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When any man of you offereth an oblation unto the LORD, ye shall offer your oblation of the cattle, [even] of the herd and of the flock.
003	LEV	001	003	If his oblation be a burnt offering of the herd, he shall offer it a male without blemish: he shall offer it at the door of the tent of meeting, that he may be accepted before the LORD.
003	LEV	001	004	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.
003	LEV	001	005	And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and Aaron’s sons, the priests, shall present the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about upon the altar that is at the door of the tent of meeting.
003	LEV	001	006	And he shall flay the burnt offering, and cut it into its pieces.
003	LEV	001	007	And the sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire upon the altar, and lay wood in order upon the fire:
003	LEV	001	008	and Aaron’s sons, the priests, shall lay the pieces, the head, and the fat, in order upon the wood that is on the fire which is upon the altar:
003	LEV	001	009	but its inwards and its legs shall he wash with water: and the priest shall burn the whole on the altar, for a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	001	010	And if his oblation be of the flock, of the sheep, or of the goats, for a burnt offering; he shall offer it a male without blemish.
003	LEV	001	011	And he shall kill it on the side of the altar northward before the LORD: and Aaron’s sons, the priests, shall sprinkle its blood upon the altar round about.
003	LEV	001	012	And he shall cut it into its pieces, with its head and its fat: and the priest shall lay them in order on the wood that is on the fire which is upon the altar:
003	LEV	001	013	but the inwards and the legs shall he wash with water: and the priest shall offer the whole, and burn it upon the altar: it is a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	001	014	And if his oblation to the LORD be a burnt offering of fowls, then he shall offer his oblation of turtledoves, or of young pigeons.
003	LEV	001	015	And the priest shall bring it unto the altar, and wring off its head, and burn it on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be drained out on the side of the altar:
003	LEV	001	016	and he shall take away its crop with the filth thereof, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, in the place of the ashes:
003	LEV	001	017	and he shall rend it by the wings thereof, [but] shall not divide it asunder: and the priest shall burn it upon the altar, upon the wood that is upon the fire: it is a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	002	001	And when any one offereth an oblation of a meal offering unto the LORD, his oblation shall be of fine flour; and he shall pour oil upon it, and put frankincense thereon:
003	LEV	002	002	and he shall bring it to Aaron’s sons the priests: and he shall take thereout his handful of the fine flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn [it as] the memorial thereof upon the altar, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD:
003	LEV	002	003	and that which is left of the meal offering shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
003	LEV	002	004	And when thou offerest an oblation of a meal offering baken in the oven, it shall be unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil.
003	LEV	002	005	And if thy oblation be a meal offering of the baking pan, it shall be of fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil.
003	LEV	002	006	Thou shalt part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon: it is a meal offering.
003	LEV	002	007	And if thy oblation be a meal offering of the frying pan, it shall be made of fine flour with oil.
003	LEV	002	008	And thou shalt bring the meal offering that is made of these things unto the LORD: and it shall be presented unto the priest, and he shall bring it unto the altar.
003	LEV	002	009	And the priest shall take up from the meal offering the memorial thereof, and shall burn it upon the altar: an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	002	010	And that which is left of the meal offering shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
003	LEV	002	011	No meal offering, which ye shall offer unto the LORD, shall be made with leaven: for ye shall burn no leaven, nor any honey, as an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	002	012	As an oblation of first[fruits] ye shall offer them unto the LORD: but they shall not come up for a sweet savour on the altar.
003	LEV	002	013	And every oblation of thy meal offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meal offering: with all thine oblations thou shalt offer salt.
003	LEV	002	014	And if thou offer a meal offering of firstfruits unto the LORD, thou shalt offer for the meal offering of thy firstfruits corn in the ear parched with fire, bruised corn of the fresh ear.
003	LEV	002	015	And thou shalt put oil upon it, and lay frankincense thereon: it is a meal offering.
003	LEV	002	016	And the priest shall burn the memorial of it, part of the bruised corn thereof, and part of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof: it is an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	003	001	And if his oblation be a sacrifice of peace offerings; if he offer of the herd, whether male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.
003	LEV	003	002	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his oblation, and kill it at the door of the tent of meeting: and Aaron’s sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.
003	LEV	003	003	And he shall offer of the sacrifice of peace offerings an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards,
003	LEV	003	004	and the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the caul upon the liver, with the kidneys, shall he take away.
003	LEV	003	005	And Aaron’s sons shall burn it on the altar upon the burnt offering, which is upon the wood that is on the fire: it is an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	003	006	And if his oblation for a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD be of the flock; male or female, he shall offer it without blemish.
003	LEV	003	007	If he offer a lamb for his oblation, then shall he offer it before the LORD:
