003	LEV	014	009	And it shall be on the seventh day, that he shall shave all his hair off his head and his beard and his eyebrows, even all his hair he shall shave off: and he shall wash his clothes, and he shall bathe his flesh in water, and he shall be clean.
003	LEV	014	010	And on the eighth day he shall take two he-lambs without blemish, and one ewe-lamb of the first year without blemish, and three tenth parts [of an ephah] of fine flour for a meal offering, mingled with oil, and one log of oil.
003	LEV	014	011	And the priest that cleanseth him shall set the man that is to be cleansed, and those things, before the LORD, at the door of the tent of meeting:
003	LEV	014	012	and the priest shall take one of the he-lambs, and offer him for a guilt offering, and the log of oil, and wave them for a wave offering before the LORD:
003	LEV	014	013	and he shall kill the he-lamb in the place where they kill the sin offering and the burnt offering, in the place of the sanctuary: for as the sin offering is the priest’s, so is the guilt offering: it is most holy:
003	LEV	014	014	and the priest shall take of the blood of the guilt offering, and the priest shall put it upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot:
003	LEV	014	015	and the priest shall take of the log of oil, and pour it into the palm of his own left hand:
003	LEV	014	016	and the priest shall dip his right finger in the oil that is in his left hand, and shall sprinkle of the oil with his finger seven times before the LORD:
003	LEV	014	017	and of the rest of the oil that is in his hand shall the priest put upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot, upon the blood of the guilt offering:
003	LEV	014	018	and the rest of the oil that is in the priest’s hand he shall put upon the head of him that is to be cleansed: and the priest shall make atonement for him before the LORD.
003	LEV	014	019	And the priest shall offer the sin offering, and make atonement for him that is to be cleansed because of his uncleanness; and afterward he shall kill the burnt offering:
003	LEV	014	020	and the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the meal offering upon the altar: and the priest shall make atonement for him, and he shall be clean.
003	LEV	014	021	And if he be poor, and cannot get so much, then he shall take one he-lamb for a guilt offering to be waved, to make atonement for him, and one tenth part [of an ephah] of fine flour mingled with oil for a meal offering, and a log of oil;
003	LEV	014	022	and two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, such as he is able to get; and the one shall be a sin offering, and the other a burnt offering.
003	LEV	014	023	And on the eighth day he shall bring them for his cleansing unto the priest, unto the door of the tent of meeting, before the LORD.
003	LEV	014	024	And the priest shall take the lamb of the guilt offering, and the log of oil, and the priest shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD:
003	LEV	014	025	and he shall kill the lamb of the guilt offering, and the priest shall take of the blood of the guilt offering, and put it upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot:
003	LEV	014	026	and the priest shall pour of the oil into the palm of his own left hand:
003	LEV	014	027	and the priest shall sprinkle with his right finger some of the oil that is in his left hand seven times before the LORD:
003	LEV	014	028	and the priest shall put of the oil that is in his hand upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot, upon the place of the blood of the guilt offering:
003	LEV	014	029	and the rest of the oil that is in the priest’s hand he shall put upon the head of him that is to be cleansed, to make atonement for him before the LORD.
003	LEV	014	030	And he shall offer one of the turtledoves, or of the young pigeons, such as he is able to get;
003	LEV	014	031	even such as he is able to get, the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, with the meal offering: and the priest shall make atonement for him that is to be cleansed before the LORD.
003	LEV	014	032	This is the law of him in whom is the plague of leprosy, who is not able to get [that which pertaineth] to his cleansing.
003	LEV	014	033	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
003	LEV	014	034	When ye be come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a possession, and I put the plague of leprosy in a house of the land of your possession;
003	LEV	014	035	then he that owneth the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, There seemeth to me to be as it were a plague in the house:
003	LEV	014	036	and the priest shall command that they empty the house, before the priest go in to see the plague, that all that is in the house be not made unclean: and afterward the priest shall go in to see the house:
003	LEV	014	037	and he shall look on the plague, and, behold, if the plague be in the walls of the house with hollow strakes, greenish or reddish, and the appearance thereof be lower than the wall;
003	LEV	014	038	then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days:
003	LEV	014	039	and the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look: and, behold, if the plague be spread in the walls of the house;
003	LEV	014	040	then the priest shall command that they take out the stones in which the plague is, and cast them into an unclean place without the city:
003	LEV	014	041	and he shall cause the house to be scraped within round about, and they shall pour out the mortar that they scrape off without the city into an unclean place:
003	LEV	014	042	and they shall take other stones, and put them in the place of those stones; and he shall take other mortar, and shall plaister the house.
003	LEV	014	043	And if the plague come again, and break out in the house, after that he hath taken out the stones, and after he hath scraped the house, and after it is plaistered;
003	LEV	014	044	then the priest shall come in and look, and, behold, if the plague be spread in the house, it is a fretting leprosy in the house: it is unclean.
003	LEV	014	045	And he shall break down the house, the stones of it, and the timber thereof, and all the mortar of the house; and he shall carry them forth out of the city into an unclean place.
003	LEV	014	046	Moreover he that goeth into the house all the while that it is shut up shall be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	014	047	And he that lieth in the house shall wash his clothes; and he that eateth in the house shall wash his clothes.
003	LEV	014	048	And if the priest shall come in, and look, and, behold, the plague hath not spread in the house, after the house was plaistered; then the priest shall pronounce the house clean, because the plague is healed.
003	LEV	014	049	And he shall take to cleanse the house two birds, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:
003	LEV	014	050	and he shall kill one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water:
003	LEV	014	051	and he shall take the cedar wood, and the hyssop, and the scarlet, and the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slain bird, and in the running water, and sprinkle the house seven times:
003	LEV	014	052	and he shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the running water, and with the living bird, and with the cedar wood, and with the hyssop, and with the scarlet:
003	LEV	014	053	but he shall let go the living bird out of the city into the open field: so shall he make atonement for the house: and it shall be clean.
003	LEV	014	054	This is the law for all manner of plague of leprosy, and for a scall;
003	LEV	014	055	and for the leprosy of a garment, and for a house;
003	LEV	014	056	and for a rising, and for a scab, and for a bright spot:
003	LEV	014	057	to teach when it is unclean, and when it is clean: this is the law of leprosy.
003	LEV	015	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses and to Aaron, saying,
003	LEV	015	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When any man hath an issue out of his flesh, because of his issue he is unclean.
003	LEV	015	003	And this shall be his uncleanness in his issue: whether his flesh run with his issue, or his flesh be stopped from his issue, it is his uncleanness.
003	LEV	015	004	Every bed whereon he that hath the issue lieth shall be unclean: and every thing whereon he sitteth shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	005	And whosoever toucheth his bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	006	And he that sitteth on any thing whereon he that hath the issue sat shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	007	And he that toucheth the flesh of him that hath the issue shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	008	And if he that hath the issue spit upon him that is clean; then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	009	And what saddle soever he that hath the issue rideth upon shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	010	And whosoever toucheth any thing that was under him shall be unclean until the even: and he that beareth those things shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	011	And whomsoever he that hath the issue toucheth, without having rinsed his hands in water, he shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	012	And the earthen vessel, which he that hath the issue toucheth, shall be broken: and every vessel of wood shall be rinsed in water.
003	LEV	015	013	And when he that hath an issue is cleansed of his issue, then he shall number to himself seven days for his cleansing, and wash his clothes; and he shall bathe his flesh in running water, and shall be clean.
003	LEV	015	014	And on the eighth day he shall take to him two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and come before the LORD unto the door of the tent of meeting, and give them unto the priest:
003	LEV	015	015	and the priest shall offer them, the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering; and the priest shall make atonement for him before the LORD for his issue.
003	LEV	015	016	And if any man’s seed of copulation go out from him, then he shall bathe all his flesh in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	017	And every garment, and every skin, whereon is the seed of copulation, shall be washed with water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	018	The woman also with whom a man shall lie with seed of copulation, they shall both bathe themselves in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	019	And if a woman have an issue, [and] her issue in her flesh be blood, she shall be in her impurity seven days: and whosoever toucheth her shall be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	020	And every thing that she lieth upon in her impurity shall be unclean: every thing also that she sitteth upon shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	021	And whosoever toucheth her bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	022	And whosoever toucheth any thing that she sitteth upon shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	023	And if it be on the bed, or on any thing whereon she sitteth, when he toucheth it, he shall be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	024	And if any man lie with her, and her impurity be upon him, he shall be unclean seven days; and every bed whereon he lieth shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	025	And if a woman have an issue of her blood many days not in the time of her impurity, or if she have an issue beyond the time of her impurity; all the days of the issue of her uncleanness she shall be as in the days of her impurity: she is unclean.
003	LEV	015	026	Every bed whereon she lieth all the days of her issue shall be unto her as the bed of her impurity: and every thing whereon she sitteth shall be unclean, as the uncleanness of her impurity.
003	LEV	015	027	And whosoever toucheth those things shall be unclean, and shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even.
003	LEV	015	028	But if she be cleansed of her issue, then she shall number to herself seven days, and after that she shall be clean.
003	LEV	015	029	And on the eighth day she shall take unto her two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and bring them unto the priest, to the door of the tent of meeting.
003	LEV	015	030	And the priest shall offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering; and the priest shall make atonement for her before the LORD for the issue of her uncleanness.
003	LEV	015	031	Thus shall ye separate the children of Israel from their uncleanness; that they die not in their uncleanness, when they defile my tabernacle that is in the midst of them.
003	LEV	015	032	This is the law of him that hath an issue, and of him whose seed of copulation goeth from him, so that he is unclean thereby;
003	LEV	015	033	and of her that is sick with her impurity, and of him that hath an issue, of the man, and of the woman, and of him that lieth with her that is unclean.
003	LEV	016	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, after the death of the two sons of Aaron, when they drew near before the LORD, and died;
003	LEV	016	002	and the LORD said unto Moses, Speak unto Aaron thy brother, that he come not at all times into the holy place within the veil, before the mercy-seat which is upon the ark; that he die not: for I will appear in the cloud upon the mercy-seat.
003	LEV	016	003	Herewith shall Aaron come into the holy place: with a young bullock for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering.
003	LEV	016	004	He shall put on the holy linen coat, and he shall have the linen breeches upon his flesh, and shall be girded with the linen girdle, and with the linen mitre shall he be attired: they are the holy garments; and he shall bathe his flesh in water, and put them on.
003	LEV	016	005	And he shall take of the congregation of the children of Israel two he-goats for a sin offering, and one ram for a burnt offering.
003	LEV	016	006	And Aaron shall present the bullock of the sin offering, which is for himself, and make atonement for himself, and for his house.
003	LEV	016	007	And he shall take the two goats, and set them before the LORD at the door of the tent of meeting.
003	LEV	016	008	And Aaron shall cast lots upon the two goats; one lot for the LORD, and the other lot for Azazel.
003	LEV	016	009	And Aaron shall present the goat upon which the lot fell for the LORD, and offer him for a sin offering.
003	LEV	016	010	But the goat, on which the lot fell for Azazel, shall be set alive before the LORD, to make atonement for him, to send him away for Azazel into the wilderness.
003	LEV	016	011	And Aaron shall present the bullock of the sin offering, which is for himself, and shall make atonement for himself, and for his house, and shall kill the bullock of the sin offering which is for himself:
003	LEV	016	012	and he shall take a censer full of coals of fire from off the altar before the LORD, and his hands full of sweet incense beaten small, and bring it within the veil:
003	LEV	016	013	and he shall put the incense upon the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy-seat that is upon the testimony, that he die not:
003	LEV	016	014	and he shall take of the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle it with his finger upon the mercy-seat on the east; and before the mercy-seat shall he sprinkle of the blood with his finger seven times.
003	LEV	016	015	Then shall he kill the goat of the sin offering, that is for the people, and bring his blood within the veil, and do with his blood as he did with the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle it upon the mercy-seat, and before the mercy-seat:
003	LEV	016	016	and he shall make atonement for the holy place, because of the uncleannesses of the children of Israel, and because of their transgressions, even all their sins: and so shall he do for the tent of meeting, that dwelleth with them in the midst of their uncleannesses.
003	LEV	016	017	And there shall be no man in the tent of meeting when he goeth in to make atonement in the holy place, until he come out, and have made atonement for himself, and for his household, and for all the assembly of Israel.
003	LEV	016	018	And he shall go out unto the altar that is before the LORD, and make atonement for it; and shall take of the blood of the bullock, and of the blood of the goat, and put it upon the horns of the altar round about.
003	LEV	016	019	And he shall sprinkle of the blood upon it with his finger seven times, and cleanse it, and hallow it from the uncleannesses of the children of Israel.
003	LEV	016	020	And when he hath made an end of atoning for the holy place, and the tent of meeting, and the altar, he shall present the live goat:
003	LEV	016	021	and Aaron shall lay both his hands upon the head of the live goat, and confess over him all the iniquities of the children of Israel, and all their transgressions, even all their sins; and he shall put them upon the head of the goat, and shall send him away by the hand of a man that is in readiness into the wilderness:
003	LEV	016	022	and the goat shall bear upon him all their iniquities unto a solitary land: and he shall let go the goat in the wilderness.
003	LEV	016	023	And Aaron shall come into the tent of meeting, and shall put off the linen garments, which he put on when he went into the holy place, and shall leave them there:
003	LEV	016	024	and he shall bathe his flesh in water in a holy place, and put on his garments, and come forth, and offer his burnt offering and the burnt offering of the people, and make atonement for himself and for the people.
003	LEV	016	025	And the fat of the sin offering shall he burn upon the altar.
003	LEV	016	026	And he that letteth go the goat for Azazel shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp.
003	LEV	016	027	And the bullock of the sin offering, and the goat of the sin offering, whose blood was brought in to make atonement in the holy place, shall be carried forth without the camp; and they shall burn in the fire their skins, and their flesh, and their dung.
003	LEV	016	028	And he that burneth them shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp.
003	LEV	016	029	And it shall be a statute for ever unto you: in the seventh month, on the tenth day of the month, ye shall afflict your souls, and shall do no manner of work, the homeborn, or the stranger that sojourneth among you:
003	LEV	016	030	for on this day shall atonement be made for you, to cleanse you; from all your sins shall ye be clean before the LORD.
003	LEV	016	031	It is a sabbath of solemn rest unto you, and ye shall afflict your souls; it is a statute for ever.
003	LEV	016	032	And the priest, who shall be anointed and who shall be consecrated to be priest in his father’s stead, shall make the atonement, and shall put on the linen garments, even the holy garments:
003	LEV	016	033	and he shall make atonement for the holy sanctuary, and he shall make atonement for the tent of meeting and for the altar; and he shall make atonement for the priests and for all the people of the assembly.
003	LEV	016	034	And this shall be an everlasting statute unto you, to make atonement for the children of Israel because of all their sins once in the year. And he did as the LORD commanded Moses.
003	LEV	017	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	017	002	Speak unto Aaron, and unto his sons, and unto all the children of Israel, and say unto them; This is the thing which the LORD hath commanded, saying,
003	LEV	017	003	What man soever there be of the house of Israel, that killeth an ox, or lamb, or goat, in the camp, or that killeth it without the camp,
003	LEV	017	004	and hath not brought it unto the door of the tent of meeting, to offer it as an oblation unto the LORD before the tabernacle of the LORD: blood shall be imputed unto that man; he hath shed blood; and that man shall be cut off from among his people:
003	LEV	017	005	To the end that the children of Israel may bring their sacrifices, which they sacrifice in the open field, even that they may bring them unto the LORD, unto the door of the tent of meeting, unto the priest, and sacrifice them for sacrifices of peace offerings unto the LORD.
003	LEV	017	006	And the priest shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar of the LORD at the door of the tent of meeting, and burn the fat for a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	017	007	And they shall no more sacrifice their sacrifices unto the he-goats, after whom they go a whoring. This shall be a statute for ever unto them throughout their generations.
003	LEV	017	008	And thou shalt say unto them, Whatsoever man there be of the house of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among them, that offereth a burnt offering or sacrifice,
003	LEV	017	009	and bringeth it not unto the door of the tent of meeting, to sacrifice it unto the LORD; even that man shall be cut off from his people.
003	LEV	017	010	And whatsoever man there be of the house of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among them, that eateth any manner of blood; I will set my face against that soul that eateth blood, and will cut him off from among his people.
003	LEV	017	011	For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make atonement for your souls: for it is the blood that maketh atonement by reason of the life.
003	LEV	017	012	Therefore I said unto the children of Israel, No soul of you shall eat blood, neither shall any stranger that sojourneth among you eat blood.
003	LEV	017	013	And whatsoever man there be of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among them, which taketh in hunting any beast or fowl that may be eaten; he shall pour out the blood thereof, and cover it with dust.
003	LEV	017	014	For as to the life of all flesh, the blood thereof is [all one] with the life thereof: therefore I said unto the children of Israel, Ye shall eat the blood of no manner of flesh: for the life of all flesh is the blood thereof: whosoever eateth it shall be cut off.
003	LEV	017	015	And every soul that eateth that which dieth of itself, or that which is torn of beasts, whether he be homeborn or a stranger, he shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the even: then shall he be clean.
003	LEV	017	016	But if he wash them not, nor bathe his flesh, then he shall bear his iniquity.
003	LEV	018	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	018	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	018	003	After the doings of the land of Egypt, wherein ye dwelt, shall ye not do: and after the doings of the land of Canaan, whither I bring you, shall ye not do: neither shall ye walk in their statutes.
003	LEV	018	004	My judgments shall ye do, and my statutes shall ye keep, to walk therein: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	018	005	Ye shall therefore keep my statutes, and my judgments: which if a man do, he shall live in them: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	018	006	None of you shall approach to any that is near of kin to him, to uncover [their] nakedness: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	018	007	The nakedness of thy father, even the nakedness of thy mother, shalt thou not uncover: she is thy mother; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
003	LEV	018	008	The nakedness of thy father’s wife shalt thou not uncover: it is thy father’s nakedness.
003	LEV	018	009	The nakedness of thy sister, the daughter of thy father, or the daughter of thy mother, whether born at home, or born abroad, even their nakedness thou shalt not uncover.
003	LEV	018	010	The nakedness of thy son’s daughter, or of thy daughter’s daughter, even their nakedness thou shalt not uncover: for theirs is thine own nakedness.
003	LEV	018	011	The nakedness of thy father’s wife’s daughter, begotten of thy father, she is thy sister, thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
003	LEV	018	012	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father’s sister: she is thy father’s near kinswoman.
003	LEV	018	013	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy mother’s sister: for she is thy mother’s near kinswoman.
003	LEV	018	014	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father’s brother, thou shalt not approach to his wife: she is thine aunt.
003	LEV	018	015	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy daughter in law: she is thy son’s wife; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
003	LEV	018	016	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy brother’s wife: it is thy brother’s nakedness.
003	LEV	018	017	Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of a woman and her daughter; thou shalt not take her son’s daughter, or her daughter’s daughter, to uncover her nakedness; they are near kinswomen: it is wickedness.
003	LEV	018	018	And thou shalt not take a woman to her sister, to be a rival [to her], to uncover her nakedness, beside the other in her life time.
003	LEV	018	019	And thou shalt not approach unto a woman to uncover her nakedness, as long as she is impure by her uncleanness.
003	LEV	018	020	And thou shalt not lie carnally with thy neighbour’s wife, to defile thyself with her.
003	LEV	018	021	And thou shalt not give any of thy seed to make them pass through [the fire] to Molech, neither shalt thou profane the name of thy God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	018	022	Thou shalt not lie with mankind, as with womankind: it is abomination.
003	LEV	018	023	And thou shalt not lie with any beast to defile thyself therewith: neither shall any woman stand before a beast, to lie down thereto: it is confusion.
003	LEV	018	024	Defile not ye yourselves in any of these things: for in all these the nations are defiled which I cast out from before you:
003	LEV	018	025	And the land is defiled: therefore I do visit the iniquity thereof upon it, and the land vomiteth out her inhabitants.
003	LEV	018	026	Ye therefore shall keep my statutes and my judgments, and shall not do any of these abominations; neither the homeborn, nor the stranger that sojourneth among you:
003	LEV	018	027	(for all these abominations have the men of the land done, which were before you, and the land is defiled;)
003	LEV	018	028	that the land vomit not you out also, when ye defile it, as it vomited out the nation that was before you.
003	LEV	018	029	For whosoever shall do any of these abominations, even the souls that do them shall be cut off from among their people.
003	LEV	018	030	Therefore shall ye keep my charge, that ye do not any of these abominable customs, which were done before you, and that ye defile not yourselves therein: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	019	002	Speak unto all the congregation of the children of Israel, and say unto them, Ye shall be holy: for I the LORD your God am holy.
003	LEV	019	003	Ye shall fear every man his mother, and his father, and ye shall keep my sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	004	Turn ye not unto idols, nor make to yourselves molten gods: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	005	And when ye offer a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD, ye shall offer it that ye may be accepted.
003	LEV	019	006	It shall be eaten the same day ye offer it, and on the morrow: and if aught remain until the third day, it shall be burnt with fire.
003	LEV	019	007	And if it be eaten at all on the third day, it is an abomination; it shall not be accepted:
003	LEV	019	008	but every one that eateth it shall bear his iniquity, because he hath profaned the holy thing of the LORD: and that soul shall be cut off from his people.
003	LEV	019	009	And when ye reap the harvest of your land, thou shalt not wholly reap the corners of thy field, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning of thy harvest.
003	LEV	019	010	And thou shalt not glean thy vineyard, neither shalt thou gather the fallen fruit of thy vineyard; thou shalt leave them for the poor and for the stranger: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	011	Ye shall not steal; neither shall ye deal falsely, nor lie one to another.
003	LEV	019	012	And ye shall not swear by my name falsely, so that thou profane the name of thy God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	013	Thou shalt not oppress thy neighbour, nor rob him: the wages of a hired servant shall not abide with thee all night until the morning.
003	LEV	019	014	Thou shalt not curse the deaf, nor put a stumblingblock before the blind, but thou shalt fear thy God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	015	Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment: thou shalt not respect the person of the poor, nor honour the person of the mighty: but in righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour.
003	LEV	019	016	Thou shalt not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people: neither shalt thou stand against the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	017	Thou shalt not hate thy brother in thine heart: thou shalt surely rebuke thy neighbour, and not bear sin because of him.
003	LEV	019	018	Thou shalt not take vengeance, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	019	Ye shall keep my statutes. Thou shalt not let thy cattle gender with a diverse kind: thou shalt not sow thy field with two kinds of seed: neither shall there come upon thee a garment of two kinds of stuff mingled together.
003	LEV	019	020	And whosoever lieth carnally with a woman, that is a bondmaid, betrothed to an husband, and not at all redeemed, nor freedom given her; they shall be punished; they shall not be put to death, because she was not free.
003	LEV	019	021	And he shall bring his guilt offering unto the LORD, unto the door of the tent of meeting, even a ram for a guilt offering.
003	LEV	019	022	And the priest shall make atonement for him with the ram of the guilt offering before the LORD for his sin which he hath sinned: and he shall be forgiven for his sin which he hath sinned.
003	LEV	019	023	And when ye shall come into the land, and shall have planted all manner of trees for food, then ye shall count the fruit thereof as their uncircumcision: three years shall they be as uncircumcised unto you; it shall not be eaten.
003	LEV	019	024	But in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy, for giving praise unto the LORD.
003	LEV	019	025	And in the fifth year shall ye eat of the fruit thereof, that it may yield unto you the increase thereof: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	026	Ye shall not eat any thing with the blood: neither shall ye use enchantments, nor practise augury.
003	LEV	019	027	Ye shall not round the corners of your heads, neither shalt thou mar the corners of thy beard.
003	LEV	019	028	Ye shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor print any marks upon you: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	029	Profane not thy daughter, to make her a harlot; lest the land fall to whoredom, and the land become full of wickedness.
003	LEV	019	030	Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	031	Turn ye not unto them that have familiar spirits, nor unto the wizards; seek them not out, to be defiled by them: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	032	Thou shalt rise up before the hoary head, and honour the face of the old man, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	019	033	And if a stranger sojourn with thee in your land, ye shall not do him wrong.
003	LEV	019	034	The stranger that sojourneth with you shall be unto you as the homeborn among you, and thou shalt love him as thyself; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	019	035	Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment, in meteyard, in weight, or in measure.
003	LEV	019	036	Just balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just hin, shall ye have: I am the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt.
003	LEV	019	037	And ye shall observe all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	020	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	020	002	Moreover, thou shalt say to the children of Israel, Whosoever he be of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn in Israel, that giveth of his seed unto Molech; he shall surely be put to death: the people of the land shall stone him with stones.
003	LEV	020	003	I also will set my face against that man, and will cut him off from among his people; because he hath given of his seed unto Molech, to defile my sanctuary, and to profane my holy name.
003	LEV	020	004	And if the people of the land do any ways hide their eyes from that man, when he giveth of his seed unto Molech, and put him not to death:
003	LEV	020	005	then I will set my face against that man, and against his family, and will cut him off, and all that go a whoring after him, to commit whoredom with Molech, from among their people.
003	LEV	020	006	And the soul that turneth unto them that have familiar spirits, and unto the wizards, to go a whoring after them, I will even set my face against that soul, and will cut him off from among his people.
003	LEV	020	007	Sanctify yourselves therefore, and be ye holy: for I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	020	008	And ye shall keep my statutes, and do them: I am the LORD which sanctify you.
003	LEV	020	009	For every one that curseth his father or his mother shall surely be put to death: he hath cursed his father or his mother; his blood shall be upon him.
003	LEV	020	010	And the man that committeth adultery with another man’s wife, even he that committeth adultery with his neighbour’s wife, the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death.
003	LEV	020	011	And the man that lieth with his father’s wife hath uncovered his father’s nakedness: both of them shall surely be put to death; their blood shall be upon them.
003	LEV	020	012	And if a man lie with his daughter in law, both of them shall surely be put to death: they have wrought confusion; their blood shall be upon them.
003	LEV	020	013	And if a man lie with mankind, as with womankind, both of them have committed abomination: they shall surely be put to death; their blood shall be upon them.
003	LEV	020	014	And if a man take a wife and her mother, it is wickedness: they shall be burnt with fire, both he and they; that there be no wickedness among you.
003	LEV	020	015	And if a man lie with a beast, he shall surely be put to death: and ye shall slay the beast.
003	LEV	020	016	And if a woman approach unto any beast, and lie down thereto, thou shalt kill the woman, and the beast: they shall surely be put to death; their blood shall be upon them.
003	LEV	020	017	And if a man shall take his sister, his father’s daughter, or his mother’s daughter, and see her nakedness, and she see his nakedness; it is a shameful thing; and they shall be cut off in the sight of the children of their people: he hath uncovered his sister’s nakedness; he shall bear his iniquity.
003	LEV	020	018	And if a man shall lie with a woman having her sickness, and shall uncover her nakedness; he hath made naked her fountain, and she hath uncovered the fountain of her blood: and both of them shall be cut off from among their people.
003	LEV	020	019	And thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy mother’s sister, nor of thy father’s sister: for he hath made naked his near kin: they shall bear their iniquity.
003	LEV	020	020	And if a man shall lie with his uncle’s wife, he hath uncovered his uncle’s nakedness: they shall bear their sin; they shall die childless.
003	LEV	020	021	And if a man shall take his brother’s wife, it is impurity: he hath uncovered his brother’s nakedness; they shall be childless.
003	LEV	020	022	Ye shall therefore keep all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: that the land, whither I bring you to dwell therein, vomit you not out.
003	LEV	020	023	And ye shall not walk in the customs of the nation, which I cast out before you: for they did all these things, and therefore I abhorred them.
003	LEV	020	024	But I have said unto you, Ye shall inherit their land, and I will give it unto you to possess it, a land flowing with milk and honey: I am the LORD your God, which have separated you from the peoples.
003	LEV	020	025	Ye shall therefore separate between the clean beast and the unclean, and between the unclean fowl and the clean: and ye shall not make your souls abominable by beast, or by fowl, or by any thing wherewith the ground teemeth, which I have separated from you as unclean.
003	LEV	020	026	And ye shall be holy unto me: for I the LORD am holy, and have separated you from the peoples, that ye should be mine.
003	LEV	020	027	A man also or a woman that hath a familiar spirit, or that is a wizard, shall surely be put to death: they shall stone them with stones: their blood shall be upon them.
003	LEV	021	001	And the LORD said unto Moses, Speak unto the priests the sons of Aaron, and say unto them, There shall none defile himself for the dead among his people;
003	LEV	021	002	except for his kin, that is near unto him, for his mother, and for his father, and for his son, and for his daughter, and for his brother;
003	LEV	021	003	and for his sister a virgin, that is near unto him, which hath had no husband, for her may he defile himself.
003	LEV	021	004	He shall not defile himself, [being] a chief man among his people, to profane himself.
003	LEV	021	005	They shall not make baldness upon their head, neither shall they shave off the corner of their beard, nor make any cuttings in their flesh.
003	LEV	021	006	They shall be holy unto their God, and not profane the name of their God: for the offerings of the LORD made by fire, the bread of their God, they do offer: therefore they shall be holy.
003	LEV	021	007	They shall not take a woman that is a harlot, or profane; neither shall they take a woman put away from her husband: for he is holy unto his God.
003	LEV	021	008	Thou shalt sanctify him therefore; for he offereth the bread of thy God: he shall be holy unto thee: for I the LORD, which sanctify you, am holy.
003	LEV	021	009	And the daughter of any priest, if she profane herself by playing the harlot, she profaneth her father: she shall be burnt with fire.
003	LEV	021	010	And he that is the high priest among his brethren, upon whose head the anointing oil is poured, and that is consecrated to put on the garments, shall not let the hair of his head go loose, nor rend his clothes;
003	LEV	021	011	neither shall he go in to any dead body, nor defile himself for his father, or for his mother;
003	LEV	021	012	neither shall he go out of the sanctuary, nor profane the sanctuary of his God; for the crown of the anointing oil of his God is upon him: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	021	013	And he shall take a wife in her virginity.
003	LEV	021	014	A widow, or one divorced, or a profane woman, an harlot, these shall he not take: but a virgin of his own people shall he take to wife.
003	LEV	021	015	And he shall not profane his seed among his people: for I am the LORD which sanctify him.
003	LEV	021	016	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	021	017	Speak unto Aaron, saying, Whosoever he be of thy seed throughout their generations that hath a blemish, let him not approach to offer the bread of his God.
003	LEV	021	018	For whatsoever man he be that hath a blemish, he shall not approach: a blind man, or a lame, or he that hath a flat nose, or any thing superfluous,
003	LEV	021	019	or a man that is brokenfooted, or brokenhanded,
003	LEV	021	020	or crookbackt, or a dwarf, or that hath a blemish in his eye, or is scurvy, or scabbed, or hath his stones broken;
003	LEV	021	021	no man of the seed of Aaron the priest, that hath a blemish, shall come nigh to offer the offerings of the LORD made by fire: he hath a blemish; he shall not come nigh to offer the bread of his God.
003	LEV	021	022	He shall eat the bread of his God, both of the most holy, and of the holy.
003	LEV	021	023	Only he shall not go in unto the veil, nor come nigh unto the altar, because he hath a blemish; that he profane not my sanctuaries: for I am the LORD which sanctify them.
003	LEV	021	024	So Moses spake unto Aaron, and to his sons, and unto all the children of Israel.
003	LEV	022	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	022	002	Speak unto Aaron and to his sons, that they separate themselves from the holy things of the children of Israel, which they hallow unto me, and that they profane not my holy name: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	022	003	Say unto them, Whosoever he be of all your seed throughout your generations, that approacheth unto the holy things, which the children of Israel hallow unto the LORD, having his uncleanness upon him, that soul shall be cut off from before me: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	022	004	What man soever of the seed of Aaron is a leper, or hath an issue; he shall not eat of the holy things, until he be clean. And whoso toucheth any thing that is unclean by the dead, or a man whose seed goeth from him;
003	LEV	022	005	or whosoever toucheth any creeping thing, whereby he may be made unclean, or a man of whom he may take uncleanness, whatsoever uncleanness he hath;
003	LEV	022	006	the soul which toucheth any such shall be unclean until the even, and shall not eat of the holy things, unless he bathe his flesh in water.
003	LEV	022	007	And when the sun is down, he shall be clean; and afterward he shall eat of the holy things, because it is his bread.
003	LEV	022	008	That which dieth of itself, or is torn of beasts, he shall not eat to defile himself therewith: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	022	009	They shall therefore keep my charge, lest they bear sin for it, and die therein, if they profane it: I am the LORD which sanctify them.
003	LEV	022	010	There shall no stranger eat of the holy thing: a sojourner of the priest’s, or an hired servant, shall not eat of the holy thing.
003	LEV	022	011	But if a priest buy any soul, the purchase of his money, he shall eat of it; and such as are born in his house, they shall eat of his bread.
003	LEV	022	012	And if a priest’s daughter be married unto a stranger, she shall not eat of the heave offering of the holy things.
003	LEV	022	013	But if a priest’s daughter be a widow, or divorced, and have no child, and is returned unto her father’s house, as in her youth, she shall eat of her father’s bread: but there shall no stranger eat thereof.
003	LEV	022	014	And if a man eat of the holy thing unwittingly, then he shall put the fifth part thereof unto it, and shall give unto the priest the holy thing.
003	LEV	022	015	And they shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, which they offer unto the LORD;
003	LEV	022	016	and [so] cause them to bear the iniquity that bringeth guilt, when they eat their holy things: for I am the LORD which sanctify them.
003	LEV	022	017	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	022	018	Speak unto Aaron, and to his sons, and unto all the children of Israel, and say unto them, Whosoever he be of the house of Israel, or of the strangers in Israel, that offereth his oblation, whether it be any of their vows, or any of their freewill offerings, which they offer unto the LORD for a burnt offering;
003	LEV	022	019	that ye may be accepted, [ye shall offer] a male without blemish, of the beeves, of the sheep, or of the goats.
003	LEV	022	020	But whatsoever hath a blemish, that shall ye not offer: for it shall not be acceptable for you.
003	LEV	022	021	And whosoever offereth a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD to accomplish a vow, or for a freewill offering, of the herd or of the flock, it shall be perfect to be accepted; there shall be no blemish therein.
003	LEV	022	022	Blind, or broken, or maimed, or having a wen, or scurvy, or scabbed, ye shall not offer these unto the LORD, nor make an offering by fire of them upon the altar unto the LORD.
003	LEV	022	023	Either a bullock or a lamb that hath any thing superfluous or lacking in his parts, that mayest thou offer for a freewill offering; but for a vow it shall not be accepted.
003	LEV	022	024	That which hath its stones bruised, or crushed, or broken, or cut, ye shall not offer unto the LORD; neither shall ye do [thus] in your land.
003	LEV	022	025	Neither from the hand of a foreigner shall ye offer the bread of your God of any of these; because their corruption is in them, there is a blemish in them: they shall not be accepted for you.
003	LEV	022	026	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	022	027	When a bullock, or a sheep, or a goat, is brought forth, then it shall be seven days under the dam; and from the eighth day and thenceforth it shall be accepted for the oblation of an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	022	028	And whether it be cow or ewe, ye shall not kill it and her young both in one day.
003	LEV	022	029	And when ye sacrifice a sacrifice of thanksgiving unto the LORD, ye shall sacrifice it that ye may be accepted.
003	LEV	022	030	On the same day it shall be eaten; ye shall leave none of it until the morning: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	022	031	Therefore shall ye keep my commandments, and do them: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	022	032	And ye shall not profane my holy name; but I will be hallowed among the children of Israel: I am the LORD which hallow you,
003	LEV	022	033	that brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	023	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	023	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, The set feasts of the LORD, which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my set feasts.
003	LEV	023	003	Six days shall work be done: but on the seventh day is a sabbath of solemn rest, an holy convocation; ye shall do no manner of work: it is a sabbath unto the LORD in all your dwellings.
003	LEV	023	004	These are the set feasts of the LORD, even holy convocations, which ye shall proclaim in their appointed season.
003	LEV	023	005	In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month at even, is the LORD’S passover.
003	LEV	023	006	And on the fifteenth day of the same month is the feast of unleavened bread unto the LORD: seven days ye shall eat unleavened bread.
003	LEV	023	007	In the first day ye shall have an holy convocation: ye shall do no servile work.
003	LEV	023	008	But ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD seven days: in the seventh day is an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work.
003	LEV	023	009	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	023	010	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye be come into the land which I give unto you, and shall reap the harvest thereof, then ye shall bring the sheaf of the firstfruits of your harvest unto the priest:
003	LEV	023	011	and he shall wave the sheaf before the LORD, to be accepted for you: on the morrow after the sabbath the priest shall wave it.
003	LEV	023	012	And in the day when ye wave the sheaf, ye shall offer a he-lamb without blemish of the first year for a burnt offering unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	013	And the meal offering thereof shall be two tenth parts [of an ephah] of fine flour mingled with oil, an offering made by fire unto the LORD for a sweet savour: and the drink offering thereof shall be of wine, the fourth part of an hin.
003	LEV	023	014	And ye shall eat neither bread, nor parched corn, nor fresh ears, until this selfsame day, until ye have brought the oblation of your God: it is a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
003	LEV	023	015	And ye shall count unto you from the morrow after the sabbath, from the day that ye brought the sheaf of the wave offering; seven sabbaths shall there be complete:
003	LEV	023	016	even unto the morrow after the seventh sabbath shall ye number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meal offering unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	017	Ye shall bring out of your habitations two wave loaves of two tenth parts [of an ephah]: they shall be of fine flour, they shall be baken with leaven, for firstfruits unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	018	And ye shall present with the bread seven lambs without blemish of the first year, and one young bullock, and two rams: they shall be a burnt offering unto the LORD, with their meal offering, and their drink offerings, even an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	019	And ye shall offer one he-goat for a sin offering, and two he-lambs of the first year for a sacrifice of peace offerings.
003	LEV	023	020	And the priest shall wave them with the bread of the firstfruits for a wave offering before the LORD, with the two lambs: they shall be holy to the LORD for the priest.
003	LEV	023	021	And ye shall make proclamation on the selfsame day; there shall be an holy convocation unto you: ye shall do no servile work: it is a statute for ever in all your dwellings throughout your generations.
003	LEV	023	022	And when ye reap the harvest of your land, thou shalt not wholly reap the corners of thy field, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning of thy harvest: thou shalt leave them for the poor, and for the stranger: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	023	023	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	023	024	Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, In the seventh month, in the first day of the month, shall be a solemn rest unto you, a memorial of blowing of trumpets, an holy convocation.
003	LEV	023	025	Ye shall do no servile work: and ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	026	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	023	027	Howbeit on the tenth day of this seventh month is the day of atonement: it shall be an holy convocation unto you, and ye shall afflict your souls; and ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	028	And ye shall do no manner of work in that same day: for it is a day of atonement, to make atonement for you before the LORD your God.
003	LEV	023	029	For whatsoever soul it be that shall not be afflicted in that same day, he shall be cut off from his people.
003	LEV	023	030	And whatsoever soul it be that doeth any manner of work in that same day, that soul will I destroy from among his people.
003	LEV	023	031	Ye shall do no manner of work: it is a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
003	LEV	023	032	It shall be unto you a sabbath of solemn rest, and ye shall afflict your souls: in the ninth day of the month at even, from even unto even, shall ye keep your sabbath.
003	LEV	023	033	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	023	034	Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, On the fifteenth day of this seventh month is the feast of tabernacles for seven days unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	035	On the first day shall be an holy convocation: ye shall do no servile work.
003	LEV	023	036	Seven days ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD: on the eighth day shall be an holy convocation unto you; and ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD: it is a solemn assembly; ye shall do no servile work.
003	LEV	023	037	These are the set feasts of the LORD, which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, to offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD, a burnt offering, and a meal offering, a sacrifice, and drink offerings, each on its own day:
003	LEV	023	038	beside the sabbaths of the LORD, and beside your gifts, and beside all your vows, and beside all your freewill offerings, which ye give unto the LORD.
003	LEV	023	039	Howbeit on the fifteenth day of the seventh month, when ye have gathered in the fruits of the land, ye shall keep the feast of the LORD seven days: on the first day shall be a solemn rest, and on the eighth day shall be a solemn rest.
003	LEV	023	040	And ye shall take you on the first day the fruit of goodly trees, branches of palm trees, and boughs of thick trees, and willows of the brook; and ye shall rejoice before the LORD your God seven days.
003	LEV	023	041	And ye shall keep it a feast unto the LORD seven days in the year: it is a statute for ever in your generations: ye shall keep it in the seventh month.
003	LEV	023	042	Ye shall dwell in booths seven days; all that are homeborn in Israel shall dwell in booths:
003	LEV	023	043	that your generations may know that I made the children of Israel to dwell in booths, when I brought them out of the land of Egypt: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	023	044	And Moses declared unto the children of Israel the set feasts of the LORD.
003	LEV	024	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	024	002	Command the children of Israel, that they bring unto thee pure olive oil beaten for the light, to cause a lamp to burn continually.
003	LEV	024	003	Without the veil of the testimony, in the tent of meeting, shall Aaron order it from evening to morning before the LORD continually: it shall be a statute for ever throughout your generations.
003	LEV	024	004	He shall order the lamps upon the pure candlestick before the LORD continually.
003	LEV	024	005	And thou shalt take fine flour, and bake twelve cakes thereof: two tenth parts [of an ephah] shall be in one cake.
003	LEV	024	006	And thou shalt set them in two rows, six on a row, upon the pure table before the LORD.
003	LEV	024	007	And thou shalt put pure frankincense upon each row, that it may be to the bread for a memorial, even an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
003	LEV	024	008	Every sabbath day he shall set it in order before the LORD continually; it is on the behalf of the children of Israel, an everlasting covenant.
003	LEV	024	009	And it shall be for Aaron and his sons; and they shall eat it in a holy place: for it is most holy unto him of the offerings of the LORD made by fire by a perpetual statute.
003	LEV	024	010	And the son of an Israelitish woman, whose father was an Egyptian, went out among the children of Israel: and the son of the Israelitish woman and a man of Israel strove together in the camp;
003	LEV	024	011	and the son of the Israelitish woman blasphemed the Name, and cursed: and they brought him unto Moses. And his mother’s name was Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of the tribe of Dan.
003	LEV	024	012	And they put him in ward, that it might be declared unto them at the mouth of the LORD.
003	LEV	024	013	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
