003	LEV	024	015	And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, Whosoever curseth his God shall bear his sin.
003	LEV	024	016	And he that blasphemeth the name of the LORD, he shall surely be put to death; all the congregation shall certainly stone him: as well the stranger, as the homeborn, when he blasphemeth the name [of the LORD], shall be put to death.
003	LEV	024	017	And he that smiteth any man mortally shall surely be put to death;
003	LEV	024	018	and he that smiteth a beast mortally shall make it good: life for life.
003	LEV	024	019	And if a man cause a blemish in his neighbour; as he hath done, so shall it be done to him;
003	LEV	024	020	breach for breach, eye for eye, tooth for tooth: as he hath caused a blemish in a man, so shall it be rendered unto him.
003	LEV	024	021	And he that killeth a beast shall make it good: and he that killeth a man shall be put to death.
003	LEV	024	022	Ye shall have one manner of law, as well for the stranger, as for the homeborn: for I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	024	023	And Moses spake to the children of Israel, and they brought forth him that had cursed out of the camp, and stoned him with stones. And the children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses.
003	LEV	025	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses in mount Sinai, saying,
003	LEV	025	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye come into the land which I give you, then shall the land keep a sabbath unto the LORD.
003	LEV	025	003	Six years thou shalt sow thy field, and six years thou shalt prune thy vineyard, and gather in the fruits thereof;
003	LEV	025	004	but in the seventh year shall be a sabbath of solemn rest for the land, a sabbath unto the LORD: thou shalt neither sow thy field, nor prune thy vineyard.
003	LEV	025	005	That which groweth of itself of thy harvest thou shalt not reap, and the grapes of thy undressed vine thou shalt not gather: it shall be a year of solemn rest for the land.
003	LEV	025	006	And the sabbath of the land shall be for food for you; for thee, and for thy servant and for thy maid, and for thy hired servant and for thy stranger that sojourn with thee;
003	LEV	025	007	and for thy cattle, and for the beasts that are in thy land, shall all the increase thereof be for food.
003	LEV	025	008	And thou shalt number seven sabbaths of years unto thee, seven times seven years; and there shall be unto thee the days of seven sabbaths of years, even forty and nine years.
003	LEV	025	009	Then shalt thou send abroad the loud trumpet on the tenth day of the seventh month; in the day of atonement shall ye send abroad the trumpet throughout all your land.
003	LEV	025	010	And ye shall hallow the fiftieth year, and proclaim liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof: it shall be a jubile unto you; and ye shall return every man unto his possession, and ye shall return every man unto his family.
003	LEV	025	011	A jubile shall that fiftieth year be unto you: ye shall not sow, neither reap that which groweth of itself in it, nor gather [the grapes] in it of the undressed vines.
003	LEV	025	012	For it is a jubile; it shall be holy unto you: ye shall eat the increase thereof out of the field.
003	LEV	025	013	In this year of jubile ye shall return every man unto his possession.
003	LEV	025	014	And if thou sell aught unto thy neighbour, or buy of thy neighbour’s hand, ye shall not wrong one another:
003	LEV	025	015	according to the number of years after the jubile thou shalt buy of thy neighbour, [and] according unto the number of years of the crops he shall sell unto thee.
003	LEV	025	016	According to the multitude of the years thou shalt increase the price thereof, and according to the fewness of the years thou shalt diminish the price of it; for the number of the crops doth he sell unto thee.
003	LEV	025	017	And ye shall not wrong one another; but thou shalt fear thy God: for I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	025	018	Wherefore ye shall do my statutes, and keep my judgments and do them; and ye shall dwell in the land in safety.
003	LEV	025	019	And the land shall yield her fruit, and ye shall eat your fill, and dwell therein in safety.
003	LEV	025	020	And if ye shall say, What shall we eat the seventh year? behold, we shall not sow, nor gather in our increase:
003	LEV	025	021	then I will command my blessing upon you in the sixth year, and it shall bring forth fruit for the three years.
003	LEV	025	022	And ye shall sow the eighth year, and eat of the fruits, the old store; until the ninth year, until her fruits come in, ye shall eat the old store.
003	LEV	025	023	And the land shall not be sold in perpetuity; for the land is mine: for ye are strangers and sojourners with me.
003	LEV	025	024	And in all the land of your possession ye shall grant a redemption for the land.
003	LEV	025	025	If thy brother be waxen poor, and sell some of his possession, then shall his kinsman that is next unto him come, and shall redeem that which his brother hath sold.
003	LEV	025	026	And if a man have no one to redeem it, and he be waxen rich and find sufficient to redeem it;
003	LEV	025	027	then let him count the years of the sale thereof, and restore the overplus unto the man to whom he sold it; and he shall return unto his possession.
003	LEV	025	028	But if he be not able to get it back for himself, then that which he hath sold shall remain in the hand of him that hath bought it until the year of jubile: and in the jubile it shall go out, and he shall return unto his possession.
003	LEV	025	029	And if a man sell a dwelling house in a walled city, then he may redeem it within a whole year after it is sold; for a full year shall he have the right of redemption.
003	LEV	025	030	And if it be not redeemed within the space of a full year, then the house that is in the walled city shall be made sure in perpetuity to him that bought it, throughout his generations: it shall not go out in the jubile.
003	LEV	025	031	But the houses of the villages which have no wall round about them shall be reckoned with the fields of the country: they may be redeemed, and they shall go out in the jubile.
003	LEV	025	032	Nevertheless the cities of the Levites, the houses of the cities of their possession, may the Levites redeem at any time.
003	LEV	025	033	And if one of the Levites redeem, then the house that was sold, and the city of his possession, shall go out in the jubile: for the houses of the cities of the Levites are their possession among the children of Israel.
003	LEV	025	034	But the field of the suburbs of their cities may not be sold; for it is their perpetual possession.
003	LEV	025	035	And if thy brother be waxen poor, and his hand fail with thee; then thou shalt uphold him: [as] a stranger and a sojourner shall he live with thee.
003	LEV	025	036	Take thou no usury of him or increase; but fear thy God: that thy brother may live with thee.
003	LEV	025	037	Thou shalt not give him thy money upon usury, nor give him thy victuals for increase.
003	LEV	025	038	I am the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, to give you the land of Canaan, to be your God.
003	LEV	025	039	And if thy brother be waxen poor with thee, and sell himself unto thee; thou shalt not make him to serve as a bondservant:
003	LEV	025	040	as an hired servant, and as a sojourner, he shall be with thee; he shall serve with thee unto the year of jubile:
003	LEV	025	041	then shall he go out from thee, he and his children with him, and shall return unto his own family, and unto the possession of his fathers shall he return.
003	LEV	025	042	For they are my servants, which I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: they shall not be sold as bondmen.
003	LEV	025	043	Thou shalt not rule over him with rigour; but shalt fear thy God.
003	LEV	025	044	And as for thy bondmen, and thy bondmaids, which thou shalt have; of the nations that are round about you, of them shall ye buy bondmen and bondmaids.
003	LEV	025	045	Moreover of the children of the strangers that do sojourn among you, of them shall ye buy, and of their families that are with you, which they have begotten in your land: and they shall be your possession.
003	LEV	025	046	And ye shall make them an inheritance for your children after you, to hold for a possession; of them shall ye take your bondmen for ever: but over your brethren the children of Israel ye shall not rule, one over another, with rigour.
003	LEV	025	047	And if a stranger or sojourner with thee be waxen rich, and thy brother be waxen poor beside him, and sell himself unto the stranger [or] sojourner with thee, or to the stock of the stranger’s family:
003	LEV	025	048	after that he is sold he may be redeemed; one of his brethren may redeem him:
003	LEV	025	049	or his uncle, or his uncle’s son, may redeem him, or any that is nigh of kin unto him of his family may redeem him; or if he be waxen rich, he may redeem himself.
003	LEV	025	050	And he shall reckon with him that bought him from the year that he sold himself to him unto the year of jubile: and the price of his sale shall be according unto the number of years; according to the time of an hired servant shall he be with him.
003	LEV	025	051	If there be yet many years, according unto them he shall give back the price of his redemption out of the money that he was bought for.
003	LEV	025	052	And if there remain but few years unto the year of jubile, then he shall reckon with him; according unto his years shall he give back the price of his redemption.
003	LEV	025	053	As a servant hired year by year shall he be with him: he shall not rule with rigour over him in thy sight.
003	LEV	025	054	And if he be not redeemed by these [means], then he shall go out in the year of jubile, he, and his children with him.
003	LEV	025	055	For unto me the children of Israel are servants; they are my servants whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	026	001	Ye shall make you no idols, neither shall ye rear you up a graven image, or a pillar, neither shall ye place any figured stone in your land, to bow down unto it: for I am the LORD your God.
003	LEV	026	002	Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	026	003	If ye walk in my statutes, and keep my commandments, and do them;
003	LEV	026	004	then I will give your rains in their season, and the land shall yield her increase, and the trees of the field shall yield their fruit.
003	LEV	026	005	And your threshing shall reach unto the vintage, and the vintage shall reach unto the sowing time: and ye shall eat your bread to the full, and dwell in your land safely.
003	LEV	026	006	And I will give peace in the land, and ye shall lie down, and none shall make you afraid: and I will cause evil beasts to cease out of the land, neither shall the sword go through your land.
003	LEV	026	007	And ye shall chase your enemies, and they shall fall before you by the sword.
003	LEV	026	008	And five of you shall chase an hundred, and an hundred of you shall chase ten thousand: and your enemies shall fall before you by the sword.
003	LEV	026	009	And I will have respect unto you, and make you fruitful, and multiply you; and will establish my covenant with you.
003	LEV	026	010	And ye shall eat old store long kept, and ye shall bring forth the old because of the new.
003	LEV	026	011	And I will set my tabernacle among you: and my soul shall not abhor you.
003	LEV	026	012	And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and ye shall be my people.
003	LEV	026	013	I am the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, that ye should not be their bondmen; and I have broken the bars of your yoke, and made you go upright.
003	LEV	026	014	But if ye will not hearken unto me, and will not do all these commandments;
003	LEV	026	015	and if ye shall reject my statutes, and if your soul abhor my judgments, so that ye will not do all my commandments, but break my covenant;
003	LEV	026	016	I also will do this unto you; I will appoint terror over you, even consumption and fever, that shall consume the eyes, and make the soul to pine away: and ye shall sow your seed in vain, for your enemies shall eat it.
003	LEV	026	017	And I will set my face against you, and ye shall be smitten before your enemies: they that hate you shall rule over you; and ye shall flee when none pursueth you.
003	LEV	026	018	And if ye will not yet for these things hearken unto me, then I will chastise you seven times more for your sins.
003	LEV	026	019	And I will break the pride of your power; and I will make your heaven as iron, and your earth as brass:
003	LEV	026	020	and your strength shall be spent in vain: for your land shall not yield her increase, neither shall the trees of the land yield their fruit.
003	LEV	026	021	And if ye walk contrary unto me, and will not hearken unto me; I will bring seven times more plagues upon you according to your sins.
003	LEV	026	022	And I will send the beast of the field among you, which shall rob you of your children, and destroy your cattle, and make you few in number; and your ways shall become desolate.
003	LEV	026	023	And if by these things ye will not be reformed unto me, but will walk contrary unto me;
003	LEV	026	024	then will I also walk contrary unto you; and I will smite you, even I, seven times for your sins.
003	LEV	026	025	And I will bring a sword upon you, that shall execute the vengeance of the covenant; and ye shall be gathered together within your cities: and I will send the pestilence among you; and ye shall be delivered into the hand of the enemy.
003	LEV	026	026	When I break your staff of bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver your bread again by weight: and ye shall eat, and not be satisfied.
003	LEV	026	027	And if ye will not for all this hearken unto me, but walk contrary unto me;
003	LEV	026	028	then I will walk contrary unto you in fury; and I also will chastise you seven times for your sins.
003	LEV	026	029	And ye shall eat the flesh of your sons, and the flesh of your daughters shall ye eat.
003	LEV	026	030	And I will destroy your high places, and cut down your sun-images, and cast your carcases upon the carcases of your idols; and my soul shall abhor you.
003	LEV	026	031	And I will make your cities a waste, and will bring your sanctuaries unto desolation, and I will not smell the savour of your sweet odours.
003	LEV	026	032	And I will bring the land into desolation: and your enemies which dwell therein shall be astonished at it.
003	LEV	026	033	And you will I scatter among the nations, and I will draw out the sword after you: and your land shall be a desolation, and your cities shall be a waste.
003	LEV	026	034	Then shall the land enjoy her sabbaths, as long as it lieth desolate, and ye be in your enemies’ land; even then shall the land rest, and enjoy her sabbaths.
003	LEV	026	035	As long as it lieth desolate it shall have rest; even the rest which it had not in your sabbaths, when ye dwelt upon it.
003	LEV	026	036	And as for them that are left of you, I will send a faintness into their heart in the lands of their enemies: and the sound of a driven leaf shall chase them; and they shall flee, as one fleeth from the sword; and they shall fall when none pursueth.
003	LEV	026	037	And they shall stumble one upon another, as it were before the sword, when none pursueth: and ye shall have no power to stand before your enemies.
003	LEV	026	038	And ye shall perish among the nations, and the land of your enemies shall eat you up.
003	LEV	026	039	And they that are left of you shall pine away in their iniquity in your enemies’ lands; and also in the iniquities of their fathers shall they pine away with them.
003	LEV	026	040	And they shall confess their iniquity, and the iniquity of their fathers, in their trespass which they trespassed against me, and also that because they have walked contrary unto me,
003	LEV	026	041	I also walked contrary unto them, and brought them into the land of their enemies: if then their uncircumcised heart be humbled, and they then accept of the punishment of their iniquity;
003	LEV	026	042	then will I remember my covenant with Jacob; and also my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham will I remember; and I will remember the land.
003	LEV	026	043	The land also shall be left of them, and shall enjoy her sabbaths, while she lieth desolate without them; and they shall accept of the punishment of their iniquity: because, even because they rejected my judgments, and their soul abhorred my statutes.
003	LEV	026	044	And yet for all that, when they be in the land of their enemies, I will not reject them, neither will I abhor them, to destroy them utterly, and to break my covenant with them: for I am the LORD their God:
003	LEV	026	045	but I will for their sakes remember the covenant of their ancestors, whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt in the sight of the nations, that I might be their God: I am the LORD.
003	LEV	026	046	These are the statutes and judgments and laws, which the LORD made between him and the children of Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of Moses.
003	LEV	027	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
003	LEV	027	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When a man shall accomplish a vow, the persons shall be for the LORD by thy estimation.
003	LEV	027	003	And thy estimation shall be of the male from twenty years old even unto sixty years old, even thy estimation shall be fifty shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary.
003	LEV	027	004	And if it be a female, then thy estimation shall be thirty shekels.
003	LEV	027	005	And if it be from five years old even unto twenty years old, then thy estimation shall be of the male twenty shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
003	LEV	027	006	And if it be from a month old even unto five years old, then thy estimation shall be of the male five shekels of silver, and for the female thy estimation shall be three shekels of silver.
003	LEV	027	007	And if it be from sixty years old and upward; if it be a male, then thy estimation shall be fifteen shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
003	LEV	027	008	But if he be poorer than thy estimation, then he shall be set before the priest, and the priest shall value him; according to the ability of him that vowed shall the priest value him.
003	LEV	027	009	And if it be a beast, whereof men offer an oblation unto the LORD, all that any man giveth of such unto the LORD shall be holy.
003	LEV	027	010	He shall not alter it, nor change it, a good for a bad, or a bad for a good: and if he shall at all change beast for beast, then both it and that for which it is changed shall be holy.
003	LEV	027	011	And if it be any unclean beast, of which they do not offer an oblation unto the LORD, then he shall set the beast before the priest:
003	LEV	027	012	and the priest shall value it, whether it be good or bad: as thou the priest valuest it, so shall it be.
003	LEV	027	013	But if he will indeed redeem it, then he shall add the fifth part thereof unto thy estimation.
003	LEV	027	014	And when a man shall sanctify his house to be holy unto the LORD, then the priest shall estimate it, whether it be good or bad: as the priest shall estimate it, so shall it stand.
003	LEV	027	015	And if he that sanctified it will redeem his house, then he shall add the fifth part of the money of thy estimation unto it, and it shall be his.
003	LEV	027	016	And if a man shall sanctify unto the LORD part of the field of his possession, then thy estimation shall be according to the sowing thereof: the sowing of a homer of barley [shall be valued] at fifty shekels of silver.
003	LEV	027	017	If he sanctify his field from the year of jubile, according to thy estimation it shall stand.
003	LEV	027	018	But if he sanctify his field after the jubile, then the priest shall reckon unto him the money according to the years that remain unto the year of jubile, and an abatement shall be made from thy estimation.
003	LEV	027	019	And if he that sanctified the field will indeed redeem it, then he shall add the fifth part of the money of thy estimation unto it, and it shall be assured to him.
003	LEV	027	020	And if he will not redeem the field, or if he have sold the field to another man, it shall not be redeemed any more:
003	LEV	027	021	but the field, when it goeth out in the jubile, shall be holy unto the LORD, as a field devoted; the possession thereof shall be the priest’s.
003	LEV	027	022	And if he sanctify unto the LORD a field which he hath bought, which is not of the field of his possession;
003	LEV	027	023	then the priest shall reckon unto him the worth of thy estimation unto the year of jubile: and he shall give thine estimation in that day, as a holy thing unto the LORD.
003	LEV	027	024	In the year of jubile the field shall return unto him of whom it was bought, even to him to whom the possession of the land belongeth.
003	LEV	027	025	And all thy estimations shall be according to the shekel of the sanctuary: twenty gerahs shall be the shekel.
003	LEV	027	026	Only the firstling among beasts, which is made a firstling to the LORD, no man shall sanctify it; whether it be ox or sheep, it is the LORD’S.
003	LEV	027	027	And if it be of an unclean beast, then he shall ransom it according to thine estimation, and shall add unto it the fifth part thereof: or if it be not redeemed, then it shall be sold according to thy estimation.
003	LEV	027	028	Notwithstanding, no devoted thing, that a man shall devote unto the LORD of all that he hath, whether of man or beast, or of the field of his possession, shall be sold or redeemed: every devoted thing is most holy unto the LORD.
003	LEV	027	029	None devoted, which shall be devoted of men, shall be ransomed; he shall surely be put to death.
003	LEV	027	030	And all the tithe of the land, whether of the seed of the land, or of the fruit of the tree, is the LORD’S: it is holy unto the LORD.
003	LEV	027	031	And if a man will redeem aught of his tithe, he shall add unto it the fifth part thereof.
003	LEV	027	032	And all the tithe of the herd or the flock, whatsoever passeth under the rod, the tenth shall be holy unto the LORD.
003	LEV	027	033	He shall not search whether it be good or bad, neither shall he change it: and if he change it at all, then both it and that for which it is changed shall be holy; it shall not be redeemed.
003	LEV	027	034	These are the commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel in mount Sinai.
