# BOOK	004	NUM	Numbers	Numbers
004	NUM	001	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tent of meeting, on the first day of the second month, in the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,
004	NUM	001	002	Take ye the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, every male, by their polls;
004	NUM	001	003	from twenty years old and upward, all that are able to go forth to war in Israel, thou and Aaron shall number them by their hosts.
004	NUM	001	004	And with you there shall be a man of every tribe; every one head of his fathers’ house.
004	NUM	001	005	And these are the names of the men that shall stand with you: of Reuben; Elizur the son of Shedeur.
004	NUM	001	006	Of Simeon; Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.
004	NUM	001	007	Of Judah; Nahshon the son of Amminadab.
004	NUM	001	008	Of Issachar; Nethanel the son of Zuar.
004	NUM	001	009	Of Zebulun; Eliab the son of Helon.
004	NUM	001	010	Of the children of Joseph: of Ephraim; Elishama the son of Ammihud: of Manasseh; Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.
004	NUM	001	011	Of Benjamin; Abidan the son of Gideoni.
004	NUM	001	012	Of Dan; Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.
004	NUM	001	013	Of Asher; Pagiel the son of Ochran.
004	NUM	001	014	Of Gad; Eliasaph the son of Deuel.
004	NUM	001	015	Of Naphtali; Ahira the son of Enan.
004	NUM	001	016	These are they that were called of the congregation, the princes of the tribes of their fathers; they were the heads of the thousands of Israel.
004	NUM	001	017	And Moses and Aaron took these men which are expressed by name:
004	NUM	001	018	And they assembled all the congregation together on the first day of the second month, and they declared their pedigrees after their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, by their polls.
004	NUM	001	019	As the LORD commanded Moses, so he numbered them in the wilderness of Sinai.
004	NUM	001	020	And the children of Reuben, Israel’s firstborn, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, by their polls, every male from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	021	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Reuben, were forty and six thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	001	022	Of the children of Simeon, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, those that were numbered thereof, according to the number of the names, by their polls, every male from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	023	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Simeon, were fifty and nine thousand and three hundred.
004	NUM	001	024	Of the children of Gad, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	025	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Gad, were forty and five thousand six hundred and fifty.
004	NUM	001	026	Of the children of Judah, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	027	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Judah, were threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.
004	NUM	001	028	Of the children of Issachar, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	029	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Issachar, were fifty and four thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	001	030	Of the children of Zebulun, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	031	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Zebulun, were fifty and seven thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	001	032	Of the children of Joseph, [namely], of the children of Ephraim, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	033	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Ephraim, were forty thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	001	034	Of the children of Manasseh, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	035	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Manasseh, were thirty and two thousand and two hundred.
004	NUM	001	036	Of the children of Benjamin, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	037	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Benjamin, were thirty and five thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	001	038	Of the children of Dan, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	039	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Dan, were threescore and two thousand and seven hundred.
004	NUM	001	040	Of the children of Asher, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	041	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Asher, were forty and one thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	001	042	Of the children of Naphtali, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
004	NUM	001	043	those that were numbered of them, of the tribe of Naphtali, were fifty and three thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	001	044	These are they that were numbered, which Moses and Aaron numbered, and the princes of Israel, being twelve men: they were each one for his fathers’ house.
004	NUM	001	045	So all they that were numbered of the children of Israel by their fathers’ houses, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war in Israel;
004	NUM	001	046	even all they that were numbered were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.
004	NUM	001	047	But the Levites after the tribe of their fathers were not numbered among them.
004	NUM	001	048	For the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	001	049	Only the tribe of Levi thou shalt not number, neither shalt thou take the sum of them among the children of Israel:
004	NUM	001	050	but appoint thou the Levites over the tabernacle of the testimony, and over all the furniture thereof, and over all that belongeth to it: they shall bear the tabernacle, and all the furniture thereof; and they shall minister unto it, and shall encamp round about the tabernacle.
004	NUM	001	051	And when the tabernacle setteth forward, the Levites shall take it down: and when the tabernacle is to be pitched, the Levites shall set it up: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
004	NUM	001	052	And the children of Israel shall pitch their tents, every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard, according to their hosts.
004	NUM	001	053	But the Levites shall pitch round about the tabernacle of the testimony, that there be no wrath upon the congregation of the children of Israel: and the Levites shall keep the charge of the tabernacle of the testimony.
004	NUM	001	054	Thus did the children of Israel; according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they.
004	NUM	002	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
004	NUM	002	002	The children of Israel shall pitch every man by his own standard, with the ensigns of their fathers’ houses: over against the tent of meeting shall they pitch round about.
004	NUM	002	003	And those that pitch on the east side toward the sunrising shall be they of the standard of the camp of Judah, according to their hosts: and the prince of the children of Judah shall be Nahshon the son of Amminadab.
004	NUM	002	004	And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.
004	NUM	002	005	And those that pitch next unto him shall be the tribe of Issachar: and the prince of the children of Issachar shall be Nethanel the son of Zuar:
004	NUM	002	006	and his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were fifty and four thousand and four hundred:
004	NUM	002	007	[and] the tribe of Zebulun: and the prince of the children of Zebulun shall be Eliab the son of Helon:
004	NUM	002	008	and his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were fifty and seven thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	002	009	All that were numbered of the camp of Judah were an hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred, according to their hosts. They shall set forth first.
004	NUM	002	010	On the south side shall be the standard of the camp of Reuben according to their hosts: and the prince of the children of Reuben shall be Elizur the son of Shedeur.
004	NUM	002	011	And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were forty and six thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	002	012	And those that pitch next unto him shall be the tribe of Simeon: and the prince of the children of Simeon shall be Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai:
004	NUM	002	013	and his host, and those that were numbered of them, were fifty and nine thousand and three hundred:
004	NUM	002	014	and the tribe of Gad: and the prince of the children of Gad shall be Eliasaph the son of Reuel.
004	NUM	002	015	And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty and five thousand and six hundred and fifty.
004	NUM	002	016	All that were numbered of the camp of Reuben were an hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty, according to their hosts. And they shall set forth second.
004	NUM	002	017	Then the tent of meeting shall set forward, with the camp of the Levites in the midst of the camps: as they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place, by their standards.
004	NUM	002	018	On the west side shall be the standard of the camp of Ephraim according to their hosts: and the prince of the children of Ephraim shall be Elishama the son of Ammihud.
004	NUM	002	019	And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	002	020	And next unto him shall be the tribe of Manasseh: and the prince of the children of Manasseh shall be Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur:
004	NUM	002	021	and his host, and those that were numbered of them, were thirty and two thousand and two hundred:
004	NUM	002	022	and the tribe of Benjamin: and the prince of the children of Benjamin shall be Abidan the son of Gideoni:
004	NUM	002	023	and his host, and those that were numbered of them, were thirty and five thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	002	024	All that were numbered of the camp of Ephraim were an hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred, according to their hosts. And they shall set forth third.
004	NUM	002	025	On the north side shall be the standard of the camp of Dan according to their hosts: and the prince of the children of Dan shall be Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.
004	NUM	002	026	And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were threescore and two thousand and seven hundred.
004	NUM	002	027	And those that pitch next unto him shall be the tribe of Asher: and the prince of the children of Asher shall be Pagiel the son of Ochran:
004	NUM	002	028	and his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty and one thousand and five hundred:
004	NUM	002	029	and the tribe of Naphtali: and the prince of the children of Naphtali shall be Ahira the son of Enan:
004	NUM	002	030	and his host, and those that were numbered of them, were fifty and three thousand and four hundred.
004	NUM	002	031	All that were numbered of the camp of Dan were an hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred. They shall set forth hindmost by their standards.
004	NUM	002	032	These are they that were numbered of the children of Israel by their fathers’ houses: all that were numbered of the camps according to their hosts were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.
004	NUM	002	033	But the Levites were not numbered among the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses.
004	NUM	002	034	Thus did the children of Israel; according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so they pitched by their standards, and so they set forward, every one by their families, according to their fathers’ houses.
004	NUM	003	001	Now these are the generations of Aaron and Moses in the day that the LORD spake with Moses in mount Sinai.
004	NUM	003	002	And these are the names of the sons of Aaron; Nadab the firstborn, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
004	NUM	003	003	These are the names of the sons of Aaron, the priests which were anointed, whom he consecrated to minister in the priest’s office.
004	NUM	003	004	And Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD, when they offered strange fire before the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children: and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest’s office in the presence of Aaron their father.
004	NUM	003	005	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	003	006	Bring the tribe of Levi near, and set them before Aaron the priest, that they may minister unto him.
004	NUM	003	007	And they shall keep his charge, and the charge of the whole congregation before the tent of meeting, to do the service of the tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	008	And they shall keep all the furniture of the tent of meeting, and the charge of the children of Israel, to do the service of the tabernacle.
004	NUM	003	009	And thou shalt give the Levites unto Aaron and to his sons: they are wholly given unto him on the behalf of the children of Israel.
004	NUM	003	010	And thou shalt appoint Aaron and his sons, and they shall keep their priesthood: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
004	NUM	003	011	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	003	012	And I, behold, I have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel instead of all the firstborn that openeth the womb among the children of Israel; and the Levites shall be mine:
004	NUM	003	013	for all the firstborn are mine; on the day that I smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I hallowed unto me all the firstborn in Israel, both man and beast: mine they shall be; I am the LORD.
004	NUM	003	014	And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying,
004	NUM	003	015	Number the children of Levi by their fathers’ houses, by their families: every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them.
004	NUM	003	016	And Moses numbered them according to the word of the LORD, as he was commanded.
004	NUM	003	017	And these were the sons of Levi by their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari.
004	NUM	003	018	And these are the names of the sons of Gershon by their families; Libni and Shimei.
004	NUM	003	019	And the sons of Kohath by their families; Amram, and Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.
004	NUM	003	020	And the sons of Merari by their families; Mahli and Mushi. These are the families of the Levites according to their fathers’ houses.
004	NUM	003	021	Of Gershon was the family of the Libnites, and the family of the Shimeites: these are the families of the Gershonites.
004	NUM	003	022	Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, even those that were numbered of them were seven thousand and five hundred.
004	NUM	003	023	The families of the Gershonites shall pitch behind the tabernacle westward.
004	NUM	003	024	And the prince of the fathers’ house of the Gershonites shall be Eliasaph the son of Lael.
004	NUM	003	025	And the charge of the sons of Gershon in the tent of meeting shall be the tabernacle, and the Tent, the covering thereof, and the screen for the door of the tent of meeting,
004	NUM	003	026	and the hangings of the court, and the screen for the door of the court, which is by the tabernacle, and by the altar round about, and the cords of it for all the service thereof.
004	NUM	003	027	And of Kohath was the family of the Amramites, and the family of the Izharites, and the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites: these are the families of the Kohathites.
004	NUM	003	028	According to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, there were eight thousand and six hundred, keeping the charge of the sanctuary.
004	NUM	003	029	The families of the sons of Kohath shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle southward.
004	NUM	003	030	And the prince of the fathers’ house of the families of the Kohathites shall be Elizaphan the son of Uzziel.
004	NUM	003	031	And their charge shall be the ark, and the table, and the candlestick, and the altars, and the vessels of the sanctuary wherewith they minister, and the screen, and all the service thereof.
004	NUM	003	032	And Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be prince of the princes of the Levites, [and have] the oversight of them that keep the charge of the sanctuary.
004	NUM	003	033	Of Merari was the family of the Mahlites, and the family of the Mushites: these are the families of Merari.
004	NUM	003	034	And those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were six thousand and two hundred.
004	NUM	003	035	And the prince of the fathers’ house of the families of Merari was Zuriel the son of Abihail: they shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle northward.
004	NUM	003	036	And the appointed charge of the sons of Merari shall be the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and the sockets thereof, and all the instruments thereof, and all the service thereof;
004	NUM	003	037	and the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords.
004	NUM	003	038	And those that pitch before the tabernacle eastward, before the tent of meeting toward the sunrising, shall be Moses, and Aaron and his sons, keeping the charge of the sanctuary for the charge of the children of Israel; and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
004	NUM	003	039	All that were numbered of the Levites, which Moses and Aaron numbered at the commandment of the LORD, by their families, all the males from a month old and upward, were twenty and two thousand.
004	NUM	003	040	And the LORD said unto Moses, Number all the firstborn males of the children of Israel from a month old and upward, and take the number of their names.
004	NUM	003	041	And thou shalt take the Levites for me (I am the LORD) instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel; and the cattle of the Levites instead of all the firstlings among the cattle of the children of Israel.
004	NUM	003	042	And Moses numbered, as the LORD commanded him, all the firstborn among the children of Israel.
004	NUM	003	043	And all the firstborn males according to the number of names, from a month old and upward, of those that were numbered of them, were twenty and two thousand two hundred and threescore and thirteen.
004	NUM	003	044	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	003	045	Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle: and the Levites shall be mine; I am the LORD.
004	NUM	003	046	And for the redemption of the two hundred and threescore and thirteen of the firstborn of the children of Israel, which are over and above [the number of] the Levites,
004	NUM	003	047	thou shalt take five shekels apiece by the poll; after the shekel of the sanctuary shalt thou take them (the shekel is twenty gerahs):
004	NUM	003	048	and thou shalt give the money wherewith the odd number of them is redeemed unto Aaron and to his sons.
004	NUM	003	049	And Moses took the redemption-money from them that were over and above them that were redeemed by the Levites:
004	NUM	003	050	from the firstborn of the children of Israel took he the money; a thousand three hundred and threescore and five [shekels], after the shekel of the sanctuary:
004	NUM	003	051	and Moses gave the redemption-money unto Aaron and to his sons, according to the word of the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses.
004	NUM	004	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
004	NUM	004	002	Take the sum of the sons of Kohath from among the sons of Levi, by their families, by their fathers’ houses,
004	NUM	004	003	from thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all that enter upon the service, to do the work in the tent of meeting.
004	NUM	004	004	This is the service of the sons of Kohath in the tent of meeting, [about] the most holy things:
004	NUM	004	005	when the camp setteth forward, Aaron shall go in, and his sons, and they shall take down the veil of the screen, and cover the ark of the testimony with it:
004	NUM	004	006	and shall put thereon a covering of sealskin, and shall spread over it a cloth all of blue, and shall put in the staves thereof.
004	NUM	004	007	And upon the table of shewbread they shall spread a cloth of blue, and put thereon the dishes, and the spoons, and the bowls, and the cups to pour out withal: and the continual bread shall be thereon:
004	NUM	004	008	and they shall spread upon them a cloth of scarlet, and cover the same with a covering of sealskin, and shall put in the staves thereof.
004	NUM	004	009	And they shall take a cloth of blue, and cover the candlestick of the light, and its lamps, and its tongs, and its snuffdishes, and all the oil vessels thereof, wherewith they minister unto it:
004	NUM	004	010	and they shall put it and all the vessels thereof within a covering of sealskin, and shall put it upon the frame.
004	NUM	004	011	And upon the golden altar they shall spread a cloth of blue, and cover it with a covering of sealskin, and shall put in the staves thereof:
004	NUM	004	012	and they shall take all the vessels of ministry, wherewith they minister in the sanctuary, and put them in a cloth of blue, and cover them with a covering of sealskin, and shall put them on the frame.
004	NUM	004	013	And they shall take away the ashes from the altar, and spread a purple cloth thereon:
004	NUM	004	014	and they shall put upon it all the vessels thereof, wherewith they minister about it, the firepans, the fleshhooks, and the shovels, and the basons, all the vessels of the altar; and they shall spread upon it a covering of sealskin, and put in the staves thereof.
004	NUM	004	015	And when Aaron and his sons have made an end of covering the sanctuary, and all the furniture of the sanctuary, as the camp is to set forward; after that, the sons of Kohath shall come to bear it: but they shall not touch the sanctuary, lest they die. These things are the burden of the sons of Kohath in the tent of meeting.
004	NUM	004	016	And the charge of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be the oil for the light, and the sweet incense, and the continual meal offering, and the anointing oil, the charge of all the tabernacle, and of all that therein is, the sanctuary, and the furniture thereof.
004	NUM	004	017	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
004	NUM	004	018	Cut ye not off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites from among the Levites:
004	NUM	004	019	but thus do unto them, that they may live, and not die, when they approach unto the most holy things: Aaron and his sons shall go in, and appoint them every one to his service and to his burden:
004	NUM	004	020	but they shall not go in to see the sanctuary even for a moment, lest they die.
004	NUM	004	021	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	004	022	Take the sum of the sons of Gershon also, by their fathers’ houses, by their families;
004	NUM	004	023	from thirty years old and upward until fifty years old shalt thou number them; all that enter in to wait upon the service, to do the work in the tent of meeting.
004	NUM	004	024	This is the service of the families of the Gershonites, in serving and in bearing burdens:
004	NUM	004	025	they shall bear the curtains of the tabernacle, and the tent of meeting, its covering, and the covering of sealskin that is above upon it, and the screen for the door of the tent of meeting;
004	NUM	004	026	and the hangings of the court, and the screen for the door of the gate of the court, which is by the tabernacle and by the altar round about, and their cords, and all the instruments of their service, and whatsoever shall be done with them, therein shall they serve.
004	NUM	004	027	At the commandment of Aaron and his sons shall be all the service of the sons of the Gershonites, in all their burden, and in all their service: and ye shall appoint unto them in charge all their burden.
004	NUM	004	028	This is the service of the families of the sons of the Gershonites in the tent of meeting: and their charge shall be under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.
004	NUM	004	029	As for the sons of Merari, thou shalt number them by their families, by their fathers’ houses;
004	NUM	004	030	from thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old shalt thou number them, every one that entereth upon the service, to do the work of the tent of meeting.
004	NUM	004	031	And this is the charge of their burden, according to all their service in the tent of meeting; the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and the sockets thereof;
004	NUM	004	032	and the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords, with all their instruments, and with all their service: and by name ye shall appoint the instruments of the charge of their burden.
004	NUM	004	033	This is the service of the families of the sons of Merari, according to all their service, in the tent of meeting, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.
004	NUM	004	034	And Moses and Aaron and the princes of the congregation numbered the sons of the Kohathites by their families, and by their fathers’ houses,
004	NUM	004	035	from thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entered upon the service, for work in the tent of meeting:
004	NUM	004	036	and those that were numbered of them by their families were two thousand seven hundred and fifty.
004	NUM	004	037	These are they that were numbered of the families of the Kohathites, all that did serve in the tent of meeting, whom Moses and Aaron numbered according to the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
004	NUM	004	038	And those that were numbered of the sons of Gershon, by their families, and by their fathers’ houses,
004	NUM	004	039	from thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entered upon the service, for work in the tent of meeting,
004	NUM	004	040	even those that were numbered of them, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, were two thousand and six hundred and thirty.
004	NUM	004	041	These are they that were numbered of the families of the sons of Gershon, all that did serve in the tent of meeting, whom Moses and Aaron numbered according to the commandment of the LORD.
004	NUM	004	042	And those that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, by their families, by their fathers’ houses,
004	NUM	004	043	from thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entered upon the service, for work in the tent of meeting,
004	NUM	004	044	even those that were numbered of them by their families, were three thousand and two hundred.
004	NUM	004	045	These are they that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, whom Moses and Aaron numbered according to the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
004	NUM	004	046	All those that were numbered of the Levites, whom Moses and Aaron and the princes of Israel numbered, by their families, and by their fathers’ houses,
004	NUM	004	047	from thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entered in to do the work of service, and the work of bearing burdens in the tent of meeting,
004	NUM	004	048	even those that were numbered of them, were eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore.
004	NUM	004	049	According to the commandment of the LORD they were numbered by the hand of Moses, every one according to his service, and according to his burden: thus were they numbered of him, as the LORD commanded Moses.
004	NUM	005	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	005	002	Command the children of Israel, that they put out of the camp every leper, and every one that hath an issue, and whosoever is unclean by the dead:
004	NUM	005	003	both male and female shall ye put out, without the camp shall ye put them; that they defile not their camp, in the midst whereof I dwell.
004	NUM	005	004	And the children of Israel did so, and put them out without the camp: as the LORD spake unto Moses, so did the children of Israel.
004	NUM	005	005	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	005	006	Speak unto the children of Israel, When a man or woman shall commit any sin that men commit, to do a trespass against the LORD, and that soul be guilty;
004	NUM	005	007	then they shall confess their sin which they have done: and he shall make restitution for his guilt in full, and add unto it the fifth part thereof, and give it unto him in respect of whom he hath been guilty.
004	NUM	005	008	But if the man have no kinsman to whom restitution may be made for the guilt, the restitution for guilt which is made unto the LORD shall be the priest’s; besides the ram of the atonement, whereby atonement shall be made for him.
004	NUM	005	009	And every heave offering of all the holy things of the children of Israel, which they present unto the priest, shall be his.
004	NUM	005	010	And every man’s hallowed things shall be his: whatsoever any man giveth the priest, it shall be his.
004	NUM	005	011	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	005	012	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man’s wife go aside, and commit a trespass against him,
004	NUM	005	013	and a man lie with her carnally, and it be hid from the eyes of her husband, and be kept close, and she be defiled, and there be no witness against her, neither she be taken in the act;
004	NUM	005	014	and the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be defiled: or if the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be not defiled:
004	NUM	005	015	then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and shall bring her oblation for her, the tenth part of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it is a meal offering of jealousy, a meal offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.
004	NUM	005	016	And the priest shall bring her near, and set her before the LORD:
004	NUM	005	017	and the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and of the dust that is on the floor of the tabernacle the priest shall take, and put it into the water:
004	NUM	005	018	and the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and let the hair of the woman’s head go loose, and put the meal offering of memorial in her hands, which is the meal offering of jealousy: and the priest shall have in his hand the water of bitterness that causeth the curse:
004	NUM	005	019	and the priest shall cause her to swear, and shall say unto the woman, If no man have lain with thee, and if thou hast not gone aside to uncleanness, being under thy husband, be thou free from this water of bitterness that causeth the curse:
004	NUM	005	020	but if thou hast gone aside, being under thy husband, and if thou be defiled, and some man have lain with thee besides thine husband:
004	NUM	005	021	then the priest shall cause the woman to swear with the oath of cursing, and the priest shall say unto the woman, The LORD make thee a curse and an oath among thy people, when the LORD doth make thy thigh to fall away, and thy belly to swell;
004	NUM	005	022	and this water that causeth the curse shall go into thy bowels, and make thy belly to swell, and thy thigh to fall away: and the woman shall say, Amen, Amen.
004	NUM	005	023	And the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot them out into the water of bitterness:
004	NUM	005	024	and he shall make the woman drink the water of bitterness that causeth the curse: and the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her [and become] bitter.
004	NUM	005	025	And the priest shall take the meal offering of jealousy out of the woman’s hand, and shall wave the meal offering before the LORD, and bring it unto the altar:
004	NUM	005	026	and the priest shall take an handful of the meal offering, as the memorial thereof, and burn it upon the altar, and afterward shall make the woman drink the water.
004	NUM	005	027	And when he hath made her drink the water, then it shall come to pass, if she be defiled, and have committed a trespass against her husband, that the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her [and become] bitter, and her belly shall swell, and her thigh shall fall away: and the woman shall be a curse among her people.
004	NUM	005	028	And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed.
004	NUM	005	029	This is the law of jealousy, when a wife, being under her husband, goeth aside, and is defiled;
004	NUM	005	030	or when the spirit of jealousy cometh upon a man, and he be jealous over his wife; then shall he set the woman before the LORD, and the priest shall execute upon her all this law.
004	NUM	005	031	And the man shall be free from iniquity, and that woman shall bear her iniquity.
004	NUM	006	001	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	006	002	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When either man or woman shall make a special vow, the vow of a Nazirite, to separate himself unto the LORD:
004	NUM	006	003	he shall separate himself from wine and strong drink; he shall drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar of strong drink, neither shall he drink any liquor of grapes, nor eat fresh grapes or dried.
004	NUM	006	004	All the days of his separation shall he eat nothing that is made of the grape-vine, from the kernels even to the husk.
004	NUM	006	005	All the days of his vow of separation there shall no razor come upon his head: until the days be fulfilled, in the which he separateth himself unto the LORD, he shall be holy, he shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow long.
004	NUM	006	006	All the days that he separateth himself unto the LORD he shall not come near to a dead body.
004	NUM	006	007	He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die: because his separation unto God is upon his head.
004	NUM	006	008	All the days of his separation he is holy unto the LORD.
004	NUM	006	009	And if any man die very suddenly beside him, and he defile the head of his separation; then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing, on the seventh day shall he shave it.
004	NUM	006	010	And on the eighth day he shall bring two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, to the priest, to the door of the tent of meeting:
004	NUM	006	011	and the priest shall offer one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, and make atonement for him, for that he sinned by reason of the dead, and shall hallow his head that same day.
004	NUM	006	012	And he shall separate unto the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a he-lamb of the first year for a guilt offering: but the former days shall be void, because his separation was defiled.
004	NUM	006	013	And this is the law of the Nazirite, when the days of his separation are fulfilled: he shall be brought unto the door of the tent of meeting:
004	NUM	006	014	and he shall offer his oblation unto the LORD, one he-lamb of the first year without blemish for a burnt offering, and one ewe-lamb of the first year without blemish for a sin offering, and one ram without blemish for peace offerings,
004	NUM	006	015	and a basket of unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and their meal offering, and their drink offerings.
004	NUM	006	016	And the priest shall present them before the LORD, and shall offer his sin offering, and his burnt offering:
004	NUM	006	017	and he shall offer the ram for a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD, with the basket of unleavened bread: the priest shall offer also the meal offering thereof, and the drink offering thereof.
004	NUM	006	018	And the Nazirite shall shave the head of his separation at the door of the tent of meeting, and shall take the hair of the head of his separation, and put it on the fire which is under the sacrifice of peace offerings.
004	NUM	006	019	And the priest shall take the sodden shoulder of the ram, and one unleavened cake out of the basket, and one unleavened wafer, and shall put them upon the hands of the Nazirite, after he hath shaven [the head of] his separation:
004	NUM	006	020	and the priest shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD; this is holy for the priest, together with the wave breast and heave thigh: and after that the Nazirite may drink wine.
004	NUM	006	021	This is the law of the Nazirite who voweth, [and of] his oblation unto the LORD for his separation, beside that which he is able to get: according to his vow which he voweth, so he must do after the law of his separation.
004	NUM	006	022	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	006	023	Speak unto Aaron and unto his sons, saying, On this wise ye shall bless the children of Israel; ye shall say unto them,
004	NUM	006	024	The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:
004	NUM	006	025	The LORD make his face to shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee:
004	NUM	006	026	The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.
004	NUM	006	027	So shall they put my name upon the children of Israel; and I will bless them.
004	NUM	007	001	And it came to pass on the day that Moses had made an end of setting up the tabernacle, and had anointed it and sanctified it, and all the furniture thereof, and the altar and all the vessels thereof, and had anointed them and sanctified them;
004	NUM	007	002	that the princes of Israel, the heads of their fathers’ houses, offered; these were the princes of the tribes, these are they that were over them that were numbered:
004	NUM	007	003	and they brought their oblation before the LORD, six covered wagons, and twelve oxen; a wagon for every two of the princes, and for each one an ox: and they presented them before the tabernacle.
004	NUM	007	004	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
004	NUM	007	005	Take it of them, that they may be to do the service of the tent of meeting; and thou shalt give them unto the Levites, to every man according to his service.
