005	DEU	011	010	For the land, whither thou goest in to possess it, is not as the land of Egypt, from whence ye came out, where thou sowedst thy seed, and wateredst it with thy foot, as a garden of herbs:
005	DEU	011	011	but the land, whither ye go over to possess it, is a land of hills and valleys, [and] drinketh water of the rain of heaven:
005	DEU	011	012	a land which the LORD thy God careth for; the eyes of the LORD thy God are always upon it, from the beginning of the year even unto the end of the year.
005	DEU	011	013	And it shall come to pass, if ye shall hearken diligently unto my commandments which I command you this day, to love the LORD your God, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul,
005	DEU	011	014	that I will give the rain of your land in its season, the former rain and the latter rain, that thou mayest gather in thy corn, and thy wine, and thine oil.
005	DEU	011	015	And I will give grass in thy fields for thy cattle, and thou shalt eat and be full.
005	DEU	011	016	Take heed to yourselves, lest your heart be deceived, and ye turn aside, and serve other gods, and worship them;
005	DEU	011	017	and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, and he shut up the heaven, that there be no rain, and that the land yield not her fruit; and ye perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD giveth you.
