005	DEU	034	006	And he buried him in the valley in the land of Moab over against Beth-peor: but no man knoweth of his sepulchre unto this day.
005	DEU	034	007	And Moses was an hundred and twenty years old when he died: his eye was not dim, nor his natural force abated.
005	DEU	034	008	And the children of Israel wept for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days: so the days of weeping in the mourning for Moses were ended.
005	DEU	034	009	And Joshua the son of Nun was full of the spirit of wisdom; for Moses had laid his hands upon him: and the children of Israel hearkened unto him, and did as the LORD commanded Moses.
005	DEU	034	010	And there hath not arisen a prophet since in Israel like unto Moses, whom the LORD knew face to face;
005	DEU	034	011	in all the signs and the wonders, which the LORD sent him to do in the land of Egypt, to Pharaoh, and to all his servants, and to all his land;
005	DEU	034	012	and in all the mighty hand, and in all the great terror, which Moses wrought in the sight of all Israel.
