010	2SA	013	038	So Absalom fled, and went to Geshur, and was there three years.
010	2SA	013	039	And [the soul of] king David longed to go forth unto Absalom: for he was comforted concerning Amnon, seeing he was dead.
010	2SA	014	001	Now Joab the son of Zeruiah perceived that the king’s heart was toward Absalom.
010	2SA	014	002	And Joab sent to Tekoa, and fetched thence a wise woman, and said unto her, I pray thee, feign thyself to be a mourner, and put on mourning apparel, I pray thee, and anoint not thyself with oil, but be as a woman that had a long time mourned for the dead:
010	2SA	014	003	and go in to the king, and speak on this manner unto him. So Joab put the words in her mouth.
010	2SA	014	004	And when the woman of Tekoa spake to the king, she fell on her face to the ground, and did obeisance, and said, Help, O king.
010	2SA	014	005	And the king said unto her, What aileth thee? And she answered; Of a truth I am a widow woman, and mine husband is dead.
010	2SA	014	006	And thy handmaid had two sons, and they two strove together in the field, and there was none to part them, but the one smote the other, and killed him.
010	2SA	014	007	And, behold, the whole family is risen against thine handmaid, and they said, Deliver him that smote his brother, that we may kill him for the life of his brother whom he slew, and so destroy the heir also: thus shall they quench my coal which is left, and shall leave to my husband neither name nor remainder upon the face of the earth.
010	2SA	014	008	And the king said unto the woman, Go to thine house, and I will give charge concerning thee.
010	2SA	014	009	And the woman of Tekoa said unto the king, My lord, O king, the iniquity be on me, and on my father’s house: and the king and his throne be guiltless.
010	2SA	014	010	And the king said, Whosoever saith aught unto thee, bring him to me, and he shall not touch thee any more.
010	2SA	014	011	Then said she, I pray thee, let the king remember the LORD thy God, that the avenger of blood destroy not any more, lest they destroy my son. And he said, As the LORD liveth, there shalt not one hair of thy son fall to the earth.
010	2SA	014	012	Then the woman said, Let thine handmaid, I pray thee, speak a word unto my lord the king. And he said, Say on.
010	2SA	014	013	And the woman said, Wherefore then hast thou devised such a thing against the people of God? for in speaking this word the king is as one which is guilty, in that the king doth not fetch home again his banished one.
010	2SA	014	014	For we must needs die, and are as water spilt on the ground, which cannot be gathered up again; neither doth God take away life, but deviseth means, that he that is banished be not an outcast from him.
010	2SA	014	015	Now therefore seeing that I am come to speak this word unto my lord the king, it is because the people have made me afraid: and thy handmaid said, I will now speak unto the king; it may be that the king will perform the request of his servant.
010	2SA	014	016	For the king will hear to deliver his servant out of the hand of the man that would destroy me and my son together out of the inheritance of God.
010	2SA	014	017	Then thine handmaid said, Let, I pray thee, the word of my lord the king be comfortable: for as an angel of God, so is my lord the king to discern good and bad: and the LORD thy God be with thee.
010	2SA	014	018	Then the king answered and said unto the woman, Hide not from me, I pray thee, aught that I shall ask thee. And the woman said, Let my lord the king now speak.
