010	2SA	019	009	And all the people were at strife throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, The king delivered us out of the hand of our enemies, and he saved us out of the hand of the Philistines; and now he is fled out of the land from Absalom.
010	2SA	019	010	And Absalom, whom we anointed over us, is dead in battle. Now therefore why speak ye not a word of bringing the king back?
010	2SA	019	011	And king David sent to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, saying, Speak unto the elders of Judah, saying, Why are ye the last to bring the king back to his house? seeing the speech of all Israel is come to the king, [to bring him] to his house.
010	2SA	019	012	Ye are my brethren, ye are my bone and my flesh: wherefore then are ye the last to bring back the king?
010	2SA	019	013	And say ye to Amasa, Art thou not my bone and my flesh? God do so to me, and more also, if thou be not captain of the host before me continually in the room of Joab.
010	2SA	019	014	And he bowed the heart of all the men of Judah, even as [the heart of] one man; so that they sent unto the king, [saying], Return thou, and all thy servants.
010	2SA	019	015	So the king returned, and came to Jordan. And Judah came to Gilgal, to go to meet the king, to bring the king over Jordan.
010	2SA	019	016	And Shimei the son of Gera, the Benjamite, which was of Bahurim, hasted and came down with the men of Judah to meet king David.
010	2SA	019	017	And there were a thousand men of Benjamin with him, and Ziba the servant of the house of Saul, and his fifteen sons and his twenty servants with him; and they went through Jordan in the presence of the king.
010	2SA	019	018	And there went over a ferry boat to bring over the king’s household, and to do what he thought good. And Shimei the son of Gera fell down before the king, when he was come over Jordan.
010	2SA	019	019	And he said unto the king, Let not my lord impute iniquity unto me, neither do thou remember that which thy servant did perversely the day that my lord the king went out of Jerusalem, that the king should take it to his heart.
010	2SA	019	020	For thy servant doth know that I have sinned: therefore, behold, I am come this day the first of all the house of Joseph to go down to meet my lord the king.
010	2SA	019	021	But Abishai the son of Zeruiah answered and said, Shall not Shimei be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD’S anointed?
010	2SA	019	022	And David said, What have I to do with you, ye sons of Zeruiah, that ye should this day be adversaries unto me? shall there any man be put to death this day in Israel? for do not I know that I am this day king over Israel?
010	2SA	019	023	And the king said unto Shimei, Thou shalt not die. And the king sware unto him.
010	2SA	019	024	And Mephibosheth the son of Saul came down to meet the king; and he had neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes, from the day the king departed until the day he came home in peace.
010	2SA	019	025	And it came to pass, when he was come to Jerusalem to meet the king, that the king said unto him, Wherefore wentest not thou with me, Mephibosheth?
010	2SA	019	026	And he answered, My lord, O king, my servant deceived me: for thy servant said, I will saddle me an ass, that I may ride thereon, and go with the king; because thy servant is lame.
010	2SA	019	027	And he hath slandered thy servant unto my lord the king; but my lord the king is as an angel of God: do therefore what is good in thine eyes.
010	2SA	019	028	For all my father’s house were but dead men before my lord the king: yet didst thou set thy servant among them that did eat at thine own table. What right therefore have I yet that I should cry any more unto the king?
010	2SA	019	029	And the king said unto him, Why speakest thou any more of thy matters? I say, Thou and Ziba divide the land.
010	2SA	019	030	And Mephibosheth said unto the king, Yea, let him take all, forasmuch as my lord the king is come in peace unto his own house:
010	2SA	019	031	And Barzillai the Gileadite came down from Rogelim; and he went over Jordan with the king, to conduct him over Jordan.
010	2SA	019	032	Now Barzillai was a very aged man, even fourscore years old: and he had provided the king with sustenance while he lay at Mahanaim; for he was a very great man.
010	2SA	019	033	And the king said unto Barzillai, Come thou over with me, and I will sustain thee with me in Jerusalem.
010	2SA	019	034	And Barzillai said unto the king, How many are the days of the years of my life, that I should go up with the king unto Jerusalem?
010	2SA	019	035	I am this day fourscore years old: can I discern between good and bad? can thy servant taste what I eat or what I drink? can I hear any more the voice of singing men and singing women? wherefore then should thy servant be yet a burden unto my lord the king?
010	2SA	019	036	Thy servant would but just go over Jordan with the king: and why should the king recompense it me with such a reward?
010	2SA	019	037	Let thy servant, I pray thee, turn back again, that I may die in mine own city, by the grave of my father and my mother. But behold, thy servant Chimham; let him go over with my lord the king; and do to him what shall seem good unto thee.
010	2SA	019	038	And the king answered, Chimham shall go over with me, and I will do to him that which shall seem good unto thee: and whatsoever thou shalt require of me, that will I do for thee.
010	2SA	019	039	And all the people went over Jordan, and the king went over: and the king kissed Barzillai, and blessed him; and he returned unto his own place.
010	2SA	019	040	So the king went over to Gilgal, and Chimham went over with him: and all the people of Judah brought the king over, and also half the people of Israel.
010	2SA	019	041	And, behold, all the men of Israel came to the king; and said unto the king, Why have our brethren the men of Judah stolen thee away, and brought the king, and his household, over Jordan, and all David’s men with him?
010	2SA	019	042	And all the men of Judah answered the men of Israel, Because the king is near of kin to us: wherefore then be ye angry for this matter? have we eaten at all of the king’s cost? or hath he given us any gift?
010	2SA	019	043	And the men of Israel answered the men of Judah, and said, We have ten parts in the king; and we have also more [right] in David than ye: why then did ye despise us, that our advice should not be first had in bringing back our king? And the words of the men of Judah were fiercer than the words of the men of Israel.
010	2SA	020	001	And there happened to be there a man of Belial, whose name was Sheba, the son of Bichri, a Benjamite: and he blew the trumpet, and said, We have no portion in David, neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to his tents, O Israel.
010	2SA	020	002	So all the men of Israel went up from following David, and followed Sheba the son of Bichri: but the men of Judah clave unto their king, from Jordan even to Jerusalem.
010	2SA	020	003	And David came to his house at Jerusalem; and the king took the ten women his concubines, whom he had left to keep the house, and put them in ward, and provided them with sustenance, but went not in unto them. So they were shut up unto the day of their death, living in widowhood.
010	2SA	020	004	Then said the king to Amasa, Call me the men of Judah together within three days, and be thou here present.
010	2SA	020	005	So Amasa went to call [the men of] Judah together: but he tarried longer than the set time which he had appointed him.
010	2SA	020	006	And David said to Abishai, Now shall Sheba the son of Bichri do us more harm than did Absalom: take thou thy lord’s servants, and pursue after him, lest he get him fenced cities, and escape out of our sight.
010	2SA	020	007	And there went out after him Joab’s men, and the Cherethites and the Pelethites, and all the mighty men: and they went out of Jerusalem, to pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.
010	2SA	020	008	When they were at the great stone which is in Gibeon, Amasa came to meet them. And Joab was girded with his apparel of war that he had put on, and thereon was a girdle with a sword fastened upon his loins in the sheath thereof; and as he went forth it fell out.
010	2SA	020	009	And Joab said to Amasa, Is it well with thee, my brother? And Joab took Amasa by the beard with his right hand to kiss him.
010	2SA	020	010	But Amasa took no heed to the sword that was in Joab’s hand: so he smote him therewith in the belly, and shed out his bowels to the ground, and struck him not again; and he died. And Joab and Abishai his brother pursued after Sheba the son of Bichri.
010	2SA	020	011	And there stood by him one of Joab’s young men, and said, He that favoureth Joab, and he that is for David, let him follow Joab.
010	2SA	020	012	And Amasa lay wallowing in his blood in the midst of the highway. And when the man saw that all the people stood still, he carried Amasa out of the highway into the field, and cast a garment over him, when he saw that every one that came by him stood still.
010	2SA	020	013	When he was removed out of the highway, all the people went on after Joab, to pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.
010	2SA	020	014	And he went through all the tribes of Israel unto Abel, and to Beth-maacah, and all the Berites: and they were gathered together, and went also after him.
010	2SA	020	015	And they came and besieged him in Abel of Beth-maacah, and they cast up a mount against the city, and it stood against the rampart: and all the people that were with Joab battered the wall, to throw it down.
010	2SA	020	016	Then cried a wise woman out of the city, Hear, hear; say, I pray you, unto Joab, Come near hither, that I may speak with thee.
010	2SA	020	017	And he came near unto her, and the woman said, Art thou Joab? And he answered, I am. Then she said unto him, Hear the words of thine handmaid. And he answered, I do hear.
010	2SA	020	018	Then she spake, saying, they were wont to speak in old time, saying, They shall surely ask [counsel] at Abel: and so they ended [the matter].
010	2SA	020	019	I am of them that are peaceable and faithful in Israel: thou seekest to destroy a city and a mother in Israel: why wilt thou swallow up the inheritance of the LORD?
010	2SA	020	020	And Joab answered and said, Far be it, far be it from me, that I should swallow up or destroy.
010	2SA	020	021	The matter is not so: but a man of the hill country of Ephraim, Sheba the son of Bichri by name, hath lifted up his hand against the king, even against David: deliver him only, and I will depart from the city. And the woman said unto Joab, Behold, his head shall be thrown to thee over the wall.
010	2SA	020	022	Then the woman went unto all the people in her wisdom. And they cut off the head of Sheba the son of Bichri, and threw it out to Joab. And he blew the trumpet, and they were dispersed from the city, every man to his tent. And Joab returned to Jerusalem unto the king.
010	2SA	020	023	Now Joab was over all the host of Israel: and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and over the Pelethites:
010	2SA	020	024	and Adoram was over the tribute: and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was the recorder:
010	2SA	020	025	and Sheva was scribe: and Zadok and Abiathar were priests:
010	2SA	020	026	and Ira also the Jairite was priest unto David.
010	2SA	021	001	And there was a famine in the days of David three years, year after year; and David sought the face of the LORD. And the LORD said, It is for Saul, and for his bloody house, because he put to death the Gibeonites.
010	2SA	021	002	And the king called the Gibeonites, and said unto them; (now the Gibeonites were not of the children of Israel, but of the remnant of the Amorites; and the children of Israel had sworn unto them: and Saul sought to slay them in his zeal for the children of Israel and Judah:)
010	2SA	021	003	and David said unto the Gibeonites, What shall I do for you? and wherewith shall I make atonement, that ye may bless the inheritance of the LORD?
010	2SA	021	004	And the Gibeonites said unto him, It is no matter of silver or gold between us and Saul, or his house; neither is it for us to put any man to death in Israel. And he said, What ye shall say, that will I do for you.
010	2SA	021	005	And they said unto the king, The man that consumed us, and that devised against us, [that] we should be destroyed from remaining in any of the borders of Israel,
010	2SA	021	006	let seven men of his sons be delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD in Gibeah of Saul, the chosen of the LORD; And the king said, I will give them.
010	2SA	021	007	But the king spared Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the LORD’S oath that was between them, between David and Jonathan the son of Saul.
010	2SA	021	008	But the king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bare unto Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Michal the daughter of Saul, whom she bare to Adriel the son of Barzillai the Meholathite:
010	2SA	021	009	And he delivered them into the hands of the Gibeonites, and they hanged them in the mountain before the LORD, and they fell [all] seven together: and they were put to death in the days of harvest, in the first days, at the beginning of barley harvest.
010	2SA	021	010	And Rizpah the daughter of Aiah took sackcloth, and spread it for her upon the rock, from the beginning of harvest until water was poured upon them from heaven; and she suffered neither the birds of the air to rest on them by day, nor the beasts of the field by night.
010	2SA	021	011	And it was told David what Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, the concubine of Saul, had done.
010	2SA	021	012	And David went and took the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of Jabesh-gilead, which had stolen them from the street of Beth-shan, where the Philistines had hanged them, in the day that the Philistines slew Saul in Gilboa:
010	2SA	021	013	and he brought up from thence the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son; and they gathered the bones of them that were hanged.
010	2SA	021	014	And they buried the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son in the country of Benjamin in Zela, in the sepulchre of Kish his father: and they performed all that the king commanded. And after that God was entreated for the land.
010	2SA	021	015	And the Philistines had war again with Israel; and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines: and David waxed faint.
010	2SA	021	016	and Ishbi-benob, which was of the sons of the giant, the weight of whose spear was three hundred [shekels] of brass in weight, he being girded with a new [sword], thought to have slain David.
010	2SA	021	017	But Abishai the son of Zeruiah succoured him, and smote the Philistine, and killed him. Then the men of David sware unto him, saying, Thou shalt go no more out with us to battle, that thou quench not the lamp of Israel.
010	2SA	021	018	And it came to pass after this, that there was again war with the Philistines at Gob: then Sibbecai the Hushathite slew Saph, which was of the sons of the giant.
010	2SA	021	019	And there was again war with the Philistines at Gob; and Elhanan the son of Jaare-oregim the Beth-lehemite slew Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.
010	2SA	021	020	And there was again war at Gath, where was a man of great stature, that had on every hand six fingers, and on every foot six toes, four and twenty in number; and he also was born to the giant.
010	2SA	021	021	And when he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimei David’s brother slew him.
010	2SA	021	022	These four were born to the giant in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David, and by the hand of his servants.
010	2SA	022	001	And David spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day that the LORD delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul:
010	2SA	022	002	and he said, The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer, even mine;
010	2SA	022	003	The God of my rock, in him will I trust; my shield and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge; my saviour, thou savest me from violence.
010	2SA	022	004	I will call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.
010	2SA	022	005	For the waves of death compassed me, the floods of ungodliness made me afraid.
010	2SA	022	006	The cords of Sheol were round about me: the snares of death came upon me.
010	2SA	022	007	In my distress I called upon the LORD, yea, I called unto my God: and he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry [came] into his ears.
010	2SA	022	008	Then the earth shook and trembled, the foundations of heaven moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.
010	2SA	022	009	There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.
010	2SA	022	010	He bowed the heavens also, and came down; and thick darkness was under his feet.
010	2SA	022	011	And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he was seen upon the wings of the wind.
010	2SA	022	012	And he made darkness pavilions round about him, gathering of waters, thick clouds of the skies.
010	2SA	022	013	At the brightness before him coals of fire were kindled.
010	2SA	022	014	The LORD thundered from heaven, and the Most High uttered his voice.
010	2SA	022	015	And he sent out arrows, and scattered them; lightning, and discomfited them.
010	2SA	022	016	Then the channels of the sea appeared, the foundations of the world were laid bare, by the rebuke of the LORD, at the blast of the breath of his nostrils.
010	2SA	022	017	He sent from on high, he took me; he drew me out of many waters;
010	2SA	022	018	He delivered me from my strong enemy, from them that hated me; for they were too mighty for me.
010	2SA	022	019	They came upon me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.
010	2SA	022	020	He brought me forth also into a large place: he delivered me, because he delighted in me.
010	2SA	022	021	The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness: according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.
010	2SA	022	022	For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
010	2SA	022	023	For all his judgments were before me: and as for his statutes, I did not depart from them.
010	2SA	022	024	I was also perfect toward him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.
010	2SA	022	025	Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness; according to my cleanness in his eyesight.
010	2SA	022	026	With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful, with the perfect man thou wilt shew thyself perfect;
010	2SA	022	027	With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the perverse thou wilt shew thyself froward.
010	2SA	022	028	And the afflicted people thou wilt save: but thine eyes are upon the haughty, that thou mayest bring them down.
010	2SA	022	029	For thou art my lamp, O LORD: and the LORD will lighten my darkness.
010	2SA	022	030	For by thee I run upon a troop: by my God do I leap over a wall.
010	2SA	022	031	As for God, his way is perfect: the word of the LORD is tried; he is a shield unto all them that trust in him.
010	2SA	022	032	For who is God, save the LORD? and who is a rock, save our God?
010	2SA	022	033	God is my strong fortress: and he guideth the perfect in his way.
010	2SA	022	034	He maketh his feet like hinds’ [feet]: and setteth me upon my high places.
010	2SA	022	035	He teacheth my hands to war; so that mine arms do bend a bow of brass.
010	2SA	022	036	Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy gentleness hath made me great.
010	2SA	022	037	Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, and my feet have not slipped.
010	2SA	022	038	I have pursued mine enemies, and destroyed them; neither did I turn again till they were consumed.
010	2SA	022	039	And I have consumed them, and smitten them through, that they cannot arise; yea, they are fallen under my feet.
010	2SA	022	040	For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.
010	2SA	022	041	Thou hast also made mine enemies turn their backs unto me, that I might cut off them that hate me.
010	2SA	022	042	They looked, but there was none to save; even unto the LORD, but he answered them not.
010	2SA	022	043	Then did I beat them small as the dust of the earth, I did stamp them as the mire of the streets, and did spread them abroad.
010	2SA	022	044	Thou also hast delivered me from the strivings of my people; thou hast kept me to be the head of the nations: a people whom I have not known shall serve me.
010	2SA	022	045	The strangers shall submit themselves unto me: as soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me.
010	2SA	022	046	The strangers shall fade away, and shall come trembling out of their close places.
010	2SA	022	047	The LORD liveth; and blessed be my rock; and exalted be the God of the rock of my salvation:
010	2SA	022	048	Even the God that executeth vengeance for me, and bringeth down peoples under me,
010	2SA	022	049	And that bringeth me forth from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above them that rise up against me: thou deliverest me from the violent man.
010	2SA	022	050	Therefore I will give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the nations, and will sing praises unto thy name.
010	2SA	022	051	Great deliverance giveth he to his king: and sheweth lovingkindness to his anointed, to David and to his seed, for evermore.
010	2SA	023	001	Now these be the last words of David. David the son of Jesse saith, and the man who was raised on high saith, the anointed of the God of Jacob, and the sweet psalmist of Israel:
010	2SA	023	002	The spirit of the LORD spake by me, and his word was upon my tongue.
010	2SA	023	003	The God of Israel said, the Rock of Israel spake to me: One that ruleth over men righteously, that ruleth in the fear of God,
010	2SA	023	004	[He shall be] as the light of the morning, when the sun riseth, a morning without clouds; [when] the tender grass [springeth] out of the earth, through clear shining after rain.
010	2SA	023	005	Verily my house is not so with God; yet he hath made with me an everlasting covenant, ordered in all things, and sure: for it is all my salvation, and all [my] desire, although he maketh it not to grow.
010	2SA	023	006	But the ungodly shall be all of them as thorns to be thrust away, for they cannot be taken with the hand:
010	2SA	023	007	But the man that toucheth them must be armed with iron and the staff of a spear; and they shall be utterly burned with fire in [their] place.
010	2SA	023	008	These be the names of the mighty men whom David had: Josheb-basshebeth a Tahchemonite, chief of the captains; the same was Adino the Eznite, against eight hundred slain at one time.
010	2SA	023	009	And after him was Eleazar the son of Dodai the son of an Ahohite, one of the three mighty men with David, when they defied the Philistines that were there gathered together to battle, and the men of Israel were gone away:
010	2SA	023	010	He arose, and smote the Philistines until his hand was weary, and his hand clave unto the sword: and the LORD wrought a great victory that day; and the people returned after him only to spoil.
010	2SA	023	011	And after him was Shammah the son of Agce a Hararite. And the Philistines were gathered together into a troop, where was a plot of ground full of lentils; and the people fled from the Philistines.
010	2SA	023	012	But he stood in the midst of the plot, and defended it, and slew the Philistines: and the LORD wrought a great victory.
010	2SA	023	013	And three of the thirty chief went down, and came to David in the harvest time unto the cave of Adullam; and the troop of the Philistines were encamped in the valley of Rephaim.
010	2SA	023	014	And David was then in the hold, and the garrison of the Philistines was then in Beth-lehem.
010	2SA	023	015	And David longed and said, Oh that one would give me water to drink of the well of Beth-lehem which is by the gate!
010	2SA	023	016	And the three mighty men brake through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Beth-lehem, that was by the gate, and took it, and brought it to David: but he would not drink thereof, but poured it out unto the LORD.
010	2SA	023	017	And he said, Be it far from me, O LORD, that I should do this: [shall I drink] the blood of the men that went in jeopardy of their lives? therefore he would not drink it. These things did the three mighty men.
010	2SA	023	018	And Abishai, the brother of Joab, the son of Zeruiah, was chief of the three. And he lifted up his spear against three hundred and slew them, and had a name among the three.
010	2SA	023	019	Was he not most honourable of the three? therefore he was made their captain: howbeit he attained not unto the [first] three.
010	2SA	023	020	And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done mighty deeds, he slew the two [sons of] Ariel of Moab: he went down also and slew a lion in the midst of a pit in time of snow:
010	2SA	023	021	And he slew an Egyptian, a goodly man: and the Egyptian had a spear in his hand; but he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian’s hand, and slew him with his own spear.
010	2SA	023	022	These things did Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and had a name among the three mighty men.
010	2SA	023	023	He was more honourable than the thirty, but he attained not to the [first] three. And David set him over his guard.
010	2SA	023	024	Asahel the brother of Joab was one of the thirty; Elhanan the son of Dodo of Beth-lehem;
010	2SA	023	025	Shammah the Harodite, Elika the Harodite;
010	2SA	023	026	Helez the Paltite, Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite;
010	2SA	023	027	Abiezer the Anathothite, Mebunnai the Hushathite;
010	2SA	023	028	Zalmon the Ahohite, Maharai the Netophathite;
010	2SA	023	029	Heleb the son of Baanah the Netophathite, Ittai the son of Ribai of Gibeah of the children of Benjamin;
010	2SA	023	030	Benaiah a Pirathonite, Hiddai of the brooks of Gaash;
010	2SA	023	031	Abi-albon the Arbathite, Azmaveth the Barhumite;
010	2SA	023	032	Eliahba the Shaalbonite, the sons of Jashen, Jonathan;
010	2SA	023	033	Shammah the Hararite, Ahiam the son of Sharar the Ararite;
010	2SA	023	034	Eliphelet the son of Ahasbai, the son of the Maacathite, Eliam the son of Ahithophel the Gilonite;
010	2SA	023	035	Hezro the Carmelite, Paarai the Arbite;
010	2SA	023	036	Igal the son of Nathan of Zobah, Bani the Gadite;
010	2SA	023	037	Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Beerothite, armourbearers to Joab the son of Zeruiah;
010	2SA	023	038	Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite;
010	2SA	023	039	Uriah the Hittite: thirty and seven in all.
010	2SA	024	001	And again the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he moved David against them, saying, Go, number Israel and Judah.
010	2SA	024	002	And the king said to Joab the captain of the host, which was with him, Go now to and fro through all the tribes of Israel, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, and number ye the people, that I may know the sum of the people.
010	2SA	024	003	And Joab said unto the king, Now the LORD thy God add unto the people, how many soever they be, an hundredfold, and may the eyes of my lord the king see it: but why doth my lord the king delight in this thing?
010	2SA	024	004	Notwithstanding the king’s word prevailed against Joab, and against the captains of the host. And Joab and the captains of the host went out from the presence of the king, to number the people of Israel.
010	2SA	024	005	And they passed over Jordan, and pitched in Aroer, on the right side of the city that is in the middle of the valley of Gad, and unto Jazer.
010	2SA	024	006	then they came to Gilead, and to the land of Tahtim-hodshi; and they came to Dan-jaan, and round about to Zidon,
010	2SA	024	007	and came to the strong hold of Tyre, and to all the cities of the Hivites, and of the Canaanites: and they went out to the south of Judah, at Beer-sheba.
010	2SA	024	008	So when they had gone to and fro through all the land, they came to Jerusalem at the end of nine months and twenty days.
010	2SA	024	009	And Joab gave up the sum of the numbering of the people unto the king: and there were in Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword; and the men of Judah were five hundred thousand men.
010	2SA	024	010	And David’s heart smote him after that he had numbered the people. And David said unto the LORD, I have sinned greatly in that I have done: but now, O LORD, put away, I beseech thee, the iniquity of thy servant; for I have done very foolishly.
010	2SA	024	011	And when David rose up in the morning, the word of the LORD came unto the prophet Gad, David’s seer, saying,
010	2SA	024	012	Go and speak unto David, Thus saith the LORD, I offer thee three things; choose thee one of them, that I may do it unto thee.
010	2SA	024	013	So Gad came to David, and told him, and said unto him, Shall seven years of famine come unto thee in thy land? or wilt thou flee three months before thy foes while they pursue thee? or shall there be three days pestilence in thy land? now advise thee, and consider what answer I shall return to him that sent me.
010	2SA	024	014	And David said unto Gad, I am in a great strait: let us fall now into the hand of the LORD; for his mercies are great: and let me not fall into the hand of man.
010	2SA	024	015	So the LORD sent a pestilence upon Israel from the morning even to the time appointed: and there died of the people from Dan even to Beer-sheba seventy thousand men.
010	2SA	024	016	And when the angel stretched out his hand toward Jerusalem to destroy it, the LORD repented him of the evil, and said to the angel that destroyed the people, It is enough; now stay thine hand. And the angel of the LORD was by the threshing-floor of Araunah the Jebusite.
010	2SA	024	017	And David spake unto the LORD when he saw the angel that smote the people, and said, Lo, I have sinned, and I have done perversely: but these sheep, what have they done? let thine hand, I pray thee, be against me, and against my father’s house.
010	2SA	024	018	And Gad came that day to David, and said unto him, Go up, rear an altar unto the LORD in the threshing-floor of Araunah the Jebusite.
010	2SA	024	019	And David went up according to the saying of Gad, as the LORD commanded.
010	2SA	024	020	And Araunah looked forth, and saw the king and his servants coming on toward him: and Araunah went out, and bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.
010	2SA	024	021	And Araunah said, Wherefore is my lord the king come to his servant? And David said, To buy the threshing-floor of thee, to build an altar unto the LORD, that the plague may be stayed from the people.
010	2SA	024	022	And Araunah said unto David, Let my lord the king take and offer up what seemeth good unto him: behold, the oxen for the burnt offering, and the threshing instruments and the furniture of the oxen for the wood:
010	2SA	024	023	all this, O king, doth Araunah give unto the king. And Araunah said unto the king, The LORD thy God accept thee.
010	2SA	024	024	And the king said unto Araunah, Nay; but I will verily buy it of thee at a price: neither will I offer burnt offerings unto the LORD my God which cost me nothing. So David bought the threshing-floor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver.
010	2SA	024	025	And David built there an altar unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the LORD was entreated for the land, and the plague was stayed from Israel.
