011	1KI	018	021	And Elijah came near unto all the people, and said, How long halt ye between two opinions? if the LORD be God, follow him: but if Baal, then follow him. And the people answered him not a word.
011	1KI	018	022	Then said Elijah unto the people, I, even I only, am left a prophet of the LORD; but Baal’s prophets are four hundred and fifty men.
011	1KI	018	023	Let them therefore give us two bullocks; and let them choose one bullock for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under: and I will dress the other bullock, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under.
011	1KI	018	024	And call ye on the name of your god, and I will call on the name of the LORD: and the God that answereth by fire, let him be God. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.
011	1KI	018	025	And Elijah said unto the prophets of Baal, Choose you one bullock for yourselves, and dress it first; for ye are many; and call on the name of your god, but put no fire under.
011	1KI	018	026	And they took the bullock which was given them, and they dressed it, and called on the name of Baal from morning even until noon, saying, O Baal, hear us. But there was no voice, nor any that answered. And they leaped about the altar which was made.
011	1KI	018	027	And it came to pass at noon, that Elijah mocked them, and said, Cry aloud: for he is a god; either he is musing, or he is gone aside, or he is in a journey, or peradventure he sleepeth, and must be awaked.
011	1KI	018	028	And they cried aloud, and cut themselves after their manner with knives and lances, till the blood gushed out upon them.
011	1KI	018	029	And it was so, when midday was past, that they prophesied until the time of the offering of the [evening] oblation; but there was neither voice, nor any to answer, nor any that regarded.
011	1KI	018	030	And Elijah said unto all the people, Come near unto me; and all the people came near unto him. And he repaired the altar of the LORD that was thrown down.
011	1KI	018	031	And Elijah took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob, unto whom the word of the LORD came, saying, Israel shall be thy name.
011	1KI	018	032	And with the stones he built an altar in the name of the LORD; and he made a trench about the altar, as great as would contain two measures of seed.
011	1KI	018	033	And he put the wood in order, and cut the bullock in pieces, and laid it on the wood. And he said, Fill four barrels with water, and pour it on the burnt offering, and on the wood.
011	1KI	018	034	And he said, Do it the second time; and they did it the second time. And he said, Do it the third time; and they did it the third time.
011	1KI	018	035	And the water ran round about the altar; and he filled the trench also with water.
011	1KI	018	036	And it came to pass at the time of the offering of the [evening] oblation, that Elijah the prophet came near, and said, O LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, let it be known this day that thou art God in Israel, and that I am thy servant, and that I have done all these things at thy word.
011	1KI	018	037	Hear me, O LORD, hear me, that this people may know that thou, LORD, art God, and [that] thou hast turned their heart back again.
011	1KI	018	038	Then the fire of the LORD fell, and consumed the burnt offering, and the wood, and the stones, and the dust, and licked up the water that was in the trench.
011	1KI	018	039	And when all the people saw it, they fell on their faces: and they said, The LORD, he is God; the LORD, he is God.
011	1KI	018	040	and Elijah said unto them, Take the prophets of Baal; let not one of them escape. And they took them: and Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon, and slew them there.
011	1KI	018	041	And Elijah said unto Ahab, Get thee up, eat and drink; for there is the sound of abundance of rain.
