011	1KI	019	004	But he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree: and he requested for himself that he might die; and said, It is enough; now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers.
011	1KI	019	005	And he lay down and slept under a juniper tree; and, behold, an angel touched him, and said unto him, Arise and eat.
011	1KI	019	006	And he looked, and, behold, there was at his head a cake baken on the coals, and a cruse of water. And he did eat and drink, and laid him down again.
