012	2KI	006	006	And the man of God said, Where fell it? And he shewed him the place. And he cut down a stick, and cast it in thither, and made the iron to swim.
012	2KI	006	007	And he said, Take it up to thee. So he put out his hand, and took it.
012	2KI	006	008	Now the king of Syria warred against Israel; and he took counsel with his servants, saying, In such and such a place shall be my camp.
012	2KI	006	009	And the man of God sent unto the king of Israel, saying, Beware that thou pass not such a place; for thither the Syrians are coming down.
012	2KI	006	010	And the king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of; and he saved himself there, not once nor twice.
012	2KI	006	011	And the heart of the king of Syria was sore troubled for this thing; and he called his servants, and said unto them, Will ye not shew me which of us is for the king of Israel?
012	2KI	006	012	And one of his servants said, Nay, my lord, O king: but Elisha, the prophet that is in Israel, telleth the king of Israel the words that thou speakest in thy bedchamber.
012	2KI	006	013	And he said, Go and see where he is, that I may send and fetch him. And it was told him, saying, Behold, he is in Dothan.
