014	2CH	016	013	And Asa slept with his fathers, and died in the one and fortieth year of his reign.
014	2CH	016	014	And they buried him in his own sepulchres, which he had hewn out for himself in the city of David, and laid him in the bed which was filled with sweet odours and divers kinds [of spices] prepared by the apothecaries’ art: and they made a very great burning for him.
014	2CH	017	001	And Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his stead, and strengthened himself against Israel.
014	2CH	017	002	And he placed forces in all the fenced cities of Judah, and set garrisons in the land of Judah, and in the cities of Ephraim, which Asa his father had taken.
