018	JOB	003	001	After this opened Job his mouth, and cursed his day.
018	JOB	003	002	And Job answered and said:
018	JOB	003	003	Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night which said, There is a man child conceived.
018	JOB	003	004	Let that day be darkness; let not God regard it from above, neither let the light shine upon it.
018	JOB	003	005	Let darkness and the shadow of death claim it for their own; let a cloud dwell upon it; let all that maketh black the day terrify it.
018	JOB	003	006	As for that night, let thick darkness seize upon it: let it not rejoice among the days of the year; let it not come into the number of the months.
018	JOB	003	007	Lo, let that night be barren; let no joyful voice come therein.
018	JOB	003	008	Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to rouse up leviathan.
018	JOB	003	009	Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark: let it look for light, but have none; neither let it behold the eyelids of the morning:
018	JOB	003	010	Because it shut not up the doors of my [mother’s] womb, nor hid trouble from mine eyes.
018	JOB	003	011	Why died I not from the womb? why did I not give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?
018	JOB	003	012	Why did the knees receive me? or why the breasts, that I should suck?
018	JOB	003	013	For now should I have lain down and been quiet; I should have slept; then had I been at rest:
018	JOB	003	014	With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built up waste places for themselves;
018	JOB	003	015	Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:
018	JOB	003	016	Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants which never saw light.
018	JOB	003	017	There the wicked cease from troubling; and there the weary be at rest.
018	JOB	003	018	There the prisoners are at ease together; they hear not the voice of the taskmaster.
018	JOB	003	019	The small and great are there; and the servant is free from his master.
018	JOB	003	020	Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and life unto the bitter in soul;
018	JOB	003	021	Which long for death, but it cometh not; and dig for it more than for hid treasures;
018	JOB	003	022	Which rejoice exceedingly, and are glad, when they can find the grave?
018	JOB	003	023	[Why is light given] to a man whose way is hid, and whom God hath hedged in?
018	JOB	003	024	For my sighing cometh before I eat, and my roarings are poured out like water.
018	JOB	003	025	For the thing which I fear cometh upon me, and that which I am afraid of cometh unto me.
