018	JOB	004	001	Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,
018	JOB	004	002	If one assay to commune with thee, wilt thou be grieved? but who can withhold himself from speaking?
018	JOB	004	003	Behold, thou hast instructed many, and thou hast strengthened the weak hands.
018	JOB	004	004	Thy words have upholden him that was falling, and thou hast confirmed the feeble knees.
018	JOB	004	005	But now it is come unto thee, and thou faintest; it toucheth thee, and thou art troubled.
018	JOB	004	006	Is not thy fear [of God] thy confidence, [and] thy hope the integrity of thy ways?
018	JOB	004	007	Remember, I pray thee, who [ever] perished, being innocent? or where were the upright cut off?
018	JOB	004	008	According as I have seen, they that plow iniquity, and sow trouble, reap the same.
018	JOB	004	009	By the breath of God they perish, and by the blast of his anger are they consumed.
018	JOB	004	010	The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion, and the teeth of the young lions, are broken.
018	JOB	004	011	The old lion perisheth for lack of prey, and the whelps of the lioness are scattered abroad.
018	JOB	004	012	Now a thing was secretly brought to me, and mine ear received a whisper thereof.
018	JOB	004	013	In thoughts from the visions of the night, when deep sleep falleth on men,
018	JOB	004	014	Fear came upon me, and trembling, which made all my bones to shake.
018	JOB	004	015	Then a spirit passed before my face; the hair of my flesh stood up.
018	JOB	004	016	It stood still, but I could not discern the appearance thereof; a form was before mine eyes: [there was] silence, and I heard a voice, [saying],
018	JOB	004	017	Shall mortal man be more just than God? shall a man be more pure than his Maker?
018	JOB	004	018	Behold, he putteth no trust in his servants; and his angels he chargeth with folly:
018	JOB	004	019	How much more them that dwell in houses of clay, whose foundation is in the dust, which are crushed before the moth!
018	JOB	004	020	Betwixt morning and evening they are destroyed: they perish for ever without any regarding it.
018	JOB	004	021	Is not their tent-cord plucked up within them? they die, and that without wisdom.
018	JOB	005	001	Call now; is there any that will answer thee? and to which of the holy ones wilt thou turn?
018	JOB	005	002	For vexation killeth the foolish man, and jealousy slayeth the silly one.
018	JOB	005	003	I have seen the foolish taking root: but suddenly I cursed his habitation.
018	JOB	005	004	His children are far from safety, and they are crushed in the gate, neither is there any to deliver them.
018	JOB	005	005	Whose harvest the hungry eateth up, and taketh it even out of the thorns, and the snare gapeth for their substance.
018	JOB	005	006	For affliction cometh not forth of the dust, neither doth trouble spring out of the ground;
018	JOB	005	007	But man is born unto trouble, as the sparks fly upward.
018	JOB	005	008	But as for me, I would seek unto God, and unto God would I commit my cause:
018	JOB	005	009	Which doeth great things and unsearchable; marvelous things without number:
018	JOB	005	010	Who giveth rain upon the earth, and sendeth waters upon the fields:
018	JOB	005	011	So that he setteth up on high those that be low; and those which mourn are exalted to safety.
018	JOB	005	012	He frustrateth the devices of the crafty, so that their hands cannot perform their enterprise.
018	JOB	005	013	He taketh the wise in their own craftiness: and the counsel of the froward is carried headlong.
018	JOB	005	014	They meet with darkness in the daytime, and grope at noonday as in the night.
018	JOB	005	015	But he saveth from the sword of their mouth, even the needy from the hand of the mighty.
018	JOB	005	016	So the poor hath hope, and iniquity stoppeth her mouth.
018	JOB	005	017	Behold, happy is the man whom God correcteth: therefore despise not thou the chastening of the Almighty.
018	JOB	005	018	For he maketh sore, and bindeth up; he woundeth, and his hands make whole.
018	JOB	005	019	He shall deliver thee in six troubles; yea, in seven there shall no evil touch thee.
018	JOB	005	020	In famine he shall redeem thee from death; and in war from the power of the sword.
018	JOB	005	021	Thou shalt be hid from the scourge of the tongue; neither shalt thou be afraid of destruction when it cometh.
018	JOB	005	022	At destruction and dearth thou shalt laugh; neither shalt thou be afraid of the beasts of the earth.
018	JOB	005	023	For thou shalt be in league with the stones of the field; and the beasts of the field shall be at peace with thee.
018	JOB	005	024	And thou shalt know that thy tent is in peace; and thou shalt visit thy fold, and shalt miss nothing.
018	JOB	005	025	Thou shalt know also that thy seed shall be great, and thine offspring as the grass of the earth.
018	JOB	005	026	Thou shalt come to thy grave in a full age, like as a shock of corn cometh in in its season.
018	JOB	005	027	Lo this, we have searched it, so it is; hear it, and know thou it for thy good.
018	JOB	006	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	006	002	Oh that my vexation were but weighed, and my calamity laid in the balances together!
018	JOB	006	003	For now it would be heavier than the sand of the seas: therefore have my words been rash.
018	JOB	006	004	For the arrows of the Almighty are within me, the poison whereof my spirit drinketh up: the terrors of God do set themselves in array against me.
018	JOB	006	005	Doth the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or loweth the ox over his fodder?
018	JOB	006	006	Can that which hath no savour be eaten without salt? or is there any taste in the white of an egg?
018	JOB	006	007	My soul refuseth to touch [them]; they are as loathsome meat to me.
018	JOB	006	008	Oh that I might have my request; and that God would grant [me] the thing that I long for.
018	JOB	006	009	Even that it would please God to crush me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!
018	JOB	006	010	Then should I yet have comfort; yea, I would exult in pain that spareth not: for I have not denied the words of the Holy One.
018	JOB	006	011	What is my strength, that I should wait? and what is mine end, at I should be patient?
018	JOB	006	012	Is my strength the strength of stones? or is my flesh of brass?
018	JOB	006	013	Is it not that I have no help in me, and that effectual working is driven quite from me?
018	JOB	006	014	To him that is ready to faint kindness [should be shewed] from his friend; even to him that forsaketh the fear of the Almighty.
018	JOB	006	015	My brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook, as the channel of brooks that pass away;
018	JOB	006	016	Which are black by reason of the ice, [and] wherein the snow hideth itself:
018	JOB	006	017	What time they wax warm, they vanish: when it is hot, they are consumed out of their place.
018	JOB	006	018	The caravans [that travel] by the way of them turn aside; they go up into the waste, and perish.
018	JOB	006	019	The caravans of Tema looked, the companies of Sheba waited for them.
018	JOB	006	020	They were ashamed because they had hoped; they came thither, and were confounded.
018	JOB	006	021	For now ye are nothing; ye see a terror, and are afraid.
018	JOB	006	022	Did I say, Give unto me? or, offer a present for me of your substance?
018	JOB	006	023	Or, Deliver me from the adversary’s hand? or, Redeem me from the hand of the oppressors?
018	JOB	006	024	Teach me, and I will hold my peace: and cause me to understand wherein I have erred.
018	JOB	006	025	How forcible are words of uprightness! but what doth your arguing reprove?
018	JOB	006	026	Do ye imagine to reprove words? seeing that the speeches of one that is desperate are as wind.
018	JOB	006	027	Yea, ye would cast [lots] upon the fatherless, and make merchandise of your friend.
018	JOB	006	028	Now therefore be pleased to look upon me; for surely I shall not lie to your face.
018	JOB	006	029	Return, I pray you, let there be no injustice; yea, return again, my cause is righteous.
018	JOB	006	030	Is there injustice on my tongue? cannot my taste discern mischievous things?
018	JOB	007	001	Is there not a warfare to man upon earth? and are not his days like the days of an hireling?
018	JOB	007	002	As a servant that earnestly desireth the shadow, and as an hireling that looketh for his wages:
018	JOB	007	003	So am I made to possess months of vanity, and wearisome nights are appointed to me.
018	JOB	007	004	When I lie down, I say, When shall I arise? but the night is long; and I am full of tossings to and fro unto the dawning of the day.
018	JOB	007	005	My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust; my skin closeth up and breaketh out afresh.
018	JOB	007	006	My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle, and are spent without hope.
018	JOB	007	007	Oh remember that my life is wind: mine eye shall no more see good.
018	JOB	007	008	The eye of him that seeth me shall behold me no more: thine eyes shall be upon me, but I shall not be.
018	JOB	007	009	As the cloud is consumed and vanisheth away, so he that goeth down to Sheol shall come up no more.
018	JOB	007	010	He shall return no more to his house, neither shall his place know him any more.
018	JOB	007	011	Therefore I will not refrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.
018	JOB	007	012	Am I a sea, or a sea-monster, that thou settest a watch over me?
018	JOB	007	013	When I say, My bed shall comfort me, my couch shall ease my complaint;
018	JOB	007	014	Then thou scarest me with dreams, and terrifiest me through visions:
018	JOB	007	015	So that my soul chooseth strangling, and death rather than [these] my bones.
018	JOB	007	016	I loathe [my life]; I would not live alway: let me alone; for my days are vanity.
018	JOB	007	017	What is man, that thou shouldest magnify him, and that thou shouldest set thine heart upon him,
018	JOB	007	018	And that thou shouldest visit him every morning, and try him every moment?
018	JOB	007	019	How long wilt thou not look away from me, nor let me alone till I swallow down my spittle?
018	JOB	007	020	If I have sinned, what do I unto thee, O thou watcher of men? why hast thou set me as a mark for thee, so that I am a burden to myself?
018	JOB	007	021	And why dost thou not pardon my transgression, and take away mine iniquity? for now shall I lie down in the dust; and thou shall seek me diligently, but I shall not be.
018	JOB	008	001	Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,
018	JOB	008	002	How long wilt thou speak these things? and [how long] shall the words of thy mouth be [like] a mighty wind?
018	JOB	008	003	Doth God pervert judgment? or doth the Almighty pervert justice?
018	JOB	008	004	If thy children have sinned against him, and he have delivered them into the hand of their transgression:
018	JOB	008	005	If thou wouldest seek diligently unto God, and make thy supplication to the Almighty;
018	JOB	008	006	If thou wert pure and upright; surely now he would awake for thee, and make the habitation of thy righteousness prosperous.
018	JOB	008	007	And though thy beginning was small, yet thy latter end should greatly increase.
018	JOB	008	008	For inquire, I pray thee, of the former age, and apply thyself to that which their fathers have searched out:
018	JOB	008	009	(For we are but of yesterday, and know nothing, because our days upon earth are a shadow:)
018	JOB	008	010	Shall not they teach thee, and tell thee, and utter words out of their heart?
018	JOB	008	011	Can the rush grow up without mire? can the flag grow without water?
018	JOB	008	012	Whilst it is yet in its greenness, [and] not cut down, it withereth before any [other] herb.
018	JOB	008	013	So are the paths of all that forget God; and the hope of the godless man shall perish:
018	JOB	008	014	Whose confidence shall break in sunder, and whose trust is a spider’s web.
018	JOB	008	015	He shall lean upon his house, but it shall not stand: he shall hold fast thereby, but it shall not endure.
018	JOB	008	016	He is green before the sun, and his shoots go forth over his garden.
018	JOB	008	017	His roots are wrapped about the heap, he beholdeth the place of stones.
018	JOB	008	018	If he be destroyed from his place, then it shall deny him, [saying], I have not seen thee.
018	JOB	008	019	Behold, this is the joy of his way, and out of the earth shall others spring.
018	JOB	008	020	Behold, God will not cast away a perfect man, neither will he uphold the evil-doers.
018	JOB	008	021	He will yet fill thy mouth with laughter, and thy lips with shouting.
018	JOB	008	022	They that hate thee shall be clothed with shame; and the tent of the wicked shall be no more.
018	JOB	009	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	009	002	Of a truth I know that it is so: but how can man be just with God?
018	JOB	009	003	If he be pleased to contend with him, he cannot answer him one of a thousand.
018	JOB	009	004	[He is] wise in heart, and mighty in strength: who hath hardened himself against him, and prospered?
018	JOB	009	005	Which removeth the mountains, and they know it not, when he overturneth them in his anger.
018	JOB	009	006	Which shaketh the earth out of her place, and the pillars thereof tremble.
018	JOB	009	007	Which commandeth the sun, and it riseth not; and sealeth up the stars.
018	JOB	009	008	Which alone stretcheth out the heavens, and treadeth upon the waves of the sea.
018	JOB	009	009	Which maketh the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades, and the chambers of the south.
018	JOB	009	010	Which doeth great things past finding out; yea, marvelous things without number.
018	JOB	009	011	Lo, he goeth by me, and I see him not: he passeth on also, but I perceive him not.
018	JOB	009	012	Behold, he seizeth [the prey], who can hinder him? who will say unto him, What doest thou?
018	JOB	009	013	God will not withdraw his anger; the helpers of Rahab do stoop under him.
018	JOB	009	014	How much less shall I answer him, and choose out my words [to reason] with him?
018	JOB	009	015	Whom, though I were righteous, yet would I not answer; I would make supplication to mine adversary.
018	JOB	009	016	If I had called, and he had answered me; yet would I not believe that he hearkened unto my voice.
018	JOB	009	017	For he breaketh me with a tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause.
018	JOB	009	018	He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness.
018	JOB	009	019	If [we speak] of the strength of the mighty, lo, [he is there]! and if of judgment, who will appoint me a time?
018	JOB	009	020	Though I be righteous, mine own mouth shall condemn me: though I be perfect, it shall prove me perverse.
018	JOB	009	021	I am perfect; I regard not myself; I despise my life.
018	JOB	009	022	It is all one; therefore I say, He destroyeth the perfect and the wicked.
018	JOB	009	023	If the scourge slay suddenly, he will mock at the trial of the innocent.
018	JOB	009	024	The earth is given into the hand of the wicked: he covereth the faces of the judges thereof; if [it be] not [he], who then is it?
018	JOB	009	025	Now my days are swifter than a post: they flee away, they see no good.
018	JOB	009	026	They are passed away as the swift ships: as the eagle that swoopeth on the prey.
018	JOB	009	027	If I say, I will forget my complaint, I will put off my [sad] countenance, and be of good cheer:
018	JOB	009	028	I am afraid of all my sorrows, I know that thou wilt not hold me innocent.
018	JOB	009	029	I shall be condemned; why then do I labour in vain?
018	JOB	009	030	If I wash myself with snow water, and make my hands never so clean;
018	JOB	009	031	Yet wilt thou plunge me in the ditch, and mine own clothes shall abhor me.
018	JOB	009	032	For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him, that we should come together in judgment.
018	JOB	009	033	There is no daysman betwixt us, that might lay his hand upon us both.
018	JOB	009	034	Let him take his rod away from me, and let not his terror make me afraid:
018	JOB	009	035	Then would I speak, and not fear him; for I am not so in myself.
018	JOB	010	001	My soul is weary of my life; I will give free course to my complaint; I will speak in the bitterness of my soul.
018	JOB	010	002	I will say unto God, Do not condemn me; shew me wherefore thou contendest with me.
018	JOB	010	003	Is it good unto thee that thou shouldest oppress, that thou shouldest despise the work of thine hands, and shine upon the counsel of the wicked?
018	JOB	010	004	Hast thou eyes of flesh, or seest thou as man seeth?
018	JOB	010	005	Are thy days as the days of man, or thy years as man’s days,
018	JOB	010	006	That thou inquirest after mine iniquity, and searchest after my sin,
018	JOB	010	007	Although thou knowest that I am not wicked; and there is none that can deliver out of thine hand?
018	JOB	010	008	Thine hands have framed me and fashioned me together round about; yet thou dost destroy me.
018	JOB	010	009	Remember, I beseech thee, that thou hast fashioned me as clay; and wilt thou bring me into dust again?
018	JOB	010	010	Hast thou not poured me out as milk, and curdled me like cheese?
018	JOB	010	011	Thou hast clothed me with skin and flesh, and knit me together with bones and sinews.
018	JOB	010	012	Thou hast granted me life and favour, and thy visitation hath preserved my spirit.
018	JOB	010	013	Yet these things thou didst hide in thine heart; I know that this is with thee:
018	JOB	010	014	If I sin, then thou markest me, and thou wilt not acquit me from mine iniquity.
018	JOB	010	015	If I be wicked, woe unto me; and if I be righteous, yet shall I not lift up my head; being filled with ignominy and looking upon mine affliction.
018	JOB	010	016	And if [my head] exalt itself, thou huntest me as a lion: and again thou shewest thyself marvelous upon me.
018	JOB	010	017	Thou renewest thy witnesses against me, and increasest thine indignation upon me; changes and warfare are with me.
018	JOB	010	018	Wherefore then hast thou brought me forth out of the womb? I had given up the ghost, and no eye had seen me.
018	JOB	010	019	I should have been as though I had not been; I should have been carried from the womb to the grave.
018	JOB	010	020	Are not my days few? cease then, and let me alone, that I may take comfort a little,
018	JOB	010	021	Before I go whence I shall not return, [even] to the land of darkness and of the shadow of death;
018	JOB	010	022	A land of thick darkness, as darkness [itself]; [a land] of the shadow of death, without any order, and where the light is as darkness.
018	JOB	011	001	Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,
018	JOB	011	002	Should not the multitude of words be answered? and should a man full of talk be justified?
018	JOB	011	003	Should thy boastings make men hold their peace? and when thou mockest, shall no man make thee ashamed?
018	JOB	011	004	For thou sayest, My doctrine is pure, and I am clean in thine eyes.
018	JOB	011	005	But Oh that God would speak, and open his lips against thee;
018	JOB	011	006	And that he would shew thee the secrets of wisdom, that is manifold in effectual working! Know therefore that God exacteth of thee less than thine iniquity deserveth.
018	JOB	011	007	Canst thou by searching find out God? canst thou find out the Almighty unto perfection?
018	JOB	011	008	It is high as heaven; what canst thou do? deeper than Sheol; what canst thou know?
018	JOB	011	009	The measure thereof is longer than the earth, and broader than the sea.
018	JOB	011	010	If he pass through, and shut up, and call unto judgment, then who can hinder him?
018	JOB	011	011	For he knoweth vain men: he seeth iniquity also, even though he consider it not.
018	JOB	011	012	But vain man is void of understanding, yea, man is born as a wild ass’s colt.
018	JOB	011	013	If thou set thine heart aright, and stretch out thine hands toward him;
018	JOB	011	014	If iniquity be in thine hand, put it far away, and let not unrighteousness dwell in thy tents;
018	JOB	011	015	Surely then shalt thou lift up thy face without spot; yea, thou shalt be stedfast, and shalt not fear:
018	JOB	011	016	For thou shalt forget thy misery; thou shalt remember it as waters that are passed away:
018	JOB	011	017	And [thy] life shall be clearer than the noonday; though there be darkness, it shall be as the morning.
018	JOB	011	018	And thou shalt be secure, because there is hope; yea, thou shalt search [about thee], and shalt take thy rest in safety.
018	JOB	011	019	Also thou shalt lie down, and none shall make thee afraid; yea, many shall make suit unto thee.
018	JOB	011	020	But the eyes of the wicked shall fail, and they shall have no way to flee, and their hope shall be the giving up of the ghost.
018	JOB	012	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	012	002	No doubt but ye are the people, and wisdom shall die with you.
018	JOB	012	003	But I have understanding as well as you; I am not inferior to you: yea, who knoweth not such things as these?
018	JOB	012	004	I am as one that is a laughing-stock to his neighbour, [a man] that called upon God, and he answered him: the just, the perfect man is a laughing-stock.
018	JOB	012	005	In the thought of him that is at ease there is contempt for misfortune; it is ready for them whose foot slippeth.
018	JOB	012	006	The tents of robbers prosper, and they that provoke God are secure; into whose hand God bringeth [abundantly].
018	JOB	012	007	But ask now the beasts, and they shall teach thee; and the fowls of the air, and they shall tell thee:
018	JOB	012	008	Or speak to the earth, and it shall teach thee; and the fishes of the sea shall declare unto thee.
018	JOB	012	009	Who knoweth not in all these, that the hand of LORD hath wrought this?
018	JOB	012	010	In whose hand is the soul of every living thing, and the breath of all mankind.
018	JOB	012	011	Doth not the ear try words, even as the palate tasteth its meat?
018	JOB	012	012	With aged men is wisdom, and in length of days understanding.
018	JOB	012	013	With him is wisdom and might; he hath counsel and understanding.
018	JOB	012	014	Behold, he breaketh down, and it cannot be built again; he shutteth up a man, and there can be no opening.
018	JOB	012	015	Behold, he withholdeth the waters, and they dry up; again, he sendeth them out, and they overturn the earth.
018	JOB	012	016	With him is strength and effectual working; the deceived and the deceiver are his.
018	JOB	012	017	He leadeth counsellors away spoiled, and judges maketh he fools.
018	JOB	012	018	He looseth the bond of kings, and bindeth their loins with a girdle.
018	JOB	012	019	He leadeth priests away spoiled, and overthroweth the mighty.
018	JOB	012	020	He removeth the speech of the trusty, and taketh away the understanding of the elders.
018	JOB	012	021	He poureth contempt upon princes, and looseth the belt of the strong.
018	JOB	012	022	He discovereth deep things out of darkness, and bringeth out to light the shadow of death.
018	JOB	012	023	He increaseth the nations, and destroyeth them: he spreadeth the nations abroad, and bringeth them in.
018	JOB	012	024	He taketh away the heart of the chiefs of the people of the earth, and causeth them to wander in a wilderness where there is no way.
018	JOB	012	025	They grope in the dark without light, and he maketh them to stagger like a drunken man.
018	JOB	013	001	Lo, mine eye hath seen all [this], mine ear hath heard and understood it.
018	JOB	013	002	What ye know, [the same] do I know also: I am not inferior unto you.
018	JOB	013	003	Surely I would speak to the Almighty, and I desire to reason with God.
018	JOB	013	004	But ye are forgers of lies, ye are all physicians of no value.
018	JOB	013	005	Oh that ye would altogether hold your peace! and it should be your wisdom.
018	JOB	013	006	Hear now my reasoning, and hearken to the pleadings of my lips.
018	JOB	013	007	Will ye speak unrighteously for God, and talk deceitfully for him?
018	JOB	013	008	Will ye respect his person? will ye contend for God?
018	JOB	013	009	Is it good that he should search you out? or as one deceiveth a man, will ye deceive him?
018	JOB	013	010	He will surely reprove you, if ye do secretly respect persons.
018	JOB	013	011	Shall not his excellency make you afraid, and his dread fall upon you?
018	JOB	013	012	Your memorable sayings [are] proverbs of ashes, your defences [are] defences of clay.
018	JOB	013	013	Hold your peace, let me alone, that I may speak, and let come on me what wilt.
018	JOB	013	014	Wherefore should I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in mine hand?
018	JOB	013	015	Though he slay me, yet will I wait for him: nevertheless I will maintain my ways before him.
018	JOB	013	016	This also shall be my salvation; for a godless man shall not come before him.
018	JOB	013	017	Hear diligently my speech, and let my declaration be in your ears.
018	JOB	013	018	Behold now, I have ordered my cause; I know that I am righteous.
018	JOB	013	019	Who is he that will contend with me? for now shall I hold my peace and give up the ghost.
018	JOB	013	020	Only do not two things unto me, then will I not hide myself from thy face:
018	JOB	013	021	Withdraw thine hand far from me; and let not thy terror make me afraid.
018	JOB	013	022	Then call thou, and I will answer; or let me speak, and answer thou me.
018	JOB	013	023	How many are mine iniquities and sins? make me to know my transgression and my sin.
018	JOB	013	024	Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and holdest me for thine enemy?
018	JOB	013	025	Wilt thou harass a driven leaf? and wilt thou pursue the dry stubble?
018	JOB	013	026	For thou writest bitter things against me, and makest me to inherit the iniquities of my youth:
018	JOB	013	027	Thou puttest my feet also in the stocks, and markest all my paths; thou drawest thee a line about the soles of my feet:
018	JOB	013	028	Though I am like a rotten thing that consumeth, like a garment that is moth-eaten.
018	JOB	014	001	Man that is born of a woman is of few days, and full of trouble.
018	JOB	014	002	He cometh forth like a flower, and is cut down: he fleeth also as a shadow, and continueth not.
018	JOB	014	003	And dost thou open thine eyes upon such an one, and bringest me into judgment with thee?
018	JOB	014	004	Who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean? not one.
018	JOB	014	005	Seeing his days are determined, the number of his months is with thee, and thou hast appointed his bounds that he cannot pass;
018	JOB	014	006	Look away from him, that he may rest, till he shall accomplish, as an hireling, his day.
018	JOB	014	007	For there is hope of a tree, if it be cut down, that it will sprout again, and that the tender branch thereof will not cease.
018	JOB	014	008	Though the root thereof wax old in the earth, and the stock thereof die in the ground;
018	JOB	014	009	Yet through the scent of water it will bud, and put forth boughs like a plant.
018	JOB	014	010	But man dieth, and wasteth away: yea, man giveth up the ghost, and where is he?
018	JOB	014	011	[As] the waters fail from the sea, and the river decayeth and drieth up;
018	JOB	014	012	So man lieth down and riseth not: till the heavens be no more, they shall not awake, nor be roused out of their sleep.
018	JOB	014	013	Oh that thou wouldest hide me in Sheol, that thou wouldest keep me secret, until thy wrath be past, that thou wouldest appoint me a set time, and remember me!
018	JOB	014	014	If a man die, shall he live [again]? all the days of my warfare would I wait, till my release should come.
018	JOB	014	015	Thou shouldest call, and I would answer thee: thou wouldest have a desire to the work of thine hands.
018	JOB	014	016	But now thou numberest my steps: dost thou not watch over my sin?
018	JOB	014	017	My transgression is sealed up in a bag, and thou fastenest up mine iniquity.
018	JOB	014	018	And surely the mountain falling cometh to nought, and the rock is removed out of its place;
018	JOB	014	019	The waters wear the stones; the overflowings thereof wash away the dust of the earth: and thou destroyest the hope of man.
018	JOB	014	020	Thou prevailest for ever against him, and he passeth; thou changest his countenance, and sendest him away.
018	JOB	014	021	His sons come to honour, and he knoweth it not; and they are brought low, but he perceiveth it not of them.
018	JOB	014	022	But his flesh upon him hath pain, and his soul within him mourneth.
018	JOB	015	001	Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,
018	JOB	015	002	Should a wise man make answer with vain knowledge, and fill his belly with the east wind?
018	JOB	015	003	Should he reason with unprofitable talk, or with speeches wherewith he can do no good?
018	JOB	015	004	Yea, thou doest away with fear, and restrainest devotion before God.
018	JOB	015	005	For thine iniquity teacheth thy mouth, and thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.
018	JOB	015	006	Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and not I; yea, thine own lips testify against thee.
018	JOB	015	007	Art thou the first man that was born? or wast thou brought forth before the hills?
018	JOB	015	008	Hast thou heard the secret counsel of God? and dost thou restrain wisdom to thyself?
018	JOB	015	009	What knowest thou, that we know not? what understandest thou, which is not in us?
018	JOB	015	010	With us are both the grayheaded and the very aged men, much elder than thy father.
018	JOB	015	011	Are the consolations of God too small for thee, and the word [that dealeth] gently with thee?
018	JOB	015	012	Why doth thine heart carry thee away? and why do thine eyes wink?
018	JOB	015	013	That thou turnest thy spirit against God, and lettest [such] words go out of thy mouth.
018	JOB	015	014	What is man, that he should be clean? and he which is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?
018	JOB	015	015	Behold, he putteth no trust in his holy ones; yea, the heavens are not clean in his sight.
018	JOB	015	016	How much less one that is abominable and corrupt, a man that drinketh iniquity like water!
018	JOB	015	017	I will shew thee, hear thou me; and that which I have seen I will declare:
018	JOB	015	018	(Which wise men have told from their fathers, and have not hid it;
018	JOB	015	019	Unto whom alone the land was given, and no stranger passed among them:)
018	JOB	015	020	The wicked man travaileth with pain all his days, even the number of years that are laid up for the oppressor.
018	JOB	015	021	A sound of terrors is in his ears; in prosperity the spoiler shall come upon him:
018	JOB	015	022	He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness, and he is waited for of the sword:
018	JOB	015	023	He wandereth abroad for bread, [saying], Where is it? he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand:
018	JOB	015	024	Distress and anguish make him afraid; they prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle:
018	JOB	015	025	Because he hath stretched out his hand against God, and behaveth himself proudly against the Almighty;
018	JOB	015	026	He runneth upon him with a [stiff] neck, with the thick bosses of his bucklers:
018	JOB	015	027	Because he hath covered his face with his fatness, and made collops of fat on his flanks;
018	JOB	015	028	And he hath dwelt in desolate cities, in houses which no man inhabited, which were ready to become heaps.
018	JOB	015	029	He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall their produce bend to the earth.
018	JOB	015	030	He shall not depart out of darkness; the flame shall dry up his branches, and by the breath of his mouth shall he go away.
018	JOB	015	031	Let him not trust in vanity, deceiving himself: for vanity shall be his recompence.
018	JOB	015	032	It shall be accomplished before his time, and his branch shall not be green.
018	JOB	015	033	He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and shall cast off his flower as the olive.
018	JOB	015	034	For the company of the godless shall be barren, and fire shall consume the tents of bribery.
018	JOB	015	035	They conceive mischief, and bring forth iniquity, and their belly prepareth deceit.
018	JOB	016	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	016	002	I have heard many such things: miserable comforters are ye all.
018	JOB	016	003	Shall vain words have an end? or what provoketh thee that thou answerest?
018	JOB	016	004	I also could speak as ye do; if your soul were in my soul’s stead, I could join words together against you, and shake mine head at you.
018	JOB	016	005	[But] I would strengthen you with my mouth, and the solace of my lips should assuage [your grief].
018	JOB	016	006	Though I speak, my grief is not assuaged: and though I forbear, what am I eased?
018	JOB	016	007	But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company.
018	JOB	016	008	And thou hast laid fast hold on me, [which] is a witness [against me]: and my leanness riseth up against me, it testifieth to my face.
018	JOB	016	009	He hath torn me in his wrath, and persecuted me; he hath gnashed upon me with his teeth: mine adversary sharpeneth his eyes upon me.
018	JOB	016	010	They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully: they gather themselves together against me.
018	JOB	016	011	God delivereth me to the ungodly, and casteth me into the hands of the wicked.
018	JOB	016	012	I was at ease, and he brake me asunder; yea, he hath taken me by the neck, and dashed me to pieces: he hath also set me up for his mark.
018	JOB	016	013	His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground.
018	JOB	016	014	He breaketh me with breach upon breach; he runneth upon me like a giant.
018	JOB	016	015	I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and have laid my horn in the dust.
018	JOB	016	016	My face is foul with weeping, and on my eyelids is the shadow of death;
018	JOB	016	017	Although there is no violence in mine hands, and my prayer is pure.
018	JOB	016	018	O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no [resting] place.
018	JOB	016	019	Even now, behold, my witness is in heaven, and he that coucheth for me is on high.
018	JOB	016	020	My friends scorn me: [but] mine eye poureth out tears unto God;
018	JOB	016	021	That he would maintain the right of a man with God, and of a son of man with his neighbour!
018	JOB	016	022	For when a few years are come, I shall go the way whence I shall not return.
018	JOB	017	001	My spirit is consumed, my days are extinct, the grave is [ready] for me.
018	JOB	017	002	Surely there are mockers with me, and mine eye abideth in their provocation.
018	JOB	017	003	Give now a pledge, be surety for me with thyself; who is there that will strike hands with me?
018	JOB	017	004	For thou hast hid their heart from understanding: therefore shalt thou not exalt [them].
018	JOB	017	005	He that denounceth his friends for a prey, even the eyes of his children shall fail.
018	JOB	017	006	He hath made me also a byword of the people; and I am become an open abhorring.
018	JOB	017	007	Mine eye also is dim by reason of sorrow, and all my members are as a shadow.
018	JOB	017	008	Upright men shall be astonied at this, and the innocent shall stir up himself against the godless.
018	JOB	017	009	Yet shall the righteous hold on his way, and he that hath clean hands shall wax stronger and stronger.
018	JOB	017	010	But return ye, all of you, and come now: and I shall not find a wise man among you.
018	JOB	017	011	My days are past, my purposes are broken off, even the droughts of my heart.
018	JOB	017	012	They change the night into a day: the fight, [say they], is near unto the darkness.
018	JOB	017	013	If I look for Sheol as mine house; if I have spread my couch in the darkness;
018	JOB	017	014	If I have said to corruption, Thou art my father; to the worm, [Thou art] my mother, and my sister;
018	JOB	017	015	Where then is my hope? and as for my hope, who shall see it?
018	JOB	017	016	It shall go down to the bars of Sheol, when once there is rest in the dust.
018	JOB	018	001	Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,
018	JOB	018	002	How long will ye lay snares for words? consider, and afterwards we will speak.
018	JOB	018	003	Wherefore are we counted as beasts, [and] are become unclean in your sight?
018	JOB	018	004	Thou that tearest thyself in thine anger, shall the earth be forsaken for thee? or shall the rock be removed out of its place?
018	JOB	018	005	Yea, the light of the wicked shall be put out, and the spark of his fire shall not shine.
018	JOB	018	006	The light shall be dark in his tent, and his lamp above him shall be put out.
018	JOB	018	007	The steps of his strength shall be straitened, and his own counsel shall cast him down.
018	JOB	018	008	For he is cast into a net by his own feet, and he walketh upon the toils.
018	JOB	018	009	A gin shall take [him] by the heel, [and] a snare shall lay hold on him.
018	JOB	018	010	A noose is hid for him in the ground, and a trap for him in the way.
018	JOB	018	011	Terrors shall make him afraid on every side, and shall chase him at his heels.
018	JOB	018	012	His strength shall be hunger-bitten and calamity shall be ready for his halting.
018	JOB	018	013	It shall devour the members of his body, [yea], the firstborn of death shall devour his members.
018	JOB	018	014	He shall be rooted out of his tent wherein he trusteth; and he shall be brought to the king of terrors.
018	JOB	018	015	There shall dwell in his tent that which is none of his: brimstone shall be scattered upon his habitation.
018	JOB	018	016	His roots shall be dried up beneath, and above shall his branch be cut off.
018	JOB	018	017	His remembrance shall perish from the earth, and he shall have no name in the street.
018	JOB	018	018	He shall be driven from light into darkness, and chased out of the world.
018	JOB	018	019	He shall have neither son nor son’s son among his people, nor any remaining where he sojourned.
018	JOB	018	020	They that come after shall be astonied at his day, as they that went before were affrighted.
018	JOB	018	021	Surely such are the dwellings of the unrighteous, and this is the place of him that knoweth not God.
018	JOB	019	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	019	002	How long will ye vex my soul and break me in pieces with words?
018	JOB	019	003	These ten times have ye reproached me: ye are not ashamed that ye deal hardly with me.
018	JOB	019	004	And be it indeed that I have erred, mine error remaineth with myself.
018	JOB	019	005	If indeed ye will magnify yourselves against me, and plead against me my reproach:
018	JOB	019	006	Know now that God hath subverted me [in my cause], and hath compassed me with his net.
018	JOB	019	007	Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard: I cry for help, but there is no judgment.
018	JOB	019	008	He hath fenced up my way that I cannot pass, and hath set darkness in my paths.
018	JOB	019	009	He hath stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown from my head.
018	JOB	019	010	He hath broken me down on every side, and I am gone: and mine hope hath he plucked up like a tree.
018	JOB	019	011	He hath also kindled his wrath against me, and he counteth me unto him as [one of] his adversaries.
018	JOB	019	012	His troops come on together, and cast up their way against me, and encamp round about my tent.
018	JOB	019	013	He hath put my brethren far from me, and mine acquaintance are wholly estranged from me.
018	JOB	019	014	My kinsfolk have failed, and my familiar friends have forgotten me.
018	JOB	019	015	They that dwell in mine house, and my maids, count me for a stranger: I am an alien in their sight.
018	JOB	019	016	I call unto my servant, and he giveth me no answer, [though] I entreat him with my mouth.
018	JOB	019	017	My breath is strange to my wife, and my supplication to the children of my [mother’s] womb.
018	JOB	019	018	Even young children despise me; if I arise, they speak against me.
018	JOB	019	019	All my inward friends abhor me: and they whom I loved are turned against me.
018	JOB	019	020	My bone cleaveth to my skin and to my flesh, and I am escaped with the skin of my teeth.
018	JOB	019	021	Have pity upon me, have pity upon me, O ye my friends; for the hand of God hath touched me.
018	JOB	019	022	Why do ye persecute me as God, and are not satisfied with my flesh?
018	JOB	019	023	Oh that my words were now written! oh that they were inscribed in a book!
018	JOB	019	024	That with an iron pen and lead they were graven in the rock for ever!
018	JOB	019	025	But I know that my redeemer liveth, and that he shall stand up at the last upon the earth:
018	JOB	019	026	And after my skin hath been thus destroyed, yet from my flesh shall I see God:
018	JOB	019	027	Whom I shall see for myself, and mine eyes shall behold, and not another. My reins are consumed within me.
018	JOB	019	028	If ye say, How we will persecute him! seeing that the root of the matter is found in me;
018	JOB	019	029	Be ye afraid of the sword: for wrath [bringeth] the punishments of the sword, that ye may know there is a judgment.
018	JOB	020	001	Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,
018	JOB	020	002	Therefore do my thoughts give answer to me, even by reason of my haste that is in me.
018	JOB	020	003	I have heard the reproof which putteth me to shame, and the spirit of my understanding answereth me.
018	JOB	020	004	Knowest thou [not] this of old time, since man was placed upon earth,
018	JOB	020	005	That the triumphing of the wicked is short, and the joy of the godless but for a moment?
018	JOB	020	006	Though his excellency mount up to the heavens, and his head reach unto the clouds;
018	JOB	020	007	Yet he shall perish for ever like his own dung: they which have seen him shall say, Where is he?
018	JOB	020	008	He shall fly away as a dream, and shall not be found: yea, he shall be chased away as a vision of the night.
018	JOB	020	009	The eye which saw him shall see him no more; neither shall his place any more behold him.
018	JOB	020	010	His children shall seek the favour of the poor, and his hands shall give back his wealth.
018	JOB	020	011	His bones are full of his youth, but it shall lie down with him in the dust.
018	JOB	020	012	Though wickedness be sweet in his mouth, though he hide it under his tongue;
018	JOB	020	013	Though he spare it, and will not let it go, but keep it still within his mouth;
018	JOB	020	014	Yet his meat in his bowels is turned, it is the gall of asps within him.
018	JOB	020	015	He hath swallowed down riches, and he shall vomit them up again: God shall cast them out of his belly.
018	JOB	020	016	He shall suck the poison of asps: the viper’s tongue shall slay him.
018	JOB	020	017	He shall not look upon the rivers, the flowing streams of honey and butter.
018	JOB	020	018	That which he laboured for shall he restore, and shall not swallow it down; according to the substance that he hath gotten, he shall not rejoice.
018	JOB	020	019	For he hath oppressed and forsaken the poor; he hath violently taken away an house, and he shall not build it up.
018	JOB	020	020	Because he knew no quietness within him, he shall not save aught of that wherein he delighteth.
018	JOB	020	021	There was nothing left that he devoured not; therefore his prosperity shall not endure.
018	JOB	020	022	In the fulness of his sufficiency he shall be in straits: the hand of every one that is in misery shall come upon him.
018	JOB	020	023	When he is about to fill his belly, [God] shall cast the fierceness of his wrath upon him, and shall rain it upon him while he is eating.
018	JOB	020	024	He shall flee from the iron weapon, and the bow of brass shall strike him through.
018	JOB	020	025	He draweth it forth, and it cometh out of his body: yea, the glittering point cometh out of his gall; terrors are upon him.
018	JOB	020	026	All darkness is laid up for his treasures: a fire not blown [by man] shall devour him; it shall consume that which is left in his tent.
018	JOB	020	027	The heavens shall reveal his iniquity, and the earth shall rise up against him.
018	JOB	020	028	The increase of his house shall depart, [his goods] shall flow away in the day of his wrath.
018	JOB	020	029	This is the portion of a wicked man from God, and the heritage appointed unto him by God.
018	JOB	021	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	021	002	Hear diligently my speech; and let this be your consolations.
018	JOB	021	003	Suffer me, and I also will speak; and after that I have spoken, mock on.
018	JOB	021	004	As for me, is my complaint to man? and why should I not be impatient?
018	JOB	021	005	Mark me, and be astonished, and lay your hand upon your mouth.
018	JOB	021	006	Even when I remember I am troubled, and horror taketh hold on my flesh.
018	JOB	021	007	Wherefore do the wicked live, become old, yea, wax mighty in power?
018	JOB	021	008	Their seed is established with them in their sight, and their offspring before their eyes.
018	JOB	021	009	Their houses are safe from fear, neither is the rod of God upon them.
018	JOB	021	010	Their bull gendereth, and faileth not; their cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.
018	JOB	021	011	They send forth their little ones like a flock, and their children dance.
018	JOB	021	012	They sing to the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the pipe.
018	JOB	021	013	They spend their days in prosperity, and in a moment they go down to Sheol.
018	JOB	021	014	Yet they said unto God, Depart from us; for we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.
018	JOB	021	015	What is the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what profit should we have, if we pray unto him?
018	JOB	021	016	Lo, their prosperity is not in their hand: the counsel of the wicked is far from me.
018	JOB	021	017	How oft is it that the lamp of the wicked is put out? that their calamity cometh upon them? that [God] distributeth sorrows in his anger?
018	JOB	021	018	That they are as stubble before the wind, and as chaff that the storm carrieth away?
018	JOB	021	019	[Ye say], God layeth up his iniquity for his children. Let him recompense it unto himself, that he may know it.
018	JOB	021	020	Let his own eyes see his destruction, and let him drink of the wrath of the Almighty.
018	JOB	021	021	For what pleasure hath he in his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off in the midst?
018	JOB	021	022	Shall any teach God knowledge? seeing he judgeth those that are high.
018	JOB	021	023	One dieth in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet:
018	JOB	021	024	His breasts are full of milk, and the marrow of his bones is moistened.
018	JOB	021	025	And another dieth in bitterness of soul, and never tasteth of good.
018	JOB	021	026	They lie down alike in the dust, and the worm covereth them.
018	JOB	021	027	Behold, I know your thoughts, and the devices which ye wrongfully imagine against me.
018	JOB	021	028	For ye say, Where is the house of the prince? and where is the tent wherein the wicked dwelt?
018	JOB	021	029	Have ye not asked them that go by the way? and do ye not know their tokens?
018	JOB	021	030	That the evil man is reserved to the day of calamity? that they are led forth to the day of wrath?
018	JOB	021	031	Who shall declare his way to his face? and who shall repay him what he hath done?
018	JOB	021	032	Yet shall he be borne to the grave, and shall keep watch over the tomb.
018	JOB	021	033	The clods of the valley shall be sweet unto him, and all men shall draw after him, as there were innumerable before him.
018	JOB	021	034	How then comfort ye me in vain, seeing in your answers there remaineth only falsehood?
018	JOB	022	001	Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,
018	JOB	022	002	Can a man be profitable unto God? surely he that is wise is profitable unto himself.
018	JOB	022	003	Is it any pleasure to the Almighty, that thou art righteous? or is it gain [to him], that thou makest thy ways perfect?
018	JOB	022	004	Is it for thy fear [of him] that he reproveth thee, that he entereth with thee into judgment?
018	JOB	022	005	Is not thy wickedness great? neither is there any end to thine iniquities.
018	JOB	022	006	For thou hast taken pledges of thy brother for nought, and stripped the naked of their clothing.
018	JOB	022	007	Thou hast not given water to the weary to drink, and thou hast withholden bread from the hungry.
018	JOB	022	008	But as for the mighty man, he had the earth; and the honourable man, he dwelt in it.
018	JOB	022	009	Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.
018	JOB	022	010	Therefore snares are round about thee, and sudden fear troubleth thee,
018	JOB	022	011	Or darkness, that thou canst not see, and abundance of waters cover thee.
018	JOB	022	012	Is not God in the height of heaven? and behold the height of the stars, how high they are!
018	JOB	022	013	And thou sayest, What doth God know? can he judge through the thick darkness?
018	JOB	022	014	Thick clouds are a covering to him, that he seeth not; and he walketh in the circuit of heaven.
018	JOB	022	015	Wilt thou keep the old way which wicked men have trodden?
018	JOB	022	016	Who were snatched away before their time, whose foundation was poured out as a stream:
018	JOB	022	017	Who said unto God, Depart from us; and, What can the Almighty do for us?
018	JOB	022	018	Yet he fired their houses with good things: but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.
018	JOB	022	019	The righteous see it, and are glad; and the innocent laugh them to scorn:
018	JOB	022	020	[Saying], Surely they that did rise up against us are cut off, and the remnant of them the fire hath consumed.
018	JOB	022	021	Acquaint now thyself with him, and be at peace: thereby good shall come unto thee.
018	JOB	022	022	Receive, I pray thee, the law from his mouth, and lay up his words in thine heart.
018	JOB	022	023	If thou return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up; if thou put away unrighteousness far from thy tents.
018	JOB	022	024	And lay thou [thy] treasure in the dust, and [the gold of] Ophir among the stones of the brooks;
018	JOB	022	025	And the Almighty shall be thy treasure, and precious silver unto thee.
018	JOB	022	026	For then shalt thou delight thyself in the Almighty, and shalt lift up thy face unto God.
018	JOB	022	027	Thou shalt make thy prayer unto him, and he shall hear thee; and thou shalt pay thy vows.
018	JOB	022	028	Thou shalt also decree a thing, and it shall be established unto thee; and light shall shine upon thy ways.
018	JOB	022	029	When they cast [thee] down, thou shalt say, [There is] lifting up; and the humble person he shall save.
018	JOB	022	030	He shall deliver [even] him that is not innocent: yea, he shall be delivered through the cleanness of thine hands.
018	JOB	023	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	023	002	Even today is my complaint rebellious: my stroke is heavier than my groaning.
018	JOB	023	003	Oh that I knew where I might find him, that I might come even to his seat!
018	JOB	023	004	I would order my cause before him, and fill my mouth with arguments.
018	JOB	023	005	I would know the words which he would answer me, and understand what he would say unto me.
018	JOB	023	006	Would he contend with me in the greatness of his power? Nay; but he would give heed unto me.
018	JOB	023	007	There the upright might reason with him; so should I be delivered for ever from my judge.
018	JOB	023	008	Behold, I go forward, but he is not [there]; and backward, but I cannot perceive him:
018	JOB	023	009	On the left hand, when he doth work, but I cannot behold him: he hideth himself on the right hand, that I cannot see him.
018	JOB	023	010	But he knoweth the way that I take; when he hath tried me, I shall come forth as gold.
018	JOB	023	011	My foot hath held fast to his steps; his way have I kept, and turned not aside.
018	JOB	023	012	I have not gone back from the commandment of his lips; I have treasured up the words of his mouth more than my necessary food.
018	JOB	023	013	But he is in one [mind], and who can turn him? and what his soul desireth, even that he doeth.
018	JOB	023	014	For he performeth that which is appointed for me: and many such things are with him.
018	JOB	023	015	Therefore am I troubled at his presence; when I consider, I am afraid of him.
018	JOB	023	016	For God hath made my heart faint, and the Almighty hath troubled me:
018	JOB	023	017	Because I was not cut off before the darkness, neither did he cover the thick darkness from my face.
018	JOB	024	001	Why are times not laid up by the Almighty? and why do not they which know him see his days?
018	JOB	024	002	There are that remove the landmarks; they violently take away flocks, and feed them.
018	JOB	024	003	They drive away the ass of the fatherless, they take the widow’s ox for a pledge.
018	JOB	024	004	They turn the needy out of the way: the poor of the earth hide themselves together.
018	JOB	024	005	Behold, as wild asses in the desert they go forth to their work, seeking diligently for meat; the wilderness [yieldeth] them food for their children.
018	JOB	024	006	They cut their provender in the field; and they glean the vintage of the wicked.
018	JOB	024	007	They lie all night naked without clothing, and have no covering in the cold.
018	JOB	024	008	They are wet with the showers of the mountains, and embrace the rock for want of a shelter.
018	JOB	024	009	There are that pluck the fatherless from the breast, and take a pledge of the poor:
018	JOB	024	010	[So that] they go about naked without clothing, and being an-hungred they carry the sheaves;
018	JOB	024	011	They make oil within the walls of these men; they tread [their] winepresses, and suffer thirst.
018	JOB	024	012	From out of the populous city men groan, and the soul of the wounded crieth out: yet God imputeth it not for folly.
018	JOB	024	013	These are of them that rebel against the light; they know not the ways thereof, nor abide in the paths thereof.
018	JOB	024	014	The murderer riseth with the light, he killeth the poor and needy; and in the night he is as a thief.
018	JOB	024	015	The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight, saying, No eye shall see me: and he disguiseth his face.
018	JOB	024	016	In the dark they dig through houses: they shut themselves up in the daytime; they know not the light.
018	JOB	024	017	For the morning is to all of them as the shadow of death; for they know the terrors of the shadow of death.
018	JOB	024	018	He is swift upon the face of the waters; their portion is cursed in the earth: he turneth not by the way of the vineyards.
018	JOB	024	019	Drought and heat consume the snow waters: [so doth] Sheol [those which] have sinned.
018	JOB	024	020	The womb shall forget him; the worm shall feed sweetly on him; he shall be no more remembered: and unrighteousness shall be broken as a tree.
018	JOB	024	021	He devoureth the barren that beareth not; and doeth not good to the widow.
018	JOB	024	022	He draweth away the mighty also by his power: he riseth up, and no man is sure of life.
018	JOB	024	023	[God] giveth them to be in security, and they rest thereon; and his eyes are upon their ways.
018	JOB	024	024	They are exalted; yet a little while, and they are gone; yea, they are brought low, they are taken out of the way as all other, and are cut off as the tops of the ears of corn.
018	JOB	024	025	And if it be not so now, who will prove me a liar, and make my speech nothing worth?
018	JOB	025	001	Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,
018	JOB	025	002	Dominion and fear are with him; he maketh peace in his high places.
018	JOB	025	003	Is there any number of his armies? and upon whom doth not his light arise?
018	JOB	025	004	How then can man be just with God? or how can he be clean that is born of a woman?
018	JOB	025	005	Behold, even the moon hath no brightness, and the stars are not pure in his sight:
018	JOB	025	006	How much less man, that is a worm! and the son of man, which is a worm!
018	JOB	026	001	Then Job answered and said,
018	JOB	026	002	How hast thou helped him that is without power! how hast thou saved the arm that hath no strength!
018	JOB	026	003	How hast thou counselled him that hath no wisdom, and plentifully declared sound knowledge!
018	JOB	026	004	To whom hast thou uttered words? and whose spirit came forth from thee?
018	JOB	026	005	They that are deceased tremble beneath the waters and the inhabitants thereof.
018	JOB	026	006	Sheol is naked before him, and Abaddon hath no covering.
018	JOB	026	007	He stretcheth out the north over empty space, and hangeth the earth upon nothing.
018	JOB	026	008	He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds; and the cloud is not rent under them.
018	JOB	026	009	He closeth in the face of his throne, and spreadeth his cloud upon it.
018	JOB	026	010	He hath described a boundary upon the face of the waters, unto the confines of light and darkness.
018	JOB	026	011	The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his rebuke.
018	JOB	026	012	He stirreth up the sea with his power, and by his understanding he smiteth through Rahab.
018	JOB	026	013	By his spirit the heavens are garnished; his hand hath pierced the swift serpent.
018	JOB	026	014	Lo, these are but the outskirts of his ways: and how small a whisper do we hear of him! but the thunder of his power who can understand?
018	JOB	027	001	And Job again took up his parable, and said,
018	JOB	027	002	As God liveth, who hath taken away my right; and the Almighty, who hath vexed my soul;
018	JOB	027	003	(For my life is yet whole in me, and the spirit of God is in my nostrils;)
018	JOB	027	004	Surely my lips shall not speak unrighteousness, neither shall my tongue utter deceit.
018	JOB	027	005	God forbid that I should justify you: till I die I will not put away mine integrity from me.
018	JOB	027	006	My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach [me] so long as I live.
018	JOB	027	007	Let mine enemy be as the wicked, and let him that riseth up against me be as the unrighteous.
018	JOB	027	008	For what is the hope of the godless, though he get him gain, when God taketh away his soul?
018	JOB	027	009	Will God hear his cry, when trouble cometh upon him?
018	JOB	027	010	Will he delight himself in the Almighty, and call upon God at all times?
018	JOB	027	011	I will teach you concerning the hand of God; that which is with the Almighty will I not conceal.
018	JOB	027	012	Behold, all ye yourselves have seen it; why then are ye become altogether vain?
018	JOB	027	013	This is the portion of a wicked man with God, and the heritage of oppressors, which they receive from the Almighty.
018	JOB	027	014	If his children be multiplied, it is for the sword; and his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread.
018	JOB	027	015	Those that remain of him shall be buried in death, and his widows shall make no lamentation.
018	JOB	027	016	Though he heap up silver as the dust, and prepare raiment as the clay;
018	JOB	027	017	He may prepare it, but the just shall put it on, and the innocent shall divide the silver.
018	JOB	027	018	He buildeth his house as the moth, and as a booth which the keeper maketh.
018	JOB	027	019	He lieth down rich, but he shall not be gathered; he openeth his eyes, and he is not.
018	JOB	027	020	Terrors overtake him like waters; a tempest stealeth him away in the night.
018	JOB	027	021	The east wind carrieth him away, and he departeth; and it sweepeth him out of his place.
018	JOB	027	022	For [God] shall hurl at him, and not spare: he would fain flee out of his hand.
018	JOB	027	023	Men shall clap their hands at him, and shall hiss him out of his place.
018	JOB	028	001	Surely there is a mine for silver, and a place for gold which they refine.
018	JOB	028	002	Iron is taken out of the earth, and brass is molten out of the stone.
018	JOB	028	003	[Man] setteth an end to darkness, and searcheth out to the furthest bound the stones of thick darkness and of the shadow of death.
018	JOB	028	004	He breaketh open a shaft away from where men sojourn; they are forgotten of the foot [that passeth by]; they hang afar from men, they swing to and fro.
018	JOB	028	005	As for the earth, out of it cometh bread: and underneath it is turned up as it were by fire.
018	JOB	028	006	The stones thereof are the place of sapphires, and it hath dust of gold.
018	JOB	028	007	That path no bird of prey knoweth, neither hath the falcon’s eye seen it:
018	JOB	028	008	The proud beasts have not trodden it, nor hath the fierce lion passed thereby.
018	JOB	028	009	He putteth forth his hand upon the flinty rock; he overturneth the mountains by the roots.
018	JOB	028	010	He cutteth out channels among the rocks; and his eye seeth every precious thing.
018	JOB	028	011	He bindeth the streams that they trickle not; and the thing that is hid bringeth he forth to light.
018	JOB	028	012	But where shall wisdom be found? and where is the place of understanding?
018	JOB	028	013	Man knoweth not the price thereof; neither is it found in the land of the living.
018	JOB	028	014	The deep saith, It is not in me: and the sea saith, It is not with me.
018	JOB	028	015	It cannot be gotten for gold, neither shall silver be weighed for the price thereof.
018	JOB	028	016	It cannot be valued with the gold of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or the sapphire.
018	JOB	028	017	Gold and glass cannot equal it: neither shall the exchange thereof be jewels of fine gold.
018	JOB	028	018	No mention shall be made of coral or of crystal: yea, the price of wisdom is above rubies.
018	JOB	028	019	The topaz of Ethiopia shall not equal it, neither shall it be valued with pure gold.
018	JOB	028	020	Whence then cometh wisdom? and where is the place of understanding?
018	JOB	028	021	Seeing it is hid from the eyes of all living, and kept close from the fowls of the air.
018	JOB	028	022	Destruction and Death say, We have heard a rumour thereof with our ears.
018	JOB	028	023	God understandeth the way thereof, and he knoweth the place thereof.
018	JOB	028	024	For he looketh to the ends of the earth, and seeth under the whole heaven;
018	JOB	028	025	To make a weight for the wind; yea, he meteth out the waters by measure.
018	JOB	028	026	When he made a decree for the rain, and a way for the lightning of the thunder:
018	JOB	028	027	Then did he see it, and declare it; he established it, yea, and searched it out.
018	JOB	028	028	And unto man he said, Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom; and to depart from evil is understanding.
018	JOB	029	001	And Job again took up his parable, and said,
018	JOB	029	002	Oh that I were as in the months of old, as in the days when God watched over me;
018	JOB	029	003	When his lamp shined upon my head, and by his light I walked through darkness;
018	JOB	029	004	As I was in the ripeness of my days, when the secret of God was upon my tent;
018	JOB	029	005	When the Almighty was yet with me, and my children were about me;
018	JOB	029	006	When my steps were washed with butter, and the rock poured me out rivers of oil!
018	JOB	029	007	When I went forth to the gate unto the city, when I prepared my seat in the street,
018	JOB	029	008	The young men saw me and hid themselves, and the aged rose up and stood;
018	JOB	029	009	The princes refrained talking, and laid their hand on their mouth;
018	JOB	029	010	The voice of the nobles was hushed, and their tongue cleaved to the roof of their mouth.
018	JOB	029	011	For when the ear heard [me], then it blessed me; and when the eye saw [me], it gave witness unto me:
018	JOB	029	012	Because I delivered the poor that cried, the fatherless also, that had none to help him.
018	JOB	029	013	The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me: and I caused the widow’s heart to sing for joy.
018	JOB	029	014	I put on righteousness, and it clothed me: my justice was as a robe and a diadem.
018	JOB	029	015	I was eyes to the blind, and feet was I to the lame.
018	JOB	029	016	I was a father to the needy: and the cause of him that I knew not I searched out.
018	JOB	029	017	And I brake the jaws of the unrighteous, and plucked the prey out of his teeth.
018	JOB	029	018	Then I said, I shall die in my nest, and I shall multiply my days as the sand:
018	JOB	029	019	My root is spread out to the waters, and the dew lieth all night upon my branch:
018	JOB	029	020	My glory is fresh in me, and my bow is renewed in my hand.
018	JOB	029	021	Unto me men gave ear, and waited, and kept silence for my counsel.
018	JOB	029	022	After my words they spake not again; and my speech dropped upon them.
018	JOB	029	023	And they waited for me as for the rain; and they opened their mouth wide as for the latter rain.
018	JOB	029	024	If I laughed on them, they believed [it] not; and the light of my countenance they cast not down.
018	JOB	029	025	I chose out their way, and sat [as] chief, and dwelt as a king in the army, as one that comforteth the mourners.
018	JOB	030	001	But now they that are younger than I have me in derision, whose fathers I disdained to set with the dogs of my flock.
018	JOB	030	002	Yea, the strength of their hands, whereto should it profit me? men in whom ripe age is perished.
018	JOB	030	003	They are gaunt with want and famine; they gnaw the dry ground; in the gloom of wasteness and desolation.
018	JOB	030	004	They pluck salt-wort by the bushes; and the roots of the broom [are] their meat.
018	JOB	030	005	They are driven forth from the midst [of men]; they cry after them as after a thief.
018	JOB	030	006	In the clefts of the valleys must they dwell, in holes of the earth and of the rocks.
018	JOB	030	007	Among the bushes they bray; under the nettles they are gathered together.
018	JOB	030	008	[They are] children of fools, yea, children of base men; they were scourged out of the land.
018	JOB	030	009	And now I am become their song, yea, I am a byword unto them.
018	JOB	030	010	They abhor me, they stand aloof from me, and spare not to spit in my face.
018	JOB	030	011	For he hath loosed his cord, and afflicted me, and they have cast off the bridle before me.
018	JOB	030	012	Upon my right hand rise the rabble; they thrust aside my feet, and they cast up against me their ways of destruction.
018	JOB	030	013	They mar my path, they set forward my calamity, [even] men that have no helper.
018	JOB	030	014	As through a wide breach they come: in the midst of the ruin they roll themselves [upon me].
018	JOB	030	015	Terrors are turned upon me, they chase mine honour as the wind; and my welfare is passed away as a cloud.
018	JOB	030	016	And now my soul is poured out within me; days of affliction have taken hold upon me.
018	JOB	030	017	In the night season my bones are pierced in me, and the [pains] that gnaw me take no rest.
018	JOB	030	018	By the great force [of my disease] is my garment disfigured: it bindeth me about as the collar of my coat.
018	JOB	030	019	He hath cast me into the mire, and I am become like dust and ashes.
018	JOB	030	020	I cry unto thee, and thou dost not answer me: I stand up, and thou lookest at me.
018	JOB	030	021	Thou art turned to be cruel to me: with the might of thy hand thou persecutest me.
018	JOB	030	022	Thou liftest me up to the wind, thou causest me to ride [upon it]; and thou dissolvest me in the storm.
018	JOB	030	023	For I know that thou wilt bring me to death, and to the house appointed for all living.
018	JOB	030	024	Surely against a ruinous heap he will not put forth his hand; though [it be] in his destruction, [one may utter] a cry because of these things.
018	JOB	030	025	Did not I weep for him that was in trouble? was not my soul grieved for the needy?
018	JOB	030	026	When I looked for good, then evil came; and when I waited for light, there came darkness.
018	JOB	030	027	My bowels boil, and rest not; days of affliction are come upon me.
018	JOB	030	028	I go mourning without the sun: I stand up in the assembly, and cry for help.
018	JOB	030	029	I am a brother to jackals, and a companion to ostriches.
018	JOB	030	030	My skin is black, [and falleth] from me, and my bones are burned with heat.
018	JOB	030	031	Therefore is my harp [turned] to mourning, and my pipe into the voice of them that weep.
018	JOB	031	001	I MADE a covenant with mine eyes; how then should I look upon a maid?
018	JOB	031	002	For what [is] the portion of God from above, and the heritage of the Almighty from on high?
018	JOB	031	003	Is it not calamity to the unrighteous, and disaster to the workers of iniquity?
018	JOB	031	004	Doth not he see my ways, and number all my steps?
018	JOB	031	005	If I have walked with vanity, and my foot hath hasted to deceit;
018	JOB	031	006	(Let me be weighed in an even balance, that God may know mine integrity;)
018	JOB	031	007	If my step hath turned out of the way, and mine heart walked after mine eyes, and if any spot hath cleaved to mine hands:
018	JOB	031	008	Then let me sow, and let another eat; yea, let the produce of my field be rooted out.
018	JOB	031	009	If mine heart have been enticed unto a woman, and I have laid wait at my neighbour’s door:
018	JOB	031	010	Then let my wife grind unto another, and let others bow down upon her.
018	JOB	031	011	For that were an heinous crime; yea, it were an iniquity to be punished by the judges:
018	JOB	031	012	For it is a fire that consumeth unto Destruction, and would root out all mine increase.
018	JOB	031	013	If I did despise the cause of my manservant or of my maidservant, when they contended with me:
018	JOB	031	014	What then shall I do when God riseth up? and when he visiteth, what shall I answer him?
018	JOB	031	015	Did not he that made me in the womb make him? and did not one fashion us in the womb?
018	JOB	031	016	If I have withheld the poor from [their] desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail;
018	JOB	031	017	Or have eaten my morsel alone, and the fatherless hath not eaten thereof;
018	JOB	031	018	(Nay, from my youth he grew up with me as with a father, and I have been her guide from my mother’s womb;)
018	JOB	031	019	If I have seen any perish for want of clothing, or that the needy had no covering;
018	JOB	031	020	If his loins have not blessed me, and if he were not warmed with the fleece of my sheep;
018	JOB	031	021	If I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, because I saw my help in the gate:
018	JOB	031	022	Then let my shoulder fall from the shoulder blade, and mine arm be broken from the bone.
018	JOB	031	023	For calamity from God was a terror to me, and by reason of his excellency I could do nothing.
018	JOB	031	024	If I have made gold my hope, and have said to the fine gold, [Thou art] my confidence;
018	JOB	031	025	If I rejoiced because my wealth was great, and because mine hand had gotten much;
018	JOB	031	026	If I beheld the sun when it shined, or the moon walking in brightness;
018	JOB	031	027	And my heart hath been secretly enticed, and my mouth hath kissed my hand:
018	JOB	031	028	This also were an iniquity to be punished by the judges: for I should have lied to God that is above.
018	JOB	031	029	If I rejoiced at the destruction of him that hated me, or lifted up myself when evil found him;
018	JOB	031	030	(Yea, I suffered not my mouth to sin by asking his life with a curse;)
018	JOB	031	031	If the men of my tent said not, Who can find one that hath not been satisfied with his flesh?
018	JOB	031	032	The stranger did not lodge in the street; but I opened my doors to the traveller;
018	JOB	031	033	If like Adam I covered my transgressions, by hiding mine iniquity in my bosom;
018	JOB	031	034	Because I feared the great multitude, and the contempt of families terrified me, so that I kept silence, and went not out of the door—
018	JOB	031	035	Oh that I had one to hear me! (lo, here is my signature, let the Almighty answer me;) and [that I had] the indictment which mine adversary hath written!
018	JOB	031	036	Surely I would carry it upon my shoulder; I would bind it unto me as a crown.
018	JOB	031	037	I would declare unto him the number of my steps; as a prince would I go near unto him.
018	JOB	031	038	If my land cry out against me, and the furrows thereof weep together;
018	JOB	031	039	If I have eaten the fruits thereof without money, or have caused the owners thereof to lose their life:
018	JOB	031	040	Let thistles grow instead of wheat, and cockle instead of barley. The words of Job are ended.
018	JOB	032	001	So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.
018	JOB	032	002	Then was kindled the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite, of the family of Ram: against Job was his wrath kindled, because he justified himself rather than God.
018	JOB	032	003	Also against his three friends was his wrath kindled, because they had found no answer, and yet had condemned Job.
018	JOB	032	004	Now Elihu had waited to speak unto Job, because they were elder than he.
018	JOB	032	005	And when Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of these three men, his wrath was kindled.
018	JOB	032	006	And Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said, I am young, and ye are very old; wherefore I held back, and durst not shew you mine opinion.
018	JOB	032	007	I said, Days should speak, and multitude of years should teach wisdom.
018	JOB	032	008	But there is a spirit in man, and the breath of the Almighty giveth them understanding.
018	JOB	032	009	It is not the great that are wise, nor the aged that understand judgment.
018	JOB	032	010	Therefore I said, Hearken to me; I also will shew mine opinion.
018	JOB	032	011	Behold, I waited for your words, I listened for your reasons, whilst ye searched out what to say.
018	JOB	032	012	Yea, I attended unto you, and, behold, there was none that convinced Job, or that answered his words, among you.
018	JOB	032	013	Beware lest ye say, We have found wisdom; God may vanquish him, not man:
018	JOB	032	014	For he hath not directed his words against me; neither will I answer him with your speeches.
018	JOB	032	015	They are amazed, they answer no more: they have not a word to say.
018	JOB	032	016	And shall I wait, because they speak not, because they stand still, and answer no more?
018	JOB	032	017	I also will answer my part, I also will shew mine opinion.
018	JOB	032	018	For I am full of words; the spirit within me constraineth me.
018	JOB	032	019	Behold, my belly is as wine which hath no vent; like new bottles it is ready to burst.
018	JOB	032	020	I will speak, that I may be refreshed; I will open my lips and answer.
018	JOB	032	021	Let me not, I pray you, respect any man’s person; neither will I give flattering titles unto any man.
018	JOB	032	022	For I know not to give flattering titles; [else] would my Maker soon take me away.
018	JOB	033	001	Howbeit, Job, I pray thee, hear my speech, and hearken to all my words.
018	JOB	033	002	Behold now, I have opened my mouth, my tongue hath spoken in my mouth.
018	JOB	033	003	My words [shall utter] the uprightness of my heart: and that which my lips know they shall speak sincerely.
018	JOB	033	004	The spirit of God hath made me, and the breath of the Almighty giveth me life.
018	JOB	033	005	If thou canst, answer thou me; set [thy words] in order before me, stand forth.
018	JOB	033	006	Behold, I am toward God even as thou art: I also am formed out of the clay.
018	JOB	033	007	Behold, my terror shall not make thee afraid, neither shall my pressure be heavy upon thee.
018	JOB	033	008	Surely thou hast spoken in mine hearing, and I have heard the voice of [thy] words, [saying],
018	JOB	033	009	I am clean, without transgression; I am innocent, neither is there iniquity in me:
018	JOB	033	010	Behold, he findeth occasions against me, he counteth me for his enemy;
018	JOB	033	011	He putteth my feet in the stocks, he marketh all my paths.
018	JOB	033	012	Behold, I will answer thee, in this thou art not just; for God is greater than man.
018	JOB	033	013	Why dost thou strive against him? for he giveth not account of any of his matters.
018	JOB	033	014	For God speaketh once, yea twice, [though man] regardeth it not.
018	JOB	033	015	In a dream, in a vision of the night, when deep sleep falleth upon men, in slumberings upon the bed;
018	JOB	033	016	Then he openeth the ears of men, and sealeth their instruction,
018	JOB	033	017	That he may withdraw man [from his] purpose, and hide pride from man;
018	JOB	033	018	He keepeth back his soul from the pit, and his life from perishing by the sword.
018	JOB	033	019	He is chastened also with pain upon his bed, and with continual strife in his bones:
018	JOB	033	020	So that his life abhorreth bread, and his soul dainty meat.
018	JOB	033	021	His flesh is consumed away, that it cannot be seen; and his bones that were not seen stick out.
018	JOB	033	022	Yea, his soul draweth near unto the pit, and his life to the destroyers.
018	JOB	033	023	If there be with him an angel, an interpreter, one among a thousand, to shew unto man what is right for him;
018	JOB	033	024	Then he is gracious unto him, and saith, Deliver him from going down to the pit, I have found a ransom.
018	JOB	033	025	His flesh shall be fresher than a child’s; he returneth to the days of his youth:
018	JOB	033	026	He prayeth unto God, and he is favourable unto him; so that he seeth his face with joy: and he restoreth unto man his righteousness.
018	JOB	033	027	He singeth before men, and saith, I have sinned, and perverted that which was right, and it profited me not:
018	JOB	033	028	He hath redeemed my soul from going into the pit, and my life shall behold the light.
018	JOB	033	029	Lo, all these things doth God work, twice, [yea] thrice, with a man,
018	JOB	033	030	To bring back his soul from the pit, that he may be enlightened with the light of the living.
018	JOB	033	031	Mark well, O Job, hearken unto me: hold thy peace, and I will speak.
018	JOB	033	032	If thou hast any thing to say, answer me: speak, for I desire to justify thee.
018	JOB	033	033	If not, hearken thou unto me: hold thy peace, and I will teach thee wisdom.
018	JOB	034	001	Moreover Elihu answered and said,
018	JOB	034	002	Hear my words, ye wise men; and give ear unto me, ye that have knowledge.
018	JOB	034	003	For the ear trieth words, as the palate tasteth meat.
018	JOB	034	004	Let us choose for us that which is right: let us know among ourselves what is good.
018	JOB	034	005	For Job hath said, I am righteous, and God hath taken away my right:
018	JOB	034	006	Notwithstanding my right I am [accounted] a liar; my wound is incurable, [though I am] without transgression.
018	JOB	034	007	What man is like Job, who drinketh up scorning like water?
018	JOB	034	008	Which goeth in company with the workers of iniquity, and walketh with wicked men.
018	JOB	034	009	For he hath said, it profiteth a man nothing that he should delight himself with God.
018	JOB	034	010	Therefore hearken unto me, ye men of understanding: far be it from God, that he should do wickedness; and from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity.
018	JOB	034	011	For the work of a man shall he render unto him, and cause every man to find according to his ways.
018	JOB	034	012	Yea, of a surety, God will not do wickedly, neither will the Almighty pervert judgment.
018	JOB	034	013	Who gave him a charge over the earth? or who hath disposed the whole world?
018	JOB	034	014	If he set his heart upon man, [if] he gather unto himself his spirit and his breath;
018	JOB	034	015	All flesh shall perish together, and man shall turn again unto dust.
018	JOB	034	016	If now [thou hast] understanding, hear this: hearken to the voice of my words.
018	JOB	034	017	Shall even one that hateth right govern? and wilt thou condemn him that is just [and] mighty?
018	JOB	034	018	Is it [fit] to say to a king, [Thou art] vile? [or] to nobles, [Ye are] wicked?
018	JOB	034	019	[How much less to] him that respecteth not the persons of princes, nor regardeth the rich more than the poor? for they all are the work of his hands.
018	JOB	034	020	In a moment they die, even at midnight; the people are shaken and pass away, and the mighty are taken away without hand.
018	JOB	034	021	For his eyes are upon the ways of a man, and he seeth all his goings.
018	JOB	034	022	There is no darkness, nor shadow of death, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.
018	JOB	034	023	For he needeth not further to consider a man, that he should go before God in judgment.
018	JOB	034	024	He breaketh in pieces mighty men [in ways] past finding out, and setteth others in their stead.
018	JOB	034	025	Therefore he taketh knowledge of their works; and he overturneth them in the night, so that they are destroyed.
018	JOB	034	026	He striketh them as wicked men in the open sight of others;
018	JOB	034	027	Because they turned aside from following him, and would not have regard to any of his ways:
018	JOB	034	028	So that they caused the cry of the poor to come unto him, and he heard the cry of the afflicted.
018	JOB	034	029	When he giveth quietness, who then can condemn? and when he hideth his face, who then can behold him? whether [it be done] unto a nation, or unto a man, alike:
018	JOB	034	030	That the godless man reign not, that there be none to ensnare the people.
018	JOB	034	031	For hath any said unto God, I have borne [chastisement], I will not offend [any more]:
018	JOB	034	032	That which I see not teach thou me: if I have done iniquity, I will do it no more?
018	JOB	034	033	Shall his recompence be as thou wilt, that thou refusest it? for thou must choose, and not I: therefore speak what thou knowest.
018	JOB	034	034	Men of understanding will say unto me, yea, every wise man that heareth me:
018	JOB	034	035	Job speaketh without knowledge, and his words are without wisdom.
018	JOB	034	036	Would that Job were tried unto the end, because of his answering like wicked men.
018	JOB	034	037	For he addeth rebellion unto his sin, he clappeth his hands among us, and multiplieth his words against God.
018	JOB	035	001	Moreover Elihu answered and said,
018	JOB	035	002	Thinkest thou this to be [thy] right, [or] sayest thou, My righteousness is more than God’s,
018	JOB	035	003	That thou sayest, What advantage will it be unto thee? [and], What profit shall I have, more than if I had sinned?
018	JOB	035	004	I will answer thee, and thy companions with thee.
018	JOB	035	005	Look unto the heavens, and see; and behold the skies, which are higher than thou.
018	JOB	035	006	If thou hast sinned, what doest thou against him? and if thy transgressions be multiplied, what doest thou unto him.
018	JOB	035	007	If thou be righteous, what givest thou him? or what receiveth he of thine hand?
018	JOB	035	008	Thy wickedness [may hurt] a man as thou art; and thy righteousness [may profit] a son of man.
018	JOB	035	009	By reason of the multitude of oppressions they cry out; they cry for help by reason of the arm of the mighty.
018	JOB	035	010	But none saith, Where is God my Maker, who giveth songs in the night;
018	JOB	035	011	Who teacheth us more than the beasts of the earth, and maketh us wiser than the fowls of heaven?
018	JOB	035	012	There they cry, but none giveth answer, because of the pride of evil men.
018	JOB	035	013	Surely God will not hear vanity, neither will the Almighty regard it.
018	JOB	035	014	How much less when thou sayest thou beholdest him not, the cause is before him, and thou waitest for him!
018	JOB	035	015	But now, because he hath not visited in his anger, neither doth he greatly regard arrogance;
018	JOB	035	016	Therefore doth Job open his mouth in vanity; he multiplieth words without knowledge.
018	JOB	036	001	Elihu also proceeded, and said,
018	JOB	036	002	Suffer me a little, and I will shew thee: for I have yet somewhat to say on God’s behalf.
018	JOB	036	003	I will fetch my knowledge from afar, and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker.
018	JOB	036	004	For truly my words are not false: one that is perfect in knowledge is with thee.
018	JOB	036	005	Behold, God is mighty, and despiseth not any: he is mighty in strength of understanding.
018	JOB	036	006	He preserveth not the life of the wicked: but giveth to the afflicted [their] right.
018	JOB	036	007	He withdraweth not his eyes from the righteous: but with kings upon the throne he setteth them for ever, and they are exalted.
018	JOB	036	008	And if they be bound in fetters, and be taken in the cords of affliction;
018	JOB	036	009	Then he sheweth them their work, and their transgressions, that they have behaved themselves proudly.
018	JOB	036	010	He openeth also their ear to instruction, and commandeth that they return from iniquity.
018	JOB	036	011	If they hearken and serve [him], they shall spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures.
018	JOB	036	012	But if they hearken not, they shall perish by the sword, and they shall die without knowledge.
018	JOB	036	013	But they that are godless in heart lay up anger: they cry not for help when he bindeth them.
018	JOB	036	014	They die in youth, and their life [perisheth] among the unclean.
018	JOB	036	015	He delivereth the afflicted by his affliction, and openeth their ear in oppression.
018	JOB	036	016	Yea, he would have led thee away out of distress into a broad place, where there is no straitness; and that which is set on thy table should be full of fatness.
018	JOB	036	017	But thou art full of the judgment of the wicked: judgment and justice take hold [on thee].
018	JOB	036	018	Because there is wrath, beware lest thou be led away by [thy] sufficiency; neither let the greatness of the ransom turn thee aside.
018	JOB	036	019	Will thy riches suffice, [that thou be] not in distress, or all the forces of [thy] strength?
018	JOB	036	020	Desire not the night, when peoples are cut off in their place.
018	JOB	036	021	Take heed, regard not iniquity: for this hast thou chosen rather than affliction.
018	JOB	036	022	Behold, God doeth loftily in his power: who is a teacher like unto him?
018	JOB	036	023	Who hath enjoined him his way? or who can say, Thou hast wrought unrighteousness?
018	JOB	036	024	Remember that thou magnify his work, whereof men have sung.
018	JOB	036	025	All men have looked thereon; man beholdeth it afar off.
018	JOB	036	026	Behold, God is great, and we know him not; the number of his years is unsearchable.
018	JOB	036	027	For he draweth up the drops of water, which distil in rain from his vapour:
018	JOB	036	028	Which the skies pour down and drop upon man abundantly.
018	JOB	036	029	Yea, can any understand the spreadings of the clouds, the thunderings of his pavilion?
018	JOB	036	030	Behold, he spreadeth his light around him; and he covereth the bottom of the sea.
018	JOB	036	031	For by these he judgeth the peoples; he giveth meat in abundance.
018	JOB	036	032	He covereth his hands with the lightning; and giveth it a charge that it strike the mark.
018	JOB	036	033	The noise thereof telleth concerning him, the cattle also concerning [the storm] that cometh up.
018	JOB	037	001	At this also my heart trembleth, and is moved out of its place.
018	JOB	037	002	Hearken ye unto the noise of his voice, and the sound that goeth out of his mouth.
018	JOB	037	003	He sendeth it forth under the whole heaven, and his lightning unto the ends of the earth.
018	JOB	037	004	After it a voice roareth; he thundereth with the voice of his majesty: and he stayeth them not when his voice is heard.
018	JOB	037	005	God thundereth marvelously with his voice; great things doeth he, which we cannot comprehend.
018	JOB	037	006	For he saith to the snow, Fall thou on the earth; likewise to the shower of rain, and to the showers of his mighty rain.
018	JOB	037	007	He sealeth up the hand of every man; that all men whom he hath made may know [it].
018	JOB	037	008	Then the beasts go into coverts, and remain in their dens.
018	JOB	037	009	Out of the chamber [of the south] cometh the storm: and cold out of the north.
018	JOB	037	010	By the breath of God ice is given: and the breadth of the waters is straitened.
018	JOB	037	011	Yea, he ladeth the thick cloud with moisture; he spreadeth abroad the cloud of his lightning:
018	JOB	037	012	And it is turned round about by his guidance, that they may do whatsoever he commandeth them upon the face of the habitable world.
018	JOB	037	013	Whether it be for correction, or for his land, or for mercy, that he cause it to come.
018	JOB	037	014	Hearken unto this, O Job: stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God.
018	JOB	037	015	Dost thou know how God layeth [his charge] upon them, and causeth the lightning of his cloud to shine?
018	JOB	037	016	Dost thou know the balancings of the clouds, the wondrous works of him which is perfect in knowledge?
018	JOB	037	017	How thy garments are warm, when the earth is still by reason of the south [wind]?
018	JOB	037	018	Canst thou with him spread out the sky, which is strong as a molten mirror?
018	JOB	037	019	Teach us what we shall say unto him; [for] we cannot order [our speech] by reason of darkness.
018	JOB	037	020	Shall it be told him that I would speak? or should a man wish that he were swallowed up?
018	JOB	037	021	And now men see not the light which is bright in the skies: but the wind passeth, and cleanseth them.
018	JOB	037	022	Out of the north cometh golden splendour: God hath upon him terrible majesty.
018	JOB	037	023	[Touching] the Almighty, we can not find him out; he is excellent in power: and in judgment and plenteous justice he will not afflict.
018	JOB	037	024	Men do therefore fear him: he regardeth not any that are wise of heart.
018	JOB	038	001	Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,
018	JOB	038	002	Who is this that darkeneth counsel by words without knowledge?
018	JOB	038	003	Gird up now thy loins like a man; for I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.
018	JOB	038	004	Where wast thou when I laid the foundations of the earth? declare, if thou hast understanding.
018	JOB	038	005	Who determined the measures thereof, if thou knowest? or who stretched the line upon it?
018	JOB	038	006	Whereupon were the foundations thereof fastened? or who laid the corner stone thereof;
018	JOB	038	007	When the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy?
018	JOB	038	008	[Or who] shut up the sea with doors, when it brake forth, [as if] it had issued out of the womb;
018	JOB	038	009	When I made the cloud the garment thereof, and thick darkness a swaddlingband for it,
018	JOB	038	010	And prescribed for it my decree, and set bars and doors,
018	JOB	038	011	And said, Hitherto shalt thou come, but no further; and here shall thy proud waves be stayed?
018	JOB	038	012	Hast thou commanded the morning since thy days [began, and] caused the dayspring to know its place;
018	JOB	038	013	That it might take hold of the ends of the earth, and the wicked be shaken out of it?
018	JOB	038	014	It is changed as clay under the seal; and [all things] stand forth as a garment:
018	JOB	038	015	And from the wicked their light is withholden, and the high arm is broken.
018	JOB	038	016	Hast thou entered into the springs of the sea? or hast thou walked in the recesses of the deep?
018	JOB	038	017	Have the gates of death been revealed unto thee? or hast thou seen the gates of the shadow of death?
018	JOB	038	018	Hast thou comprehended the breadth of the earth? declare, if thou knowest it all.
018	JOB	038	019	Where is the way to the dwelling of light, and as for darkness, where is the place thereof;
018	JOB	038	020	That thou shouldest take it to the bound thereof, and that thou shouldest discern the paths to the house thereof?
018	JOB	038	021	[Doubtless], thou knowest, for thou wast then born, and the number of thy days is great!
018	JOB	038	022	Hast thou entered the treasuries of the snow, or hast thou seen the treasuries of the hail,
018	JOB	038	023	Which I have reserved against the time of trouble, against the day of battle and war?
018	JOB	038	024	By what way is the light parted, or the east wind scattered upon the earth?
018	JOB	038	025	Who hath cleft a channel for the waterflood, or a way for the lightning of the thunder;
018	JOB	038	026	To cause it to rain on a land where no man is; on the wilderness, wherein there is no man;
018	JOB	038	027	To satisfy the waste and desolate [ground]; and to cause the tender grass to spring forth?
018	JOB	038	028	Hath the rain a father? or who hath begotten the drops of dew?
018	JOB	038	029	Out of whose womb came the ice? and the hoary frost of heaven, who hath gendered it?
018	JOB	038	030	The waters are hidden as [with] stone, and the face of the deep is frozen.
018	JOB	038	031	Canst thou bind the cluster of the Pleiades, or loose the bands of Orion?
018	JOB	038	032	Canst thou lead forth the Mazzaroth in their season? or canst thou guide the Bear with her train?
018	JOB	038	033	Knowest thou the ordinances of the heavens? canst thou establish the dominion thereof in the earth?
018	JOB	038	034	Canst thou lift up thy voice to the clouds, that abundance of waters may cover thee?
018	JOB	038	035	Canst thou send forth lightnings, that they may go, and say unto thee, Here we are?
018	JOB	038	036	Who hath put wisdom in the inward parts? or who hath given understanding to the mind?
018	JOB	038	037	Who can number the clouds by wisdom? or who can pour out the bottles of heaven,
018	JOB	038	038	When the dust runneth into a mass, and the clods cleave fast together?
018	JOB	038	039	Wilt thou hunt the prey for the lioness? or satisfy the appetite of the young lions,
018	JOB	038	040	When they couch in their dens, [and] abide in the covert to lie in wait?
018	JOB	038	041	Who provideth for the raven his food, when his young ones cry unto God, [and] wander for lack of meat?
018	JOB	039	001	Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? [or] canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?
018	JOB	039	002	Canst thou number the months that they fulfill? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?
018	JOB	039	003	They bow themselves, they bring forth their young, they cast out their sorrows.
018	JOB	039	004	Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up in the open field; they go forth, and return not again,
018	JOB	039	005	Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?
018	JOB	039	006	Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the salt land his dwelling place.
018	JOB	039	007	He scorneth the tumult of the city, neither heareth he the shoutings of the driver.
018	JOB	039	008	The range of the mountains is his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.
018	JOB	039	009	Will the wild-ox be content to serve thee? or will he abide by thy crib?
018	JOB	039	010	Canst thou bind the wild-ox with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?
018	JOB	039	011	Wilt thou trust him, because his strength is great? or wilt thou leave to him thy labour?
018	JOB	039	012	Wilt thou confide in him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather [the corn of] thy threshingfloor?
018	JOB	039	013	The wing of the ostrich rejoiceth, [but] are her pinions and feathers kindly?
018	JOB	039	014	For she leaveth her eggs on the earth, and warmeth them in the dust,
018	JOB	039	015	And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may trample them.
018	JOB	039	016	She is hardened against her young ones, as if they were not hers: though her labour be in vain, [she is] without fear;
018	JOB	039	017	Because God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.
018	JOB	039	018	What time she lifteth up herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.
018	JOB	039	019	Hast thou given the horse [his] might? hast thou clothed his neck with the quivering mane?
018	JOB	039	020	Hast thou made him to leap as a locust? the glory of his snorting is terrible.
018	JOB	039	021	He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in his strength: he goeth out to meet the armed men.
018	JOB	039	022	He mocketh at fear, and is not dismayed; neither turneth he back from the sword.
018	JOB	039	023	The quiver rattleth against him, the flashing spear and the javelin.
018	JOB	039	024	He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage; neither believeth he that it is the voice of the trumpet.
018	JOB	039	025	As oft as the trumpet [soundeth] he saith, Aha! and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.
018	JOB	039	026	Doth the hawk soar by thy wisdom, [and] stretch her wings toward the south?
018	JOB	039	027	Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?
018	JOB	039	028	She dwelleth on the rock, and hath her lodging [there], upon the crag of the rock, and the strong hold.
018	JOB	039	029	From thence she spieth out the prey; her eyes behold it afar off.
018	JOB	039	030	Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain are, there is she.
018	JOB	040	001	Moreover the LORD answered Job, and said,
018	JOB	040	002	Shall he that cavilleth contend with the Almighty? he that argueth with God, let him answer it.
018	JOB	040	003	Then Job answered the LORD, and said,
018	JOB	040	004	Behold, I am of small account; what shall I answer thee? I lay mine hand upon my mouth.
018	JOB	040	005	Once have I spoken, and I will not answer; yea twice, but I will proceed no further.
018	JOB	040	006	Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,
018	JOB	040	007	Gird up thy loins now like a man: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.
018	JOB	040	008	Wilt thou even disannul my judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be justified?
018	JOB	040	009	Or hast thou an arm like God? and canst thou thunder with a voice like him?
018	JOB	040	010	Deck thyself now with excellency and dignity; and array thyself with honour and majesty.
018	JOB	040	011	Pour forth the overflowings of thine anger: and look upon every one that is proud, and abase him.
018	JOB	040	012	Look on every one that is proud, [and] bring him low; and tread down the wicked where they stand.
018	JOB	040	013	Hide them in the dust together; bind their faces in the hidden [place].
018	JOB	040	014	Then wilt I also confess of thee that thine own right hand can save thee.
018	JOB	040	015	Behold now behemoth, which I made with thee; he eateth grass as all ox.
018	JOB	040	016	Lo now, his strength is in his loins, and his force is in the muscles of his belly.
018	JOB	040	017	He moveth his tail like a cedar: the sinews of his thighs are knit together.
018	JOB	040	018	His bones are as tubes of brass; his limbs are like bars of iron.
018	JOB	040	019	He is the chief of the ways of God: he [only] that made him can make his sword to approach [unto him].
018	JOB	040	020	Surely the mountains bring him forth food; where all the beasts of the field do play.
018	JOB	040	021	He lieth under the lotus trees, in the covert of the reed, and the fen.
018	JOB	040	022	The lotus trees cover him with their shadow; the willows of the brook compass him about.
018	JOB	040	023	Behold, if a river overflow, he trembleth not: he is confident, though Jordan swell even to his mouth.
018	JOB	040	024	Shall any take him when he is on the watch, or pierce through his nose with a snare?
018	JOB	041	001	Canst thou draw out leviathan with a fish hook? or press down his tongue with a cord?
018	JOB	041	002	Canst thou put a rope into his nose? or pierce his jaw through with a hook?
018	JOB	041	003	Will he make many supplications unto thee? or will he speak soft words unto thee?
018	JOB	041	004	Will he make a covenant with thee, that thou shouldest take him for a servant for ever?
018	JOB	041	005	Wilt thou play with him as with a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens?
018	JOB	041	006	Shall the bands [of fishermen] make traffic of him? shall they part him among the merchants?
018	JOB	041	007	Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons, or his head with fish spears?
018	JOB	041	008	Lay thine hand upon him; remember the battle, and do so no more.
018	JOB	041	009	Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not one be cast down even at the sight of him?
018	JOB	041	010	None is so fierce that he dare stir him up: who then is he that can stand before me?
018	JOB	041	011	Who hath first given unto me, that I should repay him? [whatsoever is] under the whole heaven is mine.
018	JOB	041	012	I will not keep silence concerning his limbs, nor his mighty strength, nor his comely proportion.
018	JOB	041	013	Who can strip off his outer garment? who shall come within his double bridle?
018	JOB	041	014	Who can open the doors of his face? round about his teeth is terror.
018	JOB	041	015	His strong scales are [his] pride, shut up together [as with] a close seal.
018	JOB	041	016	One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.
018	JOB	041	017	They are joined one to another; they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.
018	JOB	041	018	His neesings flash forth light, and his eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.
018	JOB	041	019	Out of his mouth go burning torches, and sparks of fire leap forth.
018	JOB	041	020	Out of his nostrils a smoke goeth, as of a seething pot and [burning] rushes.
018	JOB	041	021	His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth forth from his mouth.
018	JOB	041	022	In his neck abideth strength, and terror danceth before him.
018	JOB	041	023	The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm upon him; they cannot be moved.
018	JOB	041	024	His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, firm as the nether millstone.
018	JOB	041	025	When he raiseth himself up, the mighty are afraid: by reason of consternation they are beside themselves.
018	JOB	041	026	If one lay at him with the sword, it cannot avail; nor the spear, the dart, nor the pointed shaft.
018	JOB	041	027	He counteth iron as straw, [and] brass as rotten wood.
018	JOB	041	028	The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.
018	JOB	041	029	Clubs are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the rushing of the javelin.
018	JOB	041	030	His underparts are [like] sharp potsherds: he spreadeth [as it were] a threshing wain upon the mire.
018	JOB	041	031	He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like ointment.
018	JOB	041	032	He maketh a path to shine after him; one would think the deep to be hoary.
018	JOB	041	033	Upon earth there is not his like, that is made without fear.
018	JOB	041	034	He beholdeth every thing that is high: he is king over all the sons of pride.
018	JOB	042	001	Then Job answered the LORD, and said,
018	JOB	042	002	I know that thou canst do all things, and that no purpose of thine can be restrained.
018	JOB	042	003	Who is this that hideth counsel without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that which I understood not, things too wonderful for me, which I knew not.
018	JOB	042	004	Hear, I beseech thee, and I will speak; I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.
018	JOB	042	005	I had heard of thee by the hearing of the ear; but now mine eye seeth thee,
018	JOB	042	006	Wherefore I abhor [myself], and repent in dust and ashes.
018	JOB	042	007	And it was so, that after the LORD had spoken these words unto Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends: for ye have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job hath.
018	JOB	042	008	Now therefore, take unto you seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you; for him will I accept, that I deal not with you after your folly; for ye have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job hath.
018	JOB	042	009	So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite and Zophar the Naamathite went, and did according as the LORD commanded them: and the LORD accepted Job.
018	JOB	042	010	And the LORD turned the captivity of Job, when he prayed for his friends: and the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before.
018	JOB	042	011	Then came there unto him all his brethren, and all his sisters, and all they that had been of his acquaintance before, and did eat bread with him in his house: and they bemoaned him, and comforted him concerning all the evil that the LORD had brought upon him: every man also gave him a piece of money, and every one a ring of gold.
018	JOB	042	012	So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning: and he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she-asses.
018	JOB	042	013	He had also seven sons and three daughters.
018	JOB	042	014	And he called the name of the first, Jemimah; and the name of the second, Keziah; and the name of the third, Keren-happuch.
018	JOB	042	015	And in all the land were no women found so fair as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.
018	JOB	042	016	And after this Job lived an hundred and forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons’ sons, [even] four generations.
018	JOB	042	017	So Job died, being old and full of days.
#
# BOOK	019	PSA	Psalms	Psalms
019	PSA	001	001	Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the wicked, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.
019	PSA	001	002	But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.
019	PSA	001	003	And he shall be like a tree planted by the streams of water, that bringeth forth its fruit in its season, whose leaf also doth not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.
019	PSA	001	004	The wicked are not so; but are like the chaff which the wind driveth away.
019	PSA	001	005	Therefore the wicked shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.
019	PSA	001	006	For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the wicked shall perish.
019	PSA	002	001	Why do the nations rage, and the peoples imagine a vain thing?
019	PSA	002	002	The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his anointed, [saying],
019	PSA	002	003	Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.
019	PSA	002	004	He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision.
019	PSA	002	005	Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure:
019	PSA	002	006	Yet I have set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.
019	PSA	002	007	I will tell of the decree: the LORD said unto me, Thou art my son; this day have I begotten thee.
019	PSA	002	008	Ask of me, and I will give thee the nations for thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth for thy possession.
019	PSA	002	009	Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.
019	PSA	002	010	Now therefore be wise, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.
019	PSA	002	011	Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.
019	PSA	002	012	Kiss the son, lest he be angry, and ye perish in the way, for his wrath will soon be kindled. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him.
019	PSA	003	001	A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son. LORD, how are mine adversaries increased! many are they that rise up against me.
019	PSA	003	002	Many there be which say of my soul, There is no help for him in God. (Selah)
019	PSA	003	003	But thou, O LORD, art a shield about me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.
019	PSA	003	004	I cry unto the LORD with my voice, and he answereth me out of his holy hill. (Selah)
019	PSA	003	005	I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustaineth me.
019	PSA	003	006	I will not be afraid of ten thousands of the people, that have set themselves against me round about.
019	PSA	003	007	Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies upon the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the wicked.
019	PSA	003	008	Salvation belongeth unto the LORD: thy blessing be upon thy people. (Selah)
019	PSA	004	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. A Psalm of David. Answer me when I call, O God of my righteousness; thou hast set me at large [when I was] in distress: have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.
019	PSA	004	002	O ye sons of men, how long shall my glory be turned into dishonour? [how long] will ye love vanity, and seek after falsehood? (Selah)
019	PSA	004	003	But know that the LORD hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the LORD will hear when I call unto him.
019	PSA	004	004	Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. (Selah)
019	PSA	004	005	Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the LORD.
019	PSA	004	006	Many there be that say, Who will shew us [any] good? LORD, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.
019	PSA	004	007	Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than [they have] when their corn and their wine are increased.
019	PSA	004	008	In peace will I both lay me down and sleep: for thou, LORD, alone makest me dwell in safety.
019	PSA	005	001	For the Chief Musician; with the Nehiloth. A Psalm of David. Give ear to my words, O LORD, consider my (meditation)
019	PSA	005	002	Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for unto thee do I pray.
019	PSA	005	003	O LORD, in the morning shalt thou hear my voice; in the morning will I order [my prayer] unto thee, and will keep watch.
019	PSA	005	004	For thou art not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: evil shall not sojourn with thee.
019	PSA	005	005	The arrogant shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.
019	PSA	005	006	Thou shalt destroy them that speak lies: the LORD abhorreth the bloodthirsty and deceitful man.
019	PSA	005	007	But as for me, in the multitude of thy lovingkindness will I come into thy house: in thy fear will I worship toward thy holy temple.
019	PSA	005	008	Lead me, O LORD, in thy righteousness because of mine enemies; make thy way plain before my face.
019	PSA	005	009	For there is no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part is very wickedness: their throat is an open sepulchre; they flatter with their tongue.
019	PSA	005	010	Hold them guilty, O God; let them fall by their own counsels: thrust them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee.
019	PSA	005	011	But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice, let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.
019	PSA	005	012	For thou wilt bless the righteous; O LORD, thou wilt compass him with favour as with a shield.
019	PSA	006	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments, set to the Sheminith. A Psalm of David. O LORD, rebuke me not in thine anger, neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.
019	PSA	006	002	Have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I am withered away: O LORD, heal me; for my bones are vexed.
019	PSA	006	003	My soul also is sore vexed: and thou, O LORD, how long?
019	PSA	006	004	Return, O LORD, deliver my soul: save me for thy lovingkindness’ sake.
019	PSA	006	005	For in death there is no remembrance of thee: in Sheol who shall give thee thanks?
019	PSA	006	006	I am weary with my groaning; every night make I my bed to swim; I water my couch with my tears.
019	PSA	006	007	Mine eye wasteth away because of grief; it waxeth old because of all mine adversaries.
019	PSA	006	008	Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for the LORD hath heard the voice of my weeping.
019	PSA	006	009	The LORD hath heard my supplication; the LORD will receive my prayer.
019	PSA	006	010	All mine enemies shall be ashamed and sore vexed: they shall turn back, they shall be ashamed suddenly.
019	PSA	007	001	Shiggaion of David, which he sang unto the LORD; concerning the words of Cush a Benjamite. O LORD my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that pursue me, and deliver me:
019	PSA	007	002	Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending it in pieces, while there is none to deliver.
019	PSA	007	003	O LORD my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;
019	PSA	007	004	If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause was mine adversary:)
019	PSA	007	005	Let the enemy pursue my soul, and overtake it; yea, let him tread my life down to the earth, and lay my glory in the dust. (Selah)
019	PSA	007	006	Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself against the rage of mine adversaries: and awake for me; thou hast commanded judgment.
019	PSA	007	007	And let the congregation of the peoples compass thee about: and over them return thou on high.
019	PSA	007	008	The LORD ministereth judgment to the peoples: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and to mine integrity that is in me.
019	PSA	007	009	Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end, but establish thou the righteous: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.
019	PSA	007	010	My shield is with God, which saveth the upright in heart.
019	PSA	007	011	God is a righteous judge, yea, a God that hath indignation every day.
019	PSA	007	012	If a man turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.
019	PSA	007	013	He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he maketh his arrows fiery [shafts].
019	PSA	007	014	Behold, he travaileth with iniquity; yea, he hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.
019	PSA	007	015	He hath made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch which he made.
019	PSA	007	016	His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violence shall come down upon his own pate.
019	PSA	007	017	I will give thanks unto the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.
019	PSA	008	001	For the Chief Musician; set to the Gittith. A Psalm of David. O LORD, our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth! who hast set thy glory upon the heavens.
019	PSA	008	002	Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings hast thou established strength, because of thine adversaries, that thou mightest still the enemy and the avenger.
019	PSA	008	003	When I consider thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon and the stars, which thou hast ordained;
019	PSA	008	004	What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of man, that thou visitest him?
019	PSA	008	005	For thou hast made him but little lower than God, and crownest him with glory and honour.
019	PSA	008	006	Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all things under his feet:
019	PSA	008	007	All sheep and oxen, yea, and the beasts of the field;
019	PSA	008	008	The fowl of the air, and the fish of the sea, whatsoever passeth through the paths of the seas.
019	PSA	008	009	O LORD, our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth!
019	PSA	009	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Muthlabben. A Psalm of David. I will give thanks unto the LORD with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvelous works.
019	PSA	009	002	I will be glad and exult in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou Most High.
019	PSA	009	003	When mine enemies turn back, they stumble and perish at thy presence.
019	PSA	009	004	For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou satest in the throne judging righteously.
019	PSA	009	005	Thou hast rebuked the nations, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast blotted out their name for ever and ever.
019	PSA	009	006	The enemy are come to an end, they are desolate for ever; and the cities which thou hast overthrown, their very memorial is perished.
019	PSA	009	007	But the LORD sitteth [as king] for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.
019	PSA	009	008	And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the peoples in uprightness.
019	PSA	009	009	The LORD also will be a high tower for the oppressed, a high tower in times of trouble;
019	PSA	009	010	And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee; for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.
019	PSA	009	011	Sing praises to the LORD, which dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.
019	PSA	009	012	For he that maketh inquisition for blood remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the poor.
019	PSA	009	013	Have mercy upon me, O LORD; behold my affliction [which I suffer] of them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death;
019	PSA	009	014	That I may shew forth all thy praise: in the gates of the daughter of Zion, I will rejoice in thy salvation.
019	PSA	009	015	The nations are sunk down in the pit that they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.
019	PSA	009	016	The LORD hath made himself known, he hath executed judgment: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. (Higaion, Selah)
019	PSA	009	017	The wicked shall return to Sheol, even all the nations that forget God.
019	PSA	009	018	For the needy shall not alway be forgotten, nor the expectation of the poor perish for ever.
019	PSA	009	019	Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the nations be judged in thy sight.
019	PSA	009	020	Put them in fear, O LORD: let the nations know themselves to be but men. (Selah)
019	PSA	010	001	Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? why hidest thou thyself in times of trouble?
019	PSA	010	002	In the pride of the wicked the poor is hotly pursued; let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.
019	PSA	010	003	For the wicked boasteth of his heart’s desire, and the covetous renounceth, [yea], contemneth the LORD.
019	PSA	010	004	The wicked, in the pride of his countenance, [saith], He will not require [it]. All his thoughts are, There is no God.
019	PSA	010	005	His ways are firm at all times; thy judgments are far above out of his sight: as for all his adversaries, he puffeth at them.
019	PSA	010	006	He saith in his heart, I shall not be moved: to all generations I shall not be in adversity.
019	PSA	010	007	His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and oppression: under his tongue is mischief and iniquity.
019	PSA	010	008	He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the covert places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the helpless.
019	PSA	010	009	He lurketh in the covert as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him in his net.
019	PSA	010	010	He croucheth, he boweth down, and the helpless fall by his strong ones.
019	PSA	010	011	He saith in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see it.
019	PSA	010	012	Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the poor.
019	PSA	010	013	Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God, and say in his heart, Thou wilt not require [it]?
019	PSA	010	014	Thon hast seen [it]; for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to take it into thy hand: the helpless committeth [himself] unto thee; thou hast been the helper of the fatherless.
019	PSA	010	015	Break thou the arm of the wicked; and as for the evil man, seek out his wickedness till thou find none.
019	PSA	010	016	The LORD is King for ever and ever: the nations are perished out of his land.
019	PSA	010	017	LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the meek: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear:
019	PSA	010	018	To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that man which is of the earth may be terrible no more.
019	PSA	011	001	For the Chief Musician. [A Psalm] of David. In the LORD put I my trust: how say ye to my soul, Flee as a bird to your mountain?
019	PSA	011	002	For, lo, the wicked bend the bow, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may shoot in darkness at the upright in heart.
019	PSA	011	003	If the foundations be destroyed, what can the righteous do?
019	PSA	011	004	The LORD is in his holy temple, the LORD, his throne is in heaven; his eyes behold, his eyelids try, the children of men.
019	PSA	011	005	The LORD trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth.
019	PSA	011	006	Upon the wicked he shall rain snares; fire and brimstone and burning wind shall be the portion of their cup.
019	PSA	011	007	For the LORD is righteous; he loveth righteousness: the upright shall behold his face.
019	PSA	012	001	For the Chief Musician; set to the Sheminith. A Psalm of David. Help, LORD; for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men.
019	PSA	012	002	They speak vanity every one with his neighbour: with flattering lip, and with a double heart, do they speak.
019	PSA	012	003	The LORD shall cut off all flattering lips, the tongue that speaketh great things:
019	PSA	012	004	Who have said, with our tongue will we prevail; our lips are our own: who is lord over us?
019	PSA	012	005	For the spoiling of the poor, for the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, saith the LORD; I will set him in safety at whom they puff.
019	PSA	012	006	The words of the LORD are pure words; as silver tried in a furnace on the earth, purified seven times.
019	PSA	012	007	Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever.
019	PSA	012	008	The wicked walk on every side, when vileness is exalted among the sons of men.
019	PSA	013	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. How long, O LORD, wilt thou forget me for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me?
019	PSA	013	002	How long shall I take counsel in my soul, having sorrow in my heart all the day? how long shall mine enemy be exalted over me?
019	PSA	013	003	Consider [and] answer me, O LORD my God: lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the [sleep of] death;
019	PSA	013	004	Lest mine enemy say, I have prevailed against him; [lest] mine adversaries rejoice when I am moved.
019	PSA	013	005	But I have trusted in thy mercy; my heart shall rejoice in thy salvation:
019	PSA	013	006	I will sing unto the LORD, because he hath dealt bountifully with me.
019	PSA	014	001	For the Chief Musician. [A Psalm] of David. The fool hath said in his heart, There is no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works; there is none that doeth good.
019	PSA	014	002	The LORD looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, that did seek after God.
019	PSA	014	003	They are all gone aside; they are together become filthy; there is none that doeth good, no, not one.
019	PSA	014	004	Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people as they eat bread, and call not upon the LORD.
019	PSA	014	005	There were they in great fear: for God is in the generation of the righteous.
019	PSA	014	006	Ye put to shame the counsel of the poor, because the LORD is his refuge.
019	PSA	014	007	Oh that the salvation of Israel were come out of Zion! when the LORD bringeth back the captivity of his people, then shall Jacob rejoice, [and] Israel shall be glad.
019	PSA	015	001	A Psalm of David. LORD, who shall sojourn in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill?
019	PSA	015	002	He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh truth in his heart.
019	PSA	015	003	He that slandereth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his friend, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour.
019	PSA	015	004	In whose eyes a reprobate is despised; but he honoureth them that fear the LORD. He that sweareth to his own hurt, and changeth not.
019	PSA	015	005	He that putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these things shall never be moved.
019	PSA	016	001	Michtam of David. Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust.
019	PSA	016	002	I have said unto the LORD, Thou art my Lord: I have no good beyond thee.
019	PSA	016	003	As for the saints that are in the earth, they are the excellent in whom is all my delight.
019	PSA	016	004	Their sorrows shall be multiplied that exchange [the LORD] for another [god]: their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take their names upon my lips.
019	PSA	016	005	The LORD is the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot.
019	PSA	016	006	The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places; yea, I have a goodly heritage.
019	PSA	016	007	I will bless the LORD, who hath given me counsel: yea, my reins instruct me in the night seasons.
019	PSA	016	008	I have set the LORD always before me: because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved.
019	PSA	016	009	Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall dwell in safety.
019	PSA	016	010	For thou wilt not leave my soul to Sheol; neither wilt thou suffer thine holy one to see corruption.
019	PSA	016	011	Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; in thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.
019	PSA	017	001	A Prayer of David. Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto my cry; give ear unto my prayer, that goeth not out of feigned lips.
019	PSA	017	002	Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes look upon equity.
019	PSA	017	003	Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited me in the night; thou hast tried me, and findest nothing; I am purposed that my mouth shall not transgress.
019	PSA	017	004	As for the works of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept me from the ways of the violent.
019	PSA	017	005	My steps have held fast to thy paths, my feet have not slipped.
019	PSA	017	006	I have called upon thee, for thou wilt answer me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, [and] hear my speech.
019	PSA	017	007	Shew thy marvelous lovingkindness, O thou that savest them which put their trust [in thee] from those that rise up [against them], by thy right hand.
019	PSA	017	008	Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,
019	PSA	017	009	From the wicked that spoil me, my deadly enemies, that compass me about.
019	PSA	017	010	They are enclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.
019	PSA	017	011	They have now compassed us in our steps: they set their eyes to cast [us] down to the earth.
019	PSA	017	012	He is like a lion that is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.
019	PSA	017	013	Arise, O LORD, confront him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked by thy sword;
019	PSA	017	014	From men, by thy hand, O LORD, from men of the world, whose portion is in [this] life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy treasure: they are satisfied with children, and leave the rest of their substance to their babes.
019	PSA	017	015	As for me, I shall behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.
019	PSA	018	001	For the Chief Musician. [A Psalm] of David the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day that the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: and he said, I love thee, O LORD, my strength.
019	PSA	018	002	The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strong rock, in him will I trust; my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower.
019	PSA	018	003	I will call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.
019	PSA	018	004	The cords of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodliness made me afraid.
019	PSA	018	005	The cords of Sheol were round about me: the snares of death came on me.
019	PSA	018	006	In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry before him came into his ears.
019	PSA	018	007	Then the earth shook and trembled, me foundations also of the mountains moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.
019	PSA	018	008	There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.
019	PSA	018	009	He bowed the heavens also, and came down, and thick darkness was under his feet.
019	PSA	018	010	And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly, yea, he flew swiftly upon the wings of the wind.
019	PSA	018	011	He made darkness his hiding place, his pavilion round about him; darkness of waters, thick clouds of the skies.
019	PSA	018	012	At the brightness before him his thick clouds passed, hailstones and coals of fire.
019	PSA	018	013	The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Most High uttered his voice; hailstones and coals of fire.
019	PSA	018	014	And he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; yea, lightnings manifold, and discomfited them.
019	PSA	018	015	Then the channels of waters appeared, and the foundations of the world were laid bare, at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.
019	PSA	018	016	He sent from on high, he took me; he drew me out of many waters.
019	PSA	018	017	He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them that hated me, for they were too mighty for me.
019	PSA	018	018	They came upon me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.
019	PSA	018	019	He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.
019	PSA	018	020	The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.
019	PSA	018	021	For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
019	PSA	018	022	For all his judgments were before me, and I put not away his statutes from me.
019	PSA	018	023	I was also perfect with him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.
019	PSA	018	024	Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.
019	PSA	018	025	With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with the perfect man thou wilt shew thyself perfect;
019	PSA	018	026	With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the perverse thou wilt shew thyself froward.
019	PSA	018	027	For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but the haughty eyes thou wilt bring down.
019	PSA	018	028	For thou wilt light my lamp: the LORD my God will lighten my darkness.
019	PSA	018	029	For by thee I run upon a troop; and by my God do I leap over a wall.
019	PSA	018	030	As for God, his way is perfect: the word of the LORD is tried; he is a shield unto all them that trust in him.
019	PSA	018	031	For who is God, save the LORD? and who is a rock, beside our God?
019	PSA	018	032	The God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.
019	PSA	018	033	He maketh my feet like hinds’ [feet]: and setteth me upon my high places,
019	PSA	018	034	He teacheth my hands to war; so that mine arms do bend a bow of brass.
019	PSA	018	035	Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.
019	PSA	018	036	Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, and my feet have not slipped.
019	PSA	018	037	I will pursue mine enemies, and overtake them: neither will I turn again till they are consumed.
019	PSA	018	038	I will smite them through that they shall not be able to rise: they shall fall under my feet.
019	PSA	018	039	For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.
019	PSA	018	040	Thou hast also made mine enemies turn their backs unto me, that I might cut off them that hate me.
019	PSA	018	041	They cried, but there was none to save: even unto the LORD, but he answered them not.
019	PSA	018	042	Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the mire of the streets.
019	PSA	018	043	Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; thou hast made me the head of the nations: a people whom I have not known shall serve me.
019	PSA	018	044	As soon as they hear of me they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me.
019	PSA	018	045	The strangers shall fade away, and shall come trembling out of their close places.
019	PSA	018	046	The LORD liveth; and blessed be my rock; and exalted be the God of my salvation:
019	PSA	018	047	Even the God that executeth vengeance for me, and subdueth peoples under me.
019	PSA	018	048	He rescueth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above them that rise up against me: thou deliverest me from the violent man.
019	PSA	018	049	Therefore I will give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the nations, and will sing praises unto thy name.
019	PSA	018	050	Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth lovingkindness to his anointed, to David and to his seed, for evermore.
019	PSA	019	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.
019	PSA	019	002	Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.
019	PSA	019	003	There is no speech nor language; their voice cannot be heard.
019	PSA	019	004	Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,
019	PSA	019	005	Which is as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, and rejoiceth as a strong man to run his course.
019	PSA	019	006	His going forth is from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.
019	PSA	019	007	The law of the LORD is perfect, restoring the soul: the testimony of the LORD is sure, making wise the simple.
019	PSA	019	008	The precepts of the LORD are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD is pure, enlightening the eyes.
019	PSA	019	009	The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD are true, [and] righteous altogether.
019	PSA	019	010	More to be desired are they than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.
019	PSA	019	011	Moreover by them is thy servant warned: in keeping of them there is great reward.
019	PSA	019	012	Who can discern [his] errors? clear thou me from hidden [faults].
019	PSA	019	013	Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous [sins]; let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be perfect, and I shall be clear from great transgression.
019	PSA	019	014	Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my rock, and my redeemer.
019	PSA	020	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. The LORD answer thee in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob set thee up on high;
019	PSA	020	002	Send thee help from the sanctuary, and strengthen thee out of Zion;
019	PSA	020	003	Remember all thy offerings, and accept thy burnt sacrifice; (Selah)
019	PSA	020	004	Grant thee thy heart’s desire, and fulfill all thy counsel.
019	PSA	020	005	We will triumph in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up our banners: the LORD fulfill all thy petitions.
019	PSA	020	006	Now know I that the LORD saveth his anointed; he wilt answer him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand.
019	PSA	020	007	Some [trust] in chariots, and some in horses: but we will make mention of the name of the LORD our God.
019	PSA	020	008	They are bowed down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright.
019	PSA	020	009	Save, LORD: let the King answer us when we call.
019	PSA	021	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. The king shall joy in thy strength, O LORD; and in thy salvation how greatly shall he rejoice!
019	PSA	021	002	Thou hast given him his heart’s desire, and hast not withholden the request of his lips. (Selah)
019	PSA	021	003	For thou preventest him with the blessings of goodness: thou settest a crown of fine gold on his head.
019	PSA	021	004	He asked life of thee, thou gavest it him; even length of days for ever and ever.
019	PSA	021	005	His glory is great in thy salvation: honour and majesty dost thou lay upon him.
019	PSA	021	006	For thou makest him most blessed for ever: thou makest him glad with joy in thy presence.
019	PSA	021	007	For the king trusteth in the LORD, and through the lovingkindness of the Most High he shall not be moved.
019	PSA	021	008	Thine hand shall find out all thine enemies: thy right hand shall find out those that hate thee.
019	PSA	021	009	Thou shalt make them as a fiery furnace in the time of thine anger. The LORD shall swallow them up in his wrath, and the fire shall devour them.
019	PSA	021	010	Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth, and their seed from among the children of men.
019	PSA	021	011	For they intended evil against thee: they imagined a device, which they are not able to perform.
019	PSA	021	012	For thou shalt make them turn their back, thou shalt make ready with thy bowstrings against the face of them.
019	PSA	021	013	Be thou exalted, O LORD, in thy strength: so will we sing and praise thy power.
019	PSA	022	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Aijeleth hash-Shahar. A Psalm of David. My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me? [why art thou so] far from helping me, [and from] the words of my roaring?
019	PSA	022	002	O my God, I cry in the day-time, but thou answerest not; and in the night season, and am not silent.
019	PSA	022	003	But thou art holy, O thou that inhabitest the praises of Israel.
019	PSA	022	004	Our fathers trusted in thee: they trusted, and thou didst deliver them.
019	PSA	022	005	They cried unto thee, and were delivered: they trusted in thee, and were not ashamed.
019	PSA	022	006	But I am a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised of the people.
019	PSA	022	007	All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head, [saying],
019	PSA	022	008	Commit [thyself] unto the LORD; let him deliver him: let him deliver him, seeing he delighteth in him.
019	PSA	022	009	But thou art he that took me out the womb: thou didst make me trust [when I was] upon my mother’s breasts.
019	PSA	022	010	I was cast upon thee from the womb: thou art my God from my mother’s belly.
019	PSA	022	011	Be not far from me; for trouble is near; for there is none to help.
019	PSA	022	012	Many bulls have compassed me: strong bulls of Bashan have beset me round.
019	PSA	022	013	They gape upon me with their mouth, [as] a ravening and a roaring lion.
019	PSA	022	014	I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels.
019	PSA	022	015	My Strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the dust of death.
019	PSA	022	016	For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of evil-doers have enclosed me; they pierced my hands and my feet.
019	PSA	022	017	I may tell all my bones; they look and stare upon me:
019	PSA	022	018	They part my garments among them, and upon my vesture do they cast lots.
019	PSA	022	019	But be not thou far off, O LORD: O thou my succour, haste thee to help me.
019	PSA	022	020	Deliver my soul from the sword; my darling from the power of the dog;
019	PSA	022	021	Save me from the lion’s mouth; yea, from the horns of the wild-oxen thou hast answered me.
019	PSA	022	022	I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.
019	PSA	022	023	Ye that fear the LORD, praise him; all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him; and stand in awe of him, all ye the seed of Israel.
019	PSA	022	024	For he hath not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, he heard.
019	PSA	022	025	Of thee cometh my praise in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before them that fear him.
019	PSA	022	026	The meek shall eat and be satisfied: they shall praise the LORD that seek after him: let your heart live for ever.
019	PSA	022	027	All the ends of the earth shall remember and turn unto the LORD: and all the kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee.
019	PSA	022	028	For the kingdom is the LORD’S: and he is the ruler over the nations.
019	PSA	022	029	All the fat ones of the earth shall eat and worship: all they that go down to the dust shall bow before him, even he that cannot keep his soul alive.
019	PSA	022	030	A seed shall serve him; it shall be told of the Lord unto the [next] generation.
019	PSA	022	031	They shall come and shall declare his righteousness unto a people that shall be born, that he hath done it.
019	PSA	023	001	A Psalm of David. The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.
019	PSA	023	002	He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.
019	PSA	023	003	He restoreth my soul: he guideth me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.
019	PSA	023	004	Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil; for thou art with me: thy rod and thy staff, they comfort me.
019	PSA	023	005	Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou hast anointed my head with oil; my cup runneth over.
019	PSA	023	006	Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.
019	PSA	024	001	A Psalm of David. The earth is the LORD’S, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.
019	PSA	024	002	For he hath founded it upon the seas, and established it upon the floods.
019	PSA	024	003	Who shall ascend into the hill of the LORD? and who shall stand in his holy place?
019	PSA	024	004	He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart; who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, and hath not sworn deceitfully.
019	PSA	024	005	He shall receive a blessing from the LORD, and righteousness from the God of his salvation.
019	PSA	024	006	This is the generation of them that seek after him, that seek thy face, [O God of] Jacob. (Selah)
019	PSA	024	007	Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors: and the King of glory shall come in.
019	PSA	024	008	Who is the King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.
019	PSA	024	009	Lift up your heads, O ye gates; yea, lift them up, ye everlasting doors: and the King of glory shall come in.
019	PSA	024	010	Who is this King of glory? The LORD of hosts, he is the King of glory. (Selah)
019	PSA	025	001	[A Psalm] of David. Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my soul.
019	PSA	025	002	O my God, in thee have I trusted, let me not be ashamed; let not mine enemies triumph over me.
019	PSA	025	003	Yea, none that wait on thee shall be ashamed: they shall be ashamed that deal treacherously without cause.
019	PSA	025	004	Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths.
019	PSA	025	005	Guide me in thy truth, and teach me; for thou art the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.
019	PSA	025	006	Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they have been ever of old.
019	PSA	025	007	Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy lovingkindness remember thou me, for thy goodness’ sake, O LORD.
019	PSA	025	008	Good and upright is the LORD: therefore will he instruct sinners in the way.
019	PSA	025	009	The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.
019	PSA	025	010	All the paths of the LORD are lovingkindness and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.
019	PSA	025	011	For thy name’s sake, O LORD, pardon mine iniquity, for it is great.
019	PSA	025	012	What man is he that feareth the LORD? him shall he instruct in the way that he shall choose.
019	PSA	025	013	His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the land.
019	PSA	025	014	The secret of the LORD is with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.
019	PSA	025	015	Mine eyes are ever toward the LORD; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.
019	PSA	025	016	Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I am desolate and afflicted.
019	PSA	025	017	The troubles of my heart are enlarged: O bring thou me out of my distresses.
019	PSA	025	018	Consider mine affliction and my travail; and forgive all my sins.
019	PSA	025	019	Consider mine enemies, for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.
019	PSA	025	020	O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed, for I put my trust in thee.
019	PSA	025	021	Let integrity and uprightness preserve me, for I wait on thee.
019	PSA	025	022	Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.
019	PSA	026	001	[A Psalm] of David. Judge me, O LORD, for I have walked in mine integrity: I have trusted also in the LORD without wavering.
019	PSA	026	002	Examine me, O LORD, and prove me; try my reins and my heart.
019	PSA	026	003	For thy lovingkindness is before mine eyes; and I have walked in thy truth.
019	PSA	026	004	I have not sat with vain persons; neither will I go in with dissemblers.
019	PSA	026	005	I hate the congregation of evil-doers, and will not sit with the wicked.
019	PSA	026	006	I will wash mine hands in innocency; so will I compass thine altar, O LORD:
019	PSA	026	007	That I may make the voice of thanksgiving to be heard, and tell of all thy wondrous works.
019	PSA	026	008	LORD, I love the habitation of thy house, and the place where thy glory dwelleth.
019	PSA	026	009	Gather not my soul with sinners, nor my life with men of blood:
019	PSA	026	010	In whose hands is mischief, and their right hand is full of bribes.
019	PSA	026	011	But as for me, I will walk in mine integrity: redeem me, and be merciful unto me.
019	PSA	026	012	My foot standeth in an even place: in the congregations will I bless the LORD.
019	PSA	027	001	[A Psalm] of David. The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?
019	PSA	027	002	When evil-doers came upon me to eat up my flesh, [even] mine adversaries and my foes, they stumbled and fell.
019	PSA	027	003	Though an host should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear: though war should rise against me, even then will I be confident.
019	PSA	027	004	One thing have I asked of the LORD, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the LORD, and to inquire in his temple.
019	PSA	027	005	For in the day of trouble he shall keep me secretly in his pavilion: in the covert of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall lift me up upon a rock.
019	PSA	027	006	And now shall mine head be lifted up above mine enemies round about me; and I will offer in his tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises unto the LORD.
019	PSA	027	007	Hear, O LORD, when I cry with my voice: have mercy also upon me, and answer me.
019	PSA	027	008	[When thou saidst], Seek ye my face; my heart said unto thee, Thy face, LORD, will I seek.
019	PSA	027	009	Hide not thy face from me; put not thy servant away in anger: thou hast been my help; cast me not off, neither forsake me, O God of my salvation.
019	PSA	027	010	For my father and my mother have forsaken me, but the LORD will take me up.
019	PSA	027	011	Teach me thy way, O LORD; and lead me in a plain path, because of mine enemies.
019	PSA	027	012	Deliver me not over unto the will of mine adversaries: for false witnesses are risen up against me, and such as breathe out cruelty.
019	PSA	027	013	[I had fainted], unless I had believed to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.
019	PSA	027	014	Wait on the LORD: be strong, and let thine heart take courage; yea, wait thou on the LORD.
019	PSA	028	001	[A Psalm] of David. Unto thee, O LORD, will I call; my rock, be not thou deaf unto me: lest, if thou be silent unto me, I become like them that go down into the pit.
019	PSA	028	002	Hear the voice of my supplications, when I cry unto thee, when I lift up my hands toward thy holy oracle.
019	PSA	028	003	Draw me not away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity; which speak peace with their neighbours, but mischief is in their hearts.
019	PSA	028	004	Give them according to their work, and according to the wickedness of their doings: give them after the operation of their hands; render to them their desert.
019	PSA	028	005	Because they regard not the works of the LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he shall break them down and not build them up.
019	PSA	028	006	Blessed be the LORD, because he hath heard the voice of my supplications.
019	PSA	028	007	The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart hath trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will praise him.
019	PSA	028	008	The LORD is their strength, and he is a strong hold of salvation to his anointed.
019	PSA	028	009	Save thy people, and bless thine inheritance: feed them also, and bear them up for ever.
019	PSA	029	001	A Psalm of David. Give unto the LORD, O ye sons of the mighty, give unto the LORD glory and strength.
019	PSA	029	002	Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name; worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness.
019	PSA	029	003	The voice of the LORD is upon the waters: the God of glory thundereth, even the LORD upon many waters.
019	PSA	029	004	The voice of the LORD is powerful; the voice of the LORD is full of majesty.
019	PSA	029	005	The voice of the LORD breaketh the cedars; yea, the LORD breaketh in pieces the cedars of Lebanon.
019	PSA	029	006	He maketh them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young wild-ox.
019	PSA	029	007	The voice of the LORD cleaveth the flames of fire.
019	PSA	029	008	The voice of the LORD shaketh the wilderness; the LORD shaketh the wilderness of Kadesh.
019	PSA	029	009	The voice of the LORD maketh the hinds to calve, and strippeth the forests bare: and in his temple every thing saith, Glory.
019	PSA	029	010	The LORD sat [as king] at the Flood; yea, the LORD sitteth as king for ever.
019	PSA	029	011	The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.
019	PSA	030	001	A Psalm; a Song at the Dedication of the House; [a Psalm] of David. I will extol thee, O LORD; for thou hast raised me up, and hast not made my foes to rejoice over me.
019	PSA	030	002	O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.
019	PSA	030	003	O LORD, thou hast brought up my soul from Sheol: thou hast kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.
019	PSA	030	004	Sing praise unto the LORD, O ye saints of his, and give thanks to his holy name.
019	PSA	030	005	For his anger is but for a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may tarry for the night, but joy [cometh] in the morning.
019	PSA	030	006	As for me, I said in my prosperity, I shall never be moved.
019	PSA	030	007	Thou, LORD, of thy favour hadst made my mountain to stand strong: thou didst hide thy face; I was troubled.
019	PSA	030	008	I cried to thee, O LORD; and unto the LORD I made supplication:
019	PSA	030	009	What profit is there in my blood, when I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? shall it declare thy truth?
019	PSA	030	010	Hear, O LORD, and have mercy upon me: LORD, be thou my helper.
019	PSA	030	011	Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing; thou hast loosed my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness:
019	PSA	030	012	To the end that [my] glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever.
019	PSA	031	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in thy righteousness.
019	PSA	031	002	Bow down thine ear unto me; deliver me speedily: be thou to me a strong rock, an house of defence to save me.
019	PSA	031	003	For thou art my rock and my fortress; therefore for thy name’s sake lead me and guide me.
019	PSA	031	004	Pluck me out of the net that they have laid privily for me; for thou art my strong hold.
019	PSA	031	005	Into thine hand I commend my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O LORD, thou God of truth.
019	PSA	031	006	I hate them that regard lying vanities: but I trust in the LORD.
019	PSA	031	007	I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy: for thou hast seen my affliction; thou hast known my soul in adversities:
019	PSA	031	008	And thou hast not shut me up into the hand of the enemy; thou hast set my feet in a large place.
019	PSA	031	009	Have mercy upon me, O LORD, for I am in distress: mine eye wasteth away with grief, [yea], my soul and my body.
019	PSA	031	010	For my life is spent with sorrow, and my years with sighing: my strength faileth because of mine iniquity, and my bones are wasted away.
019	PSA	031	011	Because of all mine adversaries I am become a reproach, yea, unto my neighbours exceedingly, and a fear to mine acquaintance: they that did see me without fled from me.
019	PSA	031	012	I am forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am like a broken vessel.
019	PSA	031	013	For I have heard the defaming of many, terror on every side: while they took counsel together against me, they devised to take away my life.
019	PSA	031	014	But I trusted in thee, O LORD: I said, Thou art my God.
019	PSA	031	015	My times are in thy hand: deliver me from the hand of mine enemies, and from them that persecute me.
019	PSA	031	016	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: save me in thy lovingkindness.
019	PSA	031	017	Let me not he ashamed, O LORD; for I have called upon thee: let the wicked be ashamed, let them be silent in Sheol.
019	PSA	031	018	Let the lying lips be dumb; which speak against the righteous insolently, with pride and contempt.
019	PSA	031	019	Oh how great is thy goodness, which thou hast laid up for them that fear thee, which thou hast wrought for them that put their trust in thee, before the sons of men!
019	PSA	031	020	In the covert of thy presence shalt thou hide them from the plottings of man: thou shalt keep them secretly in a pavilion from the strife of tongues.
019	PSA	031	021	Blessed be the LORD: for he hath shewed me his marvelous lovingkindness in a strong city.
019	PSA	031	022	As for me, I said in my haste, I am cut off from before thine eyes: nevertheless thou heardest the voice of my supplications when I cried unto thee.
019	PSA	031	023	O love the LORD, all ye his saints: the LORD preserveth the faithful, and plentifully rewardeth the proud doer.
019	PSA	031	024	Be strong, and let your heart take courage, all ye that hope in the LORD.
019	PSA	032	001	[A Psalm] of David. Maschil. Blessed is he whose transgression is forgiven, whose sin is covered.
019	PSA	032	002	Blessed is the man unto whom the LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit there is no guile.
019	PSA	032	003	When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.
019	PSA	032	004	For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture was changed [as] with the drought of summer. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	005	I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid: I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	006	For this let every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely when the great waters overflow they shall not reach unto him.
019	PSA	032	007	Thou art my hiding place; thou wilt preserve me from trouble; thou wilt compass me about with songs of deliverance. (Selah)
019	PSA	032	008	I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will counsel thee with mine eye upon thee.
019	PSA	032	009	Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule, which have no understanding: whose trappings must be bit and bridle to hold them in, [else] they will not come near unto thee.
019	PSA	032	010	Many sorrows shall be to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the LORD, mercy shall compass him about.
019	PSA	032	011	Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all ye that are upright in heart.
019	PSA	033	001	Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous: praise is comely for the upright.
019	PSA	033	002	Give thanks unto the LORD with harp: sing praises unto him with the psaltery of ten strings.
019	PSA	033	003	Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.
019	PSA	033	004	For the word of the LORD is right; and all his work is [done] in faithfulness.
019	PSA	033	005	He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the lovingkindness of the LORD.
019	PSA	033	006	By the word of the LORD were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.
019	PSA	033	007	He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the deeps in storehouses.
019	PSA	033	008	Let all the earth fear the LORD: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.
019	PSA	033	009	For he spake, and it was done; he commanded, and it stood fast.
019	PSA	033	010	The LORD bringeth the counsel of the nations to nought: he maketh the thoughts of the peoples to be of none effect.
019	PSA	033	011	The counsel of the LORD standeth fast for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.
019	PSA	033	012	Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD; the people whom he hath chosen for his own inheritance.
019	PSA	033	013	The LORD looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men;
019	PSA	033	014	From the place of his habitation he looketh forth upon all the inhabitants of the earth;
019	PSA	033	015	He that fashioneth the hearts of them all, that considereth all their works.
019	PSA	033	016	There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by great strength.
019	PSA	033	017	An horse is a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver any by his great power.
019	PSA	033	018	Behold, the eye of the LORD is upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;
019	PSA	033	019	To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.
019	PSA	033	020	Our soul hath waited for the LORD: he is our help and our shield.
019	PSA	033	021	For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.
019	PSA	033	022	Let thy mercy, O LORD, be upon us, according as we have hoped in thee.
019	PSA	034	001	[A Psalm] of David; when he changed his behaviour before Abimelech, who drove him away, and he departed. I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise shall continually be in my mouth.
019	PSA	034	002	My soul shall make her boast in the LORD: the meek shall hear thereof, and be glad.
019	PSA	034	003	O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.
019	PSA	034	004	I sought the LORD, and he answered me, and delivered me from all my fears.
019	PSA	034	005	They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces shall never be confounded.
019	PSA	034	006	This poor man cried, and the LORD heard him, and saved him out of all his troubles.
019	PSA	034	007	The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.
019	PSA	034	008	O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.
019	PSA	034	009	O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for there is no want to them that fear him.
019	PSA	034	010	The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good thing.
019	PSA	034	011	Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the LORD.
019	PSA	034	012	What man is he that desireth life, and loveth [many] days, that he may see good?
019	PSA	034	013	Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.
019	PSA	034	014	Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.
019	PSA	034	015	The eyes of the LORD are toward the righteous, and his ears are [open] unto their cry.
019	PSA	034	016	The face of the LORD is against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.
019	PSA	034	017	[The righteous] cried, and the LORD heard, and delivered them out of all their troubles.
019	PSA	034	018	The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart, and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.
019	PSA	034	019	Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all.
019	PSA	034	020	He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.
019	PSA	034	021	Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be condemned.
019	PSA	034	022	The LORD redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be condemned.
019	PSA	035	001	[A Psalm] of David. Strive thou, O LORD, with them that strive with me: fight thou against them that fight against me.
019	PSA	035	002	Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for mine help.
019	PSA	035	003	Draw out also the spear, and stop the way against them that pursue me: say unto my soul, I am thy salvation.
019	PSA	035	004	Let them be ashamed and brought to dishonour that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and confounded that devise my hurt.
019	PSA	035	005	Let them be as chaff before the wind, and the angel of the LORD driving [them] on.
019	PSA	035	006	Let their way be dark and slippery, and the angel of the LORD pursuing them.
019	PSA	035	007	For without cause have they hid for me their net [in] a pit, without cause have they digged [a pit] for my soul.
019	PSA	035	008	Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: with destruction let him fall therein.
019	PSA	035	009	And my soul shall be joyful in the LORD: it shall rejoice in his salvation.
019	PSA	035	010	All my bones shall say, LORD, who is like unto thee, which deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, yea, the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?
019	PSA	035	011	Unrighteous witnesses rise up; they ask me of things that I know not.
019	PSA	035	012	They reward me evil for good, [to] the bereaving of my soul.
019	PSA	035	013	But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth: I afflicted my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into mine own bosom.
019	PSA	035	014	I behaved myself as though it had been my friend or my brother: I bowed down mourning, as one that bewaileth his mother.
019	PSA	035	015	But when I halted they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together: the abjects gathered themselves together against me, and I knew [it] not; they did tear me, and ceased not:
019	PSA	035	016	Like the profane mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.
019	PSA	035	017	Lord, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions.
019	PSA	035	018	I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among much people.
019	PSA	035	019	Let not them that are mine enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: neither let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause.
019	PSA	035	020	For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful words against them that are quiet in the land.
019	PSA	035	021	Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me; they said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen it.
019	PSA	035	022	Thou hast seen it, O LORD; keep not silence: O Lord, be not far from me.
019	PSA	035	023	Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, [even] unto my cause, my God and my Lord.
019	PSA	035	024	Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.
019	PSA	035	025	Let them not say in their heart, Aha, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up.
019	PSA	035	026	Let them be ashamed and confounded together that rejoice at mine hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify themselves against me.
019	PSA	035	027	Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause: yea, let them say continually, The LORD be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.
019	PSA	035	028	And my tongue shall talk of thy righteousness, [and] of thy praise all the day long.
019	PSA	036	001	For the Chief Musician. [A Psalm] of David the servant of the LORD. The transgression of the wicked saith within my heart, There is no fear of God before his eyes.
019	PSA	036	002	For he flattereth himself in his own eyes, that his iniquity shall not be found out and be hated.
019	PSA	036	003	The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit: he hath left off to be wise [and] to do good.
019	PSA	036	004	He deviseth iniquity upon his bed; he setteth himself in a way that is not good; he abhorreth not evil.
019	PSA	036	005	Thy lovingkindness, O LORD, is in the heavens; thy faithfulness [reacheth] unto the skies.
019	PSA	036	006	Thy righteousness is like the mountains of God; thy judgments are a great deep: O LORD, thou preservest man and beast.
019	PSA	036	007	How precious is thy lovingkindness, O God! and the children of men take refuge under the shadow of thy wings.
019	PSA	036	008	They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.
019	PSA	036	009	For with thee is the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.
019	PSA	036	010	O continue thy lovingkindness unto them that know thee; and thy righteousness to the upright in heart.
019	PSA	036	011	Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of the wicked drive me away.
019	PSA	036	012	There are the workers of iniquity fallen: they are thrust down, and shall not be able to rise.
019	PSA	037	001	[A Psalm] of David. Fret not thyself because of evil-doers, neither be thou envious against them that work unrighteousness.
019	PSA	037	002	For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb.
019	PSA	037	003	Trust in the LORD, and do good; dwell in the land, and follow after faithfulness.
019	PSA	037	004	Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.
019	PSA	037	005	Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him, and he shall bring it to pass.
019	PSA	037	006	Add he shall make thy righteousness to go forth as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.
019	PSA	037	007	Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.
019	PSA	037	008	Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not thyself, [it tendeth] only to evil-doing.
019	PSA	037	009	For evil-doers shall be cut off: but those that wait upon the LORD, they shall inherit the land.
019	PSA	037	010	For yet a little while, and the wicked shall not be: yea, thou shalt diligently consider his place, and he shall not be.
019	PSA	037	011	But the meek shall inherit the land; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.
019	PSA	037	012	The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth.
019	PSA	037	013	The Lord shall laugh at him: for he seeth that his day is coming.
019	PSA	037	014	The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow; to cast down the poor and needy, to slay such as be upright in the way:
019	PSA	037	015	Their sword shall enter into their own heart, and their bows shall be broken.
019	PSA	037	016	Better is a little that the righteous hath than the abundance of many wicked.
019	PSA	037	017	For the arms of the wicked shall be broken: but the LORD upholdeth the righteous.
019	PSA	037	018	The LORD knoweth the days of the perfect: and their inheritance shall be for ever.
019	PSA	037	019	They shall not be ashamed in the time of evil: and in the days of famine they shall be satisfied.
019	PSA	037	020	But the wicked shall perish, and the enemies of the LORD shall be as the excellency of the pastures: they shall consume; in smoke shall they consume away.
019	PSA	037	021	The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous dealeth graciously, and giveth.
019	PSA	037	022	For such as be blessed of him shall inherit the land; and they that be cursed of him shall be cut off.
019	PSA	037	023	A man’s goings are established of the LORD; and he delighteth in his way.
019	PSA	037	024	Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the LORD upholdeth him with his hand.
019	PSA	037	025	I have been young, and now am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging [their] bread.
019	PSA	037	026	All the day long he dealeth graciously, and lendeth; and his seed is blessed.
019	PSA	037	027	Depart from evil, and do good; dwell for evermore.
019	PSA	037	028	For the LORD loveth judgment, and forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever: but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.
019	PSA	037	029	The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever.
019	PSA	037	030	The mouth of the righteous talketh of wisdom, and his tongue speaketh judgment.
019	PSA	037	031	The law of his God is in his heart; none of his steps shall slide.
019	PSA	037	032	The wicked watcheth the righteous, and seeketh to slay him.
019	PSA	037	033	The LORD will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.
019	PSA	037	034	Wait on the LORD, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land: when the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see it.
019	PSA	037	035	I have seen the wicked in great power, and spreading himself like a green tree in its native soil.
019	PSA	037	036	But one passed by, and, lo, he was not: yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.
019	PSA	037	037	Mark the perfect man, and behold the upright: for the latter end of [that] man is peace.
019	PSA	037	038	As for transgressors, they shall be destroyed together: the latter end of the wicked shall be cut off.
019	PSA	037	039	But the salvation of the righteous is of the LORD: he is their strong hold in the time of trouble.
019	PSA	037	040	And the LORD helpeth them, and rescueth them: he rescueth them from the wicked, and saveth them, because they have taken refuge in him.
019	PSA	038	001	A Psalm of David, to bring to remembrance. O LORD, rebuke me not in thy wrath: neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.
019	PSA	038	002	For thine arrows stick fast in me, and thy hand presseth me sore.
019	PSA	038	003	There is no soundness in my flesh because of thine indignation; neither is there any health in my bones because of my sin.
019	PSA	038	004	For mine iniquities are gone over mine head: as an heavy burden they are too heavy for me.
019	PSA	038	005	My wounds stink and are corrupt, because of my foolishness.
019	PSA	038	006	I am pained and bowed down greatly; I go mourning all the day long.
019	PSA	038	007	For my loins are filled with burning; and there is no soundness in my flesh.
019	PSA	038	008	I am faint and sore bruised: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.
019	PSA	038	009	Lord, all my desire is before thee; and my groaning is not hid from thee.
019	PSA	038	010	My heart throbbeth, my strength faileth me: as for the light of mine eyes, it also is gone from me.
019	PSA	038	011	My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my plague; and my kinsmen stand afar off.
019	PSA	038	012	They also that seek after my life lay snares [for me]; and they that seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and imagine deceits all the day long.
019	PSA	038	013	But I, as a deaf man, hear not; and I am as a dumb man that openeth not his mouth.
019	PSA	038	014	Yea, I am as a man that heareth not, and in whose mouth are no reproofs.
019	PSA	038	015	For in thee, O LORD, do I hope: thou wilt answer, O Lord my God.
019	PSA	038	016	For I said, Lest they rejoice over me: when my foot slippeth, they magnify themselves against me.
019	PSA	038	017	For I am ready to halt, and my sorrow is continually before me.
019	PSA	038	018	For I will declare mine iniquity; I will be sorry for my sin.
019	PSA	038	019	But mine enemies are lively, [and] are strong: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied.
019	PSA	038	020	They also that render evil for good are adversaries unto me, because I follow the thing that is good.
019	PSA	038	021	Forsake me not, O LORD: O my God, be not far from me.
019	PSA	038	022	Make haste to help me, O Lord my salvation.
019	PSA	039	001	For the Chief Musician, for Jeduthun. A Psalm of David. I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.
019	PSA	039	002	I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, even from good; and my sorrow was stirred.
019	PSA	039	003	My heart was hot within me; while I was musing the fire kindled: [then] spake I with my tongue:
019	PSA	039	004	LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it is; let me know how frail I am.
019	PSA	039	005	Behold, thou hast made my days [as] handbreadths; and mine age is as nothing before thee: surely every man at his best estate is altogether vanity. (Selah)
019	PSA	039	006	Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up [riches], and knoweth not who shall gather them.
019	PSA	039	007	And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope is in thee.
019	PSA	039	008	Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.
019	PSA	039	009	I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst it.
019	PSA	039	010	Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand.
019	PSA	039	011	When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man is vanity. (Selah)
019	PSA	039	012	Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I am a stranger with thee, a sojourner, as all my fathers were.
019	PSA	039	013	O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.
019	PSA	040	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry.
019	PSA	040	002	He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay; and he set my feet upon a rock, and established my goings.
019	PSA	040	003	And he hath put a new song in my mouth, even praise unto our God: many shall see it, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.
019	PSA	040	004	Blessed is the man that maketh the LORD his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.
019	PSA	040	005	Many, O LORD my God, are the wonderful works which thou hast done, and thy thoughts which are to us-ward: they cannot be set in order unto thee; if I would declare and speak of them, they are more than can be numbered.
019	PSA	040	006	Sacrifice and offering thou hast no delight in; mine ears hast thou opened: burnt offering and sin offering hast thou not required.
019	PSA	040	007	Then said I, Lo, I am come; in the roll of the book it is written of me:
019	PSA	040	008	I delight to do thy will, O my God; yea, thy law is within my heart.
019	PSA	040	009	I have published righteousness in the great congregation; lo, I will not refrain my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.
019	PSA	040	010	I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy lovingkindness and thy truth from the great congregation.
019	PSA	040	011	Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O LORD: let thy lovingkindness and thy truth continually preserve me.
019	PSA	040	012	For innumerable evils have compassed me about, mine iniquities have overtaken me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of mine head, and my heart hath failed me.
019	PSA	040	013	Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me: make haste to help me, O LORD.
019	PSA	040	014	Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it: let them be turned backward and brought to dishonour that delight in my hurt.
019	PSA	040	015	Let them be desolate by reason of their shame that say unto me, Aha, Aha.
019	PSA	040	016	Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The LORD be magnified.
019	PSA	040	017	But I am poor and needy; [yet] the Lord thinketh upon me: thou art my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.
019	PSA	041	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. Blessed is he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in the day of evil.
019	PSA	041	002	The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive, and he shall be blessed upon the earth; and deliver not thou him unto the will of his enemies.
019	PSA	041	003	The LORD will support him upon the couch of languishing: thou makest all his bed in his sickness.
019	PSA	041	004	I said, O LORD, have mercy upon me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.
019	PSA	041	005	Mine enemies speak evil against me, [saying], When shall he die, and his name perish?
019	PSA	041	006	And if he come to see [me], he speaketh vanity; his heart gathereth iniquity to itself: when he goeth abroad, he telleth it.
019	PSA	041	007	All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt.
019	PSA	041	008	An evil disease, [say they], cleaveth fast unto him: and now that he lieth he shall rise up no more.
019	PSA	041	009	Yea, mine own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, which did eat of my bread, hath lifted up his heel against me.
019	PSA	041	010	But thou, O LORD, have mercy upon me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.
019	PSA	041	011	By this I know that thou delightest in me, because mine enemy doth not triumph over me.
019	PSA	041	012	And as for me, thou upholdest me in mine integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.
019	PSA	041	013	Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting and to everlasting. Amen, and Amen.
019	PSA	042	001	For the Chief Musician; Maschil of the sons of Korah. As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God.
019	PSA	042	002	My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?
019	PSA	042	003	My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where is thy God?
019	PSA	042	004	These things I remember, and pour out my soul within me, how I went with the throng, and led them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, a multitude keeping holyday.
019	PSA	042	005	Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and [why] art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him [for] the health of his countenance.
019	PSA	042	006	O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore do I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and the Hermons, from the hill Mizar.
019	PSA	042	007	Deep calleth unto deep at the noise of thy waterspouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.
019	PSA	042	008	[Yet] the LORD will command his lovingkindness in the day-time, and in the night his song shall be with me, [even] a prayer unto the God of my life.
019	PSA	042	009	I will say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
019	PSA	042	010	As with a sword in my bones, mine adversaries reproach me; while they continually say unto me, Where is thy God?
019	PSA	042	011	Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, [who is] the health of my countenance, and my God.
019	PSA	043	001	Judge me, O God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation: O deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man.
019	PSA	043	002	For thou art the God of my strength; why hast thou cast me off? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
019	PSA	043	003	O send out thy light and thy truth; let them lead me: let them bring me unto thy holy hill, and to thy tabernacles.
019	PSA	043	004	Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: and upon the harp will I praise thee, O God, my God.
019	PSA	043	005	Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, [who is] the health of my countenance, and my God.
019	PSA	044	001	For the Chief Musician; [a Psalm] of the sons of Korah. Maschil. We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, what work thou didst in their days, in the days of old.
019	PSA	044	002	Thou didst drive out the nations with thy hand, and plantedst them in; thou didst afflict the peoples, and didst spread them abroad.
019	PSA	044	003	For they gat not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favour unto them.
019	PSA	044	004	Thou art my King, O God: command deliverance for Jacob.
019	PSA	044	005	Through thee will we push down our adversaries: through thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.
019	PSA	044	006	For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.
019	PSA	044	007	But thou hast saved us from our adversaries, and hast put them to shame that hate us.
019	PSA	044	008	In God have we made our boast all the day long, and we will give thanks unto thy name for ever. (Selah)
019	PSA	044	009	But now thou hast cast [us] off, and brought us to dishonour; and goest not forth with our hosts.
019	PSA	044	010	Thou makest us to turn back from the adversary: and they which hate us spoil for themselves.
019	PSA	044	011	Thou hast given us like sheep [appointed] for meat; and hast scattered us among the nations.
019	PSA	044	012	Thou sellest thy people for nought, and hast not increased [thy wealth] by their price.
019	PSA	044	013	Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us.
019	PSA	044	014	Thou makest us a byword among the nations, a shaking of the head among the peoples.
019	PSA	044	015	All the day long is my dishonour before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,
019	PSA	044	016	For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and the avenger.
019	PSA	044	017	All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.
019	PSA	044	018	Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way;
019	PSA	044	019	That thou hast sore broken us in the place of jackals, and covered us with the shadow of death.
019	PSA	044	020	If we have forgotten the name of our God, or spread forth our hands to a strange god;
019	PSA	044	021	Shall not God search this out? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.
019	PSA	044	022	Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.
019	PSA	044	023	Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, cast [us] not off for ever.
019	PSA	044	024	Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and forgettest our affliction and our oppression?
019	PSA	044	025	For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth unto the earth.
019	PSA	044	026	Rise up for our help, and redeem us for thy lovingkindness’ sake.
019	PSA	045	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Shoshannim; [a Psalm] of the sons of Korah. Maschil. A Song of loves. My heart overfloweth with a goodly matter: I speak the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue is the pen of a ready writer.
019	PSA	045	002	Thou art fairer than the children of men; grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever.
019	PSA	045	003	Gird thy sword upon thy thigh, O mighty one, thy glory and thy majesty.
019	PSA	045	004	And in thy majesty ride on prosperously, because of truth and meekness [and] righteousness: and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things.
019	PSA	045	005	Thine arrows are sharp; the peoples fall under thee; [they are] in the heart of the king’s enemies.
019	PSA	045	006	Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever: a sceptre of equity is the sceptre of thy kingdom.
019	PSA	045	007	Thou hast loved righteousness, and hated wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.
019	PSA	045	008	All thy garments [smell of] myrrh, and aloes, [and] cassia; out of ivory palaces stringed instruments have made thee glad.
019	PSA	045	009	Kings’ daughters are among thy honourable women: at thy right hand doth stand the queen in gold of Ophir.
019	PSA	045	010	Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father’s house;
019	PSA	045	011	So shall the king desire thy beauty: for he is thy Lord; and worship thou him.
019	PSA	045	012	And the daughter of Tyre [shall be there] with a gift; even the rich among the people shall entreat thy favour.
019	PSA	045	013	The king’s daughter within [the palace] is all glorious: her clothing is inwrought with gold.
019	PSA	045	014	She shall be led unto the king in broidered work: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee.
019	PSA	045	015	With gladness and rejoicing shall they be led: they shall enter into the king’s palace.
019	PSA	045	016	Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou shalt make princes in all the earth.
019	PSA	045	017	I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the peoples give thee thanks for ever and ever.
019	PSA	046	001	For the Chief Musician: [a Psalm] of the sons of Korah; set to Alamoth. A Song. God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.
019	PSA	046	002	Therefore will we not fear, though the earth do change, and though the mountains be moved in the heart of the seas;
019	PSA	046	003	Though the waters thereof roar and be troubled, though the mountains shake with the swelling thereof. (Selah)
019	PSA	046	004	There is a river, the streams whereof make glad the city of God, the holy place of the tabernacles of the Most High.
019	PSA	046	005	God is in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, and that right early.
019	PSA	046	006	The nations raged, the kingdoms were moved: he uttered his voice, the earth melted.
019	PSA	046	007	The LORD of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our refuge. (Selah)
019	PSA	046	008	Come, behold the works of the LORD, what desolations he hath made in the earth.
019	PSA	046	009	He maketh wars to cease unto the end of the earth; he breaketh the bow, and cutteth the spear in sunder; he burneth the chariots in the fire.
019	PSA	046	010	Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted in the earth.
019	PSA	046	011	The LORD of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our refuge. (Selah)
019	PSA	047	001	For the Chief Musician; a Psalm of the sons of Korah. O clap your hands, all ye peoples; shout unto God with the voice of triumph.
019	PSA	047	002	For the LORD Most High is terrible; he is a great King over all the earth.
019	PSA	047	003	He shall subdue the peoples under us, and the nations under our feet.
019	PSA	047	004	He shall choose our inheritance for us, the excellency of Jacob whom he loved. (Selah)
019	PSA	047	005	God is gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.
019	PSA	047	006	Sing praises to God, sing praises: sing praises unto our King, sing praises.
019	PSA	047	007	For God is the King of all the earth: sing ye praises with understanding.
019	PSA	047	008	God reigneth over the nations: God sitteth upon his holy throne.
019	PSA	047	009	The princes of the peoples are gathered together [to be] the people of the God of Abraham: for the shields of the earth belong unto God; he is greatly exalted.
019	PSA	048	001	A Song; a Psalm of the sons of Korah. Great is the LORD, and highly to be praised, in the city of our God, in his holy mountain.
019	PSA	048	002	Beautiful in elevation, the joy of the whole earth, is mount Zion, [on] the sides of the north, the city of the great King.
019	PSA	048	003	God hath made himself known in her palaces for a refuge.
019	PSA	048	004	For, lo, the kings assembled themselves, they passed by together.
019	PSA	048	005	They saw it, then were they amazed; they were dismayed, they hasted away.
019	PSA	048	006	Trembling took hold of them there; pain, as of a woman in travail.
019	PSA	048	007	With the east wind thou breakest the ships of Tarshish.
019	PSA	048	008	As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the LORD of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. (Selah)
019	PSA	048	009	We have thought on thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.
019	PSA	048	010	As is thy name, O God, so is thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.
019	PSA	048	011	Let mount Zion be glad, let the daughters of Judah rejoice, because of thy judgments.
019	PSA	048	012	Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.
019	PSA	048	013	Mark ye welt her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell it to the generation following.
019	PSA	048	014	For this God is our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide [even] unto death.
019	PSA	049	001	For the Chief Musician; a Psalm of the sons of Korah. Hear this, all ye peoples; give ear, all ye inhabitants of the world:
019	PSA	049	002	Both low and high, rich and poor together.
019	PSA	049	003	My mouth shall speak wisdom; and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.
019	PSA	049	004	I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.
019	PSA	049	005	Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, when iniquity at my heels compasseth me about?
019	PSA	049	006	They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;
019	PSA	049	007	None [of them] can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:
019	PSA	049	008	(For the redemption of their soul is costly, and must be let alone for ever:)
019	PSA	049	009	That he should still live alway, that he should not see corruption.
019	PSA	049	010	For he seeth that wise men die, the fool and the brutish together perish, and leave their wealth to others.
019	PSA	049	011	Their inward thought is, [that] their houses [shall continue] for ever, [and] their dwelling places to all generations; they call their lands after their own names.
019	PSA	049	012	But man abideth not in honour: he is like the beasts that perish.
019	PSA	049	013	This their way is their folly: yet after them men approve their sayings. (Selah)
019	PSA	049	014	They are appointed as a flock for Sheol; death shall be their shepherd: and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall be for Sheol to consume, that there be no habitation for it.
019	PSA	049	015	But God will redeem my soul from the power of Sheol: for he shall receive me. (Selah)
019	PSA	049	016	Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased:
019	PSA	049	017	For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away; his glory shall not descend after him.
019	PSA	049	018	Though while he lived he blessed his soul, and men praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself,
019	PSA	049	019	He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see the light.
019	PSA	049	020	Man that is in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts that perish.
019	PSA	050	001	A Psalm of Asaph. God, [even] God, the LORD, hath spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun unto the going down thereof.
019	PSA	050	002	Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God hath shined forth.
019	PSA	050	003	Our God shall come, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall devour before him, and it shall be very tempestuous round about him.
019	PSA	050	004	He shall call to the heavens above, and to the earth, that he may judge his people:
019	PSA	050	005	Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.
019	PSA	050	006	And the heavens shall declare his righteousness; for God is judge himself. (Selah)
019	PSA	050	007	Hear, O my people, and I will speak; O Israel, and I will testify unto thee: I am God, [even] thy God.
019	PSA	050	008	I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices; and thy burnt offerings are continually before me.
019	PSA	050	009	I will take no bullock out of thy house, nor he-goats out of thy folds.
019	PSA	050	010	For every beast of the forest is mine, and the cattle upon a thousand hills.
019	PSA	050	011	I know all the fowls of the mountains: and the wild beasts of the field are mine.
019	PSA	050	012	If I were hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world is mine, and the fulness thereof.
019	PSA	050	013	Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?
019	PSA	050	014	Offer unto God the sacrifice of thanksgiving; and pay thy vows unto the Most High:
019	PSA	050	015	And call upon me in the day of trouble; I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.
019	PSA	050	016	But unto the wicked God saith, What hast thou to do to declare my statutes; and that thou hast taken my covenant in thy mouth?
019	PSA	050	017	Seeing thou hatest instruction, and castest my words behind thee.
019	PSA	050	018	When thou sawest a thief, thou consentedst with him, and hast been partaker with adulterers.
019	PSA	050	019	Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and thy tongue frameth deceit.
019	PSA	050	020	Thou sittest and speakest against thy brother; thou slanderest thine own mother’s son.
019	PSA	050	021	These things hast thou done, and I kept silence; thou thoughtest that I was altogether such an one as thyself: [but] I will reprove thee, and set [them] in order before thine eyes.
019	PSA	050	022	Now consider this, ye that forget God, lest I tear you in pieces, and there be none to deliver:
019	PSA	050	023	Whoso offereth the sacrifice of thanksgiving glorifieth me; and to him that ordereth his conversation [aright] will I shew the salvation of God.
019	PSA	051	001	For the Chief Musician. A psalm of David: when Nathan the prophet came unto him, after he had gone in to Bath-sheba. Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness; according to the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.
019	PSA	051	002	Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.
019	PSA	051	003	For I acknowledge my transgressions: and my sin is ever before me.
019	PSA	051	004	Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done that which is evil in thy sight: that thou mayest be justified when thou speakest, and be clear when thou judgest.
019	PSA	051	005	Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me.
019	PSA	051	006	Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts: and in the hidden part thou shalt make me to know wisdom.
019	PSA	051	007	Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean: wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.
019	PSA	051	008	Make me to hear joy and gladness; that the bones which thou hast broken may rejoice.
019	PSA	051	009	Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all mine iniquities.
019	PSA	051	010	Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.
019	PSA	051	011	Cast me not away from thy presence; and take not thy holy spirit from me.
019	PSA	051	012	Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation: and uphold me with a free spirit.
019	PSA	051	013	Then will I teach transgressors thy ways; and sinners shall be converted unto thee.
019	PSA	051	014	Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation; [and] my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness.
019	PSA	051	015	O Lord, open thou my lips; and my mouth shall shew forth thy praise.
019	PSA	051	016	For thou delightest not in sacrifice; else would I give it: thou hast no pleasure in burnt offering.
019	PSA	051	017	The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.
019	PSA	051	018	Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion: build thou the walls of Jerusalem.
019	PSA	051	019	Then shalt thou delight in the sacrifices of righteousness, in burnt offering and whole burnt offering: then shall they offer bullocks upon thine altar.
019	PSA	052	001	For the Chief Musician. Maschil of David: when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, and said unto him, David is come to the house of Ahimelech. Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the mercy of God [endureth] continually.
019	PSA	052	002	Thy tongue deviseth very wickedness; like a sharp razor, working deceitfully.
019	PSA	052	003	Thou lovest evil more than good; and lying rather than to speak righteousness. (Selah)
019	PSA	052	004	Thou lovest all devouring words, O thou deceitful tongue.
019	PSA	052	005	God shall likewise destroy thee for ever, he shall take thee up, and pluck thee out of thy tent, and root thee out of the land of the living. (Selah)
019	PSA	052	006	The righteous also shall see [it], and fear, and shall laugh at him, [saying],
019	PSA	052	007	Lo, this is the man that made not God his strength; but trusted in the abundance of his riches, and strengthened himself in his wickedness.
019	PSA	052	008	But as for me, I am like a green olive tree in the house of God: I trust in the mercy of God for ever and ever.
019	PSA	052	009	I will give thee thanks for ever, because thou hast done it: and I will wait on thy name, for it is good, in the presence of thy saints.
019	PSA	053	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Mahalath. Maschil of David. The fool hath said in his heart, There is no God. Corrupt are they, and have done abominable iniquity; there is none that doeth good.
019	PSA	053	002	God looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, that did seek after God.
019	PSA	053	003	Every one of them is gone back; they are together become filthy; there is none that doeth good, no, not one.
019	PSA	053	004	Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people as they eat bread, and call not upon God.
019	PSA	053	005	There were they in great fear, where no fear was: for God hath scattered the bones of him that encampeth against thee; thou hast put them to shame, because God hath rejected them.
019	PSA	053	006	Oh that the salvation of Israel were come out of Zion! When God bringeth back the captivity of his people, then shall Jacob rejoice, [and] Israel shall be glad.
019	PSA	054	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. Maschil of David: when the Ziphites came and said to Saul, Doth not David hide himself with us? Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me in thy might.
019	PSA	054	002	Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to the words of my mouth.
019	PSA	054	003	For strangers are risen up against me, and violent men have sought after my soul: they have not set God before them. (Selah)
019	PSA	054	004	Behold, God is mine helper: the Lord is of them that uphold my soul.
019	PSA	054	005	He shall requite the evil unto mine enemies: destroy thou them in thy truth.
019	PSA	054	006	With a freewill offering will I sacrifice unto thee: I will give thanks unto thy name, O LORD, for it is good.
019	PSA	054	007	For he hath delivered me out of all trouble; and mine eye hath seen [my desire] upon mine enemies.
019	PSA	055	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. Maschil of David. Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.
019	PSA	055	002	Attend unto me, and answer me: I am restless in my complaint, and moan;
019	PSA	055	003	Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked; for they cast iniquity upon me, and in anger they persecute me.
019	PSA	055	004	My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.
019	PSA	055	005	Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.
019	PSA	055	006	And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! then would I fly away, and be at rest.
019	PSA	055	007	Lo, then would I wander far off, I would lodge in the wilderness. (Selah)
019	PSA	055	008	I would haste me to a shelter from the stormy wind and tempest.
019	PSA	055	009	Destroy, O Lord, [and] divide their tongue: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.
019	PSA	055	010	Day and night they go about upon the walls thereof: iniquity also and mischief are in the midst of it.
019	PSA	055	011	Wickedness is in the midst thereof: oppression and guile depart not from her streets.
019	PSA	055	012	For it was not an enemy that reproached me; then I could have borne it: neither was it he that hated me that did magnify himself against me; then I would have hid myself from him:
019	PSA	055	013	But it was thou, a man mine equal, my companion, and my familiar friend.
019	PSA	055	014	We took sweet counsel together, we walked in the house of God with the throng.
019	PSA	055	015	Let death come suddenly upon them, let them go down alive into the pit: for wickedness is in their dwelling, in the midst of them.
019	PSA	055	016	As for me, I will call upon God; and the LORD shall save me.
019	PSA	055	017	Evening, and morning, and at noonday, will I complain, and moan: and he shall hear my voice.
019	PSA	055	018	He hath redeemed my soul in peace from the battle that was against me: for they were many [that strove] with me.
019	PSA	055	019	God shall hear, and answer them, even he that abideth of old, (Selah) [the men] who have no changes, and who fear not God.
019	PSA	055	020	He hath put forth his hands against such as were at peace with him: he hath profaned his covenant.
019	PSA	055	021	His mouth was smooth as butter, but his heart was war: his words were softer than oil, yet were they drawn swords.
019	PSA	055	022	Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.
019	PSA	055	023	But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.
019	PSA	056	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Jonath elem rehokim. [A Psalm] of David: Michtam: when the Philistines took him in Gath. Be merciful unto me, O God; for man would swallow me up: all the day long he fighting oppresseth me.
019	PSA	056	002	Mine enemies would swallow me up all the day long: for they be many that fight proudly against me.
019	PSA	056	003	What time I am afraid, I will put my trust in thee.
019	PSA	056	004	In God I will praise his word: in God have I put my trust, I will not be afraid; what can flesh do unto me?
019	PSA	056	005	All the day long they wrest my words: all their thoughts are against me for evil.
019	PSA	056	006	They gather themselves together, they hide themselves, they mark my steps, even as they have waited for my soul.
019	PSA	056	007	Shall they escape by iniquity? in anger cast down the peoples, O God.
019	PSA	056	008	Thou tellest my wanderings: put thou my tears into thy bottle; are they not in thy book?
019	PSA	056	009	Then shall mine enemies turn back in the day that I call: this I know, that God is for me.
019	PSA	056	010	In God will I praise [his] word: in the LORD will I praise [his] word.
019	PSA	056	011	In God have I put my trust, I will not be afraid; what can man do unto me?
019	PSA	056	012	Thy vows are upon me, O God: I will render thank offerings unto thee.
019	PSA	056	013	For thou hast delivered my soul from death: [hast thou] not [delivered] my feet from falling? that I may walk before God in the light of the living.
019	PSA	057	001	For the Chief Musician; [set to] Al-tashheth. [A Psalm] of David: Michtam: when he fled from Saul, in the cave. Be merciful unto me, O God, be merciful unto me; for my soul taketh refuge in thee: yea, in the shadow of thy wings will I take refuge, until [these] calamities be overpast.
019	PSA	057	002	I will cry unto God Most High; unto God that performeth [all things] for me.
019	PSA	057	003	He shall send from heaven, and save me, [when] he that would swallow me up reproacheth; (Selah) God shall send forth his mercy and his truth.
019	PSA	057	004	My soul is among lions; I lie among them that are set on fire, even the sons of men, whose teeth are spears and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.
019	PSA	057	005	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens; [let] thy glory [be] above all the earth.
019	PSA	057	006	They have prepared a net for my steps; thy soul is bowed down: they have digged a pit before me; they are fallen into the midst thereof themselves. (Selah)
019	PSA	057	007	My heart is fixed, O God, my heart is fixed: I will sing, yea, I will sing praises.
019	PSA	057	008	Awake up, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I myself will awake right early.
019	PSA	057	009	I will give thanks unto thee, O Lord, among the peoples: I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.
019	PSA	057	010	For thy mercy is great unto the heavens, and thy truth unto the skies.
019	PSA	057	011	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens; [let] thy glory [be] above all the earth.
019	PSA	058	001	For the Chief Musician; [set to] Al-tashheth. [A Psalm] of David: Michtam. Do ye indeed in silence speak righteousness? do ye judge uprightly, O ye sons of men?
019	PSA	058	002	Yea, in heart ye work wickedness; ye weigh out the violence of your hands in the earth.
019	PSA	058	003	The wicked are estranged from the womb: they go astray as soon as they be born, speaking lies.
019	PSA	058	004	Their poison is like the poison of a serpent: [they are] like the deaf adder that stoppeth her ear;
019	PSA	058	005	Which hearkeneth not to the voice of charmers, charming never so wisely.
019	PSA	058	006	Break their teeth, O God, in their mouth: break out the great teeth of the young lions, O LORD.
019	PSA	058	007	Let them melt away as water that runneth apace: when he aimeth his arrows, let them be as though they were cut off.
019	PSA	058	008	[Let them be] as a snail which melteth and passeth away: [like] the untimely birth of a woman, that hath not seen the sun.
019	PSA	058	009	Before your pots can feel the thorns, he shall take them away with a whirlwind, the green and the burning alike.
019	PSA	058	010	The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.
019	PSA	058	011	So that men shall say, Verily there is a reward for the righteous: verily there is a God that judgeth in the earth.
019	PSA	059	001	For the Chief Musician; [set to] Al-tashheth. [A Psalm] of David: Michtam: when Saul sent, and they watched the house to kill him. Deliver me from mine enemies, O my God: set me on high from them that rise up against me.
019	PSA	059	002	Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from the bloodthirsty men.
019	PSA	059	003	For, lo, they lie in wait for my soul; the mighty gather themselves together against me: not for my transgression, nor for my sin, O LORD.
019	PSA	059	004	They run and prepare themselves without [my] fault: awake thou to help me, and behold.
019	PSA	059	005	Even thou, O LORD God of hosts, the God of Israel, arise to visit all the heathen: be not merciful to any wicked transgressors. (Selah)
019	PSA	059	006	They return at evening, they make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
019	PSA	059	007	Behold, they belch out with their mouth; swords are in their lips: for who, [say they], doth hear?
019	PSA	059	008	But thou, O LORD, shalt laugh at them; thou shalt have all the heathen in derision.
019	PSA	059	009	O my strength, I will wait upon thee: for God is my high tower.
019	PSA	059	010	The God of my mercy shall prevent me: God shall let me see [my desire] upon mine enemies.
019	PSA	059	011	Slay them not, lest my people forget: scatter them by thy power, and bring them down, O Lord our shield.
019	PSA	059	012	[For] the sin of their mouth, [and] the words of their lips, let them even be taken in their pride, and for cursing and lying which they speak.
019	PSA	059	013	Consume them in wrath, consume them, that they be no more: and let them know that God ruleth in Jacob, unto the ends of the earth. (Selah)
019	PSA	059	014	And at evening let them return, let them make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
019	PSA	059	015	They shall wander up and down for meat and tarry all night if they be not satisfied.
019	PSA	059	016	But I will sing of thy strength; yea, I will sing aloud of thy mercy in the morning: for thou hast been my high tower, and a refuge in the day of my distress.
019	PSA	059	017	Unto thee, O my strength, will I sing praises: for God is my high tower, the God of my mercy.
019	PSA	060	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Shushan Eduth: Michtam of David, to teach: when he strove with Aram-naharaim and with Aram-zobah, and Joab returned, and smote of Edom in the Valley of Salt twelve thousand. O God, thou hast cast us off, thou hast broken us down; thou hast been angry; O restore us again.
019	PSA	060	002	Thou hast made the land to tremble; thou hast rent it: heal the breaches thereof; for it shaketh.
019	PSA	060	003	Thou hast shewed thy people hard things: thou hast made us to drink the wine of staggering.
019	PSA	060	004	Thou hast given a banner to them that fear thee, that it may be displayed because of the truth. (Selah)
019	PSA	060	005	That thy beloved may be delivered, save with thy right hand, and answer us.
019	PSA	060	006	God hath spoken in his holiness; I will exult: I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
019	PSA	060	007	Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine; Ephraim also is the defence of mine head; Judah is my sceptre.
019	PSA	060	008	Moab is my washpot; upon Edom will I cast my shoe: Philistia, shout thou because of me.
019	PSA	060	009	Who will bring me into the strong city? who hath led me unto Edom?
019	PSA	060	010	Hast not thou, O God, cast us off? and thou goest not forth, O God, with our hosts.
019	PSA	060	011	Give us help against the adversary: for vain is the help of man.
019	PSA	060	012	Through God we shall do valiantly: for he it is that shall tread down our adversaries.
019	PSA	061	001	For the Chief Musician; on a stringed instrument. [A Psalm] of David. Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my prayer.
019	PSA	061	002	From the end of the earth will I call unto thee, when my heart is overwhelmed: lead me to the rock that is higher than I.
019	PSA	061	003	For thou hast been a refuge for me, a strong tower from the enemy.
019	PSA	061	004	I will dwell in thy tabernacle for ever: I will take refuge in the covert of thy wings. (Selah)
019	PSA	061	005	For thou, O God, hast heard my vows: thou hast given [me] the heritage of those that fear thy name.
019	PSA	061	006	Thou wilt prolong the king’s life: his years shall be as many generations.
019	PSA	061	007	He shall abide before God for ever: O prepare lovingkindness and truth, that they may preserve him.
019	PSA	061	008	So will I sing praise unto thy name for ever, that I may daily perform my vows.
019	PSA	062	001	For the Chief Musician; after the manner of Jeduthun. A Psalm of David. My soul waiteth only upon God: from him [cometh] my salvation.
019	PSA	062	002	He only is my rock and my salvation: [he is] my high tower; I shall not be greatly moved.
019	PSA	062	003	How long will ye set upon a man, that ye may slay [him], all of you, like a bowing wall, like a tottering fence?
019	PSA	062	004	They only consult to thrust him down from his excellency; they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. (Selah)
019	PSA	062	005	My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.
019	PSA	062	006	He only is my rock and my salvation: [he is] my high tower; I shall not be moved.
019	PSA	062	007	With God is my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God.
019	PSA	062	008	Trust in him at all times, ye people; pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. (Selah)
019	PSA	062	009	Surely men of low degree are vanity, and men of high degree are a lie: in the balances they will go up; they are together lighter than vanity.
019	PSA	062	010	Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart [thereon].
019	PSA	062	011	God hath spoken once, twice have I heard this; that power belongeth unto God:
019	PSA	062	012	Also unto thee, O Lord, belongeth mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.
019	PSA	063	001	A Psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Judah. O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee, in a dry and weary land, where no water is.
019	PSA	063	002	So have I looked upon thee in the sanctuary, to see thy power and thy glory.
019	PSA	063	003	For thy lovingkindness is better than life; my lips shall praise thee.
019	PSA	063	004	So will I bless thee while I live: I will lift up my hands in thy name.
019	PSA	063	005	My soul shall be satisfied as with marrow and fatness; and my mouth shall praise thee with joyful lips;
019	PSA	063	006	When I remember thee upon my bed, [and] meditate on thee in the night watches.
019	PSA	063	007	For thou hast been my help, and in the shadow of thy wings will I rejoice.
019	PSA	063	008	My soul followeth hard after thee: thy right hand upholdeth me.
019	PSA	063	009	But those that seek my soul, to destroy it, shall go into the lower parts of the earth.
019	PSA	063	010	They shall be given over to the power of the sword: they shall be a portion for foxes.
019	PSA	063	011	But the king shall rejoice in God: every one that sweareth by him shall glory; for the mouth of them that speak lies shall be stopped.
019	PSA	064	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. Hear my voice, O God, in my complaint: preserve my life from fear of the enemy.
019	PSA	064	002	Hide me from the secret counsel of evil-doers; from the tumult of the workers of iniquity:
019	PSA	064	003	Who have whet their tongue like a sword, and have aimed their arrows, even bitter words:
019	PSA	064	004	That they may shoot in secret places at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not.
019	PSA	064	005	They encourage themselves in an evil purpose; they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who shall see them?
019	PSA	064	006	They search out iniquities; We have accomplished, [say they], a diligent search: and the inward thought of every one, and the heart, is deep.
019	PSA	064	007	But God shall shoot at them; with an arrow suddenly shall they be wounded.
019	PSA	064	008	So they shall be made to stumble, their own tongue being against them: all that see them shall wag the head.
019	PSA	064	009	And all men shall fear; and they shall declare the work of God, and shall wisely consider of his doing.
019	PSA	064	010	The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory.
019	PSA	065	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm. A Song of David. Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Zion: and unto thee shall the vow be performed.
019	PSA	065	002	O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.
019	PSA	065	003	Iniquities prevail against me: as for our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.
019	PSA	065	004	Blessed is the man whom thou choosest, and causest to approach [unto thee], that he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, the holy place of thy temple.
019	PSA	065	005	By terrible things thou wilt answer us in righteousness, O God of our salvation; thou that art the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off upon the sea:
019	PSA	065	006	Which by his strength setteth fast the mountains; being girded about with might:
019	PSA	065	007	Which stilleth the roaring of the seas, the roaring of their waves, and the tumult of the peoples.
019	PSA	065	008	They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.
019	PSA	065	009	Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it, thou greatly enrichest it; the river of God is full of water: thou providest them corn, when thou hast so prepared the earth.
019	PSA	065	010	Thou waterest her furrows abundantly; thou settlest the ridges thereof: thou makest it soft with showers; thou blessest the springing thereof.
019	PSA	065	011	Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.
019	PSA	065	012	They drop upon the pastures of the wilderness: and the hills are girded with joy.
019	PSA	065	013	The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.
019	PSA	066	001	For the Chief Musician. A Song, a Psalm. Make a joyful noise unto God, all the earth:
019	PSA	066	002	Sing forth the glory of his name: make his praise glorious.
019	PSA	066	003	Say unto God, How terrible are thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee.
019	PSA	066	004	All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing to thy name. (Selah)
019	PSA	066	005	Come, and see the works of God; [he is] terrible in his doing toward the children of men.
019	PSA	066	006	He turned the sea into dry land: they went through the river on foot: there did we rejoice in him.
019	PSA	066	007	He ruleth by his might for ever; his eyes observe the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. (Selah)
019	PSA	066	008	O bless our God, ye peoples, and make the voice of his praise to be heard.
019	PSA	066	009	Which holdeth our soul in life, and suffereth not our feet to be moved.
019	PSA	066	010	For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried.
019	PSA	066	011	Thou broughtest us into the net; thou layedst a sore burden upon our loins.
019	PSA	066	012	Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water; but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place.
019	PSA	066	013	I will come into thy house with burnt offerings, I will pay thee my vows,
019	PSA	066	014	Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in distress.
019	PSA	066	015	I will offer unto thee burnt offerings of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. (Selah)
019	PSA	066	016	Come, and hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul.
019	PSA	066	017	I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue.
019	PSA	066	018	If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear:
019	PSA	066	019	But verily God hath heard; he hath attended to the voice of my prayer.
019	PSA	066	020	Blessed be God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.
019	PSA	067	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. A Psalm, a Song. God be merciful unto us, and bless us, [and] cause his face to shine upon us; (Selah)
019	PSA	067	002	That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.
019	PSA	067	003	Let the peoples praise thee, O God; let all the peoples praise thee.
019	PSA	067	004	O let the nations be glad and sing for joy: for thou shalt judge the peoples with equity, and govern the nations upon earth. (Selah)
019	PSA	067	005	Let the peoples praise thee, O God; let all the peoples praise thee.
019	PSA	067	006	The earth hath yielded her increase: God, even our own God, shall bless us.
019	PSA	067	007	God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.
019	PSA	068	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David, a Song. Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered; let them also that hate him flee before him.
019	PSA	068	002	As smoke is driven away, so drive them away: as wax melteth before the fire, so let the wicked perish at the presence of God.
019	PSA	068	003	But let the righteous be glad; let them exult before God: yea, let them rejoice with gladness.
019	PSA	068	004	Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: cast up a highway for him that rideth through the deserts; his name is JAH; and exult ye before him.
019	PSA	068	005	A father of the fatherless, and a judge of the widows, is God in his holy habitation.
019	PSA	068	006	God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out the prisoners into prosperity: but the rebellious dwell in a parched land.
019	PSA	068	007	O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; (Selah)
019	PSA	068	008	The earth trembled, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: [even] yon Sinai [trembled] at the presence of God, the God of Israel.
019	PSA	068	009	Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary.
019	PSA	068	010	Thy congregation dwelt therein: thou, O God, didst prepare of thy goodness for the poor.
019	PSA	068	011	The Lord giveth the word: the women that publish the tidings are a great host.
019	PSA	068	012	Kings of armies flee, they flee: and she that tarrieth at home divideth the spoil.
019	PSA	068	013	Will ye lie among the sheepfolds, [as] the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her pinions with yellow gold?
019	PSA	068	014	When the Almighty scattered kings therein, [it was as when] it snoweth in Zalmon.
019	PSA	068	015	A mountain of God is the mountain of Bashan; an high mountain is the mountain of Bashan.
019	PSA	068	016	Why look ye askance, ye high mountains, at the mountain which God hath desired for his abode? yea, the LORD will dwell [in it] for ever.
019	PSA	068	017	The chariots of God are twenty thousand, even thousands upon thousands: the Lord is among them, [as in] Sinai, in the sanctuary.
019	PSA	068	018	Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led [thy] captivity captive; thou hast received gifts among men, yea, [among] the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell [with them].
019	PSA	068	019	Blessed be the Lord, who daily beareth our burden, even the God who is our salvation. (Selah)
019	PSA	068	020	God is unto us a God of deliverances; and unto JEHOVAH the Lord belong the issues from death.
019	PSA	068	021	But God shall smite through the head of his enemies, the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his guiltiness.
019	PSA	068	022	The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring [them] again from the depths of the sea:
019	PSA	068	023	That thou mayest dip thy foot in blood, that the tongue of thy dogs may have its portion from [thine] enemies.
019	PSA	068	024	They have seen thy goings, O God, even the goings of my God, my King, into the sanctuary.
019	PSA	068	025	The singers went before, the minstrels followed after, in the midst of the damsels playing with timbrels.
019	PSA	068	026	Bless ye God in the congregations, even the Lord, [ye that are] of the fountain of Israel.
019	PSA	068	027	There is little Benjamin their ruler, the princes of Judah [and] their council, the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Naphtali.
019	PSA	068	028	Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.
019	PSA	068	029	Because of thy temple at Jerusalem kings shall bring presents unto thee.
019	PSA	068	030	Rebuke the wild beast of the reeds, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the peoples, trampling under foot the pieces of silver; he hath scattered the peoples that delight in war.
019	PSA	068	031	Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall haste to stretch out her hands unto God.
019	PSA	068	032	Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; (Selah)
019	PSA	068	033	To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, which are of old; lo, he uttereth his voice, [and that] a mighty voice.
019	PSA	068	034	Ascribe ye strength unto God: his excellency is over Israel, and his strength is in the skies.
019	PSA	068	035	O God, [thou art] terrible out of thy holy places: the God of Israel, he giveth strength and power unto [his] people. Blessed be God.
019	PSA	069	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Shoshannim. [A Psalm] of David. Save me, O God; for the waters are come in unto my soul.
019	PSA	069	002	I sink in deep mire, where there is no standing: I am come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.
019	PSA	069	003	I am weary with my crying; my throat is dried: mine eyes fail while I wait for my God.
019	PSA	069	004	They that hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of mine head: they that would cut me off, being mine enemies wrongfully, are mighty: then I restored that which I took not away.
019	PSA	069	005	O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my sins are not hid from thee.
019	PSA	069	006	Let not them that wait on thee be ashamed through me, O Lord GOD of hosts: let not those that seek thee be brought to dishonour through me, O God of Israel.
019	PSA	069	007	Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.
019	PSA	069	008	I am become a stranger unto my brethren, and an alien unto my mother’s children.
019	PSA	069	009	For the zeal of thine house hath eaten me up; and the reproaches of them that reproach thee are fallen upon me.
019	PSA	069	010	When I wept, [and chastened] my soul with fasting, that was to my reproach.
019	PSA	069	011	When I made sackcloth my clothing, I became a proverb unto them.
019	PSA	069	012	They that sit in the gate talk of me; and [I am] the song of the drunkards.
019	PSA	069	013	But as for me, my prayer is unto thee, O LORD, in an acceptable time: O God, in the multitude of thy mercy, answer me in the truth of thy salvation.
019	PSA	069	014	Deliver me out of the mire, and let me not sink: let me be delivered from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.
019	PSA	069	015	Let not the waterflood overwhelm me, neither let the deep swallow me up; and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.
019	PSA	069	016	Answer me, O LORD; for thy lovingkindness is good: according to the multitude of thy tender mercies turn thou unto me.
019	PSA	069	017	And hide not thy face from thy servant; for I am in distress; answer me speedily.
019	PSA	069	018	Draw nigh unto my soul, and redeem it: ransom me because of mine enemies.
019	PSA	069	019	Thou knowest my reproach, and my shame, and my dishonour: mine adversaries are all before thee.
019	PSA	069	020	Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness: and I looked for some to take pity, but there was none; and for comforters, but I found none.
019	PSA	069	021	They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.
019	PSA	069	022	Let their table before them become a snare; and when they are in peace, [let it become] a trap.
019	PSA	069	023	Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not; and make their loins continually to shake.
019	PSA	069	024	Pour out thine indignation upon them, and let the fierceness of thine anger overtake them.
019	PSA	069	025	Let their habitation be desolate; let none dwell in their tents.
019	PSA	069	026	For they persecute him whom thou hast smitten; and they tell of the sorrow of those whom thou hast wounded,
019	PSA	069	027	Add iniquity unto their iniquity: and let them not come into thy righteousness.
019	PSA	069	028	Let them be blotted out of the book of life, and not be written with the righteous.
019	PSA	069	029	But I am poor and sorrowful: let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.
019	PSA	069	030	I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.
019	PSA	069	031	And it shall please the LORD better than an ox, [or] a bullock that hath horns and hoofs.
019	PSA	069	032	The meek have seen it, and are glad: ye that seek after God, let your heart live.
019	PSA	069	033	For the LORD heareth the needy, and despiseth not his prisoners.
019	PSA	069	034	Let heaven and earth praise him, the seas, and every thing that moveth therein.
019	PSA	069	035	For God will save Zion, and build the cities of Judah; and they shall abide there, and have it in possession.
019	PSA	069	036	The seed also of his servants shall inherit it; and they that love his name shall dwell therein.
019	PSA	070	001	For the Chief Musician. [A Psalm] of David; to bring to remembrance. [Make haste], O God, to deliver me; make haste to help me, O LORD.
019	PSA	070	002	Let them be ashamed and confounded that seek after my soul: let them be turned backward and brought to dishonour that delight in my hurt.
019	PSA	070	003	Let them be turned back by reason of their shame that say, Aha, Aha.
019	PSA	070	004	Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee; and let such as love thy salvation say continually, Let God be magnified.
019	PSA	070	005	But I am poor and needy; make haste unto me, O God: thou art my help and my deliverer; O LORD, make no tarrying.
019	PSA	071	001	In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust: let me never be ashamed.
019	PSA	071	002	Deliver me in thy righteousness, and rescue me: bow down thine ear unto me, and save me.
019	PSA	071	003	Be thou to me a rock of habitation, whereunto I may continually resort: thou hast given commandment to save me; for thou art my rock and my fortress.
019	PSA	071	004	Rescue me, O my God, out of the hand of the wicked, out of the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man.
019	PSA	071	005	For thou art my hope, O Lord GOD: [thou art] my trust from my youth.
019	PSA	071	006	By thee have I been holden up from the womb: thou art he that took me out of my mother’s bowels: my praise shall be continually of thee.
019	PSA	071	007	I am as a wonder unto many; but thou art my strong refuge.
019	PSA	071	008	My mouth shall be filled with thy praise, and with thy honour all the day.
019	PSA	071	009	Cast me not off in the time of old age; forsake me not when my strength faileth.
019	PSA	071	010	For mine enemies speak concerning me; and they that watch for my soul take counsel together,
019	PSA	071	011	Saying, God hath forsaken him: pursue and take him; for there is none to deliver.
019	PSA	071	012	O God, be not far from me: O my God, make haste to help me.
019	PSA	071	013	Let them be ashamed [and] consumed that are adversaries to my soul; let them be covered with reproach and dishonour that seek my hurt.
019	PSA	071	014	But I will hope continually, and will praise thee yet more and more.
019	PSA	071	015	My mouth shall tell of thy righteousness, [and] of thy salvation all the day; for I know not the numbers [thereof].
019	PSA	071	016	I will come with the mighty acts of the Lord GOD: I will make mention of thy righteousness, even of thine only.
019	PSA	071	017	O God, thou hast taught me from my youth; and hitherto have I declared thy wondrous works.
019	PSA	071	018	Yea, even when I am old and grayheaded, O God, forsake me not; until I have declared thy strength unto [the next] generation, thy might to every one that is to come.
019	PSA	071	019	Thy righteousness also, O God, is very high; thou who hast done great things, O God, who is like unto thee?
019	PSA	071	020	Thou, which hast shewed us many and sore troubles, shalt quicken us again, and shalt bring us up again from the depths of the earth.
019	PSA	071	021	Increase thou my greatness, and turn again and comfort me.
019	PSA	071	022	I will also praise thee with the psaltery, [even] thy truth, O my God: unto thee will I sing praises with the harp, O thou Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	071	023	My lips shall greatly rejoice when I sing praises unto thee; and my soul, which thou hast redeemed.
019	PSA	071	024	My tongue also shall talk of thy righteousness all the day long: for they are ashamed, for they are confounded, that seek my hurt.
019	PSA	072	001	[A Psalm] of Solomon. Give the king thy judgments, O God, and thy righteousness unto the king’s son.
019	PSA	072	002	He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment.
019	PSA	072	003	The mountains shall bring peace to the people, and the hills, in righteousness.
019	PSA	072	004	He shall judge the poor of the people, he shall save the children of the needy, and shall break in pieces the oppressor.
019	PSA	072	005	They shall fear thee while the sun endureth, and so long as the moon, throughout all generations.
019	PSA	072	006	He shall come down like rain upon the mown grass: as showers that water the earth.
019	PSA	072	007	In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace, till the moon be no more.
019	PSA	072	008	He shall have dominion also from sea to sea, and from the River unto the ends of the earth.
019	PSA	072	009	They that dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him; and his enemies shall lick the dust.
019	PSA	072	010	The kings of Tarshish and of the isles shall bring presents: the kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts.
019	PSA	072	011	Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him.
019	PSA	072	012	For he shall deliver the needy when he crieth; and the poor, that hath no helper.
019	PSA	072	013	He shall have pity on the poor and needy, and the souls of the needy he shall save.
019	PSA	072	014	He shall redeem their soul from oppression and violence; and precious shall their blood be in his sight:
019	PSA	072	015	And they shall live; and to him shall be given of the gold of Sheba: and men shall pray for him continually; they shall bless him all the day long.
019	PSA	072	016	There shall be abundance of corn in the earth upon the top of the mountains; the fruit thereof shall shake like Lebanon: and they of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.
019	PSA	072	017	His name shall endure for ever; his name shall be continued as long as the sun: and men shall be blessed in him; all nations shall call him happy.
019	PSA	072	018	Blessed be the LORD God, the God of Israel, who only doeth wondrous things:
019	PSA	072	019	And blessed be his glorious name for ever; and let the whole earth be filled with his glory. Amen, and Amen.
019	PSA	072	020	The prayers of David the son of Jesse are ended.
019	PSA	073	001	A Psalm of Asaph. Surely God is good to Israel, [even] to such as are pure in heart.
019	PSA	073	002	But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.
019	PSA	073	003	For I was envious at the arrogant, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.
019	PSA	073	004	For there are no bands in their death: but their strength is firm.
019	PSA	073	005	They are not in trouble as [other] men; neither are they plagued like [other] men.
019	PSA	073	006	Therefore pride is as a chain about their neck; violence covereth them as a garment.
019	PSA	073	007	Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.
019	PSA	073	008	They scoff, and in wickedness utter oppression: they speak loftily.
019	PSA	073	009	They have set their mouth in the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.
019	PSA	073	010	Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full [cup] are wrung out by them.
019	PSA	073	011	And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the Most High?
019	PSA	073	012	Behold, these are the wicked; and, being alway at ease, they increase in riches.
019	PSA	073	013	Surely in vain have I cleansed my heart, and washed my hands in innocency;
019	PSA	073	014	For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.
019	PSA	073	015	If I had said, I will speak thus; behold, I had dealt treacherously with the generation of thy children.
019	PSA	073	016	When I thought how I might know this, it was too painful for me;
019	PSA	073	017	Until I went into the sanctuary of God, and considered their latter end.
019	PSA	073	018	Surely thou settest them in slippery places: thou castest them down to destruction.
019	PSA	073	019	How are they become a desolation in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.
019	PSA	073	020	As a dream when one awaketh; so, O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.
019	PSA	073	021	For my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins:
019	PSA	073	022	So brutish was I, and ignorant; I was [as] a beast before thee.
019	PSA	073	023	Nevertheless I am continually with thee: thou hast holden my right hand.
019	PSA	073	024	Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.
019	PSA	073	025	Whom have I in heaven [but thee]? and there is none upon earth that I desire beside thee.
019	PSA	073	026	My flesh and my heart faileth: [but] God is the strength of my heart and my portion for ever.
019	PSA	073	027	For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.
019	PSA	073	028	But it is good for me to draw near unto God: I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may tell of all thy works.
019	PSA	074	001	Maschil of Asaph. O God, why hast thou cast [us] off for ever? why doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?
019	PSA	074	002	Remember thy congregation, which thou hast purchased of old, which thou hast redeemed to be the tribe of thine inheritance; [and] mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.
019	PSA	074	003	Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual ruins, all the evil that the enemy hath done in the sanctuary.
019	PSA	074	004	Thine adversaries have roared in the midst of thine assembly; they have set up their ensigns for signs.
019	PSA	074	005	They seemed as men that lifted up axes upon a thicket of trees.
019	PSA	074	006	And now all the carved work thereof together they break down with hatchet and hammers.
019	PSA	074	007	They have set thy sanctuary on fire; they have profaned the dwelling place of thy name even to the ground.
019	PSA	074	008	They said in their heart, Let us make havoc of them altogether: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.
019	PSA	074	009	We see not our signs: there is no more any prophet; neither is there among us any that knoweth how long.
019	PSA	074	010	How long, O God, shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?
019	PSA	074	011	Why drawest thou back thy hand, even thy right hand? [pluck it] out of thy bosom [and] consume [them].
019	PSA	074	012	Yet God is my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.
019	PSA	074	013	Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou brakest the heads of the dragons in the waters.
019	PSA	074	014	Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces, thou gavest him to be meat to the people inhabiting the wilderness.
019	PSA	074	015	Thou didst cleave fountain and flood: thou driedst up mighty rivers.
019	PSA	074	016	The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.
019	PSA	074	017	Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.
019	PSA	074	018	Remember this, that the enemy hath reproached, O LORD, and that foolish people have blasphemed thy name.
019	PSA	074	019	O deliver not the soul of thy turtle-dove unto the wild beast: forget not the life of thy poor for ever.
019	PSA	074	020	Have respect unto the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of violence.
019	PSA	074	021	O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.
019	PSA	074	022	Arise, O God, plead thine own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee all the day.
019	PSA	074	023	Forget not the voice of thine adversaries: the tumult of those that rise up against thee ascendeth continually.
019	PSA	075	001	For the Chief Musician; [set to] Al-tashheth. A Psalm of Asaph, a Song. We give thanks unto thee, O God; we give thanks, for thy name is near: men tell of thy wondrous works.
019	PSA	075	002	When I shall find the set time, I will judge uprightly.
019	PSA	075	003	The earth and all the inhabitants thereof are dissolved: I have set up the pillars of it. (Selah)
019	PSA	075	004	I said unto the arrogant, Deal not arrogantly: and to the wicked, Lift not up the horn:
019	PSA	075	005	Lift not up your horn on high; speak not with a stiff neck.
019	PSA	075	006	For neither from the east, nor from the west, nor yet from the south, [cometh] lifting up.
019	PSA	075	007	But God is the judge: he putteth down one, and lifteth up another.
019	PSA	075	008	For in the hand of the LORD there is a cup, and the wine foameth; it is full of mixture, and he poureth out of the same: surely the dregs thereof, all the wicked of the earth shall wring them out, and drink them.
019	PSA	075	009	But I will declare for ever, I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	075	010	All the horns of the wicked also will I cut off; but the horns of the righteous shall be lifted up.
019	PSA	076	001	For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. A Psalm of Asaph, a Song. In Judah is God known: his name is great in Israel.
019	PSA	076	002	In Salem also is his tabernacle, and his dwelling place in Zion.
019	PSA	076	003	There he brake the arrows of the bow; the shield, and the sword, and the battle. (Selah)
019	PSA	076	004	Glorious art thou [and] excellent, from the mountains of prey.
019	PSA	076	005	The stouthearted are spoiled, they have slept their sleep; and none of the men of might have found their hands.
019	PSA	076	006	At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.
019	PSA	076	007	Thou, even thou, art to be feared: and who may stand in thy sight when once thou art angry?
019	PSA	076	008	Thou didst cause sentence to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,
019	PSA	076	009	When God arose to judgment, to save all the meek of the earth. (Selah)
019	PSA	076	010	Surely the wrath of man shall praise thee: the residue of wrath shalt thou gird upon thee.
019	PSA	076	011	Vow, and pay unto the LORD your God: let all that be round about him bring presents unto him that ought to be feared.
019	PSA	076	012	He shall cut off the spirit of princes: he is terrible to the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	077	001	For the Chief Musician; after the manner of Jeduthun. A Psalm of Asaph. I will cry unto God with my voice; even unto God with my voice, and he wilt give ear unto me.
019	PSA	077	002	In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord: my hand was stretched out in the night, and slacked not; my soul refused to be comforted.
019	PSA	077	003	I remember God, and am disquieted: I complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed. (Selah)
019	PSA	077	004	Thou holdest mine eyes watching: I am so troubled that I cannot speak.
019	PSA	077	005	I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.
019	PSA	077	006	I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with mine own heart; and my spirit made diligent search.
019	PSA	077	007	Will the Lord cast off for ever? and will he be favourable no more?
019	PSA	077	008	Is his mercy clean gone for ever? doth his promise fail for evermore?
019	PSA	077	009	Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? (Selah)
019	PSA	077	010	And I said, This is my infirmity; [but I will remember] the years of the right hand of the Most High.
019	PSA	077	011	I will make mention of the deeds of the LORD; for I will remember thy wonders of old.
019	PSA	077	012	I will meditate also upon all thy work, and muse on thy doings.
019	PSA	077	013	Thy way, O God, is in the sanctuary: who is a great god like unto God?
019	PSA	077	014	Thou art the God that doest wonders: thou hast made known thy strength among the peoples.
019	PSA	077	015	Thou hast with thine arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. (Selah)
019	PSA	077	016	The waters saw thee, O God; the waters saw thee, they were afraid: the depths also trembled.
019	PSA	077	017	The clouds poured out water; the skies sent out a sound: thine arrows also went abroad.
019	PSA	077	018	The voice of thy thunder was in the whirlwind; the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook.
019	PSA	077	019	Thy way was in the sea, and thy paths in the great waters, and thy footsteps were not known.
019	PSA	077	020	Thou leddest thy people like a flock, by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
019	PSA	078	001	Maschil of Asaph. Give ear, O my people, to my law; incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
019	PSA	078	002	I will open my mouth in a parable; I will utter dark sayings of old:
019	PSA	078	003	Which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.
019	PSA	078	004	We will not hide them from their children, telling to the generation to come the praises of the LORD, and his strength, and his wondrous works that he hath done.
019	PSA	078	005	For he established a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children:
019	PSA	078	006	That the generation to come might know [them], even the children which should be born; who should arise and tell [them] to their children:
019	PSA	078	007	That they might set their hope in God, and not forget the works of God, but keep his commandments:
019	PSA	078	008	And might not be as their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation; a generation that set not their heart aright, and whose spirit was not stedfast with God.
019	PSA	078	009	The children of Ephraim, being armed and carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.
019	PSA	078	010	They kept not the covenant of God, and refused to walk in his law;
019	PSA	078	011	And they forgat his doings, and his wondrous works that he had shewed them.
019	PSA	078	012	Marvelous things did he in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Zoan.
019	PSA	078	013	He clave the sea, and caused them to pass through; and he made the waters to stand as an heap.
019	PSA	078	014	In the day-time also he led them with a cloud, and all the night with a light of fire.
019	PSA	078	015	He clave rocks in the wilderness, and gave them drink abundantly as out of the depths.
019	PSA	078	016	He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.
019	PSA	078	017	Yet went they on still to sin against him, to rebel against the Most High in the desert.
019	PSA	078	018	And they tempted God in their heart by asking meat for their lust.
019	PSA	078	019	Yea, they spake against God; they said, Can God prepare a table in the wilderness?
019	PSA	078	020	Behold, he smote the rock, that waters gushed out, and streams overflowed; can he give bread also? will he provide flesh for his people?
019	PSA	078	021	Therefore the LORD heard, and was wroth: and a fire was kindled against Jacob, and anger also went up against Israel;
019	PSA	078	022	Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation.
019	PSA	078	023	Yet he commanded the skies above, and opened the doors of heaven;
019	PSA	078	024	And he rained down manna upon them to eat, and gave them of the corn of heaven.
019	PSA	078	025	Man did eat the bread of the mighty: he sent them meat to the full.
019	PSA	078	026	He caused the east wind to blow in the heaven: and by his power he guided the south wind.
019	PSA	078	027	He rained flesh also upon them as the dust, and winged fowl as the sand of the seas:
019	PSA	078	028	And he let it fall in the midst of their camp, round about their habitations.
019	PSA	078	029	So they did eat, and were well filled; and he gave them that they lusted after.
019	PSA	078	030	They were not estranged from their lust, their meat was yet in their mouths,
019	PSA	078	031	When the anger of God went up against them, and slew of the fattest of them, and smote down the young men of Israel.
019	PSA	078	032	For all this they sinned still, and believed not in his wondrous works.
019	PSA	078	033	Therefore their days did he consume in vanity, and their years in terror.
019	PSA	078	034	When he slew them, then they inquired after him: and they returned and sought God early.
019	PSA	078	035	And they remembered that God was their rock, and the Most High God their redeemer.
019	PSA	078	036	But they flattered him with their mouth, and lied unto him with their tongue.
019	PSA	078	037	For their heart was not right with him, neither were they faithful in his covenant.
019	PSA	078	038	But he, being full of compassion, forgave [their] iniquity, and destroyed [them] not: yea, many a time turned he his anger away, and did not stir up all his wrath.
019	PSA	078	039	And he remembered that they were but flesh; a wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.
019	PSA	078	040	How oft did they rebel against him in the wilderness, and grieve him in the desert!
019	PSA	078	041	And they turned again and tempted God, and provoked the Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	078	042	They remembered not his hand, nor the day when he redeemed them from the adversary.
019	PSA	078	043	How he set his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Zoan;
019	PSA	078	044	And turned their rivers into blood, and their streams, that they could not drink.
019	PSA	078	045	He sent among them swarms of flies, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.
019	PSA	078	046	He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller, and their labour unto the locust.
019	PSA	078	047	He destroyed their vines with hail, and their sycomore trees with frost.
019	PSA	078	048	He gave over their cattle also to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.
019	PSA	078	049	He cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble, a band of angels of evil.
019	PSA	078	050	He made a path for his anger; he spared not their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence;
019	PSA	078	051	And smote all the firstborn in Egypt, the chief of their strength in the tents of Ham:
019	PSA	078	052	But he led forth his own people like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.
019	PSA	078	053	And he led them safely, so that they feared not: but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.
019	PSA	078	054	And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary, to this mountain, which his right hand had purchased.
019	PSA	078	055	He drove out the nations also before them, and allotted them for an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.
019	PSA	078	056	Yet they tempted and rebelled against the Most High God, and kept not his testimonies;
019	PSA	078	057	But turned back, and dealt treacherously like their fathers: they were turned aside like a deceitful bow.
019	PSA	078	058	For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.
019	PSA	078	059	When God heard [this], he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel:
019	PSA	078	060	So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent which he placed among men;
019	PSA	078	061	And delivered his strength into captivity, and his glory into the adversary’s hand.
019	PSA	078	062	He gave his people over also unto the sword; and was wroth with his inheritance.
019	PSA	078	063	Fire devoured their young men; and their maidens had no marriage-song.
019	PSA	078	064	Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows made no lamentation.
019	PSA	078	065	Then the Lord awaked as one out of sleep, like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.
019	PSA	078	066	And he smote his adversaries backward: he put them to a perpetual reproach.
019	PSA	078	067	Moreover he refused the tent of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim;
019	PSA	078	068	But chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved.
019	PSA	078	069	And he built his sanctuary like the heights, like the earth which he hath established for ever.
019	PSA	078	070	He chose David also his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds:
019	PSA	078	071	From following the ewes that give suck he brought him, to feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.
019	PSA	078	072	So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.
019	PSA	079	001	A Psalm of Asaph. O God, the heathen are come into thine inheritance; thy holy temple have they defiled; they have laid Jerusalem on heaps.
019	PSA	079	002	The dead bodies of thy servants have they given to be meat unto the fowls of the heaven, the flesh of thy saints unto the beasts of the earth.
019	PSA	079	003	Their blood have they shed like water round about Jerusalem; and there was none to bury them.
019	PSA	079	004	We are become a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to them that are round about us.
019	PSA	079	005	How long, O LORD, wilt thou be angry for ever? shall thy jealousy burn like fire?
019	PSA	079	006	Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen that know thee not, and upon the kingdoms that call not upon thy name.
019	PSA	079	007	For they have devoured Jacob, and laid waste his habitation.
019	PSA	079	008	Remember not against us the iniquities of our forefathers: let thy tender mercies speedily prevent us: for we are brought very low.
019	PSA	079	009	Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name’s sake.
019	PSA	079	010	Wherefore should the heathen say, Where is their God? let the revenging of the blood of thy servants which is shed be known among the heathen in our sight.
019	PSA	079	011	Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to death;
019	PSA	079	012	And render unto our neighbours sevenfold into their bosom their reproach, wherewith they have reproached thee, O Lord.
019	PSA	079	013	So we thy people and sheep of thy pasture will give thee thanks for ever: we will shew forth thy praise to all generations.
019	PSA	080	001	For the Chief Musician; set to Shoshannim Eduth. A Psalm of Asaph. Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel, thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that sittest upon the cherubim, shine forth.
019	PSA	080	002	Before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh, stir up thy might, and come to save us.
019	PSA	080	003	Turn us again, O God; and cause thy face to shine, and we shall be saved.
019	PSA	080	004	O LORD God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy people?
019	PSA	080	005	Thou hast fed them with the bread of tears, and given them tears to drink in large measure.
019	PSA	080	006	Thou makest us a strife unto our neighbours: and our enemies laugh among themselves.
019	PSA	080	007	Turn us again, O God of hosts; and cause thy face to shine, and we shall be saved.
019	PSA	080	008	Thou broughtest a vine out of Egypt: thou didst drive out the nations, and plantedst it.
019	PSA	080	009	Thou preparedst [room] before it, and it took deep root, and filled the land.
019	PSA	080	010	The mountains were covered with the shadow of it, and the boughs thereof were [like] cedars of God.
019	PSA	080	011	She sent out her branches unto the sea, and her shoots unto the River.
019	PSA	080	012	Why hast thou broken down her fences, so that all they which pass by the way do pluck her?
019	PSA	080	013	The boar out of the wood doth ravage it, and the wild beasts of the field feed on it.
019	PSA	080	014	Turn again, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine,
019	PSA	080	015	And the stock which thy right hand hath planted, and the branch that thou madest strong for thyself.
019	PSA	080	016	It is burned with fire, it is cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.
019	PSA	080	017	Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man whom thou madest strong for thyself.
019	PSA	080	018	So shall we not go back from thee: quicken thou us, and we will call upon thy name,
019	PSA	080	019	Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts; cause thy face to shine, and we shall be saved.
019	PSA	081	001	For the Chief Musician; set to the Gittith. A Psalm of Asaph. Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	002	Take up the psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.
019	PSA	081	003	Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, at the full moon, on our solemn feast day.
019	PSA	081	004	For it is a statute for Israel, an ordinance of the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	005	He appointed it in Joseph for testimony, when he went out over the land of Egypt: [where] I heard a language that I knew not.
019	PSA	081	006	I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were freed from the basket.
019	PSA	081	007	Thou calledst in trouble, and I answered thee in the secret place of thunder; I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. (Selah)
019	PSA	081	008	Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wouldest hearken unto me!
019	PSA	081	009	There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.
019	PSA	081	010	I am the LORD thy God, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.
019	PSA	081	011	But my people hearkened not to my voice; and Israel would none of me.
019	PSA	081	012	So I let them go after the stubbornness of their heart, that they might walk in their own counsels.
019	PSA	081	013	Oh that my people would hearken unto me, that Israel would walk in my ways!
019	PSA	081	014	I should soon subdue their enemies, and turn my hand against their adversaries.
019	PSA	081	015	The haters of the LORD should submit themselves unto him: but their time should endure for ever.
019	PSA	081	016	He should feed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I satisfy thee.
019	PSA	082	001	A Psalm of Asaph. God standeth in the congregation of God; he judgeth among the gods.
019	PSA	082	002	How long will ye judge unjustly, and respect the persons of the wicked? (Selah)
019	PSA	082	003	Judge the poor and fatherless: do justice to the afflicted and destitute.
019	PSA	082	004	Rescue the poor and needy: deliver them out of the hand of the wicked.
019	PSA	082	005	They know not, neither do they understand; they walk to and fro in darkness: all the foundations of the earth are moved.
019	PSA	082	006	I said, Ye are gods, and all of you sons of the Most High.
019	PSA	082	007	Nevertheless ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes.
019	PSA	082	008	Arise, O God, judge the earth: for thou shalt inherit all the nations.
019	PSA	083	001	A Song, a Psalm of Asaph. O God, keep not thou silence: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.
019	PSA	083	002	For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.
019	PSA	083	003	They take crafty counsel against thy people, and consult together against thy hidden ones.
019	PSA	083	004	They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.
019	PSA	083	005	For they have consulted together with one consent; against thee do they make a covenant:
019	PSA	083	006	The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites; Moab, and the Hagarenes;
019	PSA	083	007	Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; Philistia with the inhabitants of Tyre:
019	PSA	083	008	Assyria also is joined with them; they have holpen the children of Lot. (Selah)
019	PSA	083	009	Do thou unto them as unto Midian; as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon:
019	PSA	083	010	Which perished at En-dor; they became as dung for the earth.
019	PSA	083	011	Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb; yea, all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna:
019	PSA	083	012	Who said, Let us take to ourselves in possession the habitations of God.
019	PSA	083	013	O my God, make them like the whirling dust; as stubble before the wind.
019	PSA	083	014	As the fire that burneth the forest, and as the flame that setteth the mountains on fire;
019	PSA	083	015	So pursue them with thy tempest, and terrify them with thy storm.
019	PSA	083	016	Fill their faces with confusion; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.
019	PSA	083	017	Let them be ashamed and dismayed for ever; yea, let them be confounded and perish:
019	PSA	083	018	That they may know that thou alone, whose name is JEHOVAH, art the Most High over all the earth.
019	PSA	084	001	For the Chief Musician; set to the Gittith. A Psalm of the sons of Korah. How amiable are thy tabernacles, O LORD of hosts!
019	PSA	084	002	My soul longeth, yea, even fainteth for the courts of the LORD; my heart and my flesh cry out unto the living God.
019	PSA	084	003	Yea, the sparrow hath found her an house, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, even thine altars, O LORD of hosts, my King, and my God.
019	PSA	084	004	Blessed are they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. (Selah)
019	PSA	084	005	Blessed is the man whose strength is in thee; in whose heart are the highways [to Zion].
019	PSA	084	006	Passing through the valley of Weeping they make it a place of springs; yea, the early rain covereth it with blessings.
019	PSA	084	007	They go from strength to strength, every one of them appeareth before God in Zion.
019	PSA	084	008	O LORD God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob. (Selah)
019	PSA	084	009	Behold, O God our shield, and look upon the face of thine anointed.
019	PSA	084	010	For a day in thy courts is better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.
019	PSA	084	011	For the LORD God is a sun and a shield: the LORD will give grace and glory: no good thing will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.
019	PSA	084	012	O LORD of hosts, blessed is the man that trusteth in thee.
019	PSA	085	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of the sons of Korah. LORD, Thou hast been favourable unto thy land: thou hast brought back the captivity of Jacob.
019	PSA	085	002	Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people, thou hast covered all their sin. (Selah)
019	PSA	085	003	Thou hast taken away all thy wrath: thou hast turned [thyself] from the fierceness of thine anger.
019	PSA	085	004	Turn us, O God of our salvation, and cause thine indignation toward us to cease.
019	PSA	085	005	Wilt thou be angry with us for ever? wilt thou draw out thine anger to all generations?
019	PSA	085	006	Wilt thou not quicken us again: that thy people may rejoice in thee?
019	PSA	085	007	Shew us thy mercy, O LORD, and grant us thy salvation.
019	PSA	085	008	I will hear what God the LORD will speak: for he will speak peace unto his people, and to his saints: but let them not turn again to folly.
019	PSA	085	009	Surely his salvation is nigh them that fear him; that glory may dwell in our land.
019	PSA	085	010	Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed each other.
019	PSA	085	011	Truth springeth out of the earth; and righteousness hath looked down from heaven.
019	PSA	085	012	Yea, the LORD shall give that which is good; and our land shall yield her increase.
019	PSA	085	013	Righteousness shall go before him; and shall make his footsteps a way [to walk in].
019	PSA	086	001	A Prayer Of David. Bow down thine ear, O LORD, and answer me; for I am poor and needy.
019	PSA	086	002	Preserve my soul; for I am godly: O thou my God, save thy servant that trusteth in thee.
019	PSA	086	003	Be merciful unto me, O Lord; for unto thee do I cry all the day long.
019	PSA	086	004	Rejoice the soul of thy servant; for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.
019	PSA	086	005	For thou, Lord, art good, and ready to forgive, and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.
019	PSA	086	006	Give ear, O LORD, unto my prayer; and hearken unto the voice of my supplications.
019	PSA	086	007	In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee; for thou wilt answer me.
019	PSA	086	008	There is none like unto thee among the gods, O Lord; neither [are there any works] like unto thy works.
019	PSA	086	009	All nations whom thou hast made shall come and worship before thee, O Lord; and they shall glorify thy name.
019	PSA	086	010	For thou art great, and doest wondrous things: thou art God alone.
019	PSA	086	011	Teach me thy way, O LORD; I will walk in thy truth: unite my heart to fear thy name.
019	PSA	086	012	I will praise thee, O Lord my God, with my whole heart; and I will glorify thy name for evermore.
019	PSA	086	013	For great is thy mercy toward me; and thou hast delivered my soul from the lowest pit.
019	PSA	086	014	O God, the proud are risen up against me, and the congregation of violent men have sought after my soul, and have not set thee before them.
019	PSA	086	015	But thou, O Lord, art a God full of compassion and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy and truth.
019	PSA	086	016	O turn unto me, and have mercy upon me; give thy strength unto thy servant, and save the son of thine handmaid.
019	PSA	086	017	Shew me a token for good; that they which hate me may see it, and be ashamed, because thou, LORD, hast holpen me, and comforted me,
019	PSA	087	001	A Psalm of the sons of Korah; a Song. His foundation is in the holy mountains.
019	PSA	087	002	The LORD loveth the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.
019	PSA	087	003	Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God. (Selah)
019	PSA	087	004	I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon as among them that know me: behold Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia; this one was born there.
019	PSA	087	005	Yea, of Zion it shall be said, This one and that one was born in her; and the Most High himself shall establish her.
019	PSA	087	006	The LORD shall count, when he writeth up the peoples, this one was born there. (Selah)
019	PSA	087	007	They that sing as well as they that dance [shall say], All my fountains are in thee.
019	PSA	088	001	A Song, a Psalm of the sons of Korah; for the Chief Musician; set to Mahalath Leannoth. Maschil of Heman the Ezrahite. O LORD, the God of my salvation, I have cried day and night before thee:
019	PSA	088	002	Let my prayer enter into thy presence; incline thine ear unto my cry:
019	PSA	088	003	For my soul is full of troubles, and my life draweth nigh unto Sheol.
019	PSA	088	004	I am counted with them that go down into the pit; I am as a man that hath no help:
019	PSA	088	005	Cast off among the dead, like the slain that lie in the grave, whom thou rememberest no more; and they are cut off from thy hand.
019	PSA	088	006	Thou hast laid me in the lowest pit, in dark places, in the deeps.
019	PSA	088	007	Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and thou hast afflicted me with all thy waves. (Selah)
019	PSA	088	008	Thou hast put mine acquaintance far from me; thou hast made me an abomination unto them: I am shut up, and I cannot come forth.
019	PSA	088	009	Mine eye wasteth away by reason of affliction: I have called daily upon thee, O LORD, I have spread forth my hands unto thee.
019	PSA	088	010	Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? shall they that are deceased arise and praise thee? (Selah)
019	PSA	088	011	Shall thy lovingkindness be declared in the grave? or thy faithfulness in Destruction?
019	PSA	088	012	Shall thy wonders be known in the dark? and thy righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?
019	PSA	088	013	But unto thee, O LORD, have I cried, and in the morning shall my prayer come before thee.
019	PSA	088	014	LORD, why castest thou off my soul? why hidest thou thy face from me?
019	PSA	088	015	I am afflicted and ready to die from my youth up: while I suffer thy terrors I am distracted.
019	PSA	088	016	Thy fierce wrath is gone over me; thy terrors have cut me off.
019	PSA	088	017	They came round about me like water all the day long; they compassed me about together.
019	PSA	088	018	Lover and friend hast thou put far from me, and mine acquaintance into darkness.
019	PSA	089	001	Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite. I will sing of the mercies of the LORD for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations.
019	PSA	089	002	For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever; thy faithfulness shalt thou establish in the very heavens.
019	PSA	089	003	I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn unto David my servant;
019	PSA	089	004	Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. (Selah)
019	PSA	089	005	And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O LORD; thy faithfulness also in the assembly of the holy ones.
019	PSA	089	006	For who in the skies can be compared unto the LORD? who among the sons of the mighty is like unto the LORD,
019	PSA	089	007	A God very terrible in the council of the holy ones, and to be feared above all them that are round about him?
019	PSA	089	008	O LORD God of hosts, who is a mighty one, like unto thee, O JAH? and thy faithfulness is round about thee.
019	PSA	089	009	Thou rulest the pride of the sea: when the waves thereof arise, thou stillest them.
019	PSA	089	010	Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with the arm of thy strength.
019	PSA	089	011	The heavens are thine, the earth also is thine: the world and the fulness thereof, thou hast founded them.
019	PSA	089	012	The north and the south, thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon rejoice in thy name.
019	PSA	089	013	Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, and high is thy right hand.
019	PSA	089	014	Righteousness and judgment are the foundation of thy throne: mercy and truth go before thy face.
019	PSA	089	015	Blessed is the people that know the joyful sound: they walk, O LORD, in the light of thy countenance.
019	PSA	089	016	In thy name do they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness are they exalted.
019	PSA	089	017	For thou art the glory of their strength: and in thy favour our horn shall be exalted.
019	PSA	089	018	For our shield belongeth unto the LORD; and our king to the Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	089	019	Then thou spakest in vision to thy saints, and saidst, I have laid help upon one that is mighty; I have exalted one chosen out of the people.
019	PSA	089	020	I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:
019	PSA	089	021	With whom my hand shall be established; mine arm also shall strengthen him.
019	PSA	089	022	The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.
019	PSA	089	023	And I will beat down his adversaries before him, and smite them that hate him.
019	PSA	089	024	But my faithfulness and my mercy shall be with him; and in my name shall his horn be exalted.
019	PSA	089	025	I will set his hand also on the sea, and his right hand on the rivers.
019	PSA	089	026	He shall cry unto me, Thou art my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.
019	PSA	089	027	I also will make him [my] firstborn, the highest of the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	089	028	My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.
019	PSA	089	029	His seed also will I make to endure for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.
019	PSA	089	030	If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;
019	PSA	089	031	If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments;
019	PSA	089	032	Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.
019	PSA	089	033	But my mercy will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.
019	PSA	089	034	My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.
019	PSA	089	035	Once have I sworn by my holiness; I will not lie unto David;
019	PSA	089	036	His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.
019	PSA	089	037	It shall be established for ever as the moon, and [as] the faithful witness in the sky. (Selah)
019	PSA	089	038	But thou hast cast off and rejected, thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.
019	PSA	089	039	Thou hast abhorred the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown [even] to the ground.
019	PSA	089	040	Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to rain.
019	PSA	089	041	All that pass by the way spoil him: he is become a reproach to his neighbours.
019	PSA	089	042	Thou hast exalted the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.
019	PSA	089	043	Yea, thou turnest back the edge his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.
019	PSA	089	044	Thou hast made his brightness to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground.
019	PSA	089	045	The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. (Selah)
019	PSA	089	046	How long, O LORD, wilt thou hid thyself for ever? [how long] shall thy wrath burn like fire?
019	PSA	089	047	O remember how short my time is: for what vanity hast thou created all the children of men!
019	PSA	089	048	What man is he that shall live and not see death, that shall deliver his soul from the power of Sheol? (Selah)
019	PSA	089	049	Lord, where are thy former mercies, which thou swarest unto David in thy faithfulness?
019	PSA	089	050	Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy servants; how I do bear in my bosom [the reproach of] all the mighty peoples:
019	PSA	089	051	Wherewith thine enemies have reproached, O LORD, wherewith they have reproached the footsteps of thine anointed.
019	PSA	089	052	Blessed be the LORD for evermore. Amen, and Amen.
019	PSA	090	001	A Prayer of Moses the man of God. Lord, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations.
019	PSA	090	002	Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou art God.
019	PSA	090	003	Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.
019	PSA	090	004	For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night.
019	PSA	090	005	Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are as a sleep: in the morning they are like grass which groweth up.
019	PSA	090	006	In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.
019	PSA	090	007	For we are consumed in thine anger, and in thy wrath are we troubled.
019	PSA	090	008	Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret sins in the light of thy countenance.
019	PSA	090	009	For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we bring our years to an end as a tale [that is told].
019	PSA	090	010	The days of our years are threescore years and ten, or even by reason of strength fourscore years; yet is their pride but labour and sorrow; for it is soon gone, and we fly away.
019	PSA	090	011	Who knoweth the power of thine anger, and thy wrath according to the fear that is due unto thee?
019	PSA	090	012	So teach us to number our days, that we may get us an heart of wisdom.
019	PSA	090	013	Return, O LORD; how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.
019	PSA	090	014	O satisfy us in the morning with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.
019	PSA	090	015	Make us glad according to the days wherein thou hast afflicted us, and the years wherein we have seen evil.
019	PSA	090	016	Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory upon their children.
019	PSA	090	017	And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.
019	PSA	091	001	He that dwelleth in the secret place of the Most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.
019	PSA	091	002	I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress; my God, in whom I trust.
019	PSA	091	003	For he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, and from the noisome pestilence.
019	PSA	091	004	He shall cover thee with his pinions, and under his wings shalt thou take refuge: his truth is a shield and a buckler.
019	PSA	091	005	Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night, nor for the arrow that flieth by day;
019	PSA	091	006	For the pestilence that walketh in darkness, nor for the destruction that wasteth at noonday.
019	PSA	091	007	A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; [but] it shall not come nigh thee.
019	PSA	091	008	Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold, and see the reward of the wicked.
019	PSA	091	009	For thou, O LORD, art my refuge! thou hast made the Most High thy habitation;
019	PSA	091	010	There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy tent.
019	PSA	091	011	For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.
019	PSA	091	012	They shall bear thee up in their hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.
019	PSA	091	013	Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the serpent shalt thou trample under feet.
019	PSA	091	014	Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.
019	PSA	091	015	He shall call upon me, and I will answer him; I will be with him in trouble: I will deliver him, and honour him.
019	PSA	091	016	With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.
019	PSA	092	001	A Psalm, a Song for the sabbath day. It is a good thing to give thanks unto the LORD, and to sing praises unto thy name, O Most High:
019	PSA	092	002	To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,
019	PSA	092	003	With an instrument of ten strings, and with the psaltery; with a solemn sound upon the harp.
019	PSA	092	004	For thou, LORD, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.
019	PSA	092	005	How great are thy works, O LORD! thy thoughts are very deep.
019	PSA	092	006	A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this:
019	PSA	092	007	When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; it is that they shall be destroyed for ever:
019	PSA	092	008	But thou, O LORD, art on high for evermore.
019	PSA	092	009	For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.
019	PSA	092	010	But my horn hast thou exalted like [the horn of] the wild-ox: I am anointed with fresh oil.
019	PSA	092	011	Mine eye also hath seen [my desire] on mine enemies, mine ears have heard [my desire] of the evil-doers that rise up against me.
019	PSA	092	012	The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.
019	PSA	092	013	They that are planted in the house of the LORD shall flourish in the courts of our God.
019	PSA	092	014	They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be full of sap and green:
019	PSA	092	015	To shew that the LORD is upright; he is my rock, and there is no unrighteousness in him.
019	PSA	093	001	The LORD reigneth; he is apparelled with majesty; the LORD is apparelled, he hath girded himself with strength: the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved.
019	PSA	093	002	Thy throne is established of old: thou art from everlasting.
019	PSA	093	003	The floods have lifted up, O LORD, the floods have lifted up their voice; the floods lift up their waves.
019	PSA	093	004	Above the voices of many waters, the mighty breakers of the sea, the LORD on high is mighty.
019	PSA	093	005	Thy testimonies are very sure: holiness becometh thine house, O LORD, for evermore.
019	PSA	094	001	O LORD, thou God to whom vengeance belongeth, thou God to whom vengeance belongeth, shine forth.
019	PSA	094	002	Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render to the proud [their] desert.
019	PSA	094	003	LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?
019	PSA	094	004	They prate, they speak arrogantly: all the workers of iniquity boast themselves.
019	PSA	094	005	They break in pieces thy people, O LORD, and afflict thine heritage.
019	PSA	094	006	They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.
019	PSA	094	007	And they say, The LORD shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob consider.
019	PSA	094	008	Consider, ye brutish among the people: and ye fools, when will ye be wise?
019	PSA	094	009	He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?
019	PSA	094	010	He that chastiseth the nations, shall not he correct, [even] he that teacheth man knowledge?
019	PSA	094	011	The LORD knoweth the thoughts of man, that they are vanity.
019	PSA	094	012	Blessed is the man whom thou chastenest, O LORD, and teachest out of thy law;
019	PSA	094	013	That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.
019	PSA	094	014	For the LORD will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.
019	PSA	094	015	For judgment shall return unto righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it.
019	PSA	094	016	Who will rise up for me against the evil-doers? who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?
019	PSA	094	017	Unless the LORD had been my help, my soul had soon dwelt in silence.
019	PSA	094	018	When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O LORD, held me up.
019	PSA	094	019	In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.
019	PSA	094	020	Shall the throne of wickedness have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by statute?
019	PSA	094	021	They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.
019	PSA	094	022	But the LORD hath been my high tower; and my God the rock of my refuge.
019	PSA	094	023	And he hath brought upon them their own iniquity, and shall cut them off in their own evil; the LORD our God shall cut them off.
019	PSA	095	001	O COME, let us sing unto the LORD: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.
019	PSA	095	002	Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, let us make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.
019	PSA	095	003	For the LORD is a great God, and a great King above all gods.
019	PSA	095	004	In his hand are the deep places of the earth; the heights of the mountains are his also.
019	PSA	095	005	The sea is his, and he made it; and his hands formed the dry land.
019	PSA	095	006	O come, let us worship and bow down; let us kneel before the LORD our Maker:
019	PSA	095	007	For he is our God, and we are the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. Today, Oh that ye would hear his voice!
019	PSA	095	008	Harden not your heart, as at Meribah, as in the day of Massah in the wilderness:
019	PSA	095	009	When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.
019	PSA	095	010	Forty years long was I grieved with [that] generation, and said, It is a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:
019	PSA	095	011	Wherefore I sware in my wrath, that they should not enter into my rest.
019	PSA	096	001	O SING unto the LORD a new song: sing unto the LORD, all the earth.
019	PSA	096	002	Sing unto the LORD, bless his name; shew forth his salvation from day to day.
019	PSA	096	003	Declare his glory among the nations, his marvelous works among all the peoples.
019	PSA	096	004	For great is the LORD, and highly to be praised: he is to be feared above all gods.
019	PSA	096	005	For all the gods of the peoples are idols: but the LORD made the heavens.
019	PSA	096	006	Honour and majesty are before him: strength and beauty are in his sanctuary.
019	PSA	096	007	Give unto the LORD, ye kindreds of the peoples, give unto the LORD glory and strength.
019	PSA	096	008	Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name: bring an offering, and come into his courts.
019	PSA	096	009	O worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness: tremble before him, all the earth.
019	PSA	096	010	Say among the nations, The LORD reigneth: the world also is stablished that it cannot be moved: he shall judge the peoples with equity.
019	PSA	096	011	Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice; let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof;
019	PSA	096	012	Let the field exult, and all that is therein; then shall all the trees of the wood sing for joy;
019	PSA	096	013	Before the LORD, for he cometh; for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the peoples with his truth.
019	PSA	097	001	The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice; let the multitude of isles be glad.
019	PSA	097	002	Clouds and darkness are round about him: righteousness and judgment are the foundation of his throne.
019	PSA	097	003	A fire goeth before him, and burneth up his adversaries round about.
019	PSA	097	004	His lightnings lightened the world: the earth saw, and trembled.
019	PSA	097	005	The hills melted like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth;
019	PSA	097	006	The heavens declare his righteousness, and all the peoples have seen his glory.
019	PSA	097	007	Ashamed be all they that serve graven images, that boast themselves of idols: worship him, all ye gods.
019	PSA	097	008	Zion heard and was glad, and the daughters of Judah rejoiced; because of thy judgments, O LORD.
019	PSA	097	009	For thou, LORD, art most high above all the earth: thou art exalted far above all gods.
019	PSA	097	010	O ye that love the LORD, hate evil: he preserveth the souls of his saints; he delivereth them out of the hand of the wicked.
019	PSA	097	011	Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.
019	PSA	097	012	Be glad in the LORD, ye righteous; and give thanks to his holy name.
019	PSA	098	001	A Psalm. Sing unto the LORD a new song; for he hath done marvelous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath wrought salvation for him.
019	PSA	098	002	The LORD hath made known his salvation: his righteousness hath he openly shewed in the sight of the nations.
019	PSA	098	003	He hath remembered his mercy and his faithfulness toward the house of Israel: all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.
019	PSA	098	004	Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all the earth: break forth and sing for joy, yea, sing praises.
019	PSA	098	005	Sing praises unto the LORD with the harp; with the harp and the voice of melody:
019	PSA	098	006	With trumpets and sound of cornet make a joyful noise before the King, the LORD.
019	PSA	098	007	Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein;
019	PSA	098	008	Let the floods clap their hands; let the hills sing for joy together;
019	PSA	098	009	Before the LORD, for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the peoples with equity.
019	PSA	099	001	The LORD reigneth; let the peoples tremble: he sitteth upon the cherubim; let the earth be moved.
019	PSA	099	002	The LORD is great in Zion; and he is high above all the peoples.
019	PSA	099	003	Let them praise thy great and terrible name: holy is he.
019	PSA	099	004	The king’s strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.
019	PSA	099	005	Exalt ye the LORD our God, and worship at his footstool: holy is he.
019	PSA	099	006	Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call on his name; they called upon the LORD, and he answered them.
019	PSA	099	007	He spake unto them in the pillar of cloud: they kept his testimonies, and the statute that he gave them.
019	PSA	099	008	Thou answeredst them, O LORD our God: thou wast a God that forgavest them, though thou tookest vengeance of their doings.
019	PSA	099	009	Exalt ye the LORD our God, and worship at his holy hill; for the LORD our God is holy.
019	PSA	100	001	A Psalm of thanksgiving. Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands.
019	PSA	100	002	Serve the LORD with gladness: come before his presence with singing.
019	PSA	100	003	Know ye that the LORD he is God: it is he that hath made us, and we are his; we are his people, and the sheep of his pasture.
019	PSA	100	004	Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise: give thanks unto him, and bless his name.
019	PSA	100	005	For the LORD is good; his mercy [endureth] for ever; and his faithfulness unto all generations.
019	PSA	101	001	A Psalm of David. I will sing of mercy and judgment: unto thee, O LORD, will I sing praises.
019	PSA	101	002	I will behave myself wisely in a perfect way: Oh when wilt thou come unto me? I will walk within my house with a perfect heart.
019	PSA	101	003	I will set no base thing before mine eyes: I hate the work of them that turn aside; it shall not cleave unto me.
019	PSA	101	004	A froward heart shall depart from me: I will know no evil thing.
019	PSA	101	005	Whoso privily slandereth his neighbour, him will I destroy: him that hath an high look and a proud heart will I not suffer.
019	PSA	101	006	Mine eyes shall be upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walketh in a perfect way, he shall minister unto me.
019	PSA	101	007	He that worketh deceit shall not dwell within my house: he that speaketh falsehood shall not be established before mine eyes.
019	PSA	101	008	Morning by morning will I destroy all the wicked of the land; to cut off all the workers of iniquity from the city of the LORD.
019	PSA	102	001	A Prayer of the afflicted, when he is overwhelmed, and poureth out his complaint before the LORD. Hear my prayer, O LORD, and let my cry come unto thee.
019	PSA	102	002	Hide not thy face from me in the day of my distress: incline thine ear unto me; in the day when I call answer me speedily.
019	PSA	102	003	For my days consume away like smoke, and my bones are burned as a firebrand.
019	PSA	102	004	My heart is smitten like grass, and withered; for I forget to eat my bread.
019	PSA	102	005	By reason of the voice of my groaning my bones cleave to my flesh.
019	PSA	102	006	I am like a pelican of the wilderness; I am become as an owl of the waste places.
019	PSA	102	007	I watch, and am become like a sparrow that is alone upon the housetop.
019	PSA	102	008	Mine enemies reproach me all the day; they that are mad against me do curse by me.
019	PSA	102	009	For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping.
019	PSA	102	010	Because of thine indignation and thy wrath: for thou hast taken me up, and cast me away.
019	PSA	102	011	My days are like a shadow that declineth; and I am withered like grass.
019	PSA	102	012	But thou, O LORD, shalt abide for ever; and thy memorial unto all generations.
019	PSA	102	013	Thou shalt arise, and have mercy upon Zion: for it is time to have pity upon her, yea, the set time is come.
019	PSA	102	014	For thy servants take pleasure in her stones, and have pity upon her dust.
019	PSA	102	015	So the nations shall fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth thy glory:
019	PSA	102	016	For the LORD hath built up Zion, he hath appeared in his glory;
019	PSA	102	017	He hath regarded the prayer of the destitute, and hath not despised their prayer.
019	PSA	102	018	This shall be written for the generation to come: and a people which shall be created shall praise the LORD.
019	PSA	102	019	For he hath looked down from the height of his sanctuary; from heaven did the LORD behold the earth;
019	PSA	102	020	To hear the sighing of the prisoner; to loose those that are appointed to death;
019	PSA	102	021	That men may declare the name of the LORD in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;
019	PSA	102	022	When the peoples are gathered together, and the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.
019	PSA	102	023	He weakened my strength in the way; he shortened my days.
019	PSA	102	024	I said, O my God, take me not away in the midst of my days: thy years are throughout all generations.
019	PSA	102	025	Of old hast thou laid the foundation of the earth; and the heavens are the work of thy hands.
019	PSA	102	026	They shall perish, but thou shalt endure: yea, all of them shall wax old like a garment; as a vesture shalt thou change them, and they shall be changed:
019	PSA	102	027	But thou art the same, and thy years shall have no end.
019	PSA	102	028	The children of thy servants shall continue, and their seed shall be established before thee.
019	PSA	103	001	A Psalm of David. Bless the LORD, O my soul; and all that is within me, [bless] his holy name.
019	PSA	103	002	Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:
019	PSA	103	003	Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases;
019	PSA	103	004	Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies:
019	PSA	103	005	Who satisfieth thy mouth with good things; [so that] thy youth is renewed like the eagle.
019	PSA	103	006	The LORD executeth righteous acts, and judgments for all that are oppressed.
019	PSA	103	007	He made known his ways unto Moses, his doings unto the children of Israel.
019	PSA	103	008	The LORD is full of compassion and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy.
019	PSA	103	009	He will not always chide; neither will he keep [his anger] for ever.
019	PSA	103	010	He hath not dealt with us after our sins, nor rewarded us after our iniquities.
019	PSA	103	011	For as the heaven is high above the earth, so great is his mercy toward them that fear him.
019	PSA	103	012	As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our transgressions from us.
019	PSA	103	013	Like as a father pitieth his children, so the LORD pitieth them that fear him.
019	PSA	103	014	For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust.
019	PSA	103	015	As for man, his days are as grass; as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth.
019	PSA	103	016	For the wind passeth over it, and it is gone; and the place thereof shall know it no more.
019	PSA	103	017	But the mercy of the LORD is from everlasting to everlasting upon them that fear him, and his righteousness unto children’s children;
019	PSA	103	018	To such as keep his covenant, and to those that remember his precepts to do them.
019	PSA	103	019	The LORD hath established his throne in the heavens; and his kingdom ruleth over all.
019	PSA	103	020	Bless the LORD, ye angels of his: ye mighty in strength, that fulfill his word, hearkening unto the voice of his word.
019	PSA	103	021	Bless the LORD, all ye his hosts; ye ministers of his, that do his pleasure.
019	PSA	103	022	Bless the LORD, all ye his works, in all places of his dominion: bless the LORD, O my soul.
019	PSA	104	001	Bless the LORD O my soul, O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.
019	PSA	104	002	Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment; who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:
019	PSA	104	003	Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters; who maketh the clouds his chariot; who walketh upon the wings of the wind:
019	PSA	104	004	Who maketh winds his messengers; his ministers a flaming fire:
019	PSA	104	005	Who laid the foundations of the earth, that it should not be moved for ever.
019	PSA	104	006	Thou coveredst it with the deep as with a vesture; the waters stood above the mountains.
019	PSA	104	007	At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away;
019	PSA	104	008	They went up by the mountains, they went down by the valleys, unto the place which thou hadst founded for them.
019	PSA	104	009	Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.
019	PSA	104	010	He sendeth forth springs into the valleys; they run among the mountains:
019	PSA	104	011	They give drink to every beast of the field; the wild asses quench their thirst.
019	PSA	104	012	By them the fowl of the heaven have their habitation, they sing among the branches.
019	PSA	104	013	He watereth the mountains from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.
019	PSA	104	014	He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man; that he may bring forth food out of the earth:
019	PSA	104	015	And wine that maketh glad the heart of man, [and] oil to make his face to shine, and bread that strengtheneth man’s heart.
019	PSA	104	016	The trees of the LORD are satisfied; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;
019	PSA	104	017	Where the birds make their nests: as for the stork, the fir trees are her house.
019	PSA	104	018	The high mountains are for the wild goats; the rocks are a refuge for the conies.
019	PSA	104	019	He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.
019	PSA	104	020	Thou makest darkness, and it is night; Wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep forth.
019	PSA	104	021	The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.
019	PSA	104	022	The sun ariseth, they get them away, and lay them down in their dens.
019	PSA	104	023	Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.
019	PSA	104	024	O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.
019	PSA	104	025	Yonder is the sea, great and wide, wherein are things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.
019	PSA	104	026	There go the ships; there is leviathan, whom thou hast formed to take his pastime therein.
019	PSA	104	027	These wait all upon thee, that thou mayest give them their meat in due season.
019	PSA	104	028	That thou givest unto them they gather; thou openest thine hand, they are satisfied with good.
019	PSA	104	029	Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled; thou takest away their breath they die, and return to their dust.
019	PSA	104	030	Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created; and thou renewest the face of the ground.
019	PSA	104	031	Let the glory of the LORD endure for ever; let the LORD rejoice in his works:
019	PSA	104	032	Who looketh on the earth, and it trembleth; he toucheth the mountains, and they smoke.
019	PSA	104	033	I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have any being.
019	PSA	104	034	Let my meditation be sweet unto him: I will rejoice in the LORD.
019	PSA	104	035	Let sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	105	001	Give thanks unto the LORD, call upon his name; make known his doings among the peoples.
019	PSA	105	002	Sing unto him, sing praises unto him; talk ye of all his marvelous works.
019	PSA	105	003	Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.
019	PSA	105	004	Seek ye the LORD and his strength; seek his face evermore.
019	PSA	105	005	Remember his marvelous works that he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;
019	PSA	105	006	O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye children of Jacob, his chosen ones.
019	PSA	105	007	He is the LORD our God: his judgments are in all the earth.
019	PSA	105	008	He hath remembered his covenant for ever, the word which he commanded to a thousand generations;
019	PSA	105	009	[The covenant] which he made with Abraham, and his oath unto Isaac;
019	PSA	105	010	And confirmed the same unto Jacob for a statute, to Israel for an everlasting covenant:
019	PSA	105	011	Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance:
019	PSA	105	012	When they were but a few men in number; yea, very few, and sojourners in it;
019	PSA	105	013	And they went about from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another people.
019	PSA	105	014	He suffered no man to do them wrong; yea, he reproved kings for their sakes;
019	PSA	105	015	[Saying], Touch not mine anointed ones, and do my prophets no harm.
019	PSA	105	016	And he called for a famine upon the land; he brake the whole staff of bread.
019	PSA	105	017	He sent a man before them; Joseph was sold for a servant:
019	PSA	105	018	His feet they hurt with fetters; he was laid in [chains of] iron:
019	PSA	105	019	Until the time that his word came to pass; the word of the LORD tried him.
019	PSA	105	020	The king sent and loosed him; even the ruler of peoples, and let him go free.
019	PSA	105	021	He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all his substance:
019	PSA	105	022	To bind his princes at his pleasure, and teach his senators wisdom.
019	PSA	105	023	Israel also came into Egypt; and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.
019	PSA	105	024	And he increased his people greatly, and made them stronger than their adversaries.
019	PSA	105	025	He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal subtilly with his servants.
019	PSA	105	026	He sent Moses his servant, [and] Aaron whom he had chosen.
019	PSA	105	027	They set among them his signs, and wonders in the land of Ham.
019	PSA	105	028	He sent darkness, and made it dark; and they rebelled not against his words.
019	PSA	105	029	He turned their waters into blood, and slew their fish.
019	PSA	105	030	Their land swarmed with frogs, in the chambers of their kings.
019	PSA	105	031	He spake, and there came swarms of flies, and lice in all their borders.
019	PSA	105	032	He gave them hail for rain, [and] flaming fire in their land.
019	PSA	105	033	He smote their vines also and their fig trees; and brake the trees of their borders.
019	PSA	105	034	He spake, and the locust came, and the cankerworm, and that without number,
019	PSA	105	035	And did eat up every herb in their land, and did eat up the fruit of their ground.
019	PSA	105	036	He smote also all the firstborn in their land, the chief of all their strength.
019	PSA	105	037	And he brought them forth with silver and gold: and there was not one feeble person among his tribes.
019	PSA	105	038	Egypt was glad when they departed; for the fear of them had fallen upon them.
019	PSA	105	039	He spread a cloud for a covering; and fire to give light in the night.
019	PSA	105	040	They asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.
019	PSA	105	041	He opened the rock, and waters gushed out; they ran in the dry places [like] a river.
019	PSA	105	042	For he remembered his holy word, [and] Abraham his servant.
019	PSA	105	043	And he brought forth his people with joy, [and] his chosen with singing.
019	PSA	105	044	And he gave them the lands of the nations; and they took the labour of the peoples in possession:
019	PSA	105	045	That they might keep his statutes, and observe his laws. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	106	001	Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	106	002	Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD, or shew forth all his praise?
019	PSA	106	003	Blessed are they that keep judgment, and he that doeth righteousness at all times.
019	PSA	106	004	Remember me, O LORD, with the favour that thou bearest unto thy people; O visit me with thy salvation:
019	PSA	106	005	That I may see the prosperity of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.
019	PSA	106	006	We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.
019	PSA	106	007	Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but were rebellious at the sea, even at the Red Sea.
019	PSA	106	008	Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.
019	PSA	106	009	He rebuked the Red Sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through a wilderness.
019	PSA	106	010	And he saved them from the hand of him that hated them, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.
019	PSA	106	011	And the waters covered their adversaries: there was not one of them left.
019	PSA	106	012	Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.
019	PSA	106	013	They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel:
019	PSA	106	014	But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert.
019	PSA	106	015	And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.
019	PSA	106	016	They envied Moses also in the camp, [and] Aaron the saint of the LORD.
019	PSA	106	017	The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.
019	PSA	106	018	And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.
019	PSA	106	019	They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped a molten image.
019	PSA	106	020	Thus they changed their glory for the likeness of an ox that eateth grass.
019	PSA	106	021	They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;
019	PSA	106	022	Wondrous works in the land of Ham, [and] terrible things by the Red Sea.
019	PSA	106	023	Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy [them].
019	PSA	106	024	Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word;
019	PSA	106	025	But murmured in their tents, and hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD.
019	PSA	106	026	Therefore he lifted up his hand unto them, that he would overthrow them in the wilderness:
019	PSA	106	027	And that he would overthrow their seed among the nations, and scatter them in the lands.
019	PSA	106	028	They joined themselves also unto Baal-peor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
019	PSA	106	029	Thus they provoked him to anger with their doings; and the plague brake in upon them.
019	PSA	106	030	Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and so the plague was stayed.
019	PSA	106	031	And that was counted unto him for righteousness, unto all generations for evermore.
019	PSA	106	032	They angered him also at the waters of Meribah, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:
019	PSA	106	033	Because they were rebellious against his spirit, and he spake unadvisedly with his lips.
019	PSA	106	034	They did not destroy the peoples, as the LORD commanded them;
019	PSA	106	035	But mingled themselves with the nations, and learned their works:
019	PSA	106	036	And they served their idols; which became a snare unto them:
019	PSA	106	037	Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto demons,
019	PSA	106	038	And shed innocent blood, even the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan; and the land was polluted with blood.
019	PSA	106	039	Thus were they defiled with their works, and went a whoring in their doings.
019	PSA	106	040	Therefore was the wrath of the LORD kindled against his people, and he abhorred his inheritance.
019	PSA	106	041	And he gave them into the hand of the nations; and they that hated them ruled over them.
019	PSA	106	042	Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.
019	PSA	106	043	Many times did he deliver them; but they were rebellious in their counsel, and were brought low in their iniquity.
019	PSA	106	044	Nevertheless he regarded their distress, when he heard their cry:
019	PSA	106	045	And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.
019	PSA	106	046	He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.
019	PSA	106	047	Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from among the nations, to give thanks unto thy holy name, and to triumph in thy praise.
019	PSA	106	048	Blessed be the LORD, the God or Israel, from everlasting even to everlasting. And let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	107	001	O GIVE thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	107	002	Let the redeemed of the LORD say so, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the adversary;
019	PSA	107	003	And gathered them out of the lands, from the east and from the west, from the north and from the south.
019	PSA	107	004	They wandered in the wilderness in a desert way; they found no city of habitation.
019	PSA	107	005	Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.
019	PSA	107	006	Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, and he delivered them out of their distresses.
019	PSA	107	007	He led them also by a straight way, that they might go to a city of habitation.
019	PSA	107	008	Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!
019	PSA	107	009	For he satisfieth the longing soul, and the hungry soul he filleth with good.
019	PSA	107	010	Such as sat in darkness and in the shadow of death, being bound in affliction and iron;
019	PSA	107	011	Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the Most High:
019	PSA	107	012	Therefore he brought down their heart with labour; they fell down, and there was none to help.
019	PSA	107	013	Then they cried unto the LORD hi their trouble, and he saved them out of their distresses.
019	PSA	107	014	He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder.
019	PSA	107	015	Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!
019	PSA	107	016	For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron in sunder.
019	PSA	107	017	Fools because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.
019	PSA	107	018	Their soul abhorreth all manner of meat; and they draw near unto the gates of death.
019	PSA	107	019	Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he saveth them out of their distresses.
019	PSA	107	020	He sendeth his word, and healeth them, and delivereth [them] from their destructions.
019	PSA	107	021	Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!
019	PSA	107	022	And let them offer the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with singing.
019	PSA	107	023	They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business in great waters;
019	PSA	107	024	These see the works of the LORD, and his wonders in the deep.
019	PSA	107	025	For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up the waves thereof.
019	PSA	107	026	They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul melteth away because of trouble.
019	PSA	107	027	They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wits’ end.
019	PSA	107	028	Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.
019	PSA	107	029	He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.
019	PSA	107	030	Then are they glad because they be quiet: so he bringeth them unto the haven where they would be.
019	PSA	107	031	Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!
019	PSA	107	032	Let them exalt him also in the assembly of the people, and praise him in the seat of the elders.
019	PSA	107	033	He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and watersprings into a thirsty ground;
019	PSA	107	034	A fruitful land into a salt desert, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein.
019	PSA	107	035	He turneth a wilderness into a pool of water, and a dry land into watersprings.
019	PSA	107	036	And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city of habitation;
019	PSA	107	037	And sow fields, and plant vineyards, and get them fruits of increase.
019	PSA	107	038	He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and he suffereth not their cattle to decrease.
019	PSA	107	039	Again, they are minished and bowed down through oppression, trouble, and sorrow.
019	PSA	107	040	He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the waste, where there is no way.
019	PSA	107	041	Yet setteth he the needy on high from affliction, and maketh [him] families like a flock.
019	PSA	107	042	The upright shall see it, and be glad; and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.
019	PSA	107	043	Whoso is wise shall give heed to these things, and they shall consider the mercies of the LORD.
019	PSA	108	001	A Song, a Psalm Of David. My heart is fixed, O God; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises, even with my glory.
019	PSA	108	002	Awake, psaltery and harp: I myself will awake right early.
019	PSA	108	003	I will give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the peoples: and I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.
019	PSA	108	004	For thy mercy is great above the heavens, and thy truth [reacheth] unto the skies.
019	PSA	108	005	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth.
019	PSA	108	006	That thy beloved may be delivered, save with thy right hand, and answer us.
019	PSA	108	007	God hath spoken in his holiness; I will exult: I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
019	PSA	108	008	Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine; Ephraim also is the defence of mine head; Judah is my sceptre.
019	PSA	108	009	Moab is my washpot; upon Edom will I cast my shoe: over Philistia will I shout.
019	PSA	108	010	Who will bring me into the fenced city? who hath led me unto Edom?
019	PSA	108	011	Hast not thou cast us off, O God? and thou goest not forth, O God, with our hosts.
019	PSA	108	012	Give us help against the adversary: for vain is the help of man.
019	PSA	108	013	Through God we shall do valiantly: for he it is that shall tread down our adversaries.
019	PSA	109	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;
019	PSA	109	002	For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of deceit have they opened against me: they have spoken unto me with a lying tongue.
019	PSA	109	003	They compassed me about also with words of hatred, and fought against me without a cause.
019	PSA	109	004	For my love they are my adversaries: but I [give myself unto] prayer.
019	PSA	109	005	And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.
019	PSA	109	006	Set thou a wicked man over him: and let an adversary stand at his right hand.
019	PSA	109	007	When he is judged, let him come forth guilty; and let his prayer be turned into sin.
019	PSA	109	008	Let his days be few; [and] let another take his office.
019	PSA	109	009	Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.
019	PSA	109	010	Let his children be vagabonds, and beg; and let them seek [their bread] out of their desolate places.
019	PSA	109	011	Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let strangers make spoil of his labour.
019	PSA	109	012	Let there be none to extend mercy unto him; neither let there be any to have pity on his fatherless children.
019	PSA	109	013	Let his posterity be cut off; in the generation following let their name be blotted out.
019	PSA	109	014	Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the LORD; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.
019	PSA	109	015	Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.
019	PSA	109	016	Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, and the broken in heart, to slay [them].
019	PSA	109	017	Yea, he loved cursing, and it came unto him; and he delighted not in blessing, and it was far from him.
019	PSA	109	018	He clothed himself also with cursing as with his garment, and it came into his inward parts like water, and like oil into his bones. Let it be unto him as the raiment
019	PSA	109	019	wherewith he covereth himself, and for the girdle wherewith he is girded continually.
019	PSA	109	020	This is the reward of mine adversaries from the LORD, and of them that speak evil against my soul.
019	PSA	109	021	But deal thou with me, O GOD the Lord, for thy name’s sake: because thy mercy is good, deliver thou me,
019	PSA	109	022	For I am poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.
019	PSA	109	023	I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.
019	PSA	109	024	My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.
019	PSA	109	025	I am become also a reproach unto them: when they see me, they shake their head.
019	PSA	109	026	Help me, O LORD my God; O save me according to thy mercy:
019	PSA	109	027	That they may know that this is thy hand; [that] thou, LORD, hast done it.
019	PSA	109	028	Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, they shall be ashamed, but thy servant shall rejoice.
019	PSA	109	029	Let mine adversaries be clothed with dishonour, and let them cover themselves with their own shame as with a mantle.
019	PSA	109	030	I will give great thanks unto the LORD with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.
019	PSA	109	031	For he shall stand at the right hand of the needy, to save him from them that judge his soul.
019	PSA	110	001	A Psalm of David. The LORD saith unto my lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.
019	PSA	110	002	The LORD shall send forth the rod of thy strength out of Zion: rule thou in the midst of thine enemies.
019	PSA	110	003	Thy people offer themselves willingly in the day of thy power: in the beauties of holiness, from the womb of the morning, thou hast the dew of thy youth.
019	PSA	110	004	The LORD hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melchizedek.
019	PSA	110	005	The Lord at thy right hand shall strike through kings in the day of his wrath.
019	PSA	110	006	He shall judge among the nations, he shall fill [the places] with dead bodies; he shall strike through the head in many countries.
019	PSA	110	007	He shall drink of the brook in the way: therefore shall he lift up the head.
019	PSA	111	001	Praise ye the LORD. I will give thanks unto the LORD with my whole heart, in the council of the upright, and in the congregation.
019	PSA	111	002	The works of the LORD are great, sought out of all them that have pleasure therein.
019	PSA	111	003	His work is honour and majesty: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
019	PSA	111	004	He hath made his wonderful works to be remembered: the LORD is gracious and full of compassion.
019	PSA	111	005	He hath given meat unto them that fear him: he will ever be mindful of his covenant.
019	PSA	111	006	He hath shewed his people the power of his works, in giving them the heritage of the nations.
019	PSA	111	007	The works of his hands are truth and judgment; all his precepts are sure.
019	PSA	111	008	They are established for ever and ever, they are done in truth and uprightness.
019	PSA	111	009	He hath sent redemption unto his people; he hath commanded his covenant for ever: holy and reverend is his name.
019	PSA	111	010	The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom; a good understanding have all they that do thereafter: his praise endureth for ever.
019	PSA	112	001	Praise ye the LORD. Blessed is the man that feareth the LORD, that delighteth greatly in his commandments.
019	PSA	112	002	His seed shall be mighty upon earth: the generation of the upright shall be blessed.
019	PSA	112	003	Wealth and riches are in his house: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
019	PSA	112	004	Unto the upright there ariseth light in the darkness: [he is] gracious, and full of compassion, and righteous.
019	PSA	112	005	Well is it with the man that dealeth graciously and lendeth; he shall maintain his cause in judgment.
019	PSA	112	006	For he shall never be moved; the righteous shall be had in everlasting remembrance.
019	PSA	112	007	He shall not be afraid of evil tidings: his heart is fixed, trusting in the LORD.
019	PSA	112	008	His heart is established, he shall not be afraid, until he see [his desire] upon his adversaries.
019	PSA	112	009	He hath dispersed, he hath given to the needy; his righteousness endureth for ever: his horn shall be exalted with honour.
019	PSA	112	010	The wicked shall see it, and be grieved; he shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away: the desire of the wicked shall perish.
019	PSA	113	001	Praise ye the LORD. Praise, O ye servants of the LORD, praise the name of the LORD.
019	PSA	113	002	Blessed be the name of the LORD from this time forth and for evermore.
019	PSA	113	003	From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same the LORD’S name is to be praised.
019	PSA	113	004	The LORD is high above all nations, and his glory above the heavens.
019	PSA	113	005	Who is like unto the LORD our God, that hath his seat on high,
019	PSA	113	006	That humbleth himself to behold [the things that are] in heaven and in the earth?
019	PSA	113	007	He raiseth up the poor out of the dust, and lifteth up the needy from the dunghill;
019	PSA	113	008	That he may set him with princes, even with the princes of his people.
019	PSA	113	009	He maketh the barren woman to keep house, [and to be] a joyful mother of children. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	114	001	When Israel went forth out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of strange language;
019	PSA	114	002	Judah became his sanctuary, Israel his dominion.
019	PSA	114	003	The sea saw it, and fled; Jordan was driven back.
019	PSA	114	004	The mountains skipped like rams, the little hills like young sheep.
019	PSA	114	005	What aileth thee, O thou sea, that thou fleest? thou Jordan, that thou turnest back?
019	PSA	114	006	Ye mountains, that ye skip like rams; ye little hills, like young sheep?
019	PSA	114	007	Tremble, thou earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob;
019	PSA	114	008	Which turned the rock into a pool of water, the flint into a fountain of waters.
019	PSA	115	001	Not unto us, O LORD, not unto us, but unto thy name give glory, for thy mercy, and for thy truth’s sake.
019	PSA	115	002	Wherefore should the nations say, Where is now their God?
019	PSA	115	003	But our God is in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he pleased.
019	PSA	115	004	Their idols are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.
019	PSA	115	005	They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;
019	PSA	115	006	They have ears, but they hear not; noses have they, but they smell not;
019	PSA	115	007	They have hands, but they handle not; feet have they, but they walk not; neither speak they through their throat.
019	PSA	115	008	They that make them shall be like unto them; yea, every one that trusteth in them.
019	PSA	115	009	O Israel, trust thou in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.
019	PSA	115	010	O house of Aaron, trust ye in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.
019	PSA	115	011	Ye that fear the LORD, trust in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.
019	PSA	115	012	The LORD hath been mindful of us; he will bless [us]: he will bless the house of Israel; he will bless the house of Aaron.
019	PSA	115	013	He will bless them that fear the LORD, both small and great.
019	PSA	115	014	The LORD increase you more and more, you and your children.
019	PSA	115	015	Blessed are ye of the LORD, which made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	115	016	The heavens are the heavens of the LORD; but the earth hath he given to the children of men.
019	PSA	115	017	The dead praise not the LORD, neither any that go down into silence;
019	PSA	115	018	But we will bless the LORD from this time forth and for evermore. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	116	001	I LOVE the LORD, because he hath heard my voice and my supplications.
019	PSA	116	002	Because he hath inclined his ear unto me, therefore will I call [upon him] as long as I live.
019	PSA	116	003	The cords of death compassed me, and the pains of Sheol gat hold upon me: I found trouble and sorrow.
019	PSA	116	004	Then called I upon the name of the LORD; O LORD, I beseech thee, deliver my soul.
019	PSA	116	005	Gracious is the LORD, and righteous; yea, our God is merciful.
019	PSA	116	006	The LORD preserveth the simple: I was brought low, and he saved me.
019	PSA	116	007	Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee.
019	PSA	116	008	For thou hast delivered my soul from death, mine eyes from tears, [and] my feet from falling.
019	PSA	116	009	I will walk before the LORD in the land of the living.
019	PSA	116	010	I believe, for I will speak: I was greatly afflicted:
019	PSA	116	011	I said in my haste, All men are a lie.
019	PSA	116	012	What shall I render unto the LORD for all his benefits toward me?
019	PSA	116	013	I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the LORD.
019	PSA	116	014	I will pay my vows unto the LORD, yea, in the presence of all his people.
019	PSA	116	015	Precious in the sight of the LORD is the death of his saints.
019	PSA	116	016	O LORD, truly I am thy servant: I am thy servant, the son of thine handmaid; thou hast loosed my bonds.
019	PSA	116	017	I will offer to thee the sacrifice of thanksgiving, and will call upon the name of the LORD.
019	PSA	116	018	I will pay my vows unto the LORD, yea, in the presence of all his people.
019	PSA	116	019	In the courts of the LORD’S house, in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	117	001	O PRAISE the LORD, all ye nations; laud him, all ye peoples.
019	PSA	117	002	For his mercy is great toward us; and the truth of the LORD [endureth] for ever. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	118	001	O GIVE thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	118	002	Let Israel now say, that his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	118	003	Let the house of Aaron now say, that his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	118	004	Let them now that fear the LORD say, that his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	118	005	Out of my distress I called upon the LORD: the LORD answered me [and set me] in a large place.
019	PSA	118	006	The LORD is on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me?
019	PSA	118	007	The LORD is on my side among them that help me: therefore shall I see [my desire] upon them that hate me.
019	PSA	118	008	It is better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in man.
019	PSA	118	009	It is better to trust in the LORD, than to put confidence in princes.
019	PSA	118	010	All nations compassed me about: in the name of the LORD I will cut them off.
019	PSA	118	011	They compassed me about; yea, they compassed me about: in the name of the LORD I will cut them off.
019	PSA	118	012	They compassed me about like bees; they are quenched as the fire of thorns: in the name of the LORD I will cut them off.
019	PSA	118	013	Thou didst thrust sore at me that I might fall: but the LORD helped me.
019	PSA	118	014	The LORD is my strength and song; and he is become my salvation.
019	PSA	118	015	The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tents of the righteous: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.
019	PSA	118	016	The right hand of the LORD is exalted: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.
019	PSA	118	017	I shall not die, but live, and declare the works of the LORD.
019	PSA	118	018	The LORD hath chastened me sore: but he hath not given me over unto death.
019	PSA	118	019	Open to me the gates of righteousness: I will enter into them, I will give thanks unto the LORD.
019	PSA	118	020	This is the gate of the LORD; the righteous shall enter into it.
019	PSA	118	021	I will give thanks unto thee, for thou hast answered me, and art become my salvation.
019	PSA	118	022	The stone which the builders rejected is become the head of the corner.
019	PSA	118	023	This is the LORD’S doing; it is marvelous in our eyes.
019	PSA	118	024	This is the day which the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.
019	PSA	118	025	Save now, we beseech thee, O LORD: O LORD, we beseech thee, send now prosperity.
019	PSA	118	026	Blessed be he that cometh in the name of the LORD: we have blessed you out of the house of the LORD.
019	PSA	118	027	The LORD is God, and he hath given us light: bind the sacrifice with cords, even unto the horns of the altar.
019	PSA	118	028	Thou art my God, and I will give thanks unto thee: thou art my God, I will exalt thee.
019	PSA	118	029	O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	119	001	Blessed are they that are perfect in the way, who walk in the law of the LORD.
019	PSA	119	002	Blessed are they that keep his testimonies, that seek him with the whole heart.
019	PSA	119	003	Yea, they do no unrighteousness; they walk in his ways.
019	PSA	119	004	Thou hast commanded [us] thy precepts, that we should observe them diligently.
019	PSA	119	005	Oh that my ways were established to observe thy statutes!
019	PSA	119	006	Then shall I not be ashamed, when I have respect unto all thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	007	I will give thanks unto thee with uprightness of heart, when I learn thy righteous judgments.
019	PSA	119	008	I will observe thy statutes: O forsake me not utterly.
019	PSA	119	009	Wherewithal shall a young man cleanse his way? by taking heed [thereto] according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	010	With my whole heart have I sought thee: O let me not wander from thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	011	Thy word have I laid up in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.
019	PSA	119	012	Blessed art thou, O LORD: teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	013	With my lips have I declared all the judgments of thy mouth.
019	PSA	119	014	I have rejoiced in the way of thy testimonies, as much as in all riches.
019	PSA	119	015	I will meditate in thy precepts, and have respect unto thy ways.
019	PSA	119	016	I will delight myself in thy statutes: I will not forget thy word.
019	PSA	119	017	Deal bountifully with thy servant, that I may live; so will I observe thy word.
019	PSA	119	018	Open thou mine eyes, that I may behold wondrous things out of thy law.
019	PSA	119	019	I am a sojourner in the earth: hide not thy commandments from me.
019	PSA	119	020	My soul breaketh for the longing that it hath unto thy judgments at all times.
019	PSA	119	021	Thou hast rebuked the proud that are cursed, which do wander from thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	022	Take away from me reproach and contempt; for I have kept thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	023	Princes also sat and talked against me: [but] thy servant did meditate in thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	024	Thy testimonies also are my delight [and] my counsellors.
019	PSA	119	025	My soul cleaveth unto the dust: quicken thou me according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	026	I declared my ways, and thou answeredst me: teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	027	Make me to understand the way of thy precepts: so shall I meditate of thy wondrous works.
019	PSA	119	028	My soul melteth for heaviness: strengthen thou me according unto thy word.
019	PSA	119	029	Remove from me the way of falsehood: and grant me thy law graciously.
019	PSA	119	030	I have chosen the way of faithfulness: thy judgments have I set [before me].
019	PSA	119	031	I cleave unto thy testimonies: O LORD, put me not to shame.
019	PSA	119	032	I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart.
019	PSA	119	033	Teach me, O LORD, the way of thy statutes; and I shall keep it unto the end.
019	PSA	119	034	Give me understanding, and I shall keep thy law; yea, I shall observe it with my whole heart.
019	PSA	119	035	Make me to go in the path of thy commandments; for therein do I delight.
019	PSA	119	036	Incline my heart unto thy testimonies, and not to covetousness.
019	PSA	119	037	Turn away mine eyes from beholding vanity, and quicken me in thy ways.
019	PSA	119	038	Confirm thy word unto thy servant, which [belongeth] unto the fear of thee.
019	PSA	119	039	Turn away my reproach whereof I am afraid; for thy judgments are good.
019	PSA	119	040	Behold, I have longed after thy precepts: quicken me in thy righteousness.
019	PSA	119	041	Let thy mercies also come unto me, O LORD, even thy salvation, according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	042	So shall I have an answer for him that reproacheth me; for I trust in thy word.
019	PSA	119	043	And take not the word of truth utterly out of my mouth; for I have hoped in thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	044	So shall I observe thy law continually for ever and ever.
019	PSA	119	045	And I will walk at liberty; for I have sought thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	046	I will also speak of thy testimonies before kings, and will not be ashamed.
019	PSA	119	047	And I will delight myself in thy commandments, which I have loved.
019	PSA	119	048	I will lift up my hands also unto thy commandments, which I have loved; and I will meditate in thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	049	Remember the word unto thy servant, because thou hast made me to hope.
019	PSA	119	050	This is my comfort in my affliction: for thy word hath quickened me.
019	PSA	119	051	The proud have had me greatly in derision: [yet] have I not swerved from thy law.
019	PSA	119	052	I have remembered thy judgments of old, O LORD, and have comforted myself.
019	PSA	119	053	Hot indignation hath taken hold upon me, because of the wicked that forsake thy law.
019	PSA	119	054	Thy statutes have been my songs in the house of my pilgrimage.
019	PSA	119	055	I have remembered thy name, O LORD, in the night, and have observed thy law.
019	PSA	119	056	This I have had, because I kept thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	057	The LORD is my portion: I have said that I would observe thy words.
019	PSA	119	058	I entreated thy favour with my whole heart: be merciful unto me according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	059	I thought on my ways, and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	060	I made haste, and delayed not, to observe thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	061	The cords of the wicked have wrapped me round; [but] I have not forgotten thy law.
019	PSA	119	062	At midnight I will rise to give thanks unto thee because of thy righteous judgments.
019	PSA	119	063	I am a companion of all them that fear thee, and of them that observe thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	064	The earth, O LORD, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	065	Thou hast dealt well with thy servant, O LORD, according unto thy word.
019	PSA	119	066	Teach me good judgment and knowledge; for I have believed in thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	067	Before I was afflicted I went astray; but now I observe thy word.
019	PSA	119	068	Thou art good, and doest good; teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	069	The proud have forged a lie against me: with my whole heart will I keep thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	070	Their heart is as fat as grease; but I delight in thy law.
019	PSA	119	071	It is good for me that I have been afflicted; that I might learn thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	072	The law of thy mouth is better unto me than thousands of gold and silver.
019	PSA	119	073	Thy hands have made me and fashioned me: give me understanding, that I may learn thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	074	They that fear thee shall see me and be glad; because I have hoped in thy word.
019	PSA	119	075	I know, O LORD, that thy judgments are righteous, and that in faithfulness thou hast afflicted me.
019	PSA	119	076	Let, I pray thee, thy lovingkindness be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant.
019	PSA	119	077	Let thy tender mercies come unto me, that I may live: for thy law is my delight.
019	PSA	119	078	Let the proud be ashamed; for they have overthrown me wrongfully: [but] I will meditate in thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	079	Let those that fear thee turn unto me, and they shall know thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	080	Let my heart be perfect in thy statutes; that I be not ashamed.
019	PSA	119	081	My soul fainteth for thy salvation: [but] I hope in thy word.
019	PSA	119	082	Mine eyes fail for thy word, while I say, When wilt thou comfort me?
019	PSA	119	083	For I am become like a bottle in the smoke; yet do I not forget thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	084	How many are the days of thy servant? when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?
019	PSA	119	085	The proud have digged pits for me, who are not after thy law.
019	PSA	119	086	All thy commandments are faithful: they persecute me wrongfully; help thou me.
019	PSA	119	087	They had almost consumed me upon earth; but I forsook not thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	088	Quicken me after thy lovingkindness; so shall I observe the testimony of thy mouth.
019	PSA	119	089	For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven.
019	PSA	119	090	Thy faithfulness is unto all generations: thou hast established the earth, and it abideth.
019	PSA	119	091	They abide this day according to thine ordinances; for all things are thy servants.
019	PSA	119	092	Unless thy law had been my delight, I should then have perished in mine affliction.
019	PSA	119	093	I will never forget thy precepts; for with them thou hast quickened me.
019	PSA	119	094	I am thine, save me; for I have sought thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	095	The wicked have waited for me to destroy me; [but] I will consider thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	096	I have seen an end of all perfection; [but] thy commandment is exceeding broad.
019	PSA	119	097	Oh how love I thy law! it is my meditation all the day.
019	PSA	119	098	Thy commandments make me wiser than mine enemies; for they are ever with me.
019	PSA	119	099	I have more understanding than all my teachers; for thy testimonies are my (meditation)
019	PSA	119	100	I understand more than the aged, because I have kept thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	101	I have refrained my feet from every evil way, that I might observe thy word.
019	PSA	119	102	I have not turned aside from thy judgments; for thou hast taught me.
019	PSA	119	103	How sweet are thy words unto my taste! [yea, sweeter] than honey to my mouth!
019	PSA	119	104	Through thy precepts I get understanding: therefore I hate every false way.
019	PSA	119	105	Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and light unto my path,
019	PSA	119	106	I have sworn, and have confirmed it, that I will observe thy righteous judgments.
019	PSA	119	107	I am afflicted very much: quicken me, O LORD, according unto thy word.
019	PSA	119	108	Accept, I beseech thee, the freewill offerings of my mouth, O LORD, and teach me thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	109	My soul is continually in my hand; yet do I not forget thy law.
019	PSA	119	110	The wicked have laid a snare for me; yet went I not astray from thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	111	Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage for ever; for they are the rejoicing of my heart.
019	PSA	119	112	I have inclined mine heart to perform thy statutes, for ever, even unto the end.
019	PSA	119	113	I hate them that are of a double mind; but thy law do I love.
019	PSA	119	114	Thou art my hiding place and my shield: I hope in thy word.
019	PSA	119	115	Depart from me, ye evil-doers; that I may keep the commandments of my God.
019	PSA	119	116	Uphold me according unto thy word, that I may live; and let me not be ashamed of my hope.
019	PSA	119	117	Hold thou me up, and I shall be safe, and shall have respect unto thy statutes continually.
019	PSA	119	118	Thou hast set at nought all them that err from thy statutes; for their deceit is falsehood.
019	PSA	119	119	Thou puttest away all the wicked of the earth like dross: therefore I love thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	120	My flesh trembleth for fear of thee; and I am afraid of thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	121	I have done judgment and justice: leave me not to mine oppressors.
019	PSA	119	122	Be surety for thy servant for good: let not the proud oppress me.
019	PSA	119	123	Mine eyes fail for thy salvation, and for thy righteous word.
019	PSA	119	124	Deal with thy servant according unto thy mercy, and teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	125	I am thy servant, give me understanding; that I may know thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	126	It is time for the LORD to work; [for] they have made void thy law.
019	PSA	119	127	Therefore I love thy commandments above gold, yea, above fine gold.
019	PSA	119	128	Therefore I esteem all [thy] precepts concerning all [things] to be right; [and] I hate every false way.
019	PSA	119	129	Thy testimonies are wonderful: therefore doth my soul keep them.
019	PSA	119	130	The opening of thy words giveth light; it giveth understanding unto the simple.
019	PSA	119	131	I opened wide my mouth, and panted; for I longed for thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	132	Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me, as thou usest to do unto those that love thy name.
019	PSA	119	133	Order my footsteps in thy word; and let not any iniquity have dominion over me.
019	PSA	119	134	Redeem me from the oppression of man: so will I observe thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	135	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; and teach me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	136	Mine eyes run down with rivers of water, because they observe not thy law.
019	PSA	119	137	Righteous art thou, O LORD, and upright are thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	138	Thou hast commanded thy testimonies in righteousness and very faithfulness.
019	PSA	119	139	My zeal hath consumed me, because mine adversaries have forgotten thy words.
019	PSA	119	140	Thy word is very pure; therefore thy servant loveth it.
019	PSA	119	141	I am small and despised: [yet] do not I forget thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	142	Thy righteousness is an everlasting righteousness, and thy law is truth.
019	PSA	119	143	Trouble and anguish have taken hold on me: [yet] thy commandments are my delight.
019	PSA	119	144	Thy testimonies are righteous for ever: give me understanding, and I shall live.
019	PSA	119	145	I have called with my whole heart; answer me, O LORD: I will keep thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	146	I have called unto thee; save me, and I shall observe thy testimonies.
019	PSA	119	147	I prevented the dawning of the morning, and cried: I hoped in thy words.
019	PSA	119	148	Mine eyes prevented the night watches, that I might meditate in thy word.
019	PSA	119	149	Hear my voice according unto thy lovingkindness: quicken me, O LORD, according to thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	150	They draw nigh that follow after wickedness; they are far from thy law.
019	PSA	119	151	Thou art nigh, O LORD; and all thy commandments are truth.
019	PSA	119	152	Of old have I known from thy testimonies, that thou hast founded them for ever.
019	PSA	119	153	Consider mine affliction, and deliver me; for I do not forget thy law.
019	PSA	119	154	Plead thou my cause, and redeem me: quicken me according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	155	Salvation is far from the wicked; for they seek not thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	156	Great are thy tender mercies, O LORD: quicken me according to thy judgments.
019	PSA	119	157	Many are my persecutors and mine adversaries; [yet] have I not swerved from they testimonies.
019	PSA	119	158	I beheld the treacherous dealers, and was grieved; because they observed not thy word.
019	PSA	119	159	Consider how I love thy precepts: quicken me, O LORD, according to thy lovingkindness.
019	PSA	119	160	The sum of thy word is truth; and every one of thy righteous judgments [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	119	161	Princes have persecuted me without a cause; but my heart standeth in awe of thy words.
019	PSA	119	162	I rejoice at thy word, as one that findeth great spoil.
019	PSA	119	163	I hate and abhor falsehood; [but] thy law do I love.
019	PSA	119	164	Seven times a day do I praise thee, because of thy righteous judgments.
019	PSA	119	165	Great peace have they which love thy law; and they have none occasion of stumbling.
019	PSA	119	166	I have hoped for thy salvation, O LORD, and have done thy commandments.
019	PSA	119	167	My soul hath observed thy testimonies; and I love them exceedingly.
019	PSA	119	168	I have observed thy precepts and thy testimonies; for all my ways are before thee.
019	PSA	119	169	Let my cry come near before thee, O LORD: give me understanding according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	170	Let my supplication come before thee: deliver me according to thy word.
019	PSA	119	171	Let my lips utter praise; for thou teachest me thy statutes.
019	PSA	119	172	Let my tongue sing of thy word; for all thy commandments are righteousness.
019	PSA	119	173	Let thine hand be ready to help me; for I have chosen thy precepts.
019	PSA	119	174	I have longed for thy salvation, O LORD; and thy law is my delight.
019	PSA	119	175	Let my soul live, and it shall praise thee; and let thy judgments help me.
019	PSA	119	176	I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not forget thy commandments.
019	PSA	120	001	A Song of Ascents. In my distress I cried unto the LORD, and he answered me.
019	PSA	120	002	Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips, [and] from a deceitful tongue.
019	PSA	120	003	What shall be given unto thee, and what shall be done more unto thee, thou deceitful tongue?
019	PSA	120	004	Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.
019	PSA	120	005	Woe is me, that I sojourn in Meshech, that I dwell among the tents of Kedar!
019	PSA	120	006	My soul hath long had her dwelling with him that hateth peace.
019	PSA	120	007	I am [for] peace: but when I speak, they are for war.
019	PSA	121	001	A Song of Ascents. I will lift up mine eyes unto the mountains: from whence shall my help come?
019	PSA	121	002	My help [cometh] from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	121	003	He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber.
019	PSA	121	004	Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.
019	PSA	121	005	The LORD is thy keeper: the LORD is thy shade upon thy right hand.
019	PSA	121	006	The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.
019	PSA	121	007	The LORD shall keep thee from all evil; he shall keep thy soul.
019	PSA	121	008	The LORD shall keep thy going out and thy coming in, from this time forth and for evermore.
019	PSA	122	001	A Song of Ascents; of David. I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go unto the house of the LORD.
019	PSA	122	002	Our feet are standing within thy gates, O Jerusalem;
019	PSA	122	003	Jerusalem, that art builded as a city that is compact together:
019	PSA	122	004	Whither the tribes go up, even the tribes of the LORD [for] a testimony unto Israel, to give thanks into the name of the LORD.
019	PSA	122	005	For there are set thrones for judgment, the thrones of the house of David.
019	PSA	122	006	Pray for the peace of Jerusalem: they shall prosper that love thee.
019	PSA	122	007	Peace be within thy walls, and prosperity within thy palaces.
019	PSA	122	008	For my brethren and companions’ sakes, I will now say, Peace be within thee.
019	PSA	122	009	For the sake of the house of the LORD our God I will seek thy good.
019	PSA	123	001	A Song of Ascents. Unto thee do I lift up mine eyes, O thou that sittest in the heavens.
019	PSA	123	002	Behold, as the eyes of servants [look] unto the hand of their master, as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes [look] unto the LORD our God, until he have mercy upon us.
019	PSA	123	003	Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.
019	PSA	123	004	Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, and with the contempt of the proud.
019	PSA	124	001	A Song of Ascents; of David. If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, let Israel now say;
019	PSA	124	002	If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, when men rose up against us:
019	PSA	124	003	Then they had swallowed us up alive, when their wrath was kindled against us:
019	PSA	124	004	Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:
019	PSA	124	005	Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.
019	PSA	124	006	Blessed be the LORD, who hath not given us as a prey to their teeth.
019	PSA	124	007	Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.
019	PSA	124	008	Our help is in the name of the LORD, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	125	001	A Song of Ascents. They that trust in the LORD are as mount Zion, which cannot be moved, but abideth for ever.
019	PSA	125	002	As the mountains are round about Jerusalem, so the LORD is round about his people, from this time forth and for evermore.
019	PSA	125	003	For the sceptre of wickedness shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous; that the righteous put not forth their hands unto iniquity.
019	PSA	125	004	Do good, O LORD, unto those that be good, and to them that are upright in their hearts.
019	PSA	125	005	But as for such as turn aside unto their crooked ways, the LORD shall lead them forth with the workers of iniquity. Peace be upon Israel.
019	PSA	126	001	A Song of Ascents. When the LORD turned again the captivity of Zion, we were like unto them that dream.
019	PSA	126	002	Then was our mouth filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing: then said they among the nations, The LORD hath done great things for them.
019	PSA	126	003	The LORD hath done great things for us; [whereof] we are glad.
019	PSA	126	004	Turn again our captivity, O LORD, as the streams in the South.
019	PSA	126	005	They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.
019	PSA	126	006	Though he goeth on his way weeping, bearing forth the seed; he shall come again with joy, bringing his sheaves [with him].
019	PSA	127	001	A Song of Ascents; of Solomon. Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the LORD keep the city, the watchman waketh but in vain.
019	PSA	127	002	It is vain for you that ye rise up early, and so late take rest, and eat the bread of toil: [for] so he giveth unto his beloved sleep.
019	PSA	127	003	Lo, children are an heritage of the LORD: [and] the fruit of the womb is [his] reward.
019	PSA	127	004	As arrows in the hand of a mighty man, so are the children of youth.
019	PSA	127	005	Happy is the man that hath his quiver full of them: they shall not be ashamed, when they speak with their enemies in the gate.
019	PSA	128	001	A Song of Ascents. Blessed is every one that feareth the LORD, that walketh in his ways.
019	PSA	128	002	For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy shalt thou be, and it shall be well with thee.
019	PSA	128	003	Thy wife shall be as a fruitful vine, in the innermost parts of thine house: thy children like olive plants, round about thy table.
019	PSA	128	004	Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the LORD.
019	PSA	128	005	The LORD shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.
019	PSA	128	006	Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s children. Peace be upon Israel.
019	PSA	129	001	A Song of Ascents. Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth up, let Israel now say;
019	PSA	129	002	Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth up: yet they have not prevailed against me.
019	PSA	129	003	The plowers plowed upon my back; they made long their furrows.
019	PSA	129	004	The LORD is righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.
019	PSA	129	005	Let them be ashamed and turned backward, all they that hate Zion.
019	PSA	129	006	Let them be as the grass upon the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:
019	PSA	129	007	Wherewith the reaper filleth not his hand, nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.
019	PSA	129	008	Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD be upon you; we bless you in the name of the LORD.
019	PSA	130	001	A Song of Ascents. Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O LORD.
019	PSA	130	002	Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications.
019	PSA	130	003	If thou, LORD, shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?
019	PSA	130	004	But there is forgiveness with thee, that thou mayest be feared.
019	PSA	130	005	I wait for the LORD, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope.
019	PSA	130	006	My soul [looketh] for the Lord, more than watchmen [look] for the morning; [yea, more than] watchmen for the morning.
019	PSA	130	007	O Israel, hope in the LORD; for with the LORD there is mercy, and with him is plenteous redemption.
019	PSA	130	008	And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.
019	PSA	131	001	A Song of Ascents; of David. LORD, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty; neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too wonderful for me.
019	PSA	131	002	Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul; like a weaned child with his mother, my soul is with me like a weaned child.
019	PSA	131	003	O Israel, hope in the LORD from this time forth and for evermore.
019	PSA	132	001	A Song of Ascents. LORD, remember for David all his affliction;
019	PSA	132	002	How he sware unto the LORD, and vowed unto the Mighty One of Jacob:
019	PSA	132	003	Surely I will not come into the tabernacle of my house, nor go up into my bed;
019	PSA	132	004	I will not give sleep to mine eyes, or slumber to mine eyelids;
019	PSA	132	005	Until I find out a place for the LORD, a tabernacle for the Mighty One of Jacob.
019	PSA	132	006	Lo, we heard of it in Ephrathah: we found it in the field of the wood.
019	PSA	132	007	We will go into his tabernacles; we will worship at his footstool.
019	PSA	132	008	Arise, O LORD, into thy resting place; thou, and the ark of thy strength.
019	PSA	132	009	Let thy priests be clothed with righteousness; and let thy saints shout for joy.
019	PSA	132	010	For thy servant David’s sake turn not away the face of thine anointed.
019	PSA	132	011	The LORD hath sworn unto David in truth; he will not turn from it: of the fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne.
019	PSA	132	012	If thy children will keep my covenant and my testimony that I shall teach them, their children also shall sit upon thy throne for evermore.
019	PSA	132	013	For the LORD hath chosen Zion; he hath desired it for his habitation.
019	PSA	132	014	This is my resting place for ever: here will I dwell; for I have desired it.
019	PSA	132	015	I will abundantly bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread.
019	PSA	132	016	Her priests also will I clothe with salvation: and her saints shall shout aloud for joy.
019	PSA	132	017	There will I make the horn of David to bud: I have ordained a lamp for mine anointed.
019	PSA	132	018	His enemies will I clothe with shame: but upon himself shall his crown flourish.
019	PSA	133	001	A Song of Ascents; of David. Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!
019	PSA	133	002	It is like the precious oil upon the head, that ran down upon the beard, even Aaron’s beard; that came down upon the skirt of his garments;
019	PSA	133	003	Like the dew of Hermon, that cometh down upon the mountains of Zion: for there the LORD commanded the blessing, even life for evermore.
019	PSA	134	001	A Song of Ascents. Behold, bless ye the LORD, all ye servants of the LORD, which by night stand in the house of the LORD.
019	PSA	134	002	Lift up your hands to the sanctuary, and bless ye the LORD.
019	PSA	134	003	The LORD bless thee out of Zion; even he that made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	135	001	Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the name of the LORD; praise [him], O ye servants of the LORD:
019	PSA	135	002	Ye that stand in the house of the LORD, in the courts of the house of our God.
019	PSA	135	003	Praise ye the LORD; for the LORD is good: sing praises unto his name; for it is pleasant.
019	PSA	135	004	For the LORD hath chosen Jacob unto himself, [and] Israel for his peculiar treasure.
019	PSA	135	005	For I know that the LORD is great, and that our Lord is above all gods.
019	PSA	135	006	Whatsoever the LORD pleased, that hath he done, in heaven and in earth, in the seas and in all deeps.
019	PSA	135	007	He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth forth the wind out of his treasuries.
019	PSA	135	008	Who smote the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast.
019	PSA	135	009	He sent signs and wonders into the midst of thee, O Egypt, upon Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.
019	PSA	135	010	Who smote many nations, and slew mighty kings;
019	PSA	135	011	Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan:
019	PSA	135	012	And gave their land for an heritage, an heritage unto Israel his people.
019	PSA	135	013	Thy name, O LORD, [endureth] for ever; thy memorial, O LORD, throughout all generations.
019	PSA	135	014	For the LORD shall judge his people, and repent himself concerning his servants.
019	PSA	135	015	The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.
019	PSA	135	016	They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;
019	PSA	135	017	They have ears, but they hear not; neither is there any breath in their mouths.
019	PSA	135	018	They that make them shall be like unto them; yea, every one that trusteth in them.
019	PSA	135	019	O house of Israel, bless ye the LORD: O house of Aaron, bless ye the LORD:
019	PSA	135	020	O house of Levi, bless ye the LORD: ye that fear the LORD, bless ye the LORD.
019	PSA	135	021	Blessed be the LORD out of Zion, who dwelleth at Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	136	001	O GIVE thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	002	O give thanks unto the God of gods: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	003	O give thanks unto the Lord of lords: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	004	To him who alone doeth great wonders: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	005	To him that by understanding made the heavens: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	006	To him that spread forth the earth above the waters: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	007	To him that made great lights: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	008	The sun to rule by day: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	009	The moon and stars to rule by night: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	010	To him that smote Egypt in their firstborn: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	011	And brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	012	With a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	013	To him which divided the Red Sea in sunder: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	014	And made Israel to pass through the midst of it: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	015	But overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red Sea: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	016	To him which led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	017	To him which smote great kings: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	018	And slew famous kings: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	019	Sihon king of the Amorites: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	020	And Og king of Bashan: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	021	And gave their land for an heritage: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	022	Even an heritage unto Israel his servant: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	023	Who remembered us in our low estate: for his mercy [endureth] for ever:
019	PSA	136	024	And hath delivered us from our adversaries: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	025	He giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	136	026	O give thanks unto the God of heaven: for his mercy [endureth] for ever.
019	PSA	137	001	By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion.
019	PSA	137	002	Upon the willows in the midst thereof we hanged up our harps.
019	PSA	137	003	For there they that led us captive required of us songs, and they that wasted us [required of us] mirth, [saying], Sing us one of the songs of Zion.
019	PSA	137	004	How shall we sing the LORD’S song in a strange land?
019	PSA	137	005	If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget [her cunning].
019	PSA	137	006	Let my tongue cleave to the roof of my mouth, if I remember thee not; if I prefer not Jerusalem above my chief joy.
019	PSA	137	007	Remember, O LORD, against the children of Edom the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase it, rase it, even to the foundation thereof.
019	PSA	137	008	O daughter of Babylon, that art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us.
019	PSA	137	009	Happy shall he be, that taketh and dasheth thy little ones against the rock.
019	PSA	138	001	[A Psalm] of David. I will give thee thanks with my whole heart: before the gods will I sing praises unto thee.
019	PSA	138	002	I will worship toward thy holy temple, and give thanks unto thy name for thy lovingkindness and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name.
019	PSA	138	003	In the day that I called thou answeredst me, thou didst encourage me with strength in my soul.
019	PSA	138	004	All the kings of the earth shall give thee thanks, O LORD, for they have heard the words of thy mouth.
019	PSA	138	005	Yea, they shall sing of the ways of the LORD; for great is the glory of the LORD.
019	PSA	138	006	For though the LORD be high, yet hath he respect unto the lowly: but the haughty he knoweth from afar.
019	PSA	138	007	Though I walk in the midst of trouble, thou wilt revive me; thou shalt stretch forth thine hand against the wrath of mine enemies, and thy right hand shall save me.
019	PSA	138	008	The LORD will perfect that which concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD, [endureth] for ever; forsake not the works of thine own hands.
019	PSA	139	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. LORD, thou hast searched me, and known [me].
019	PSA	139	002	Thou knowest my downsitting and mine uprising, thou understandest my thought afar off.
019	PSA	139	003	Thou searchest out my path and my lying down, and art acquainted with all my ways.
019	PSA	139	004	For there is not a word in my tongue, but, lo, O LORD, thou knowest it altogether.
019	PSA	139	005	Thou hast beset me behind and before, and laid thine hand upon me.
019	PSA	139	006	[Such] knowledge is too wonderful for me; it is high, I cannot attain unto it.
019	PSA	139	007	Whither shall I from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence?
019	PSA	139	008	If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in Sheol, behold, thou art there.
019	PSA	139	009	If I take the wings of the morning, and dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea;
019	PSA	139	010	Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me.
019	PSA	139	011	If I say, Surely the darkness shall overwhelm me, and the light about me shall be night;
019	PSA	139	012	Even the darkness hideth not from thee, but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light are both alike [to thee].
019	PSA	139	013	For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother’s womb.
019	PSA	139	014	I will give thanks unto thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: wonderful are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.
019	PSA	139	015	My frame was not hidden from thee, when I was made in secret, and curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth.
019	PSA	139	016	Thine eyes did see mine unperfect substance, and in thy book were all [my members] written, which day by day were fashioned, when as yet there was none of them.
019	PSA	139	017	How precious also are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of them!
019	PSA	139	018	If I should count them, they are more in number than the sand: when I awake, I am still with thee.
019	PSA	139	019	Surely thou wilt slay the wicked, O God: depart from me therefore, ye bloodthirsty men.
019	PSA	139	020	For they speak against thee wickedly, and thine enemies take [thy name] in vain.
019	PSA	139	021	Do not I hate them, O LORD, that hate thee? and am not I grieved with those that rise up against thee?
019	PSA	139	022	I hate them with perfect hatred: I count them mine enemies.
019	PSA	139	023	Search me, O God, and know my heart: try me and know my thoughts:
019	PSA	139	024	And see if there be any way of wickedness in me, and lead me in the way everlasting.
019	PSA	140	001	For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. Deliver me, O LORD, from the evil man; preserve me from the violent man:
019	PSA	140	002	Which imagine mischiefs in their heart; continually do they gather themselves together for war.
019	PSA	140	003	They have sharpened their tongue like a serpent; adders’ poison is under their lips. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	004	Keep me, O LORD, from the hands of the wicked; preserve me from the violent man: Who have purposed to thrust aside my steps.
019	PSA	140	005	The proud have hid a snare for me, and cords; they have spread a net by the way side; they have set gins for me. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	006	I said unto the LORD, Thou art my God: give ear unto the voice of my supplications, O LORD.
019	PSA	140	007	O GOD the Lord, the strength of my salvation, thou hast covered my head in the day of battle.
019	PSA	140	008	Grant not, O LORD, the desires of the wicked; further not his evil device; [lest] they exalt themselves. (Selah)
019	PSA	140	009	As for the head of those that compass me about, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.
019	PSA	140	010	Let burning coals fall upon them: let them be cast into the fire; into deep pits, that they rise not up again.
019	PSA	140	011	An evil speaker shall not be established in the earth: evil shall hunt the violent man to overthrow him.
019	PSA	140	012	I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted, and the right of the needy.
019	PSA	140	013	Surely the righteous shall give thanks unto thy name: the upright shall dwell in thy presence.
019	PSA	141	001	A Psalm of David. LORD, I have called upon thee; make haste unto me: give ear unto my voice, when I call unto thee.
019	PSA	141	002	Let my prayer be set forth as incense before thee; the lifting up of my hands as the evening sacrifice.
019	PSA	141	003	Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth; keep the door of my tips.
019	PSA	141	004	Incline not my heart to any evil thing, to be occupied in deeds of wickedness with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.
019	PSA	141	005	Let the righteous smite me, [it shall be] a kindness; and let him reprove me, [it shall be as] oil upon the head; let not my head refuse it: for even in their wickedness shall my prayer continue.
019	PSA	141	006	Their judges are thrown down by the sides of the rock; and they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.
019	PSA	141	007	As when one ploweth and cleaveth the earth, our bones are scattered at the grave’s mouth.
019	PSA	141	008	For mine eyes are unto thee, O GOD the Lord: in thee do I put my trust; leave not my soul destitute.
019	PSA	141	009	Keep me from the snare which they have laid for me, and from the gins of the workers of iniquity.
019	PSA	141	010	Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape.
019	PSA	142	001	Maschil of David, when he was in the cave; a Prayer. I cry with my voice unto the LORD; with my voice unto the LORD do I make supplication.
019	PSA	142	002	I pour out my complaint before him; I shew before him my trouble.
019	PSA	142	003	When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walk have they hidden a snare for me.
019	PSA	142	004	Look on [my] right hand, and see; for there is no man that knoweth me: refuge hath failed me; no man careth for my soul.
019	PSA	142	005	I cried unto thee, O LORD; I said, Thou art my refuge, my portion in the land of the living.
019	PSA	142	006	Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.
019	PSA	142	007	Bring my soul out of prison, that I may give thanks unto thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.
019	PSA	143	001	A Psalm of David. Hear my prayer, O LORD; give ear to my supplications: in thy faithfulness answer me, [and] in thy righteousness.
019	PSA	143	002	And enter not into judgment with thy servant; for in thy sight shall no man living be justified.
019	PSA	143	003	For the enemy hath persecuted my soul; he hath smitten my life down to the ground: he hath made me to dwell in dark places, as those that have been long dead.
019	PSA	143	004	Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed within me; my heart within me is desolate.
019	PSA	143	005	I remember the days of old; I meditate on all thy doings: I muse on the work of thy hands.
019	PSA	143	006	I spread forth my hands unto thee: my soul [thirsteth] after thee, as a weary land. (Selah)
019	PSA	143	007	Make haste to answer me, O LORD; my spirit faileth: hide not thy face from me; lest I become like them that go down into the pit.
019	PSA	143	008	Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.
019	PSA	143	009	Deliver me, O LORD, from mine enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me.
019	PSA	143	010	Teach me to do thy will; for thou art my God: thy spirit is good; lead me in the land of uprightness.
019	PSA	143	011	Quicken me, O LORD, for thy name’s sake: in thy righteousness bring my soul out of trouble.
019	PSA	143	012	And in thy lovingkindness cut off mine enemies, and destroy all them that afflict my soul; for I am thy servant.
019	PSA	144	001	[A Psalm off] David. Blessed be the LORD my rock, which teacheth my hands to war, [and] my fingers to fight:
019	PSA	144	002	My lovingkindness, and my fortress, my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and he in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me.
019	PSA	144	003	LORD, what is man, that thou takest knowledge of him? or the son of man, that thou makest account of him?
019	PSA	144	004	Man is like to vanity: his days are as a shadow that passeth away.
019	PSA	144	005	Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.
019	PSA	144	006	Cast forth lightning, and scatter them; send out thine arrows, and discomfit them.
019	PSA	144	007	Stretch forth thine hand from above; rescue me, and deliver me out of great waters, out of the hand of strangers;
019	PSA	144	008	Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood.
019	PSA	144	009	I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.
019	PSA	144	010	It is he that giveth salvation unto kings: who rescueth David his servant from the hurtful sword.
019	PSA	144	011	Rescue me, and deliver me out of the hand of strangers, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood.
019	PSA	144	012	When our sons shall be as plants grown up in their youth; and our daughters as corner stones hewn after the fashion of a palace;
019	PSA	144	013	[When] our garners are full, affording all manner of store; [and] our sheep bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our fields;
019	PSA	144	014	[When] our oxen are well laden; [when there is] no breaking in, and no going forth, and no outcry in our streets;
019	PSA	144	015	Happy is the people, that is in such a case: [yea], happy is the people, whose God is the LORD.
019	PSA	145	001	[A Psalm of] praise; of David. I will extol thee, my God, O King; and I will bless thy name for ever and ever.
019	PSA	145	002	Every day will I bless thee; and I will praise thy name for ever and ever.
019	PSA	145	003	Great is the LORD, and highly to be praised; and his greatness is unsearchable.
019	PSA	145	004	One generation shall laud thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.
019	PSA	145	005	Of the glorious majesty of thine honour, and of thy wondrous works, will I meditate.
019	PSA	145	006	And men shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts; and I will declare thy greatness.
019	PSA	145	007	They shall utter the memory of thy great goodness, and shall sing of thy righteousness.
019	PSA	145	008	The LORD is gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy.
019	PSA	145	009	The LORD is good to all; and his tender mercies are over all his works.
019	PSA	145	010	All thy works shall give thanks unto thee, O LORD; and thy saints shall bless thee.
019	PSA	145	011	They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;
019	PSA	145	012	To make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, and the glory of the majesty of his kingdom.
019	PSA	145	013	Thy kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and thy dominion [endureth] throughout all generations.
019	PSA	145	014	The LORD upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all those that be bowed down.
019	PSA	145	015	The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season.
019	PSA	145	016	Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.
019	PSA	145	017	The LORD is righteous in all his ways, and gracious in all his works.
019	PSA	145	018	The LORD is nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.
019	PSA	145	019	He will fulfill the desire of them that fear him; he also will hear their cry, and will save them.
019	PSA	145	020	The LORD preserveth all them that love him; but all the wicked will he destroy.
019	PSA	145	021	My mouth shall speak the praise of the LORD; and let all flesh bless his holy name for ever and ever.
019	PSA	146	001	Praise ye the LORD. Praise the LORD, O my soul.
019	PSA	146	002	While I live will I praise the LORD: I will sing praises unto my God while I have any being.
019	PSA	146	003	Put not your trust in princes, nor in the son of man, in whom there is no help.
019	PSA	146	004	His breath goeth forth, he returneth to his earth; in that very day his thoughts perish.
019	PSA	146	005	Happy is he that hath the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope is in the LORD his God:
019	PSA	146	006	Which made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is; which keepeth truth for ever:
019	PSA	146	007	Which executeth judgment for the oppressed; which giveth food to the hungry: the LORD looseth the prisoners;
019	PSA	146	008	The LORD openeth [the eyes of] the blind; the LORD raiseth up them that are bowed down; the LORD loveth the righteous;
019	PSA	146	009	The LORD preserveth the strangers; he upholdeth the fatherless and widow; but the way of the wicked he turneth upside down.
019	PSA	146	010	The LORD shall reign for ever, thy God, O Zion, unto all generations. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	147	001	Praise ye the LORD; for it is good to sing praises unto our God; for it is pleasant, [and] praise is comely.
019	PSA	147	002	The LORD doth build up Jerusalem; he gathereth together the outcasts of Israel.
019	PSA	147	003	He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.
019	PSA	147	004	He telleth the number of the stars; he giveth them all their names.
019	PSA	147	005	Great is our Lord, and mighty in power; his understanding is infinite.
019	PSA	147	006	The LORD upholdeth the meek: he bringeth the wicked down to the ground.
019	PSA	147	007	Sing unto the LORD with thanksgiving; sing praises upon the harp unto our God:
019	PSA	147	008	Who covereth the heaven with clouds, who prepareth rain for the earth, who maketh grass to grow upon the mountains.
019	PSA	147	009	He giveth to the beast his food, and to the young ravens which cry.
019	PSA	147	010	He delighteth not in the strength of the horse: he taketh no pleasure in the legs of a man.
019	PSA	147	011	The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy.
019	PSA	147	012	Praise the LORD, O Jerusalem; praise thy God, O Zion.
019	PSA	147	013	For he hath strengthened the bars of thy gates; he hath blessed thy children within thee.
019	PSA	147	014	He maketh peace in thy borders; he filleth thee with the finest of the wheat.
019	PSA	147	015	He sendeth out his commandment upon earth; his word runneth very swiftly.
019	PSA	147	016	He giveth snow like wool; he scattereth the hoar frost like ashes.
019	PSA	147	017	He casteth forth his ice like morsels: who can stand before his cold?
019	PSA	147	018	He sendeth out his word, and melteth them: he causeth his wind to blow, and the waters flow.
019	PSA	147	019	He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his statutes and his judgments unto Israel.
019	PSA	147	020	He hath not dealt so with any nation: and as for his judgments, they have not known them. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	148	001	Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the LORD from the heavens: praise him in the heights.
019	PSA	148	002	Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his host.
019	PSA	148	003	Praise ye him, sun and moon; praise him, all ye stars of light.
019	PSA	148	004	Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that be above the heavens.
019	PSA	148	005	Let them praise the name of the LORD: for he commanded, and they were created.
019	PSA	148	006	He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass away.
019	PSA	148	007	Praise the LORD from the earth, ye dragons, and all deeps:
019	PSA	148	008	Fire and hail, snow and vapour; stormy wind, fulfilling his word:
019	PSA	148	009	Mountains and all hills; fruitful trees and all cedars:
019	PSA	148	010	Beasts and all cattle; creeping things and flying fowl:
019	PSA	148	011	Kings of the earth and all peoples; princes and all judges of the earth:
019	PSA	148	012	Both young men and maidens; old men and children:
019	PSA	148	013	Let them praise the name of the LORD; for his name alone is exalted: his glory is above the earth and heaven.
019	PSA	148	014	And he hath lifted up the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints; even of the children of Israel, a people near unto him. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	149	001	Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the LORD a new song, and his praise in the assembly of the saints.
019	PSA	149	002	Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.
019	PSA	149	003	Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp.
019	PSA	149	004	For the LORD taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.
019	PSA	149	005	Let the saints exult in glory: let them sing for joy upon their beds.
019	PSA	149	006	[Let] the high praises of God [be] in their mouth, and a two-edged sword in their hand;
019	PSA	149	007	To execute vengeance upon the nations, and punishments upon the peoples;
019	PSA	149	008	To bind their king’s with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;
019	PSA	149	009	To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the LORD.
019	PSA	150	001	Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power.
019	PSA	150	002	Praise him for his mighty acts: praise him according to his excellent greatness.
019	PSA	150	003	Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp.
019	PSA	150	004	Praise him with the timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and the pipe.
019	PSA	150	005	Praise him upon the loud cymbals: praise him upon the high sounding cymbals.
019	PSA	150	006	Let every thing that hath breath praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.
#
# BOOK	020	PRO	Proverbs	Proverbs
020	PRO	001	001	The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel:
020	PRO	001	002	To know wisdom and instruction; to discern the words of understanding;
020	PRO	001	003	To receive instruction in wise dealing, in righteousness and judgment and equity;
020	PRO	001	004	To give subtilty to the simple, to the young man knowledge and discretion:
020	PRO	001	005	That the wise man may hear, and increase in learning; and that the man of understanding may attain unto sound counsels:
020	PRO	001	006	To understand a proverb, and a figure; the words of the wise, and their dark sayings.
020	PRO	001	007	The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: [but] the foolish despise wisdom and instruction.
020	PRO	001	008	My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:
020	PRO	001	009	For they shall be a chaplet of grace unto thy head, and chains about thy neck.
020	PRO	001	010	My son, if sinners entice thee, consent thou not.
020	PRO	001	011	If they say, Come with us, let us lay wait for blood, let us lurk privily for the innocent without cause;
020	PRO	001	012	Let us swallow them up alive as Sheol, and whole, as those that go down into the pit;
020	PRO	001	013	We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoil;
020	PRO	001	014	Thou shalt cast thy lot among us; we will all have one purse:
020	PRO	001	015	My son, walk not thou in the way with them; refrain thy foot from their path:
020	PRO	001	016	For their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed blood.
020	PRO	001	017	For in vain is the net spread, in the eyes of any bird:
020	PRO	001	018	And these lay wait for their own blood, they lurk privily for their own lives.
020	PRO	001	019	So are the ways of every one that is greedy of gain; it taketh away the life of the owners thereof.
020	PRO	001	020	Wisdom crieth aloud in the street; she uttereth her voice in the broad places;
020	PRO	001	021	She crieth in the chief place of concourse; at the entering in of the gates, in the city, she uttereth her words:
020	PRO	001	022	How long, ye simple ones, will ye love simplicity? and scorners delight them in scorning, and fools hate knowledge?
020	PRO	001	023	Turn you at my reproof: behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you, I will make known my words unto you.
020	PRO	001	024	Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;
020	PRO	001	025	But ye have set at nought all my counsel, and would none of my reproof:
020	PRO	001	026	I also will laugh in [the day of] your calamity; I will mock when your fear cometh;
020	PRO	001	027	When your fear cometh as a storm, and your calamity cometh on as a whirlwind; when distress and anguish come upon you.
020	PRO	001	028	Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me diligently, but they shall not find me:
020	PRO	001	029	For that they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of the LORD:
020	PRO	001	030	They would none of my counsel; they despised all my reproof:
020	PRO	001	031	Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.
020	PRO	001	032	For the backsliding of the simple shall slay them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.
020	PRO	001	033	But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell securely, and shall be quiet without fear of evil.
020	PRO	002	001	My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and lay up my commandments with thee;
020	PRO	002	002	So that thou incline thine ear unto wisdom, and apply thine heart to understanding;
020	PRO	002	003	Yea, if thou cry after discernment, and lift up thy voice for understanding;
020	PRO	002	004	If thou seek her as silver, and search for her as for hid treasures;
020	PRO	002	005	Then shalt thou understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.
020	PRO	002	006	For the LORD giveth wisdom; out of his mouth [cometh] knowledge and understanding:
020	PRO	002	007	He layeth up sound wisdom for the upright, [he is] a shield to them that walk in integrity;
020	PRO	002	008	That he may guard the paths of judgment, and preserve the way of his saints.
020	PRO	002	009	Then shalt thou understand righteousness and judgment, and equity, [yea], every good path.
020	PRO	002	010	For wisdom shall enter into thine heart, and knowledge shall be pleasant unto thy soul;
020	PRO	002	011	Discretion shall watch over thee, understanding shall keep thee:
020	PRO	002	012	To deliver thee from the way of evil, from the men that speak froward things;
020	PRO	002	013	Who forsake the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness;
020	PRO	002	014	Who rejoice to do evil, and delight in the frowardness of evil;
020	PRO	002	015	Who are crooked in their ways, and perverse in their paths:
020	PRO	002	016	To deliver thee from the strange woman, even from the stranger which flattereth with her words;
020	PRO	002	017	Which forsaketh the friend of her youth, and forgetteth the covenant of her God:
020	PRO	002	018	For her house inclineth unto death, and her paths unto the dead:
020	PRO	002	019	None that go unto her return again, neither do they attain unto the paths of life:
020	PRO	002	020	That thou mayest walk in the way of good men, and keep the paths of the righteous.
020	PRO	002	021	For the upright shall dwell in the land, and the perfect shall remain in it.
020	PRO	002	022	But the wicked shall be cut off from the land, and they that deal treacherously shall be rooted out of it.
020	PRO	003	001	My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:
020	PRO	003	002	For length of days, and years of life, and peace, shall they add to thee.
020	PRO	003	003	Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:
020	PRO	003	004	So shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man.
020	PRO	003	005	Trust in the LORD with all thine heart, and lean not upon thine own understanding:
020	PRO	003	006	In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.
020	PRO	003	007	Be not wise in thine own eyes; fear the LORD, and depart from evil:
020	PRO	003	008	It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones.
020	PRO	003	009	Honour the LORD with thy substance, and with the firstfruits of all thine increase:
020	PRO	003	010	So shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy vats shall overflow with new wine.
020	PRO	003	011	My son, despise not the chastening of the LORD; neither be weary of his reproof:
020	PRO	003	012	For whom the LORD loveth he reproveth; even as a father the son in whom he delighteth.
020	PRO	003	013	Happy is the man that findeth wisdom, and the man that getteth understanding.
020	PRO	003	014	For the merchandise of it is better than the merchandise of silver, and the gain thereof than fine gold.
020	PRO	003	015	She is more precious than rubies: and none of the things thou canst desire are to be compared unto her.
020	PRO	003	016	Length of days is in her right had; in her left hand are riches and honour.
020	PRO	003	017	Her ways are ways of pleasantness, and all her paths are peace.
020	PRO	003	018	She is a tree of life to them that lay hold upon her: and happy is every one that retaineth her.
020	PRO	003	019	The LORD by wisdom founded the earth; by understanding he established the heavens.
020	PRO	003	020	By his knowledge the depths were broken up, and the skies drop down the dew.
020	PRO	003	021	My son, let not them depart from thine eyes; keep sound wisdom and discretion;
020	PRO	003	022	So shall they be life unto thy soul, and grace to thy neck.
020	PRO	003	023	Then shalt thou walk in thy way securely, and thy foot shall not stumble.
020	PRO	003	024	When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.
020	PRO	003	025	Be not afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh:
020	PRO	003	026	For the LORD shall be thy confidence, and shall keep thy foot from being taken.
020	PRO	003	027	Withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do it.
020	PRO	003	028	Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again, and tomorrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.
020	PRO	003	029	Devise not evil against thy neighbour, seeing he dwelleth securely by thee.
020	PRO	003	030	Strive not with a man without cause, if he have done thee no harm.
020	PRO	003	031	Envy thou not the man of violence, and choose none of his ways.
020	PRO	003	032	For the perverse is an abomination to the LORD: but his secret is with the upright.
020	PRO	003	033	The curse of the LORD is in the house of the wicked; but he blesseth the habitation of the righteous.
020	PRO	003	034	Surely he scorneth the scorners, but he giveth grace unto the lowly.
020	PRO	003	035	The wise shall inherit glory; but shame shall be the promotion of fools.
020	PRO	004	001	Hear, [my] sons, the instruction of a father, and attend to know understanding:
020	PRO	004	002	For I give you good doctrine; forsake ye not my law.
020	PRO	004	003	For I was a son unto my father, tender and only beloved in the sight of my mother.
020	PRO	004	004	And he taught me, and said unto me, Let thine heart retain my words; keep my commandments, and live:
020	PRO	004	005	Get wisdom, get understanding; forget [it] not, neither decline from the words of my mouth:
020	PRO	004	006	Forsake her not, and she shall preserve thee; love her, and she shall keep thee.
020	PRO	004	007	Wisdom [is] the principal thing; [therefore] get wisdom: yea, with all thou hast gotten get understanding.
020	PRO	004	008	Exalt her, and she shall promote thee: she shall bring thee to honour, when thou dost embrace her.
020	PRO	004	009	She shall give to thine head a chaplet of grace: a crown of beauty shall she deliver to thee.
020	PRO	004	010	Hear, O my son, and receive my sayings; and the years of thy life shall be many.
020	PRO	004	011	I have taught thee in the way of wisdom; I have led thee in paths of uprightness.
020	PRO	004	012	When thou goest, thy steps shall not be straitened; and if thou runnest, thou shalt not stumble.
020	PRO	004	013	Take fast hold of instruction; let her not go: keep her; for she is thy life.
020	PRO	004	014	Enter not into the path of the wicked, and walk not in the way of evil men.
020	PRO	004	015	Avoid it, pass not by it; turn from it, and pass on.
020	PRO	004	016	For they sleep not, except they have done mischief; and their sleep is taken away, unless they cause some to fall.
020	PRO	004	017	For they eat the bread of wickedness, and drink the wine of violence.
020	PRO	004	018	But the path of the righteous is as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day.
020	PRO	004	019	The way of the wicked is as darkness: they know not at what they stumble.
020	PRO	004	020	My son, attend to my words; incline thine ear unto my sayings.
020	PRO	004	021	Let them not depart from thine eyes; keep them in the midst of thine heart.
020	PRO	004	022	For they are life unto those that find them, and health to all their flesh.
020	PRO	004	023	Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.
020	PRO	004	024	Put away from thee a froward mouth, and perverse lips put far from thee.
020	PRO	004	025	Let thine eyes look right on, and let thine eyelids look straight before thee.
020	PRO	004	026	Make level the path of thy feet, and let all thy ways be established.
020	PRO	004	027	Turn not to the right hand nor to the left: remove thy foot from evil.
020	PRO	005	001	My son, attend unto my wisdom; incline thine ear to my understanding:
020	PRO	005	002	That thou mayest preserve discretion, and that thy lips may keep knowledge.
020	PRO	005	003	For the lips of a strange woman drop honey, and her mouth is smoother than oil:
020	PRO	005	004	But her latter end is bitter as wormwood, sharp as a two-edged sword.
020	PRO	005	005	Her feet go down to death; her steps take hold on Sheol;
020	PRO	005	006	So that she findeth not the level path of life: her ways are unstable [and] she knoweth [it] not.
020	PRO	005	007	Now therefore, [my] sons, hearken unto me, and depart not from the words of my mouth.
020	PRO	005	008	Remove thy way far from her, and come not nigh the door of her house:
020	PRO	005	009	Lest thou give thine honour unto others, and thy years unto the cruel:
020	PRO	005	010	Lest strangers be filled with thy strength; and thy labours [be] in the house of an alien;
020	PRO	005	011	And thou mourn at thy latter end, when thy flesh and thy body are consumed,
020	PRO	005	012	And say, How have I hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof;
020	PRO	005	013	Neither have I obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor inclined mine ear to them that instructed me!
020	PRO	005	014	I was well nigh in all evil in the midst of the congregation and assembly.
020	PRO	005	015	Drink waters out of thine own cistern, and running waters out of thine own well.
020	PRO	005	016	Should thy springs be dispersed abroad, and rivers of water in the streets?
020	PRO	005	017	Let them be for thyself alone, and not for strangers with thee.
020	PRO	005	018	Let thy fountain be blessed; and rejoice in the wife of thy youth.
020	PRO	005	019	[As] a loving hind and a pleasant doe, let her breasts satisfy thee at all times; and be thou ravished always with her love.
020	PRO	005	020	For why shouldest thou, my son, be ravished with a strange woman, and embrace the bosom of a stranger?
020	PRO	005	021	For the ways of man are before the eyes of the LORD, and he maketh level all his paths.
020	PRO	005	022	His own iniquities shall take the wicked, and he shall be holden with the cords of his sin.
020	PRO	005	023	He shall die for lack of instruction; and in the greatness of his folly he shall go astray.
020	PRO	006	001	My son, if thou art become surety for thy neighbour, if thou hast stricken thy hands for a stranger,
020	PRO	006	002	Thou art snared with the words of thy mouth, thou art taken with the words of thy mouth.
020	PRO	006	003	Do this now, my son, and deliver thyself, seeing thou art come into the hand of thy neighbour; go, humble thyself, and importune thy neighbour.
020	PRO	006	004	Give not sleep to thine eyes, nor slumber to thine eyelids.
020	PRO	006	005	Deliver thyself as a roe from the hand [of the hunter], and as a bird from the hand of the fowler.
020	PRO	006	006	Go to the ant, thou sluggard; consider her ways, and be wise:
020	PRO	006	007	Which having no chief, overseer, or ruler,
020	PRO	006	008	Provideth her meat in the summer, and gathereth her food in the harvest.
020	PRO	006	009	How long wilt thou sleep, O sluggard? when wilt thou arise out of thy sleep?
020	PRO	006	010	[Yet] a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:
020	PRO	006	011	So shall thy poverty come as a robber, and thy want as an armed man.
020	PRO	006	012	A worthless person, a man of iniquity; he walketh with a froward mouth;
020	PRO	006	013	He winketh with his eyes, he speaketh with his feet, he maketh signs with his fingers;
020	PRO	006	014	Frowardness is in his heart, he deviseth evil continually; he soweth discord.
020	PRO	006	015	Therefore shall his calamity come suddenly; on a sudden shall he be broken and that without remedy.
020	PRO	006	016	There be six things which the LORD hateth; yea, seven which are an abomination unto him:
020	PRO	006	017	Haughty eyes, a lying tongue, and hands that shed innocent blood;
020	PRO	006	018	An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations, feet that be swift in running to mischief;
020	PRO	006	019	A false witness that uttereth lies, and he that soweth discord among brethren.
020	PRO	006	020	My son, keep the commandment of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:
020	PRO	006	021	Bind them continually upon thine heart, tie them about thy neck.
020	PRO	006	022	When thou walkest, it shall lead thee; when thou sleepest, it shall watch over thee; and when thou awakest, it shall talk with thee.
020	PRO	006	023	For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life:
020	PRO	006	024	To keep thee from the evil woman, from the flattery of the stranger’s tongue.
020	PRO	006	025	Lust not after her beauty in thine heart; neither let her take thee with her eyelids.
020	PRO	006	026	For on account of a whorish woman [a man is brought] to a piece of bread: and the adulteress hunteth for the precious life.
020	PRO	006	027	Can a man take fire in his bosom, and his clothes not be burned?
020	PRO	006	028	Or can one walk upon hot coals, and his feet not be scorched?
020	PRO	006	029	So he that goeth in to his nieghbour’s wife; whosoever toucheth her shall not be unpunished.
020	PRO	006	030	Men do not despise a thief, if he steal to satisfy his soul when he is hungry:
020	PRO	006	031	But if he be found, he shall restore sevenfold; he shall give all the substance of his house.
020	PRO	006	032	He that committeth adultery with a woman is void of understanding: he doeth it that would destroy his own soul.
020	PRO	006	033	Wounds and dishonour shall he get; and his reproach shall not be wiped away.
020	PRO	006	034	For jealousy is the rage of a man; and he will not spare in the day of vengeance.
020	PRO	006	035	He will not regard any ransom; neither will he rest content, though thou givest many gifts.
020	PRO	007	001	My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.
020	PRO	007	002	Keep my commandments and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.
020	PRO	007	003	Bind them upon thy fingers; write them upon the table of thine heart.
020	PRO	007	004	Say unto wisdom, Thou art my sister; and call understanding [thy] kinswoman:
020	PRO	007	005	That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger which flattereth with her words.
020	PRO	007	006	For at the window of my house I looked forth through my lattice;
020	PRO	007	007	And I beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,
020	PRO	007	008	Passing through the street near her corner, and he went the way to her house;
020	PRO	007	009	In the twilight, in the evening of the day, in the blackness of night and the darkness.
020	PRO	007	010	And, behold, there met him a woman with the attire of an harlot, and wily of heart.
020	PRO	007	011	She is clamorous, and wilful; her feet abide not in her house:
020	PRO	007	012	Now she is in the streets, now in the broad places, and lieth in wait at every corner.
020	PRO	007	013	So she caught him, and kissed him, [and] with an impudent face she said unto him:
020	PRO	007	014	Sacrifices of peace offerings are with me; this day have I paid my vows.
020	PRO	007	015	Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.
020	PRO	007	016	I have spread my couch with carpets of tapestry, with striped cloths of the yarn of Egypt.
020	PRO	007	017	I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
020	PRO	007	018	Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning; let us solace ourselves with loves.
020	PRO	007	019	For the goodman is not at home, he is gone a long journey:
020	PRO	007	020	He hath taken a bag of money with him; he will come home at the full moon.
020	PRO	007	021	With her much fair speech she causeth him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forceth him away.
020	PRO	007	022	He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as fetters to the correction of the fool;
020	PRO	007	023	Till an arrow strike through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it is for his life.
020	PRO	007	024	Now therefore, [my] sons, hearken unto me, and attend to the words of my mouth.
020	PRO	007	025	Let not thine heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.
020	PRO	007	026	For she hath cast down many wounded: yea, all her slain are a mighty host.
020	PRO	007	027	Her house is the way to Sheol, going down to the chambers of death.
020	PRO	008	001	Doth not wisdom cry, and understanding put forth her voice?
020	PRO	008	002	In the top of high places by the way, where the paths meet, she standeth;
020	PRO	008	003	Beside the gates, at the entry of the city, at the coming in at the doors, she crieth aloud:
020	PRO	008	004	Unto you, O men, I call; and my voice is to the sons of men.
020	PRO	008	005	O ye simple, understand subtilty; and, ye fools, be ye of an understanding heart.
020	PRO	008	006	Hear, for I will speak excellent things; and the opening of my lips shall be right things.
020	PRO	008	007	For my mouth shall utter truth; and wickedness is an abomination to my lips.
020	PRO	008	008	All the words of my mouth are in righteousness; there is nothing crooked or perverse in them.
020	PRO	008	009	They are all plain to him that understandeth, and right to them that find knowledge.
020	PRO	008	010	Receive my instruction, and not silver; and knowledge rather than choice gold.
020	PRO	008	011	For wisdom is better than rubies; and all the things that may be desired are not to be compared unto her.
020	PRO	008	012	I wisdom have made subtilty my dwelling, and find out knowledge [and] discretion.
020	PRO	008	013	The fear of the LORD is to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate.
020	PRO	008	014	Counsel is mine, and sound knowledge: I am understanding; I have might.
020	PRO	008	015	By me kings reign, and princes decree justice.
020	PRO	008	016	By me princes rule, and nobles, [even] all the judges of the earth.
020	PRO	008	017	I love them that love me; and those that seek me diligently shall find me.
020	PRO	008	018	Riches and honour are with me; [yea], durable riches and righteousness.
020	PRO	008	019	My fruit is better than gold, yea, than fine gold; and my revenue than choice silver.
020	PRO	008	020	I walk in the way of righteousness, in the midst of the paths of judgment:
020	PRO	008	021	That I may cause those that love me to inherit substance, and that I may fill their treasuries.
020	PRO	008	022	The LORD possessed me in the beginning of his way, before his works of old.
020	PRO	008	023	I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning, or ever the earth was.
020	PRO	008	024	When there were no depths, I was brought forth; when there were no fountains abounding with water.
020	PRO	008	025	Before the mountains were settled, before the hills was I brought forth:
020	PRO	008	026	While as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields, nor the beginning of the dust of the world.
020	PRO	008	027	When he established the heavens, I was there: when he set a circle upon the face of the deep:
020	PRO	008	028	When he made firm the sides above: when the fountains of the deep became strong:
020	PRO	008	029	When he gave to the sea its bound, that the waters should not transgress his commandment: when he marked out the foundations of the earth:
020	PRO	008	030	Then I was by him, [as] a master workman: and I was daily [his] delight, rejoicing always before him;
020	PRO	008	031	Rejoicing in his habitable earth; and my delight was with the sons of men.
020	PRO	008	032	Now therefore, [my] sons, hearken unto me: for blessed are they that keep my ways.
020	PRO	008	033	Hear instruction, and be wise, and refuse it not.
020	PRO	008	034	Blessed is the man that heareth me, watching daily at my gates, waiting at the posts of my doors.
020	PRO	008	035	For whoso findeth me findeth life, and shall obtain favour of the LORD.
020	PRO	008	036	But he that sinneth against me wrongeth his own soul: all they that hate me love death.
020	PRO	009	001	Wisdom hath builded her house, she hath hewn out her seven pillars:
020	PRO	009	002	She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine; she hath also furnished her table.
020	PRO	009	003	She hath sent forth her maidens, she crieth upon the highest places of the city,
020	PRO	009	004	Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: as for him that is void of understanding, she saith to him,
020	PRO	009	005	Come, eat ye of my bread, and drink of the wine which I have mingled.
020	PRO	009	006	Leave off, ye simple ones, and live; and walk in the way of understanding.
020	PRO	009	007	He that correcteth a scorner getteth to himself shame: and he that reproveth a wicked man [getteth] himself a blot.
020	PRO	009	008	Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate thee: reprove a wise man, and he will love thee.
020	PRO	009	009	Give [instruction] to a wise man, and he will be yet wiser: teach a righteous man, and he will increase in learning.
020	PRO	009	010	The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the Holy One is understanding.
020	PRO	009	011	For by me thy days shall be multiplied, and the years of thy life shall be increased.
020	PRO	009	012	If thou art wise, thou art wise for thyself: and if thou scornest, thou alone shalt bear it.
020	PRO	009	013	The foolish woman is clamorous; [she is] simple, and knoweth nothing.
020	PRO	009	014	And she sitteth at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city,
020	PRO	009	015	To call to them that pass by, who go right on their ways,
020	PRO	009	016	Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: and as for him that is void of understanding, she saith to him,
020	PRO	009	017	Stolen waters are sweet, and bread [eaten] in secret is pleasant.
020	PRO	009	018	But he knoweth not that the dead are there; that her guests are in the depths of Sheol.
020	PRO	010	001	The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish son is the heaviness of his mother.
020	PRO	010	002	Treasures of wickedness profit nothing: but righteousness delivereth from death.
020	PRO	010	003	The LORD will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish: but he thrusteth away the desire of the wicked.
020	PRO	010	004	He becometh poor that dealeth with a slack hand: but the hand of the diligent maketh rich.
020	PRO	010	005	He that gathereth in summer is a wise son: [but] he that sleepeth in harvest is a son that causeth shame.
020	PRO	010	006	Blessings are upon the head of the righteous: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.
020	PRO	010	007	The memory of the just is blessed: but the name of the wicked shall rot.
020	PRO	010	008	The wise in heart will receive commandments: but a prating fool shall fall.
020	PRO	010	009	He that walketh uprightly walketh surely: but he that perverteth his ways shall be known.
020	PRO	010	010	He that winketh with the eye causeth sorrow: but a prating fool shall fall.
020	PRO	010	011	The mouth of the righteous is a fountain of life: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.
020	PRO	010	012	Hatred stirreth up strifes: but love covereth all transgressions.
020	PRO	010	013	In the lips of him that hath discernment wisdom is found: but a rod is for the back of him that is void of understanding.
020	PRO	010	014	Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish is a present destruction.
020	PRO	010	015	The rich man’s wealth is his strong city: the destruction of the poor is their poverty.
020	PRO	010	016	The labour of the righteous [tendeth] to life; the increase of the wicked to sin.
020	PRO	010	017	He is in the way of life that heedeth correction: but he that forsaketh reproof erreth.
020	PRO	010	018	He that hideth hatred is of lying lips; and he that uttereth a slander is a fool.
020	PRO	010	019	In the multitude of words there wanteth not transgression: but he that refraineth his lips doeth wisely.
020	PRO	010	020	The tongue of the righteous is as choice silver: the heart of the wicked is little worth.
020	PRO	010	021	The lips of the righteous feed many: but the foolish die for lack of understanding.
020	PRO	010	022	The blessing of the LORD, it maketh rich, and he addeth no sorrow therewith.
020	PRO	010	023	It is as sport to a fool to do wickedness: and [so is] wisdom to a man of understanding.
020	PRO	010	024	The fear of the wicked, it shall come upon him: and the desire of the righteous shall be granted.
020	PRO	010	025	When the whirlwind passeth, the wicked is no more: but the righteous is an everlasting foundation.
020	PRO	010	026	As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard to them that send him.
020	PRO	010	027	The fear of the LORD prolongeth days: but the years of the wicked shall be shortened.
020	PRO	010	028	The hope of the righteous [shall] be gladness: but the expectation of the wicked shall perish.
020	PRO	010	029	The way of the LORD is a strong hold to the upright; but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.
020	PRO	010	030	The righteous shall never be removed: but the wicked shall not dwell in the land.
020	PRO	010	031	The mouth of the righteous bringeth forth wisdom: but the froward tongue shall be cut off.
020	PRO	010	032	The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable: but the mouth of the wicked [speaketh] frowardness.
020	PRO	011	001	A FALSE balance is an abomination to the LORD: but a just weight is his delight.
020	PRO	011	002	When pride cometh, then cometh shame: but with the lowly is wisdom.
020	PRO	011	003	The integrity of the upright shall guide them: but the perverseness of the treacherous shall destroy them.
020	PRO	011	004	Riches profit not in the day of wrath: but righteousness delivereth from death.
020	PRO	011	005	The righteousness of the perfect shall direct his way: but the wicked shall fall by his own wickedness.
020	PRO	011	006	The righteousness of the upright shall deliver them: but they that deal treacherously shall be taken in their own mischief.
020	PRO	011	007	When a wicked man dieth [his] expectation shall perish: and the hope of iniquity perisheth.
020	PRO	011	008	The righteous is delivered out of trouble, and the wicked cometh in his stead.
020	PRO	011	009	With his mouth the godless man destroyeth his neighbour: but through knowledge shall the righteous be delivered.
020	PRO	011	010	When it goeth well with the righteous, the city rejoiceth: and when the wicked perish, there is shouting.
020	PRO	011	011	By the blessing of the upright the city is exalted: but it is overthrown by the mouth of the wicked.
020	PRO	011	012	He that despiseth his neighbour is void of wisdom: but a man of understanding holdeth his peace.
020	PRO	011	013	He that goeth about as a talebearer revealeth secrets: but he that is of a faithful spirit concealeth the matter.
020	PRO	011	014	Where no wise guidance is, the people falleth: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.
020	PRO	011	015	He that is surety for a stranger shall smart for it: but he that hateth suretiship is sure.
020	PRO	011	016	A gracious woman retaineth honour: and violent men retain riches.
020	PRO	011	017	The merciful man doeth good to his own soul: but he that is cruel troubleth his own flesh.
020	PRO	011	018	The wicked earneth deceitful wages: but he that soweth righteousness [hath] a sure reward.
020	PRO	011	019	He that is stedfast in righteousness [shall attain] unto life: and he that pursueth evil [doeth it] to his own death.
020	PRO	011	020	They that are perverse in heart are an abomination to the LORD: but such as are perfect in [their] way are his delight.
020	PRO	011	021	[Though] hand [join] in hand, the evil man shall not be unpunished: but the seed of the righteous shall be delivered.
020	PRO	011	022	[As a] jewel of gold in a swine’s snout, [so is] a fair woman which is without discretion.
020	PRO	011	023	The desire of the righteous is only good: [but] the expectation of the wicked is wrath.
020	PRO	011	024	There is that scattereth, and increaseth yet more; and there is that withholdeth more than is meet, but [it tendeth] only to want.
020	PRO	011	025	The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.
020	PRO	011	026	He that withholdeth corn, the people shall curse him: but blessing shall be upon the head of him that selleth it.
020	PRO	011	027	He that diligently seeketh good seeketh favour: but he that searcheth after mischief, it shall come unto him.
020	PRO	011	028	He that trusteth in his riches shall fall: but the righteous shall flourish as the green leaf.
020	PRO	011	029	He that troubleth his own house shall inherit the wind: and the foolish shall be servant to the wise of heart.
020	PRO	011	030	The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life; and he that is wise winneth souls.
020	PRO	011	031	Behold, the righteous shall be recompensed in the earth: how much more the wicked and the sinner!
020	PRO	012	001	Whoso loveth correction loveth knowledge: but he that hateth reproof is brutish.
020	PRO	012	002	A good man shall obtain favour of the LORD: but a man of wicked devices will he condemn.
020	PRO	012	003	A man shall not be established by wickedness: but the root of the righteous shall never be moved.
020	PRO	012	004	A virtuous woman is a crown to her husband: but she that maketh ashamed is as rottenness in his bones.
020	PRO	012	005	The thoughts of the righteous are just: [but] the counsels of the wicked are deceit.
020	PRO	012	006	The words of the wicked are of lying in wait for blood: but the mouth of the upright shall deliver them.
020	PRO	012	007	The wicked are overthrown, and are not: but the house of the righteous shall stand.
020	PRO	012	008	A man shall be commended according to his wisdom: but he that is of a perverse heart shall be despised.
020	PRO	012	009	Better is he that is lightly esteemed, and hath a servant, than he that honoureth himself, and lacketh bread.
020	PRO	012	010	A righteous man regardeth the life of his beast: but the tender mercies of the wicked are cruel.
020	PRO	012	011	He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain [persons] is void of understanding.
020	PRO	012	012	The wicked desireth the net of evil men: but the root of the righteous yieldeth [fruit].
020	PRO	012	013	In the transgression of the lips is a snare to the evil man: but the righteous shall come out of trouble.
020	PRO	012	014	A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth: and the doings of a man’s hands shall be rendered unto him.
020	PRO	012	015	The way of the foolish is right in his own eyes: but he that is wise hearkeneth unto counsel.
020	PRO	012	016	A fool’s vexation is presently known: but a prudent man concealeth shame.
020	PRO	012	017	He that uttereth truth sheweth forth righteousness, but a false witness deceit.
020	PRO	012	018	There is that speaketh rashly like the piercings of a sword: but the tongue of the wise is health.
020	PRO	012	019	The lip of truth shall be established for ever: but a lying tongue is but for a moment.
020	PRO	012	020	Deceit is in the heart of them that devise evil: but to the counsellors of peace is joy.
020	PRO	012	021	There shall no mischief happen to the righteous: but the wicked shall be filled with evil.
020	PRO	012	022	Lying lips are an abomination to the LORD: but they that deal truly are his delight.
020	PRO	012	023	A prudent man concealeth knowledge: but the heart of fools proclaimeth foolishness.
020	PRO	012	024	The hand of the diligent shall bear rule: but the slothful shall be put under taskwork.
020	PRO	012	025	Heaviness in the heart of a man maketh it stoop; but a good word maketh it glad.
020	PRO	012	026	The righteous is a guide to his neighbour: but the way of the wicked causeth them to err.
020	PRO	012	027	The slothful man roasteth not that which he took in hunting: but the precious substance of men [is to] the diligent.
020	PRO	012	028	In the way of righteousness is life; and in the pathway thereof there is no death.
020	PRO	013	001	A WISE son [heareth] his father’s instruction: but a scorner heareth not rebuke.
020	PRO	013	002	A man shall eat good by the fruit of his mouth: but the soul of the treacherous [shall eat] violence.
020	PRO	013	003	He that guardeth his mouth keepeth his life: [but] he that openeth wide his lips shall have destruction.
020	PRO	013	004	The soul of the sluggard desireth, and hath nothing: but the soul of the diligent shall be made fat.
020	PRO	013	005	A righteous man hateth lying: but a wicked man is loathsome, and cometh to shame.
020	PRO	013	006	Righteousness guardeth him that is upright in the way: but wickedness overthroweth the sinner.
020	PRO	013	007	There is that maketh himself rich, yet hath nothing: there is that maketh himself poor, yet hath great wealth.
020	PRO	013	008	The ransom of a man’s life is his riches: but the poor heareth no threatening.
020	PRO	013	009	The light of the righteous rejoiceth: but the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.
020	PRO	013	010	By pride cometh only contention: but with the well advised is wisdom.
020	PRO	013	011	Wealth gotten by vanity shall be diminished: but he that gathereth by labour shall have increase.
020	PRO	013	012	Hope deferred maketh the heart sick: but when the desire cometh, it is a tree of life.
020	PRO	013	013	Whoso despiseth the word bringeth destruction on himself: but he that feareth the commandment shall be rewarded.
020	PRO	013	014	The law of the wise is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.
020	PRO	013	015	Good understanding giveth favour: but the way of the treacherous is rugged.
020	PRO	013	016	Every prudent man worketh with knowledge: but a fool spreadeth out folly.
020	PRO	013	017	A wicked messenger falleth into evil: but a faithful ambassador is health.
020	PRO	013	018	Poverty and shame [shall be to] him that refuseth correction: but he that regardeth reproof shall be honoured.
020	PRO	013	019	The desire accomplished is sweet to the soul: but it is an abomination to fools to depart from evil.
020	PRO	013	020	Walk with wise men, and thou shalt be wise: but the companion of fools shall smart for it.
020	PRO	013	021	Evil pursueth sinners: but the righteous shall be recompensed with good.
020	PRO	013	022	A good man leaveth an inheritance to his children’s children; and the wealth of the sinner is laid up for the righteous.
020	PRO	013	023	Much food [is in] the tillage of the poor: but there is that is destroyed by reason of injustice.
020	PRO	013	024	He that spareth his rod hateth his son: but he that loveth him chasteneth him betimes.
020	PRO	013	025	The righteous eateth to the satisfying of his soul: but the belly of the wicked shall want.
020	PRO	014	001	Every wise woman buildeth her house: but the foolish plucketh it down with her own hands.
020	PRO	014	002	He that walketh in his uprightness feareth the LORD: but he that is perverse in his ways despiseth him.
020	PRO	014	003	In the mouth of the foolish is a rod of pride: but the lips of the wise shall preserve them.
020	PRO	014	004	Where no oxen are, the crib is clean: but much increase is by the strength of the ox.
020	PRO	014	005	A faithful witness will not lie: but a false witness uttereth lies.
020	PRO	014	006	A scorner seeketh wisdom, and [findeth it] not: but knowledge is easy unto him that hath understanding.
020	PRO	014	007	Go into the presence of a foolish man, and thou shalt not perceive [in him] the lips of knowledge.
020	PRO	014	008	The wisdom of the prudent is to understand his way: but the folly of fools is deceit.
020	PRO	014	009	The foolish make a mock at guilt: but among the upright there is good will.
020	PRO	014	010	The heart knoweth its own bitterness; and a stranger doth not intermeddle with its joy.
020	PRO	014	011	The house of the wicked shall be overthrown: but the tent of the upright shall flourish.
020	PRO	014	012	There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.
020	PRO	014	013	Even in laughter the heart is sorrowful; and the end of mirth is heaviness.
020	PRO	014	014	The backslider in heart shall be filled with his own ways: and a good man [shall be satisfied] from himself.
020	PRO	014	015	The simple believeth every word: but the prudent man looketh well to his going.
020	PRO	014	016	A wise man feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool beareth himself insolently, and is confident.
020	PRO	014	017	He that is soon angry will deal foolishly: and a man of wicked devices is hated.
020	PRO	014	018	The simple inherit folly: but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.
020	PRO	014	019	The evil bow before the good; and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.
020	PRO	014	020	The poor is hated even of his own neighbour: but the rich hath many friends.
020	PRO	014	021	He that despiseth his neighbour sinneth: but he that hath pity on the poor, happy is he.
020	PRO	014	022	Do they not err that devise evil? but mercy and truth [shall be to] them that devise good.
020	PRO	014	023	In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips [tendeth] only to penury.
020	PRO	014	024	The crown of the wise is their riches: [but] the folly of fools is [only] folly.
020	PRO	014	025	A true witness delivereth souls: but he that uttereth lies [causeth] deceit.
020	PRO	014	026	In the fear of the LORD is strong confidence: and his children shall have a place of refuge.
020	PRO	014	027	The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.
020	PRO	014	028	In the multitude of people is the king’s glory: but in the want of people is the destruction of the prince.
020	PRO	014	029	He that is slow to anger is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.
020	PRO	014	030	A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy is the rottenness of the bones.
020	PRO	014	031	He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that hath mercy on the needy honoureth him.
020	PRO	014	032	The wicked is thrust down in his evil-doing: but the righteous hath hope in his death.
020	PRO	014	033	Wisdom resteth in the heart of him that hath understanding: but [that which is] in the inward part of fools is made known.
020	PRO	014	034	Righteousness exalteth a nation: but sin is a reproach to any people.
020	PRO	014	035	The king’s favour is toward a servant that dealeth wisely: but his wrath shall be [against] him that causeth shame.
020	PRO	015	001	A SOFT answer turneth away wrath: but a grievous word stirreth up anger.
020	PRO	015	002	The tongue of the wise uttereth knowledge aright: but the mouth of fools poureth out folly.
020	PRO	015	003	The eyes of the LORD are in every place, keeping watch upon the evil and the good.
020	PRO	015	004	A wholesome tongue is a tree of life: but perverseness therein is a breaking of the spirit.
020	PRO	015	005	A fool despiseth his father’s correction: but he that regardeth reproof getteth prudence.
020	PRO	015	006	In the house of the righteous is much treasure: but in the revenues of the wicked is trouble.
020	PRO	015	007	The lips of the wise disperse knowledge: but the heart of the foolish [doeth] not so.
020	PRO	015	008	The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination to the LORD: but the prayer of the upright is his delight.
020	PRO	015	009	The way of the wicked is an abomination to the LORD: but he loveth him that followeth after righteousness.
020	PRO	015	010	There is grievous correction for him that forsaketh the way: [and] he that hateth reproof shall die.
020	PRO	015	011	Sheol and Abaddon are before the LORD: how much more then the hearts of the children of men!
020	PRO	015	012	A scorner loveth not to be reproved: he will not go unto the wise.
020	PRO	015	013	A merry heart maketh a cheerful countenance: but by sorrow of heart the spirit is broken.
020	PRO	015	014	The heart of him that hath understanding seeketh knowledge: but the mouth of fools feedeth on folly.
020	PRO	015	015	All the days of the afflicted are evil: but he that is of a cheerful heart [hath] a continual feast.
020	PRO	015	016	Better is little with the fear of the LORD, than great treasure and trouble therewith.
020	PRO	015	017	Better is a dinner of herbs where love is, than a stalled ox and hatred therewith.
020	PRO	015	018	A wrathful man stirreth up contention: but he that is slow to anger appeaseth strife.
020	PRO	015	019	The way of the sluggard is as an hedge of thorns: but the path of the upright is made an highway.
020	PRO	015	020	A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish man despiseth his mother.
020	PRO	015	021	Folly is joy to him that is void of wisdom: but a man of understanding maketh straight his going.
020	PRO	015	022	Where there is no counsel, purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.
020	PRO	015	023	A man hath joy in the answer of his mouth: and a word in due season, how good is it!
020	PRO	015	024	To the wise the way of life [goeth] upward, that he may depart from Sheol beneath.
020	PRO	015	025	The LORD will root up the house of the proud: but he will establish the border of the widow.
020	PRO	015	026	Evil devices are an abomination to the LORD: but pleasant words [are] pure.
020	PRO	015	027	He that is greedy of gain troubleth his own house: but he that hateth gifts shall live.
020	PRO	015	028	The heart of the righteous studieth to answer: but the mouth of the wicked poureth out evil things.
020	PRO	015	029	The LORD is far from the wicked: but he heareth the prayer of the righteous.
020	PRO	015	030	The light of the eyes rejoiceth the heart: [and] good tidings make the bones fat.
020	PRO	015	031	The ear that hearkeneth to the reproof of life shall abide among the wise.
020	PRO	015	032	He that refuseth correction despiseth his own soul: but he that hearkeneth to reproof getteth understanding.
020	PRO	015	033	The fear of the LORD is the instruction of wisdom; and before honour [goeth] humility.
020	PRO	016	001	The preparations of the heart belong to man: but the answer of the tongue is from the LORD.
020	PRO	016	002	All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes: but the LORD weigheth the spirits.
020	PRO	016	003	Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.
020	PRO	016	004	The LORD hath made every thing for its own end: yea, even the wicked for the day of evil.
020	PRO	016	005	Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD: [though] hand [join] in hand, he shall not be unpunished.
020	PRO	016	006	By mercy and truth iniquity is purged: and by the fear of the LORD men depart from evil.
020	PRO	016	007	When a man’s ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.
020	PRO	016	008	Better is a little with righteousness than great revenues with injustice.
020	PRO	016	009	A man’s heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.
020	PRO	016	010	A divine sentence is in the lips of the king: his mouth shall not transgress in judgment.
020	PRO	016	011	A just balance and scales are the LORD’S: all the weights of the bag are his work.
020	PRO	016	012	It is an abomination to kings to commit wickedness: for the throne is established by righteousness.
020	PRO	016	013	Righteous lips are the delight or kings; and they love him that speaketh right.
020	PRO	016	014	The wrath of a king is [as] messengers of death: but a wise man will pacify it.
020	PRO	016	015	In the light of the king’s countenance is life; and his favour is as a cloud of the latter rain.
020	PRO	016	016	How much better is it to get wisdom than gold! yea, to get understanding is rather to be chosen than silver.
020	PRO	016	017	The highway of the upright is to depart from evil: he that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.
020	PRO	016	018	Pride [goeth] before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.
020	PRO	016	019	Better it is to be of a lowly spirit with the poor, than to divide the spoil with the proud.
020	PRO	016	020	He that giveth heed unto the word shall find good: and whoso trusteth in the LORD, happy is he.
020	PRO	016	021	The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.
020	PRO	016	022	Understanding is a wellspring of life unto him that hath it: but the correction of fools is [their] folly.
020	PRO	016	023	The heart of the wise instructeth his mouth, and addeth learning to his lips.
020	PRO	016	024	Pleasant words are [as] an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.
020	PRO	016	025	There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.
020	PRO	016	026	The appetite of the labouring man laboureth for him; for his mouth craveth it of him.
020	PRO	016	027	A worthless man deviseth mischief: and in his lips there is as a scorching fire.
020	PRO	016	028	A froward man scattereth abroad strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.
020	PRO	016	029	A man of violence enticeth his neighbour, and leadeth him in a way that is not good.
020	PRO	016	030	He that shutteth his eyes, [it is] to devise froward things: he that compresseth his lips bringeth evil to pass.
020	PRO	016	031	The hoary head is a crown of glory, it shall be found in the way of righteousness.
020	PRO	016	032	He that is slow to anger is better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh a city.
020	PRO	016	033	The lot is cast into the lap; but the whole disposing thereof is of the LORD.
020	PRO	017	001	Better is a dry morsel and quietness therewith, than an house full of feasting with strife.
020	PRO	017	002	A servant that dealeth wisely shall have rule over a son that causeth shame, and shall have part in the inheritance among the brethren.
020	PRO	017	003	The fining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the LORD trieth the hearts.
020	PRO	017	004	An evil-doer giveth heed to wicked lips; [and] a liar giveth ear to a mischievous tongue.
020	PRO	017	005	Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker: [and] he that is glad at calamity shall not be unpunished.
020	PRO	017	006	Children’s children are the crown of old men; and the glory of children are their fathers.
020	PRO	017	007	Excellent speech becometh not a fool: much less do lying lips a prince.
020	PRO	017	008	A gift is [as] a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it: whithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.
020	PRO	017	009	He that covereth a transgression seeketh love: but he that harpeth on a matter separateth chief friends.
020	PRO	017	010	A rebuke entereth deeper into one that hath understanding than an hundred stripes into a fool.
020	PRO	017	011	An evil man seeketh only rebellion; therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.
020	PRO	017	012	Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.
020	PRO	017	013	Whoso rewardeth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.
020	PRO	017	014	The beginning of strife is [as] when one letteth out water: therefore leave off contention, before there be quarrelling.
020	PRO	017	015	He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the righteous, both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD.
020	PRO	017	016	Wherefore is there a price in the hand of a fool to buy wisdom, seeing he hath no understanding?
020	PRO	017	017	A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.
020	PRO	017	018	A man void of understanding striketh hands, and becometh surety in the presence of his neighbour.
020	PRO	017	019	He loveth transgression that loveth strife: he that raiseth high his gate seeketh destruction.
020	PRO	017	020	He that hath a froward heart findeth no good: and he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.
020	PRO	017	021	He that begetteth a fool [doeth it] to his sorrow: and the father of a fool hath no joy.
020	PRO	017	022	A merry heart is a good medicine: but a broken spirit drieth up the bones.
020	PRO	017	023	A wicked man taketh a gift out of the bosom, to pervert the ways of judgment.
020	PRO	017	024	Wisdom is before the face of him that hath understanding: but the eyes of a fool are in the ends of the earth.
020	PRO	017	025	A foolish son is a grief to his father, and bitterness to her that bare him.
020	PRO	017	026	Also to punish the righteous is not good, [nor] to smite the noble for [their] uprightness.
020	PRO	017	027	He that spareth his words hath knowledge: and he that is of a cool spirit is a man of understanding.
020	PRO	017	028	Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise: when he shutteth his lips, he is [esteemed as] prudent.
020	PRO	018	001	He that separateth himself seeketh [his own] desire, and rageth against all sound wisdom.
020	PRO	018	002	A fool hath no delight in understanding, but only that his heart may reveal itself.
020	PRO	018	003	When the wicked cometh, there cometh also contempt, and with ignominy cometh reproach.
020	PRO	018	004	The words of a man’s mouth are as deep waters; the wellspring of wisdom is as a flowing brook.
020	PRO	018	005	To accept the person of the wicked is not good, [nor] to turn aside the righteous in judgment.
020	PRO	018	006	A fool’s lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for stripes.
020	PRO	018	007	A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are the snare of his soul.
020	PRO	018	008	The words of a whisperer are as dainty, morsels, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.
020	PRO	018	009	He also that is slack in his work is brother to him that is a destroyer.
020	PRO	018	010	The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.
020	PRO	018	011	The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, and as an high wall in his own imagination.
020	PRO	018	012	Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honour [goeth] humility.
020	PRO	018	013	He that giveth answer before he heareth, it is folly and shame unto him.
020	PRO	018	014	The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a broken spirit who can bear?
020	PRO	018	015	The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.
020	PRO	018	016	A man’s gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.
020	PRO	018	017	He that pleadeth his cause first [seemeth] just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him out.
020	PRO	018	018	The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.
020	PRO	018	019	A brother offended [is harder to be won] than a strong city: and [such] contentions are like the bars of a castle.
020	PRO	018	020	A man’s belly shall be filled with the fruit of his mouth; with the increase of his lips shall he be satisfied.
020	PRO	018	021	Death and life are in the power of the tongue; and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.
020	PRO	018	022	Whoso findeth a wife findeth a good thing, and obtaineth favour of the LORD.
020	PRO	018	023	The poor useth entreaties: but the rich answereth roughly.
020	PRO	018	024	He that maketh many friends [doeth it] to his own destruction: but there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother.
020	PRO	019	001	Better is the poor that walketh in his integrity than he that perverse in his lips and is a fool.
020	PRO	019	002	Also, that the soul be without knowledge is not good; and he that hasteth with his feet sinneth.
020	PRO	019	003	The foolishness of man subverteth his way; and his heart fretteth against the LORD.
020	PRO	019	004	Wealth addeth many friends: but the poor is separated from his friend.
020	PRO	019	005	A false witness shall not be unpunished; and he that uttereth lies shall not escape.
020	PRO	019	006	Many will entreat the favour of the liberal man: and every man is a friend to him that giveth gifts.
020	PRO	019	007	All the brethren of the poor do hate him: how much more do his friends go far from him! he pursueth [them with] words, [but] they are gone.
020	PRO	019	008	He that getteth wisdom loveth his own soul: he that keepeth understanding shall find good.
020	PRO	019	009	A false witness shall not be unpunished; and he that uttereth lies shall perish.
020	PRO	019	010	Delicate living is not seemly for a fool; much less for a servant to have rule over princes.
020	PRO	019	011	The discretion of a man maketh him slow to anger; and it is his glory to pass over a transgression.
020	PRO	019	012	The king’s wrath is as the roaring of a lion; but his favour is as dew upon the grass.
020	PRO	019	013	A foolish son is the calamity of his father: and the contentions of a wife are a continual dropping.
020	PRO	019	014	House and riches are an inheritance from fathers: but a prudent wife is from the LORD.
020	PRO	019	015	Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep; and the idle soul shall suffer hunger.
020	PRO	019	016	He that keepeth the commandment keepeth his soul: [but] he that is careless of his ways shall die.
020	PRO	019	017	He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD, and his good deed will he pay him again.
020	PRO	019	018	Chasten thy son, seeing there is hope; and set not thy heart on his destruction.
020	PRO	019	019	A man of great wrath shall bear the penalty: for if thou deliver [him], thou must do it yet again.
020	PRO	019	020	Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.
020	PRO	019	021	There are many devices in a man’s heart; but the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand.
020	PRO	019	022	The desire of a man is [the measure of] his kindness: and a poor man is better than a liar.
020	PRO	019	023	The fear of the LORD [tendeth] to life: and he [that hath it] shall abide satisfied; he shall not be visited with evil.
020	PRO	019	024	The sluggard burieth his hand in the dish, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.
020	PRO	019	025	smite a scorner, and the simple will learn prudence: and reprove one that hath understanding, [and] he will understand knowledge.
020	PRO	019	026	He that spoileth his father, and chaseth away his mother, is a son that causeth shame and bringeth reproach.
020	PRO	019	027	Cease, my son, to hear instruction [only] to err from the words of knowledge.
020	PRO	019	028	A worthless witness mocketh at judgment: and the mouth of the wicked swalloweth iniquity.
020	PRO	019	029	Judgments are prepared for scorners, and stripes for the back of fools.
020	PRO	020	001	Wine is a mocker, strong drink a brawler; and whosoever erreth thereby is not wise.
020	PRO	020	002	The terror of a king is as the roaring of a lion: he that provoketh him to anger sinneth [against] his own life.
020	PRO	020	003	It is an honour for a man to keep aloof from strife: but every fool will be quarrelling.
020	PRO	020	004	The slothful will not plow by reason of the winter; therefore he shall beg in harvest, and have nothing.
020	PRO	020	005	Counsel in the heart of man is [like] deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.
020	PRO	020	006	Most men wilt proclaim every one his own kindness: but a faithful man who can find?
020	PRO	020	007	A just man that walketh in his integrity, blessed are his children after him.
020	PRO	020	008	A king that sitteth on the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.
020	PRO	020	009	Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?
020	PRO	020	010	Divers weights, and divers measures, both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD.
020	PRO	020	011	Even a child maketh himself known by his doings, whether his work be pure, and whether it be right.
020	PRO	020	012	The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD hath made even both of them.
020	PRO	020	013	Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, [and] thou shalt be satisfied with bread.
020	PRO	020	014	It is naught, it is naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone his way, then he boasteth.
020	PRO	020	015	There is gold, and abundance of rubies: but the lips of knowledge are a precious jewel.
020	PRO	020	016	Take his garment that is surety for a stranger; and hold him in pledge [that is surety] for strangers.
020	PRO	020	017	Bread of falsehood is sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.
020	PRO	020	018	Every purpose is established by counsel: and by wise guidance make thou war,
020	PRO	020	019	He that goeth about as a talebearer revealeth secrets: therefore meddle not with him that openeth wide his lips.
020	PRO	020	020	Whoso curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in the blackest darkness.
020	PRO	020	021	An inheritance [may be] gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end thereof shall not be blessed.
020	PRO	020	022	Say not thou, I will recompense evil: wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.
020	PRO	020	023	Divers weights are an abomination to the LORD; and a false balance is not good.
020	PRO	020	024	A man’s goings are of the LORD; how then can man understand his way?
020	PRO	020	025	It is a snare to a man rashly to say, [It is] holy, and after vows to make inquiry.
020	PRO	020	026	A wise king winnoweth the wicked, and bringeth the [threshing] wheel over them.
020	PRO	020	027	The spirit of man is the lamp of the LORD, searching all the innermost parts of the belly.
020	PRO	020	028	Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upholden by mercy.
020	PRO	020	029	The glory of young men is their strength: and the beauty of old men is the hoary head.
020	PRO	020	030	Stripes that wound cleanse away evil: and strokes [reach] the innermost parts of the belly.
020	PRO	021	001	The king’s heart is in the hand of the LORD as the watercourses: he turneth it whithersoever he will.
020	PRO	021	002	Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the LORD weigheth the hearts.
020	PRO	021	003	To do justice and judgment is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.
020	PRO	021	004	An high look, and a proud heart, [even] the lamp of the wicked, is sin.
020	PRO	021	005	The thoughts of the diligent [tend] only to plenteousness: but every one that is hasty [hasteth] only to want.
020	PRO	021	006	The getting of treasures by a lying tongue is a vapour driven to and fro; they [that seek them] seek death.
020	PRO	021	007	The violence of the wicked shall sweep them away; because they refuse to do judgment.
020	PRO	021	008	The way of him that is laden with guilt is exceeding crooked: but as for the pure, his work is right.
020	PRO	021	009	It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop, than with a contentious woman in a wide house.
020	PRO	021	010	The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbour findeth no favour in his eyes.
020	PRO	021	011	When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.
020	PRO	021	012	The righteous man considereth the house of the wicked; [how] the wicked are overthrown to [their] ruin.
020	PRO	021	013	Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry, but shall not be heard.
020	PRO	021	014	A gift in secret pacifieth anger, and a present in the bosom strong wrath.
020	PRO	021	015	It is joy to the righteous to do judgment; but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.
020	PRO	021	016	The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall rest in the congregation of the dead.
020	PRO	021	017	He that loveth pleasure shall be a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.
020	PRO	021	018	The wicked is a ransom for the righteous; and the treacherous [cometh] in the stead of the upright.
020	PRO	021	019	It is better to dwell in a desert land, than with a contentious and fretful woman.
020	PRO	021	020	There is precious treasure and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man swalloweth it up.
020	PRO	021	021	He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honour.
020	PRO	021	022	A wise man scaleth the city of the mighty, and bringeth down the strength of the confidence thereof.
020	PRO	021	023	Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.
020	PRO	021	024	The proud and haughty man, scorner is his name, he worketh in the arrogance of pride.
020	PRO	021	025	The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labour.
020	PRO	021	026	There is that coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and withholdeth not.
020	PRO	021	027	The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination: how much more, when he bringeth it with a wicked mind!
020	PRO	021	028	A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth shall speak unchallenged.
020	PRO	021	029	A wicked man hardeneth his face: but as for the upright, he ordereth his ways.
020	PRO	021	030	There is no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.
020	PRO	021	031	The horse is prepared against the day of battle: but victory is of the LORD,
020	PRO	022	001	A [good] name is rather to be chosen than great riches, [and] loving favour rather than silver and gold.
020	PRO	022	002	The rich and the poor meet together: the LORD is the maker of them all.
020	PRO	022	003	A prudent man seeth the evil, and hideth himself: but the simple pass on, and suffer for it.
020	PRO	022	004	The reward of humility [and] the fear of the LORD [is] riches, and honour, and life.
020	PRO	022	005	Thorns [and] snares are in the way of the froward: he that keepeth his soul shall be far from them.
020	PRO	022	006	Train up a child in the way he should go, and even when he is old he will not depart from it.
020	PRO	022	007	The rich ruleth over the poor, and the borrower is servant to the lender.
020	PRO	022	008	He that soweth iniquity shall reap calamity: and the rod of his wrath shall fail.
020	PRO	022	009	He that hath a bountiful eye shall be blessed; for he giveth of his bread to the poor.
020	PRO	022	010	Cast out the scorner, and contention shall go out; yea, strife and ignominy shall cease.
020	PRO	022	011	He that loveth pureness of heart, [for] the grace of his lips the king shall be his friend.
020	PRO	022	012	The eyes of the LORD preserve [him that hath] knowledge, but he overthroweth the words of the treacherous man.
020	PRO	022	013	The sluggard saith, There is a lion without: I shall be murdered in the streets.
020	PRO	022	014	The mouth of strange women is a deep pit: he that is abhorred of the LORD shall fall therein.
020	PRO	022	015	Foolishness is bound up in the heart of a child; [but] the rod of correction shall drive it far from him.
020	PRO	022	016	He that oppresseth the poor to increase his [gain, and] he that giveth to the rich, [cometh] only to want.
020	PRO	022	017	Incline thine ear, and hear the words of the wise, and apply thine heart unto my knowledge.
020	PRO	022	018	For it is a pleasant thing if thou keep them within thee, if they be established together upon thy lips.
020	PRO	022	019	That thy trust may be in the LORD, I have made [them] known to thee this day, even to thee.
020	PRO	022	020	Have not I written unto thee excellent things of counsels and knowledge;
020	PRO	022	021	To make thee know the certainty of the words of truth, that thou mayest carry back words of truth to them that send thee?
020	PRO	022	022	Rob not the poor, because he is poor, neither oppress the afflicted in the gate:
020	PRO	022	023	For the LORD will plead their cause, and despoil of life those that despoil them.
020	PRO	022	024	Make no friendship with a man that is given to anger; and with a wrathful man thou shalt not go:
020	PRO	022	025	Lest thou learn his ways, and get a snare to thy soul.
020	PRO	022	026	Be thou not one of them that strike hands, [or] of them that are sureties for debts:
020	PRO	022	027	If thou hast not wherewith to pay, why should he take away thy bed from under thee?
020	PRO	022	028	Remove not the ancient landmark, which thy fathers have set.
020	PRO	022	029	Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean men.
020	PRO	023	001	When thou sittest to eat with a ruler, consider diligently him that is before thee;
020	PRO	023	002	And put a knife to thy throat, if thou be a man given to appetite.
020	PRO	023	003	Be not desirous of his dainties; seeing they are deceitful meat.
020	PRO	023	004	Weary not thyself to be rich; cease from thine own wisdom.
020	PRO	023	005	Wilt thou set thine eyes upon that which is not? for [riches] certainly make themselves wings, like an eagle that flieth toward heaven.
020	PRO	023	006	Eat thou not the bread of him that hath an evil eye, neither desire thou his dainties:
020	PRO	023	007	For as he reckoneth within himself, so is he: Eat and drink, saith he to thee; but his heart is not with thee.
020	PRO	023	008	The morsel which thou hast eaten shalt thou vomit up, and lose thy sweet words.
020	PRO	023	009	Speak not in the hearing of a fool; for he will despise the wisdom of thy words.
020	PRO	023	010	Remove not the ancient landmark; and enter not into the fields of the fatherless:
020	PRO	023	011	For their redeemer is strong; he shall plead their cause against thee.
020	PRO	023	012	Apply thine heart unto instruction, and thine ears to the words of knowledge.
020	PRO	023	013	Withhold not correction from the child: [for] if thou beat him with the rod, he shall not die.
020	PRO	023	014	Thou shalt beat him with the rod, and shalt deliver his soul from Sheol.
020	PRO	023	015	My son, if thine heart be wise, my heart shall be glad, even mine:
020	PRO	023	016	Yea, my reins shall rejoice, when thy lips speak right things.
020	PRO	023	017	Let not thine heart envy sinners: but [be thou] in the fear of the LORD all the day long:
020	PRO	023	018	For surely there is a reward; and thy hope shall not be cut off.
020	PRO	023	019	Hear thou, my son, and be wise, and guide thine heart in the way.
020	PRO	023	020	Be not among winebibbers; among gluttonous eaters of flesh:
020	PRO	023	021	For the drunkard and the glutton shall come to poverty: and drowsiness shall clothe [a man] with rags.
020	PRO	023	022	Hearken unto thy father that begat thee, and despise not thy mother when she is old.
020	PRO	023	023	Buy the truth, and sell it not; [yea], wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.
020	PRO	023	024	The father of the righteous shall greatly rejoice: and he that begetteth a wise child shall have joy of him.
020	PRO	023	025	Let thy father and thy mother be glad, and let her that bare thee rejoice.
020	PRO	023	026	My son, give me thine heart, and let thine eyes delight in my ways.
020	PRO	023	027	For a whore is a deep ditch; and a strange woman is a narrow pit.
020	PRO	023	028	Yea, she lieth in wait as a robber, and increaseth the treacherous among men.
020	PRO	023	029	Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who hath contentions? who hath complaining? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes?
020	PRO	023	030	They that tarry long at the wine; they that go to seek out mixed wine.
020	PRO	023	031	Look not thou upon the wine when it is red, when it giveth its colour in the cup, when it goeth down smoothly.
020	PRO	023	032	At the last it biteth like a serpent, and stingeth like an adder.
020	PRO	023	033	Thine eyes shall behold strange things, and thine heart shall utter froward things.
020	PRO	023	034	Yea, thou shalt be as he that lieth down in the midst of the sea, or as he that lieth upon the top of a mast.
020	PRO	023	035	They have stricken me, [shalt thou say], and I was not hurt; they have beaten me, and I felt it not: when shall I awake? I will seek it yet again.
020	PRO	024	001	Be not thou envious against evil men, neither desire to be with them.
020	PRO	024	002	For their heart studieth oppression, and their lips talk of mischief.
020	PRO	024	003	Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established:
020	PRO	024	004	And by knowledge are the chambers filled with all precious and pleasant riches.
020	PRO	024	005	A wise man is strong; yea, a man of knowledge increaseth might.
020	PRO	024	006	For by wise guidance thou shalt make thy war: and in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.
020	PRO	024	007	Wisdom is too high for a fool: he openeth not his mouth in the gate.
020	PRO	024	008	He that deviseth to do evil, men shall call him a mischievous person.
020	PRO	024	009	The thought of the foolish is sin: and the scorner is an abomination to men.
020	PRO	024	010	If thou faint in the day of adversity, thy strength is small.
020	PRO	024	011	Deliver them that are carried away unto death, and those that are ready to be slain see that thou hold back.
020	PRO	024	012	If thou sayest, Behold, we knew not this: doth not he that weigheth the hearts consider it? and he that keepeth thy soul, doth not he know it? and shall not he render to every man according to his work?
020	PRO	024	013	My son, eat thou honey, for it is good; and the honeycomb, which is sweet to thy taste:
020	PRO	024	014	So shalt thou know wisdom to be unto thy soul: if thou hast found it, then shall there be a reward, and thy hope shall not be cut off.
020	PRO	024	015	Lay not wait, O wicked man, against the habitation of the righteous; spoil not his resting place:
020	PRO	024	016	For a righteous man falleth seven times, and riseth up again: but the wicked are overthrown by calamity.
020	PRO	024	017	Rejoice not when thine enemy falleth, and let not thine heart be glad when he is overthrown:
020	PRO	024	018	Lest the LORD see it, and it displease him, and he turn away his wrath from him.
020	PRO	024	019	Fret not thyself because of evil-doers; neither be thou envious at the wicked:
020	PRO	024	020	For there will be no reward to the evil man; the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.
020	PRO	024	021	My son, fear thou the LORD and the king: [and] meddle not with them that are given to change:
020	PRO	024	022	For their calamity shall rise suddenly; and who knoweth the destruction of them both?
020	PRO	024	023	These also are [sayings] of the wise. To have respect of persons in judgment is not good.
020	PRO	024	024	He that saith unto the wicked, Thou art righteous; peoples shall curse him, nations shall abhor him:
020	PRO	024	025	But to them that rebuke [him] shall be delight, and a good blessing shall come upon them.
020	PRO	024	026	He kisseth the lips that giveth a right answer.
020	PRO	024	027	Prepare thy work without, and make it ready for thee in the field; and afterwards build thine house.
020	PRO	024	028	Be not a witness against thy neighbour without cause; and deceive not with thy lips.
020	PRO	024	029	Say not, I will do so to him as he hath done to me; I will render to the man according to his work.
020	PRO	024	030	I went by the field of the slothful, and by the vineyard of the man void of understanding;
020	PRO	024	031	And, lo, it was all grown over with thorns, the face thereof was covered with nettles, and the stone wall thereof was broken down.
020	PRO	024	032	Then I beheld, and considered well: I saw, and received instruction.
020	PRO	024	033	[Yet] a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:
020	PRO	024	034	So shall thy poverty come as a robber; and thy want as an armed man.
020	PRO	025	001	These also are proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.
020	PRO	025	002	It is the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the glory of kings is to search out a matter.
020	PRO	025	003	The heaven for height, and the earth for depth, and the heart of kings is unsearchable.
020	PRO	025	004	Take away the dross from the silver, and there cometh forth a vessel for the finer:
020	PRO	025	005	Take away the wicked [from] before the king, and his throne shall be established in righteousness.
020	PRO	025	006	Put not thyself forward in the presence of the king, and stand not in the place of great men:
020	PRO	025	007	For better is it that it be said unto thee, Come up hither; than that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince, whom thine eyes have seen.
020	PRO	025	008	Go not forth hastily to strive, lest [thou know not] what to do in the end thereof, when thy neighbour hath put thee to shame.
020	PRO	025	009	Debate thy cause with thy neighbour [himself], and disclose not the secret of another:
020	PRO	025	010	Lest he that heareth it revile thee, and thine infamy turn not away.
020	PRO	025	011	A word fitly spoken is [like] apples of gold in baskets of silver.
020	PRO	025	012	[As] an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, [so is] a wise reprover upon an obedient ear.
020	PRO	025	013	As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, [so is] a faithful messenger to them that send him; for he refresheth the soul of his masters.
020	PRO	025	014	[As] clouds and wind without rain, [so is] he that boasteth himself of his gifts falsely.
020	PRO	025	015	By long forbearing is a ruler persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh the bone.
020	PRO	025	016	Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee; lest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it.
020	PRO	025	017	Let thy foot be seldom in thy neighbour’s house; lest he be weary of thee, and hate thee.
020	PRO	025	018	A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour is a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow.
020	PRO	025	019	Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble is [like] a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint.
020	PRO	025	020	[As] one that taketh off a garment in cold weather, [and as] vinegar upon nitre, so is he that singeth songs to an heavy heart.
020	PRO	025	021	If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:
020	PRO	025	022	For thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head, and the LORD shall reward thee.
020	PRO	025	023	The north wind bringeth forth rain: so doth a backbiting tongue an angry countenance.
020	PRO	025	024	It is better to dwell in the comer of the housetop, than with a contentious woman in a wide house.
020	PRO	025	025	[As] cold waters to a thirsty soul, so is good news from a far country.
020	PRO	025	026	[As] a troubled fountain, and a corrupted spring, [so is] a righteous man that giveth way before the wicked.
020	PRO	025	027	It is not good to eat much honey: so [for men] to search out their own glory is [not] glory.
020	PRO	025	028	He whose spirit is without restraint is [like] a city that is broken down and hath no wall.
020	PRO	026	001	As snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honour is not seemly for a fool.
020	PRO	026	002	As the sparrow in her wandering, as the swallow in her flying, so the curse that is causeless lighteth not.
020	PRO	026	003	A whip for the horse, a bridle for the ass, and a rod for the back of fools.
020	PRO	026	004	Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou also be like unto him.
020	PRO	026	005	Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own conceit.
020	PRO	026	006	He that sendeth a message by the hand of a fool cutteth off [his own] feet, [and] drinketh in damage.
020	PRO	026	007	The legs of the lame hang loose: so is a parable in the mouth of fools.
020	PRO	026	008	As a bag of gems in a heap of stones, so is he that giveth honour to a fool.
020	PRO	026	009	[As] a thorn that goeth up into the hand of a drunkard, so is a parable in the month of fools.
020	PRO	026	010	[As] an archer that woundeth all, so is he that hireth the fool and he that hireth them that pass by.
020	PRO	026	011	As a dog that returneth to his vomit, [so is] a fool that repeateth his folly.
020	PRO	026	012	Seest thou a man wise in his own conceit? there is more hope of a fool than of him.
020	PRO	026	013	The sluggard saith, There is a lion in the way; a lion is in the streets.
020	PRO	026	014	[As] the door turneth upon its hinges, so doth the sluggard upon his bed.
020	PRO	026	015	The sluggard burieth his hand in the dish; it wearieth him to bring it again to his mouth.
020	PRO	026	016	The sluggard is wiser in his own conceit than seven men that can render a reason.
020	PRO	026	017	He that passeth by, [and] vexeth himself with strife belonging not to him, is [like] one that taketh a dog by the ears.
020	PRO	026	018	As a madman who casteth firebrands, arrows, and death;
020	PRO	026	019	So is the man that deceiveth his neighbour, and saith, Am not I in sport?
020	PRO	026	020	For lack of wood the fire goeth out: and where there is no whisperer, contention ceaseth.
020	PRO	026	021	[As] coals are to hot embers, and wood to fire; so is a contentious man to inflame strife.
020	PRO	026	022	The words of a whisperer are as dainty morsels, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.
020	PRO	026	023	Fervent lips and a wicked heart are [like] an earthen vessel overlaid with silver dross.
020	PRO	026	024	He that hateth dissembleth with his lips, but he layeth up deceit within him:
020	PRO	026	025	When he speaketh fair, believe him not; for there are seven abominations in his heart:
020	PRO	026	026	Though [his] hatred cover itself with guile, his wickedness shall be openly shewed before the congregation.
020	PRO	026	027	Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein: and he that rolleth a stone, it shall return upon him.
020	PRO	026	028	A lying tongue hateth those whom it hath wounded; and a flattering mouth worketh ruin.
020	PRO	027	001	Boast not thyself of tomorrow; for thou knowest not what a day may bring forth.
020	PRO	027	002	Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips.
020	PRO	027	003	A stone is heavy, and the sand weighty; but a fool’s vexation is heavier than them both.
020	PRO	027	004	Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before jealousy?
020	PRO	027	005	Better is open rebuke than love that is hidden.
020	PRO	027	006	Faithful are the wounds of a friend: but the kisses of an enemy are profuse.
020	PRO	027	007	The full soul loatheth an honeycomb: but to the hungry soul every bitter thing is sweet.
020	PRO	027	008	As a bird that wandereth from her nest, so is a man that wandereth from his place.
020	PRO	027	009	Ointment and perfume rejoice the heart: so doth the sweetness of a man’s friend [that cometh] of hearty counsel.
020	PRO	027	010	Thine own friend, and thy father’s friend, forsake not; and go not to thy brother’s house in the day of thy calamity: better is a neighbour that is near than a brother far off.
020	PRO	027	011	My son, be wise, and make my heart glad, that I may answer him that reproacheth me.
020	PRO	027	012	A prudent man seeth the evil, [and] hideth himself: [but] the simple pass on, [and] suffer for it.
020	PRO	027	013	Take his garment that is surety for a stranger; and hold him in pledge [that is surety] for a strange woman.
020	PRO	027	014	He that blesseth his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, it shall be counted a curse to him.
020	PRO	027	015	A continual dropping in a very rainy day and a contentious woman are alike:
020	PRO	027	016	He that would restrain her restraineth the wind, and his right hand encountereth oil.
020	PRO	027	017	Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.
020	PRO	027	018	Whoso keepeth the fig tree shall eat the fruit thereof; and he that waiteth on his master shall be honoured.
020	PRO	027	019	As in water face [answereth] to face, so the heart of man to man.
020	PRO	027	020	Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied; and the eyes of man are never satisfied.
020	PRO	027	021	The fining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold, and a man is [tried] by his praise.
020	PRO	027	022	Though thou shouldest bray a fool in a mortar with a pestle among bruised corn, yet will not his foolishness depart from him.
020	PRO	027	023	Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, [and] look well to thy herds:
020	PRO	027	024	For riches are not for ever; and doth the crown endure unto all generations?
020	PRO	027	025	The hay is carried, and the tender grass sheweth itself, and the herbs of the mountains are gathered in.
020	PRO	027	026	The lambs are for thy clothing, and the goats are the price of the field:
020	PRO	027	027	And [there will be] goats’ milk enough for thy food, for the food of thy household; and maintenance for thy maidens.
020	PRO	028	001	The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.
020	PRO	028	002	For the transgression of a land many are the princes thereof: but by men of understanding [and] knowledge the state [thereof] shall be prolonged.
020	PRO	028	003	A needy man that oppresseth the poor is [like] a sweeping rain which leaveth no food.
020	PRO	028	004	They that forsake the law praise the wicked: but such as keep the law contend with them.
020	PRO	028	005	Evil men understand not judgment: but they that seek the LORD understand all things.
020	PRO	028	006	Better is the poor that walketh in his integrity, than he that is perverse in [his] ways, though he be rich.
020	PRO	028	007	Whoso keepeth the law is a wise son: but he that is a companion of gluttonous men shameth his father.
020	PRO	028	008	He that augmenteth his substance by usury and increase, gathereth it for him that hath pity on the poor.
020	PRO	028	009	He that turneth away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer is an abomination.
020	PRO	028	010	Whoso causeth the upright to go astray in an evil way, he shall fall himself into his own pit: but the perfect shall inherit good.
020	PRO	028	011	The rich man is wise in his own conceit; but the poor that hath understanding searcheth him out.
020	PRO	028	012	When the righteous triumph, there is great glory: but when the wicked rise, men hide themselves.
020	PRO	028	013	He that covereth his transgressions shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall obtain mercy.
020	PRO	028	014	Happy is the man that feareth alway: but he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief.
020	PRO	028	015	[As] a roaring lion, and a ranging bear; [so is] a wicked ruler over a poor people.
020	PRO	028	016	The prince that lacketh understanding is also a great oppressor: [but] he that hateth covetousness shall prolong his days.
020	PRO	028	017	A man that is laden with the blood of any person shall flee unto the pit; let no man stay him.
020	PRO	028	018	Whoso walketh uprightly shall be delivered: but he that is perverse in [his] ways shall fall at once.
020	PRO	028	019	He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain [persons] shall have poverty enough.
020	PRO	028	020	A faithful man shall abound with blessings: but he that maketh haste to be rich shall not be unpunished.
020	PRO	028	021	To have respect of persons is not good: neither that a man should transgress for a piece of bread.
020	PRO	028	022	He that hath an evil eye hasteth after riches, and knoweth not that want shall come upon him.
020	PRO	028	023	He that rebuketh a man shall afterward find more favour than he that flattereth with the tongue.
020	PRO	028	024	Whoso robbeth his father or his mother, and saith, It is no transgression; the same is the companion of a destroyer.
020	PRO	028	025	He that is of a greedy spirit stirreth up strife: but he that putteth his trust in the LORD shall be made fat.
020	PRO	028	026	He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.
020	PRO	028	027	He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack: but he that hideth his eyes shall have many a curse.
020	PRO	028	028	When the wicked rise, men hide themselves: but when they perish, the righteous increase.
020	PRO	029	001	He that being often reproved hardeneth his neck shall suddenly be broken, and that without remedy.
020	PRO	029	002	When the righteous are increased, the people rejoice: but when a wicked man beareth rule, the people sigh.
020	PRO	029	003	Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father: but he that keepeth company with harlots wasteth [his] substance.
020	PRO	029	004	The king by judgment establisheth the land: but he that exacteth gifts overthroweth it.
020	PRO	029	005	A man that flattereth his neighbour spreadeth a net for his steps.
020	PRO	029	006	In the transgression of an evil man there is a snare: but the righteous doth sing and rejoice.
020	PRO	029	007	The righteous taketh knowledge of the cause of the poor: the wicked hath not understanding to know [it].
020	PRO	029	008	Scornful men set a city in a flame: but wise men turn away wrath.
020	PRO	029	009	If a wise man hath a controversy with a foolish man, whether he be angry or laugh, there will be no rest.
020	PRO	029	010	The bloodthirsty hate him that is perfect: and as for the upright, they seek his life.
020	PRO	029	011	A fool uttereth all his anger: but a wise man keepeth it back and stilleth it.
020	PRO	029	012	If a ruler hearkeneth to falsehood, all his servants are wicked.
020	PRO	029	013	The poor man and the oppressor meet together: the LORD lighteneth the eyes of them both.
020	PRO	029	014	The king that faithfully judgeth the poor, his throne shall be established for ever.
020	PRO	029	015	The rod and reproof give wisdom: but a child left to himself causeth shame to his mother.
020	PRO	029	016	When the wicked are increased, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall look upon their fall.
020	PRO	029	017	Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest; yea, he shall give delight unto thy soul.
020	PRO	029	018	Where there is no vision, the people cast off restraint: but he that keepeth the law, happy is he.
020	PRO	029	019	A servant will not be corrected by words: for though he understand he will not give heed.
020	PRO	029	020	Seest thou a man that is hasty in his words? there is more hope of a fool than of him.
020	PRO	029	021	He that delicately bringeth up his servant from a child shall have him become a son at the last.
020	PRO	029	022	An angry man stirreth up strife, and a wrathful man aboundeth in transgression.
020	PRO	029	023	A man’s pride shall bring him low: but he that is of a lowly spirit shall obtain honour.
020	PRO	029	024	Whoso is partner with a thief hateth his own soul: he heareth the adjuration and uttereth nothing.
020	PRO	029	025	The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.
020	PRO	029	026	Many seek the ruler’s favour: but a man’s judgment [cometh] from the LORD.
020	PRO	029	027	An unjust man is an abomination to the righteous: and he that is upright in the way is an abomination to the wicked.
020	PRO	030	001	The words of Agur the son of Jakeh; the oracle. The man saith unto Ithiel, unto Ithiel and Ucal:
020	PRO	030	002	Surely I am more brutish than any man, and have not the understanding of a man:
020	PRO	030	003	And I have not learned wisdom, neither have I the knowledge of the Holy One.
020	PRO	030	004	Who hath ascended up into heaven, and descended? who hath gathered the wind in his fists? who hath bound the waters in his garment? who hath established all the ends of the earth? what is his name, and what is his son’s name, if thou knowest?
020	PRO	030	005	Every word of God is tried: he is a shield unto them that trust in him.
020	PRO	030	006	Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar.
020	PRO	030	007	Two things have I asked of thee; deny me [them] not before I die:
020	PRO	030	008	Remove far from me vanity and lies: give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with the food that is needful for me:
020	PRO	030	009	Lest I be full, and deny [thee], and say, Who is the LORD? or lest I be poor, and steal, and use profanely the name of my God.
020	PRO	030	010	Slander not a servant unto his master, lest he curse thee, and thou be held guilty.
020	PRO	030	011	There is a generation that curseth their father, and doth not bless their mother.
020	PRO	030	012	There is a generation that are pure in their own eyes; and [yet] are not washed from their filthiness.
020	PRO	030	013	There is a generation, Oh how lofty are their eyes! and their eyelids are lifted up.
020	PRO	030	014	There is a generation whose teeth are [as] swords, and their jaw teeth [as] knives, to devour the poor from off the earth, and the needy from among men.
020	PRO	030	015	The horseleach hath two daughters, [Crying], Give, give. There are three things that are never satisfied, [yea], four that say not, Enough:
020	PRO	030	016	The grave; and the barren womb; the earth that is not satisfied with water; and the fire that saith not, Enough.
020	PRO	030	017	The eye that mocketh at his father, and despiseth to obey his mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, and the young eagles shall eat it.
020	PRO	030	018	There be three things which are too wonderful for me, yea, four which I know not:
020	PRO	030	019	The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent upon a rock; the way of a ship in the midst of the sea; and the way of a man with a maid.
020	PRO	030	020	So is the way of an adulterous woman; she eateth, and wipeth her mouth, and saith, I have done no wickedness.
020	PRO	030	021	For three things the earth doth tremble, and for four, [which] it cannot bear:
020	PRO	030	022	For a servant when he is king; and a fool when he is filled with meat;
020	PRO	030	023	For an odious woman when she is married; and an handmaid that is heir to her mistress.
020	PRO	030	024	There be four things which are little upon the earth, but they are exceeding wise:
020	PRO	030	025	The ants are a people not strong, yet they provide their meat in the summer;
020	PRO	030	026	The conies are but a feeble folk, yet make they their houses in the rocks;
020	PRO	030	027	The locusts have no king, yet go they forth all of them by bands;
020	PRO	030	028	The lizard taketh hold with her hands, yet is she in kings’ palaces,
020	PRO	030	029	There be three things which are stately in their march, yea, four which are stately in going:
020	PRO	030	030	The lion, which is mightiest among beasts, and turneth not away for any;
020	PRO	030	031	The greyhound; the he-goat also; and the king, against whom there is no rising up.
020	PRO	030	032	If thou hast done foolishly in lifting up thyself, or if thou hast thought evil, [lay] thine hand upon thy mouth.
020	PRO	030	033	For the churning of milk bringeth forth butter, and the wringing of the nose bringeth forth blood: so the forcing of wrath bringeth forth strife.
020	PRO	031	001	The words of king Lemuel; the oracle which his mother taught him.
020	PRO	031	002	What, my son? and what, O son of my womb, and what, O son of my vows?
020	PRO	031	003	Give not thy strength unto women, nor thy ways to that which destroyeth kings.
020	PRO	031	004	It is not for kings, O Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine; nor for princes [to say], Where is strong drink?
020	PRO	031	005	Lest they drink, and forget the law, and pervert the judgment of any that is afflicted.
020	PRO	031	006	Give strong drink unto him that is ready to perish, and wine unto the bitter in soul:
020	PRO	031	007	Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.
020	PRO	031	008	Open thy mouth for the dumb, in the cause of all such as are left desolate.
020	PRO	031	009	Open thy mouth, judge righteously, and minister judgment to the poor and needy.
020	PRO	031	010	A virtuous woman who can find? for her price is far above rubies.
020	PRO	031	011	The heart of her husband trusteth in her, and he shall have no lack of gain.
020	PRO	031	012	She doeth him good and not evil all the days of her life.
020	PRO	031	013	She seeketh wool and flax, and worketh willingly with her hands.
020	PRO	031	014	She is like the merchant-ships; she bringeth her food from afar.
020	PRO	031	015	She riseth also while it is yet night, and giveth meat to her household, and their task to her maidens.
020	PRO	031	016	She considereth a field, and buyeth it: with the fruit of her hands she planteth a vineyard.
020	PRO	031	017	She girdeth her loins with strength, and maketh strong her arms.
020	PRO	031	018	She perceiveth that her merchandise is profitable: her lamp goeth not out by night.
020	PRO	031	019	She layeth her hands to the distaff, and her hands hold the spindle.
020	PRO	031	020	She spreadeth out her hand to the poor; yea, she reacheth forth her hands to the needy.
020	PRO	031	021	She is not afraid of the snow for her household; for all her household are clothed with scarlet.
020	PRO	031	022	She maketh for herself carpets of tapestry; her clothing is fine linen and purple.
020	PRO	031	023	Her husband is known in the gates, when he sitteth among the elders of the land.
020	PRO	031	024	She maketh linen garments and selleth them; and delivereth girdles unto the merchant.
020	PRO	031	025	Strength and dignity are her clothing; and she laugheth at the time to come.
020	PRO	031	026	She openeth her mouth with wisdom; and the law of kindness is on her tongue.
020	PRO	031	027	She looketh well to the ways of her household, and eateth not the bread of idleness.
020	PRO	031	028	Her children rise up, and call her blessed; her husband [also], and he praiseth her, [saying]:
020	PRO	031	029	Many daughters have done virtuously, but thou excellest them all.
020	PRO	031	030	Favour is deceitful, and beauty is vain: [but] a woman that feareth the LORD, she shall be praised.
020	PRO	031	031	Give her of the fruit of her hands; and let her works praise her in the gates.
#
# BOOK	021	ECC	Ecclesiastes	Ecclesiastes
021	ECC	001	001	The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem.
021	ECC	001	002	Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher; vanity of vanities, all is vanity.
021	ECC	001	003	What profit hath man of all his labour wherein he laboureth under the sun?
021	ECC	001	004	One generation goeth, and another generation cometh; and the earth abideth for ever.
021	ECC	001	005	The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he ariseth.
021	ECC	001	006	The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it turneth about continually in its course, and the wind returneth again to its circuits.
021	ECC	001	007	All the rivers run into the sea, yet the sea is not full; unto the place whither the rivers go, thither they go again.
021	ECC	001	008	All things are full of weariness; man cannot utter [it]: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.
021	ECC	001	009	That which hath been is that which shall be; and that which hath been done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.
021	ECC	001	010	Is there a thing whereof men say, See, this is new? it hath been already, in the ages which were before us.
021	ECC	001	011	There is no remembrance of the former [generations]; neither shall there be any remembrance of the latter [generations] that are to come, among those that shall come after.
021	ECC	001	012	I the Preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.
021	ECC	001	013	And I applied my heart to seek and to search out by wisdom concerning all that is done under heaven: it is a sore travail that God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised therewith.
021	ECC	001	014	I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and, behold, all is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	001	015	That which is crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.
021	ECC	001	016	I communed with mine own heart, saying, Lo, I have gotten me great wisdom above all that were before me in Jerusalem: yea, my heart hath had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.
021	ECC	001	017	And I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also was a striving after wind.
021	ECC	001	018	For in much wisdom is much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.
021	ECC	002	001	I SAID in mine heart, Go to now, I will prove thee with mirth; therefore enjoy pleasure: and, behold, this also was vanity.
021	ECC	002	002	I said of laughter, It is mad: and of mirth, What doeth it?
021	ECC	002	003	I searched in mine heart how to cheer my flesh with wine, mine heart yet guiding [me] with wisdom, and how to lay hold on folly, till I might see what it was good for the sons of men that they should do under the heaven all the days of their life.
021	ECC	002	004	I made me great works; I builded me houses; I planted me vineyards;
021	ECC	002	005	I made me gardens and parks, and I planted trees in them of all kinds of fruit:
021	ECC	002	006	I made me pools of water, to water therefrom the forest where trees were reared:
021	ECC	002	007	I bought menservants and maidens, and had servants born in my house; also I had great possessions of herds and flocks, above all that were before me in Jerusalem:
021	ECC	002	008	I gathered me also silver and gold, and the peculiar treasure of kings and of the provinces: I gat me men singers and women singers, and the delights of the sons of men, concubines very many.
021	ECC	002	009	So I was great, and increased more than all that were before me in Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained with me.
021	ECC	002	010	And whatsoever mine eyes desired I kept not from them: I withheld not my heart from any joy, for my heart rejoiced because of all my labour; and this was my portion from all my labour.
021	ECC	002	011	Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labour that I had laboured to do: and, behold, all was vanity and a striving after wind, and there was no profit under the sun.
021	ECC	002	012	And I turned myself to behold wisdom, and madness and folly; for what [can] the man [do] that cometh after the king? [even] that which hath been already done.
021	ECC	002	013	Then I saw that wisdom excelleth folly, as far as light excelleth darkness.
021	ECC	002	014	The wise man’s eyes are in his head, and the fool walketh in darkness: and yet I perceived that one event happeneth to them all.
021	ECC	002	015	Then said I in my heart, As it happeneth to the fool, so will it happen even to me; and why was I then more wise? Then I said in my heart, that this also was vanity.
021	ECC	002	016	For of the wise man, even as of the fool, there is no remembrance for ever; seeing that in the days to come all will have been already forgotten. And how doth the wise man die even as the fool!
021	ECC	002	017	So I hated life; because the work that is wrought under the sun was grievous unto me: for all is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	002	018	And I hated all my labour wherein I laboured under the sun: seeing that I must leave it unto the man that shall be after me.
021	ECC	002	019	And who knoweth whether he shall be a wise man or a fool? yet shall he have rule over all my labour wherein I have laboured, and wherein I have shewed wisdom under the sun. This also is vanity.
021	ECC	002	020	Therefore I turned about to cause my heart to despair concerning all the labour wherein I had laboured under the sun.
021	ECC	002	021	For there is a man whose labour is with wisdom, and with knowledge, and with skilfulness; yet to a man that hath not laboured therein shall he leave it for his portion. This also is vanity and a great evil.
021	ECC	002	022	For what hath a man of all his labour, and of the striving of his heart, wherein he laboureth under the sun?
021	ECC	002	023	For all his days are [but] sorrows, and his travail is grief; yea, even in the night his heart taketh no rest. This also is vanity.
021	ECC	002	024	There is nothing better for a man [than] that he should eat and drink, and make his soul enjoy good in his labour. This also I saw, that it is from the hand of God.
021	ECC	002	025	For who can eat, or who can have enjoyment, more than I?
021	ECC	002	026	For to the man that pleaseth him [God] giveth wisdom, and knowledge, and joy: but to the sinner he giveth travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to him that pleaseth God. This also is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	003	001	To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven:
021	ECC	003	002	a time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up that which is planted;
021	ECC	003	003	a time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;
021	ECC	003	004	a time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;
021	ECC	003	005	a time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;
021	ECC	003	006	a time to seek, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;
021	ECC	003	007	a time to rend, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;
021	ECC	003	008	a time to love, and a time to hate; a time for war, and a time for peace.
021	ECC	003	009	What profit hath he that worketh in that wherein he laboureth?
021	ECC	003	010	I have seen the travail which God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised therewith.
021	ECC	003	011	He hath made every thing beautiful in its time: also he hath set the world in their heart, yet so that man cannot find out the work that God hath done from the beginning even to the end.
021	ECC	003	012	I know that there is nothing better for them, than to rejoice, and to do good so long as they live.
021	ECC	003	013	And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy good in all his labour, is the gift of God.
021	ECC	003	014	I know that, whatsoever God doeth, it shall be for ever: nothing can be put to it, nor any thing taken from it: and God hath done it, that men should fear before him.
021	ECC	003	015	That which is hath been already; and that which is to be hath already been: and God seeketh again that which is passed away.
021	ECC	003	016	And moreover I saw under the sun, in the place of judgment, that wickedness was there; and in the place of righteousness, that wickedness was there.
021	ECC	003	017	I said in mine heart, God shall judge the righteous and the wicked: for there is a time there for every purpose and for every work.
021	ECC	003	018	I said in mine heart, [It is] because of the sons of men, that God may prove them, and that they may see that they themselves are [but as] beasts.
021	ECC	003	019	For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they have all one breath; and man hath no preeminence above the beasts: for all is vanity.
021	ECC	003	020	All go unto one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.
021	ECC	003	021	Who knoweth the spirit of man whether it goeth upward, and the spirit of the beast whether it goeth downward to the earth?
021	ECC	003	022	Wherefore I saw that there is nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his works; for that is his portion: for who shall bring him [back] to see what shall be after him?
021	ECC	004	001	Then I returned and saw all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold, the tears of such as were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power, but they had no comforter.
021	ECC	004	002	Wherefore I praised the dead which are already dead more than the living which are yet alive;
021	ECC	004	003	yea, better than them both [did I esteem] him which hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.
021	ECC	004	004	Then I saw all labour and every skilful work, that for this a man is envied of his neighbour. This also is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	004	005	The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh.
021	ECC	004	006	Better is an handful with quietness, than two handfuls with labour and striving after wind.
021	ECC	004	007	Then I returned and saw vanity under the sun.
021	ECC	004	008	There is one that is alone, and he hath not a second; yea, he hath neither son nor brother; yet is there no end of all his labour, neither are his eyes satisfied with riches. For whom then, [saith he], do I labour, and deprive my soul of good? This also is vanity, yea, it is a sore travail.
021	ECC	004	009	Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.
021	ECC	004	010	For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him that is alone when he falleth, and hath not another to lift him up.
021	ECC	004	011	Again, if two lie together, then they have warmth: but how can one be warm [alone]?
021	ECC	004	012	And if a man prevail against him that is alone, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.
021	ECC	004	013	Better is a poor and wise youth than an old and foolish king, who knoweth not how to receive admonition any more.
021	ECC	004	014	For out of prison he came forth to be king; yea, even in his kingdom he was born poor.
021	ECC	004	015	I saw all the living which walk under the sun, that they were with the youth, the second, that stood up in his stead.
021	ECC	004	016	There was no end of all the people, even of all them over whom he was: yet they that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	005	001	Keep thy foot when thou goest to the house of God; for to draw nigh to hear is better than to give the sacrifice of fools: for they know not that they do evil.
021	ECC	005	002	Be not rash with thy month, and let not thine heart be hasty to utter any thing before God; for God is in heaven, and thou upon earth: therefore let thy words be few.
021	ECC	005	003	For a dream cometh with a multitude of business; and a fool’s voice with a multitude of words.
021	ECC	005	004	When thou vowest a vow unto God, defer not to pay it; for he hath no pleasure in fools: pay that which thou vowest.
021	ECC	005	005	Better is it that thou shouldest not vow, than that thou shouldest vow and not pay.
021	ECC	005	006	Suffer not thy mouth to cause thy flesh to sin; neither say thou before the angel, that it was an error: wherefore should God be angry at thy voice, and destroy the work of thine hands?
021	ECC	005	007	For [thus it cometh to pass] through the multitude of dreams and vanities and many words: but fear thou God.
021	ECC	005	008	If thou seest the oppression of the poor, and the violent taking away of judgment and justice in a province, marvel not at the matter: for one higher than the high regardeth; and there be higher than they.
021	ECC	005	009	Moreover the profit of the earth is for all: the king [himself] is served by the field.
021	ECC	005	010	He that loveth silver shall not be satisfied with silver; nor he that loveth abundance with increase: this also is vanity.
021	ECC	005	011	When goods increase, they are increased that eat them: and what advantage is there to the owner thereof, saving the beholding [of them] with his eyes?
021	ECC	005	012	The sleep of a labouring man is sweet, whether he eat little or much: but the fulness of the rich will not suffer him to sleep.
021	ECC	005	013	There is a grievous evil, which I have seen under the sun, [namely], riches kept by the owner thereof to his hurt:
021	ECC	005	014	and those riches perish by evil adventure; and if he hath begotten a son, there is nothing in his hand.
021	ECC	005	015	As he came forth of his mother’s womb, naked shall he go again as he came, and shall take nothing for his labour, which he may carry away in his hand.
021	ECC	005	016	And this also is a grievous evil, that in all points as he came, so shall he go: and what profit hath he that he laboureth for the wind?
021	ECC	005	017	All his days also he eateth in darkness, and he is sore vexed and hath sickness and wrath.
021	ECC	005	018	Behold, that which I have seen to be good and to be comely is for one to eat and to drink, and to enjoy good in all his labour, wherein he laboureth under the sun, all the days of his life which God hath given him: for this is his portion.
021	ECC	005	019	Every man also to whom God hath given riches and wealth, and hath given him power to eat thereof, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labour; this is the gift of God.
021	ECC	005	020	For he shall not much remember the days of his life; because God answereth [him] in the joy of his heart.
021	ECC	006	001	There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, and it is heavy upon men:
021	ECC	006	002	a man to whom God giveth riches, wealth, and honour, so that he lacketh nothing for his soul of all that he desireth, yet God giveth him not power to eat thereof, but a stranger eateth it; this is vanity, and it is an evil disease.
021	ECC	006	003	If a man beget an hundred children and live many years, so that the days of his years be many, but his soul be not filled with good, and moreover he have no burial; I say, that an untimely birth is better than he:
021	ECC	006	004	for it cometh in vanity, and departeth in darkness, and the name thereof is covered with darkness;
021	ECC	006	005	moreover it hath not seen the sun nor known it; this hath rest rather than the other:
021	ECC	006	006	yea, though he live a thousand years twice told, and yet enjoy no good: do not all go to one place?
021	ECC	006	007	All the labour of man is for his mouth, and yet the appetite is not filled.
021	ECC	006	008	For what advantage hath the wise more than the fool? [or] what hath the poor man, that knoweth to walk before the living?
021	ECC	006	009	Better is the sight of the eyes than the wandering of the desire: this also is vanity and a striving after wind.
021	ECC	006	010	Whatsoever hath been, the name thereof was given long ago, and it is known that it is man: neither can he contend with him that is mightier than he.
021	ECC	006	011	Seeing there be many things that increase vanity, what is man the better?
021	ECC	006	012	For who knoweth what is good for man in [his] life, all the days of his vain life which he spendeth as a shadow? for who can tell a man what shall be after him under the sun?
021	ECC	007	001	A [good] name is better than precious ointment; and the day of death than the day of one’s birth.
021	ECC	007	002	It is better to go to the house of mourning, than to go to the house of feasting: for that is the end of all men; and the living will lay it to his heart.
021	ECC	007	003	Sorrow is better than laughter: for by the sadness of the countenance the heart is made glad.
021	ECC	007	004	The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house of mirth.
021	ECC	007	005	It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise, than for a man to hear the song of fools.
021	ECC	007	006	For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so is the laughter of the fool: this also is vanity.
021	ECC	007	007	Surely extortion maketh a wise man foolish; and a gift destroyeth the understanding.
021	ECC	007	008	Better is the end of a thing than the beginning thereof: [and] the patient in spirit is better than the proud in spirit.
021	ECC	007	009	Be not hasty in thy spirit to be angry: for anger resteth in the bosom of fools.
021	ECC	007	010	Say not thou, What is the cause that the former days were better than these? for thou dost not inquire wisely concerning this.
021	ECC	007	011	Wisdom is as good as an inheritance: yea, more excellent is it for them that see the sun.
021	ECC	007	012	For wisdom is a defence, even as money is a defence: but the excellency of knowledge is, that wisdom preserveth the life of him that hath it.
021	ECC	007	013	Consider the work of God: for who can make that straight, which he hath made crooked?
021	ECC	007	014	In the day of prosperity be joyful, and in the day of adversity consider: God hath even made the one side by side with the other, to the end that man should not find out any thing [that shall be] after him.
021	ECC	007	015	All this have I seen in the days of my vanity: there is a righteous man that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man that prolongeth [his life] in his evil-doing.
021	ECC	007	016	Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldest thou destroy thyself?
021	ECC	007	017	Be not over much wicked, neither be thou foolish: why shouldest thou die before thy time?
021	ECC	007	018	It is good that thou shouldest take hold of this; yea, also from that withdraw not thine hand: for he that feareth God shall come forth of them all.
021	ECC	007	019	Wisdom is a strength to the wise man more than ten rulers which are in a city.
021	ECC	007	020	Surely there is not a righteous man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not.
021	ECC	007	021	Also take not heed unto all words that are spoken; lest thou hear thy servant curse thee:
021	ECC	007	022	for oftentimes also thine own heart knoweth that thou thyself likewise hast cursed others.
021	ECC	007	023	All this have I proved in wisdom: I said, I will be wise; but it was far from me.
021	ECC	007	024	That which is is far off, and exceeding deep; who can find it out?
021	ECC	007	025	I turned about, and my heart [was set] to know and to search out, and to seek wisdom and the reason [of things], and to know that wickedness is folly, and that foolishness is madness:
021	ECC	007	026	And I find a thing more bitter than death, [even] the woman whose heart is snares and nets, [and] her hands [as] bands: whoso pleaseth God shall escape from her; but the sinner shall be taken by her.
021	ECC	007	027	Behold, this have I found, saith the Preacher; [laying] one thing to another, to find out the account:
021	ECC	007	028	which my soul still seeketh, but I have not found: one man among a thousand have I found; but a woman among all those have I not found.
021	ECC	007	029	Behold, this only have I found, that God made man upright; but they have sought out many inventions.
021	ECC	008	001	Who is as the wise man? and who knoweth the interpretation of a thing? A man’s wisdom maketh his face to shine, and the hardness of his face is changed.
021	ECC	008	002	I [counsel thee], Keep the king’s command, and that in regard of the oath of God.
021	ECC	008	003	Be not hasty to go out of his presence; persist not in an evil thing: for he doeth whatsoever pleaseth him.
021	ECC	008	004	Because the king’s word [hath] power; and who may say unto him, What doest thou?
021	ECC	008	005	Whoso keepeth the commandment shall know no evil thing; and a wise man’s heart discerneth time and judgment:
021	ECC	008	006	for to every purpose there is a time and judgment; because the misery of man is great upon him:
021	ECC	008	007	for he knoweth not that which shall be; for who can tell him how it shall be?
021	ECC	008	008	There is no man that hath power over the spirit to retain the spirit; neither hath he power over the day of death; and there is no discharge in [that] war: neither shall wickedness deliver him that is given to it.
021	ECC	008	009	All this have I seen, and applied my heart unto every work that is done under the sun: [there is] a time wherein one man hath power over another to his hurt.
021	ECC	008	010	And withal I saw the wicked buried, and they came [to the grave]; and they that had done right went away from the holy place, and were forgotten in the city: this also is vanity.
021	ECC	008	011	Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil.
021	ECC	008	012	Though a sinner do evil an hundred times, and prolong his [days], yet surely I know that it shall be well with them that fear God, which fear before him:
021	ECC	008	013	but it shall not be well with the wicked, neither shall he prolong his days, [which are] as a shadow; because he feareth not before God.
021	ECC	008	014	There is a vanity which is done upon the earth; that there be righteous men, unto whom it happeneth according to the work of the wicked; again, there be wicked men, to whom it happeneth according to the work of the righteous: I said that this also is vanity.
021	ECC	008	015	Then I commended mirth, because a man hath no better thing under the sun, than to eat, and to drink, and to be merry: for that shall abide with him in his labour [all] the days of his life which God hath given him under the sun.
021	ECC	008	016	When I applied mine heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done upon the earth: (for also there is that neither day nor night seeth sleep with his eyes:)
021	ECC	008	017	then I beheld all the work of God, that man cannot find out the work that is done under the sun: because however much a man labour to seek it out, yet he shall not find it; yea moreover, though a wise man think to know it, yet shall he not be able to find it.
021	ECC	009	001	For all this I laid to my heart, even to explore all this; that the righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God: whether it be love or hatred, man knoweth it not; all is before them.
021	ECC	009	002	All things come alike to all: there is one event to the righteous and to the wicked; to the good and to the clean and to the unclean; to him that sacrificeth and to him that sacrificeth not: as is the good, so is the sinner; [and] he that sweareth, as he that feareth an oath.
021	ECC	009	003	This is an evil in all that is done under the sun, that there is one event unto all: yea also, the heart of the sons of men is full of evil, and madness is in their heart while they live, and after that [they go] to the dead.
021	ECC	009	004	For to him that is joined with all the living there is hope: for a living dog is better than a dead lion.
021	ECC	009	005	For the living know that they shall die: but the dead know not any thing, neither have they any more a reward; for the memory of them is forgotten.
021	ECC	009	006	As well their love, as their hatred and their envy, is now perished; neither have they any more a portion for ever in any thing that is done under the sun.
021	ECC	009	007	Go thy way, eat thy bread with joy, and drink thy wine with a merry heart; for God hath already accepted thy works.
021	ECC	009	008	Let thy garments be always white; and let not thy head lack ointment.
021	ECC	009	009	Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest all the days of the life of thy vanity, which he hath given thee under the sun, all the days of thy vanity: for that is thy portion in life, and in thy labour wherein thou labourest under the sun.
021	ECC	009	010	Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do [it] with thy might; for there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest.
021	ECC	009	011	I returned, and saw under the sun, that the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding, nor yet favour to men of skill; but fame and chance happeneth to them all.
021	ECC	009	012	For man also knoweth not his time: as the fishes that are taken in an evil net, and as the birds that are caught in the snare, even so, are the sons of men snared in an evil time, when it falleth suddenly upon them.
021	ECC	009	013	I have also seen wisdom under the sun on this wise, and it seemed great unto me:
021	ECC	009	014	There was a little city, and few men within it; and there came a great king against it, and besieged it, and built great bulwarks against it:
021	ECC	009	015	Now there was found in it a poor wise man, and he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet no man remembered that same poor man.
021	ECC	009	016	Then said I, Wisdom is better than strength: nevertheless the poor man’s wisdom is despised, and his words are not heard.
021	ECC	009	017	The words of the wise [spoken] in quiet are heard more than the cry of him that ruleth among fools.
021	ECC	009	018	Wisdom is better than weapons of war: but one sinner destroyeth much good.
021	ECC	010	001	Dead flies cause the ointment of the perfumer to send forth a stinking savour: [so] doth a little folly outweigh wisdom and honour.
021	ECC	010	002	A wise man’s heart is at his right hand; but a fool’s heart at his left.
021	ECC	010	003	Yea also, when the fool walketh by the way, his understanding faileth him, and he saith to every one [that] he is a fool.
021	ECC	010	004	If the spirit of the ruler rise up against thee, leave not thy place; for yielding allayeth great offences.
021	ECC	010	005	There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, as it were an error which proceedeth from the ruler:
021	ECC	010	006	folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in low place.
021	ECC	010	007	I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking as servants upon the earth.
021	ECC	010	008	He that diggeth a pit shall fall into it; and whoso breaketh through a fence, a serpent shall bite him.
021	ECC	010	009	Whoso heweth out stones shall be hurt therewith; [and] he that cleaveth wood is endangered thereby.
021	ECC	010	010	If the iron be blunt, and one do not whet the edge, then must he put to more strength: but wisdom is profitable to direct.
021	ECC	010	011	If the serpent bite before it be charmed, then is there no advantage in the charmer.
021	ECC	010	012	The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious; but the lips of a fool will swallow up himself.
021	ECC	010	013	The beginning of the words of his mouth is foolishness: and the end of his talk is mischievous madness.
021	ECC	010	014	A fool also multiplieth words: [yet] man knoweth not what shall be; and that which shall be after him, who can tell him?
021	ECC	010	015	The labour of fools wearieth every one of them, for he knoweth not how to go to the city.
021	ECC	010	016	Woe to thee, O land, when thy king is a child, and thy princes eat in the morning!
021	ECC	010	017	Happy art thou, O land, when thy king is the son of nobles, and thy princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!
021	ECC	010	018	By slothfulness the roof sinketh in; and through idleness of the hands the house leaketh.
021	ECC	010	019	A feast is made for laughter, and wine maketh glad the life: and money answereth all things.
021	ECC	010	020	Curse not the king, no, not in thy thought; and curse not the rich in thy bedchamber: for a bird of the air shall carry the voice, and that which hath wings shall tell the matter.
021	ECC	011	001	Cast thy bread upon the waters: for thou shalt find it after many days.
021	ECC	011	002	Give a portion to seven, yea, even unto eight; for thou knowest not what evil shall be upon the earth.
021	ECC	011	003	If the clouds be full of rain, they empty themselves upon the earth: and if a tree fall toward the south, or toward the north, in the place where the tree falleth, there shall it be.
021	ECC	011	004	He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.
021	ECC	011	005	As thou knowest not what is the way of the wind, [nor] how the bones [do grow] in the womb of her that is with child; even so thou knowest not the work of God who doeth all.
021	ECC	011	006	In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thine hand: for thou knowest not which shall prosper, whether this or that, or whether they both shall be alike good.
021	ECC	011	007	Truly the light is sweet, and a pleasant thing it is for the eyes to behold the sun.
021	ECC	011	008	Yea, if a man live many years, let him rejoice in them all; but let him remember the days of darkness, for they shall be many. All that cometh is vanity.
021	ECC	011	009	Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth; and let thy heart cheer thee in the days of thy youth, and walk in the ways of thine heart, and in the sight of thine eyes: but know thou, that for all these things God will bring thee into judgment.
021	ECC	011	010	Therefore remove sorrow from thy heart, and put away evil from thy flesh: for youth and the prime of life are vanity.
021	ECC	012	001	Remember also thy Creator in the days of thy youth, or ever the evil days come, and the years draw nigh, when thou shalt say, I have no pleasure in them;
021	ECC	012	002	or ever the sun, and the light, and the moon, and the stars, be darkened, and the clouds return after the rain:
021	ECC	012	003	in the day when the keepers of the house shall tremble, and the strong men shall bow themselves, and the grinders cease because they are few, and those that look out of the windows be darkened,
021	ECC	012	004	and the door shall be shut in the street; when the sound of the grinding is low, and one shall rise up at the voice of a bird, and all the daughters of music shall be brought low;
021	ECC	012	005	yea, they shall be afraid of [that which is] high, and terrors [shall be] in the way; and the almond tree shall blossom, and the grasshopper shall be a burden, and the caper-berry shall fail: because man goeth to his long home, and the mourners go about the streets:
021	ECC	012	006	or ever the silver cord be loosed, or the golden bowl be broken, or the pitcher be broken at the fountain, or the wheel broken at the cistern;
021	ECC	012	007	and the dust return to the earth as it was, and the spirit return unto God who gave it.
021	ECC	012	008	Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher; all is vanity.
021	ECC	012	009	And further, because the Preacher was wise, he still taught the people knowledge; yea, he pondered, and sought out, [and] set in order many proverbs.
021	ECC	012	010	The Preacher sought to find out acceptable words, and that which was written uprightly, [even] words of truth.
021	ECC	012	011	The words of the wise are as goads, and as nails well fastened are [the words of] the masters of assemblies, [which] are given from one shepherd.
021	ECC	012	012	And furthermore, my son, be admonished: of making many books there is no end; and much study is a weariness of the flesh.
021	ECC	012	013	[This is] the end of the matter; all hath been heard: fear God, and keep his commandments; for this is the whole [duty] of man.
021	ECC	012	014	For God shall bring every work into judgment, with every hidden thing, whether it be good or whether it be evil.
#
# BOOK	022	SOL	Song of Solomon	Song of Solomon
022	SOL	001	001	The Song of songs, which is Solomon’s.
022	SOL	001	002	Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love is better than wine.
022	SOL	001	003	Thine ointments have a goodly fragrance; thy name is [as] ointment poured forth; therefore do the virgins love thee.
022	SOL	001	004	Draw me; we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers: we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will make mention of thy love more than of wine: rightly do they love thee.
022	SOL	001	005	I am black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.
022	SOL	001	006	Look not upon me, because I am swarthy, because the sun hath scorched me. My mother’s sons were incensed against me, they made me keeper of the vineyards; [but] mine own vineyard have I not kept.
022	SOL	001	007	Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest [thy flock], where thou makest [it] to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that is veiled beside the flocks of thy companions?
022	SOL	001	008	If thou know not, O thou fairest among women, go thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds’ tents.
022	SOL	001	009	I have compared thee, O my love, to a steed in Pharaoh’s chariots.
022	SOL	001	010	Thy cheeks are comely with plaits [of hair], thy neck with strings of jewels
022	SOL	001	011	We will make thee plaits of gold with studs of silver.
022	SOL	001	012	While the king sat at his table, my spikenard sent forth its fragrance.
022	SOL	001	013	My beloved is unto me [as] a bundle of myrrh, that lieth betwixt my breasts.
022	SOL	001	014	My beloved is unto me [as] a cluster of henna-flowers in the vineyards of En-gedi.
022	SOL	001	015	Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thine eyes are [as] doves.
022	SOL	001	016	Behold, thou art fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant: also our couch is green.
022	SOL	001	017	The beams of our house are cedars, [and] our rafters are firs.
022	SOL	002	001	I AM a rose of Sharon, a lily of the valleys.
022	SOL	002	002	As a lily among thorns, so is my love among the daughters.
022	SOL	002	003	As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so is my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit was sweet to my taste.
022	SOL	002	004	He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me was love.
022	SOL	002	005	Stay ye me with raisins, comfort me with apples: for I am sick of love.
022	SOL	002	006	His left hand [is] under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me.
022	SOL	002	007	I adjure you, O daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awaken love, until it please.
022	SOL	002	008	The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh, leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills.
022	SOL	002	009	My beloved is like a roe or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh in at the windows, he sheweth himself through the lattice.
022	SOL	002	010	My beloved spake, and said unto me, Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.
022	SOL	002	011	For, lo, the winter is past, the rain is over and gone;
022	SOL	002	012	The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing [of birds] is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;
022	SOL	002	013	The fig tree ripeneth her green figs, and the vines are in blossom, they give forth their fragrance. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away.
022	SOL	002	014	O my dove, that art in the clefts of the rock, in the covert of the steep place, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice: for sweet is thy voice, and thy countenance is comely.
022	SOL	002	015	Take us the foxes, the little foxes, that spoil the vineyards; for our vineyards are in blossom.
022	SOL	002	016	My beloved is mine, and I am his: he feedeth [his flock] among the lilies.
022	SOL	002	017	Until the day be cool, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of Bether.
022	SOL	003	001	By night on my bed I sought him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.
022	SOL	003	002	[I said], I will rise now, and go about the city, in the streets and in the broad ways, I will seek him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.
022	SOL	003	003	The watchmen that go about the city found me: [to whom I said], Saw ye him whom my soul loveth?
022	SOL	003	004	It was but a little that I passed from them, when I found him whom my soul loveth: I held him, and would not let him go, until I had brought him into my mother’s house, and into the chamber of her that conceived me.
022	SOL	003	005	I adjure you, O daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awaken love, until it please.
022	SOL	003	006	Who is this that cometh up out of the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all powders of the merchant?
022	SOL	003	007	Behold, it is the litter of Solomon; threescore mighty men are about it, of the mighty men of Israel.
022	SOL	003	008	They all handle the sword, [and] are expert in war: every man hath his sword upon his thigh, because of fear in the night.
022	SOL	003	009	King Solomon made himself a palanquin of the wood of Lebanon.
022	SOL	003	010	He made the pillars thereof of silver, the bottom thereof of gold, the seat of it of purple, the midst thereof being paved with love, from the daughters of Jerusalem.
022	SOL	003	011	Go forth, O ye daughters of Zion, and behold king Solomon, with the crown wherewith his mother hath crowned him in the day of his espousals, and in the day of the gladness of his heart.
022	SOL	004	001	Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thine eyes are as doves behind thy veil: thy hair is as a flock of goats, that lie along the side of mount Gilead.
022	SOL	004	002	Thy teeth are like a flock [of ewes] that are [newly] shorn, which are come up from the washing; whereof every one hath twins, and none is bereaved among them.
022	SOL	004	003	Thy lips are like a thread of scarlet, and thy mouth is comely: thy temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind thy veil.
022	SOL	004	004	Thy neck is like the tower of David builded for an armoury, whereon there hang a thousand bucklers, all the shields of the mighty men.
022	SOL	004	005	Thy two breasts are like two fawns that are twins of a roe, which feed among the lilies.
022	SOL	004	006	Until the day be cool, and the shadows flee away, I will get me to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense.
022	SOL	004	007	Thou art all fair, my love; and there is no spot in thee.
022	SOL	004	008	Come with me from Lebanon, [my] bride, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Senir and Hermon, from the lions’ dens, from the mountains of the leopards.
022	SOL	004	009	Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, [my] bride; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes, with one chain of thy neck.
022	SOL	004	010	How fair is thy love, my sister, [my] bride! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thine ointments than all manner of spices!
022	SOL	004	011	Thy lips, [O my] bride, drop [as] the honeycomb: honey and milk are under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments is like the smell of Lebanon.
022	SOL	004	012	A garden shut up is my sister, [my] bride; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed.
022	SOL	004	013	Thy shoots are an orchard of pomegranates, with precious fruits; henna with spikenard plants,
022	SOL	004	014	Spikenard and saffron, calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices.
022	SOL	004	015	[Thou art] a fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, and flowing streams from Lebanon.
022	SOL	004	016	Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south; blow upon my garden, that the spices thereof may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and eat his precious fruits.
022	SOL	005	001	I AM come into my garden, my sister, [my] bride: I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk. Eat, O friends; drink, yea, drink abundantly, O beloved.
022	SOL	005	002	I was asleep, but my heart waked: it is the voice of my beloved that knocketh, [saying], Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled: for my head is filled with dew, my locks with the drops of the night.
022	SOL	005	003	I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on? I have washed my feet; how shall I defile them?
022	SOL	005	004	My beloved put in his hand by the hole [of the door], and my heart was moved for him.
022	SOL	005	005	I rose up to open to my beloved; and my hands dropped with myrrh, and my fingers with liquid myrrh, upon the handles of the bolt.
022	SOL	005	006	I opened to my beloved; but my beloved had withdrawn himself, [and] was gone. My soul had failed me when he spake: I sought him, but I could not find him; I called him, but he gave me no answer.
022	SOL	005	007	The watchmen that go about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me; the keepers of the walls took away my mantle from me.
022	SOL	005	008	I adjure you, O daughters of Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved, that ye tell him, that I am sick of love.
022	SOL	005	009	What is thy beloved more than [another] beloved, O thou fairest among women? what is thy beloved more than [another] beloved, that thou dost so adjure us?
022	SOL	005	010	My beloved is white and ruddy, the chiefest among ten thousand.
022	SOL	005	011	His head is [as] the most fine gold, his locks are bushy, [and] black as a raven.
022	SOL	005	012	His eyes are like doves beside the water brooks; washed with milk, [and] fitly set.
022	SOL	005	013	His cheeks are as a bed of spices, as banks of sweet herbs: his lips are as lilies, dropping liquid myrrh.
022	SOL	005	014	His hands are [as] rings of gold set with beryl: his body is [as] ivory work overlaid [with] sapphires.
022	SOL	005	015	His legs are [as] pillars of marble, set upon sockets of fine gold: his aspect is like Lebanon, excellent as the cedars.
022	SOL	005	016	His mouth is most sweet: yea, he is altogether lovely. This is my beloved, and this is my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem.
022	SOL	006	001	Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither hath thy beloved turned him, that we may seek him with thee?
022	SOL	006	002	My beloved is gone down to his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.
022	SOL	006	003	I am my beloved’s, and my beloved is mine: he feedeth [his flock] among the lilies.
022	SOL	006	004	Thou art beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as an army with banners.
022	SOL	006	005	Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me. Thy hair is as a flock of goats, that lie along the side of Gilead.
022	SOL	006	006	Thy teeth are like a flock of ewes, which are come up from the washing; whereof every one hath twins, and none is bereaved among them.
022	SOL	006	007	Thy temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind thy veil.
022	SOL	006	008	There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number.
022	SOL	006	009	My dove, my undefiled, is [but] one; she is the only one of her mother; she is the choice one of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and called her blessed; [yea], the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.
022	SOL	006	010	Who is she that looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, terrible as an army with banners?
022	SOL	006	011	I went down into the garden of nuts, to see the green plants of the valley, to see whether the vine budded, [and] the pomegranates were in flower.
022	SOL	006	012	Or ever I was aware, my soul set me [among] the chariots of my princely people.
022	SOL	006	013	Return, return, O Shulammite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. Why will ye look upon the Shulammite, as upon the dance of Mahanaim?
022	SOL	007	001	How beautiful are thy feet in sandals, O prince’s daughter! the joints of thy thighs are like jewels, the work of the hands of a cunning workman.
022	SOL	007	002	Thy navel is [like] a round goblet, [wherein] no mingled wine is wanting: thy belly is [like] an heap of wheat set about with lilies.
022	SOL	007	003	Thy two breasts are like two fawns that are twins of a roe.
022	SOL	007	004	Thy neck is like the tower of ivory; thine eyes [as] the pools in Heshbon, by the gate of Bath-rabbim; thy nose is like the tower of Lebanon which looketh toward Damascus.
022	SOL	007	005	Thine head upon thee is like Carmel, and the hair of thine head like purple; the king is held captive in the tresses [thereof].
022	SOL	007	006	How fair and how pleasant art thou, O love, for delights!
022	SOL	007	007	This thy stature is like to a palm tree, and thy breasts to clusters [of grapes].
022	SOL	007	008	I said, I will climb up into the palm tree, I will take hold of the branches thereof: let thy breasts be as clusters of the vine, and the smell of thy breath like apples;
022	SOL	007	009	And thy mouth like the best wine, that goeth down smoothly for my beloved, gliding through the lips of those that are asleep.
022	SOL	007	010	I am my beloved’s, and his desire is toward me.
022	SOL	007	011	Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field; let us lodge in the villages.
022	SOL	007	012	Let us get up early to the vineyards; let us see whether the vine hath budded, [and] its blossom be open, [and] the pomegranates be in flower: there will I give thee my love.
022	SOL	007	013	The mandrakes give forth fragrance, and at our doors are all manner of precious fruits, new and old, which I have laid up for thee, O my beloved.
022	SOL	008	001	Oh that thou wert as my brother, that sucked the breasts of my mother! [when] I should find thee without, I would kiss thee; yea, and none would despise me.
022	SOL	008	002	I would lead thee, [and] bring thee into my mother’s house, who would instruct me; I would cause thee to drink of spiced wine, of the juice of my pomegranate.
022	SOL	008	003	His left hand [should be] under my head, and his right hand should embrace me.
022	SOL	008	004	I adjure you, O daughters of Jerusalem, that ye stir not up, nor awaken love, until it please.
022	SOL	008	005	Who is this that cometh up from the wilderness, leaning upon her beloved? Under the apple tree I awakened thee: there thy mother was in travail with thee, there was she in travail that brought thee forth.
022	SOL	008	006	Set me as a seal upon thine heart, as a seal upon thine arm: for love is strong as death; jealousy is cruel as the grave: the flashes thereof are flashes of fire, a very flame of the LORD.
022	SOL	008	007	Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if a man would give all the substance of his house for love, he would utterly be contemned.
022	SOL	008	008	We have a little sister, and she hath no breasts: what shall we do for our sister in the day when she shall be spoken for?
022	SOL	008	009	If she be a wall, we will build upon her a turret of silver: and if she be a door, we will enclose her with boards of cedar.
022	SOL	008	010	I am a wall, and my breasts like the towers [thereof]: then was I in his eyes as one that found peace.
022	SOL	008	011	Solomon had a vineyard at Baal-hamon; he let out the vineyard unto keepers; every one for the fruit thereof was to bring a thousand [pieces] of silver.
022	SOL	008	012	My vineyard, which is mine, is before me: thou, O Solomon, shalt have the thousand, and those that keep the fruit thereof two hundred.
022	SOL	008	013	Thou that dwellest in the gardens, the companions hearken for thy voice: cause me to hear it.
022	SOL	008	014	Make haste, my beloved, and be thou like to a roe or to a young hart upon the mountains of spices.
#
# BOOK	023	ISA	Isaiah	Isaiah
023	ISA	001	001	The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.
023	ISA	001	002	Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth, for the LORD hath spoken: I have nourished and brought up children, and they have rebelled against me.
023	ISA	001	003	The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master’s crib: [but] Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider.
023	ISA	001	004	Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evil-doers, children that deal corruptly: they have forsaken the LORD, they have despised the Holy One of Israel, they are estranged [and gone] backward.
023	ISA	001	005	Why will ye be still stricken, that ye revolt more and more? the whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.
023	ISA	001	006	From the sole of the foot even unto the head there is no soundness in it; [but] wounds, and bruises, and festering sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with oil.
023	ISA	001	007	Your country is desolate; your cities are burned with fire; your land, strangers devour it in your presence, and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.
023	ISA	001	008	And the daughter of Zion is left as a booth in a vineyard, as a lodge in a garden of cucumbers, as a besieged city.
023	ISA	001	009	Except the LORD of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, we should have been like unto Gomorrah.
023	ISA	001	010	Hear the word of the LORD, ye rulers of Sodom; give ear unto the law of our God, ye people of Gomorrah.
023	ISA	001	011	To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the LORD: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he-goats.
023	ISA	001	012	When ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to trample my courts?
023	ISA	001	013	Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; new moon and sabbath, the calling of assemblies, —I cannot away with iniquity and the solemn meeting.
023	ISA	001	014	Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear them.
023	ISA	001	015	And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.
023	ISA	001	016	Wash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil:
023	ISA	001	017	learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.
023	ISA	001	018	Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.
023	ISA	001	019	If ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:
023	ISA	001	020	but if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.
023	ISA	001	021	How is the faithful city become an harlot! she that was full of judgment! righteousness lodged in her, but now murderers.
023	ISA	001	022	Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water.
023	ISA	001	023	Thy princes are rebellious, and companions of thieves; every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.
023	ISA	001	024	Therefore saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts, the Mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:
023	ISA	001	025	and I will turn my hand upon thee, and throughly purge away thy dross, and will take away all thy tin:
023	ISA	001	026	and I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called The city of righteousness, the faithful city.
023	ISA	001	027	Zion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.
023	ISA	001	028	But the destruction of the transgressors and the sinners shall be together, and they that forsake the LORD shall be consumed.
023	ISA	001	029	For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.
023	ISA	001	030	For ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.
023	ISA	001	031	And the strong shall be as tow, and his work as a spark; and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench them.
023	ISA	002	001	The word that Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.
023	ISA	002	002	And it shall come to pass in the latter days, that the mountain of the LORD’S house shall be established in the top of the mountains, and shall be exalted above the hills; and all nations shall flow unto it.
023	ISA	002	003	And many peoples shall go and say, come ye, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.
023	ISA	002	004	And he shall judge between the nations, and shall reprove many peoples: and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.
023	ISA	002	005	O house of Jacob, come ye, and let us walk in the light of the LORD.
023	ISA	002	006	For thou hast forsaken thy people the house of Jacob, because they be filled [with customs] from the east, and [are] soothsayers like the Philistines, and they strike hands with the children of strangers.
023	ISA	002	007	Their land also is full of silver and gold, neither is there any end of their treasures; their land also is full of horses, neither is there any end of their chariots.
023	ISA	002	008	Their land also is full of idols; they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made.
023	ISA	002	009	And the mean man is bowed down, and the great man is brought low; therefore forgive them not.
023	ISA	002	010	Enter into the rock, and hide thee in the dust, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty.
023	ISA	002	011	The lofty looks of man shall be brought low, and the haughtiness of men shall be bowed down, and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.
023	ISA	002	012	For there shall be a day of the LORD of hosts upon all that is proud and haughty, and upon all that is lifted up; and it shall be brought low:
023	ISA	002	013	and upon all the cedars of Lebanon, that are high and lifted up, and upon all the oaks of Bashan;
023	ISA	002	014	and upon all the high mountains, and upon all the hills that are lifted up;
023	ISA	002	015	and upon every lofty tower, and upon every fenced wall;
023	ISA	002	016	and upon all the ships of Tarshish; and upon all pleasant imagery.
023	ISA	002	017	And the loftiness of man shall be bowed down, and the haughtiness of men shall be brought low: and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.
023	ISA	002	018	And the idols shall utterly pass away.
023	ISA	002	019	And men shall go into the caves of the rocks, and into the holes of the earth, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake mightily the earth.
023	ISA	002	020	In that day a man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made for him to worship, to the moles and to the bats;
023	ISA	002	021	to go into the caverns of the rocks, and into the clefts of the ragged rocks, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake mightily the earth.
023	ISA	002	022	Cease ye from man, whose breath is in his nostrils: for wherein is he to be accounted of?
023	ISA	003	001	For, behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, doth take away from Jerusalem and from Judah stay and staff, the whole stay of bread, and the whole stay of water;
023	ISA	003	002	the mighty man, and the man of war; the judge, and the prophet, and the diviner, and the ancient;
023	ISA	003	003	the captain of fifty, and the honourable man, and the counsellor, and the cunning artificer, and the skilful enchanter.
023	ISA	003	004	And I will give children to be their princes, and babes shall rule over them.
023	ISA	003	005	And the people shall be oppressed, every one by another, and every one by his neighbour: the child shall behave himself proudly against the ancient, and the base against the honourable.
023	ISA	003	006	When a man shall take hold of his brother in the house of his father, [saying], Thou hast clothing, be thou our ruler, and let this ruin be under thy hand:
023	ISA	003	007	in that day shall he lift up [his voice], saying, I will not be an healer; for in my house is neither bread nor clothing: ye shall not make me ruler of the people.
023	ISA	003	008	For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen: because their tongue and their doings are against the LORD, to provoke the eyes of his glory.
023	ISA	003	009	The shew of their countenance doth witness against them; and they declare their sin as Sodom, they hide it not. Woe unto their soul! for they have rewarded evil unto themselves.
023	ISA	003	010	Say ye of the righteous, that [it shall be] well [with him]: for they shall eat the fruit of their doings.
023	ISA	003	011	Woe unto the wicked! [it shall be] ill [with him]: for the reward of his hands shall be given him.
023	ISA	003	012	As for my people, children are their oppressors, and women rule over them. O my people, they which lead thee cause thee to err, and destroy the way of thy paths.
023	ISA	003	013	The LORD standeth up to plead, and standeth to judge the peoples.
023	ISA	003	014	The LORD will enter into judgment with the elders of his people, and the princes thereof: It is ye that have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor is in your houses:
023	ISA	003	015	what mean ye that ye crush my people, and grind the face of the poor? saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts.
023	ISA	003	016	Moreover the LORD said, Because the daughters of Zion are haughty, and walk with stretched forth necks and wanton eyes, walking and mincing as they go, and making a tinkling with their feet:
023	ISA	003	017	therefore the Lord will smite with a scab the crown of the head of the daughters of Zion, and the LORD will lay bare their secret parts.
023	ISA	003	018	In that day the Lord will take away the bravery of their anklets, and the cauls, and the crescents;
023	ISA	003	019	the pendants, and the bracelets, and the mufflers;
023	ISA	003	020	the headtires, and the ankle chains, and the sashes, and the perfume boxes, and the amulets;
023	ISA	003	021	the rings, and the nose jewels;
023	ISA	003	022	the festival robes, and the mantles, and the shawls, and the satchels;
023	ISA	003	023	the hand mirrors, and the fine linen, and the turbans, and the veils.
023	ISA	003	024	And it shall come to pass, that instead of sweet spices there shall be rottenness; and instead of a girdle a rope; and instead of well set hair baldness; and instead of a stomacher a girding of sackcloth: branding instead of beauty.
023	ISA	003	025	Thy men shall fall by the sword, and thy mighty in the war.
023	ISA	003	026	And her gates shall lament and mourn; and she shall be desolate and sit upon the ground.
023	ISA	004	001	And seven women shall take hold of one man in that day, saying, We will eat our own bread, and wear our own apparel: only let us be called by thy name; take thou away our reproach.
023	ISA	004	002	In that day shall the branch of the LORD be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the land shall be excellent and comely for them that are escaped of Israel.
023	ISA	004	003	And it shall come to pass, that he that is left in Zion, and he that remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be called holy, even every one that is written among the living in Jerusalem:
023	ISA	004	004	when the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from the midst thereof, by the spirit of judgment, and by the spirit of burning.
023	ISA	004	005	And the LORD will create over the whole habitation of mount Zion, and over her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night: for over all the glory [shall be spread] a canopy.
023	ISA	004	006	And there shall be a pavilion for a shadow in the day-time from the heat, and for a refuge and for a covert from storm and from rain.
023	ISA	005	001	Let me sing for my wellbeloved a song of my beloved touching his vineyard. My wellbeloved had a vineyard in a very fruitful hill:
023	ISA	005	002	and he made a trench about it, and gathered out the stones thereof, and planted it with the choicest vine, and built a tower in the midst of it, and also hewed out a winepress therein: and he looked that it should bring forth grapes, and it brought forth wild grapes.
023	ISA	005	003	And now, O inhabitants of Jerusalem and men of Judah, judge, I pray you, betwixt me and my vineyard.
023	ISA	005	004	What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it? wherefore, when I looked that it should bring forth grapes, brought it forth wild grapes?
023	ISA	005	005	And now go to; I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard: I will take away the hedge thereof, and it shall be eaten up; I will break down the fence thereof, and it shall be trodden down:
023	ISA	005	006	and I will lay it waste; it shall not be pruned nor hoed; but there shall come up briers and thorns: I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain upon it.
023	ISA	005	007	For the vineyard of the LORD of hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant: and he looked for judgment, but behold oppression; for righteousness, but behold a cry.
023	ISA	005	008	Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no room, and ye be made to dwell alone in the midst of the land!
023	ISA	005	009	In mine ears [saith] the LORD of hosts, Of a truth many houses shall be desolate, even great and fair, without inhabitant.
023	ISA	005	010	For ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath, and a homer of seed shall yield [but] an ephah.
023	ISA	005	011	Woe unto them that rise up early in the morning, that they may follow strong drink; that tarry late into the night, till wine inflame them!
023	ISA	005	012	And the harp and the lute, the tabret and the pipe, and wine, are [in] their feasts: but they regard not the work of the LORD, neither have they considered the operation of his hands.
023	ISA	005	013	Therefore my people are gone into captivity, for lack of knowledge: and their honourable men are famished, and their multitude are parched with thirst.
023	ISA	005	014	Therefore hell hath enlarged her desire, and opened her mouth without measure: and their glory, and their multitude, and their pomp, and he that rejoiceth among them, descend [into it].
023	ISA	005	015	And the mean man is bowed down, and the great man is humbled, and the eyes of the lofty are humbled:
023	ISA	005	016	but the LORD of hosts is exalted in judgment, and God the Holy One is sanctified in righteousness.
023	ISA	005	017	Then shall the lambs feed as in their pasture, and the waste places of the fat ones shall wanderers eat.
023	ISA	005	018	Woe unto them that draw iniquity with cords of vanity, and sin as it were with a cart rope:
023	ISA	005	019	that say, Let him make speed, let him hasten his work, that we may see it: and let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw nigh and come, that we may know it!
023	ISA	005	020	Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!
023	ISA	005	021	Woe unto them that are wise their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!
023	ISA	005	022	Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:
023	ISA	005	023	which justify the wicked for a reward, and take away the righteousness of the righteous from him!
023	ISA	005	024	Therefore as the tongue of fire devoureth the stubble, and as the dry grass sinketh down in the flame, so their root shall be as rottenness, and their blossom shall go up as dust: because they have rejected the law of the LORD of hosts, and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.
023	ISA	005	025	Therefore is the anger of the LORD kindled against his people, and he hath stretched forth his hand against them, and hath smitten them, and the hills did tremble, and their carcases were as refuse in the midst of the streets. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.
023	ISA	005	026	And he will lift up an ensign to the nations from far, and will hiss for them from the end of the earth: and, behold, they shall come with speed swiftly:
023	ISA	005	027	None shall be weary nor stumble among them; none shall slumber nor sleep; neither shall the girdle of their loins be loosed, nor the latchet of their shoes be broken:
023	ISA	005	028	whose arrows are sharp, and all their bows bent; their horses’ hoofs shall be counted like flint, and their wheels like a whirlwind:
023	ISA	005	029	their roaring shall be like a lion, they shall roar like young lions: yea, they shall roar, and lay hold of the prey, and carry it away safe, and there shall be none to deliver.
023	ISA	005	030	And they shall roar against them in that day like the roaring of the sea: and if one look unto the land, behold darkness [and] distress, and the light is darkened in the clouds thereof.
023	ISA	006	001	In the year that king Uzziah died I saw the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.
023	ISA	006	002	Above him stood the seraphim: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.
023	ISA	006	003	And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.
023	ISA	006	004	And the foundations of the thresholds were moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke.
023	ISA	006	005	Then said I, Woe is me! for I am undone; because I am a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips: for mine eyes have seen the King, the LORD of hosts.
023	ISA	006	006	Then flew one of the seraphim unto me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar:
023	ISA	006	007	and he touched my mouth with it, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.
023	ISA	006	008	And I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then I said, Here am I; send me.
023	ISA	006	009	And he said, Go, and tell this people, Hear ye indeed, but understand not; and see ye indeed, but perceive not.
023	ISA	006	010	Make the heart of this people fat, and make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and turn again, and be healed.
023	ISA	006	011	Then said I, Lord, how long? And he answered, Until cities be waste without inhabitant, and houses without man, and the land become utterly waste,
023	ISA	006	012	and the LORD have removed men far away, and the forsaken places be many in the midst of the land.
023	ISA	006	013	And if there be yet a tenth in it, it shall again be eaten up: as a terebinth, and as an oak, whose stock remaineth, when they are felled; so the holy seed is the stock thereof.
023	ISA	007	001	And it came to pass in the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, that Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up to Jerusalem to war against it; but could not prevail against it.
023	ISA	007	002	And it was told the house of David, saying, Syria is confederate with Ephraim. And his heart was moved, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the forest are moved with the wind.
023	ISA	007	003	Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shear-jashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool, in the highway of the fuller’s field;
023	ISA	007	004	and say unto him, Take heed, and be quiet; fear not, neither let thine heart be faint, because of these two tails of smoking firebrands, for the fierce anger of Rezin and Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.
023	ISA	007	005	Because Syria hath counselled evil against thee, Ephraim [also], and the son of Remaliah, saying,
023	ISA	007	006	Let us go up against Judah, and vex it, and let us make a breach therein for us, and set up a king in the midst of it, even the son of Tabeel:
023	ISA	007	007	thus saith the Lord GOD, It shall not stand, neither shall it come to pass.
023	ISA	007	008	For the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin: and within threescore and five years shall Ephraim be broken in pieces, that it be not a people:
023	ISA	007	009	and the head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah’s son. If ye will not believe, surely ye shall not be established.
023	ISA	007	010	And the LORD spake again unto Ahaz, saying,
023	ISA	007	011	Ask thee a sign of the LORD thy God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.
023	ISA	007	012	But Ahaz said, I will not ask, neither will I tempt the LORD.
023	ISA	007	013	And he said, Hear ye now, O house of David; is it a small thing for you to weary men, that ye will weary my God also?
023	ISA	007	014	Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.
023	ISA	007	015	Butter and honey shall he eat, when he knoweth to refuse the evil, and choose the good.
023	ISA	007	016	For before the child shall know to refuse the evil, and choose the good, the land whose two kings thou abhorrest shall be forsaken.
023	ISA	007	017	The LORD shall bring upon thee, and upon thy people, and upon thy father’s house, days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah; [even] the king of Assyria.
023	ISA	007	018	And it shall come to pass in that day, that the LORD shall hiss for the fly that is in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that is in the land of Assyria.
023	ISA	007	019	And they shall come, and shall rest all of them in the desolate valleys, and in the holes of the rocks, and upon all thorns, and upon all pastures.
023	ISA	007	020	In that day shall the Lord shave with a razor that is hired, [which is] in the parts beyond the River, [even] with the king of Assyria, the head and the hair of the feet: and it shall also consume the beard.
023	ISA	007	021	And it shall come to pass in that day, that a man shall nourish a young cow, and two sheep;
023	ISA	007	022	and it shall come to pass, for the abundance of milk that they shall give he shall eat butter: for butter and honey shall every one eat that is left in the midst of the land.
023	ISA	007	023	And it shall come to pass in that day, that every place, where there were a thousand vines at a thousand silverlings, shall even be for briers and thorns.
023	ISA	007	024	With arrows and with bow shall one come thither; because all the land shall be briers and thorns.
023	ISA	007	025	And all the hills that were digged with the mattock; thou shalt not come thither for fear of briers and thorns, but it shall be for the sending forth of oxen, and for the treading of sheep.
023	ISA	008	001	And the LORD said unto me, Take thee a great tablet, and write upon it with the pen of a man, For Maher-shalal-hash-baz;
023	ISA	008	002	and I will take unto me faithful witnesses to record, Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.
023	ISA	008	003	And I went unto the prophetess; and she conceived, and bare a son. Then said the LORD unto me, Call his name Maher-shalal-hash-baz.
023	ISA	008	004	For before the child shall have knowledge to cry, My father, and, My mother, the riches of Damascus and the spoil of Samaria shall be carried away before the king of Assyria.
023	ISA	008	005	And the LORD spake unto me yet again, saying,
