023	ISA	013	007	Therefore shall all hands be feeble, and every heart of man shall melt:
023	ISA	013	008	and they shall be dismayed; pangs and sorrows shall take hold [of them]; they shall be in pain as a woman in travail: they shall be amazed one at another; their faces [shall be] faces of flame.
023	ISA	013	009	Behold, the day of the LORD cometh, cruel, with wrath and fierce anger; to make the land a desolation, and to destroy the sinners thereof out of it.
023	ISA	013	010	For the stars of heaven and the constellations thereof shall not give their light: the sun shall be darkened in his going forth, and the moon shall not cause her light to shine.
023	ISA	013	011	And I will punish the world for [their] evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.
023	ISA	013	012	I will make a man more rare than fine gold, even a man than the pure gold of Ophir.
023	ISA	013	013	Therefore I will make the heavens to tremble, and the earth shall be shaken out of her place, in the wrath of the LORD of hosts, and in the day of his fierce anger.
023	ISA	013	014	And it shall come to pass, that as the chased roe, and as sheep that no man gathereth, they shall turn every man to his own people, and shall flee every man to his own land.
023	ISA	013	015	Every one that is found shall be thrust through; and every one that is taken shall fall by the sword.
023	ISA	013	016	Their infants also shall be dashed in pieces before their eyes; their houses shall be spoiled, and their wives ravished.
023	ISA	013	017	Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, which shall not regard silver, and as for gold, they shall not delight in it.
023	ISA	013	018	And [their] bows shall dash the young men in pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb; their eye shall not spare children.
023	ISA	013	019	And Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldeans’ pride, shall be as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.
023	ISA	013	020	It shall never be inhabited, neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation: neither shall the Arabian pitch tent there; neither shall shepherds make their flocks to lie down there.
023	ISA	013	021	But wild beasts of the desert shall lie there; and their houses shall be full of doleful creatures; and ostriches shall dwell there, and satyrs shall dance there.
023	ISA	013	022	And wolves shall cry in their castles, and jackals in the pleasant palaces: and her time is near to come, and her days shall not be prolonged.
023	ISA	014	001	For the LORD will have compassion on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land: and the stranger shall join himself with them, and they shall cleave to the house of Jacob.
023	ISA	014	002	And the peoples shall take them, and bring them to their place: and the house of Israel shall possess them in the land of the LORD for servants and for handmaids: and they shall take them captive, whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors.
023	ISA	014	003	And it shall come to pass in the day that the LORD shall give thee rest from thy sorrow, and from thy trouble, and from the hard service wherein thou wast made to serve,
023	ISA	014	004	that thou shalt take up this parable against the king of Babylon, and say, How hath the oppressor ceased! the golden city ceased!
023	ISA	014	005	The LORD hath broken the staff of the wicked, the sceptre of the rulers;
023	ISA	014	006	that smote the peoples in wrath with a continual stroke, that ruled the nations in anger, with a persecution that none restrained.
023	ISA	014	007	The whole earth is at rest, [and] is quiet: they break forth into singing.
023	ISA	014	008	Yea, the fir trees rejoice at thee, [and] the cedars of Lebanon, [saying], Since thou art laid down, no feller is come up against us.
023	ISA	014	009	Hell from beneath is moved for thee to meet thee at thy coming: it stirreth up the dead for thee, even all the chief ones of the earth; it hath raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations.
023	ISA	014	010	All they shall answer and say unto thee, Art thou also become weak as we? art thou become like unto us?
023	ISA	014	011	Thy pomp is brought down to hell, [and] the noise of thy viols: the worm is spread under thee, and worms cover thee.
023	ISA	014	012	How art thou fallen from heaven, O day star, son of the morning! how art thou cut down to the ground, which didst lay low the nations!
023	ISA	014	013	And thou saidst in thine heart, I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God; and I will sit upon the mount of congregation, in the uttermost parts of the north:
023	ISA	014	014	I will ascend above the heights of the clouds; I will be like the Most High.
023	ISA	014	015	Yet thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the uttermost parts of the pit.
023	ISA	014	016	They that see thee shall narrowly look upon thee, they shall consider thee, [saying], Is this the man that made the earth to tremble, that did shake kingdoms;
023	ISA	014	017	that made the world as a wilderness, and overthrew the cities thereof; that let not loose his prisoners to their home?
023	ISA	014	018	All the kings of the nations, all of them, sleep in glory, every one in his own house.
023	ISA	014	019	But thou art cast forth away from thy sepulchre like an abominable branch, clothed with the slain, that are thrust through with the sword, that go down to the stones of the pit; as a carcase trodden under foot.
023	ISA	014	020	Thou shalt not be joined with them in burial, because thou hast destroyed thy land, thou hast slain thy people; the seed of evil-doers shall not be named for ever.
023	ISA	014	021	Prepare ye slaughter for his children for the iniquity of their fathers; that they rise not up, and possess the earth, and fill the face of the world with cities.
023	ISA	014	022	And I will rise up against them, saith the LORD of hosts, and cut off from Babylon name and remnant, and son and son’s son, saith the LORD.
023	ISA	014	023	I will also make it a possession for the porcupine, and pools of water: and I will sweep it with the besom of destruction, saith the LORD of hosts.
023	ISA	014	024	The LORD of hosts hath sworn, saying, Surely as I have thought, so shall it come to pass; and as I have purposed, so shall it stand:
023	ISA	014	025	that I will break the Assyrian in my land, and upon my mountains tread him under foot: then shall his yoke depart from off them, and his burden depart from off their shoulder.
023	ISA	014	026	This is the purpose that is purposed upon the whole earth: and this is the hand that is stretched out upon all the nations.
023	ISA	014	027	For the LORD of hosts hath purposed, and who shall disannul it? and his hand is stretched out, and who shall turn it back?
023	ISA	014	028	In the year that king Ahaz died was this burden.
023	ISA	014	029	Rejoice not, O Philistia, all of thee, because the rod that smote thee is broken: for out of the serpent’s root shall come forth a basilisk, and his fruit shall be a fiery flying serpent.
023	ISA	014	030	And the firstborn of the poor shall feed, and the needy shall lie down in safety: and I will kill thy root with famine, and thy remnant shall be slain.
023	ISA	014	031	Howl, O gate; cry, O city; thou art melted away, O Philistia, all of thee; for there cometh a smoke out of the north, and none standeth aloof at his appointed times.
023	ISA	014	032	What then shall one answer the messengers of the nation? That the LORD hath founded Zion, and in her shall the afflicted of his people take refuge.
023	ISA	015	001	The burden of Moab. For in a night Ar of Moab is laid waste, [and] brought to nought; for in a night Kir of Moab is laid waste, [and] brought to nought.
023	ISA	015	002	He is gone up to Bayith, and to Dibon, to the high places, to weep: Moab howleth over Nebo, and over Medeba: on all their heads is baldness, every beard is cut off.
023	ISA	015	003	In their streets they gird themselves with sackcloth: on their housetops, and in their broad places, every one howleth, weeping abundantly.
023	ISA	015	004	And Heshbon crieth out, and Elealeh; their voice is heard even unto Jahaz: therefore the armed men of Moab cry aloud; his soul trembleth within him.
023	ISA	015	005	My heart crieth out for Moab; her nobles [flee] unto Zoar, to Eglath-shelishiyah: for by the ascent of Luhith with weeping they go up; for in the way of Horonaim they raise up a cry of destruction.
023	ISA	015	006	For the waters of Nimrim shall be desolate: for the grass is withered away, the tender grass faileth, there is no green thing.
023	ISA	015	007	Therefore the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have laid up, shall they carry away to the brook of the willows.
023	ISA	015	008	For the cry is gone round about the borders of Moab; the howling thereof unto Eglaim, and the howling thereof unto Beer-elim.
023	ISA	015	009	For the waters of Dimon are full of blood: for I will bring yet more upon Dimon, a lion upon him that escapeth of Moab, and upon the remnant of the land.
023	ISA	016	001	Send ye the lambs for the ruler of the land from Sela [which is] toward the wilderness, unto the mount of the daughter of Zion.
023	ISA	016	002	For it shall be that, as wandering birds, as a scattered nest, so shall the daughters of Moab be at the fords of Arnon.
023	ISA	016	003	Give counsel, execute judgment; make thy shadow as the night in the midst of the noonday: hide the outcasts; bewray not the wanderer.
023	ISA	016	004	Let mine outcasts dwell with thee; as for Moab, be thou a covert to him from the face of the spoiler: for the extortioner is brought to nought, spoiling ceaseth, the oppressors are consumed out of the land.
023	ISA	016	005	And a throne shall be established in mercy, and one shall sit thereon in truth, in the tent of David; judging, and seeking judgment, and swift to do righteousness.
023	ISA	016	006	We have heard of the pride of Moab, [that] he is very proud; even of his arrogancy, and his pride, and his wrath; his boastings are nought.
023	ISA	016	007	Therefore shall Moab howl for Moab, every one shall howl: for the raisin-cakes of Kir-hareseth shall ye mourn, utterly stricken.
023	ISA	016	008	For the fields of Heshbon languish, and the vine of Sibmah; the lords of the nations have broken down the choice plants thereof; they reached even unto Jazer, they wandered into the wilderness; her branches were spread abroad, they passed over the sea.
023	ISA	016	009	Therefore I will weep with the weeping of Jazer for the vine of Sibmah: I will water thee with my tears, O Heshbon, and Elealeh: for upon thy summer fruits and upon thy harvest the [battle] shout is fallen.
023	ISA	016	010	And gladness is taken away, and joy out of the fruitful field; and in the vineyards there shall be no singing, neither joyful noise: no treader shall tread out wine in the presses; I have made the [vintage] shout to cease.
023	ISA	016	011	Wherefore my bowels sound like an harp for Moab, and mine inward parts for Kir-heres.
023	ISA	016	012	And it shall come to pass, when Moab presenteth himself, when he wearieth himself upon the high place, and shall come to his sanctuary to pray, that he shall not prevail.
023	ISA	016	013	This is the word that the LORD spake concerning Moab in time past.
023	ISA	016	014	But now the LORD hath spoken, saying, Within three years, as the years of an hireling, and the glory of Moab shall be brought into contempt, with all his great multitude; and the remnant shall be very small and of no account.
023	ISA	017	001	The burden of Damascus. Behold, Damascus is taken away from being a city, and it shall be a ruinous heap.
023	ISA	017	002	The cities of Aroer are forsaken: they shall be for flocks, which shall lie down, and none shall make them afraid.
023	ISA	017	003	The fortress also shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria; they shall be as the glory of the children of Israel, saith the LORD of hosts.
023	ISA	017	004	And it shall come to pass in that day, that the glory of Jacob shall be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh shall wax lean.
023	ISA	017	005	And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the standing corn, and his arm reapeth the ears; yea, it shall be as when one gleaneth ears in the valley of Rephaim.
023	ISA	017	006	Yet there shall be left therein gleanings, as the shaking of an olive tree, two or three berries in the top of the uppermost bough, four or five in the outmost branches of a fruitful tree, saith the LORD, the God of Israel.
023	ISA	017	007	In that day shall a man look unto his Maker, and his eyes shall have respect to the Holy One of Israel.
023	ISA	017	008	And he shall not look to the altars, the work of his hands, neither shall he have respect to that which his fingers have made, either the Asherim, or the sun-images.
023	ISA	017	009	In that day shall his strong cities be as the forsaken places in the wood and on the mountain top, which were forsaken from before the children of Israel: and it shall be a desolation.
023	ISA	017	010	For thou hast forgotten the God of thy salvation, and hast not been mindful of the rock of thy strength; therefore thou plantest pleasant plants, and settest it with strange slips:
023	ISA	017	011	In the day of thy planting thou hedgest it in, and in the morning thou makest thy seed to blossom: but the harvest fleeth away in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow.
023	ISA	017	012	Ah, the uproar of many peoples, which roar like the roaring of the seas; and the rushing of nations, that rush like the rushing of mighty waters!
023	ISA	017	013	The nations shall rush like the rushing of many waters: but he shall rebuke them, and they shall flee far off, and shall be chased as the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like the whirling dust before the storm.
023	ISA	017	014	At eventide behold terror; [and] before the morning they are not. This is the portion of them that spoil us, and the lot of them that rob us.
023	ISA	018	001	Ah, the land of the rustling of wings, which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia:
023	ISA	018	002	that sendeth ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of papyrus upon the waters, [saying], Go, ye swift messengers, to a nation tall and smooth, to a people terrible from their beginning onward; a nation that meteth out and treadeth down, whose land the rivers divide!
023	ISA	018	003	All ye inhabitants of the world, and ye dwellers on the earth, when an ensign is lifted up on the mountains, see ye; and when the trumpet is blown, hear ye.
023	ISA	018	004	For thus hath the LORD said unto me, I will be still, and I will behold in my dwelling place; like clear heat in sunshine, like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.
023	ISA	018	005	For afore the harvest, when the blossom is over, and the flower becometh a ripening grape, he shall cut off the sprigs with pruning-hooks, and the spreading branches shall he take away [and] cut down.
023	ISA	018	006	They shall be left together unto the ravenous birds of the mountains, and to the beasts of the earth: and the ravenous birds shall summer upon them, and all the beasts of the earth shall winter upon them.
023	ISA	018	007	In that time shall a present be brought unto the LORD of hosts of a people tall and smooth, and from a people terrible from their beginning onward; a nation that meteth out and treadeth down, whose land the rivers divide, to the place of the name of the LORD of hosts, the mount Zion.
023	ISA	019	001	The burden of Egypt. Behold, the LORD rideth upon a swift cloud, and cometh unto Egypt: and the idols of Egypt shall be moved at his presence, and the heart of Egypt shall melt in the midst of it.
023	ISA	019	002	And I will stir up the Egyptians against the Egyptians: and they shall fight every one against his brother, and every one against his neighbour; city against city, [and] kingdom against kingdom.
023	ISA	019	003	And the spirit of Egypt shall be made void in the midst of it; and I will destroy the counsel thereof: and they shall seek unto the idols, and to the charmers, and to them that have familiar spirits, and to the wizards.
023	ISA	019	004	And I will give over the Egyptians into the hand of a cruel lord; and a fierce king shall rule over them, saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts.
023	ISA	019	005	And the waters shall fail from the sea, and the river shall be wasted and become dry.
023	ISA	019	006	And the rivers shall stink; the streams of Egypt shall be minished and dried up: the reeds and flags shall wither away.
023	ISA	019	007	The meadows by the Nile, by the brink of the Nile, and all that is sown by the Nile, shall become dry, be driven away, and be no more.
023	ISA	019	008	The fishers also shall lament, and all they that cast angle into the Nile shall mourn, and they that spread nets upon the waters shall languish.
023	ISA	019	009	Moreover they that work in combed flax, and they that weave white cloth, shall be ashamed.
023	ISA	019	010	And her pillars shall be broken in pieces, all they that work for hire [shall be] grieved in soul.
023	ISA	019	011	The princes of Zoan are utterly foolish; the counsel of the wisest counsellors of Pharaoh is become brutish: how say ye unto Pharaoh, I am the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings?
023	ISA	019	012	Where then are thy wise men? and let them tell thee now; and let them know what the LORD of hosts hath purposed concerning Egypt.
023	ISA	019	013	The princes of Zoan are become fools, the princes of Noph are deceived; they have caused Egypt to go astray, that are the corner stone of her tribes.
023	ISA	019	014	The LORD hath mingled a spirit of perverseness in the midst of her: and they have caused Egypt to go astray in every work thereof, as a drunken man staggereth in his vomit.
023	ISA	019	015	Neither shall there be for Egypt any work, which head or tail, palm branch or rush, may do.
023	ISA	019	016	It In that day shall Egypt be like unto women: and it shall tremble and fear because of the shaking of the hand of the LORD of hosts, which he shaketh over it.
023	ISA	019	017	And the land of Judah shall become a terror unto Egypt, every one to whom mention is made thereof shall be afraid, because of the purpose of the LORD of hosts, which he purposeth against it.
023	ISA	019	018	In that day there shall be five cities in the land of Egypt that speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the LORD of hosts; one shall be called The city of destruction.
023	ISA	019	019	In that day shall there be an altar to the LORD in the midst of the land of Egypt, and a pillar at the border thereof to the LORD.
023	ISA	019	020	And it shall be for a sign and for a witness unto the LORD of hosts in the land of Egypt: for they shall cry unto the LORD because of the oppressors, and he shall send them a saviour, and a defender, and he shall deliver them.
023	ISA	019	021	And the LORD shall be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians shall know the LORD in that day; yea, they shall worship with sacrifice and oblation, and shall vow a vow unto the LORD, and shall perform it.
023	ISA	019	022	And the LORD shall smite Egypt, smiting and healing; and they shall return unto the LORD, and he shall be entreated of them, and shall heal them.
023	ISA	019	023	In that day shall there be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria; and the Egyptians shall worship with the Assyrians.
023	ISA	019	024	In that day shall Israel be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, a blessing in the midst of the earth:
023	ISA	019	025	for that the LORD of hosts hath blessed them, saying, Blessed be Egypt my people, and Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel mine inheritance.
023	ISA	020	001	In the year that Tartan came unto Ashdod, when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him, and he fought against Ashdod and took it;
023	ISA	020	002	at that time the LORD spake by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go, and loose sackcloth from off thy loins, and put thy shoe from off thy foot. And he did so, walking naked and barefoot.
023	ISA	020	003	And the LORD said, Like as my servant Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot three years for a sign and a wonder upon Egypt and upon Ethiopia;
023	ISA	020	004	so shall the king of Assyria lead away the captives of Egypt, and the exiles of Ethiopia, young and old, naked and barefoot, and with buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt.
023	ISA	020	005	And they shall be dismayed and ashamed, because of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory.
023	ISA	020	006	And the inhabitant of this coastland shall say in that day, Behold, such is our expectation, whither we fled for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria: and we, how shall we escape?
023	ISA	021	001	The burden of the wilderness of the sea. As whirlwinds in the South sweep through, it cometh from the wilderness, from a terrible land.
023	ISA	021	002	A grievous vision is declared unto me; the treacherous dealer dealeth treacherously, and the spoiler spoileth. Go up, O Elam; besiege, O Media; all the sighing thereof have I made to cease.
023	ISA	021	003	Therefore are my loins filled with anguish; pangs have taken hold upon me, as the pangs of a woman in travail: I am pained so that I cannot hear; I am dismayed so that I cannot see.
023	ISA	021	004	My heart panteth, horror hath affrighted me: the twilight that I desired hath been turned into trembling unto me.
023	ISA	021	005	They prepare the table, they set the watch, they eat, they drink: rise up, ye princes, anoint the shield.
023	ISA	021	006	For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Go, set a watchman; let him declare what he seeth:
023	ISA	021	007	and when he seeth a troop, horsemen in pairs, a troop of asses, a troop of camels, he shall hearken diligently with much heed.
023	ISA	021	008	And he cried as a lion: O Lord, I stand continually upon the watchtower in the day-time, and am set in my ward whole nights:
023	ISA	021	009	and, behold, here cometh a troop of men, horsemen in pairs. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods are broken unto the ground.
023	ISA	021	010	O thou my threshing, and the corn of my floor: that which I have heard from the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, have I declared unto you.
023	ISA	021	011	The burden of Dumah. One calleth unto me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?
023	ISA	021	012	The watchman said, The morning cometh, and also the night: if ye will inquire, inquire ye: turn ye, come.
023	ISA	021	013	The burden upon Arabia. In the forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O ye travelling companies of Dedanites.
023	ISA	021	014	Unto him that was thirsty they brought water; the inhabitants of the land of Tema did meet the fugitives with their bread.
023	ISA	021	015	For they fled away from the swords, from the drawn sword, and from the bent bow, and from the grievousness of war.
023	ISA	021	016	For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Within a year, according to the years of an hireling, and all the glory of Kedar shall fail:
023	ISA	021	017	and the residue of the number of the archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, shall be few: for the LORD, the God of Israel, hath spoken it.
023	ISA	022	001	The burden of the valley of vision. What aileth thee now, that thou art wholly gone up to the housetops?
023	ISA	022	002	O thou that art full of shoutings, a tumultuous city, a joyous town; thy slain are not slain with the sword, neither are they dead in battle.
023	ISA	022	003	All thy rulers fled away together, they were bound by the archers: all that were found of thee were bound together, they fled afar off.
023	ISA	022	004	Therefore said I, Look away from me, I will weep bitterly; labour not to comfort me, for the spoiling of the daughter of my people.
023	ISA	022	005	For it is a day of discomfiture, and of treading down, and of perplexity, from the Lord, the LORD of hosts, in the valley of vision; a breaking down of the walls, and a crying to the mountains.
