023	ISA	046	005	To whom will ye liken me, and make me equal, and compare me, that we may be like?
023	ISA	046	006	Such as lavish gold out of the bag, and weigh silver in the balance, they hire a goldsmith, and he maketh it a god; they fall down, yea, they worship.
023	ISA	046	007	They bear him upon the shoulder, they carry him, and set him in his place, and he standeth; from his place shall he not remove: yea, one shall cry unto him, yet can he not answer, nor save him out of his trouble.
023	ISA	046	008	Remember this, and shew yourselves men: bring it again to mind, O ye transgressors.
023	ISA	046	009	Remember the former things of old: for I am God, and there is none else; [I am] God, and there is none like me;
023	ISA	046	010	declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times things that are not [yet] done; saying, My counsel shall stand, and I will do all my pleasure:
023	ISA	046	011	calling a ravenous bird from the east, the man of my counsel from a far country; yea, I have spoken, I will also bring it to pass; I have purposed, I will also do it.
023	ISA	046	012	Hearken unto me, ye stouthearted, that are far from righteousness:
023	ISA	046	013	I bring near my righteousness, it shall not be far off, and my salvation shall not tarry; and I will place salvation in Zion for Israel my glory,
023	ISA	047	001	Come down, and sit in the dust, O virgin daughter of Babylon; sit on the ground without a throne, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called tender and delicate.
023	ISA	047	002	Take the millstones, and grind meal: remove thy veil, strip off the train, uncover the leg, pass through the rivers.
023	ISA	047	003	Thy nakedness shall be uncovered, yea, thy shame shall be seen: I will take vengeance, and will accept no man.
023	ISA	047	004	Our redeemer, the LORD of hosts is his name, the Holy One of Israel.
023	ISA	047	005	Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called The lady of kingdoms.
023	ISA	047	006	I was wroth with my people, I profaned mine inheritance, and gave them into thine hand: thou didst shew them no mercy; upon the aged hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.
023	ISA	047	007	And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: so that thou didst not lay these things to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end thereof.
023	ISA	047	008	Now therefore hear this, thou that art given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thine heart, I am, and there is none else beside me; I shall not sit as a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children:
023	ISA	047	009	but these two things shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: in their full measure shall they come upon thee, despite of the multitude of thy sorceries, and the great abundance of thine enchantments.
023	ISA	047	010	For thou hast trusted in thy wickedness; thou hast said, None seeth me; thy wisdom and thy knowledge, it hath perverted thee: and thou hast said in thine heart, I am, and there is none else beside me.
023	ISA	047	011	Therefore shall evil come upon thee; thou shalt not know the dawning thereof: and mischief shall fall upon thee; thou shalt not be able to put it away: and desolation shall come upon thee suddenly, which thou knowest not.
023	ISA	047	012	Stand now with thine enchantments, and with the multitude of thy sorceries, wherein thou hast laboured from thy youth; if so be thou shalt be able to profit, if so be thou mayest prevail.
023	ISA	047	013	Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels: let now the astrologers, the stargazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from the things that shall come upon thee.
023	ISA	047	014	Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them; they shall not deliver themselves from the power of the flame: it shall not be a coal to warm at, nor a fire to sit before.
023	ISA	047	015	Thus shall the things be unto thee wherein thou hast laboured: they that have trafficked with thee from thy youth shall wander every one to his quarter; there shall be none to save thee.
023	ISA	048	001	Hear ye this, O house of Jacob, which are called by the name of Israel, and are come forth out of the waters of Judah; which swear by the name of the LORD, and make mention of the God of Israel, but not in truth, nor in righteousness.
023	ISA	048	002	For they call themselves of the holy city, and stay themselves upon the God of Israel; the LORD of hosts is his name.
023	ISA	048	003	I have declared the former things from of old; yea, they went forth out of my mouth, and I shewed them: suddenly I did them, and they came to pass.
023	ISA	048	004	Because I knew that thou art obstinate, and thy neck is an iron sinew, and thy brow brass;
023	ISA	048	005	therefore I have declared it to thee from of old; before it came to pass I shewed it thee: lest thou shouldest say, Mine idol hath done them, and my graven image, and my molten image, hath commanded them.
023	ISA	048	006	Thou hast heard it; behold all this; and ye, will ye not declare it? I have shewed thee new things from this time, even hidden things, which thou hast not known.
023	ISA	048	007	They are created now, and not from of old; and before this day thou heardest them not; lest thou shouldest say, Behold, I knew them.
023	ISA	048	008	Yea, thou heardest not; yea, thou knewest not; yea, from of old thine ear was not opened: for I knew that thou didst deal very treacherously, and wast called a transgressor from the womb.
023	ISA	048	009	For my name’s sake will I defer mine anger, and for my praise will I refrain for thee, that I cut thee not off.
023	ISA	048	010	Behold, I have refined thee, but not as silver; I have chosen thee in the furnace of affliction.
023	ISA	048	011	For mine own sake, for mine own sake, will I do it; for how should [my name] be profaned? and my glory will I not give to another.
023	ISA	048	012	Hearken unto me, O Jacob, and Israel my called: I am he; I am the first, I also am the last.
023	ISA	048	013	Yea, mine hand hath laid the foundation of the earth, and my right hand hath spread out the heavens: when I call unto them, they stand up together.
023	ISA	048	014	Assemble yourselves, all ye, and hear; which among them hath declared these things? The LORD hath loved him: he shall perform his pleasure on Babylon, and his arm [shall be on] the Chaldeans.
023	ISA	048	015	I, even I, have spoken; yea, I have called him: I have brought him, and he shall make his way prosperous.
023	ISA	048	016	Come ye near unto me, hear ye this; from the beginning I have not spoken in secret; from the time that it was, there am I: and now the Lord GOD hath sent me, and his spirit.
023	ISA	048	017	Thus saith the LORD, thy redeemer, the Holy One of Israel: I am the LORD thy God, which teacheth thee to profit, which leadeth thee by the way that thou shouldest go.
023	ISA	048	018	Oh that thou hadst hearkened to my commandments! then had thy peace been as a river, and thy righteousness as the waves of the sea:
023	ISA	048	019	thy seed also had been as the sand, and the offspring of thy bowels like the grains thereof: his name should not be cut off nor destroyed from before me.
023	ISA	048	020	Go ye forth of Babylon, flee ye from the Chaldeans; with a voice of singing declare ye, tell this, utter it even to the end of the earth: say ye, The LORD hath redeemed his servant Jacob.
