024	JER	006	018	Therefore hear, ye nations, and know, O congregation, what is among them.
024	JER	006	019	Hear, O earth: behold, I will bring evil upon this people, even the fruit of their thoughts, because they have not hearkened unto my words; and as for my law, they have rejected it.
024	JER	006	020	To what purpose cometh there to me frankincense from Sheba, and the sweet cane from a far country? your burnt offerings are not acceptable, nor your sacrifices pleasing unto me.
024	JER	006	021	Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will lay stumblingblocks before this people: and the fathers and the sons together shall stumble against them; the neighbour and his friend shall perish.
024	JER	006	022	Thus saith the LORD, Behold, a people cometh from the north country; and a great nation shall be stirred up from the uttermost parts of the earth.
024	JER	006	023	They lay hold on bow and spear; they are cruel, and have no mercy; their voice roareth like the sea, and they ride upon horses; every one set in array, as a man to the battle, against thee, O daughter of Zion.
024	JER	006	024	We have heard the fame thereof; our hands wax feeble: anguish hath taken hold of us, [and] pangs as of a woman in travail.
024	JER	006	025	Go not forth into the field, nor walk by the way; for [there is] the sword of the enemy, [and] terror on every side.
024	JER	006	026	O daughter of my people, gird thee with sackcloth, and wallow thyself in ashes: make thee mourning, as for an only son, most bitter lamentation; for the spoiler shall suddenly come upon us.
024	JER	006	027	I have made thee a tower [and] a fortress among my people; that thou mayest know and try their way.
024	JER	006	028	They are all grievous revolters, going about with slanders; they are brass and iron: they all of them deal corruptly.
024	JER	006	029	The bellows blow fiercely; the lead is consumed of the fire: in vain do they go on refining; for the wicked are not plucked away.
024	JER	006	030	Refuse silver shall men call them, because the LORD hath rejected them.
024	JER	007	001	The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
024	JER	007	002	Stand in the gate of the LORD’S house, and proclaim there this word, and say, Hear the word of the LORD, all ye of Judah, that enter in at these gates to worship the LORD.
024	JER	007	003	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Amend your ways and your doings, and I will cause you to dwell in this place.
024	JER	007	004	Trust ye not in lying words, saying, The temple of the LORD, the temple of the LORD, the temple of the LORD, are these.
024	JER	007	005	For if ye throughly amend your ways and your doings; if ye throughly execute judgment between a man and his neighbour;
024	JER	007	006	if ye oppress not the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, and shed not innocent blood in this place, neither walk after other gods to your own hurt:
024	JER	007	007	then will I cause you to dwell in this place, in the land that I gave to your fathers, from of old even for evermore.
024	JER	007	008	Behold, ye trust in lying words, that cannot profit.
024	JER	007	009	Will ye steal, murder, and commit adultery, and swear falsely, and burn incense unto Baal, and walk after other gods whom ye have not known,
024	JER	007	010	and come and stand before me in this house, which is called by my name, and say, We are delivered; that ye may do all these abominations.
024	JER	007	011	Is this house, which is called by my name, become a den of robbers in your eyes? Behold, I, even I, have seen it, saith the LORD.
024	JER	007	012	But go ye now unto my place which was in Shiloh, where I caused my name to dwell at the first, and see what I did to it for the wickedness of my people Israel.
024	JER	007	013	And now, because ye have done all these works, saith the LORD, and I spake unto you, rising up early and speaking, but ye heard not; and I called you, but ye answered not:
024	JER	007	014	therefore will I do unto the house, which is called by my name, wherein ye trust, and unto the place which I gave to you and to your fathers, as I have done to Shiloh.
024	JER	007	015	And I will cast you out of my sight, as I have cast out all your brethren, even the whole seed of Ephraim.
024	JER	007	016	Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up cry nor prayer for them, neither make intercession to me: for I will not hear thee.
024	JER	007	017	Seest thou not what they do in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?
024	JER	007	018	The children gather wood, and the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead the dough, to make cakes to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto other gods, that they may provoke me to anger.
024	JER	007	019	Do they provoke me to anger? saith the LORD; [do they] not [provoke] themselves, to the confusion of their own faces?
024	JER	007	020	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD: Behold, mine anger and my fury shall be poured out upon this place, upon man, and upon beast, and upon the trees of the field, and upon the fruit of the ground; and it shall burn, and shall not be quenched.
024	JER	007	021	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel: Add your burnt offerings unto your sacrifices, and eat ye flesh.
024	JER	007	022	For I spake not unto your fathers, nor commanded them in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices:
024	JER	007	023	but this thing I commanded them, saying, Hearken unto my voice, and I will be your God, and ye shall be my people: and walk ye in all the way that I command you, that it may be well with you.
024	JER	007	024	But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear, but walked in [their own] counsels [and] in the stubbornness of their evil heart, and went backward and not forward.
024	JER	007	025	Since the day that your fathers came forth out of the land of Egypt unto this day, I have sent unto you all my servants the prophets, daily rising up early and sending them:
024	JER	007	026	yet they hearkened not unto me, nor inclined their ear, but made their neck stiff: they did worse than their fathers.
024	JER	007	027	And thou shalt speak all these words unto them; but they will not hearken to thee: thou shalt also call unto them; but they will not answer thee.
024	JER	007	028	And thou shalt say unto them, This is the nation that hath not hearkened to the voice of the LORD their God, nor received instruction: truth is perished, and is cut off from their mouth.
024	JER	007	029	Cut off thine hair, [O Jerusalem], and cast it away, and take up a lamentation on the bare heights; for the LORD hath rejected and forsaken the generation of his wrath.
024	JER	007	030	For the children of Judah have done that which is evil in my sight, saith the LORD: they have set their abominations in the house which is called by my name, to defile it.
024	JER	007	031	And they have built the high places of Topheth, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire; which I commanded not, neither came it into my mind.
024	JER	007	032	Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that it shall no more be called Topheth, nor The valley of the son of Hinnom, but The valley of Slaughter: for they shall bury in Topheth, till there be no place [to bury].
024	JER	007	033	And the carcases of this people shall be meat for the fowls of the heaven, and for the beasts of the earth; and none shall fray them away.
