#
# BOOK	025	LAM	Lamentations	Lamentations
025	LAM	001	001	How doth the city sit solitary, that was full of people! [how] is she become as a widow! she that was great among the nations, [and] princess among the provinces, [how] is she become tributary!
025	LAM	001	002	She weepeth sore in the night, and her tears are on her cheeks; among all her lovers she hath none to comfort her: all her friends have dealt treacherously with her, they are become her enemies.
025	LAM	001	003	Judah is gone into captivity because of affliction, and because of great servitude; she dwelleth among the heathen, she findeth no rest: all her persecutors overtook her within the straits.
025	LAM	001	004	The ways of Zion do mourn, because none come to the solemn assembly; all her gates are desolate, her priests do sigh: her virgins are afflicted, and she herself is in bitterness.
025	LAM	001	005	Her adversaries are become the head, her enemies prosper; for the LORD hath afflicted her for the multitude of her transgressions: her young children are gone into captivity before the adversary.
025	LAM	001	006	And from the daughter of Zion all her majesty is departed: her princes are become like harts that find no pasture, and they are gone without strength before the pursuer.
025	LAM	001	007	Jerusalem remembereth in the days of her affliction and of her miseries all her pleasant things that were from the days of old: when her people fell into the hand of the adversary, and none did help her, the adversaries saw her, they did mock at her desolations.
025	LAM	001	008	Jerusalem hath grievously sinned; therefore she is become as an unclean thing: all that honoured her despise her, because they have seen her nakedness: yea, she sigheth, and turneth backward.
025	LAM	001	009	Her filthiness was in her skirts; she remembered not her latter end; therefore is she come down wonderfully; she hath no comforter: behold, O LORD, my affliction; for the enemy hath magnified himself.
025	LAM	001	010	The adversary hath spread out his hand upon all her pleasant things: for she hath seen that the heathen are entered into her sanctuary, concerning whom thou didst command that they should not enter into thy congregation.
025	LAM	001	011	All her people sigh, they seek bread; they have given their pleasant things for meat to refresh the soul: see, O LORD, and behold; for I am become vile.
025	LAM	001	012	Is it nothing to you, all ye that pass by? behold, and see if there be any sorrow like unto my sorrow, which is done unto me, wherewith the LORD hath afflicted [me] in the day of his fierce anger.
025	LAM	001	013	From on high hath he sent fire into my bones, and it prevaileth against them: he hath spread a net for my feet, he hath turned me back; he hath made me desolate and faint all the day.
025	LAM	001	014	The yoke of my transgressions is bound by his hand; they are knit together, they are come up upon my neck; he hath made my strength to fail: the Lord hath delivered me into their hands, against whom I am not able to stand.
025	LAM	001	015	The Lord hath set at nought all my mighty men in the midst of me; he hath called a solemn assembly against me to crush my young men: the Lord hath trodden as in a winepress the virgin daughter of Judah.
025	LAM	001	016	For these things I weep; mine eye, mine eye runneth down with water; because the comforter that should refresh my soul is far from me: my children are desolate, because the enemy hath prevailed.
025	LAM	001	017	Zion spreadeth forth her hands; there is none to comfort her; the LORD hath commanded concerning Jacob, that they that are round about him should be his adversaries: Jerusalem is among them as an unclean thing.
025	LAM	001	018	The LORD is righteous; for I have rebelled against his commandment: hear, I pray you, all ye peoples, and behold my sorrow: my virgins and my young men are gone into captivity.
025	LAM	001	019	I called for my lovers, [but] they deceived me: my priests and mine elders gave up the ghost in the city, while they sought them meat to refresh their souls.
025	LAM	001	020	Behold, O LORD; for I am in distress; my bowels are troubled; mine heart is turned within me; for I have grievously rebelled: abroad the sword bereaveth, at home there is as death.
025	LAM	001	021	They have heard that I sigh; there is none to comfort me; all mine enemies have heard of my trouble; they are glad that thou hast done it: thou wilt bring the day that thou hast proclaimed, and they shall be like unto me.
025	LAM	001	022	Let all their wickedness come before thee; and do unto them, as thou hast done unto me for all my transgressions: for my sighs are many, and my heart is faint.
025	LAM	002	001	How hath the Lord covered the daughter of Zion with a cloud in his anger! he hath cast down from heaven unto the earth the beauty of Israel, and hath not remembered his footstool in the day of his anger.
025	LAM	002	002	The Lord hath swallowed up all the habitations of Jacob, and hath not pitied; he hath thrown down in his wrath the strong holds of the daughter of Judah; he hath brought them down to the ground: he hath profaned the kingdom and the princes thereof.
025	LAM	002	003	He hath cut off in fierce anger all the horn of Israel; he hath drawn back his right hand from before the enemy: and he hath burned up Jacob like a flaming fire, which devoureth round about.
025	LAM	002	004	He hath bent his bow like an enemy, he hath stood with his right hand as an adversary, and hath slain all that were pleasant to the eye: in the tent of the daughter of Zion he hath poured out his fury like fire.
025	LAM	002	005	The Lord is become as an enemy, he hath swallowed up Israel; he hath swallowed up all her palaces, he hath destroyed his strong holds: and he hath multiplied in the daughter of Judah mourning and lamentation.
025	LAM	002	006	And he hath violently taken away his tabernacle, as if it were of a garden; he hath destroyed his place of assembly: the LORD hath caused solemn assembly and sabbath to be forgotten in Zion, and hath despised in the indignation of his anger the king and the priest.
025	LAM	002	007	The Lord hath cast off his altar, he hath abhorred his sanctuary, he hath given up into the hand of the enemy the walls of her palaces: they have made a noise in the house of the LORD, as in the day of a solemn assembly.
025	LAM	002	008	The LORD hath purposed to destroy the wall of the daughter of Zion; he hath stretched out the line, he hath not withdrawn his hand from destroying: but he hath made the rampart and wall to lament; they languish together.
025	LAM	002	009	Her gates are sunk into the ground; he hath destroyed and broken her bars: her king and her princes are among the nations where the law is not; yea, her prophets find no vision from the LORD.
025	LAM	002	010	The elders of the daughter of Zion sit upon the ground, they keep silence; they have cast up dust upon their heads; they have girded themselves with sackcloth: the virgins of Jerusalem hang down their heads to the ground.
025	LAM	002	011	Mine eyes do fail with tears, my bowels are troubled, my liver is poured upon the earth, for the destruction of the daughter of my people; because the young children and the sucklings swoon in the streets of the city.
025	LAM	002	012	They say to their mothers, Where is corn and wine? when they swoon as the wounded in the streets of the city, when their soul is poured out into their mothers’ bosom.
025	LAM	002	013	What shall I testify unto thee? what shall I liken to thee, O daughter of Jerusalem? what shall I equal to thee, that I may comfort thee, O virgin daughter of Zion? for thy breach is great like the sea: who can heal thee?
025	LAM	002	014	Thy prophets have seen visions for thee of vanity and foolishness; and they have not discovered thine iniquity, to bring again thy captivity: but have seen for thee burdens of vanity and causes of banishment.
025	LAM	002	015	All that pass by clap their hands at thee; they hiss and wag their head at the daughter of Jerusalem, [saying]: Is this the city that men called The perfection of beauty, The joy of the whole earth?
025	LAM	002	016	All thine enemies have opened their mouth wide against thee; they hiss and gnash the teeth; they say, We have swallowed her up; certainly this is the day that we looked for; we have found, we have seen it.
025	LAM	002	017	The LORD hath done that which he devised; he hath fulfilled his word that he commanded in the days of old; he hath thrown down, and hath not pitied: and he hath caused the enemy to rejoice over thee, he hath exalted the horn of thine adversaries.
025	LAM	002	018	Their heart cried unto the Lord: O wall of the daughter of Zion, let tears run down like a river day and night; give thyself no respite; let not the apple of thine eye cease.
025	LAM	002	019	Arise, cry out in the night, at the beginning of the watches; pour out thine heart like water before the face of the Lord: lift up thy hands toward him for the life of thy young children, that faint for hunger at the top of every street.
025	LAM	002	020	See, O LORD, and behold, to whom thou hast done thus! shall the women eat their fruit, the children that are dandled in the hands? shall the priest and the prophet be slain in the sanctuary of the Lord?
025	LAM	002	021	The youth and the old man lie on the ground in the streets; my virgins and my young men are fallen by the sword: thou hast slain them in the day of thine anger; thou hast slaughtered, [and] not pitied.
025	LAM	002	022	Thou hast called, as in the day of a solemn assembly, my terrors on every side, and there was none that escaped or remained in the day of the LORD’S anger: those that I have dandled and brought up hath mine enemy consumed.
025	LAM	003	001	I AM the man that hath seen affliction by the rod of his wrath.
025	LAM	003	002	He hath led me and caused me to walk in darkness and not in light.
025	LAM	003	003	Surely against me he turneth his hand again and again all the day.
025	LAM	003	004	My flesh and my skin hath he made old; he hath broken my bones.
025	LAM	003	005	He hath builded against me, and compassed me with gall and travail.
025	LAM	003	006	He hath made me to dwell in dark places, as those that have been long dead.
025	LAM	003	007	He hath fenced me about, that I cannot go forth; he hath made my chain heavy.
025	LAM	003	008	Yea, when I cry and call for help, he shutteth out my prayer.
025	LAM	003	009	He hath fenced up my ways with hewn stone, he hath made my paths crooked.
025	LAM	003	010	He is unto me as a bear lying in wait, as a lion in secret places.
025	LAM	003	011	He hath turned aside my ways, and pulled me in pieces; he hath made me desolate.
025	LAM	003	012	He hath bent his bow, and set me as a mark for the arrow.
025	LAM	003	013	He hath caused the shafts of his quiver to enter into my reins.
025	LAM	003	014	I am become a derision to all my people; and their song all the day.
025	LAM	003	015	He hath filled me with bitterness, he hath sated me with wormwood.
025	LAM	003	016	He hath also broken my teeth with gravel stones, he hath covered me with ashes.
025	LAM	003	017	And thou hast removed my soul far off from peace; I forgat prosperity.
025	LAM	003	018	And I said, My strength is perished, and mine expectation from the LORD.
025	LAM	003	019	Remember mine affliction and my misery, the wormwood and the gall.
025	LAM	003	020	My soul hath them still in remembrance, and is bowed down within me.
025	LAM	003	021	This I recall to my mind, therefore have I hope.
025	LAM	003	022	[It is of] the LORD’S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.
025	LAM	003	023	They are new every morning; great is thy faithfulness.
025	LAM	003	024	The LORD is my portion, saith my soul; therefore will I hope in him.
025	LAM	003	025	The LORD is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him.
025	LAM	003	026	It is good that a man should hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD.
025	LAM	003	027	It is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth.
025	LAM	003	028	Let him sit alone and keep silence, because he hath laid it upon him.
025	LAM	003	029	Let him put his mouth in the dust; if so be there may he hope.
025	LAM	003	030	Let him give his cheek to him that smiteth him; let him be filled full with reproach.
025	LAM	003	031	For the Lord will not cast off for ever.
025	LAM	003	032	For though he cause grief, yet will he have compassion according to the multitude of his mercies.
025	LAM	003	033	For he doth not afflict willingly, nor grieve the children of men.
025	LAM	003	034	To crush under foot all the prisoners of the earth,
025	LAM	003	035	To turn aside the right of a man before the face of the Most High,
025	LAM	003	036	To subvert a man in his cause, the Lord approveth not.
025	LAM	003	037	Who is he that saith, and it cometh to pass, when the Lord commandeth it not?
025	LAM	003	038	Out of the mouth of the Most High cometh there not evil and good?
025	LAM	003	039	Wherefore doth a living man complain, a man for the punishment of his sins?
025	LAM	003	040	Let us search and try our ways, and turn again to the LORD.
025	LAM	003	041	Let us lift up our heart with our hands unto God in the heavens.
025	LAM	003	042	We have transgressed and have rebelled; thou hast not pardoned.
025	LAM	003	043	Thou hast covered with anger and pursued us; thou hast slain, thou hast not pitied.
025	LAM	003	044	Thou hast covered thyself with a cloud, that [our] prayer should not pass through.
025	LAM	003	045	Thou hast made us [as] the offscouring and refuse in the midst of the peoples.
025	LAM	003	046	all our enemies have opened their mouth wide against us.
025	LAM	003	047	Fear and the pit are come upon us, devastation and destruction.
025	LAM	003	048	Mine eye runneth down with rivers of water, for the destruction of the daughter of my people.
025	LAM	003	049	Mine eye poureth down, and ceaseth not, without any intermission,
025	LAM	003	050	Till the LORD look down, and behold from heaven.
025	LAM	003	051	Mine eye affecteth my soul, because of all the daughters of my city.
025	LAM	003	052	They have chased me sore like a bird, that are mine enemies without cause.
025	LAM	003	053	They have cut off my life in the dungeon, and have cast a stone upon me.
025	LAM	003	054	Waters flowed over mine head; I said, I am cut off.
025	LAM	003	055	I called upon thy name, O LORD, out of the lowest dungeon.
025	LAM	003	056	Thou heardest my voice; hide not thine ear at my breathing, at my cry.
025	LAM	003	057	Thou drewest near in the day that I called upon thee: thou saidst, Fear not.
025	LAM	003	058	O Lord, thou hast pleaded the causes of my soul; thou hast redeemed my life.
025	LAM	003	059	O LORD, thou hast seen my wrong; judge thou my cause.
025	LAM	003	060	Thou hast seen all their vengeance and all their devices against me.
025	LAM	003	061	Thou hast heard their reproach, O LORD, and all their devices against me;
025	LAM	003	062	The lips of those that rose up against me, and their imagination against me all the day.
025	LAM	003	063	Behold thou their sitting down, and their rising up; I am their song.
025	LAM	003	064	Thou wilt render unto them a recompence, O LORD, according to the work of their hands.
025	LAM	003	065	Thou wilt give them hardness of heart, thy curse unto them.
025	LAM	003	066	Thou wilt pursue them in anger, and destroy them from under the heavens of the LORD.
025	LAM	004	001	How is the gold become dim! [how] is the most pure gold changed! the stones of the sanctuary are poured out at the top of every street.
025	LAM	004	002	The precious sons of Zion, comparable to fine gold, how are they esteemed as earthen pitchers, the work of the hands of the potter!
025	LAM	004	003	Even the jackals draw out the breast, they give suck to their young ones: the daughter of my people is become cruel, like the ostriches in the wilderness.
025	LAM	004	004	The tongue of the sucking child cleaveth to the roof of his mouth for thirst: the young children ask bread, and no man breaketh it unto them.
025	LAM	004	005	They that did feed delicately are desolate in the streets: they that were brought up in scarlet embrace dung-hills.
025	LAM	004	006	For the iniquity of the daughter of my people is greater than the sin of Sodom, that was overthrown as in a moment, and no hands were laid upon her.
025	LAM	004	007	Her nobles were purer than snow, they were whiter than milk, they were more ruddy in body than rubies, their polishing was as of sapphire:
025	LAM	004	008	Their visage is blacker than a coal; they are not known in the streets: their skin cleaveth to their bones; it is withered, it is become like a stick.
025	LAM	004	009	They that be slain with the sword are better than they that be slain with hunger; for these pine away, stricken through, for want of the fruits of the field.
025	LAM	004	010	The hands of the pitiful women have sodden their own children; they were their meat in the destruction of the daughter of my people.
025	LAM	004	011	The LORD hath accomplished his fury, he hath poured out his fierce anger; and he hath kindled a fire in Zion, which hath devoured the foundations thereof.
025	LAM	004	012	The kings of the earth believed not, neither all the inhabitants of the world, that the adversary and the enemy should enter into the gates of Jerusalem.
025	LAM	004	013	[It is] because of the sins of her prophets, [and] the iniquities of her priests, that have shed the blood of the just in the midst of her.
025	LAM	004	014	They wander as blind men in the streets, that are polluted with blood, so that men cannot touch their garments.
025	LAM	004	015	Depart ye, they cried unto them, Unclean! depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, men said among the nations, They shall no more sojourn [here].
025	LAM	004	016	The anger of the LORD hath divided them; he will no more regard them: they respected not the persons of the priests, they favoured not the elders.
025	LAM	004	017	Our eyes do yet fail [in looking] for our vain help; in our watching we have watched for a nation that could not save.
025	LAM	004	018	They hunt our steps, that we cannot go in our streets: our end is near, our days are fulfilled; for our end is come.
025	LAM	004	019	Our pursuers were swifter than the eagles of the heaven: they chased us upon the mountains, they laid wait for us in the wilderness.
025	LAM	004	020	The breath of our nostrils, the anointed of the LORD, was taken in their pits; of whom we said, Under his shadow we shall live among the nations.
025	LAM	004	021	Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of Edom, that dwellest in the land of Uz: the cup shall pass through unto thee also; thou shalt be drunken, and shalt make thyself naked.
025	LAM	004	022	The punishment of thine iniquity is accomplished, O daughter of Zion; he will no more carry thee away into captivity: he will visit thine iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he will discover thy sins.
025	LAM	005	001	Remember, O what is LORD, come upon us: behold, and see our reproach.
025	LAM	005	002	Our inheritance is turned unto strangers, our houses unto aliens.
025	LAM	005	003	We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers are as widows.
025	LAM	005	004	We have drunken our water for money; our wood is sold unto us.
025	LAM	005	005	Our pursuers are upon our necks: we are weary, and have no rest.
025	LAM	005	006	We have given the hand to the Egyptians, and to the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread.
025	LAM	005	007	Our fathers have sinned, and are not; and we have borne their iniquities.
025	LAM	005	008	Servants rule over us: there is none to deliver us out of their hand.
025	LAM	005	009	We get our bread with the peril of our lives because of the sword of the wilderness.
025	LAM	005	010	Our skin is black like an oven because of the burning heat of famine.
025	LAM	005	011	They ravished the women in Zion, the maidens in the cities of Judah.
025	LAM	005	012	Princes were hanged up by their hand: the faces of elders were not honoured.
025	LAM	005	013	The young men bare the mill, and the children stumbled under the wood.
025	LAM	005	014	The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their music.
025	LAM	005	015	The joy of our heart is ceased; our dance is turned into mourning.
025	LAM	005	016	The crown is fallen from our head: woe unto us! for we have sinned.
025	LAM	005	017	For this our heart is faint; for these things our eyes are dim;
025	LAM	005	018	For the mountain of Zion, which is desolate; the foxes walk upon it.
025	LAM	005	019	Thou, O LORD, abidest for ever; thy throne is from generation to generation.
025	LAM	005	020	Wherefore dost thou forget us for ever, [and] forsake us so long time?
025	LAM	005	021	Turn thou us unto thee, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old.
025	LAM	005	022	But thou hast utterly rejected us, thou art very wroth against us.
#
# BOOK	026	EZE	Ezekiel	Ezekiel
026	EZE	001	001	Now it came to pass in the thirtieth year, in the fourth [month], in the fifth [day] of the month, as I was among the captives by the river Chebar, that the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God.
026	EZE	001	002	In the fifth [day] of the month, which was the fifth year of king Jehoiachin’s captivity,
026	EZE	001	003	the word of the LORD came expressly unto Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans by the river Chebar; and the hand of the LORD was there upon him.
026	EZE	001	004	And I looked, and, behold, a stormy wind came out of the north, a great cloud, with a fire infolding itself, and a brightness round about it, and out of the midst thereof as the colour of amber, out of the midst of the fire.
026	EZE	001	005	And out of the midst thereof came the likeness of four living creatures. And this was their appearance; they had the likeness of a man.
026	EZE	001	006	And every one had four faces, and every one of them had four wings.
026	EZE	001	007	And their feet were straight feet; and the sole of their feet was like the sole of a calf’s foot: and they sparkled like the colour of burnished brass.
026	EZE	001	008	And they had the hands of a man under their wings on their four sides: and they four had their faces and their wings [thus];
026	EZE	001	009	their wings were joined one to another; they turned not when they went; they went every one straight forward.
026	EZE	001	010	As for the likeness of their faces, they had the face of a man; and they four had the face of a lion on the right side; and they four had the face of an ox on the left side; they four had also the face of an eagle.
026	EZE	001	011	And their faces and their wings were separate above; two [wings] of every one were joined one to another, and two covered their bodies.
026	EZE	001	012	And they went every one straight forward: whither the spirit was to go, they went; they turned not when they went.
026	EZE	001	013	As for the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance was like burning coals of fire, like the appearance of torches; it went up and down among the living creatures: and the fire was bright, and out of the fire went forth lightning.
026	EZE	001	014	And the living creatures ran and returned as the appearance of a flash of lightning.
026	EZE	001	015	Now as I beheld the living creatures, behold one wheel upon the earth beside the living creatures, for each of the four faces thereof.
026	EZE	001	016	The appearance of the wheels and their work was like unto the colour of a beryl: and they four had one likeness: and their appearance and their work was as it were a wheel within a wheel.
026	EZE	001	017	When they went, they went upon their four sides: they turned not when they went.
026	EZE	001	018	As for their rings, they were high and dreadful; and they four had their rings full of eyes round about.
026	EZE	001	019	And when the living creatures went, the wheels went beside them: and when the living creatures were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up.
026	EZE	001	020	Whithersoever the spirit was to go, they went; thither was the spirit to go: and the wheels were lifted up beside them; for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels.
026	EZE	001	021	When those went, these went; and when those stood, these stood; and when those were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up beside them: for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels.
026	EZE	001	022	And over the head of the living creature there was the likeness of a firmament, like the colour of the terrible crystal, stretched forth over their heads above.
026	EZE	001	023	And under the firmament were their wings straight, the one toward the other: every one had two which covered on this side, and every one had two which covered on that side, their bodies.
026	EZE	001	024	And when they went, I heard the noise of their wings, like the noise of great waters, like the voice of the Almighty, a noise of tumult like the noise of an host: when they stood, they let down their wings.
026	EZE	001	025	And there was a voice above the firmament that was over their heads: when they stood, they let down their wings.
026	EZE	001	026	And above the firmament that was over their heads was the likeness of a throne, as the appearance of a sapphire stone: and upon the likeness of the throne was a likeness as the appearance of a man upon it above.
026	EZE	001	027	And I saw as the colour of amber, as the appearance of fire within it round about, from the appearance of his loins and upward; and from the appearance of his loins and downward I saw as it were the appearance of fire, and there was brightness round about him.
026	EZE	001	028	As the appearance of the bow that is in the cloud in the day of rain, so was the appearance of the brightness round about. This was the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the LORD. And when I saw it, I fell upon my face, and I heard a voice of one that spake.
026	EZE	002	001	And he said unto me, Son of man, stand upon thy feet, and I will speak with thee.
026	EZE	002	002	And the spirit entered into me when he spake unto me, and set me upon my feet; and I heard him that spake unto me.
026	EZE	002	003	And he said unto me, Son of man, I send thee to the children of Israel, to nations that are rebellious, which have rebelled against me: they and their fathers have transgressed against me, even unto this very day.
026	EZE	002	004	And the children are impudent and stiffhearted; I do send thee unto them: and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD.
026	EZE	002	005	And they, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear, (for they are a rebellious house,) yet shall know that there hath been a prophet among them.
026	EZE	002	006	And thou, son of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns be with thee, and thou dost dwell among scorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they be a rebellious house.
026	EZE	002	007	And thou shalt speak my words unto them, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear: for they are most rebellious.
026	EZE	002	008	But thou, son of man, hear what I say unto thee; be not thou rebellious like that rebellious house: open thy mouth, and eat that I give thee.
026	EZE	002	009	And when I looked, behold, an hand was put forth unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book was therein;
026	EZE	002	010	And he spread it before me; and it was written within and without: and there was written therein lamentations, and mourning, and woe.
026	EZE	003	001	And he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go, speak unto the house of Israel.
026	EZE	003	002	So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat the roll.
026	EZE	003	003	And he said unto me, Son of man, cause thy belly to eat, and fill thy bowels with this roll that I give thee. Then did I eat it; and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness.
026	EZE	003	004	And he said unto me, Son of man, go, get thee unto the house of Israel, and speak with my words unto them.
026	EZE	003	005	For thou art not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language, but to the house of Israel;
026	EZE	003	006	not to many peoples of a strange speech and of an hard language, whose words thou canst not understand. Surely, if I sent thee to them, they would hearken unto thee.
026	EZE	003	007	But the house of Israel will not hearken unto thee; for they will not hearken unto me: for all the house of Israel are of an hard forehead and of a stiff heart.
026	EZE	003	008	Behold, I have made thy face hard against their faces, and thy forehead hard against their foreheads.
026	EZE	003	009	As an adamant harder than flint have I made thy forehead: fear them not, neither be dismayed at their looks, though they be a rebellious house.
026	EZE	003	010	Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, all my words that I shalt speak unto thee receive in thine heart, and hear with thine ears.
026	EZE	003	011	And go, get thee to them of the captivity, unto the children of thy people, and speak unto them, and tell them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear.
026	EZE	003	012	Then the spirit lifted me up, and I heard behind me the voice of a great rushing, [saying], Blessed be the glory of the LORD from his place.
026	EZE	003	013	And [I heard] the noise of the wings of the living creatures as they touched one another, and the noise of the wheels beside them, even the noise of a great rushing.
026	EZE	003	014	So the spirit lifted me up, and took me away: and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit, and the hand of the LORD was strong upon me.
026	EZE	003	015	Then I came to them of the captivity at Tel-abib, that dwelt by the river Chebar, and to where they dwelt; and I sat there astonied among them seven days.
026	EZE	003	016	And it came to pass at the end of seven days, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
026	EZE	003	017	Son of man, I have made thee a watchman unto the house of Israel: therefore hear the word at my mouth, and give them warning from me.
026	EZE	003	018	When I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; and thou givest him not warning, nor speakest to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life; the same wicked man shall die in his iniquity; but his blood wilt I require at thine hand.
026	EZE	003	019	Yet if thou warn the wicked, and he turn not from his wickedness, nor from his wicked way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.
026	EZE	003	020	Again, when a righteous man doth turn from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, and I lay a stumblingblock before him, he shall die: because thou hast not given him warning, he shall die in his sin, and his righteous deeds which he hath done shall not be remembered; but his blood will I require at thine hand.
026	EZE	003	021	Nevertheless if thou warn the righteous man, that the righteous sin not, and he doth not sin, he shall surely live, because he took warning; and thou hast delivered thy soul.
026	EZE	003	022	And the hand of the LORD was there upon me; and he said unto me, Arise, go forth into the plain, and I will there talk with thee.
026	EZE	003	023	Then I arose, and went forth into the plain: and, behold, the glory of the LORD stood there, as the glory which I saw by the river Chebar: and I fell on my face.
026	EZE	003	024	Then the spirit entered into me, and set me upon my feet; and he spake with me, and said unto me, Go, shut thyself within thine house.
026	EZE	003	025	But thou, son of man, behold, they shall lay bands upon thee, and shall bind thee with them, and thou shalt not go out among them:
026	EZE	003	026	and I will make thy tongue cleave to the roof of thy mouth, that thou shalt be dumb, and shalt not be to them a reprover: for they are a rebellious house.
026	EZE	003	027	But when I speak with thee, I will open thy mouth, and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD: He that heareth, let him hear; and he that forbeareth, let him forbear: for they are a rebellious house.
026	EZE	004	001	Thou also, son of man, take thee a tile, and lay it before thee, and pourtray upon it a city, even Jerusalem:
026	EZE	004	002	and lay siege against it, and build forts against it, and cast up a mount against it; set camps also against it, and plant battering rams against it round about.
026	EZE	004	003	And take thou unto thee an iron pan, and set it for a wall of iron between thee and the city: and set thy face toward it, and it shall be besieged, and thou shalt lay siege against it. This shall be a sign to the house of Israel.
026	EZE	004	004	Moreover lie thou upon thy left side, and lay the iniquity of the house of Israel upon it: [according to] the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon it, thou shalt bear their iniquity.
026	EZE	004	005	For I have appointed the years of their iniquity to be unto thee a number of days, even three hundred and ninety days: so shalt thou bear the iniquity of the house of Israel.
026	EZE	004	006	And again, when thou hast accomplished these, thou shalt lie on thy right side, and shalt bear the iniquity of the house of Judah: forty days, each day for a year, have I appointed it unto thee.
026	EZE	004	007	And thou shalt set thy face toward the siege of Jerusalem, with thine arm uncovered; and thou shalt prophesy against it.
026	EZE	004	008	And, behold, I lay bands upon thee, and thou shalt not turn thee from one side to another, till thou hast accomplished the days of thy siege.
026	EZE	004	009	Take thou also unto thee wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentils, and millet, and spelt, and put them in one vessel, and make thee bread thereof; [according to] the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon thy side, even three hundred and ninety days, shalt thou eat thereof.
026	EZE	004	010	And thy meat which thou shalt eat shall be by weight, twenty shekels a day: from time to time shalt thou eat it.
