# BOOK	028	HOS	Hosea	Hosea
028	HOS	001	001	The word of the LORD that came unto Hosea the son of Beeri, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel.
028	HOS	001	002	When the LORD spake at the first by Hosea, the LORD said unto Hosea, Go, take unto thee a wife of whoredom and children of whoredom: for the land doth commit great whoredom, departing from the LORD.
028	HOS	001	003	So he went and took Gomer the daughter of Diblaim; and she conceived, and bare him a son.
028	HOS	001	004	And the LORD said unto him, Call his name Jezreel; for yet a little while, and I will avenge the blood of Jezreel upon the house of Jehu, and will cause the kingdom of the house of Israel to cease.
028	HOS	001	005	And it shall come to pass at that day, that I will break the bow of Israel in the valley of Jezreel.
028	HOS	001	006	And she conceived again, and bare a daughter. And [the LORD] said unto him, Call her name Lo-ruhamah: for I will no more have mercy upon the house of Israel, that I should in any wise pardon them.
028	HOS	001	007	But I will have mercy upon the house of Judah, and will save them by the LORD their God, and will not save them by bow, nor by sword, nor by battle, by horses, nor by horsemen.
028	HOS	001	008	Now when she had weaned Lo-ruhamah, she conceived, and bare a son.
028	HOS	001	009	And [the LORD] said, Call his name Lo-ammi: for ye are not my people, and I will not be your [God].
028	HOS	001	010	Yet the number of the children of Israel shall be as the sand of the sea, which cannot be measured nor numbered; and it shall come to pass that, in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people, it shall be said unto them, [Ye are] the sons of the living God.
028	HOS	001	011	And the children of Judah and the children of Israel shall be gathered together, and they shall appoint themselves one head, and shall go up from the land: for great shall be the day of Jezreel.
028	HOS	002	001	Say ye unto your brethren, Ammi; and to your sisters, Ruhamah.
028	HOS	002	002	Plead with your mother, plead; for she is not my wife, neither am I her husband: and let her put away her whoredoms from her face, and her adulteries from between her breasts;
028	HOS	002	003	lest I strip her naked, and set her as in the day that she was born, and make her as a wilderness, and set her like a dry land, and slay her with thirst;
028	HOS	002	004	Yea, upon her children will I have no mercy; for they be children of whoredom.
028	HOS	002	005	for their mother hath played the harlot: she that conceived them hath done shamefully: for she said, I will go after my lovers, that give me my bread and my water, my wool and my flax, mine oil and my drink.
028	HOS	002	006	Therefore, behold, I will hedge up thy way with thorns, and I will make a fence against her, that she shall not find her paths.
028	HOS	002	007	And she shall follow after her lovers, but she shall not overtake them; and she shall seek them, but shall not find them: then shall she say, I will go and return to my first husband; for then was it better with me than now.
028	HOS	002	008	For she did not know that I gave her the corn, and the wine, and the oil, and multiplied unto her silver and gold, which they used for Baal.
028	HOS	002	009	Therefore will I take back my corn in the time thereof, and my wine in the season thereof, and will pluck away my wool and my flax which should have covered her nakedness.
028	HOS	002	010	And now will I discover her lewdness in the sight of her lovers, and none shall deliver her out of mine hand.
028	HOS	002	011	I will also cause all her mirth to cease, her feasts, her new moons, and her sabbaths, and all her solemn assemblies.
028	HOS	002	012	And I will lay waste her vines and her fig trees, whereof she hath said, These are my hire that my lovers have given me: and I will make them a forest, and the beasts of the field shall eat them.
028	HOS	002	013	And I will visit upon her the days of the Baalim, unto which she burned incense; when she decked herself with her earrings and her jewels, and went after her lovers, and forgat me, saith the LORD.
028	HOS	002	014	Therefore, behold, I will allure her, and bring her into the wilderness, and speak comfortably unto her.
028	HOS	002	015	And I will give her her vineyards from thence, and the valley of Achor for a door of hope: and she shall make answer there, as in the days of her youth, and as in the day when she came up out of the land of Egypt.
028	HOS	002	016	And it shall be at that day, saith the LORD, that thou shalt call me Ishi; and shalt call me no more Baali.
028	HOS	002	017	For I will take away the names of the Baalim out of her mouth, and they shall no more be mentioned by their name.
028	HOS	002	018	And in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground: and I will break the bow and the sword and the battle out of the land, and will make them to lie down safely.
028	HOS	002	019	And I will betroth thee unto me for ever; yea, I will betroth thee unto me in righteousness, and in judgment, and in lovingkindness, and in mercies.
028	HOS	002	020	I will even betroth thee unto me in faithfulness: and thou shalt know the LORD.
028	HOS	002	021	And it shall come to pass in that day, I will answer, saith the LORD, I will answer the heavens, and they shall answer the earth;
028	HOS	002	022	and the earth shall answer the corn, and the wine, and the oil; and they shall answer Jezreel.
028	HOS	002	023	And I wilt sow her unto me in the earth; and I will have mercy upon her that had not obtained mercy; and I will say to them which were not my people, Thou art my people; and they shall say, [Thou art] my God.
028	HOS	003	001	And the LORD said unto me, Go yet, love a woman beloved of [her] friend and an adulteress, even as the LORD loveth the children of Israel, though they turn unto other gods, and love cakes of raisins.
