# BOOK	029	JOE	Joel	Joel
029	JOE	001	001	The word of the LORD that came to Joel the son of Pethuel.
029	JOE	001	002	Hear this, ye old men, and give ear, all ye inhabitants of the land. Hath this been in your days, or in the days of your fathers?
029	JOE	001	003	Tell ye your children of it, and [let] your children [tell] their children, and their children another generation.
029	JOE	001	004	That which the palmerworm hath left hath the locust eaten; and that which the locust hath left hath the cankerworm eaten; and that which the cankerworm hath left hath the caterpiller eaten.
029	JOE	001	005	Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and howl, all ye drinkers of wine, because of the sweet wine; for it is cut off from your mouth.
029	JOE	001	006	For a nation is come up upon my land, strong, and without number; his teeth are the teeth of a lion, and he hath the jaw teeth of a great lion.
029	JOE	001	007	He hath laid my vine waste, and barked my fig tree: he hath made it clean bare, and cast it away; the branches thereof are made white.
029	JOE	001	008	Lament like a virgin girded with sackcloth for the husband of her youth.
029	JOE	001	009	The meal offering and the drink offering is cut off from the house of the LORD; the priests, the LORD’S ministers, mourn.
029	JOE	001	010	The field is wasted, the land mourneth; for the corn is wasted, the new wine is dried up, the oil languisheth.
029	JOE	001	011	Be ashamed, O ye husbandmen, howl, O ye vinedressers, for the wheat and for the barley; for the harvest of the field is perished.
029	JOE	001	012	The vine is withered, and the fig tree languisheth; the pomegranate tree, the palm tree also, and the apple tree, even all the trees of the field are withered: for joy is withered away from the sons of men.
029	JOE	001	013	Gird yourselves [with sackcloth], and lament, ye priests; howl, ye ministers of the altar; come, lie all night in sackcloth, ye ministers of my God: for the meal offering and the drink offering is withholden from the house of your God.
029	JOE	001	014	Sanctify a fast, call a solemn assembly, gather the old men [and] all the inhabitants of the land unto the house of the LORD your God, and cry unto the LORD.
029	JOE	001	015	Alas for the day! for the day of the LORD is at hand, and as destruction from the Almighty shall it come,
029	JOE	001	016	Is not the meat cut off before our eyes, [yea], joy and gladness from the house of our God?
029	JOE	001	017	The seeds rot under their clods; the garners are laid desolate, the barns are broken down; for the corn is withered.
029	JOE	001	018	How do the beasts groan! the herds of cattle are perplexed, because they have no pasture; yea, the flocks of sheep are made desolate.
029	JOE	001	019	O LORD, to thee do I cry: for the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness, and the flame hath burned all the trees of the field.
029	JOE	001	020	Yea, the beasts of the field pant unto thee: for the water brooks are dried up, and the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness.
029	JOE	002	001	Blow ye the trumpet in Zion, and sound an alarm in my holy mountain; let all the inhabitants of the land tremble: for the day of the LORD cometh, for it is nigh at hand;
029	JOE	002	002	a day of darkness and gloominess, a day of clouds and thick darkness, as the dawn spread upon the mountains; a great people and a strong, there hath not been ever the like, neither shall be any more after them, even to the years of many generations.
029	JOE	002	003	A fire devoureth before them; and behind them a flame burneth: the land is as the garden of Eden before them, and behind them a desolate wilderness; yea, and none hath escaped them.
029	JOE	002	004	The appearance of them is as the appearance of horses; and as horsemen, so do they run.
029	JOE	002	005	Like the noise of chariots on the tops of the mountains do they leap, like the noise of a flame of fire that devoureth the stubble, as a strong people set in battle array.
029	JOE	002	006	At their presence the peoples are in anguish: all faces are waxed pale.
029	JOE	002	007	They run like mighty men; they climb the wall like men of war; and they march every one on his ways, and they break not their ranks.
029	JOE	002	008	Neither doth one thrust another; they march every one in his path: and they burst through the weapons, and break not off [their course].
029	JOE	002	009	They leap upon the city; they run upon the wall; they climb up into the houses; they enter in at the windows like a thief.
029	JOE	002	010	The earth quaketh before them; the heavens tremble: the sun and the moon are darkened, and the stars withdraw their shining:
029	JOE	002	011	And the LORD uttereth his voice before his army; for his camp is very great; for he is strong that executeth his word: for the day of the LORD is great and very terrible; and who can abide it?
029	JOE	002	012	Yet even now, saith the LORD, turn ye unto me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning:
029	JOE	002	013	and rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God, for he is gracious and full of compassion, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy, and repenteth him of the evil.
029	JOE	002	014	Who knoweth whether he will not turn and repent, and leave a blessing behind him, even a meal offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?
029	JOE	002	015	Blow the trumpet in Zion, sanctify a fast, call a solemn assembly:
029	JOE	002	016	gather the people, sanctify the congregation, assemble the old men, gather the children, and those that suck the breasts: let the bridegroom go forth of his chamber, and the bride out of her closet.
029	JOE	002	017	Let the priests, the ministers of the LORD, weep between the porch and the altar, and let them say, Spare thy people, O LORD, and give not thine heritage to reproach, that the nations should rule over them: wherefore should they say among the peoples, Where is their God?
029	JOE	002	018	Then was the LORD jealous for his land, and had pity on his people.
029	JOE	002	019	And the LORD answered and said unto his people, Behold, I will send you corn, and wine, and oil, and ye shall be satisfied therewith: and I will no more make you a reproach among the nations:
029	JOE	002	020	but I will remove far off from you the northern [army], and will drive him into a land barren and desolate, his forepart into the eastern sea, and his hinder part into the western sea; and his stink shall come up, and his ill savour shall come up, because he hath done great things.
029	JOE	002	021	Fear not, O land, be glad and rejoice; for the LORD hath done great things.
029	JOE	002	022	Be not afraid, ye beasts of the field; for the pastures of the wilderness do spring, for the tree beareth her fruit, the fig tree and the vine do yield their strength.
029	JOE	002	023	Be glad then, ye children of Zion, and rejoice in the LORD your God: for he giveth you the former rain in just measure, and he causeth to come down for you the rain, the former rain and the latter rain, in the first [month].
029	JOE	002	024	And the floors shall be full of wheat, and the vats shall overflow with wine and oil.
029	JOE	002	025	And I will restore to you the years that the locust hath eaten, the cankerworm, and the caterpiller, and the palmerworm, my great army which I sent among you.
029	JOE	002	026	And ye shall eat in plenty and be satisfied, and shall praise the name of the LORD your God, that hath dealt wondrously with you: and my people shall never be ashamed.
029	JOE	002	027	And ye shall know that I am in the midst of Israel, and that I am the LORD your God, and there is none else: and my people shall never be ashamed.
029	JOE	002	028	And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions:
029	JOE	002	029	and also upon the servants and upon the handmaids in those days will I pour out my spirit.
029	JOE	002	030	And I will shew wonders in the heavens and in the earth, blood, and fire, and pillars of smoke.
029	JOE	002	031	The sun shall be turned into darkness, and the moon into blood, before the great and terrible day of the LORD come.
029	JOE	002	032	And it shall come to pass, that whosoever shall call on the name of the LORD shall be delivered: for in mount Zion and in Jerusalem there shall be those that escape, as the LORD hath said, and among the remnant those whom the LORD doth call.
029	JOE	003	001	For, behold, in those days, and in that time, when I shall bring again the captivity of Judah and Jerusalem,
029	JOE	003	002	I will gather all nations, and will bring them down into the valley of Jehoshaphat; and I will plead with them there for my people and for my heritage Israel, whom they have scattered among the nations, and parted my land.
029	JOE	003	003	and they have cast lots for my people: and have given a boy for an harlot, and sold a girl for wine, that they might drink.
029	JOE	003	004	Yea, and what are ye to me, [O] Tyre, and Zidon, and all the regions of Philistia? will ye render me a recompence? and if ye recompense me, swiftly and speedily will I return your recompence upon your own head.
029	JOE	003	005	Forasmuch as ye have taken my silver and my gold, and have carried into your temples my goodly pleasant things;
029	JOE	003	006	the children also of Judah and the children of Jerusalem have ye sold unto the sons of the Grecians, that ye might remove them far from their border:
029	JOE	003	007	behold, I will stir them up out of the place whither ye have sold them, and will return your recompence upon your own head;
029	JOE	003	008	and I will sell your sons and your daughters into the hand of the children of Judah, and they shall sell them to the men of Sheba, to a nation far off: for the LORD hath spoken it.
029	JOE	003	009	Proclaim ye this among the nations; prepare war: stir up the mighty men; let all the men of war draw near, let them come up.
029	JOE	003	010	Beat your plowshares into swords, and your pruninghooks into spears: let the weak say, I am strong.
029	JOE	003	011	Haste ye, and come, all ye nations round about, and gather yourselves together: thither cause thy mighty ones to come down, O LORD.
029	JOE	003	012	Let the nations bestir themselves, and come up to the valley of Jehoshaphat: for there will I sit to judge all the nations round about.
029	JOE	003	013	Put ye in the sickle, for the harvest is ripe: come, tread ye; for the winepress is full, the vats overflow; for their wickedness is great.
029	JOE	003	014	Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision! for the day of the LORD is near in the valley of decision.
029	JOE	003	015	The sun and the moon are darkened, and the stars withdraw their shining.
029	JOE	003	016	And the LORD shall roar from Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the heavens and the earth shall shake, but the LORD will be a refuge unto his people, and a strong hold to the children of Israel.
029	JOE	003	017	So shall ye know that I am the LORD your God, dwelling in Zion my holy mountain: then shall Jerusalem be holy, and there shall no strangers pass through her any more.
029	JOE	003	018	And it shall come to pass in that day, that the mountains shall drop down sweet wine, and the hills shall flow with milk, and all the brooks of Judah shall flow with waters; and a fountain shall come forth of the house of the LORD, and shall water the valley of Shittim.
029	JOE	003	019	Egypt shall be a desolation, and Edom shall be a desolate wilderness, for the violence done to the children of Judah, because they have shed innocent blood in their land.
029	JOE	003	020	But Judah shall abide for ever, and Jerusalem from generation to generation.
029	JOE	003	021	And I will cleanse their blood that I have not cleansed: for the LORD dwelleth in Zion.
#
# BOOK	030	AMO	Amos	Amos
030	AMO	001	001	The words of Amos, who was among the herdmen of Tekoa, which he saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel, two years before the earthquake.
030	AMO	001	002	And he said, The LORD shall roar from Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the pastures of the shepherds shall mourn, and the top of Carmel shall wither.
030	AMO	001	003	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Damascus, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have threshed Gilead with threshing instruments of iron:
030	AMO	001	004	but I will send a fire into the house of Hazael, and it shall devour the palaces of Ben-hadad.
030	AMO	001	005	And I will break the bar of Damascus, and cut off the inhabitant from the valley of Aven, and him that holdeth the sceptre from the house of Eden: and the people of Syria shall go into captivity unto Kir, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	001	006	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Gaza, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they carried away captive the whole people, to deliver them up to Edom:
030	AMO	001	007	But I will send a fire on the wall of Gaza, and it shall devour the palaces thereof:
030	AMO	001	008	And I will cut off the inhabitant from Ashdod, and him that holdeth the sceptre from Ashkelon; and I will turn mine hand against Ekron, and the remnant of the Philistines shall perish, saith the Lord GOD.
030	AMO	001	009	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Tyre, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they delivered up the whole people to Edom, and remembered not the brotherly covenant:
030	AMO	001	010	but I will send a fire on the wall of Tyre, and it shall devour the palaces thereof.
030	AMO	001	011	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Edom, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because he did pursue his brother with the sword, and did cast off all pity, and his anger did tear perpetually, and he kept his wrath for ever:
030	AMO	001	012	but I will send a fire upon Teman, and it shall devour the palaces of Bozrah.
030	AMO	001	013	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of the children of Ammon, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have ripped up the women with child of Gilead, that they might enlarge their border:
030	AMO	001	014	But I will kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbath and it shall devour the palaces thereof, with shouting in the day of battle, with a tempest in the day of the whirlwind:
030	AMO	001	015	and their king shall go into captivity, he and his princes together, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	002	001	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Moab, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because he burned the bones of the king of Edom into lime:
030	AMO	002	002	but I will send a fire upon Moab, and it shall devour the palaces of Kerioth; and Moab shall die with tumult, with shouting, and with the sound of the trumpet:
030	AMO	002	003	and I will cut off the judge from the midst thereof, and will slay all the princes thereof with him, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	002	004	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Judah, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have rejected the law of the LORD, and have not kept his statutes, and their lies have caused them to err, after the which their fathers did walk:
030	AMO	002	005	but I will send a fire upon Judah, and it shall devour the palaces of Jerusalem.
030	AMO	002	006	Thus saith the LORD: For three transgressions of Israel, yea, for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have sold the righteous for silver and the needy for a pair of shoes:
030	AMO	002	007	that pant after the dust of the earth on the head of the poor, and turn aside the way of the meek: and a man and his father will go unto the [same] maid, to profane my holy name:
030	AMO	002	008	and they lay themselves down beside every altar upon clothes taken in pledge, and in the house of their God they drink the wine of such as have been fined.
030	AMO	002	009	Yet destroyed I the Amorite before them, whose height was like the height of the cedars, and he was strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed his fruit from above, and his roots from beneath.
030	AMO	002	010	Also I brought you up out of the land of Egypt, and led you forty years in the wilderness, to possess the land of the Amorite.
030	AMO	002	011	And I raised up of your sons for prophets, and of your young men for Nazirites. Is it not even thus, O ye children of Israel? saith the LORD.
030	AMO	002	012	But ye gave the Nazirites wine to drink; and commanded the prophets, saying, Prophesy not.
030	AMO	002	013	Behold, I will press [you] in your place, as a cart presseth that is full of sheaves.
030	AMO	002	014	And flight shall perish from the swift, and the strong shall not strengthen his force, neither shall the mighty deliver himself:
030	AMO	002	015	neither shall he stand that handleth the bow; and he that is swift of foot shall not deliver [himself]: neither shall he that rideth the horse deliver himself:
030	AMO	002	016	and he that is courageous among the mighty shall flee away naked in that day, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	003	001	Hear this word that the LORD hath spoken against you, O children of Israel, against the whole family which I brought up out of the land of Egypt, saying,
030	AMO	003	002	You only have I known of all the families of the earth: therefore I will visit upon you all your iniquities.
030	AMO	003	003	Shall two walk together, except they have agreed?
030	AMO	003	004	Will a lion roar in the forest, when he hath no prey? will a young lion cry out of his den, if he have taken nothing?
030	AMO	003	005	Can a bird fall in a snare upon the earth, where no gin is [set] for him? shall a snare spring up from the ground, and have taken nothing at all?
030	AMO	003	006	Shall the trumpet be blown in a city, and the people not be afraid? shalt evil befall a city, and the LORD hath not done it?
030	AMO	003	007	Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing, but he revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets.
030	AMO	003	008	The lion hath roared, who will not fear? the Lord GOD hath spoken, who can but prophesy?
030	AMO	003	009	Publish ye in the palaces at Ashdod, and in the palaces in the land of Egypt, and say, Assemble yourselves upon the mountains of Samaria, and behold what great tumults are therein, and what oppressions in the midst thereof.
030	AMO	003	010	For they know not to do right, saith the LORD, who store up violence and robbery in their palaces.
030	AMO	003	011	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD: An adversary [there shall be], even round about the land: and he shall bring down thy strength from thee, and thy palaces shall be spoiled.
030	AMO	003	012	Thus saith the LORD: As the shepherd rescueth out of the mouth of the lion two legs, or a piece of an ear; so shall the children of Israel be rescued that sit in Samaria in the corner of a couch, and on the silken cushions of a bed.
030	AMO	003	013	Hear ye, and testify against the house of Jacob, saith the Lord GOD, the God of hosts.
030	AMO	003	014	For in the day that I shall visit the transgressions of Israel upon him, I will also visit the altars of Beth-el, and the horns of the altar shall be cut off, and fall to the ground.
030	AMO	003	015	And I will smite the winter house with the summer house; and the houses of ivory shall perish, and the great houses shall have an end, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	001	Hear this word, ye kine of Bashan, that are in the mountain of Samaria, which oppress the poor, which crush the needy, which say unto their lords, Bring, and let us drink.
030	AMO	004	002	The Lord GOD hath sworn by his holiness, that, lo, the days shall come upon you, that they shall take you away with hooks, and your residue with fish hooks.
030	AMO	004	003	And ye shall go out at the breaches, every one straight before her; and ye shall cast [yourselves] into Harmon, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	004	Come to Beth-el, and transgress; to Gilgal, [and] multiply transgression; and bring your sacrifices every morning, [and] your tithes every three days;
030	AMO	004	005	and offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving of that which is leavened, and proclaim freewill offerings and publish them: for this liketh you, O ye children of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.
030	AMO	004	006	And I also have given you cleanness of teeth in all your cities, and want of bread in all your places: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	007	And I also have withholden the rain from you, when there were yet three months to the harvest: and I caused it to rain upon one city, and caused it not to rain upon another city: one piece was rained upon, and the piece whereupon it rained not withered.
030	AMO	004	008	So two or three cities wandered unto one city to drink water, and were not satisfied: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	009	I have smitten you with blasting and mildew: the multitude of your gardens and your vineyards and your fig trees and your olive trees hath the palmerworm devoured: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	010	I have sent among you the pestilence after the manner of Egypt: your young men have I slain with the sword, and have carried away your horses; and I have made the stink of your camp to come up even into your nostrils: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	011	I have overthrown [some] among you, as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah, and ye were as a brand plucked out of the burning: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	004	012	Therefore thus will I do unto thee, O Israel: [and] because I will do this unto thee, prepare to meet thy God, O Israel.
030	AMO	004	013	For, lo, he that formeth the mountains, and createth the wind, and declareth unto man what is his thought, that maketh the morning darkness, and treadeth upon the high places of the earth; the LORD, the God of hosts, is his name.
030	AMO	005	001	Hear ye this word which I take up for a lamentation over you, O house of Israel.
030	AMO	005	002	The virgin of Israel is fallen; she shall no more rise: she is cast down upon her land; there is none to raise her up.
030	AMO	005	003	For thus saith the Lord GOD: The city that went forth a thousand shall have an hundred left, and that which went forth an hundred shall have ten left, to the house of Israel.
030	AMO	005	004	For thus saith the LORD unto the house of Israel, Seek ye me, and ye shall live:
030	AMO	005	005	but seek not Beth-el, nor enter into Gilgal, and pass not to Beer-sheba: for Gilgal shall surely go into captivity, and Beth-el shall come to nought.
030	AMO	005	006	Seek the LORD, and ye shall live; lest he break out like fire in the house of Joseph, and it devour and there be none to quench it in Beth-el:
030	AMO	005	007	Ye who turn judgment to wormwood, and cast down righteousness to the earth;
030	AMO	005	008	[seek him] that maketh the Pleiades and Orion, and turneth the shadow of death into the morning, and maketh the day dark with night; that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out upon the face of the earth; the LORD is his name;
030	AMO	005	009	that bringeth sudden destruction upon the strong, so that destruction cometh upon the fortress.
030	AMO	005	010	They hate him that reproveth in the gate, and they abhor him that speaketh uprightly.
030	AMO	005	011	Forasmuch therefore as ye trample upon the poor, and take exactions from him of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink the wine thereof.
030	AMO	005	012	For I know how manifold are your transgressions, and how mighty are your sins; ye that afflict the just, that take a bribe, and that turn aside the needy in the gate [from their right].
030	AMO	005	013	Therefore he that is prudent shall keep silence in such a time; for it is an evil time.
030	AMO	005	014	Seek good, and not evil, that ye may live: and so the LORD, the God of hosts, shall be with you, as ye say.
030	AMO	005	015	Hate the evil, and love the good, and establish judgment in the gate: it may be that the LORD, the God of hosts, will be gracious unto the remnant of Joseph.
030	AMO	005	016	Therefore thus saith the LORD, the God of hosts, the Lord: Wailing shall be in all the broad ways; and they shall say in all the streets, Alas! alas! and they shall call the husbandman to mourning, and such as are skilful of lamentation to wailing.
030	AMO	005	017	And in all vineyards shall be wailing: for I will pass through the midst of thee, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	005	018	Woe unto you that desire the day of the LORD! wherefore would ye have the day of the LORD? it is darkness, and not light.
030	AMO	005	019	As if a man did flee from a lion, and a bear met him; or went into the house and leaned his hand on the wall, and a serpent bit him.
030	AMO	005	020	Shall not the day of the LORD be darkness, and not light? even very dark, and no brightness in it?
030	AMO	005	021	I hate, I despise your feasts, and I will take no delight in your solemn assemblies.
030	AMO	005	022	Yea, though ye offer me your burnt offerings and meal offerings, I will not accept them: neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat beasts.
030	AMO	005	023	Take thou away from me the noise of thy songs; for I will not hear the melody of thy viols.
030	AMO	005	024	But let judgment roll down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.
030	AMO	005	025	Did ye bring unto me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, O house of Israel?
030	AMO	005	026	Yea, ye have borne Siccuth your king and Chiun your images, the star of your god, which ye made to yourselves.
030	AMO	005	027	Therefore will I cause you to go into captivity beyond Damascus, saith the LORD, whose name is the God of hosts.
030	AMO	006	001	Woe to them that are at ease in Zion, and to them that are secure in the mountain of Samaria, the notable men of the chief of the nations, to whom the house of Israel come!
030	AMO	006	002	Pass ye unto Calneh, and see; and from thence go ye to Hamath the great: then go down to Gath of the Philistines: be they better than these kingdoms? or is their border greater than your border?
030	AMO	006	003	Ye that put far away the evil day, and cause the seat of violence to come near;
030	AMO	006	004	that lie upon beds of ivory, and stretch themselves upon their couches, and eat the lambs out of the flock, and the calves out of the midst of the stall;
030	AMO	006	005	that sing idle songs to the sound of the viol; that devise for themselves instruments of music, like David;
030	AMO	006	006	that drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments; but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph.
030	AMO	006	007	Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the revelry of them that stretched themselves shall pass away.
030	AMO	006	008	The Lord GOD hath sworn by himself, saith the LORD, the God of hosts; I abhor the excellency of Jacob, and hate his palaces: therefore will I deliver up the city with all that is therein.
030	AMO	006	009	And it shall come to pass, if there remain ten men in one house, that they shall die.
030	AMO	006	010	And when a man’s uncle shall take him up, even he that burneth him, to bring out the bones out of the house, and shall say unto him that is in the innermost parts of the house, Is there yet any with thee? and he shall say, No; then shall he say, Hold thy peace; for we may not make mention of the name of the LORD.
030	AMO	006	011	For, behold, the LORD commandeth, and the great house shall be smitten with breaches, and the little house with clefts.
030	AMO	006	012	Shall horses run upon the rock? will one plow [there] with oxen? that ye have turned judgment into gall, and the fruit of righteousness into wormwood:
030	AMO	006	013	ye which rejoice in a thing of nought, which say, Have we not taken to us horns by our own strength?
030	AMO	006	014	For, behold, I will raise up against you a nation, O house of Israel, saith the LORD, the God of hosts; and they shall afflict you from the entering in of Hamath unto the brook of the Arabah.
030	AMO	007	001	Thus the Lord GOD shewed me: and, behold, he formed locusts in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and, lo, it was the latter growth after the king’s mowings.
030	AMO	007	002	And it came to pass that when they made an end of eating the grass of the land, then I said, O Lord GOD, forgive, I beseech thee: how shall Jacob stand? for he is small.
030	AMO	007	003	The LORD repented concerning this: It shall not be, saith the LORD.
030	AMO	007	004	Thus the Lord GOD shewed me: and, behold, the Lord GOD called to contend by fire; and it devoured the great deep, and would have eaten up the land.
030	AMO	007	005	Then said I, O Lord GOD, cease, I beseech thee: how shall Jacob stand? for he is small.
030	AMO	007	006	The LORD repented concerning this: This also shall not be, saith the Lord GOD.
030	AMO	007	007	Thus he shewed me: and, behold, the Lord stood beside a wall made by a plumbline, with a plumbline in his hand.
030	AMO	007	008	And the LORD said unto me, Amos, what seest thou? And I said, A plumbline. Then said the Lord, Behold, I will set a plumbline in the midst of my people Israel; I will not again pass by them any more:
030	AMO	007	009	and the high places of Isaac shall be desolate, and the sanctuaries of Israel shall be laid waste; and I will rise against the house of Jeroboam with the sword.
030	AMO	007	010	Then Amaziah the priest of Beth-el sent to Jeroboam king of Israel, saying, Amos hath conspired against thee in the midst of the house of Israel: the land is not able to bear all his words.
030	AMO	007	011	For thus Amos saith, Jeroboam shall die by the sword, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of his land.
030	AMO	007	012	Also Amaziah said unto Amos, O thou seer, go, flee thee away into the land of Judah, and there eat bread, and prophesy there:
030	AMO	007	013	but prophesy not again any more at Beth-el: for it is the king’s sanctuary, and it is a royal house.
030	AMO	007	014	Then answered Amos, and said to Amaziah, I was no prophet, neither was I a prophet’s son; but I was an herdman, and a dresser of sycomore trees:
030	AMO	007	015	and the LORD took me from following the flock, and the LORD said unto me, Go, prophesy unto my people Israel.
030	AMO	007	016	Now therefore hear thou the word of the LORD: Thou sayest, Prophesy not against Israel, and drop not [thy word] against the house of Isaac;
030	AMO	007	017	therefore thus saith the LORD: Thy wife shall be an harlot in the city, and thy sons and thy daughters shall fall by the sword, and thy land shall be divided by line; and thou thyself shalt die in a land that is unclean, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of his land.
