# BOOK	034	NAH	Nahum	Nahum
034	NAH	001	001	The burden of Nineveh. The book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite.
034	NAH	001	002	The LORD is a jealous God and avengeth; the LORD avengeth and is full of wrath; the LORD taketh vengeance on his adversaries, and he reserveth [wrath] for his enemies.
034	NAH	001	003	The LORD is slow to anger, and great in power, and will by no means clear [the guilty]: the LORD hath his way in the whirlwind and in the storm, and the clouds are the dust of his feet.
034	NAH	001	004	He rebuketh the sea, and maketh it dry, and drieth up all the rivers: Bashan languisheth, and Carmel, and the flower of Lebanon languisheth.
034	NAH	001	005	The mountains quake at him, and the hills melt; and the earth is upheaved at his presence, yea, the world, and all that dwell therein.
034	NAH	001	006	Who can stand before his indignation? and who can abide in the fierceness of his anger? his fury is poured out like fire, and the rocks are broken asunder by him.
034	NAH	001	007	The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that put their trust in him.
034	NAH	001	008	But with an overrunning flood he will make a full end of the place thereof, and will pursue his enemies into darkness.
034	NAH	001	009	What do ye imagine against the LORD? he will make a full end: affliction shall not rise up the second time.
034	NAH	001	010	For though they be like tangled thorns, told be drenched as it were in their drink, they shall be devoured utterly as dry stubble.
034	NAH	001	011	There is one gone forth out of thee, that imagineth evil against the LORD, that counselleth wickedness.
034	NAH	001	012	Thus saith the LORD: Though they be in full strength, and likewise many, even so shall they be cut down, and he shall pass away. Though I have afflicted thee, I will afflict thee no more.
034	NAH	001	013	And now will I break his yoke from off thee, and will burst thy bonds in sunder.
034	NAH	001	014	And the LORD hath given commandment concerning thee, that no more of thy name be sown: out of the house of thy gods will I cut off the graven image and the molten image; I will make thy grave; for thou art vile.
034	NAH	001	015	Behold, upon the mountains the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace! Keep thy feasts, O Judah, perform thy vows: for the wicked one shall no more pass through thee; he is utterly cut off.
034	NAH	002	001	He that dasheth in pieces is come up before thy face: keep the munition, watch the way, make thy loins strong, fortify thy power mightily.
034	NAH	002	002	For the LORD bringeth again the excellency of Jacob, as the excellency of Israel: for the emptiers have emptied them out, and marred their vine branches.
034	NAH	002	003	The shield of his mighty men is made red, the valiant men are in scarlet: the chariots flash with steel in the day of his preparation, and the spears are shaken terribly.
034	NAH	002	004	The chariots rage in the streets, they justle one against another in the broad ways: the appearance of them is like torches, they run like the lightnings.
034	NAH	002	005	He remembereth his worthies: they stumble in their march; they make haste to the wall thereof, and the mantelet is prepared.
034	NAH	002	006	The gates of the rivers are opened, and the palace is dissolved.
034	NAH	002	007	And Huzzab is uncovered, she is carried away, and her handmaids mourn as with the voice of doves, tabering upon their breasts.
034	NAH	002	008	But Nineveh hath been from of old like a pool of water: yet they flee away; Stand, stand, [they cry]; but none looketh back.
034	NAH	002	009	Take ye the spoil of silver, take the spoil of gold: for there is none end of the store, the glory of all pleasant furniture.
034	NAH	002	010	She is empty, and void, and waste: and the heart melteth, and the knees smite together, and anguish is in all loins, and the faces of them all are waxed pale.
034	NAH	002	011	Where is the den of the lions, and the feeding place of the young lions, where the lion [and] the lioness walked, the lion’s whelp, and none made them afraid?
034	NAH	002	012	The lion did tear in pieces enough for his whelps, and strangled for his lionesses, and filled his caves with prey, and his dens with ravin.
034	NAH	002	013	Behold, I am against thee, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword shall devour thy young lions: and I will cut off thy prey from the earth, and the voice of thy messengers shall no more be heard.
034	NAH	003	001	Woe to the bloody city! it is all full of lies and rapine; the prey departeth not.
034	NAH	003	002	The noise of the whip, and the noise of the rattling of wheels; and pransing horses, and jumping chariots;
034	NAH	003	003	the horseman mounting, and the flashing sword, and the glittering spear; and a multitude of slain, and a great heap of carcases: and there is none end of the corpses; they stumble upon their corpses:
034	NAH	003	004	because of the multitude of the whoredoms of the well favoured harlot, the mistress of witchcrafts, that selleth nations through her whoredoms, and families through her witchcrafts.
034	NAH	003	005	Behold, I am against thee, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will discover thy skirts upon thy face; and I will shew the nations thy nakedness, and the kingdoms thy shame.
034	NAH	003	006	And I will cast abominable filth upon thee, and make thee vile, and will set thee as a gazingstock.
034	NAH	003	007	And it shall come to pass, that all they that look upon thee shall flee from thee, and say, Nineveh is laid waste: who will bemoan her? whence shall I seek comforters for thee?
034	NAH	003	008	Art thou better than No-amon, that was situate among the rivers, that had the waters round about her; whose rampart was the sea, [and] her wall was of the sea?
034	NAH	003	009	Ethiopia and Egypt were her strength, and it was infinite; Put and Lubim were thy helpers.
034	NAH	003	010	Yet was she carried away, she went into captivity: her young children also were dashed in pieces at the top of all the streets: and they cast lots for her honourable men, and all her great men were bound in chains.
034	NAH	003	011	Thou also shalt be drunken, thou shalt be hid; thou also shalt seek a strong hold because of the enemy.
034	NAH	003	012	All thy fortresses shall be [like] fig trees with the firstripe figs: if they be shaken, they fall into the mouth of the eater.
034	NAH	003	013	Behold, thy people in the midst of thee are women; the gates of thy land are set wide open unto thine enemies: the fire hath devoured thy bars.
034	NAH	003	014	Draw thee water for the siege, strengthen thy fortresses: go into the clay, and tread the mortar, make strong the brickkiln.
034	NAH	003	015	There shall the fire devour thee; the sword shall cut thee off, it shall devour thee like the cankerworm: make thyself many as the cankerworm, make thyself many as the locust.
034	NAH	003	016	Thou hast multiplied thy merchants above the stars of heaven: the cankerworm spoileth, and flieth away.
034	NAH	003	017	Thy crowned are as the locusts, and thy marshals as the swarms of grasshoppers, which camp in the hedges in the cold day, but when the sun ariseth they flee away, and their place is not known where they are.
034	NAH	003	018	Thy shepherds slumber, O king of Assyria: thy worthies are at rest: thy people are scattered upon the mountains, and there is none to gather them.
034	NAH	003	019	There is no assuaging of thy hurt; thy wound is grievous: all that hear the bruit of thee clap the hands over thee; for upon whom hath not thy wickedness passed continually?
