# BOOK	040	MAT	Matthew	Matthew
040	MAT	001	001	The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.
040	MAT	001	002	Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judah and his brethren;
040	MAT	001	003	and Judah begat Perez and Zerah of Tamar; and Perez begat Hezron; and Hezron begat Ram;
040	MAT	001	004	and Ram begat Amminadab; and Amminadab begat Nahshon; and Nahshon begat Salmon;
040	MAT	001	005	and Salmon begat Boaz of Rahab; and Boaz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;
040	MAT	001	006	and Jesse begat David the king. And David begat Solomon of her [that had been the wife] of Uriah;
040	MAT	001	007	and Solomon begat Rehoboam; and Rehoboam begat Abijah; and Abijah begat Asa;
040	MAT	001	008	and Asa begat Jehoshaphat; and Jehoshaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Uzziah;
040	MAT	001	009	and Uzziah begat Jotham; and Jotham begat Ahaz; and Ahaz begat Hezekiah;
040	MAT	001	010	and Hezekiah begat Manasseh; and Manasseh begat Amon; and Amon begat Josiah;
040	MAT	001	011	and Josiah begat Jechoniah and his brethren, at the time of the carrying away to Babylon.
040	MAT	001	012	And after the carrying away to Babylon, Jechoniah begat Shealtiel; and Shealtiel begat Zerubbabel;
040	MAT	001	013	and Zerubbabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor;
040	MAT	001	014	and Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;
040	MAT	001	015	and Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob;
040	MAT	001	016	and Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.
040	MAT	001	017	So all the generations from Abraham unto David are fourteen generations; and from David unto the carrying away to Babylon fourteen generations; and from the carrying away to Babylon unto the Christ fourteen generations.
040	MAT	001	018	Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When his mother Mary had been betrothed to Joseph, before they came together she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.
040	MAT	001	019	And Joseph her husband, being a righteous man, and not willing to make her a public example, was minded to put her away privily.
040	MAT	001	020	But when he thought on these things, behold, an angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.
040	MAT	001	021	And she shall bring forth a son; and thou shalt call his name JESUS; for it is he that shall save his people from their sins.
040	MAT	001	022	Now all this is come to pass, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through the prophet, saying,
040	MAT	001	023	Behold, the virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, And they shall call his name Immanuel; which is, being interpreted, God with us.
040	MAT	001	024	And Joseph arose from his sleep, and did as the angel of the Lord commanded him, and took unto him his wife;
040	MAT	001	025	and knew her not till she had brought forth a son: and he called his name JESUS.
040	MAT	002	001	Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem,
040	MAT	002	002	saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we saw his star in the east, and are come to worship him.
040	MAT	002	003	And when Herod the king heard it, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.
040	MAT	002	004	And gathering together all the chief priests and scribes of the people, he inquired of them where the Christ should be born.
040	MAT	002	005	And they said unto him, In Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is written by the prophet,
040	MAT	002	006	And thou Bethlehem, land of Judah, Art in no wise least among the princes of Judah: For out of thee shall come forth a governor, Which shall be shepherd of my people Israel.
040	MAT	002	007	Then Herod privily called the wise men, and learned of them carefully what time the star appeared.
040	MAT	002	008	And he sent them to Bethlehem, and said, Go and search out carefully concerning the young child; and when ye have found [him], bring me word, that I also may come and worship him.
040	MAT	002	009	And they, having heard the king, went their way; and lo, the star, which they saw in the east, went before them, till it came and stood over where the young child was.
040	MAT	002	010	And when they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceeding great joy.
040	MAT	002	011	And they came into the house and saw the young child with Mary his mother; and they fell down and worshipped him; and opening their treasures they offered unto him gifts, gold and frankincense and myrrh.
040	MAT	002	012	And being warned [of God] in a dream that they should not return to Herod, they departed into their own country another way.
040	MAT	002	013	Now when they were departed, behold, an angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a dream, saying, Arise and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and be thou there until I tell thee: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.
040	MAT	002	014	And he arose and took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt;
040	MAT	002	015	and was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt did I call my son.
040	MAT	002	016	Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the male children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the borders thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had carefully learned of the wise men.
040	MAT	002	017	Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremiah the prophet, saying,
040	MAT	002	018	A voice was heard in Ramah, Weeping and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children; And she would not be comforted, because they are not.
040	MAT	002	019	But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of the Lord appeareth in a dream to Joseph in Egypt,
040	MAT	002	020	saying, Arise and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel: for they are dead that sought the young child’s life.
040	MAT	002	021	And he arose and took the young child and his mother, and came into the land of Israel.
040	MAT	002	022	But when he heard that Archelaus was reigning over Judaea in the room of his father Herod, he was afraid to go thither; and being warned [of God] in a dream, he withdrew into the parts of Galilee,
040	MAT	002	023	and came and dwelt in a city called Nazareth: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophets, that he should be called a Nazarene.
040	MAT	003	001	And in those days cometh John the Baptist, preaching in the wilderness of Judaea,
040	MAT	003	002	saying, Repent ye; for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.
040	MAT	003	003	For this is he that was spoken of by Isaiah the prophet, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make ye ready the way of the Lord, Make his paths straight.
040	MAT	003	004	Now John himself had his raiment of camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins; and his food was locusts and wild honey.
040	MAT	003	005	Then went out unto him Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan;
040	MAT	003	006	and they were baptized of him in the river Jordan, confessing their sins.
040	MAT	003	007	But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming to his baptism, he said unto them, Ye offspring of vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?
040	MAT	003	008	Bring forth therefore fruit worthy of repentance:
040	MAT	003	009	and think not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to our father: for I say unto you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.
040	MAT	003	010	And even now is the axe laid unto the root of the trees: every tree therefore that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.
040	MAT	003	011	I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance: but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost and [with] fire:
040	MAT	003	012	whose fan is in his hand, and he will throughly cleanse his threshing-floor; and he will gather his wheat into the garner, but the chaff he will burn up with unquenchable fire.
040	MAT	003	013	Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to the Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him.
040	MAT	003	014	But John would have hindered him, saying, I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?
040	MAT	003	015	But Jesus answering said unto him, Suffer [it] now: for thus it becometh us to fulfill all righteousness. Then he suffereth him.
040	MAT	003	016	And Jesus, when he was baptized, went up straightway from the water: and lo, the heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending as a dove, and coming upon him;
040	MAT	003	017	and lo, a voice out of the heavens, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.
040	MAT	004	001	Then was Jesus led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.
040	MAT	004	002	And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he afterward hungered.
040	MAT	004	003	And the tempter came and said unto him, If thou art the Son of God, command that these stones become bread.
040	MAT	004	004	But he answered and said, It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.
040	MAT	004	005	Then the devil taketh him into the holy city; and he set him on the pinnacle of the temple,
040	MAT	004	006	and saith unto him, If thou art the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: And on their hands they shall bear thee up, Lest haply thou dash thy foot against a stone.
040	MAT	004	007	Jesus said unto him, Again it is written, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.
040	MAT	004	008	Again, the devil taketh him unto an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;
040	MAT	004	009	and he said unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me.
040	MAT	004	010	Then saith Jesus unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.
040	MAT	004	011	Then the devil leaveth him; and behold, angels came and ministered unto him.
040	MAT	004	012	Now when he heard that John was delivered up, he withdrew into Galilee;
040	MAT	004	013	and leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is by the sea, in the borders of Zebulun and Naphtali:
040	MAT	004	014	that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the prophet, saying,
040	MAT	004	015	The land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali, Toward the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles,
040	MAT	004	016	The people which sat in darkness Saw a great light, And to them which sat in the region and shadow of death, To them did light spring up.
040	MAT	004	017	From that time began Jesus to preach, and to say, Repent ye; for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.
040	MAT	004	018	And walking by the sea of Galilee, he saw two brethren, Simon who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea; for they were fishers.
040	MAT	004	019	And he saith unto them, Come ye after me, and I will make you fishers of men.
040	MAT	004	020	And they straightway left the nets, and followed him.
040	MAT	004	021	And going on from thence he saw other two brethren, James the [son] of Zebedee, and John his brother, in the boat with Zebedee their father, mending their nets; and he called them.
040	MAT	004	022	And they straightway left the boat and their father, and followed him.
040	MAT	004	023	And Jesus went about in all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of disease and all manner of sickness among the people.
040	MAT	004	024	And the report of him went forth into all Syria: and they brought unto him all that were sick, holden with divers diseases and torments, possessed with devils, and epileptic, and palsied; and he healed them.
040	MAT	004	025	And there followed him great multitudes from Galilee and Decapolis and Jerusalem and Judaea and [from] beyond Jordan.
040	MAT	005	001	And seeing the multitudes, he went up into the mountain: and when he had sat down, his disciples came unto him:
040	MAT	005	002	and he opened his mouth and taught them, saying,
040	MAT	005	003	Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	005	004	Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.
040	MAT	005	005	Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.
040	MAT	005	006	Blessed are they that hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.
040	MAT	005	007	Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.
040	MAT	005	008	Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.
040	MAT	005	009	Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called sons of God.
040	MAT	005	010	Blessed are they that have been persecuted for righteousness’ sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	005	011	Blessed are ye when [men] shall reproach you, and persecute you, and say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake.
040	MAT	005	012	Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you.
040	MAT	005	013	Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost its savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out and trodden under foot of men.
040	MAT	005	014	Ye are the light of the world. A city set on a hill cannot be hid.
040	MAT	005	015	Neither do [men] light a lamp, and put it under the bushel, but on the stand; and it shineth unto all that are in the house.
040	MAT	005	016	Even so let your light shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.
040	MAT	005	017	Think not that I came to destroy the law or the prophets: I came not to destroy, but to fulfill.
040	MAT	005	018	For verily I say unto you, Till heaven and earth pass away, one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass away from the law, till all things be accomplished.
040	MAT	005	019	Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, shall be called least in the kingdom of heaven: but whosoever shall do and teach them, he shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	005	020	For I say unto you, that except your righteousness shall exceed [the righteousness] of the scribes and Pharisees, ye shall in no wise enter into the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	005	021	Ye have heard that it was said to them of old time, Thou shalt not kill; and whosoever shall kill shall be in danger of the judgment:
040	MAT	005	022	but I say unto you, that every one who is angry with his brother shall be in danger of the judgment; and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council; and whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of the hell of fire.
040	MAT	005	023	If therefore thou art offering thy gift at the altar, and there rememberest that thy brother hath aught against thee,
040	MAT	005	024	leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way, first be reconciled to thy brother, and then come and offer thy gift.
040	MAT	005	025	Agree with thine adversary quickly, whiles thou art with him in the way; lest haply the adversary deliver thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the officer, and thou be cast into prison.
040	MAT	005	026	Verily I say unto thee, Thou shalt by no means come out thence, till thou have paid the last farthing.
040	MAT	005	027	Ye have heard that it was said, Thou shalt not commit adultery:
040	MAT	005	028	but I say unto you, that every one that looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.
040	MAT	005	029	And if thy right eye causeth thee to stumble, pluck it out, and cast it from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not thy whole body be cast into hell.
040	MAT	005	030	And if thy right hand causeth thee to stumble, cut it off, and cast it from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not thy whole body go into hell.
040	MAT	005	031	It was said also, Whosoever shall put away his wife, let him give her a writing of divorcement:
040	MAT	005	032	but I say unto you, that every one that putteth away his wife, saving for the cause of fornication, maketh her an adulteress: and whosoever shall marry her when she is put away committeth adultery.
040	MAT	005	033	Again, ye have heard that it was said to them of old time, Thou shalt not forswear thyself, but shalt perform unto the Lord thine oaths:
040	MAT	005	034	but I say unto you, Swear not at all; neither by the heaven, for it is the throne of God;
040	MAT	005	035	nor by the earth, for it is the footstool of his feet; nor by Jerusalem, for it is the city of the great King.
040	MAT	005	036	Neither shalt thou swear by thy head, for thou canst not make one hair white or black.
040	MAT	005	037	But let your speech be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: and whatsoever is more than these is of the evil [one].
040	MAT	005	038	Ye have heard that it was said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth:
040	MAT	005	039	but I say unto you, Resist not him that is evil: but whosoever smiteth thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also.
040	MAT	005	040	And if any man would go to law with thee, and take away thy coat, let him have thy cloke also.
040	MAT	005	041	And whosoever shall compel thee to go one mile, go with him twain.
040	MAT	005	042	Give to him that asketh thee, and from him that would borrow of thee turn not thou away.
040	MAT	005	043	Ye have heard that it was said, Thou shalt love thy neighbour, and hate thine enemy:
040	MAT	005	044	but I say unto you, Love your enemies, and pray for them that persecute you;
040	MAT	005	045	that ye may be sons of your Father which is in heaven: for he maketh his sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sendeth rain on the just and the unjust.
040	MAT	005	046	For if ye love them that love you, what reward have ye? do not even the publicans the same?
040	MAT	005	047	And if ye salute your brethren only, what do ye more [than others]? do not even the Gentiles the same?
040	MAT	005	048	Ye therefore shall be perfect, as your heavenly Father is perfect.
040	MAT	006	001	Take heed that ye do not your righteousness before men, to be seen of them: else ye have no reward with your Father which is in heaven.
040	MAT	006	002	When therefore thou doest alms, sound not a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men. Verily I say unto you, They have received their reward.
040	MAT	006	003	But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth:
040	MAT	006	004	that thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret shall recompense thee.
040	MAT	006	005	And when ye pray, ye shall not be as the hypocrites: for they love to stand and pray in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men. Verily I say unto you, They have received their reward.
040	MAT	006	006	But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thine inner chamber, and having shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret, and thy Father which seeth in secret shall recompense thee.
040	MAT	006	007	And in praying use not vain repetitions, as the Gentiles do: for they think that they shall be heard for their much speaking.
040	MAT	006	008	Be not therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of, before ye ask him.
040	MAT	006	009	After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.
040	MAT	006	010	Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done, as in heaven, so on earth.
040	MAT	006	011	Give us this day our daily bread.
040	MAT	006	012	And forgive us our debts, as we also have forgiven our debtors.
040	MAT	006	013	And bring us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil [one].
040	MAT	006	014	For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.
040	MAT	006	015	But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.
040	MAT	006	016	Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may be seen of men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have received their reward.
040	MAT	006	017	But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thy head, and wash thy face;
040	MAT	006	018	that thou be not seen of men to fast, but of thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall recompense thee.
040	MAT	006	019	Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon the earth, where moth and rust doth consume, and where thieves break through and steal:
040	MAT	006	020	but lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth consume, and where thieves do not break through nor steal:
040	MAT	006	021	for where thy treasure is, there will thy heart be also.
040	MAT	006	022	The lamp of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.
040	MAT	006	023	But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness. If therefore the light that is in thee be darkness, how great is the darkness!
040	MAT	006	024	No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.
040	MAT	006	025	Therefore I say unto you, Be not anxious for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on. Is not the life more than the food, and the body than the raiment?
040	MAT	006	026	Behold the birds of the heaven, that they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; and your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are not ye of much more value than they?
040	MAT	006	027	And which of you by being anxious can add one cubit unto his stature?
040	MAT	006	028	And why are ye anxious concerning raiment? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin:
040	MAT	006	029	yet I say unto you, that even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.
040	MAT	006	030	But if God doth so clothe the grass of the field, which today is, and tomorrow is cast into the oven, [shall he] not much more [clothe] you, O ye of little faith?
040	MAT	006	031	Be not therefore anxious, saying, What shall we eat? or, What shall drink? or, Wherewithal shall we be clothed?
040	MAT	006	032	For after all these things do the Gentiles seek; for your heavenly Father knoweth that ye have need of all these things.
040	MAT	006	033	But seek ye first his kingdom, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.
040	MAT	006	034	Be not therefore anxious for the morrow: for the morrow will be anxious for itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.
040	MAT	007	001	Judge not, that ye be not judged.
040	MAT	007	002	For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured unto you.
040	MAT	007	003	And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye?
040	MAT	007	004	Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me cast out the mote out of thine eye; and lo, the beam is in thine own eye?
040	MAT	007	005	Thou hypocrite, cast out first the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye.
040	MAT	007	006	Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, neither cast your pearls before the swine, lest haply they trample them under their feet, and turn and rend you.
040	MAT	007	007	Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:
040	MAT	007	008	for every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.
040	MAT	007	009	Or what man is there of you, who, if his son shall ask him for a loaf, will give him a stone;
040	MAT	007	010	or if he shall ask for a fish, will give him a serpent?
040	MAT	007	011	If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?
040	MAT	007	012	All things therefore whatsoever ye would that men should do unto you, even so do ye also unto them: for this is the law and the prophets.
040	MAT	007	013	Enter ye in by the narrow gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many be they that enter in thereby.
040	MAT	007	014	For narrow is the gate, and straitened the way, that leadeth unto life, and few be they that find it.
040	MAT	007	015	Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly are ravening wolves.
040	MAT	007	016	By their fruits ye shall know them. Do [men] gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?
040	MAT	007	017	Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but the corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit.
040	MAT	007	018	A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.
040	MAT	007	019	Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.
040	MAT	007	020	Therefore by their fruits ye shall know them.
040	MAT	007	021	Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.
040	MAT	007	022	Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy by thy name, and by thy name cast out devils, and by thy name do many mighty works?
040	MAT	007	023	And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.
040	MAT	007	024	Every one therefore which heareth these words of mine, and doeth them, shall be likened unto a wise man, which built his house upon the rock:
040	MAT	007	025	and the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon the rock.
040	MAT	007	026	And every one that heareth these words of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand:
040	MAT	007	027	and the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and smote upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall thereof.
040	MAT	007	028	And it came to pass, when Jesus ended these words, the multitudes were astonished at his teaching:
040	MAT	007	029	for he taught them as [one] having authority, and not as their scribes.
040	MAT	008	001	And when he was come down from the mountain, great multitudes followed him.
040	MAT	008	002	And behold, there came to him a leper and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.
040	MAT	008	003	And he stretched forth his hand, and touched him, saying, I will; be thou made clean. And straightway his leprosy was cleansed.
040	MAT	008	004	And Jesus saith unto him, See thou tell no man; but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.
040	MAT	008	005	And when he was entered into Capernaum, there came unto him a centurion, beseeching him,
040	MAT	008	006	and saying, Lord, my servant lieth in the house sick of the palsy, grievously tormented.
040	MAT	008	007	And he saith unto him, I will come and heal him.
040	MAT	008	008	And the centurion answered and said, Lord, I am not worthy that thou shouldest come under my roof: but only say the word, and my servant shall be healed.
040	MAT	008	009	For I also am a man under authority, having under myself soldiers: and I say to this one, Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth it.
040	MAT	008	010	And when Jesus heard it, he marveled, and said to them that followed, Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.
040	MAT	008	011	And I say unto you, that many shall come from the east and the west, and shall sit down with Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of heaven:
040	MAT	008	012	but the sons of the kingdom shall be cast forth into the outer darkness: there shall be the weeping and gnashing of teeth.
040	MAT	008	013	And Jesus said unto the centurion, Go thy way; as thou hast believed, [so] be it done unto thee. And the servant was healed in that hour.
040	MAT	008	014	And when Jesus was come into Peter’s house, he saw his wife’s mother lying sick of a fever.
040	MAT	008	015	And he touched her hand, and the fever left her; and she arose, and ministered unto him.
040	MAT	008	016	And when even was come, they brought unto him many possessed with devils: and he cast out the spirits with a word, and healed all that were sick:
040	MAT	008	017	that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the prophet, saying, Himself took our infirmities, and bare our diseases.
040	MAT	008	018	Now when Jesus saw great multitudes about him, he gave commandment to depart unto the other side.
040	MAT	008	019	And there came a scribe, and said unto him, Master, I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.
040	MAT	008	020	And Jesus saith unto him, The foxes have holes, and the birds of the heaven [have] nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head.
040	MAT	008	021	And another of the disciples said unto him, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father.
040	MAT	008	022	But Jesus saith unto him, Follow me; and leave the dead to bury their own dead.
040	MAT	008	023	And when he was entered into a boat, his disciples followed him.
040	MAT	008	024	And behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea, insomuch that the boat was covered with the waves: but he was asleep.
040	MAT	008	025	And they came to him, and awoke him, saying, Save, Lord; we perish.
040	MAT	008	026	And he saith unto them, Why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith? Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm.
040	MAT	008	027	And the men marveled, saying, What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him?
040	MAT	008	028	And when he was come to the other side into the country of the Gadarenes, there met him two possessed with devils, coming forth out of the tombs, exceeding fierce, so that no man could pass by that way.
040	MAT	008	029	And behold, they cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, thou Son of God? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?
040	MAT	008	030	Now there was afar off from them a herd of many swine feeding.
040	MAT	008	031	And the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, send us away into the herd of swine.
040	MAT	008	032	And he said unto them, Go. And they came out, and went into the swine: and behold, the whole herd rushed down the steep into the sea, and perished in the waters.
040	MAT	008	033	And they that fed them fled, and went away into the city, and told everything, and what was befallen to them that were possessed with devils.
040	MAT	008	034	And behold, all the city came out to meet Jesus: and when they saw him, they besought [him] that he would depart from their borders.
040	MAT	009	001	And he entered into a boat, and crossed over, and came into his own city.
040	MAT	009	002	And behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy, lying on a bed: and Jesus seeing their faith said unto the sick of the palsy, Son, be of good cheer; thy sins are forgiven.
040	MAT	009	003	And behold, certain of the scribes said within themselves, This man blasphemeth.
040	MAT	009	004	And Jesus knowing their thoughts said, Wherefore think ye evil in your hearts?
040	MAT	009	005	For whether is easier, to say, Thy sins are forgiven; or to say, Arise, and walk?
040	MAT	009	006	But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins (then saith he to the sick of the palsy), Arise, and take up thy bed, and go unto thy house.
040	MAT	009	007	And he arose, and departed to his house.
040	MAT	009	008	But when the multitudes saw it, they were afraid, and glorified God, which had given such power unto men.
040	MAT	009	009	And as Jesus passed by from thence, he saw a man, called Matthew, sitting at the place of toll: and he saith unto him, Follow me. And he arose, and followed him.
040	MAT	009	010	And it came to pass, as he sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and sinners came and sat down with Jesus and his disciples.
040	MAT	009	011	And when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with the publicans and sinners?
040	MAT	009	012	But when he heard it, he said, They that are whole have no need of a physician, but they that are sick.
040	MAT	009	013	But go ye and learn what [this] meaneth, I desire mercy, and not sacrifice: for I came not to call the righteous, but sinners.
040	MAT	009	014	Then come to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft, but thy disciples fast not?
040	MAT	009	015	And Jesus said unto them, Can the sons of the bride-chamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then will they fast.
040	MAT	009	016	And no man putteth a piece of undressed cloth upon an old garment; for that which should fill it up taketh from the garment, and a worse rent is made.
040	MAT	009	017	Neither do [men] put new wine into old wineskins: else the skins burst, and the wine is spilled, and the skins perish: but they put new wine into fresh wineskins, and both are preserved.
040	MAT	009	018	While he spake these things unto them, behold, there came a ruler, and worshipped him, saying, My daughter is even now dead: but come and lay thy hand upon her, and she shall live.
040	MAT	009	019	And Jesus arose, and followed him, and [so did] his disciples.
040	MAT	009	020	And behold, a woman, who had an issue of blood twelve years, came behind him, and touched the border of his garment:
040	MAT	009	021	for she said within herself, If I do but touch his garment, I shall be made whole.
040	MAT	009	022	But Jesus turning and seeing her said, Daughter, be of good cheer; thy faith hath made thee whole. And the woman was made whole from that hour.
040	MAT	009	023	And when Jesus came into the ruler’s house, and saw the flute-players, and the crowd making a tumult,
040	MAT	009	024	he said, Give place: for the damsel is not dead, but sleepeth. And they laughed him to scorn.
040	MAT	009	025	But when the crowd was put forth, he entered in, and took her by the hand; and the damsel arose.
040	MAT	009	026	And the fame hereof went forth into all that land.
040	MAT	009	027	And as Jesus passed by from thence, two blind men followed him, crying out, and saying, Have mercy on us, thou son of David.
040	MAT	009	028	And when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and Jesus saith unto them, Believe ye that I am able to do this? They say unto him, Yea, Lord.
040	MAT	009	029	Then touched he their eyes, saying, According to your faith be it done unto you.
040	MAT	009	030	And their eyes were opened. And Jesus strictly charged them, saying, See that no man know it.
040	MAT	009	031	But they went forth, and spread abroad his fame in all that land.
040	MAT	009	032	And as they went forth, behold, there was brought to him a dumb man possessed with a devil.
040	MAT	009	033	And when the devil was cast out, the dumb man spake: and the multitudes marveled, saying, It was never so seen in Israel.
040	MAT	009	034	But the Pharisees said, By the prince of the devils casteth he out devils.
040	MAT	009	035	And Jesus went about all the cities and the villages, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of disease and all manner of sickness.
040	MAT	009	036	But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion for them, because they were distressed and scattered, as sheep not having a shepherd.
040	MAT	009	037	Then saith he unto his disciples, The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few.
040	MAT	009	038	Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he send forth labourers into his harvest.
040	MAT	010	001	And he called unto him his twelve disciples, and gave them authority over unclean spirits, to cast them out, and to heal all manner of disease and all manner of sickness.
040	MAT	010	002	Now the names of the twelve apostles are these: The first, Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother; James the [son] of Zebedee, and John his brother;
040	MAT	010	003	Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas, and Matthew the publican; James the [son] of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus;
040	MAT	010	004	Simon the Cananaean, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.
040	MAT	010	005	These twelve Jesus sent forth, and charged them, saying, Go not into [any] way of the Gentiles, and enter not into any city of the Samaritans:
040	MAT	010	006	but go rather to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.
040	MAT	010	007	And as ye go, preach, saying, The kingdom of heaven is at hand.
040	MAT	010	008	Heal the sick, raise the dead, cleanse the lepers, cast out devils: freely ye received, freely give.
040	MAT	010	009	Get you no gold, nor silver, nor brass in your purses;
040	MAT	010	010	no wallet for [your] journey, neither two coats, nor shoes, nor staff: for the labourer is worthy of his food.
040	MAT	010	011	And into whatsoever city or village ye shall enter, search out who in it is worthy; and there abide till ye go forth.
040	MAT	010	012	And as ye enter into the house, salute it.
040	MAT	010	013	And if the house be worthy, let your peace come upon it: but if it be not worthy, let your peace return to you.
040	MAT	010	014	And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear your words, as ye go forth out of that house or that city, shake off the dust of your feet.
040	MAT	010	015	Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrah in the day of judgment, than for that city.
040	MAT	010	016	Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves: be ye therefore wise as serpents, and harmless as doves.
040	MAT	010	017	But beware of men: for they will deliver you up to councils, and in their synagogues they will scourge you;
040	MAT	010	018	yea and before governors and kings shall ye be brought for my sake, for a testimony to them and to the Gentiles.
040	MAT	010	019	But when they deliver you up, be not anxious how or what ye shall speak: for it shall be given you in that hour what ye shall speak.
040	MAT	010	020	For it is not ye that speak, but the Spirit of your Father that speaketh in you.
040	MAT	010	021	And brother shall deliver up brother to death, and the father his child: and children shall rise up against parents, and cause them to be put to death.
040	MAT	010	022	And ye shall be hated of all men for my name’s sake: but he that endureth to the end, the same shall be saved.
040	MAT	010	023	But when they persecute you in this city, flee into the next: for verily I say unto you, Ye shall not have gone through the cities of Israel, till the Son of man be come.
040	MAT	010	024	A disciple is not above his master, nor a servant above his lord.
040	MAT	010	025	It is enough for the disciple that he be as his master, and the servant as his lord. If they have called the master of the house Beelzebub, how much more [shall they call] them of his household!
040	MAT	010	026	Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and hid, that shall not be known.
040	MAT	010	027	What I tell you in the darkness, speak ye in the light: and what ye hear in the ear, proclaim upon the housetops.
040	MAT	010	028	And be not afraid of them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.
040	MAT	010	029	Are not two sparrows sold for a farthing? and not one of them shall fall on the ground without your Father:
040	MAT	010	030	but the very hairs of your head are all numbered.
040	MAT	010	031	Fear not therefore; ye are of more value than many sparrows.
040	MAT	010	032	Every one therefore who shall confess me before men, him will I also confess before my Father which is in heaven.
040	MAT	010	033	But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven.
040	MAT	010	034	Think not that I came to send peace on the earth: I came not to send peace, but a sword.
040	MAT	010	035	For I came to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her mother, and the daughter in law against her mother in law:
040	MAT	010	036	and a man’s foes [shall be] they of his own household.
040	MAT	010	037	He that loveth father or mother more than me is not worthy of me; and he that loveth son or daughter more than me is not worthy of me.
040	MAT	010	038	And he that doth not take his cross and follow after me, is not worthy of me.
040	MAT	010	039	He that findeth his life shall lose it; and he that loseth his life for my sake shall find it.
040	MAT	010	040	He that receiveth you receiveth me, and he that receiveth me receiveth him that sent me.
040	MAT	010	041	He that receiveth a prophet in the name of a prophet shall receive a prophet’s reward; and he that receiveth a righteous man in the name of a righteous man shall receive a righteous man’s reward.
040	MAT	010	042	And whosoever shall give to drink unto one of these little ones a cup of cold water only, in the name of a disciple, verily I say unto you, he shall in no wise lose his reward.
040	MAT	011	001	And it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and preach in their cities.
040	MAT	011	002	Now when John heard in the prison the works of the Christ, he sent by his disciples,
040	MAT	011	003	and said unto him, Art thou he that cometh, or look we for another?
040	MAT	011	004	And Jesus answered and said unto them, Go your way and tell John the things which ye do hear and see:
040	MAT	011	005	the blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up, and the poor have good tidings preached to them.
040	MAT	011	006	And blessed is he, whosoever shall find none occasion of stumbling in me.
040	MAT	011	007	And as these went their way, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness to behold? a reed shaken with the wind?
040	MAT	011	008	But what went ye out for to see? a man clothed in soft [raiment]? Behold, they that wear soft [raiment] are in kings’ houses.
040	MAT	011	009	But wherefore went ye out? to see a prophet? Yea, I say unto you, and much more than a prophet.
040	MAT	011	010	This is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, Who shall prepare thy way before thee.
040	MAT	011	011	Verily I say unto you, Among them that are born of women there hath not arisen a greater than John the Baptist: yet he that is but little in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he.
040	MAT	011	012	And from the days of John the Baptist until now the kingdom of heaven suffereth violence, and men of violence take it by force.
040	MAT	011	013	For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John.
040	MAT	011	014	And if ye are willing to receive [it], this is Elijah, which is to come.
040	MAT	011	015	He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.
040	MAT	011	016	But whereunto shall I liken this generation? It is like unto children sitting in the marketplaces, which call unto their fellows,
040	MAT	011	017	and say, We piped unto you, and ye did not dance; we wailed, and ye did not mourn.
040	MAT	011	018	For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, He hath a devil.
040	MAT	011	019	The Son of man came eating and drinking, and they say, Behold, a gluttonous man, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners! And wisdom is justified by her works.
040	MAT	011	020	Then began he to upbraid the cities wherein most of his mighty works were done, because they repented not.
040	MAT	011	021	Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty works had been done in Tyre and Sidon which were done in you, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.
040	MAT	011	022	Howbeit I say unto you, it shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon in the day of judgment, than for you.
040	MAT	011	023	And thou, Capernaum, shalt thou be exalted unto heaven? thou shalt go down unto Hades: for if the mighty works had been done in Sodom which were done in thee, it would have remained until this day.
040	MAT	011	024	Howbeit I say unto you, that it shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom in the day of judgment, than for thee.
040	MAT	011	025	At that season Jesus answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that thou didst hide these things from the wise and understanding, and didst reveal them unto babes:
040	MAT	011	026	yea, Father, for so it was well-pleasing in thy sight.
040	MAT	011	027	All things have been delivered unto me of my Father: and no one knoweth the Son, save the Father; neither doth any know the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son willeth to reveal [him].
040	MAT	011	028	Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.
040	MAT	011	029	Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.
040	MAT	011	030	For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.
040	MAT	012	001	At that season Jesus went on the sabbath day through the cornfields; and his disciples were an hungred, and began to pluck ears of corn, and to eat.
040	MAT	012	002	But the Pharisees, when they saw it, said unto him, Behold, thy disciples do that which it is not lawful to do upon the sabbath.
040	MAT	012	003	But he said unto them, Have ye not read what David did, when he was an hungred, and they that were with him;
040	MAT	012	004	how be entered into the house of God, and did eat the shewbread, which it was not lawful for him to eat, neither for them that were with him, but only for the priests?
040	MAT	012	005	Or have ye not read in the law, how that on the sabbath day the priests in the temple profane the sabbath, and are guiltless?
040	MAT	012	006	But I say unto you, that one greater than the temple is here.
040	MAT	012	007	But if ye had known what this meaneth, I desire mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would not have condemned the guiltless.
040	MAT	012	008	For the Son of man is lord of the sabbath.
040	MAT	012	009	And he departed thence, and went into their synagogue:
040	MAT	012	010	and behold, a man having a withered hand. And they asked him, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath day? that they might accuse him.
040	MAT	012	011	And he said unto them, What man shall there be of you, that shall have one sheep, and if this fall into a pit on the sabbath day, will he not lay hold on it, and lift it out?
040	MAT	012	012	How much then is a man of more value than a sheep! Wherefore it is lawful to do good on the sabbath day.
040	MAT	012	013	Then saith he to the man, Stretch forth thy hand. And he stretched it forth; and it was restored whole, as the other.
040	MAT	012	014	But the Pharisees went out, and took counsel against him, how they might destroy him.
040	MAT	012	015	And Jesus perceiving [it] withdrew from thence: and many followed him; and he healed them all,
040	MAT	012	016	and charged them that they should not make him known:
040	MAT	012	017	that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the prophet, saying,
040	MAT	012	018	Behold, my servant whom I have chosen; My beloved in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my Spirit upon him, And he shall declare judgment to the Gentiles.
040	MAT	012	019	He shall not strive, nor cry aloud; Neither shall any one hear his voice in the streets.
040	MAT	012	020	A bruised reed shall he not break, And smoking flax shall he not quench, Till he send forth judgment unto victory.
040	MAT	012	021	And in his name shall the Gentiles hope.
040	MAT	012	022	Then was brought unto him one possessed with a devil, blind and dumb: and he healed him, insomuch that the dumb man spake and saw.
040	MAT	012	023	And all the multitudes were amazed, and said, Is this the son of David?
040	MAT	012	024	But when the Pharisees heard it, they said, This man doth not cast out devils, but by Beelzebub the prince of the devils.
040	MAT	012	025	And knowing their thoughts he said unto them, Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself shall not stand:
040	MAT	012	026	and if Satan casteth out Satan, he is divided against himself; how then shall his kingdom stand?
040	MAT	012	027	And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your sons cast them out? therefore shall they be your judges.
040	MAT	012	028	But if I by the Spirit of God cast out devils, then is the kingdom of God come upon you.
040	MAT	012	029	Or how can one enter into the house of the strong [man], and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong [man]? and then he will spoil his house.
040	MAT	012	030	He that is not with me is against me; and he that gathereth not with me scattereth.
040	MAT	012	031	Therefore I say unto you, Every sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven unto men; but the blasphemy against the Spirit shall not be forgiven.
040	MAT	012	032	And whosoever shall speak a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him; but whosoever shall speak against the Holy Spirit, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this world, nor in that which is to come.
040	MAT	012	033	Either make the tree good, and its fruit good; or make the tree corrupt, and its fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by its fruit.
040	MAT	012	034	Ye offspring of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.
040	MAT	012	035	The good man out of his good treasure bringeth forth good things: and the evil man out of his evil treasure bringeth forth evil things.
040	MAT	012	036	And I say unto you, that every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account thereof in the day of judgment.
040	MAT	012	037	For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.
040	MAT	012	038	Then certain of the scribes and Pharisees answered him, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.
040	MAT	012	039	But he answered and said unto them, An evil and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given to it but the sign of Jonah the prophet:
040	MAT	012	040	for as Jonah was three days and three nights in the belly of the whale; so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.
040	MAT	012	041	The men of Nineveh shall stand up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for they repented at the preaching of Jonah; and behold, a greater than Jonah is here.
040	MAT	012	042	The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold, a greater than Solomon is here.
040	MAT	012	043	But the unclean spirit, when he is gone out of the man, passeth through waterless places, seeking rest, and findeth it not.
040	MAT	012	044	Then he saith, I will return into my house whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth it empty, swept, and garnished.
040	MAT	012	045	Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more evil than himself, and they enter in and dwell there: and the last state of that man becometh worse than the first. Even so shall it be also unto this evil generation.
040	MAT	012	046	While he was yet speaking to the multitudes, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without, seeking to speak to him.
040	MAT	012	047	And one said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, seeking to speak to thee.
040	MAT	012	048	But he answered and said unto him that told him, Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?
040	MAT	012	049	And he stretched forth his hand towards his disciples, and said, Behold, my mother and my brethren!
040	MAT	012	050	For whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, he is my brother, and sister, and mother.
040	MAT	013	001	On that day went Jesus out of the house, and sat by the sea side.
040	MAT	013	002	And there were gathered unto him great multitudes, so that he entered into a boat, and sat; and all the multitude stood on the beach.
040	MAT	013	003	And he spake to them many things in parables, saying, Behold, the sower went forth to sow;
040	MAT	013	004	and as he sowed, some [seeds] fell by the way side, and the birds came and devoured them:
040	MAT	013	005	and others fell upon the rocky places, where they had not much earth: and straightway they sprang up, because they had no deepness of earth:
040	MAT	013	006	and when the sun was risen, they were scorched; and because they had no root, they withered away.
040	MAT	013	007	And others fell upon the thorns; and the thorns grew up, and choked them:
040	MAT	013	008	and others fell upon the good ground, and yielded fruit, some a hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.
040	MAT	013	009	He that hath ears, let him hear.
040	MAT	013	010	And the disciples came, and said unto him, Why speakest thou unto them in parables?
040	MAT	013	011	And he answered and said unto them, Unto you it is given to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given.
040	MAT	013	012	For whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that which he hath.
040	MAT	013	013	Therefore speak I to them in parables; because seeing they see not, and hearing they hear not, neither do they understand.
