040	MAT	018	035	So shall also my heavenly Father do unto you, if ye forgive not every one his brother from your hearts.
040	MAT	019	001	And it came to pass when Jesus had finished these words, he departed from Galilee, and came into the borders of Judaea beyond Jordan;
040	MAT	019	002	and great multitudes followed him; and he healed them there.
040	MAT	019	003	And there came unto him Pharisees, tempting him, and saying, Is it lawful [for a man] to put away his wife for every cause?
040	MAT	019	004	And he answered and said, Have ye not read, that he which made [them] from the beginning made them male and female,
040	MAT	019	005	and said, For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall cleave to his wife; and the twain shall become one flesh?
040	MAT	019	006	So that they are no more twain, but one flesh. What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.
040	MAT	019	007	They say unto him, Why then did Moses command to give a bill of divorcement, and to put [her] away?
040	MAT	019	008	He saith unto them, Moses for your hardness of heart suffered you to put away your wives: but from the beginning it hath not been so.
040	MAT	019	009	And I say unto you, Whosoever shall put away his wife, except for fornication, and shall marry another, committeth adultery: and he that marrieth her when she is put away committeth adultery.
040	MAT	019	010	The disciples say unto him, If the case of the man is so with his wife, it is not expedient to marry.
040	MAT	019	011	But he said unto them, All men cannot receive this saying, but they to whom it is given.
040	MAT	019	012	For there are eunuchs, which were so born from their mother’s womb: and there are eunuchs, which were made eunuchs by men: and there are eunuchs, which made themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven’s sake. He that is able to receive it, let him receive it.
040	MAT	019	013	Then were there brought unto him little children, that he should lay his hands on them, and pray: and the disciples rebuked them.
040	MAT	019	014	But Jesus said, Suffer the little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	019	015	And he laid his hands on them, and departed thence.
040	MAT	019	016	And behold, one came to him and said, Master, what good thing shall I do, that I may have eternal life?
040	MAT	019	017	And he said unto him, Why askest thou me concerning that which is good? One there is who is good: but if thou wouldest enter into life, keep the commandments.
040	MAT	019	018	He saith unto him, Which? And Jesus said, Thou shalt not kill, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness,
040	MAT	019	019	Honour thy father and thy mother: and, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.
040	MAT	019	020	The young man saith unto him, All these things have I observed: what lack I yet?
040	MAT	019	021	Jesus said unto him, If thou wouldest be perfect, go, sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, follow me.
040	MAT	019	022	But when the young man heard the saying, he went away sorrowful: for he was one that had great possessions.
040	MAT	019	023	And Jesus said unto his disciples, Verily I say unto you, It is hard for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of heaven.
040	MAT	019	024	And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through a needle’s eye, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.
040	MAT	019	025	And when the disciples heard it, they were astonished exceedingly, saying, Who then can be saved?
040	MAT	019	026	And Jesus looking upon [them] said to them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.
040	MAT	019	027	Then answered Peter and said unto him, Lo, we have left all, and followed thee; what then shall we have?
040	MAT	019	028	And Jesus said unto them, Verily I say unto you, that ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of man shall sit on the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.
040	MAT	019	029	And every one that hath left houses, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or children, or lands, for my name’s sake, shall receive a hundredfold, and shall inherit eternal life.
040	MAT	019	030	But many shall be last [that are] first; and first [that are] last.
040	MAT	020	001	For the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man that is a householder, which went out early in the morning to hire labourers into his vineyard.
040	MAT	020	002	And when he had agreed with the labourers for a penny a day, he sent them into his vineyard.
040	MAT	020	003	And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing in the marketplace idle;
040	MAT	020	004	and to them he said, Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give you. And they went their way.
040	MAT	020	005	Again he went out about the sixth and the ninth hour, and did likewise.
040	MAT	020	006	And about the eleventh [hour] he went out, and found others standing; and he saith unto them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?
040	MAT	020	007	They say unto him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go ye also into the vineyard.
040	MAT	020	008	And when even was come, the lord of the vineyard saith unto his steward, Call the labourers, and pay them their hire, beginning from the last unto the first.
040	MAT	020	009	And when they came that [were hired] about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.
040	MAT	020	010	And when the first came, they supposed that they would receive more; and they likewise received every man a penny.
040	MAT	020	011	And when they received it, they murmured against the householder,
040	MAT	020	012	saying, These last have spent [but] one hour, and thou hast made them equal unto us, which have borne the burden of the day and the scorching heat.
040	MAT	020	013	But he answered and said to one of them, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst not thou agree with me for a penny?
040	MAT	020	014	Take up that which is thine, and go thy way; it is my will to give unto this last, even as unto thee.
040	MAT	020	015	Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with mine own? or is thine eye evil, because I am good?
040	MAT	020	016	So the last shall be first, and the first last.
040	MAT	020	017	And as Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, he took the twelve disciples apart, and in the way he said unto them,
040	MAT	020	018	Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be delivered unto the chief priests and scribes; and they shall condemn him to death,
040	MAT	020	019	and shall deliver him unto the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify: and the third day he shall be raised up.
040	MAT	020	020	Then came to him the mother of the sons of Zebedee with her sons, worshipping [him], and asking a certain thing of him.
040	MAT	020	021	And he said unto her, What wouldest thou? She saith unto him, Command that these my two sons may sit, one on thy right hand, and one on thy left hand, in thy kingdom.
040	MAT	020	022	But Jesus answered and said, Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink the cup that I am about to drink? They say unto him, We are able.
040	MAT	020	023	He saith unto them, My cup indeed ye shall drink: but to sit on my right hand, and on [my] left hand, is not mine to give, but [it is for them] for whom it hath been prepared of my Father.
040	MAT	020	024	And when the ten heard it, they were moved with indignation concerning the two brethren.
040	MAT	020	025	But Jesus called them unto him, and said, Ye know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their great ones exercise authority over them.
040	MAT	020	026	Not so shall it be among you: but whosoever would become great among you shall be your minister;
040	MAT	020	027	and whosoever would be first among you shall be your servant:
040	MAT	020	028	even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.
040	MAT	020	029	And as they went out from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.
040	MAT	020	030	And behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Jesus was passing by, cried out, saying, Lord, have mercy on us, thou son of David.
040	MAT	020	031	And the multitude rebuked them, that they should hold their peace: but they cried out the more, saying, Lord, have mercy on us, thou son of David.
040	MAT	020	032	And Jesus stood still, and called them, and said, What will ye that I should do unto you?
040	MAT	020	033	They say unto him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.
040	MAT	020	034	And Jesus, being moved with compassion, touched their eyes: and straightway they received their sight, and followed him.
040	MAT	021	001	And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and came unto Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then Jesus sent two disciples,
040	MAT	021	002	saying unto them, Go into the village that is over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a colt with her: loose [them], and bring [them] unto me.
040	MAT	021	003	And if any one say aught unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and straightway he will send them.
040	MAT	021	004	Now this is come to pass, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying,
040	MAT	021	005	Tell ye the daughter of Zion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, Meek, and riding upon an ass, And upon a colt the foal of an ass.
040	MAT	021	006	And the disciples went, and did even as Jesus appointed them,
040	MAT	021	007	and brought the ass, and the colt, and put on them their garments; and he sat thereon.
040	MAT	021	008	And the most part of the multitude spread their garments in the way; and others cut branches from the trees, and spread them in the way.
040	MAT	021	009	And the multitudes that went before him, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the son of David: Blessed [is] he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.
040	MAT	021	010	And when he was come into Jerusalem, all the city was stirred, saying, Who is this?
040	MAT	021	011	And the multitudes said, This is the prophet, Jesus, from Nazareth of Galilee.
040	MAT	021	012	And Jesus entered into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the money-changers, and the seats of them that sold the doves;
040	MAT	021	013	and he saith unto them, It is written, My house shall be called a house of prayer: but ye make it a den of robbers.
040	MAT	021	014	And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple: and he healed them.
040	MAT	021	015	But when the chief priests and the scribes saw the wonderful things that he did, and the children that were crying in the temple and saying, Hosanna to the son of David; they were moved with indignation,
040	MAT	021	016	and said unto him, Hearest thou what these are saying? And Jesus saith unto them, Yea: did ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise?
040	MAT	021	017	And he left them, and went forth out of the city to Bethany, and lodged there.
040	MAT	021	018	Now in the morning as he returned to the city, he hungered.
040	MAT	021	019	And seeing a fig tree by the way side, he came to it, and found nothing thereon, but leaves only; and he saith unto it, Let there be no fruit from thee henceforward for ever. And immediately the fig tree withered away.
040	MAT	021	020	And when the disciples saw it, they marveled, saying, How did the fig tree immediately wither away?
040	MAT	021	021	And Jesus answered and said unto them, Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do what is done to the fig tree, but even if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou taken up and cast into the sea, it shall be done.
040	MAT	021	022	And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive.
040	MAT	021	023	And when he was come into the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people came unto him as he was teaching, and said, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority?
040	MAT	021	024	And Jesus answered and said unto them, I also will ask you one question, which if ye tell me, I likewise will tell you by what authority I do these things.
040	MAT	021	025	The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven or from men? And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say unto us, Why then did ye not believe him?
040	MAT	021	026	But if we shall say, From men; we fear the multitude; for all hold John as a prophet.
040	MAT	021	027	And they answered Jesus, and said, We know not. He also said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.
040	MAT	021	028	But what think ye? A man had two sons; and he came to the first, and said, Son, go work today in the vineyard.
040	MAT	021	029	And he answered and said, I will not: but afterward he repented himself, and went.
040	MAT	021	030	And he came to the second, and said likewise. And he answered and said, I [go], sir: and went not.
040	MAT	021	031	Whether of the twain did the will of his father? They say, The first. Jesus saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, that the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you.
040	MAT	021	032	For John came unto you in the way of righteousness, and ye believed him not: but the publicans and the harlots believed him: and ye, when ye saw it, did not even repent yourselves afterward, that ye might believe him.
040	MAT	021	033	Hear another parable: There was a man that was a householder, which planted a vineyard, and set a hedge about it, and digged a winepress in it, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into another country.
040	MAT	021	034	And when the season of the fruits drew near, he sent his servants to the husbandmen, to receive his fruits.
040	MAT	021	035	And the husbandmen took his servants, and beat one, and killed another, and stoned another.
040	MAT	021	036	Again, he sent other servants more than the first: and they did unto them in like manner.
040	MAT	021	037	But afterward he sent unto them his son, saying, They will reverence my son.
040	MAT	021	038	But the husbandmen, when they saw the son, said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and take his inheritance.
040	MAT	021	039	And they took him, and cast him forth out of the vineyard, and killed him.
040	MAT	021	040	When therefore the lord of the vineyard shall come, what will he do unto those husbandmen?
040	MAT	021	041	They say unto him, He will miserably destroy those miserable men, and will let out the vineyard unto other husbandmen, which shall render him the fruits in their seasons.
040	MAT	021	042	Jesus saith unto them, Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, The same was made the head of the corner: This was from the Lord, And it is marvelous in our eyes?
040	MAT	021	043	Therefore say I unto you, The kingdom of God shall be taken away from you, and shall be given to a nation bringing forth the fruits thereof.
040	MAT	021	044	And he that falleth on this stone shall be broken to pieces: but on whomsoever it shall fall, it will scatter him as dust.
040	MAT	021	045	And when the chief priests and the Pharisees heard his parables, they perceived that he spake of them.
040	MAT	021	046	And when they sought to lay hold on him, they feared the multitudes, because they took him for a prophet.
040	MAT	022	001	And Jesus answered and spake again in parables unto them, saying,
040	MAT	022	002	The kingdom of heaven is likened unto a certain king, which made a marriage feast for his son,
040	MAT	022	003	and sent forth his servants to call them that were bidden to the marriage feast: and they would not come.
040	MAT	022	004	Again he sent forth other servants, saying, Tell them that are bidden, Behold, I have made ready my dinner: my oxen and my fatlings are killed, and all things are ready: come to the marriage feast.
040	MAT	022	005	But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his own farm, another to his merchandise:
040	MAT	022	006	and the rest laid hold on his servants, and entreated them shamefully, and killed them.
040	MAT	022	007	But the king was wroth; and he sent his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned their city.
040	MAT	022	008	Then saith he to his servants, The wedding is ready, but they that were bidden were not worthy.
040	MAT	022	009	Go ye therefore unto the partings of the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage feast.
040	MAT	022	010	And those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they found, both bad and good: and the wedding was filled with guests.
040	MAT	022	011	But when the king came in to behold the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding-garment:
040	MAT	022	012	and he saith unto him, Friend, how camest thou in hither not having a wedding-garment? And he was speechless.
040	MAT	022	013	Then the king said to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and cast him out into the outer darkness; there shall be the weeping and gnashing of teeth.
040	MAT	022	014	For many are called, but few chosen.
040	MAT	022	015	Then went the Pharisees, and took counsel how they might ensnare him in [his] talk.
040	MAT	022	016	And they send to him their disciples, with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, and carest not for any one: for thou regardest not the person of men.
040	MAT	022	017	Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou? Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?
040	MAT	022	018	But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said, Why tempt ye me, ye hypocrites?
040	MAT	022	019	Shew me the tribute money. And they brought unto him a penny.
040	MAT	022	020	And he saith unto them, Whose is this image and superscription?
040	MAT	022	021	They say unto him, Caesar’s. Then saith he unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things that are Caesar’s; and unto God the things that are God’s.
040	MAT	022	022	And when they heard it, they marveled, and left him, and went their way.
040	MAT	022	023	On that day there came to him Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection: and they asked him,
040	MAT	022	024	saying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.
040	MAT	022	025	Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first married and deceased, and having no seed left his wife unto his brother;
040	MAT	022	026	in like manner the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.
040	MAT	022	027	And after them all the woman died.
040	MAT	022	028	In the resurrection therefore whose wife shall she be of the seven? for they all had her.
040	MAT	022	029	But Jesus answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.
040	MAT	022	030	For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as angels in heaven.
040	MAT	022	031	But as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken unto you by God, saying,
040	MAT	022	032	I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not [the God] of the dead, but of the living.
040	MAT	022	033	And when the multitudes heard it, they were astonished at his teaching.
040	MAT	022	034	But the Pharisees, when they heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, gathered themselves together.
040	MAT	022	035	And one of them, a lawyer, asked him a question, tempting him,
040	MAT	022	036	Master, which is the great commandment in the law?
040	MAT	022	037	And he said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.
040	MAT	022	038	This is the great and first commandment.
040	MAT	022	039	And a second like [unto it] is this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.
040	MAT	022	040	On these two commandments hangeth the whole law, and the prophets.
040	MAT	022	041	Now while the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them a question,
040	MAT	022	042	saying, What think ye of the Christ? whose son is he? They say unto him, [The son] of David.
040	MAT	022	043	He saith unto them, How then doth David in the Spirit call him Lord, saying,
040	MAT	022	044	The Lord said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, Till I put thine enemies underneath thy feet?
040	MAT	022	045	If David then calleth him Lord, how is he his son?
040	MAT	022	046	And no one was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask him any more questions.
040	MAT	023	001	Then spake Jesus to the multitudes and to his disciples,
040	MAT	023	002	saying, The scribes and the Pharisees sit on Moses’ seat:
040	MAT	023	003	all things therefore whatsoever they bid you, [these] do and observe: but do not ye after their works; for they say, and do not.
040	MAT	023	004	Yea, they bind heavy burdens and grievous to be borne, and lay them on men’s shoulders; but they themselves will not move them with their finger.
040	MAT	023	005	But all their works they do for to be seen of men: for they make broad their phylacteries, and enlarge the borders [of their garments],
040	MAT	023	006	and love the chief place at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues,
040	MAT	023	007	and the salutations in the marketplaces, and to be called of men, Rabbi.
040	MAT	023	008	But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your teacher, and all ye are brethren.
040	MAT	023	009	And call no man your father on the earth: for one is your Father, which is in heaven.
040	MAT	023	010	Neither be ye called masters: for one is your master, [even] the Christ.
040	MAT	023	011	But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant.
040	MAT	023	012	And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be humbled; and whosoever shall humble himself shall be exalted.
040	MAT	023	013	But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye shut the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye enter not in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering in to enter.
040	MAT	023	015	Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte; and when he is become so, ye make him twofold more a son of hell than yourselves.
040	MAT	023	016	Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor.
040	MAT	023	017	Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that hath sanctified the gold?
040	MAT	023	018	And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gift that is upon it, he is a debtor.
040	MAT	023	019	Ye blind: for whether is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the gift?
040	MAT	023	020	He therefore that sweareth by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon.
040	MAT	023	021	And he that sweareth by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein.
040	MAT	023	022	And he that sweareth by the heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon.
040	MAT	023	023	Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye tithe mint and anise and cummin, and have left undone the weightier matters of the law, judgment, and mercy, and faith: but these ye ought to have done, and not to have left the other undone.
040	MAT	023	024	Ye blind guides, which strain out the gnat, and swallow the camel.
040	MAT	023	025	Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye cleanse the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full from extortion and excess.
040	MAT	023	026	Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first the inside of the cup and of the platter, that the outside thereof may become clean also.
040	MAT	023	027	Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which outwardly appear beautiful, but inwardly are full of dead men’s bones, and of all uncleanness.
040	MAT	023	028	Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but inwardly ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.
040	MAT	023	029	Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye build the sepulchres of the prophets, and garnish the tombs of the righteous,
040	MAT	023	030	and say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we should not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets.
040	MAT	023	031	Wherefore ye witness to yourselves, that ye are sons of them that slew the prophets.
040	MAT	023	032	Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers.
040	MAT	023	033	Ye serpents, ye offspring of vipers, how shall ye escape the judgment of hell?
040	MAT	023	034	Therefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: some of them shall ye kill and crucify; and some of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and persecute from city to city:
040	MAT	023	035	that upon you may come all the righteous blood shed on the earth, from the blood of Abel the righteous unto the blood of Zachariah son of Barachiah, whom ye slew between the sanctuary and the altar.
040	MAT	023	036	Verily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation.
040	MAT	023	037	O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, which killeth the prophets, and stoneth them that are sent unto her! how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!
040	MAT	023	038	Behold, your house is left unto you desolate.
040	MAT	023	039	For I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed [is] he that cometh in the name of the Lord.
040	MAT	024	001	And Jesus went out from the temple, and was going on his way; and his disciples came to him to shew him the buildings of the temple.
040	MAT	024	002	But he answered and said unto them, See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.
040	MAT	024	003	And as he sat on the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what [shall be] the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?
040	MAT	024	004	And Jesus answered and said unto them, Take heed that no man lead you astray.
040	MAT	024	005	For many shall come in my name, saying, I am the Christ; and shall lead many astray.
040	MAT	024	006	And ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars: see that ye be not troubled: for [these things] must needs come to pass; but the end is not yet.
040	MAT	024	007	For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be famines and earthquakes in divers places.
040	MAT	024	008	But all these things are the beginning of travail.
040	MAT	024	009	Then shall they deliver you up unto tribulation, and shall kill you: and ye shall be hated of all the nations for my name’s sake.
040	MAT	024	010	And then shall many stumble, and shall deliver up one another, and shall hate one another.
040	MAT	024	011	And many false prophets shall arise, and shall lead many astray.
040	MAT	024	012	And because iniquity shall be multiplied, the love of the many shall wax cold.
040	MAT	024	013	But he that endureth to the end, the same shall be saved.
040	MAT	024	014	And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in the whole world for a testimony unto all the nations; and then shall the end come.
040	MAT	024	015	When therefore ye see the abomination of desolation, which was spoken of by Daniel the prophet, standing in the holy place (let him that readeth understand),
040	MAT	024	016	then let them that are in Judaea flee unto the mountains:
040	MAT	024	017	let him that is on the housetop not go down to take out the things that are in his house:
040	MAT	024	018	and let him that is in the field not return back to take his cloke.
040	MAT	024	019	But woe unto them that are with child and to them that give suck in those days!
040	MAT	024	020	And pray ye that your flight be not in the winter, neither on a sabbath:
040	MAT	024	021	for then shall be great tribulation, such as hath not been from the beginning of the world until now, no, nor ever shall be.
040	MAT	024	022	And except those days had been shortened, no flesh would have been saved: but for the elect’s sake those days shall be shortened.
040	MAT	024	023	Then if any man shall say unto you, Lo, here is the Christ, or, Here; believe [it] not.
040	MAT	024	024	For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; so as to lead astray, if possible, even the elect.
040	MAT	024	025	Behold, I have told you beforehand.
040	MAT	024	026	If therefore they shall say unto you, Behold, he is in the wilderness; go not forth: Behold, he is in the inner chambers; believe [it] not.
040	MAT	024	027	For as the lightning cometh forth from the east, and is seen even unto the west; so shall be the coming of the Son of man.
040	MAT	024	028	Wheresoever the carcase is, there will the eagles be gathered together.
040	MAT	024	029	But immediately, after the tribulation of those days, the sun shall be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken:
040	MAT	024	030	and then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming on the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.
040	MAT	024	031	And he shall send forth his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.
040	MAT	024	032	Now from the fig tree learn her parable: when her branch is now become tender, and putteth forth its leaves, ye know that the summer is nigh;
040	MAT	024	033	even so ye also, when ye see all these things, know ye that he is nigh, [even] at the doors.
040	MAT	024	034	Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass away, till all these things be accomplished.
040	MAT	024	035	Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.
040	MAT	024	036	But of that day and hour knoweth no one, not even the angels of heaven, neither the Son, but the Father only.
040	MAT	024	037	And as [were] the days of Noah, so shall be the coming of the Son of man.
040	MAT	024	038	For as in those days which were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noah entered into the ark,
040	MAT	024	039	and they knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall be the coming of the Son of man.
040	MAT	024	040	Then shall two men be in the field; one is taken, and one is left:
040	MAT	024	041	two women [shall be] grinding at the mill; one is taken, and one is left.
040	MAT	024	042	Watch therefore: for ye know not on what day your Lord cometh.
040	MAT	024	043	But know this, that if the master of the house had known in what watch the thief was coming, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken through.
040	MAT	024	044	Therefore be ye also ready: for in an hour that ye think not the Son of man cometh.
040	MAT	024	045	Who then is the faithful and wise servant, whom his lord hath set over his household, to give them their food in due season?
040	MAT	024	046	Blessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.
040	MAT	024	047	Verily I say unto you, that he will set him over all that he hath.
040	MAT	024	048	But if that evil servant shall say in his heart, My lord tarrieth;
040	MAT	024	049	and shall begin to beat his fellow-servants, and shall eat and drink with the drunken;
040	MAT	024	050	the lord of that servant shall come in a day when he expecteth not, and in an hour when he knoweth not,
040	MAT	024	051	and shall cut him asunder, and appoint his portion with the hypocrites: there shall be the weeping and gnashing of teeth.
040	MAT	025	001	Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.
040	MAT	025	002	And five of them were foolish, and five were wise.
040	MAT	025	003	For the foolish, when they took their lamps, took no oil with them:
040	MAT	025	004	but the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.
040	MAT	025	005	Now while the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.
040	MAT	025	006	But at midnight there is a cry, Behold, the bridegroom! Come ye forth to meet him.
040	MAT	025	007	Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.
040	MAT	025	008	And the foolish said unto the wise, Give us of your oil; for our lamps are going out.
040	MAT	025	009	But the wise answered, saying, Peradventure there will not be enough for us and you: go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.
040	MAT	025	010	And while they went away to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage feast: and the door was shut.
040	MAT	025	011	Afterward come also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.
040	MAT	025	012	But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.
040	MAT	025	013	Watch therefore, for ye know not the day nor the hour.
040	MAT	025	014	For [it is] as [when] a man, going into another country, called his own servants, and delivered unto them his goods.
040	MAT	025	015	And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, to another one; to each according to his several ability; and he went on his journey.
040	MAT	025	016	Straightway he that received the five talents went and traded with them, and made other five talents.
040	MAT	025	017	In like manner he also that [received] the two gained other two.
040	MAT	025	018	But he that received the one went away and digged in the earth, and hid his lord’s money.
040	MAT	025	019	Now after a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and maketh a reckoning with them.
040	MAT	025	020	And he that received the five talents came and brought other five talents, saying, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me five talents: lo, I have gained other five talents.
040	MAT	025	021	His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will set thee over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.
040	MAT	025	022	And he also that [received] the two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two talents: lo, I have gained other two talents.
040	MAT	025	023	His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will set thee over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.
040	MAT	025	024	And he also that had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art a hard man, reaping where thou didst not sow, and gathering where thou didst not scatter:
040	MAT	025	025	and I was afraid, and went away and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, thou hast thine own.
040	MAT	025	026	But his lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I did not scatter;
040	MAT	025	027	thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the bankers, and at my coming I should have received back mine own with interest.
040	MAT	025	028	Take ye away therefore the talent from him, and give it unto him that hath the ten talents.
040	MAT	025	029	For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not, even that which he hath shall be taken away.
040	MAT	025	030	And cast ye out the unprofitable servant into the outer darkness: there shall be the weeping and gnashing of teeth.
040	MAT	025	031	But when the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the angels with him, then shall he sit on the throne of his glory:
040	MAT	025	032	and before him shall be gathered all the nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as the shepherd separateth the sheep from the goats:
040	MAT	025	033	and he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.
040	MAT	025	034	Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:
040	MAT	025	035	for I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in;
040	MAT	025	036	naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.
040	MAT	025	037	Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed thee? or athirst, and gave thee drink?
040	MAT	025	038	And when saw we thee a stranger, and took thee in? or naked, and clothed thee?
040	MAT	025	039	And when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?
040	MAT	025	040	And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it unto one of these my brethren, [even] these least, ye did it unto me.
040	MAT	025	041	Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into the eternal fire which is prepared for the devil and his angels:
040	MAT	025	042	for I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:
040	MAT	025	043	I was a stranger, and ye took me not in; naked, and ye clothed me not; sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.
040	MAT	025	044	Then shall they also answer, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?
040	MAT	025	045	Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it not unto one of these least, ye did it not unto me.
040	MAT	025	046	And these shall go away into eternal punishment: but the righteous into eternal life.
040	MAT	026	001	And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these words, he said unto his disciples,
040	MAT	026	002	Ye know that after two days the passover cometh, and the Son of man is delivered up to be crucified.
040	MAT	026	003	Then were gathered together the chief priests, and the elders of the people, unto the court of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas;
040	MAT	026	004	and they took counsel together that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill him.
040	MAT	026	005	But they said, Not during the feast, lest a tumult arise among the people.
040	MAT	026	006	Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,
040	MAT	026	007	there came unto him a woman having an alabaster cruse of exceeding precious ointment, and she poured it upon his head, as he sat at meat.
040	MAT	026	008	But when the disciples saw it, they had indignation, saying, To what purpose is this waste?
040	MAT	026	009	For this [ointment] might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.
040	MAT	026	010	But Jesus perceiving it said unto them, Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me.
040	MAT	026	011	For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.
040	MAT	026	012	For in that she poured this ointment upon my body, she did it to prepare me for burial.
040	MAT	026	013	Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, that also which this woman hath done shall be spoken of for a memorial of her.
040	MAT	026	014	Then one of the twelve, who was called Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief priests,
040	MAT	026	015	and said, What are ye willing to give me, and I will deliver him unto you? And they weighed unto him thirty pieces of silver.
040	MAT	026	016	And from that time he sought opportunity to deliver him [unto them].
040	MAT	026	017	Now on the first [day] of unleavened bread the disciples came to Jesus, saying, Where wilt thou that we make ready for thee to eat the passover?
040	MAT	026	018	And he said, Go into the city to such a man, and say unto him, The Master saith, My time is at hand; I keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.
040	MAT	026	019	And the disciples did as Jesus appointed them; and they made ready the passover.
040	MAT	026	020	Now when even was come, he was sitting at meat with the twelve disciples;
040	MAT	026	021	and as they were eating, he said, Verily I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me.
040	MAT	026	022	And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began to say unto him every one, Is it I, Lord?
040	MAT	026	023	And he answered and said, He that dipped his hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.
040	MAT	026	024	The Son of man goeth, even as it is written of him: but woe unto that man through whom the Son of man is betrayed! good were it for that man if he had not been born.
040	MAT	026	025	And Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Is it I, Rabbi? He saith unto him, Thou hast said.
040	MAT	026	026	And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed, and brake it; and he gave to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.
040	MAT	026	027	And he took a cup, and gave thanks, and gave to them, saying, Drink ye all of it;
040	MAT	026	028	for this is my blood of the covenant, which is shed for many unto remission of sins.
040	MAT	026	029	But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father’s kingdom.
040	MAT	026	030	And when they had sung a hymn, they went out unto the mount of Olives.
040	MAT	026	031	Then saith Jesus unto them, All ye shall be offended in me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.
040	MAT	026	032	But after I am raised up, I will go before you into Galilee.
040	MAT	026	033	But Peter answered and said unto him, If all shall be offended in thee, I will never be offended.
040	MAT	026	034	Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, that this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.
040	MAT	026	035	Peter saith unto him, Even if I must die with thee, [yet] will I not deny thee. Likewise also said all the disciples.
040	MAT	026	036	Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto his disciples, Sit ye here, while I go yonder and pray.
040	MAT	026	037	And he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and sore troubled.
040	MAT	026	038	Then saith he unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: abide ye here, and watch with me.
040	MAT	026	039	And he went forward a little, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass away from me: nevertheless, not as I will, but as thou wilt.
040	MAT	026	040	And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them sleeping, and saith unto Peter, What, could ye not watch with me one hour?
040	MAT	026	041	Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.
040	MAT	026	042	Again a second time he went away, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if this cannot pass away, except I drink it, thy will be done.
040	MAT	026	043	And he came again and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy.
040	MAT	026	044	And he left them again, and went away, and prayed a third time, saying again the same words.
040	MAT	026	045	Then cometh he to the disciples, and saith unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.
040	MAT	026	046	Arise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that betrayeth me.
040	MAT	026	047	And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.
040	MAT	026	048	Now he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that is he: take him.
040	MAT	026	049	And straightway he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, Rabbi; and kissed him.
040	MAT	026	050	And Jesus said unto him, Friend, [do] that for which thou art come. Then they came and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.
040	MAT	026	051	And behold, one of them that were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and smote the servant of the high priest, and struck off his ear.
040	MAT	026	052	Then saith Jesus unto him, Put up again thy sword into its place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword.
040	MAT	026	053	Or thinkest thou that I cannot beseech my Father, and he shall even now send me more than twelve legions of angels?
040	MAT	026	054	How then should the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?
040	MAT	026	055	In that hour said Jesus to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a robber with swords and staves to seize me? I sat daily in the temple teaching, and ye took me not.
040	MAT	026	056	But all this is come to pass, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. Then all the disciples left him, and fled.
040	MAT	026	057	And they that had taken Jesus led him away to [the house of] Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were gathered together.
040	MAT	026	058	But Peter followed him afar off, unto the court of the high priest, and entered in, and sat with the officers, to see the end.
040	MAT	026	059	Now the chief priests and the whole council sought false witness against Jesus, that they might put him to death;
040	MAT	026	060	and they found it not, though many false witnesses came. But afterward came two,
040	MAT	026	061	and said, This man said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.
040	MAT	026	062	And the high priest stood up, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?
040	MAT	026	063	But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.
040	MAT	026	064	Jesus saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Henceforth ye shall see the Son of man sitting at the right hand of power, and coming on the clouds of heaven.
040	MAT	026	065	Then the high priest rent his garments, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy: what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard the blasphemy:
040	MAT	026	066	what think ye? They answered and said, He is worthy of death.
040	MAT	026	067	Then did they spit in his face and buffet him: and some smote him with the palms of their hands,
040	MAT	026	068	saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ: who is he that struck thee?
040	MAT	026	069	Now Peter was sitting without in the court: and a maid came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus the Galilaean.
040	MAT	026	070	But he denied before them all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.
040	MAT	026	071	And when he was gone out into the porch, another [maid] saw him, and saith unto them that were there, This man also was with Jesus the Nazarene.
040	MAT	026	072	And again he denied with an oath, I know not the man.
040	MAT	026	073	And after a little while they that stood by came and said to Peter, Of a truth thou also art [one] of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.
040	MAT	026	074	Then began he to curse and to swear, I know not the man. And straightway the cock crew.
040	MAT	026	075	And Peter remembered the word which Jesus had said, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice. And he went out, and wept bitterly.
040	MAT	027	001	Now when morning was come, all the chief priests and the elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death:
040	MAT	027	002	and they bound him, and led him away, and delivered him up to Pilate the governor.
040	MAT	027	003	Then Judas, which betrayed him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented himself, and brought back the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,
040	MAT	027	004	saying, I have sinned in that I betrayed innocent blood. But they said, What is that to us? see thou [to it].
040	MAT	027	005	And he cast down the pieces of silver into the sanctuary, and departed; and he went away and hanged himself.
040	MAT	027	006	And the chief priests took the pieces of silver, and said, It is not lawful to put them into the treasury, since it is the price of blood.
040	MAT	027	007	And they took counsel, and bought with them the potter’s field, to bury strangers in.
040	MAT	027	008	Wherefore that field was called, The field of blood, unto this day.
040	MAT	027	009	Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremiah the prophet, saying, And they took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him that was priced, whom [certain] of the children of Israel did price;
040	MAT	027	010	and they gave them for the potter’s field, as the Lord appointed me.
040	MAT	027	011	Now Jesus stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And Jesus said unto him, Thou sayest.
040	MAT	027	012	And when he was accused by the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing.
040	MAT	027	013	Then saith Pilate unto him, Hearest thou not how many things they witness against thee?
040	MAT	027	014	And he gave him no answer, not even to one word: insomuch that the governor marveled greatly.
040	MAT	027	015	Now at the feast the governor was wont to release unto the multitude one prisoner, whom they would.
040	MAT	027	016	And they had then a notable prisoner, called Barabbas.
040	MAT	027	017	When therefore they were gathered together, Pilate said unto them, Whom will ye that I release unto you? Barabbas, or Jesus which is called Christ?
040	MAT	027	018	For he knew that for envy they had delivered him up.
040	MAT	027	019	And while he was sitting on the judgment-seat, his wife sent unto him, saying, Have thou nothing to do with that righteous man: for I have suffered many things this day in a dream because of him.
040	MAT	027	020	Now the chief priests and the elders persuaded the multitudes that they should ask for Barabbas, and destroy Jesus.
040	MAT	027	021	But the governor answered and said unto them, Whether of the twain will ye that I release unto you? And they said, Barabbas.
040	MAT	027	022	Pilate saith unto them, What then shall I do unto Jesus which is called Christ? They all say, Let him be crucified.
040	MAT	027	023	And he said, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out exceedingly, saying, Let him be crucified.
040	MAT	027	024	So when Pilate saw that he prevailed nothing, but rather that a tumult was arising, he took water, and washed his hands before the multitude, saying, I am innocent of the blood of this righteous man: see ye [to it].
040	MAT	027	025	And all the people answered and said, His blood [be] on us, and on our children.
040	MAT	027	026	Then released he unto them Barabbas: but Jesus he scourged and delivered to be crucified.
040	MAT	027	027	Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the palace, and gathered unto him the whole band.
040	MAT	027	028	And they stripped him, and put on him a scarlet robe.
040	MAT	027	029	And they plaited a crown of thorns and put it upon his head, and a reed in his right hand; and they kneeled down before him, and mocked him, saying, Hail, King of the Jews!
040	MAT	027	030	And they spat upon him, and took the reed and smote him on the head.
040	MAT	027	031	And when they had mocked him, they took off from him the robe, and put on him his garments, and led him away to crucify him.
040	MAT	027	032	And as they came out, they found a man of Cyrene, Simon by name: him they compelled to go [with them], that he might bear his cross.
040	MAT	027	033	And when they were come unto a place called Golgotha, that is to say, The place of a skull,
040	MAT	027	034	they gave him wine to drink mingled with gall: and when he had tasted it, he would not drink.
040	MAT	027	035	And when they had crucified him, they parted his garments among them, casting lots:
040	MAT	027	036	and they sat and watched him there.
040	MAT	027	037	And they set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.
040	MAT	027	038	Then are there crucified with him two robbers, one on the right hand, and one on the left.
040	MAT	027	039	And they that passed by railed on him, wagging their heads,
040	MAT	027	040	and saying, Thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days, save thyself: if thou art the Son of God, come down from the cross.
040	MAT	027	041	In like manner also the chief priests mocking [him], with the scribes and elders, said,
040	MAT	027	042	He saved others; himself he cannot save. He is the King of Israel; let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe on him.
040	MAT	027	043	He trusteth on God; let him deliver him now, if he desireth him: for he said, I am the Son of God.
040	MAT	027	044	And the robbers also that were crucified with him cast upon him the same reproach.
040	MAT	027	045	Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land until the ninth hour.
040	MAT	027	046	And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?
040	MAT	027	047	And some of them that stood there, when they heard it, said, This man calleth Elijah.
040	MAT	027	048	And straightway one of them ran, and took a sponge, and filled it with vinegar, and put it on a reed, and gave him to drink.
040	MAT	027	049	And the rest said, Let be; let us see whether Elijah cometh to save him.
040	MAT	027	050	And Jesus cried again with a loud voice, and yielded up his spirit.
040	MAT	027	051	And behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake; and the rocks were rent;
040	MAT	027	052	and the tombs were opened; and many bodies of the saints that had fallen asleep were raised;
040	MAT	027	053	and coming forth out of the tombs after his resurrection they entered into the holy city and appeared unto many.
040	MAT	027	054	Now the centurion, and they that were with him watching Jesus, when they saw the earthquake, and the things that were done, feared exceedingly, saying, Truly this was the Son of God.
040	MAT	027	055	And many women were there beholding from afar, which had followed Jesus from Galilee, ministering unto him:
040	MAT	027	056	among whom was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James and Joses, and the mother of the sons of Zebedee.
040	MAT	027	057	And when even was come, there came a rich man from Arimathaea, named Joseph, who also himself was Jesus’ disciple:
040	MAT	027	058	this man went to Pilate, and asked for the body of Jesus. Then Pilate commanded it to be given up.
040	MAT	027	059	And Joseph took the body, and wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,
040	MAT	027	060	and laid it in his own new tomb, which he had hewn out in the rock: and he rolled a great stone to the door of the tomb, and departed.
040	MAT	027	061	And Mary Magdalene was there, and the other Mary, sitting over against the sepulchre.
040	MAT	027	062	Now on the morrow, which is [the day] after the Preparation, the chief priests and the Pharisees were gathered together unto Pilate,
040	MAT	027	063	saying, Sir, we remember that that deceiver said, while he was yet alive, After three days I rise again.
040	MAT	027	064	Command therefore that the sepulchre be made sure until the third day, lest haply his disciples come and steal him away, and say unto the people, He is risen from the dead: and the last error will be worse than the first.
040	MAT	027	065	Pilate said unto them, Ye have a guard: go your way, make it [as] sure as ye can.
040	MAT	027	066	So they went, and made the sepulchre sure, sealing the stone, the guard being with them.
040	MAT	028	001	Now late on the sabbath day, as it began to dawn toward the first [day] of the week, came Mary Magdalene and the other Mary to see the sepulchre.
040	MAT	028	002	And behold, there was a great earthquake; for an angel of the Lord descended from heaven, and came and rolled away the stone, and sat upon it.
040	MAT	028	003	His appearance was as lightning, and his raiment white as snow:
040	MAT	028	004	and for fear of him the watchers did quake, and became as dead men.
040	MAT	028	005	And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek Jesus, which hath been crucified.
040	MAT	028	006	He is not here; for he is risen, even as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.
040	MAT	028	007	And go quickly, and tell his disciples, He is risen from the dead; and lo, he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him: lo, I have told you.
040	MAT	028	008	And they departed quickly from the tomb with fear and great joy, and ran to bring his disciples word.
040	MAT	028	009	And behold, Jesus met them, saying, All hail. And they came and took hold of his feet, and worshipped him.
040	MAT	028	010	Then saith Jesus unto them, Fear not: go tell my brethren that they depart into Galilee, and there shall they see me.
040	MAT	028	011	Now while they were going, behold, some of the guard came into the city, and told unto the chief priests all the things that were come to pass.
040	MAT	028	012	And when they were assembled with the elders, and had taken counsel, they gave large money unto the soldiers,
040	MAT	028	013	saying, Say ye, His disciples came by night, and stole him away while we slept.
040	MAT	028	014	And if this come to the governor’s ears, we will persuade him, and rid you of care.
040	MAT	028	015	So they took the money, and did as they were taught: and this saying was spread abroad among the Jews, [and continueth] until this day.
040	MAT	028	016	But the eleven disciples went into Galilee, unto the mountain where Jesus had appointed them.
040	MAT	028	017	And when they saw him, they worshipped [him]: but some doubted.
040	MAT	028	018	And Jesus came to them and spake unto them, saying, All authority hath been given unto me in heaven and on earth.
040	MAT	028	019	Go ye therefore, and make disciples of all the nations, baptizing them into the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Ghost:
040	MAT	028	020	teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I commanded you: and lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world.
