# BOOK	041	MAR	Mark	Mark
041	MAR	001	001	The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.
041	MAR	001	002	Even as it is written in Isaiah the prophet, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, Who shall prepare thy way;
041	MAR	001	003	The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make ye ready the way of the Lord, Make his paths straight;
041	MAR	001	004	John came, who baptized in the wilderness and preached the baptism of repentance unto remission of sins.
041	MAR	001	005	And there went out unto him all the country of Judaea, and all they of Jerusalem; and they were baptized of him in the river Jordan, confessing their sins.
041	MAR	001	006	And John was clothed with camel’s hair, and [had] a leathern girdle about his loins, and did eat locusts and wild honey.
041	MAR	001	007	And he preached, saying, There cometh after me he that is mightier than I, the latchet of whose shoes I am not worthy to stoop down and unloose.
041	MAR	001	008	I baptized you with water; but he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost.
041	MAR	001	009	And it came to pass in those days, that Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized of John in the Jordan.
041	MAR	001	010	And straightway coming up out of the water, he saw the heavens rent asunder, and the Spirit as a dove descending upon him:
041	MAR	001	011	And a voice came out of the heavens, Thou art my beloved Son, in thee I am well pleased.
041	MAR	001	012	And straightway the Spirit driveth him forth into the wilderness.
041	MAR	001	013	And he was in the wilderness forty days tempted of Satan; and he was with the wild beasts; and the angels ministered unto him.
041	MAR	001	014	Now after that John was delivered up, Jesus came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of God,
041	MAR	001	015	and saying, The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe in the gospel.
041	MAR	001	016	And passing along by the sea of Galilee, he saw Simon and Andrew the brother of Simon casting a net in the sea: for they were fishers.
041	MAR	001	017	And Jesus said unto them, Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men.
041	MAR	001	018	And straightway they left the nets, and followed him.
041	MAR	001	019	And going on a little further, he saw James the [son] of Zebedee, and John his brother, who also were in the boat mending the nets.
041	MAR	001	020	And straightway he called them: and they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired servants, and went after him.
041	MAR	001	021	And they go into Capernaum; and straightway on the sabbath day he entered into the synagogue and taught.
041	MAR	001	022	And they were astonished at his teaching: for he taught them as having authority, and not as the scribes.
041	MAR	001	023	And straightway there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit; and he cried out,
041	MAR	001	024	saying, What have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God.
041	MAR	001	025	And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him.
041	MAR	001	026	And the unclean spirit, tearing him and crying with a loud voice, came out of him.
041	MAR	001	027	And they were all amazed, insomuch that they questioned among themselves, saying, What is this? a new teaching! with authority he commandeth even the unclean spirits, and they obey him.
041	MAR	001	028	And the report of him went out straightway everywhere into all the region of Galilee round about.
041	MAR	001	029	And straightway, when they were come out of the synagogue, they came into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John.
041	MAR	001	030	Now Simon’s wife’s mother lay sick of a fever; and straightway they tell him of her:
041	MAR	001	031	and he came and took her by the hand, and raised her up; and the fever left her, and she ministered unto them.
041	MAR	001	032	And at even, when the sun did set, they brought unto him all that were sick, and them that were possessed with devils.
041	MAR	001	033	And all the city was gathered together at the door.
041	MAR	001	034	And he healed many that were sick with divers diseases, and cast out many devils; and he suffered not the devils to speak, because they knew him.
041	MAR	001	035	And in the morning, a great while before day, he rose up and went out, and departed into a desert place, and there prayed.
