041	MAR	015	013	And they cried out again, Crucify him.
041	MAR	015	014	And Pilate said unto them, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out exceedingly, Crucify him.
041	MAR	015	015	And Pilate, wishing to content the multitude, released unto them Barabbas, and delivered Jesus, when he had scourged him, to be crucified.
041	MAR	015	016	And the soldiers led him away within the court, which is the Praetorium; and they call together the whole band.
041	MAR	015	017	And they clothe him with purple, and plaiting a crown of thorns, they put it on him;
041	MAR	015	018	and they began to salute him, Hail, King of the Jews!
041	MAR	015	019	And they smote his head with a reed, and did spit upon him, and bowing their knees worshipped him.
041	MAR	015	020	And when they had mocked him, they took off from him the purple, and put on him his garments. And they lead him out to crucify him.
041	MAR	015	021	And they compel one passing by, Simon of Cyrene, coming from the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to go [with them], that he might bear his cross.
041	MAR	015	022	And they bring him unto the place Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, The place of a skull.
041	MAR	015	023	And they offered him wine mingled with myrrh: but he received it not.
041	MAR	015	024	And they crucify him, and part his garments among them, casting lots upon them, what each should take.
041	MAR	015	025	And it was the third hour, and they crucified him.
041	MAR	015	026	And the superscription of his accusation was written over, THE KING OF THE JEWS.
041	MAR	015	027	And with him they crucify two robbers; one on his right hand, and one on his left.
041	MAR	015	029	And they that passed by railed on him, wagging their heads, and saying, Ha! thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days,
041	MAR	015	030	save thyself, and come down from the cross.
041	MAR	015	031	In like manner also the chief priests mocking [him] among themselves with the scribes said, He saved others; himself he cannot save.
041	MAR	015	032	Let the Christ, the King of Israel, now come down from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with him reproached him.
041	MAR	015	033	And when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour.
041	MAR	015	034	And at the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani? which is, being interpreted, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?
041	MAR	015	035	And some of them that stood by, when they heard it, said, Behold, he calleth Elijah.
041	MAR	015	036	And one ran, and filling a sponge full of vinegar, put it on a reed, and gave him to drink, saying, Let be; let us see whether Elijah cometh to take him down.
041	MAR	015	037	And Jesus uttered a loud voice, and gave up the ghost.
041	MAR	015	038	And the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.
041	MAR	015	039	And when the centurion, which stood by over against him, saw that he so gave up the ghost, he said, Truly this man was the Son of God.
041	MAR	015	040	And there were also women beholding from afar: among whom [were] both Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses, and Salome;
041	MAR	015	041	who, when he was in Galilee, followed him, and ministered unto him; and many other women which came up with him unto Jerusalem.
041	MAR	015	042	And when even was now come, because it was the Preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath,
041	MAR	015	043	there came Joseph of Arimathaea, a councillor of honourable estate, who also himself was looking for the kingdom of God; and he boldly went in unto Pilate, and asked for the body of Jesus.
041	MAR	015	044	And Pilate marveled if he were already dead: and calling unto him the centurion, he asked him whether he had been any while dead.
041	MAR	015	045	And when he learned it of the centurion, he granted the corpse to Joseph.
041	MAR	015	046	And he bought a linen cloth, and taking him down, wound him in the linen cloth, and laid him in a tomb which had been hewn out of a rock; and he rolled a stone against the door of the tomb.
041	MAR	015	047	And Mary Magdalene and Mary the [mother] of Joses beheld where he was laid.
041	MAR	016	001	And when the sabbath was past, Mary Magdalene, and Mary the [mother] of James, and Salome, bought spices, that they might come and anoint him.
041	MAR	016	002	And very early on the first day of the week, they come to the tomb when the sun was risen.
041	MAR	016	003	And they were saying among themselves, Who shall roll us away the stone from the door of the tomb?
041	MAR	016	004	and looking up, they see that the stone is rolled back: for it was exceeding great.
041	MAR	016	005	And entering into the tomb, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, arrayed in a white robe; and they were amazed.
041	MAR	016	006	And he saith unto them, Be not amazed: ye seek Jesus, the Nazarene, which hath been crucified: he is risen; he is not here: behold, the place where they laid him!
041	MAR	016	007	But go, tell his disciples and Peter, He goeth before you into Galilee: there shall ye see him, as he said unto you.
041	MAR	016	008	And they went out, and fled from the tomb; for trembling and astonishment had come upon them: and they said nothing to any one; for they were afraid.
041	MAR	016	009	(note: The most reliable and earliest manuscripts do not include Mark 16:9-20.) Now when he was risen early on the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom he had cast out seven devils.
041	MAR	016	010	She went and told them that had been with him, as they mourned and wept.
041	MAR	016	011	And they, when they heard that he was alive, and had been seen of her, disbelieved.
041	MAR	016	012	And after these things he was manifested in another form unto two of them, as they walked, on their way into the country.
041	MAR	016	013	And they went away and told it unto the rest: neither believed they them.
041	MAR	016	014	And afterward he was manifested unto the eleven themselves as they sat at meat; and he upbraided them with their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they believed not them which had seen him after he was risen.
041	MAR	016	015	And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to the whole creation.
041	MAR	016	016	He that believeth and is baptized shall be saved; but he that disbelieveth shall be condemned.
041	MAR	016	017	And these signs shall follow them that believe: in my name shall they cast out devils; they shall speak with new tongues;
041	MAR	016	018	they shall take up serpents, and if they drink any deadly thing, it shall in no wise hurt them; they shall lay hands on the sick, and they shall recover.
041	MAR	016	019	So then the Lord Jesus, after he had spoken unto them, was received up into heaven, and sat down at the right hand of God.
041	MAR	016	020	And they went forth, and preached everywhere, the Lord working with them, and confirming the word by the signs that followed. Amen.
