# BOOK	042	LUK	Luke	Luke
042	LUK	001	001	Forasmuch as many have taken in hand to draw up a narrative concerning those matters which have been fulfilled among us,
042	LUK	001	002	even as they delivered them unto us, which from the beginning were eyewitnesses and ministers of the word,
042	LUK	001	003	it seemed good to me also, having traced the course of all things accurately from the first, to write unto thee in order, most excellent Theophilus;
042	LUK	001	004	that thou mightest know the certainty concerning the things wherein thou wast instructed.
042	LUK	001	005	There was in the days of Herod, king of Judaea, a certain priest named Zacharias, of the course of Abijah: and he had a wife of the daughters of Aaron, and her name was Elisabeth.
042	LUK	001	006	And they were both righteous before God, walking in all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord blameless.
042	LUK	001	007	And they had no child, because that Elisabeth was barren, and they both were [now] well stricken in years.
042	LUK	001	008	Now it came to pass, while he executed the priest’s office before God in the order of his course,
042	LUK	001	009	according to the custom of the priest’s office, his lot was to enter into the temple of the Lord and burn incense.
042	LUK	001	010	And the whole multitude of the people were praying without at the hour of incense.
042	LUK	001	011	And there appeared unto him an angel of the Lord standing on the right side of the altar of incense.
042	LUK	001	012	And Zacharias was troubled when he saw [him], and fear fell upon him.
042	LUK	001	013	But the angel said unto him, Fear not, Zacharias: because thy supplication is heard, and thy wife Elisabeth shall bear thee a son, and thou shalt call his name John.
042	LUK	001	014	And thou shalt have joy and gladness; and many shall rejoice at his birth.
042	LUK	001	015	For he shall be great in the sight of the Lord, and he shall drink no wine nor strong drink; and he shall be filled with the Holy Ghost, even from his mother’s womb.
042	LUK	001	016	And many of the children of Israel shall he turn unto the Lord their God.
042	LUK	001	017	And he shall go before his face in the spirit and power of Elijah, to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children, and the disobedient [to walk] in the wisdom of the just; to make ready for the Lord a people prepared [for him].
042	LUK	001	018	And Zacharias said unto the angel, Whereby shall I know this? for I am an old man, and my wife well stricken in years.
042	LUK	001	019	And the angel answering said unto him, I am Gabriel, that stand in the presence of God; and I was sent to speak unto thee, and to bring thee these good tidings.
042	LUK	001	020	And behold, thou shalt be silent and not able to speak, until the day that these things shall come to pass, because thou believedst not my words, which shall be fulfilled in their season.
042	LUK	001	021	And the people were waiting for Zacharias, and they marveled while he tarried in the temple.
042	LUK	001	022	And when he came out, he could not speak unto them: and they perceived that he had seen a vision in the temple: and he continued making signs unto them, and remained dumb.
042	LUK	001	023	And it came to pass, when the days of his ministration were fulfilled, he departed unto his house.
042	LUK	001	024	And after these days Elisabeth his wife conceived; and she hid herself five months, saying,
