# BOOK	043	JOH	John	John
043	JOH	001	001	In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.
043	JOH	001	002	The same was in the beginning with God.
043	JOH	001	003	All things were made by him; and without him was not anything made that hath been made.
043	JOH	001	004	In him was life; and the life was the light of men.
043	JOH	001	005	And the light shineth in the darkness; and the darkness apprehended it not.
043	JOH	001	006	There came a man, sent from God, whose name was John.
043	JOH	001	007	The same came for witness, that he might bear witness of the light, that all might believe through him.
043	JOH	001	008	He was not the light, but [came] that he might bear witness of the light.
043	JOH	001	009	There was the true light, [even the light] which lighteth every man, coming into the world.
043	JOH	001	010	He was in the world, and the world was made by him, and the world knew him not.
043	JOH	001	011	He came unto his own, and they that were his own received him not.
043	JOH	001	012	But as many as received him, to them gave he the right to become children of God, [even] to them that believe on his name:
043	JOH	001	013	which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.
043	JOH	001	014	And the Word became flesh, and dwelt among us (and we beheld his glory, glory as of the only begotten from the Father), full of grace and truth.
043	JOH	001	015	John beareth witness of him, and crieth, saying, This was he of whom I said, He that cometh after me is become before me: for he was before me.
043	JOH	001	016	For of his fulness we all received, and grace for grace.
043	JOH	001	017	For the law was given by Moses; grace and truth came by Jesus Christ.
043	JOH	001	018	No man hath seen God at any time; the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared [him].
043	JOH	001	019	And this is the witness of John, when the Jews sent unto him from Jerusalem priests and Levites to ask him, Who art thou?
043	JOH	001	020	And he confessed, and denied not; and he confessed, I am not the Christ.
043	JOH	001	021	And they asked him, What then? Art thou Elijah? And he saith, I am not. Art thou the prophet? And he answered, No.
043	JOH	001	022	They said therefore unto him, Who art thou? that we may give an answer to them that sent us. What sayest thou of thyself?
043	JOH	001	023	He said, I am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, Make straight the way of the Lord, as said Isaiah the prophet.
043	JOH	001	024	And they had been sent from the Pharisees.
043	JOH	001	025	And they asked him, and said unto him, Why then baptizest thou, if thou art not the Christ, neither Elijah, neither the prophet?
043	JOH	001	026	John answered them, saying, I baptize with water: in the midst of you standeth one whom ye know not,
043	JOH	001	027	[even] he that cometh after me, the latchet of whose shoe I am not worthy to unloose.
043	JOH	001	028	These things were done in Bethany beyond Jordan, where John was baptizing.
043	JOH	001	029	On the morrow he seeth Jesus coming unto him, and saith, Behold, the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world!
043	JOH	001	030	This is he of whom I said, After me cometh a man which is become before me: for he was before me.
043	JOH	001	031	And I knew him not; but that he should be made manifest to Israel, for this cause came I baptizing with water.
043	JOH	001	032	And John bare witness, saying, I have beheld the Spirit descending as a dove out of heaven; and it abode upon him.
043	JOH	001	033	And I knew him not: but he that sent me to baptize with water, he said unto me, Upon whomsoever thou shalt see the Spirit descending, and abiding upon him, the same is he that baptizeth with the Holy Spirit.
043	JOH	001	034	And I have seen, and have borne witness that this is the Son of God.
043	JOH	001	035	Again on the morrow John was standing, and two of his disciples;
043	JOH	001	036	and he looked upon Jesus as he walked, and saith, Behold, the Lamb of God!
043	JOH	001	037	And the two disciples heard him speak, and they followed Jesus.
043	JOH	001	038	And Jesus turned, and beheld them following, and saith unto them, What seek ye? And they said unto him, Rabbi (which is to say, being interpreted, Master), where abidest thou?
043	JOH	001	039	He saith unto them, Come, and ye shall see. They came therefore and saw where he abode; and they abode with him that day: it was about the tenth hour.
043	JOH	001	040	One of the two that heard John [speak], and followed him, was Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother.
043	JOH	001	041	He findeth first his own brother Simon, and saith unto him, We have found the Messiah (which is, being interpreted, Christ).
043	JOH	001	042	He brought him unto Jesus. Jesus looked upon him, and said, Thou art Simon the son of John: thou shalt be called Cephas (which is by interpretation, Peter).
043	JOH	001	043	On the morrow he was minded to go forth into Galilee, and he findeth Philip: and Jesus saith unto him, Follow me.
043	JOH	001	044	Now Philip was from Bethsaida, of the city of Andrew and Peter.
043	JOH	001	045	Philip findeth Nathanael, and saith unto him, We have found him, of whom Moses in the law, and the prophets, did write, Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.
043	JOH	001	046	And Nathanael said unto him, Can any good thing come out of Nazareth? Philip saith unto him, Come and see.
043	JOH	001	047	Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him, and saith of him, Behold, an Israelite indeed, in whom is no guile!
043	JOH	001	048	Nathanael saith unto him, Whence knowest thou me? Jesus answered and said unto him, Before Philip called thee, when thou wast under the fig tree, I saw thee.
043	JOH	001	049	Nathanael answered him, Rabbi, thou art the Son of God; thou art King of Israel.
043	JOH	001	050	Jesus answered and said unto him, Because I said unto thee, I saw thee underneath the fig tree, believest thou? thou shalt see greater things than these.
043	JOH	001	051	And he saith unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Ye shall see the heaven opened, and the angels of God ascending and descending upon the Son of man.
043	JOH	002	001	And the third day there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee; and the mother of Jesus was there:
043	JOH	002	002	and Jesus also was bidden, and his disciples, to the marriage.
043	JOH	002	003	And when the wine failed, the mother of Jesus saith unto him, They have no wine.
043	JOH	002	004	And Jesus saith unto her, Woman, what have I to do with thee? mine hour is not yet come.
043	JOH	002	005	His mother saith unto the servants, Whatsoever he saith unto you, do it.
043	JOH	002	006	Now there were six waterpots of stone set there after the Jews’ manner of purifying, containing two or three firkins apiece.
043	JOH	002	007	Jesus saith unto them, Fill the waterpots with water. And they filled them up to the brim.
043	JOH	002	008	And he saith unto them, Draw out now, and bear unto the ruler of the feast. And they bare it.
043	JOH	002	009	And when the ruler of the feast tasted the water now become wine, and knew not whence it was (but the servants which had drawn the water knew), the ruler of the feast calleth the bridegroom,
043	JOH	002	010	and saith unto him, Every man setteth on first the good wine; and when [men] have drunk freely, [then] that which is worse: thou hast kept the good wine until now.
043	JOH	002	011	This beginning of his signs did Jesus in Cana of Galilee, and manifested his glory; and his disciples believed on him.
043	JOH	002	012	After this he went down to Capernaum, he, and his mother, and [his] brethren, and his disciples: and there they abode not many days.
043	JOH	002	013	And the passover of the Jews was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	002	014	And he found in the temple those that sold oxen and sheep and doves, and the changers of money sitting:
043	JOH	002	015	and he made a scourge of cords, and cast all out of the temple, both the sheep and the oxen; and he poured out the changers’ money, and overthrew their tables;
043	JOH	002	016	and to them that sold the doves he said, Take these things hence; make not my Father’s house a house of merchandise.
043	JOH	002	017	His disciples remembered that it was written, The zeal of thine house shall eat me up.
043	JOH	002	018	The Jews therefore answered and said unto him, What sign shewest thou unto us, seeing that thou doest these things?
043	JOH	002	019	Jesus answered and said unto them, Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.
043	JOH	002	020	The Jews therefore said, Forty and six years was this temple in building, and wilt thou raise it up in three days?
043	JOH	002	021	But he spake of the temple of his body.
043	JOH	002	022	When therefore he was raised from the dead, his disciples remembered that he spake this; and they believed the scripture, and the word which Jesus had said.
043	JOH	002	023	Now when he was in Jerusalem at the passover, during the feast, many believed on his name, beholding his signs which he did.
043	JOH	002	024	But Jesus did not trust himself unto them, for that he knew all men,
043	JOH	002	025	and because he needed not that any one should bear witness concerning man; for he himself knew what was in man.
043	JOH	003	001	Now there was a man of the Pharisees, named Nicodemus, a ruler of the Jews:
043	JOH	003	002	The same came unto him by night, and said to him, Rabbi, we know that thou art a teacher come from God: for no man can do these signs that thou doest, except God be with him.
043	JOH	003	003	Jesus answered and said unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born anew, he cannot see the kingdom of God.
043	JOH	003	004	Nicodemus saith unto him, How can a man be born when he is old? can he enter a second time into his mother’s womb, and be born?
043	JOH	003	005	Jesus answered, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter into the kingdom of God.
043	JOH	003	006	That which is born of the flesh is flesh; and that which is born of the Spirit is spirit.
043	JOH	003	007	Marvel not that I said unto thee, Ye must be born anew.
043	JOH	003	008	The wind bloweth where it listeth, and thou hearest the voice thereof, but knowest not whence it cometh, and whither it goeth: so is every one that is born of the Spirit.
043	JOH	003	009	Nicodemus answered and said unto him, How can these things be?
043	JOH	003	010	Jesus answered and said unto him, Art thou the teacher of Israel, and understandest not these things?
043	JOH	003	011	Verily, verily, I say unto thee, We speak that we do know, and bear witness of that we have seen; and ye receive not our witness.
043	JOH	003	012	If I told you earthly things, and ye believe not, how shall ye believe, if I tell you heavenly things?
043	JOH	003	013	And no man hath ascended into heaven, but he that descended out of heaven, [even] the Son of man, which is in heaven.
043	JOH	003	014	And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of man be lifted up:
043	JOH	003	015	that whosoever believeth may in him have eternal life.
043	JOH	003	016	For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth on him should not perish, but have eternal life.
043	JOH	003	017	For God sent not the Son into the world to judge the world; but that the world should be saved through him.
043	JOH	003	018	He that believeth on him is not judged: he that believeth not hath been judged already, because he hath not believed on the name of the only begotten Son of God.
043	JOH	003	019	And this is the judgment, that the light is come into the world, and men loved the darkness rather than the light; for their works were evil.
043	JOH	003	020	For every one that doeth ill hateth the light, and cometh not to the light, lest his works should be reproved.
043	JOH	003	021	But he that doeth the truth cometh to the light, that his works may be made manifest, that they have been wrought in God.
043	JOH	003	022	After these things came Jesus and his disciples into the land of Judaea; and there he tarried with them, and baptized.
043	JOH	003	023	And John also was baptizing in AEnon near to Salim, because there was much water there: and they came, and were baptized.
043	JOH	003	024	For John was not yet cast into prison.
043	JOH	003	025	There arose therefore a questioning on the part of John’s disciples with a Jew about purifying.
043	JOH	003	026	And they came unto John, and said to him, Rabbi, he that was with thee beyond Jordan, to whom thou hast borne witness, behold, the same baptizeth, and all men come to him.
043	JOH	003	027	John answered and said, A man can receive nothing, except it have been given him from heaven.
043	JOH	003	028	Ye yourselves bear me witness, that I said, I am not the Christ, but, that I am sent before him.
043	JOH	003	029	He that hath the bride is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, which standeth and heareth him, rejoiceth greatly because of the bridegroom’s voice: this my joy therefore is fulfilled.
043	JOH	003	030	He must increase, but I must decrease.
043	JOH	003	031	He that cometh from above is above all: he that is of the earth is of the earth, and of the earth he speaketh: he that cometh from heaven is above all.
043	JOH	003	032	What he hath seen and heard, of that he beareth witness; and no man receiveth his witness.
043	JOH	003	033	He that hath received his witness hath set his seal to [this], that God is true.
043	JOH	003	034	For he whom God hath sent speaketh the words of God: for he giveth not the Spirit by measure.
043	JOH	003	035	The Father loveth the Son, and hath given all things into his hand.
043	JOH	003	036	He that believeth on the Son hath eternal life; but he that obeyeth not the Son shall not see life, but the wrath of God abideth on him.
043	JOH	004	001	When therefore the Lord knew how that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus was making and baptizing more disciples than John
043	JOH	004	002	(although Jesus himself baptized not, but his disciples),
043	JOH	004	003	he left Judaea, and departed again into Galilee.
043	JOH	004	004	And he must needs pass through Samaria.
043	JOH	004	005	So he cometh to a city of Samaria, called Sychar, near to the parcel of ground that Jacob gave to his son Joseph:
043	JOH	004	006	and Jacob’s well was there. Jesus therefore, being wearied with his journey, sat thus by the well. It was about the sixth hour.
043	JOH	004	007	There cometh a woman of Samaria to draw water: Jesus saith unto her, Give me to drink.
043	JOH	004	008	For his disciples were gone away into the city to buy food.
043	JOH	004	009	The Samaritan woman therefore saith unto him, How is it that thou, being a Jew, askest drink of me, which am a Samaritan woman? (For Jews have no dealings with Samaritans.)
043	JOH	004	010	Jesus answered and said unto her, If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldest have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water.
043	JOH	004	011	The woman saith unto him, Sir, thou hast nothing to draw with, and the well is deep: from whence then hast thou that living water?
043	JOH	004	012	Art thou greater than our father Jacob, which gave us the well, and drank thereof himself, and his sons, and his cattle?
043	JOH	004	013	Jesus answered and said unto her, Every one that drinketh of this water shall thirst again:
043	JOH	004	014	but whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall become in him a well of water springing up unto eternal life.
043	JOH	004	015	The woman saith unto him, Sir, give me this water, that I thirst not, neither come all the way hither to draw.
043	JOH	004	016	Jesus saith unto her, Go, call thy husband, and come hither.
043	JOH	004	017	The woman answered and said unto him, I have no husband. Jesus saith unto her, Thou saidst well, I have no husband:
043	JOH	004	018	for thou hast had five husbands; and he whom thou now hast is not thy husband: this hast thou said truly.
043	JOH	004	019	The woman saith unto him, Sir, I perceive that thou art a prophet.
043	JOH	004	020	Our fathers worshipped in this mountain; and ye say, that in Jerusalem is the place where men ought to worship.
043	JOH	004	021	Jesus saith unto her, Woman, believe me, the hour cometh, when neither in this mountain, nor in Jerusalem, shall ye worship the Father.
043	JOH	004	022	Ye worship that which ye know not: we worship that which we know: for salvation is from the Jews.
043	JOH	004	023	But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and truth: for such doth the Father seek to be his worshippers.
043	JOH	004	024	God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship in spirit and truth.
043	JOH	004	025	The woman saith unto him, I know that Messiah cometh (which is called Christ): when he is come, he will declare unto us all things.
043	JOH	004	026	Jesus saith unto her, I that speak unto thee am [he].
043	JOH	004	027	And upon this came his disciples; and they marveled that he was speaking with a woman; yet no man said, What seekest thou? or, Why speakest thou with her?
043	JOH	004	028	So the woman left her waterpot, and went away into the city, and saith to the men,
043	JOH	004	029	Come, see a man, which told me all things that [ever] I did: can this be the Christ?
043	JOH	004	030	They went out of the city, and were coming to him.
043	JOH	004	031	In the mean while the disciples prayed him, saying, Rabbi, eat.
043	JOH	004	032	But he said unto them, I have meat to eat that ye know not.
043	JOH	004	033	The disciples therefore said one to another, Hath any man brought him [aught] to eat?
043	JOH	004	034	Jesus saith unto them, My meat is to do the will of him that sent me, and to accomplish his work.
043	JOH	004	035	Say not ye, There are yet four months, and [then] cometh the harvest? behold, I say unto you, Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields, that they are white already unto harvest.
043	JOH	004	036	He that reapeth receiveth wages, and gathereth fruit unto life eternal; that he that soweth and he that reapeth may rejoice together.
043	JOH	004	037	For herein is the saying true, One soweth, and another reapeth.
043	JOH	004	038	I sent you to reap that whereon ye have not laboured: others have laboured, and ye are entered into their labour.
043	JOH	004	039	And from that city many of the Samaritans believed on him because of the word of the woman, who testified, He told me all things that [ever] I did.
043	JOH	004	040	So when the Samaritans came unto him, they besought him to abide with them: and he abode there two days.
043	JOH	004	041	And many more believed because of his word;
043	JOH	004	042	and they said to the woman, Now we believe, not because of thy speaking: for we have heard for ourselves, and know that this is indeed the Saviour of the world.
043	JOH	004	043	And after the two days he went forth from thence into Galilee.
043	JOH	004	044	For Jesus himself testified, that a prophet hath no honour in his own country.
043	JOH	004	045	So when he came into Galilee, the Galilaeans received him, having seen all the things that he did in Jerusalem at the feast: for they also went unto the feast.
043	JOH	004	046	He came therefore again unto Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain nobleman, whose son was sick at Capernaum.
043	JOH	004	047	When he heard that Jesus was come out of Judaea into Galilee, he went unto him, and besought [him] that he would come down, and heal his son; for he was at the point of death.
043	JOH	004	048	Jesus therefore said unto him, Except ye see signs and wonders, ye will in no wise believe.
043	JOH	004	049	The nobleman saith unto him, Sir, come down ere my child die.
043	JOH	004	050	Jesus saith unto him, Go thy way; thy son liveth. The man believed the word that Jesus spake unto him, and he went his way.
043	JOH	004	051	And as he was now going down, his servants met him, saying, that his son lived.
043	JOH	004	052	So he inquired of them the hour when he began to amend. They said therefore unto him, Yesterday at the seventh hour the fever left him.
043	JOH	004	053	So the father knew that [it was] at that hour in which Jesus said unto him, Thy son liveth: and himself believed, and his whole house.
043	JOH	004	054	This is again the second sign that Jesus did, having come out of Judaea into Galilee.
043	JOH	005	001	After these things there was a feast of the Jews; and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	005	002	Now there is in Jerusalem by the sheep [gate] a pool, which is called in Hebrew Bethesda, having five porches.
043	JOH	005	003	In these lay a multitude of them that were sick, blind, halt, withered.
043	JOH	005	005	And a certain man was there, which had been thirty and eight years in his infirmity.
043	JOH	005	006	When Jesus saw him lying, and knew that he had been now a long time [in that case], he saith unto him, Wouldest thou be made whole?
043	JOH	005	007	The sick man answered him, Sir, I have no man, when the water is troubled, to put me into the pool: but while I am coming, another steppeth down before me.
043	JOH	005	008	Jesus saith unto him, Arise, take up thy bed, and walk.
043	JOH	005	009	And straightway the man was made whole, and took up his bed and walked. Now it was the sabbath on that day.
043	JOH	005	010	So the Jews said unto him that was cured, It is the sabbath, and it is not lawful for thee to take up thy bed.
043	JOH	005	011	But he answered them, He that made me whole, the same said unto me, Take up thy bed, and walk.
043	JOH	005	012	They asked him, Who is the man that said unto thee, Take up [thy bed], and walk?
043	JOH	005	013	But he that was healed wist not who it was: for Jesus had conveyed himself away, a multitude being in the place.
043	JOH	005	014	Afterward Jesus findeth him in the temple, and said unto him, Behold, thou art made whole: sin no more, lest a worse thing befall thee.
043	JOH	005	015	The man went away, and told the Jews that it was Jesus which had made him whole.
043	JOH	005	016	And for this cause did the Jews persecute Jesus, because he did these things on the sabbath.
043	JOH	005	017	But Jesus answered them, My Father worketh even until now, and I work.
043	JOH	005	018	For this cause therefore the Jews sought the more to kill him, because he not only brake the sabbath, but also called God his own Father, making himself equal with God.
043	JOH	005	019	Jesus therefore answered and said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, The Son can do nothing of himself, but what he seeth the Father doing: for what things soever he doeth, these the Son also doeth in like manner.
043	JOH	005	020	For the Father loveth the Son, and sheweth him all things that himself doeth: and greater works than these will he shew him, that ye may marvel.
043	JOH	005	021	For as the Father raiseth the dead and quickeneth them, even so the Son also quickeneth whom he will.
043	JOH	005	022	For neither doth the Father judge any man, but he hath given all judgment unto the Son;
043	JOH	005	023	that all may honour the Son, even as they honour the Father. He that honoureth not the Son honoureth not the Father which sent him.
043	JOH	005	024	Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that heareth my word, and believeth him that sent me, hath eternal life, and cometh not into judgment, but hath passed out of death into life.
043	JOH	005	025	Verily, verily, I say unto you, The hour cometh, and now is, when the dead shall hear the voice of the Son of God; and they that hear shall live.
043	JOH	005	026	For as the Father hath life in himself, even so gave he to the Son also to have life in himself:
043	JOH	005	027	and he gave him authority to execute judgment, because he is the Son of man.
043	JOH	005	028	Marvel not at this: for the hour cometh, in which all that are in the tombs shall hear his voice,
043	JOH	005	029	And shall come forth; they that have done good, unto the resurrection of life; and they that have done ill, unto the resurrection of judgment.
043	JOH	005	030	I can of myself do nothing: as I hear, I judge: and my judgment is righteous; because I seek not mine own will, but the will of him that sent me.
043	JOH	005	031	If I bear witness of myself, my witness is not true.
043	JOH	005	032	It is another that beareth witness of me; and I know that the witness which he witnesseth of me is true.
043	JOH	005	033	Ye have sent unto John, and he hath borne witness unto the truth.
043	JOH	005	034	But the witness which I receive is not from man: howbeit I say these things, that ye may be saved.
043	JOH	005	035	He was the lamp that burneth and shineth: and ye were willing to rejoice for a season in his light.
043	JOH	005	036	But the witness which I have is greater than [that of] John: for the works which the Father hath given me to accomplish, the very works that I do, bear witness of me, that the Father hath sent me.
043	JOH	005	037	And the Father which sent me, he hath borne witness of me. Ye have neither heard his voice at any time, nor seen his form.
043	JOH	005	038	And ye have not his word abiding in you: for whom he sent, him ye believe not.
043	JOH	005	039	Ye search the scriptures, because ye think that in them ye have eternal life; and these are they which bear witness of me;
043	JOH	005	040	and ye will not come to me, that ye may have life.
043	JOH	005	041	I receive not glory from men.
043	JOH	005	042	But I know you, that ye have not the love of God in yourselves.
043	JOH	005	043	I am come in my Father’s name, and ye receive me not: if another shall come in his own name, him ye will receive.
043	JOH	005	044	How can ye believe, which receive glory one of another, and the glory that [cometh] from the only God ye seek not?
043	JOH	005	045	Think not that I will accuse you to the Father: there is one that accuseth you, [even] Moses, on whom ye have set your hope.
043	JOH	005	046	For if ye believed Moses, ye would believe me; for he wrote of me.
043	JOH	005	047	But if ye believe not his writings, how shall ye believe my words?
043	JOH	006	001	After these things Jesus went away to the other side of the sea of Galilee, which is [the sea] of Tiberias.
043	JOH	006	002	And a great multitude followed him, because they beheld the signs which he did on them that were sick.
043	JOH	006	003	And Jesus went up into the mountain, and there he sat with his disciples.
043	JOH	006	004	Now the passover, the feast of the Jews, was at hand.
043	JOH	006	005	Jesus therefore lifting up his eyes, and seeing that a great multitude cometh unto him, saith unto Philip, Whence are we to buy bread, that these may eat?
043	JOH	006	006	And this he said to prove him: for he himself knew what he would do.
043	JOH	006	007	Philip answered him, Two hundred pennyworth of bread is not sufficient for them, that every one may take a little.
043	JOH	006	008	One of his disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, saith unto him,
043	JOH	006	009	There is a lad here, which hath five barley loaves, and two fishes: but what are these among so many?
043	JOH	006	010	Jesus said, Make the people sit down. Now there was much grass in the place. So the men sat down, in number about five thousand.
043	JOH	006	011	Jesus therefore took the loaves; and having given thanks, he distributed to them that were set down; likewise also of the fishes as much as they would.
043	JOH	006	012	And when they were filled, he saith unto his disciples, Gather up the broken pieces which remain over, that nothing be lost.
043	JOH	006	013	So they gathered them up, and filled twelve baskets with broken pieces from the five barley loaves, which remained over unto them that had eaten.
043	JOH	006	014	When therefore the people saw the sign which he did, they said, This is of a truth the prophet that cometh into the world.
043	JOH	006	015	Jesus therefore perceiving that they were about to come and take him by force, to make him king, withdrew again into the mountain himself alone.
043	JOH	006	016	And when evening came, his disciples went down unto the sea;
043	JOH	006	017	and they entered into a boat, and were going over the sea unto Capernaum. And it was now dark, and Jesus had not yet come to them.
043	JOH	006	018	And the sea was rising by reason of a great wind that blew.
043	JOH	006	019	When therefore they had rowed about five and twenty or thirty furlongs, they behold Jesus walking on the sea, and drawing nigh unto the boat: and they were afraid.
043	JOH	006	020	But he saith unto them, It is I; be not afraid.
043	JOH	006	021	They were willing therefore to receive him into the boat: and straightway the boat was at the land whither they were going.
043	JOH	006	022	On the morrow the multitude which stood on the other side of the sea saw that there was none other boat there, save one, and that Jesus entered not with his disciples into the boat, but [that] his disciples went away alone
043	JOH	006	023	(howbeit there came boats from Tiberias nigh unto the place where they ate the bread after the Lord had given thanks):
043	JOH	006	024	when the multitude therefore saw that Jesus was not there, neither his disciples, they themselves got into the boats, and came to Capernaum, seeking Jesus.
043	JOH	006	025	And when they found him on the other side of the sea, they said unto him, Rabbi, when camest thou hither?
043	JOH	006	026	Jesus answered them and said, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Ye seek me, not because ye saw signs, but because ye ate of the loaves, and were filled.
043	JOH	006	027	Work not for the meat which perisheth, but for the meat which abideth unto eternal life, which the Son of man shall give unto you: for him the Father, [even] God, hath sealed.
043	JOH	006	028	They said therefore unto him, What must we do, that we may work the works of God?
043	JOH	006	029	Jesus answered and said unto them, This is the work of God, that ye believe on him whom he hath sent.
043	JOH	006	030	They said therefore unto him, What then doest thou for a sign, that we may see, and believe thee? what workest thou?
043	JOH	006	031	Our fathers ate the manna in the wilderness; as it is written, He gave them bread out of heaven to eat.
043	JOH	006	032	Jesus therefore said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, It was not Moses that gave you the bread out of heaven; but my Father giveth you the true bread out of heaven.
043	JOH	006	033	For the bread of God is that which cometh down out of heaven, and giveth life unto the world.
043	JOH	006	034	They said therefore unto him, Lord, evermore give us this bread.
043	JOH	006	035	Jesus said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall not hunger, and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.
043	JOH	006	036	But I said unto you, that ye have seen me, and yet believe not.
043	JOH	006	037	All that which the Father giveth me shall come unto me; and him that cometh to me I will in no wise cast out.
043	JOH	006	038	For I am come down from heaven, not to do mine own will, but the will of him that sent me.
043	JOH	006	039	And this is the will of him that sent me, that of all that which he hath given me I should lose nothing, but should raise it up at the last day.
043	JOH	006	040	For this is the will of my Father, that every one that beholdeth the Son, and believeth on him, should have eternal life; and I will raise him up at the last day.
043	JOH	006	041	The Jews therefore murmured concerning him, because he said, I am the bread which came down out of heaven.
043	JOH	006	042	And they said, Is not this Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? how doth he now say, I am come down out of heaven?
043	JOH	006	043	Jesus answered and said unto them, Murmur not among yourselves.
043	JOH	006	044	No man can come to me, except the Father which sent me draw him: and I will raise him up in the last day.
043	JOH	006	045	It is written in the prophets, And they shall all be taught of God. Every one that hath heard from the Father, and hath learned, cometh unto me.
043	JOH	006	046	Not that any man hath seen the Father, save he which is from God, he hath seen the Father.
043	JOH	006	047	Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that believeth hath eternal life.
043	JOH	006	048	I am the bread of life.
043	JOH	006	049	Your fathers did eat the manna in the wilderness, and they died.
043	JOH	006	050	This is the bread which cometh down out of heaven, that a man may eat thereof, and not die.
043	JOH	006	051	I am the living bread which came down out of heaven: if any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever: yea and the bread which I will give is my flesh, for the life of the world.
043	JOH	006	052	The Jews therefore strove one with another, saying, How can this man give us his flesh to eat?
043	JOH	006	053	Jesus therefore said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except ye eat the flesh of the Son of man and drink his blood, ye have not life in yourselves.
043	JOH	006	054	He that eateth my flesh and drinketh my blood hath eternal life; and I will raise him up at the last day.
043	JOH	006	055	For my flesh is meat indeed, and my blood is drink indeed.
043	JOH	006	056	He that eateth my flesh and drinketh my blood abideth in me, and I in him.
043	JOH	006	057	As the living Father sent me, and I live because of the Father; so he that eateth me, he also shall live because of me.
043	JOH	006	058	This is the bread which came down out of heaven: not as the fathers did eat, and died: he that eateth this bread shall live for ever.
043	JOH	006	059	These things said he in the synagogue, as he taught in Capernaum.
043	JOH	006	060	Many therefore of his disciples, when they heard [this], said, This is a hard saying; who can hear it?
043	JOH	006	061	But Jesus knowing in himself that his disciples murmured at this, said unto them, Doth this cause you to stumble?
043	JOH	006	062	[What] then if ye should behold the Son of man ascending where he was before?
043	JOH	006	063	It is the spirit that quickeneth; the flesh profiteth nothing: the words that I have spoken unto you are spirit, and are life.
043	JOH	006	064	But there are some of you that believe not. For Jesus knew from the beginning who they were that believed not, and who it was that should betray him.
043	JOH	006	065	And he said, For this cause have I said unto you, that no man can come unto me, except it be given unto him of the Father.
043	JOH	006	066	Upon this many of his disciples went back, and walked no more with him.
043	JOH	006	067	Jesus said therefore unto the twelve, Would ye also go away?
043	JOH	006	068	Simon Peter answered him, Lord, to whom shall we go? thou hast the words of eternal life.
043	JOH	006	069	And we have believed and know that thou art the Holy One of God.
043	JOH	006	070	Jesus answered them, Did not I choose you the twelve, and one of you is a devil?
043	JOH	006	071	Now he spake of Judas [the son] of Simon Iscariot, for he it was that should betray him, [being] one of the twelve.
043	JOH	007	001	And after these things Jesus walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Judaea, because the Jews sought to kill him.
043	JOH	007	002	Now the feast of the Jews, the feast of tabernacles, was at hand.
043	JOH	007	003	His brethren therefore said unto him, Depart hence, and go into Judaea, that thy disciples also may behold thy works which thou doest.
043	JOH	007	004	For no man doeth anything in secret, and himself seeketh to be known openly. If thou doest these things, manifest thyself to the world.
043	JOH	007	005	For even his brethren did not believe on him.
043	JOH	007	006	Jesus therefore saith unto them, My time is not yet come; but your time is alway ready.
043	JOH	007	007	The world cannot hate you; but me it hateth, because I testify of it, that its works are evil.
043	JOH	007	008	Go ye up unto the feast: I go not up yet unto this feast; because my time is not yet fulfilled.
043	JOH	007	009	And having said these things unto them, he abode [still] in Galilee.
043	JOH	007	010	But when his brethren were gone up unto the feast, then went he also up, not publicly, but as it were in secret.
043	JOH	007	011	The Jews therefore sought him at the feast, and said, Where is he?
043	JOH	007	012	And there was much murmuring among the multitudes concerning him: some said, He is a good man; others said, Not so, but he leadeth the multitude astray.
043	JOH	007	013	Howbeit no man spake openly of him for fear of the Jews.
043	JOH	007	014	But when it was now the midst of the feast Jesus went up into the temple, and taught.
043	JOH	007	015	The Jews therefore marveled, saying, How knoweth this man letters, having never learned?
043	JOH	007	016	Jesus therefore answered them, and said, My teaching is not mine, but his that sent me.
043	JOH	007	017	If any man willeth to do his will, he shall know of the teaching, whether it be of God, or [whether] I speak from myself.
043	JOH	007	018	He that speaketh from himself seeketh his own glory: but he that seeketh the glory of him that sent him, the same is true, and no unrighteousness is in him.
043	JOH	007	019	Did not Moses give you the law, and [yet] none of you doeth the law? Why seek ye to kill me?
043	JOH	007	020	The multitude answered, Thou hast a devil: who seeketh to kill thee?
043	JOH	007	021	Jesus answered and said unto them, I did one work, and ye all marvel.
043	JOH	007	022	For this cause hath Moses given you circumcision (not that it is of Moses, but of the fathers); and on the sabbath ye circumcise a man.
043	JOH	007	023	If a man receiveth circumcision on the sabbath, that the law of Moses may not be broken; are ye wroth with me, because I made a man every whit whole on the sabbath?
043	JOH	007	024	Judge not according to appearance, but judge righteous judgment.
043	JOH	007	025	Some therefore of them of Jerusalem said, Is not this he whom they seek to kill?
043	JOH	007	026	And lo, he speaketh openly, and they say nothing unto him. Can it be that the rulers indeed know that this is the Christ?
043	JOH	007	027	Howbeit we know this man whence he is: but when the Christ cometh, no one knoweth whence he is.
043	JOH	007	028	Jesus therefore cried in the temple, teaching and saying, Ye both know me, and know whence I am; and I am not come of myself, but he that sent me is true, whom ye know not.
043	JOH	007	029	I know him; because I am from him, and he sent me.
043	JOH	007	030	They sought therefore to take him: and no man laid his hand on him, because his hour was not yet come.
043	JOH	007	031	But of the multitude many believed on him; and they said, When the Christ shall come, will he do more signs than those which this man hath done?
043	JOH	007	032	The Pharisees heard the multitude murmuring these things concerning him; and the chief priests and the Pharisees sent officers to take him.
043	JOH	007	033	Jesus therefore said, Yet a little while am I with you, and I go unto him that sent me.
043	JOH	007	034	Ye shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, ye cannot come.
043	JOH	007	035	The Jews therefore said among themselves, Whither will this man go that we shall not find him? will he go unto the Dispersion among the Greeks, and teach the Greeks?
043	JOH	007	036	What is this word that he said, Ye shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, ye cannot come?
043	JOH	007	037	Now on the last day, the great [day] of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.
043	JOH	007	038	He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.
043	JOH	007	039	But this spake he of the Spirit, which they that believed on him were to receive: for the Spirit was not yet [given]; because Jesus was not yet glorified.
043	JOH	007	040	[Some] of the multitude therefore, when they heard these words, said, This is of a truth the prophet.
043	JOH	007	041	Others said, This is the Christ. But some said, What, doth the Christ come out of Galilee?
043	JOH	007	042	Hath not the scripture said that the Christ cometh of the seed of David, and from Bethlehem, the village where David was?
043	JOH	007	043	So there arose a division in the multitude because of him.
043	JOH	007	044	And some of them would have taken him; but no man laid hands on him.
043	JOH	007	045	The officers therefore came to the chief priests and Pharisees; and they said unto them, Why did ye not bring him?
043	JOH	007	046	The officers answered, Never man so spake.
043	JOH	007	047	The Pharisees therefore answered them, Are ye also led astray?
043	JOH	007	048	Hath any of the rulers believed on him, or of the Pharisees?
043	JOH	007	049	But this multitude which knoweth not the law are accursed.
043	JOH	007	050	Nicodemus saith unto them (he that came to him before, being one of them),
043	JOH	007	051	Doth our law judge a man, except it first hear from himself and know what he doeth?
043	JOH	007	052	They answered and said unto him, Art thou also of Galilee? Search, and see that out of Galilee ariseth no prophet.
043	JOH	007	053	[And they went every man unto his own house:
043	JOH	008	001	but Jesus went unto the mount of Olives.
043	JOH	008	002	And early in the morning he came again into the temple, and all the people came unto him; and he sat down, and taught them.
043	JOH	008	003	And the scribes and the Pharisees bring a woman taken in adultery; and having set her in the midst,
043	JOH	008	004	they say unto him, Master, this woman hath been taken in adultery, in the very act.
043	JOH	008	005	Now in the law Moses commanded us to stone such: what then sayest thou of her?
043	JOH	008	006	And this they said, tempting him, that they might have [whereof] to accuse him. But Jesus stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground.
043	JOH	008	007	But when they continued asking him, he lifted up himself, and said unto them, He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone at her.
043	JOH	008	008	And again he stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground.
043	JOH	008	009	And they, when they heard it, went out one by one, beginning from the eldest, [even] unto the last: and Jesus was left alone, and the woman, where she was, in the midst.
043	JOH	008	010	And Jesus lifted up himself, and said unto her, Woman, where are they? did no man condemn thee?
043	JOH	008	011	And she said, No man, Lord. And Jesus said, Neither do I condemn thee: go thy way; from henceforth sin no more.]
043	JOH	008	012	Again therefore Jesus spake unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in the darkness, but shall have the light of life.
043	JOH	008	013	The Pharisees therefore said unto him, Thou bearest witness of thyself; thy witness is not true.
043	JOH	008	014	Jesus answered and said unto them, Even if I bear witness of myself, my witness is true; for I know whence I came, and whither I go; but ye know not whence I come, or whither I go.
043	JOH	008	015	Ye judge after the flesh; I judge no man.
043	JOH	008	016	Yea and if I judge, my judgment is true; for I am not alone, but I and the Father that sent me.
043	JOH	008	017	Yea and in your law it is written, that the witness of two men is true.
043	JOH	008	018	I am he that beareth witness of myself, and the Father that sent me beareth witness of me.
043	JOH	008	019	They said therefore unto him, Where is thy Father? Jesus answered, Ye know neither me, nor my Father: if ye knew me, ye would know my Father also.
043	JOH	008	020	These words spake he in the treasury, as he taught in the temple: and no man took him; because his hour was not yet come.
043	JOH	008	021	He said therefore again unto them, I go away, and ye shall seek me, and shall die in your sin: whither I go, ye cannot come.
043	JOH	008	022	The Jews therefore said, Will he kill himself, that he saith, Whither I go, ye cannot come?
043	JOH	008	023	And he said unto them, Ye are from beneath; I am from above: ye are of this world; I am not of this world.
043	JOH	008	024	I said therefore unto you, that ye shall die in your sins: for except ye believe that I am [he], ye shall die in your sins.
043	JOH	008	025	They said therefore unto him, Who art thou? Jesus said unto them, Even that which I have also spoken unto you from the beginning.
043	JOH	008	026	I have many things to speak and to judge concerning you: howbeit he that sent me is true; and the things which I heard from him, these speak I unto the world.
043	JOH	008	027	They perceived not that he spake to them of the Father.
043	JOH	008	028	Jesus therefore said, When ye have lifted up the Son of man, then shall ye know that I am [he], and [that] I do nothing of myself, but as the Father taught me, I speak these things.
043	JOH	008	029	And he that sent me is with me; he hath not left me alone; for I do always the things that are pleasing to him.
043	JOH	008	030	As he spake these things, many believed on him.
043	JOH	008	031	Jesus therefore said to those Jews which had believed him, If ye abide in my word, [then] are ye truly my disciples;
043	JOH	008	032	and ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.
043	JOH	008	033	They answered unto him, We be Abraham’s seed, and have never yet been in bondage to any man: how sayest thou, Ye shall be made free?
043	JOH	008	034	Jesus answered them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Every one that committeth sin is the bondservant of sin.
043	JOH	008	035	And the bondservant abideth not in the house for ever: the son abideth for ever.
043	JOH	008	036	If therefore the Son shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed.
043	JOH	008	037	I know that ye are Abraham’s seed; yet ye seek to kill me, because my word hath not free course in you.
043	JOH	008	038	I speak the things which I have seen with [my] Father: and ye also do the things which ye heard from [your] father.
043	JOH	008	039	They answered and said unto him, Our father is Abraham. Jesus saith unto them, If ye were Abraham’s children, ye would do the works of Abraham.
043	JOH	008	040	But now ye seek to kill me, a man that hath told you the truth, which I heard from God: this did not Abraham.
043	JOH	008	041	Ye do the works of your father. They said unto him, We were not born of fornication; we have one Father, [even] God.
043	JOH	008	042	Jesus said unto them, If God were your Father, ye would love me: for I came forth and am come from God; for neither have I come of myself, but he sent me.
043	JOH	008	043	Why do ye not understand my speech? [Even] because ye cannot hear my word.
043	JOH	008	044	Ye are of [your] father the devil, and the lusts of your father it is your will to do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and stood not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father thereof.
043	JOH	008	045	But because I say the truth, ye believe me not.
043	JOH	008	046	Which of you convicteth me of sin? If I say truth, why do ye not believe me?
043	JOH	008	047	He that is of God heareth the words of God: for this cause ye hear [them] not, because ye are not of God.
043	JOH	008	048	The Jews answered and said unto him, Say we not well that thou art a Samaritan, and hast a devil?
043	JOH	008	049	Jesus answered, I have not a devil; but I honour my Father, and ye dishonour me.
043	JOH	008	050	But I seek not mine own glory: there is one that seeketh and judgeth.
043	JOH	008	051	Verily, verily, I say unto you, If a man keep my word, he shall never see death.
043	JOH	008	052	The Jews said unto him, Now we know that thou hast a devil. Abraham is dead, and the prophets; and thou sayest, If a man keep my word, he shall never taste of death.
043	JOH	008	053	Art thou greater than our father Abraham, which is dead? and the prophets are dead: whom makest thou thyself?
043	JOH	008	054	Jesus answered, If I glorify myself, my glory is nothing: it is my Father that glorifieth me; of whom ye say, that he is your God;
043	JOH	008	055	and ye have not known him: but I know him; and if I should say, I know him not, I shall be like unto you, a liar: but I know him, and keep his word.
043	JOH	008	056	Your father Abraham rejoiced to see my day; and he saw it, and was glad.
043	JOH	008	057	The Jews therefore said unto him, Thou art not yet fifty years old, and hast thou seen Abraham?
043	JOH	008	058	Jesus said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Before Abraham was, I am.
043	JOH	008	059	They took up stones therefore to cast at him: but Jesus hid himself, and went out of the temple.
043	JOH	009	001	And as he passed by, he saw a man blind from his birth.
043	JOH	009	002	And his disciples asked him, saying, Rabbi, who did sin, this man, or his parents, that he should be born blind?
043	JOH	009	003	Jesus answered, Neither did this man sin, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him.
043	JOH	009	004	We must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work.
043	JOH	009	005	When I am in the world, I am the light of the world.
043	JOH	009	006	When he had thus spoken, he spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and anointed his eyes with the clay,
043	JOH	009	007	and said unto him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam (which is by interpretation, Sent). He went away therefore, and washed, and came seeing.
043	JOH	009	008	The neighbours therefore, and they which saw him aforetime, that he was a beggar, said, Is not this he that sat and begged?
043	JOH	009	009	Others said, It is he: others said, No, but he is like him. He said, I am [he].
043	JOH	009	010	They said therefore unto him, How then were thine eyes opened?
043	JOH	009	011	He answered, The man that is called Jesus made clay, and anointed mine eyes, and said unto me, Go to Siloam, and wash: so I went away and washed, and I received sight.
043	JOH	009	012	And they said unto him, Where is he? He saith, I know not.
043	JOH	009	013	They bring to the Pharisees him that aforetime was blind.
043	JOH	009	014	Now it was the sabbath on the day when Jesus made the clay, and opened his eyes.
043	JOH	009	015	Again therefore the Pharisees also asked him how he received his sight. And he said unto them, He put clay upon mine eyes, and I washed, and do see.
043	JOH	009	016	Some therefore of the Pharisees said, This man is not from God, because he keepeth not the sabbath. But others said, How can a man that is a sinner do such signs? And there was a division among them.
043	JOH	009	017	They say therefore unto the blind man again, What sayest thou of him, in that he opened thine eyes? And he said, He is a prophet.
043	JOH	009	018	The Jews therefore did not believe concerning him, that he had been blind, and had received his sight, until they called the parents of him that had received his sight,
043	JOH	009	019	and asked them, saying, Is this your son, who ye say was born blind? how then doth he now see?
043	JOH	009	020	His parents answered and said, We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind:
043	JOH	009	021	but how he now seeth, we know not; or who opened his eyes, we know not: ask him; he is of age; he shall speak for himself.
043	JOH	009	022	These things said his parents, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had agreed already, that if any man should confess him [to be] Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.
043	JOH	009	023	Therefore said his parents, He is of age; ask him.
043	JOH	009	024	So they called a second time the man that was blind, and said unto him, Give glory to God: we know that this man is a sinner.
043	JOH	009	025	He therefore answered, Whether he be a sinner, I know not: one thing I know, that, whereas I was blind, now I see.
043	JOH	009	026	They said therefore unto him, What did he to thee? how opened he thine eyes?
043	JOH	009	027	He answered them, I told you even now, and ye did not hear: wherefore would ye hear it again? would ye also become his disciples?
043	JOH	009	028	And they reviled him, and said, Thou art his disciple; but we are disciples of Moses.
043	JOH	009	029	We know that God hath spoken unto Moses: but as for this man, we know not whence he is.
043	JOH	009	030	The man answered and said unto them, Why, herein is the marvel, that ye know not whence he is, and [yet] he opened mine eyes.
043	JOH	009	031	We know that God heareth not sinners: but if any man be a worshipper of God, and do his will, him he heareth.
043	JOH	009	032	Since the world began it was never heard that any one opened the eyes of a man born blind.
043	JOH	009	033	If this man were not from God, he could do nothing.
043	JOH	009	034	They answered and said unto him, Thou wast altogether born in sins, and dost thou teach us? And they cast him out.
043	JOH	009	035	Jesus heard that they had cast him out; and finding him, he said, Dost thou believe on the Son of God?
043	JOH	009	036	He answered and said, And who is he, Lord, that I may believe on him?
043	JOH	009	037	Jesus said unto him, Thou hast both seen him, and he it is that speaketh with thee.
043	JOH	009	038	And he said, Lord, I believe. And he worshipped him.
043	JOH	009	039	And Jesus said, For judgment came I into this world, that they which see not may see; and that they which see may become blind.
043	JOH	009	040	Those of the Pharisees which were with him heard these things, and said unto him, Are we also blind?
043	JOH	009	041	Jesus said unto them, If ye were blind, ye would have no sin: but now ye say, We see: your sin remaineth.
043	JOH	010	001	Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that entereth not by the door into the fold of the sheep, but climbeth up some other way, the same is a thief and a robber.
043	JOH	010	002	But he that entereth in by the door is the shepherd of the sheep.
043	JOH	010	003	To him the porter openeth; and the sheep hear his voice: and he calleth his own sheep by name, and leadeth them out.
043	JOH	010	004	When he hath put forth all his own, he goeth before them, and the sheep follow him: for they know his voice.
043	JOH	010	005	And a stranger will they not follow, but will flee from him: for they know not the voice of strangers.
043	JOH	010	006	This parable spake Jesus unto them: but they understood not what things they were which he spake unto them.
043	JOH	010	007	Jesus therefore said unto them again, Verily, verily, I say unto you, I am the door of the sheep.
043	JOH	010	008	All that came before me are thieves and robbers: but the sheep did not hear them.
043	JOH	010	009	I am the door: by me if any man enter in, he shall be saved, and shall go in and go out, and shall find pasture.
043	JOH	010	010	The thief cometh not, but that he may steal, and kill, and destroy: I came that they may have life, and may have [it] abundantly.
043	JOH	010	011	I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd layeth down his life for the sheep.
043	JOH	010	012	He that is a hireling, and not a shepherd, whose own the sheep are not, beholdeth the wolf coming, and leaveth the sheep, and fleeth, and the wolf snatcheth them, and scattereth [them]:
043	JOH	010	013	[he fleeth] because he is a hireling, and careth not for the sheep.
043	JOH	010	014	I am the good shepherd; and I know mine own, and mine own know me,
043	JOH	010	015	even as the Father knoweth me, and I know the Father; and I lay down my life for the sheep.
043	JOH	010	016	And other sheep I have, which are not of this fold: them also I must bring, and they shall hear my voice; and they shall become one flock, one shepherd.
043	JOH	010	017	Therefore doth the Father love me, because I lay down my life, that I may take it again.
043	JOH	010	018	No one taketh it away from me, but I lay it down of myself. I have power to lay it down, and I have power to take it again. This commandment received I from my Father.
043	JOH	010	019	There arose a division again among the Jews because of these words.
043	JOH	010	020	And many of them said, He hath a devil, and is mad; why hear ye him?
043	JOH	010	021	Others said, These are not the sayings of one possessed with a devil. Can a devil open the eyes of the blind?
