043	JOH	010	023	and Jesus was walking in the temple in Solomon’s porch.
043	JOH	010	024	The Jews therefore came round about him, and said unto him, How long dost thou hold us in suspense? If thou art the Christ, tell us plainly.
043	JOH	010	025	Jesus answered them, I told you, and ye believe not: the works that I do in my Father’s name, these bear witness of me.
043	JOH	010	026	But ye believe not, because ye are not of my sheep.
043	JOH	010	027	My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me:
043	JOH	010	028	and I give unto them eternal life; and they shall never perish, and no one shall snatch them out of my hand.
043	JOH	010	029	My Father, which hath given [them] unto me, is greater than all; and no one is able to snatch [them] out of the Father’s hand.
043	JOH	010	030	I and the Father are one.
043	JOH	010	031	The Jews took up stones again to stone him.
043	JOH	010	032	Jesus answered them, Many good works have I shewed you from the Father; for which of those works do ye stone me?
043	JOH	010	033	The Jews answered him, For a good work we stone thee not, but for blasphemy; and because that thou, being a man, makest thyself God.
043	JOH	010	034	Jesus answered them, Is it not written in your law, I said, Ye are gods?
043	JOH	010	035	If he called them gods, unto whom the word of God came (and the scripture cannot be broken),
043	JOH	010	036	say ye of him, whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world, Thou blasphemest; because I said, I am [the] Son of God?
043	JOH	010	037	If I do not the works of my Father, believe me not.
043	JOH	010	038	But if I do them, though ye believe not me, believe the works: that ye may know and understand that the Father is in me, and I in the Father.
043	JOH	010	039	They sought again to take him: and he went forth out of their hand.
043	JOH	010	040	And he went away again beyond Jordan into the place where John was at the first baptizing; and there he abode.
043	JOH	010	041	And many came unto him; and they said, John indeed did no sign: but all things whatsoever John spake of this man were true.
043	JOH	010	042	And many believed on him there.
043	JOH	011	001	Now a certain man was sick, Lazarus of Bethany, of the village of Mary and her sister Martha.
043	JOH	011	002	And it was that Mary which anointed the Lord with ointment, and wiped his feet with her hair, whose brother Lazarus was sick.
043	JOH	011	003	The sisters therefore sent unto him, saying, Lord, behold, he whom thou lovest is sick.
043	JOH	011	004	But when Jesus heard it, he said, This sickness is not unto death, but for the glory of God, that the Son of God may be glorified thereby.
043	JOH	011	005	Now Jesus loved Martha, and her sister, and Lazarus.
043	JOH	011	006	When therefore he heard that he was sick, he abode at that time two days in the place where he was.
043	JOH	011	007	Then after this he saith to the disciples, Let us go into Judaea again.
043	JOH	011	008	The disciples say unto him, Rabbi, the Jews were but now seeking to stone thee; and goest thou thither again?
043	JOH	011	009	Jesus answered, Are there not twelve hours in the day? If a man walk in the day, he stumbleth not, because he seeth the light of this world.
043	JOH	011	010	But if a man walk in the night, he stumbleth, because the light is not in him.
043	JOH	011	011	These things spake he: and after this he saith unto them, Our friend Lazarus is fallen asleep; but I go, that I may awake him out of sleep.
043	JOH	011	012	The disciples therefore said unto him, Lord, if he is fallen asleep, he will recover.
043	JOH	011	013	Now Jesus had spoken of his death: but they thought that he spake of taking rest in sleep.
043	JOH	011	014	Then Jesus therefore said unto them plainly, Lazarus is dead.
043	JOH	011	015	And I am glad for your sakes that I was not there, to the intent ye may believe; nevertheless let us go unto him.
043	JOH	011	016	Thomas therefore, who is called Didymus, said unto his fellow-disciples, Let us also go, that we may die with him.
043	JOH	011	017	So when Jesus came, he found that he had been in the tomb four days already.
043	JOH	011	018	Now Bethany was nigh unto Jerusalem, about fifteen furlongs off;
043	JOH	011	019	and many of the Jews had come to Martha and Mary, to console them concerning their brother.
043	JOH	011	020	Martha therefore, when she heard that Jesus was coming, went and met him: but Mary still sat in the house.
043	JOH	011	021	Martha therefore said unto Jesus, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.
043	JOH	011	022	And even now I know that, whatsoever thou shalt ask of God, God will give thee.
043	JOH	011	023	Jesus saith unto her, Thy brother shall rise again.
043	JOH	011	024	Martha saith unto him, I know that he shall rise again in the resurrection at the last day.
043	JOH	011	025	Jesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth on me, though he die, yet shall he live:
043	JOH	011	026	and whosoever liveth and believeth on me shall never die. Believest thou this?
043	JOH	011	027	She saith unto him, Yea, Lord: I have believed that thou art the Christ, the Son of God, [even] he that cometh into the world.
043	JOH	011	028	And when she had said this, she went away, and called Mary her sister secretly, saying, The Master is here, and calleth thee.
043	JOH	011	029	And she, when she heard it, arose quickly, and went unto him.
043	JOH	011	030	(Now Jesus was not yet come into the village, but was still in the place where Martha met him.)
043	JOH	011	031	The Jews then which were with her in the house, and were comforting her, when they saw Mary, that she rose up quickly and went out, followed her, supposing that she was going unto the tomb to weep there.
043	JOH	011	032	Mary therefore, when she came where Jesus was, and saw him, fell down at his feet, saying unto him, Lord, if thou hadst been here, my brother had not died.
043	JOH	011	033	When Jesus therefore saw her weeping, and the Jews [also] weeping which came with her, he groaned in the spirit, and was troubled,
043	JOH	011	034	and said, Where have ye laid him? They say unto him, Lord, come and see.
043	JOH	011	035	Jesus wept.
043	JOH	011	036	The Jews therefore said, Behold how he loved him!
043	JOH	011	037	But some of them said, Could not this man, which opened the eyes of him that was blind, have caused that this man also should not die?
043	JOH	011	038	Jesus therefore again groaning in himself cometh to the tomb. Now it was a cave, and a stone lay against it.
043	JOH	011	039	Jesus saith, Take ye away the stone. Martha, the sister of him that was dead, saith unto him, Lord, by this time he stinketh: for he hath been [dead] four days.
043	JOH	011	040	Jesus saith unto her, Said I not unto thee, that, if thou believedst, thou shouldest see the glory of God?
043	JOH	011	041	So they took away the stone. And Jesus lifted up his eyes, and said, Father, I thank thee that thou heardest me.
