043	JOH	013	010	Jesus saith to him, He that is bathed needeth not save to wash his feet, but is clean every whit: and ye are clean, but not all.
043	JOH	013	011	For he knew him that should betray him; therefore said he, Ye are not all clean.
043	JOH	013	012	So when he had washed their feet, and taken his garments, and sat down again, he said unto them, Know ye what I have done to you?
043	JOH	013	013	Ye call me, Master, and, Lord: and ye say well; for so I am.
043	JOH	013	014	If I then, the Lord and the Master, have washed your feet, ye also ought to wash one another’s feet.
043	JOH	013	015	For I have given you an example, that ye also should do as I have done to you.
043	JOH	013	016	Verily, verily, I say unto you, A servant is not greater than his lord; neither one that is sent greater than he that sent him.
043	JOH	013	017	If ye know these things, blessed are ye if ye do them.
