043	JOH	014	027	Peace I leave with you; my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be fearful.
043	JOH	014	028	Ye heard how I said to you, I go away, and I come unto you. If ye loved me, ye would have rejoiced, because I go unto the Father: for the Father is greater than I.
043	JOH	014	029	And now I have told you before it come to pass, that, when it is come to pass, ye may believe.
043	JOH	014	030	I will no more speak much with you, for the prince of the world cometh: and he hath nothing in me;
043	JOH	014	031	but that the world may know that I love the Father, and as the Father gave me commandment, even so I do. Arise, let us go hence.
043	JOH	015	001	I am the true vine, and my Father is the husbandman.
043	JOH	015	002	Every branch in me that beareth not fruit, he taketh it away: and every [branch] that beareth fruit, he cleanseth it, that it may bear more fruit.
043	JOH	015	003	Already ye are clean because of the word which I have spoken unto you.
043	JOH	015	004	Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; so neither can ye, except ye abide in me.
043	JOH	015	005	I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same beareth much fruit: for apart from me ye can do nothing.
043	JOH	015	006	If a man abide not in me, he is cast forth as a branch, and is withered; and they gather them, and cast them into the fire, and they are burned.
043	JOH	015	007	If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ask whatsoever ye will, and it shall be done unto you.
043	JOH	015	008	Herein is my Father glorified, that ye bear much fruit; and [so] shall ye be my disciples.
043	JOH	015	009	Even as the Father hath loved me, I also have loved you: abide ye in my love.
043	JOH	015	010	If ye keep my commandments, ye shall abide in my love; even as I have kept my Father’s commandments, and abide in his love.
043	JOH	015	011	These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy may be in you, and [that] your joy may be fulfilled.
043	JOH	015	012	This is my commandment, that ye love one another, even as I have loved you.
043	JOH	015	013	Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.
043	JOH	015	014	Ye are my friends, if ye do the things which I command you.
043	JOH	015	015	No longer do I call you servants; for the servant knoweth not what his lord doeth: but I have called you friends; for all things that I heard from my Father I have made known unto you.
043	JOH	015	016	Ye did not choose me, but I chose you, and appointed you, that ye should go and bear fruit, and [that] your fruit should abide: that whatsoever ye shall ask of the Father in my name, he may give it you.
043	JOH	015	017	These things I command you, that ye may love one another.
043	JOH	015	018	If the world hateth you, ye know that it hath hated me before [it hated] you.
043	JOH	015	019	If ye were of the world, the world would love its own: but because ye are not of the world, but I chose you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you.
043	JOH	015	020	Remember the word that I said unto you, A servant is not greater than his lord. If they persecuted me, they will also persecute you; if they kept my word, they will keep yours also.
043	JOH	015	021	But all these things will they do unto you for my name’s sake, because they know not him that sent me.
043	JOH	015	022	If I had not come and spoken unto them, they had not had sin: but now they have no excuse for their sin.
043	JOH	015	023	He that hateth me hateth my Father also.
043	JOH	015	024	If I had not done among them the works which none other did, they had not had sin: but now have they both seen and hated both me and my Father.
043	JOH	015	025	But [this cometh to pass], that the word may be fulfilled that is written in their law, They hated me without a cause.
043	JOH	015	026	But when the Comforter is come, whom I will send unto you from the Father, [even] the Spirit of truth, which proceedeth from the Father, he shall bear witness of me:
043	JOH	015	027	and ye also bear witness, because ye have been with me from the beginning.
043	JOH	016	001	These things have I spoken unto you, that ye should not be made to stumble.
043	JOH	016	002	They shall put you out of the synagogues: yea, the hour cometh, that whosoever killeth you shall think that he offereth service unto God.
043	JOH	016	003	And these things will they do, because they have not known the Father, nor me.
043	JOH	016	004	But these things have I spoken unto you, that when their hour is come, ye may remember them, how that I told you. And these things I said not unto you from the beginning, because I was with you.
043	JOH	016	005	But now I go unto him that sent me; and none of you asketh me, Whither goest thou?
043	JOH	016	006	But because I have spoken these things unto you, sorrow hath filled your heart.
043	JOH	016	007	Nevertheless I tell you the truth; It is expedient for you that I go away: for if I go not away, the Comforter will not come unto you; but if I go, I will send him unto you.
043	JOH	016	008	And he, when he is come, will convict the world in respect of sin, and of righteousness, and of judgment:
043	JOH	016	009	of sin, because they believe not on me;
043	JOH	016	010	of righteousness, because I go to the Father, and ye behold me no more;
043	JOH	016	011	of judgment, because the prince of this world hath been judged.
043	JOH	016	012	I have yet many things to say unto you, but ye cannot bear them now.
043	JOH	016	013	Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he shall guide you into all the truth: for he shall not speak from himself; but what things soever he shall hear, [these] shall he speak: and he shall declare unto you the things that are to come.
043	JOH	016	014	He shall glorify me: for he shall take of mine, and shall declare [it] unto you.
043	JOH	016	015	All things whatsoever the Father hath are mine: therefore said I, that he taketh of mine, and shall declare [it] unto you.
043	JOH	016	016	A little while, and ye behold me no more; and again a little while, and ye shall see me.
043	JOH	016	017	[Some] of his disciples therefore said one to another, What is this that he saith unto us, A little while, and ye behold me not; and again a little while, and ye shall see me: and, Because I go to the Father?
043	JOH	016	018	They said therefore, What is this that he saith, A little while? We know not what he saith.
043	JOH	016	019	Jesus perceived that they were desirous to ask him, and he said unto them, Do ye inquire among yourselves concerning this, that I said, A little while, and ye behold me not, and again a little while, and ye shall see me?
043	JOH	016	020	Verily, verily, I say unto you, that ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice: ye shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy.
043	JOH	016	021	A woman when she is in travail hath sorrow, because her hour is come: but when she is delivered of the child, she remembereth no more the anguish, for the joy that a man is born into the world.
043	JOH	016	022	And ye therefore now have sorrow: but I will see you again, and your heart shall rejoice, and your joy no one taketh away from you.
043	JOH	016	023	And in that day ye shall ask me nothing. Verily, verily, I say unto you, If ye shall ask anything of the Father, he will give it you in my name.
043	JOH	016	024	Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be fulfilled.
043	JOH	016	025	These things have I spoken unto you in proverbs: the hour cometh, when I shall no more speak unto you in proverbs, but shall tell you plainly of the Father.
043	JOH	016	026	In that day ye shall ask in my name: and I say not unto you, that I will pray the Father for you;
043	JOH	016	027	for the Father himself loveth you, because ye have loved me, and have believed that I came forth from the Father.
043	JOH	016	028	I came out from the Father, and am come into the world: again, I leave the world, and go unto the Father.
043	JOH	016	029	His disciples say, Lo, now speakest thou plainly, and speakest no proverb.
043	JOH	016	030	Now know we that thou knowest all things, and needest not that any man should ask thee: by this we believe that thou camest forth from God.
043	JOH	016	031	Jesus answered them, Do ye now believe?
043	JOH	016	032	Behold, the hour cometh, yea, is come, that ye shall be scattered, every man to his own, and shall leave me alone: and [yet] I am not alone, because the Father is with me.
043	JOH	016	033	These things have I spoken unto you, that in me ye may have peace. In the world ye have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.
043	JOH	017	001	These things spake Jesus; and lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said, Father, the hour is come; glorify thy Son, that the Son may glorify thee:
043	JOH	017	002	even as thou gavest him authority over all flesh, that whatsoever thou hast given him, to them he should give eternal life.
043	JOH	017	003	And this is life eternal, that they should know thee the only true God, and him whom thou didst send, [even] Jesus Christ.
043	JOH	017	004	I glorified thee on the earth, having accomplished the work which thou hast given me to do.
043	JOH	017	005	And now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.
043	JOH	017	006	I manifested thy name unto the men whom thou gavest me out of the world: thine they were, and thou gavest them to me; and they have kept thy word.
043	JOH	017	007	Now they know that all things whatsoever thou hast given me are from thee:
043	JOH	017	008	for the words which thou gavest me I have given unto them; and they received [them], and knew of a truth that I came forth from thee, and they believed that thou didst send me.
043	JOH	017	009	I pray for them: I pray not for the world, but for those whom thou hast given me; for they are thine:
043	JOH	017	010	and all things that are mine are thine, and thine are mine: and I am glorified in them.
043	JOH	017	011	And I am no more in the world, and these are in the world, and I come to thee. Holy Father, keep them in thy name which thou hast given me, that they may be one, even as we [are].
043	JOH	017	012	While I was with them, I kept them in thy name which thou hast given me: and I guarded them, and not one of them perished, but the son of perdition; that the scripture might be fulfilled.
043	JOH	017	013	But now I come to thee; and these things I speak in the world, that they may have my joy fulfilled in themselves.
043	JOH	017	014	I have given them thy word; and the world hated them, because they are not of the world, even as I am not of the world.
043	JOH	017	015	I pray not that thou shouldest take them from the world, but that thou shouldest keep them from the evil [one].
043	JOH	017	016	They are not of the world, even as I am not of the world.
043	JOH	017	017	Sanctify them in the truth: thy word is truth.
043	JOH	017	018	As thou didst send me into the world, even so sent I them into the world.
043	JOH	017	019	And for their sakes I sanctify myself, that they themselves also may be sanctified in truth.
043	JOH	017	020	Neither for these only do I pray, but for them also that believe on me through their word;
043	JOH	017	021	that they may all be one; even as thou, Father, [art] in me, and I in thee, that they also may be in us: that the world may believe that thou didst send me.
043	JOH	017	022	And the glory which thou hast given me I have given unto them; that they may be one, even as we [are] one;
043	JOH	017	023	I in them, and thou in me, that they may be perfected into one; that the world may know that thou didst send me, and lovedst them, even as thou lovedst me.
043	JOH	017	024	Father, that which thou hast given me, I will that, where I am, they also may be with me; that they may behold my glory, which thou hast given me: for thou lovedst me before the foundation of the world.
043	JOH	017	025	O righteous Father, the world knew thee not, but I knew thee; and these knew that thou didst send me;
043	JOH	017	026	and I made known unto them thy name, and will make it known; that the love wherewith thou lovedst me may be in them, and I in them.
043	JOH	018	001	When Jesus had spoken these words, he went forth with his disciples over the brook Kidron, where was a garden, into the which he entered, himself and his disciples.
043	JOH	018	002	Now Judas also, which betrayed him, knew the place: for Jesus oft-times resorted thither with his disciples.
043	JOH	018	003	Judas then, having received the band [of soldiers], and officers from the chief priests and the Pharisees, cometh thither with lanterns and torches and weapons.
043	JOH	018	004	Jesus therefore, knowing all the things that were coming upon him, went forth, and saith unto them, Whom seek ye?
043	JOH	018	005	They answered him, Jesus of Nazareth. Jesus saith unto them, I am [he]. And Judas also, which betrayed him, was standing with them.
043	JOH	018	006	When therefore he said unto them, I am [he], they went backward, and fell to the ground.
043	JOH	018	007	Again therefore he asked them, Whom seek ye? And they said, Jesus of Nazareth.
043	JOH	018	008	Jesus answered, I told you that I am [he]: if therefore ye seek me, let these go their way:
043	JOH	018	009	that the word might be fulfilled which he spake, Of those whom thou hast given me I lost not one.
043	JOH	018	010	Simon Peter therefore having a sword drew it, and struck the high priest’s servant, and cut off his right ear. Now the servant’s name was Malchus.
043	JOH	018	011	Jesus therefore said unto Peter, Put up the sword into the sheath: the cup which the Father hath given me, shall I not drink it?
043	JOH	018	012	So the band and the chief captain, and the officers of the Jews, seized Jesus and bound him,
043	JOH	018	013	and led him to Annas first; for he was father in law to Caiaphas, which was high priest that year.
043	JOH	018	014	Now Caiaphas was he which gave counsel to the Jews, that it was expedient that one man should die for the people.
043	JOH	018	015	And Simon Peter followed Jesus, and [so did] another disciple. Now that disciple was known unto the high priest, and entered in with Jesus into the court of the high priest;
043	JOH	018	016	but Peter was standing at the door without. So the other disciple, which was known unto the high priest, went out and spake unto her that kept the door, and brought in Peter.
043	JOH	018	017	The maid therefore that kept the door saith unto Peter, Art thou also [one] of this man’s disciples? He saith, I am not.
043	JOH	018	018	Now the servants and the officers were standing [there], having made a fire of coals; for it was cold; and they were warming themselves: and Peter also was with them, standing and warming himself.
043	JOH	018	019	The high priest therefore asked Jesus of his disciples, and of his teaching.
043	JOH	018	020	Jesus answered him, I have spoken openly to the world; I ever taught in synagogues, and in the temple, where all the Jews come together; and in secret spake I nothing.
043	JOH	018	021	Why askest thou me? ask them that have heard [me], what I spake unto them: behold, these know the things which I said.
043	JOH	018	022	And when he had said this, one of the officers standing by struck Jesus with his hand, saying, Answerest thou the high priest so?
043	JOH	018	023	Jesus answered him, If I have spoken evil, bear witness of the evil: but if well, why smitest thou me?
043	JOH	018	024	Annas therefore sent him bound unto Caiaphas the high priest.
043	JOH	018	025	Now Simon Peter was standing and warming himself. They said therefore unto him, Art thou also [one] of his disciples? He denied, and said, I am not.
043	JOH	018	026	One of the servants of the high priest, being a kinsman of him whose ear Peter cut off, saith, Did not I see thee in the garden with him?
043	JOH	018	027	Peter therefore denied again: and straightway the cock crew.
043	JOH	018	028	They lead Jesus therefore from Caiaphas into the palace: and it was early; and they themselves entered not into the palace, that they might not be defiled, but might eat the passover.
043	JOH	018	029	Pilate therefore went out unto them, and saith, What accusation bring ye against this man?
043	JOH	018	030	They answered and said unto him, If this man were not an evil-doer, we should not have delivered him up unto thee.
043	JOH	018	031	Pilate therefore said unto them, Take him yourselves, and judge him according to your law. The Jews said unto him, It is not lawful for us to put any man to death:
043	JOH	018	032	that the word of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he spake, signifying by what manner of death he should die.
043	JOH	018	033	Pilate therefore entered again into the palace, and called Jesus, and said unto him, Art thou the King of the Jews?
043	JOH	018	034	Jesus answered, Sayest thou this of thyself, or did others tell it thee concerning me?
043	JOH	018	035	Pilate answered, Am I a Jew? Thine own nation and the chief priests delivered thee unto me: what hast thou done?
043	JOH	018	036	Jesus answered, My kingdom is not of this world: if my kingdom were of this world, then would my servants fight, that I should not be delivered to the Jews: but now is my kingdom not from hence.
043	JOH	018	037	Pilate therefore said unto him, Art thou a king then? Jesus answered, Thou sayest that I am a king. To this end have I been born, and to this end am I come into the world, that I should bear witness unto the truth. Every one that is of the truth heareth my voice.
043	JOH	018	038	Pilate saith unto him, What is truth? And when he had said this, he went out again unto the Jews, and saith unto them, I find no crime in him.
043	JOH	018	039	But ye have a custom, that I should release unto you one at the passover: will ye therefore that I release unto you the King of the Jews?
043	JOH	018	040	They cried out therefore again, saying, Not this man, but Barabbas. Now Barabbas was a robber.
043	JOH	019	001	Then Pilate therefore took Jesus, and scourged him.
043	JOH	019	002	And the soldiers plaited a crown of thorns, and put it on his head, and arrayed him in a purple garment;
043	JOH	019	003	and they came unto him, and said, Hail, King of the Jews! and they struck him with their hands.
043	JOH	019	004	And Pilate went out again, and saith unto them, Behold, I bring him out to you, that ye may know that I find no crime in him.
043	JOH	019	005	Jesus therefore came out, wearing the crown of thorns and the purple garment. And [Pilate] saith unto them, Behold, the man!
043	JOH	019	006	When therefore the chief priests and the officers saw him, they cried out, saying, Crucify [him], crucify [him]. Pilate saith unto them, Take him yourselves, and crucify him: for I find no crime in him.
043	JOH	019	007	The Jews answered him, We have a law, and by that law he ought to die, because he made himself the Son of God.
043	JOH	019	008	When Pilate therefore heard this saying, he was the more afraid;
043	JOH	019	009	and he entered into the palace again, and saith unto Jesus, Whence art thou? But Jesus gave him no answer.
043	JOH	019	010	Pilate therefore saith unto him, Speakest thou not unto me? knowest thou not that I have power to release thee, and have power to crucify thee?
043	JOH	019	011	Jesus answered him, Thou wouldest have no power against me, except it were given thee from above: therefore he that delivered me unto thee hath greater sin.
043	JOH	019	012	Upon this Pilate sought to release him: but the Jews cried out, saying, If thou release this man, thou art not Caesar’s friend: every one that maketh himself a king speaketh against Caesar.
043	JOH	019	013	When Pilate therefore heard these words, he brought Jesus out, and sat down on the judgment-seat at a place called The Pavement, but in Hebrew, Gabbatha.
043	JOH	019	014	Now it was the Preparation of the passover: it was about the sixth hour. And he saith unto the Jews, Behold, your King!
043	JOH	019	015	They therefore cried out, Away with [him], away with [him], crucify him. Pilate saith unto them, Shall I crucify your King? The chief priests answered, We have no king but Caesar.
043	JOH	019	016	Then therefore he delivered him unto them to be crucified.
043	JOH	019	017	They took Jesus therefore: and he went out, bearing the cross for himself, unto the place called The place of a skull, which is called in Hebrew Golgotha:
043	JOH	019	018	where they crucified him, and with him two others, on either side one, and Jesus in the midst.
043	JOH	019	019	And Pilate wrote a title also, and put it on the cross. And there was written, JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.
043	JOH	019	020	This title therefore read many of the Jews: for the place where Jesus was crucified was nigh to the city: and it was written in Hebrew, [and] in Latin, [and] in Greek.
043	JOH	019	021	The chief priests of the Jews therefore said to Pilate, Write not, The King of the Jews; but, that he said, I am King of the Jews.
043	JOH	019	022	Pilate answered, What I have written I have written.
043	JOH	019	023	The soldiers therefore, when they had crucified Jesus, took his garments, and made four parts, to every soldier a part; and also the coat: now the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout.
043	JOH	019	024	They said therefore one to another, Let us not rend it, but cast lots for it, whose it shall be: that the scripture might be fulfilled, which saith, They parted my garments among them, And upon my vesture did they cast lots. These things therefore the soldiers did.
043	JOH	019	025	But there were standing by the cross of Jesus his mother, and his mother’s sister, Mary the [wife] of Clopas, and Mary Magdalene.
043	JOH	019	026	When Jesus therefore saw his mother, and the disciple standing by, whom he loved, he saith unto his mother, Woman, behold, thy son!
043	JOH	019	027	Then saith he to the disciple, Behold, thy mother! And from that hour the disciple took her unto his own [home].
043	JOH	019	028	After this Jesus, knowing that all things are now finished, that the scripture might be accomplished, saith, I thirst.
043	JOH	019	029	There was set there a vessel full of vinegar: so they put a sponge full of the vinegar upon hyssop, and brought it to his mouth.
043	JOH	019	030	When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up his spirit.
043	JOH	019	031	The Jews therefore, because it was the Preparation, that the bodies should not remain on the cross upon the sabbath (for the day of that sabbath was a high [day]), asked of Pilate that their legs might be broken, and [that] they might be taken away.
043	JOH	019	032	The soldiers therefore came, and brake the legs of the first, and of the other which was crucified with him:
043	JOH	019	033	but when they came to Jesus, and saw that he was dead already, they brake not his legs:
043	JOH	019	034	howbeit one of the soldiers with a spear pierced his side, and straightway there came out blood and water.
043	JOH	019	035	And he that hath seen hath borne witness, and his witness is true: and he knoweth that he saith true, that ye also may believe.
043	JOH	019	036	For these things came to pass, that the scripture might be fulfilled, A bone of him shall not be broken.
043	JOH	019	037	And again another scripture saith, They shall look on him whom they pierced.
043	JOH	019	038	And after these things Joseph of Arimathaea, being a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jews, asked of Pilate that he might take away the body of Jesus: and Pilate gave [him] leave. He came therefore, and took away his body.
043	JOH	019	039	And there came also Nicodemus, he who at the first came to him by night, bringing a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about a hundred pounds [weight].
043	JOH	019	040	So they took the body of Jesus, and bound it in linen cloths with the spices, as the custom of the Jews is to bury.
043	JOH	019	041	Now in the place where he was crucified there was a garden; and in the garden a new tomb wherein was never man yet laid.
043	JOH	019	042	There then because of the Jews’ Preparation (for the tomb was nigh at hand) they laid Jesus.
043	JOH	020	001	Now on the first [day] of the week cometh Mary Magdalene early, while it was yet dark, unto the tomb, and seeth the stone taken away from the tomb.
043	JOH	020	002	She runneth therefore, and cometh to Simon Peter, and to the other disciple, whom Jesus loved, and saith unto them, They have taken away the Lord out of the tomb, and we know not where they have laid him.
043	JOH	020	003	Peter therefore went forth, and the other disciple, and they went toward the tomb.
043	JOH	020	004	And they ran both together: and the other disciple outran Peter, and came first to the tomb;
043	JOH	020	005	and stooping and looking in, he seeth the linen cloths lying; yet entered he not in.
043	JOH	020	006	Simon Peter therefore also cometh, following him, and entered into the tomb; and he beholdeth the linen cloths lying,
043	JOH	020	007	and the napkin, that was upon his head, not lying with the linen cloths, but rolled up in a place by itself.
043	JOH	020	008	Then entered in therefore the other disciple also, which came first to the tomb, and he saw, and believed.
043	JOH	020	009	For as yet they knew not the scripture, that he must rise again from the dead.
043	JOH	020	010	So the disciples went away again unto their own home.
043	JOH	020	011	But Mary was standing without at the tomb weeping: so, as she wept, she stooped and looked into the tomb;
043	JOH	020	012	and she beholdeth two angels in white sitting, one at the head, and one at the feet, where the body of Jesus had lain.
043	JOH	020	013	And they say unto her, Woman, why weepest thou? She saith unto them, Because they have taken away my Lord, and I know not where they have laid him.
043	JOH	020	014	When she had thus said, she turned herself back, and beholdeth Jesus standing, and knew not that it was Jesus.
043	JOH	020	015	Jesus saith unto her, Woman, why weepest thou? whom seekest thou? She, supposing him to be the gardener, saith unto him, Sir, if thou hast borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away.
043	JOH	020	016	Jesus saith unto her, Mary. She turneth herself, and saith unto him in Hebrew, Rabboni; which is to say, Master.
043	JOH	020	017	Jesus saith to her, Touch me not; for I am not yet ascended unto the Father: but go unto my brethren, and say to them, I ascend unto my Father and your Father, and my God and your God.
043	JOH	020	018	Mary Magdalene cometh and telleth the disciples, I have seen the Lord; and [how that] he had said these things unto her.
043	JOH	020	019	When therefore it was evening, on that day, the first [day] of the week, and when the doors were shut where the disciples were, for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood in the midst, and saith unto them, Peace [be] unto you.
043	JOH	020	020	And when he had said this, he shewed unto them his hands and his side. The disciples therefore were glad, when they saw the Lord.
043	JOH	020	021	Jesus therefore said to them again, Peace [be] unto you: as the Father hath sent me, even so send I you.
043	JOH	020	022	And when he had said this, he breathed on them, and saith unto them, Receive ye the Holy Ghost:
043	JOH	020	023	whose soever sins ye forgive, they are forgiven unto them; whose soever [sins] ye retain, they are retained.
043	JOH	020	024	But Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, was not with them when Jesus came.
043	JOH	020	025	The other disciples therefore said unto him, We have seen the Lord. But he said unto them, Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and put my hand into his side, I will not believe.
043	JOH	020	026	And after eight days again his disciples were within, and Thomas with them. Jesus cometh, the doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, Peace [be] unto you.
043	JOH	020	027	Then saith he to Thomas, Reach hither thy finger, and see my hands; and reach [hither] thy hand, and put it into my side: and be not faithless, but believing.
043	JOH	020	028	Thomas answered and said unto him, My Lord and my God.
043	JOH	020	029	Jesus saith unto him, Because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed [are] they that have not seen, and [yet] have believed.
043	JOH	020	030	Many other signs therefore did Jesus in the presence of the disciples, which are not written in this book:
043	JOH	020	031	but these are written, that ye may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God; and that believing ye may have life in his name.
043	JOH	021	001	After these things Jesus manifested himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias; and he manifested [himself] on this wise.
043	JOH	021	002	There were together Simon Peter, and Thomas called Didymus, and Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, and the [sons] of Zebedee, and two other of his disciples.
043	JOH	021	003	Simon Peter saith unto them, I go a fishing. They say unto him, We also come with thee. They went forth, and entered into the boat; and that night they took nothing.
043	JOH	021	004	But when day was now breaking, Jesus stood on the beach: howbeit the disciples knew not that it was Jesus.
043	JOH	021	005	Jesus therefore saith unto them, Children, have ye aught to eat? They answered him, No.
043	JOH	021	006	And he said unto them, Cast the net on the right side of the boat, and ye shall find. They cast therefore, and now they were not able to draw it for the multitude of fishes.
043	JOH	021	007	That disciple therefore whom Jesus loved saith unto Peter, It is the Lord. So when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he girt his coat about him (for he was naked), and cast himself into the sea.
043	JOH	021	008	But the other disciples came in the little boat (for they were not far from the land, but about two hundred cubits off), dragging the net [full] of fishes.
043	JOH	021	009	So when they got out upon the land, they see a fire of coals there, and fish laid thereon, and bread.
043	JOH	021	010	Jesus saith unto them, Bring of the fish which ye have now taken.
043	JOH	021	011	Simon Peter therefore went up, and drew the net to land, full of great fishes, a hundred and fifty and three: and for all there were so many, the net was not rent.
043	JOH	021	012	Jesus saith unto them, Come [and] break your fast. And none of the disciples durst inquire of him, Who art thou? knowing that it was the Lord.
043	JOH	021	013	Jesus cometh, and taketh the bread, and giveth them, and the fish likewise.
043	JOH	021	014	This is now the third time that Jesus was manifested to the disciples, after that he was risen from the dead.
043	JOH	021	015	So when they had broken their fast, Jesus saith to Simon Peter, Simon, [son] of John, lovest thou me more than these? He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee. He saith unto him, Feed my lambs.
043	JOH	021	016	He saith to him again a second time, Simon, [son] of John, lovest thou me? He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee. He saith unto him, Tend my sheep.
043	JOH	021	017	He saith unto him the third time, Simon, [son] of John, lovest thou me? Peter was grieved because he said unto him the third time, Lovest thou me? And he said unto him, Lord, thou knowest all things; thou knowest that I love thee. Jesus saith unto him, Feed my sheep.
043	JOH	021	018	Verily, verily, I say unto thee, When thou wast young, thou girdedst thyself, and walkedst whither thou wouldest: but when thou shalt be old, thou shalt stretch forth thy hands, and another shall gird thee, and carry thee whither thou wouldest not.
043	JOH	021	019	Now this he spake, signifying by what manner of death he should glorify God. And when he had spoken this, he saith unto him, Follow me.
043	JOH	021	020	Peter, turning about, seeth the disciple whom Jesus loved following; which also leaned back on his breast at the supper, and said, Lord, who is he that betrayeth thee?
043	JOH	021	021	Peter therefore seeing him saith to Jesus, Lord, and what shall this man do?
043	JOH	021	022	Jesus saith unto him, If I will that he tarry till I come, what [is that] to thee? follow thou me.
043	JOH	021	023	This saying therefore went forth among the brethren, that that disciple should not die: yet Jesus said not unto him, that he should not die; but, If I will that he tarry till I come, what [is that] to thee?
043	JOH	021	024	This is the disciple which beareth witness of these things, and wrote these things: and we know that his witness is true.
043	JOH	021	025	And there are also many other things which Jesus did, the which if they should be written every one, I suppose that even the world itself would not contain the books that should be written.
