044	ACT	001	001	The former treatise I made, O Theophilus, concerning all that Jesus began both to do and to teach,
044	ACT	001	002	until the day in which he was received up, after that he had given commandment through the Holy Ghost unto the apostles whom he had chosen:
044	ACT	001	003	To whom he also shewed himself alive after his passion by many proofs, appearing unto them by the space of forty days, and speaking the things concerning the kingdom of God:
044	ACT	001	004	and, being assembled together with them, he charged them not to depart from Jerusalem, but to wait for the promise of the Father, which, [said he], ye heard from me:
044	ACT	001	005	For John indeed baptized with water; but ye shall be baptized with the Holy Ghost not many days hence.
044	ACT	001	006	They therefore, when they were come together, asked him, saying, Lord, dost thou at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?
044	ACT	001	007	And he said unto them, It is not for you to know times or seasons, which the Father hath set within his own authority.
044	ACT	001	008	But ye shall receive power, when the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be my witnesses both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea and Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth.
044	ACT	001	009	And when he had said these things, as they were looking, he was taken up; and a cloud received him out of their sight.
044	ACT	001	010	And while they were looking stedfastly into heaven as he went, behold, two men stood by them in white apparel;
044	ACT	001	011	which also said, Ye men of Galilee, why stand ye looking into heaven? this Jesus, which was received up from you into heaven, shall so come in like manner as ye beheld him going into heaven.
044	ACT	001	012	Then returned they unto Jerusalem from the mount called Olivet, which is nigh unto Jerusalem, a sabbath day’s journey off.
044	ACT	001	013	And when they were come in, they went up into the upper chamber, where they were abiding; both Peter and John and James and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James [the son] of Alphaeus, and Simon the Zealot, and Judas [the son] of James.
044	ACT	001	014	These all with one accord continued stedfastly in prayer, with the women, and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with his brethren.
044	ACT	001	015	And in these days Peter stood up in the midst of the brethren, and said (and there was a multitude of persons [gathered] together, about a hundred and twenty),
044	ACT	001	016	Brethren, it was needful that the scripture should be fulfilled, which the Holy Ghost spake before by the mouth of David concerning Judas, who was guide to them that took Jesus.
044	ACT	001	017	For he was numbered among us, and received his portion in this ministry.
044	ACT	001	018	(Now this man obtained a field with the reward of his iniquity; and falling headlong, he burst asunder in the midst, and all his bowels gushed out.
044	ACT	001	019	And it became known to all the dwellers at Jerusalem; insomuch that in their language that field was called Akeldama, that is, The field of blood.)
044	ACT	001	020	For it is written in the book of Psalms, Let his habitation be made desolate, And let no man dwell therein: and, His office let another take.
044	ACT	001	021	Of the men therefore which have companied with us all the time that the Lord Jesus went in and went out among us,
044	ACT	001	022	beginning from the baptism of John, unto the day that he was received up from us, of these must one become a witness with us of his resurrection.
044	ACT	001	023	And they put forward two, Joseph called Barsabbas, who was surnamed Justus, and Matthias.
044	ACT	001	024	And they prayed, and said, Thou, Lord, which knowest the hearts of all men, shew of these two the one whom thou hast chosen,
044	ACT	001	025	to take the place in this ministry and apostleship, from which Judas fell away, that he might go to his own place.
044	ACT	001	026	And they gave lots for them; and the lot fell upon Matthias; and he was numbered with the eleven apostles.
044	ACT	002	001	And when the day of Pentecost was now come, they were all together in one place.
044	ACT	002	002	And suddenly there came from heaven a sound as of the rushing of a mighty wind, and it filled all the house where they were sitting.
044	ACT	002	003	And there appeared unto them tongues parting asunder, like as of fire; and it sat upon each one of them.
044	ACT	002	004	And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit, and began to speak with other tongues, as the Spirit gave them utterance.
044	ACT	002	005	Now there were dwelling at Jerusalem Jews, devout men, from every nation under heaven.
044	ACT	002	006	And when this sound was heard, the multitude came together, and were confounded, because that every man heard them speaking in his own language.
044	ACT	002	007	And they were all amazed and marveled, saying, Behold, are not all these which speak Galilaeans?
044	ACT	002	008	And how hear we, every man in our own language, wherein we were born?
