044	ACT	002	016	but this is that which hath been spoken by the prophet Joel;
044	ACT	002	017	And it shall be in the last days, saith God, I will pour forth of my Spirit upon all flesh: And your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, And your young men shall see visions, And your old men shall dream dreams:
044	ACT	002	018	Yea and on my servants and on my handmaidens in those days Will I pour forth of my Spirit; and they shall prophesy.
044	ACT	002	019	And I will shew wonders in the heaven above, And signs on the earth beneath; Blood, and fire, and vapour of smoke:
044	ACT	002	020	The sun shall be turned into darkness, And the moon into blood, Before the day of the Lord come, That great and notable [day]:
044	ACT	002	021	And it shall be, that whosoever shall call on the name of the Lord shall be saved.
044	ACT	002	022	Ye men of Israel, hear these words: Jesus of Nazareth, a man approved of God unto you by mighty works and wonders and signs, which God did by him in the midst of you, even as ye yourselves know;
044	ACT	002	023	him, being delivered up by the determinate counsel and foreknowledge of God, ye by the hand of lawless men did crucify and slay:
044	ACT	002	024	whom God raised up, having loosed the pangs of death: because it was not possible that he should be holden of it.
044	ACT	002	025	For David saith concerning him, I beheld the Lord always before my face; For he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved:
044	ACT	002	026	Therefore my heart was glad, and my tongue rejoiced; Moreover my flesh also shall dwell in hope:
044	ACT	002	027	Because thou wilt not leave my soul in Hades, Neither wilt thou give thy Holy One to see corruption.
044	ACT	002	028	Thou madest known unto me the ways of life; Thou shalt make me full of gladness with thy countenance.
044	ACT	002	029	Brethren, I may say unto you freely of the patriarch David, that he both died and was buried, and his tomb is with us unto this day.
044	ACT	002	030	Being therefore a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him, that of the fruit of his loins he would set [one] upon his throne;
044	ACT	002	031	he foreseeing [this] spake of the resurrection of the Christ, that neither was he left in Hades, nor did his flesh see corruption.
044	ACT	002	032	This Jesus did God raise up, whereof we all are witnesses.
044	ACT	002	033	Being therefore by the right hand of God exalted, and having received of the Father the promise of the Holy Ghost, he hath poured forth this, which ye see and hear.
044	ACT	002	034	For David ascended not into the heavens: but he saith himself, The Lord said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand,
044	ACT	002	035	Till I make thine enemies the footstool of thy feet.
044	ACT	002	036	Let all the house of Israel therefore know assuredly, that God hath made him both Lord and Christ, this Jesus whom ye crucified.
044	ACT	002	037	Now when they heard [this], they were pricked in their heart, and said unto Peter and the rest of the apostles, Brethren, what shall we do?
044	ACT	002	038	And Peter [said] unto them, Repent ye, and be baptized every one of you in the name of Jesus Christ unto the remission of your sins; and ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Ghost.
044	ACT	002	039	For to you is the promise, and to your children, and to all that are afar off, [even] as many as the Lord our God shall call unto him.
044	ACT	002	040	And with many other words he testified, and exhorted them, saying, Save yourselves from this crooked generation.
044	ACT	002	041	They then that received his word were baptized: and there were added [unto them] in that day about three thousand souls.
044	ACT	002	042	And they continued stedfastly in the apostles’ teaching and fellowship, in the breaking of bread and the prayers.
044	ACT	002	043	And fear came upon every soul: and many wonders and signs were done by the apostles.
044	ACT	002	044	And all that believed were together, and had all things common;
044	ACT	002	045	and they sold their possessions and goods, and parted them to all, according as any man had need.
044	ACT	002	046	And day by day, continuing stedfastly with one accord in the temple, and breaking bread at home, they did take their food with gladness and singleness of heart,
044	ACT	002	047	praising God, and having favour with all the people. And the Lord added to them day by day those that were being saved.
044	ACT	003	001	Now Peter and John were going up into the temple at the hour of prayer, [being] the ninth [hour].
044	ACT	003	002	And a certain man that was lame from his mother’s womb was carried, whom they laid daily at the door of the temple which is called Beautiful, to ask alms of them that entered into the temple;
044	ACT	003	003	who seeing Peter and John about to go into the temple, asked to receive an alms.
044	ACT	003	004	And Peter, fastening his eyes upon him, with John, said, Look on us.
044	ACT	003	005	And he gave heed unto them, expecting to receive something from them.
044	ACT	003	006	But Peter said, Silver and gold have I none; but what I have, that give I thee. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, walk.
044	ACT	003	007	And he took him by the right hand, and raised him up: and immediately his feet and his ankle-bones received strength.
044	ACT	003	008	And leaping up, he stood, and began to walk; and he entered with them into the temple, walking, and leaping, and praising God.
044	ACT	003	009	And all the people saw him walking and praising God:
044	ACT	003	010	and they took knowledge of him, that it was he which sat for alms at the Beautiful Gate of the temple: and they were filled with wonder and amazement at that which had happened unto him.
044	ACT	003	011	And as he held Peter and John, all the people ran together unto them in the porch that is called Solomon’s, greatly wondering.
044	ACT	003	012	And when Peter saw it, he answered unto the people, Ye men of Israel, why marvel ye at this man? or why fasten ye your eyes on us, as though by our own power or godliness we had made him to walk?
044	ACT	003	013	The God of Abraham, and of Isaac, and of Jacob, the God of our fathers, hath glorified his Servant Jesus; whom ye delivered up, and denied before the face of Pilate, when he had determined to release him.
044	ACT	003	014	But ye denied the Holy and Righteous One, and asked for a murderer to be granted unto you,
044	ACT	003	015	and killed the Prince of life; whom God raised from the dead; whereof we are witnesses.
044	ACT	003	016	And by faith in his name hath his name made this man strong, whom ye behold and know: yea, the faith which is through him hath given him this perfect soundness in the presence of you all.
044	ACT	003	017	And now, brethren, I wot that in ignorance ye did it, as did also your rulers.
044	ACT	003	018	But the things which God foreshewed by the mouth of all the prophets, that his Christ should suffer, he thus fulfilled.
044	ACT	003	019	Repent ye therefore, and turn again, that your sins may be blotted out, that so there may come seasons of refreshing from the presence of the Lord;
044	ACT	003	020	and that he may send the Christ who hath been appointed for you, [even] Jesus:
044	ACT	003	021	whom the heaven must receive until the times of restoration of all things, whereof God spake by the mouth of his holy prophets which have been since the world began.
044	ACT	003	022	Moses indeed said, A prophet shall the Lord God raise up unto you from among your brethren, like unto me; to him shall ye hearken in all things whatsoever he shall speak unto you.
044	ACT	003	023	And it shall be, that every soul, which shall not hearken to that prophet, shall be utterly destroyed from among the people.
044	ACT	003	024	Yea and all the prophets from Samuel and them that followed after, as many as have spoken, they also told of these days.
044	ACT	003	025	Ye are the sons of the prophets, and of the covenant which God made with your fathers, saying unto Abraham, And in thy seed shall all the families of the earth be blessed.
044	ACT	003	026	Unto you first God, having raised up his Servant, sent him to bless you, in turning away every one of you from your iniquities.
044	ACT	004	001	And as they spake unto the people, the priests and the captain of the temple and the Sadducees came upon them,
044	ACT	004	002	being sore troubled because they taught the people, and proclaimed in Jesus the resurrection from the dead.
044	ACT	004	003	And they laid hands on them, and put them in ward unto the morrow: for it was now eventide.
044	ACT	004	004	But many of them that heard the word believed; and the number of the men came to be about five thousand.
044	ACT	004	005	And it came to pass on the morrow, that their rulers and elders and scribes were gathered together in Jerusalem;
044	ACT	004	006	and Annas the high priest [was there], and Caiaphas, and John, and Alexander, and as many as were of the kindred of the high priest.
044	ACT	004	007	And when they had set them in the midst, they inquired, By what power, or in what name, have ye done this?
044	ACT	004	008	Then Peter, filled with the Holy Ghost, said unto them, Ye rulers of the people, and elders,
044	ACT	004	009	if we this day are examined concerning a good deed done to an impotent man, by what means this man is made whole;
044	ACT	004	010	be it known unto you all, and to all the people of Israel, that in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom ye crucified, whom God raised from the dead, [even] in him doth this man stand here before you whole.
044	ACT	004	011	He is the stone which was set at nought of you the builders, which was made the head of the corner.
044	ACT	004	012	And in none other is there salvation: for neither is there any other name under heaven, that is given among men, wherein we must be saved.
044	ACT	004	013	Now when they beheld the boldness of Peter and John, and had perceived that they were unlearned and ignorant men, they marveled; and they took knowledge of them, that they had been with Jesus.
044	ACT	004	014	And seeing the man which was healed standing with them, they could say nothing against it.
044	ACT	004	015	But when they had commanded them to go aside out of the council, they conferred among themselves,
044	ACT	004	016	saying, What shall we do to these men? for that indeed a notable miracle hath been wrought through them, is manifest to all that dwell in Jerusalem; and we cannot deny it.
044	ACT	004	017	But that it spread no further among the people, let us threaten them, that they speak henceforth to no man in this name.
044	ACT	004	018	And they called them, and charged them not to speak at all nor teach in the name of Jesus.
044	ACT	004	019	But Peter and John answered and said unto them, Whether it be right in the sight of God to hearken unto you rather than unto God, judge ye:
044	ACT	004	020	for we cannot but speak the things which we saw and heard.
044	ACT	004	021	And they, when they had further threatened them, let them go, finding nothing how they might punish them, because of the people; for all men glorified God for that which was done.
044	ACT	004	022	For the man was more than forty years old, on whom this miracle of healing was wrought.
044	ACT	004	023	And being let go, they came to their own company, and reported all that the chief priests and the elders had said unto them.
044	ACT	004	024	And they, when they heard it, lifted up their voice to God with one accord, and said, O Lord, thou that didst make the heaven and the earth and the sea, and all that in them is:
044	ACT	004	025	who by the Holy Ghost, [by] the mouth of our father David thy servant, didst say, Why did the Gentiles rage, And the peoples imagine vain things?
044	ACT	004	026	The kings of the earth set themselves in array, And the rulers were gathered together, Against the Lord, and against his Anointed:
044	ACT	004	027	for of a truth in this city against thy holy Servant Jesus, whom thou didst anoint, both Herod and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles and the peoples of Israel, were gathered together,
044	ACT	004	028	to do whatsoever thy hand and thy counsel foreordained to come to pass.
044	ACT	004	029	And now, Lord, look upon their threatenings: and grant unto thy servants to speak thy word with all boldness,
044	ACT	004	030	while thou stretchest forth thy hand to heal; and that signs and wonders may be done through the name of thy holy Servant Jesus.
044	ACT	004	031	And when they had prayed, the place was shaken wherein they were gathered together; and they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and they spake the word of God with boldness.
044	ACT	004	032	And the multitude of them that believed were of one heart and soul: and not one [of them] said that aught of the things which he possessed was his own; but they had all things common.
044	ACT	004	033	And with great power gave the apostles their witness of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus: and great grace was upon them all.
