044	ACT	005	001	But a certain man named Ananias, with Sapphira his wife, sold a possession,
044	ACT	005	002	and kept back [part] of the price, his wife also being privy to it, and brought a certain part, and laid it at the apostles’ feet.
044	ACT	005	003	But Peter said, Ananias, why hath Satan filled thy heart to lie to the Holy Ghost, and to keep back [part] of the price of the land?
044	ACT	005	004	Whiles it remained, did it not remain thine own? and after it was sold, was it not in thy power? How is it that thou hast conceived this thing in thy heart? thou hast not lied unto men, but unto God.
044	ACT	005	005	And Ananias hearing these words fell down and gave up the ghost: and great fear came upon all that heard it.
044	ACT	005	006	And the young men arose and wrapped him round, and they carried him out and buried him.
044	ACT	005	007	And it was about the space of three hours after, when his wife, not knowing what was done, came in.
044	ACT	005	008	And Peter answered unto her, Tell me whether ye sold the land for so much. And she said, Yea, for so much.
044	ACT	005	009	But Peter [said] unto her, How is it that ye have agreed together to tempt the Spirit of the Lord? behold, the feet of them which have buried thy husband are at the door, and they shall carry thee out.
044	ACT	005	010	And she fell down immediately at his feet, and gave up the ghost: and the young men came in and found her dead, and they carried her out and buried her by her husband.
044	ACT	005	011	And great fear came upon the whole church, and upon all that heard these things.
044	ACT	005	012	And by the hands of the apostles were many signs and wonders wrought among the people; and they were all with one accord in Solomon’s porch.
044	ACT	005	013	But of the rest durst no man join himself to them: howbeit the people magnified them;
044	ACT	005	014	and believers were the more added to the Lord, multitudes both of men and women;
044	ACT	005	015	insomuch that they even carried out the sick into the streets, and laid them on beds and couches, that, as Peter came by, at the least his shadow might overshadow some one of them.
044	ACT	005	016	And there also came together the multitude from the cities round about Jerusalem, bringing sick folk, and them that were vexed with unclean spirits: and they were healed every one.
044	ACT	005	017	But the high priest rose up, and all they that were with him (which is the sect of the Sadducees), and they were filled with jealousy,
044	ACT	005	018	and laid hands on the apostles, and put them in public ward.
044	ACT	005	019	But an angel of the Lord by night opened the prison doors, and brought them out, and said,
044	ACT	005	020	Go ye, and stand and speak in the temple to the people all the words of this Life.
044	ACT	005	021	And when they heard [this], they entered into the temple about daybreak, and taught. But the high priest came, and they that were with him, and called the council together, and all the senate of the children of Israel, and sent to the prison-house to have them brought.
044	ACT	005	022	But the officers that came found them not in the prison; and they returned, and told,
044	ACT	005	023	saying, The prison-house we found shut in all safety, and the keepers standing at the doors: but when we had opened, we found no man within.
044	ACT	005	024	Now when the captain of the temple and the chief priests heard these words, they were much perplexed concerning them whereunto this would grow.
044	ACT	005	025	And there came one and told them, Behold, the men whom ye put in the prison are in the temple standing and teaching the people.
044	ACT	005	026	Then went the captain with the officers, and brought them, [but] without violence; for they feared the people, lest they should be stoned.
044	ACT	005	027	And when they had brought them, they set them before the council. And the high priest asked them,
044	ACT	005	028	saying, We straitly charged you not to teach in this name: and behold, ye have filled Jerusalem with your teaching, and intend to bring this man’s blood upon us.
044	ACT	005	029	But Peter and the apostles answered and said, We must obey God rather than men.
044	ACT	005	030	The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom ye slew, hanging him on a tree.
044	ACT	005	031	Him did God exalt with his right hand [to be] a Prince and a Saviour, for to give repentance to Israel, and remission of sins.
044	ACT	005	032	And we are witnesses of these things; and [so is] the Holy Ghost, whom God hath given to them that obey him.
044	ACT	005	033	But they, when they heard this, were cut to the heart, and were minded to slay them.
044	ACT	005	034	But there stood up one in the council, a Pharisee, named Gamaliel, a doctor of the law, had in honour of all the people, and commanded to put the men forth a little while.
044	ACT	005	035	And he said unto them, Ye men of Israel, take heed to yourselves as touching these men, what ye are about to do.
