044	ACT	017	025	neither is he served by men’s hands, as though he needed anything, seeing he himself giveth to all life, and breath, and all things;
044	ACT	017	026	and he made of one every nation of men for to dwell on all the face of the earth, having determined [their] appointed seasons, and the bounds of their habitation;
044	ACT	017	027	that they should seek God, if haply they might feel after him, and find him, though he is not far from each one of us:
044	ACT	017	028	for in him we live, and move, and have our being; as certain even of your own poets have said, For we are also his offspring.
044	ACT	017	029	Being then the offspring of God, we ought not to think that the Godhead is like unto gold, or silver, or stone, graven by art and device of man.
