044	ACT	028	015	And from thence the brethren, when they heard of us, came to meet us as far as The Market of Appius, and The Three Taverns: whom when Paul saw, he thanked God, and took courage.
044	ACT	028	016	And when we entered into Rome, Paul was suffered to abide by himself with the soldier that guarded him.
044	ACT	028	017	And it came to pass, that after three days he called together those that were the chief of the Jews: and when they were come together, he said unto them, I, brethren, though I had done nothing against the people, or the customs of our fathers, yet was delivered prisoner from Jerusalem into the hands of the Romans:
044	ACT	028	018	who, when they had examined me, desired to set me at liberty, because there was no cause of death in me.
044	ACT	028	019	But when the Jews spake against it, I was constrained to appeal unto Caesar; not that I had aught to accuse my nation of.
044	ACT	028	020	For this cause therefore did I entreat you to see and to speak with [me]: for because of the hope of Israel I am bound with this chain.
044	ACT	028	021	And they said unto him, We neither received letters from Judaea concerning thee, nor did any of the brethren come hither and report or speak any harm of thee.
044	ACT	028	022	But we desire to hear of thee what thou thinkest: for as concerning this sect, it is known to us that everywhere it is spoken against.
044	ACT	028	023	And when they had appointed him a day, they came to him into his lodging in great number; to whom he expounded [the matter], testifying the kingdom of God, and persuading them concerning Jesus, both from the law of Moses and from the prophets, from morning till evening.
044	ACT	028	024	And some believed the things which were spoken, and some disbelieved.
044	ACT	028	025	And when they agreed not among themselves, they departed, after that Paul had spoken one word, Well spake the Holy Ghost by Isaiah the prophet unto your fathers,
044	ACT	028	026	saying, Go thou unto this people, and say, By hearing ye shall hear, and shall in no wise understand; And seeing ye shall see, and shall in no wise perceive:
044	ACT	028	027	For this people’s heart is waxed gross, And their ears are dull of hearing, And their eyes they have closed; Lest haply they should perceive with their eyes, And hear with their ears, And understand with their heart, And should turn again, And I should heal them.
044	ACT	028	028	Be it known therefore unto you, that this salvation of God is sent unto the Gentiles: they will also hear.
044	ACT	028	030	And he abode two whole years in his own hired dwelling, and received all that went in unto him,
044	ACT	028	031	preaching the kingdom of God, and teaching the things concerning the Lord Jesus Christ with all boldness, none forbidding him.
#
# BOOK	045	ROM	Romans	Romans
045	ROM	001	001	Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, called [to be] an apostle, separated unto the gospel of God,
045	ROM	001	002	which he promised afore by his prophets in the holy scriptures,
045	ROM	001	003	concerning his Son, who was born of the seed of David according to the flesh,
045	ROM	001	004	who was declared [to be] the Son of God with power, according to the spirit of holiness, by the resurrection of the dead; [even] Jesus Christ our Lord,
045	ROM	001	005	through whom we received grace and apostleship, unto obedience of faith among all the nations, for his name’s sake:
045	ROM	001	006	among whom are ye also, called [to be] Jesus Christ’s:
045	ROM	001	007	To all that are in Rome, beloved of God, called [to be] saints: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	001	008	First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for you all, that your faith is proclaimed throughout the whole world.
045	ROM	001	009	For God is my witness, whom I serve in my spirit in the gospel of his Son, how unceasingly I make mention of you, always in my prayers
045	ROM	001	010	making request, if by any means now at length I may be prospered by the will of God to come unto you.
045	ROM	001	011	For I long to see you, that I may impart unto you some spiritual gift, to the end ye may be established;
045	ROM	001	012	that is, that I with you may be comforted in you, each of us by the other’s faith, both yours and mine.
045	ROM	001	013	And I would not have you ignorant, brethren, that oftentimes I purposed to come unto you (and was hindered hitherto), that I might have some fruit in you also, even as in the rest of the Gentiles.
045	ROM	001	014	I am debtor both to Greeks and to Barbarians, both to the wise and to the foolish.
045	ROM	001	015	So, as much as in me is, I am ready to preach the gospel to you also that are in Rome.
045	ROM	001	016	For I am not ashamed of the gospel: for it is the power of God unto salvation to every one that believeth; to the Jew first, and also to the Greek.
045	ROM	001	017	For therein is revealed a righteousness of God by faith unto faith: as it is written, But the righteous shall live by faith.
045	ROM	001	018	For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold down the truth in unrighteousness;
045	ROM	001	019	because that which may be known of God is manifest in them; for God manifested it unto them.
045	ROM	001	020	For the invisible things of him since the creation of the world are clearly seen, being perceived through the things that are made, [even] his everlasting power and divinity; that they may be without excuse:
045	ROM	001	021	because that, knowing God, they glorified him not as God, neither gave thanks; but became vain in their reasonings, and their senseless heart was darkened.
045	ROM	001	022	Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools,
045	ROM	001	023	and changed the glory of the incorruptible God for the likeness of an image of corruptible man, and of birds, and four-footed beasts, and creeping things.
045	ROM	001	024	Wherefore God gave them up in the lusts of their hearts unto uncleanness, that their bodies should be dishonoured among themselves:
045	ROM	001	025	for that they exchanged the truth of God for a lie, and worshipped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is blessed for ever. Amen.
045	ROM	001	026	For this cause God gave them up unto vile passions: for their women changed the natural use into that which is against nature:
045	ROM	001	027	and likewise also the men, leaving the natural use of the woman, burned in their lust one toward another, men with men working unseemliness, and receiving in themselves that recompense of their error which was due.
045	ROM	001	028	And even as they refused to have God in [their] knowledge, God gave them up unto a reprobate mind, to do those things which are not fitting;
045	ROM	001	029	being filled with all unrighteousness, wickedness, covetousness, maliciousness; full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, malignity; whisperers,
045	ROM	001	030	backbiters, hateful to God, insolent, haughty, boastful, inventors of evil things, disobedient to parents,
045	ROM	001	031	without understanding, covenant-breakers, without natural affection, unmerciful:
045	ROM	001	032	who, knowing the ordinance of God, that they which practise such things are worthy of death, not only do the same, but also consent with them that practise them.
045	ROM	002	001	Wherefore thou art without excuse, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest: for wherein thou judgest another, thou condemnest thyself; for thou that judgest dost practise the same things.
045	ROM	002	002	And we know that the judgment of God is according to truth against them that practise such things.
045	ROM	002	003	And reckonest thou this, O man, who judgest them that practise such things, and doest the same, that thou shalt escape the judgment of God?
045	ROM	002	004	Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering, not knowing that the goodness of God leadeth thee to repentance?
045	ROM	002	005	but after thy hardness and impenitent heart treasurest up for thyself wrath in the day of wrath and revelation of the righteous judgment of God;
045	ROM	002	006	who will render to every man according to his works:
045	ROM	002	007	to them that by patience in well-doing seek for glory and honour and incorruption, eternal life:
045	ROM	002	008	but unto them that are factious, and obey not the truth, but obey unrighteousness, [shall be] wrath and indignation,
045	ROM	002	009	tribulation and anguish, upon every soul of man that worketh evil, of the Jew first, and also of the Greek;
045	ROM	002	010	but glory and honour and peace to every man that worketh good, to the Jew first, and also to the Greek:
045	ROM	002	011	for there is no respect of persons with God.
045	ROM	002	012	For as many as have sinned without law shall also perish without law: and as many as have sinned under law shall be judged by law;
045	ROM	002	013	for not the hearers of a law are just before God, but the doers of a law shall be justified:
045	ROM	002	014	for when Gentiles which have no law do by nature the things of the law, these, having no law, are a law unto themselves;
045	ROM	002	015	in that they shew the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience bearing witness therewith, and their thoughts one with another accusing or else excusing [them];
045	ROM	002	016	in the day when God shall judge the secrets of men, according to my gospel, by Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	002	017	But if thou bearest the name of a Jew, and restest upon the law, and gloriest in God,
045	ROM	002	018	and knowest his will, and approvest the things that are excellent, being instructed out of the law,
045	ROM	002	019	and art confident that thou thyself art a guide of the blind, a light of them that are in darkness,
045	ROM	002	020	a corrector of the foolish, a teacher of babes, having in the law the form of knowledge and of the truth;
045	ROM	002	021	thou therefore that teachest another, teachest thou not thyself? thou that preachest a man should not steal, dost thou steal?
045	ROM	002	022	thou that sayest a man should not commit adultery, dost thou commit adultery? thou that abhorrest idols, dost thou rob temples?
045	ROM	002	023	thou who gloriest in the law, through thy transgression of the law dishonourest thou God?
045	ROM	002	024	For the name of God is blasphemed among the Gentiles because of you, even as it is written.
045	ROM	002	025	For circumcision indeed profiteth, if thou be a doer of the law: but if thou be a transgressor of the law, thy circumcision is become uncircumcision.
045	ROM	002	026	If therefore the uncircumcision keep the ordinances of the law, shall not his uncircumcision be reckoned for circumcision?
045	ROM	002	027	and shall not the uncircumcision which is by nature, if it fulfill the law, judge thee, who with the letter and circumcision art a transgressor of the law?
045	ROM	002	028	For he is not a Jew, which is one outwardly; neither is that circumcision, which is outward in the flesh:
045	ROM	002	029	but he is a Jew, which is one inwardly; and circumcision is that of the heart, in the spirit, not in the letter; whose praise is not of men, but of God.
045	ROM	003	001	What advantage then hath the Jew? or what is the profit of circumcision?
045	ROM	003	002	Much every way: first of all, that they were intrusted with the oracles of God.
045	ROM	003	003	For what if some were without faith? shall their want of faith make of none effect the faithfulness of God?
045	ROM	003	004	God forbid: yea, let God be found true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy words, And mightest prevail when thou comest into judgment.
045	ROM	003	005	But if our unrighteousness commendeth the righteousness of God, what shall we say? Is God unrighteous who visiteth with wrath? (I speak after the manner of men.)
045	ROM	003	006	God forbid: for then how shall God judge the world?
045	ROM	003	007	But if the truth of God through my lie abounded unto his glory, why am I also still judged as a sinner?
045	ROM	003	008	and why not (as we be slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say), Let us do evil, that good may come? whose condemnation is just.
045	ROM	003	009	What then? are we in worse case than they? No, in no wise: for we before laid to the charge both of Jews and Greeks, that they are all under sin;
045	ROM	003	010	as it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one;
045	ROM	003	011	There is none that understandeth, There is none that seeketh after God;
045	ROM	003	012	They have all turned aside, they are together become unprofitable; There is none that doeth good, no, not so much as one:
045	ROM	003	013	Their throat is an open sepulchre; With their tongues they have used deceit: The poison of asps is under their lips:
045	ROM	003	014	Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness:
045	ROM	003	015	Their feet are swift to shed blood;
045	ROM	003	016	Destruction and misery are in their ways;
045	ROM	003	017	And the way of peace have they not known:
045	ROM	003	018	There is no fear of God before their eyes.
045	ROM	003	019	Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it speaketh to them that are under the law; that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may be brought under the judgment of God:
045	ROM	003	020	because by the works of the law shall no flesh be justified in his sight: for through the law [cometh] the knowledge of sin.
045	ROM	003	021	But now apart from the law a righteousness of God hath been manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets;
045	ROM	003	022	even the righteousness of God through faith in Jesus Christ unto all them that believe; for there is no distinction;
045	ROM	003	023	for all have sinned, and fall short of the glory of God;
045	ROM	003	024	being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus:
045	ROM	003	025	whom God set forth [to be] a propitiation, through faith, by his blood, to shew his righteousness, because of the passing over of the sins done aforetime, in the forbearance of God;
045	ROM	003	026	for the shewing, [I say], of his righteousness at this present season: that he might himself be just, and the justifier of him that hath faith in Jesus.
045	ROM	003	027	Where then is the glorying? It is excluded. By what manner of law? of works? Nay: but by a law of faith.
045	ROM	003	028	We reckon therefore that a man is justified by faith apart from the works of the law.
045	ROM	003	029	Or is God [the God] of Jews only? is he not [the God] of Gentiles also? Yea, of Gentiles also:
045	ROM	003	030	if so be that God is one, and he shall justify the circumcision by faith, and the uncircumcision through faith.
045	ROM	003	031	Do we then make the law of none effect through faith? God forbid: nay, we establish the law.
045	ROM	004	001	What then shall we say that Abraham, our forefather according to the flesh, hath found?
045	ROM	004	002	For if Abraham was justified by works, he hath whereof to glory; but not toward God.
045	ROM	004	003	For what saith the scripture? And Abraham believed God, and it was reckoned unto him for righteousness.
045	ROM	004	004	Now to him that worketh, the reward is not reckoned as of grace, but as of debt.
045	ROM	004	005	But to him that worketh not, but believeth on him that justifieth the ungodly, his faith is reckoned for righteousness.
045	ROM	004	006	Even as David also pronounceth blessing upon the man, unto whom God reckoneth righteousness apart from works,
045	ROM	004	007	[saying], Blessed are they whose iniquities are forgiven, And whose sins are covered.
045	ROM	004	008	Blessed is the man to whom the Lord will not reckon sin.
045	ROM	004	009	Is this blessing then pronounced upon the circumcision, or upon the uncircumcision also? for we say, To Abraham his faith was reckoned for righteousness.
045	ROM	004	010	How then was it reckoned? when he was in circumcision, or in uncircumcision? Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision:
045	ROM	004	011	and he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had while he was in uncircumcision: that he might be the father of all them that believe, though they be in uncircumcision, that righteousness might be reckoned unto them;
045	ROM	004	012	and the father of circumcision to them who not only are of the circumcision, but who also walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham which he had in uncircumcision.
045	ROM	004	013	For not through the law was the promise to Abraham or to his seed, that he should be heir of the world, but through the righteousness of faith.
045	ROM	004	014	For if they which are of the law be heirs, faith is made void, and the promise is made of none effect:
045	ROM	004	015	for the law worketh wrath; but where there is no law, neither is there transgression.
045	ROM	004	016	For this cause [it is] of faith, that [it may be] according to grace; to the end that the promise may be sure to all the seed; not to that only which is of the law, but to that also which is of the faith of Abraham, who is the father of us all
045	ROM	004	017	(as it is written, A father of many nations have I made thee) before him whom he believed, [even] God, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth the things that are not, as though they were.
045	ROM	004	018	Who in hope believed against hope, to the end that he might become a father of many nations, according to that which had been spoken, So shall thy seed be.
045	ROM	004	019	And without being weakened in faith he considered his own body now as good as dead (he being about a hundred years old), and the deadness of Sarah’s womb:
045	ROM	004	020	yea, looking unto the promise of God, he wavered not through unbelief, but waxed strong through faith, giving glory to God,
045	ROM	004	021	and being fully assured that, what he had promised, he was able also to perform.
045	ROM	004	022	Wherefore also it was reckoned unto him for righteousness.
045	ROM	004	023	Now it was not written for his sake alone, that it was reckoned unto him;
045	ROM	004	024	but for our sake also, unto whom it shall be reckoned, who believe on him that raised Jesus our Lord from the dead,
045	ROM	004	025	who was delivered up for our trespasses, and was raised for our justification.
045	ROM	005	001	Being therefore justified by faith, let us have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ;
045	ROM	005	002	through whom also we have had our access by faith into this grace wherein we stand; and let us rejoice in hope of the glory of God.
045	ROM	005	003	And not only so, but let us also rejoice in our tribulations: knowing that tribulation worketh patience;
045	ROM	005	004	and patience, probation; and probation, hope:
045	ROM	005	005	and hope putteth not to shame; because the love of God hath been shed abroad in our hearts through the Holy Ghost which was given unto us.
045	ROM	005	006	For while we were yet weak, in due season Christ died for the ungodly.
045	ROM	005	007	For scarcely for a righteous man will one die: for peradventure for the good man some one would even dare to die.
045	ROM	005	008	But God commendeth his own love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.
045	ROM	005	009	Much more then, being now justified by his blood, shall we be saved from the wrath [of God] through him.
045	ROM	005	010	For if, while we were enemies, we were reconciled to God through the death of his Son, much more, being reconciled, shall we be saved by his life;
045	ROM	005	011	and not only so, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received the reconciliation.
045	ROM	005	012	Therefore, as through one man sin entered into the world, and death through sin; and so death passed unto all men, for that all sinned: —
045	ROM	005	013	for until the law sin was in the world: but sin is not imputed when there is no law.
045	ROM	005	014	Nevertheless death reigned from Adam until Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the likeness of Adam’s transgression, who is a figure of him that was to come.
045	ROM	005	015	But not as the trespass, so also [is] the free gift. For if by the trespass of the one the many died, much more did the grace of God, and the gift by the grace of the one man, Jesus Christ, abound unto the many.
045	ROM	005	016	And not as through one that sinned, [so] is the gift: for the judgment [came] of one unto condemnation, but the free gift [came] of many trespasses unto justification.
045	ROM	005	017	For if, by the trespass of the one, death reigned through the one; much more shall they that receive the abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness reign in life through the one, [even] Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	005	018	So then as through one trespass [the judgment came] unto all men to condemnation; even so through one act of righteousness [the free gift came] unto all men to justification of life.
045	ROM	005	019	For as through the one man’s disobedience the many were made sinners, even so through the obedience of the one shall the many be made righteous.
045	ROM	005	020	And the law came in beside, that the trespass might abound; but where sin abounded, grace did abound more exceedingly:
045	ROM	005	021	that, as sin reigned in death, even so might grace reign through righteousness unto eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.
045	ROM	006	001	What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound?
045	ROM	006	002	God forbid. We who died to sin, how shall we any longer live therein?
045	ROM	006	003	Or are ye ignorant that all we who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into his death?
045	ROM	006	004	We were buried therefore with him through baptism into death: that like as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, so we also might walk in newness of life.
045	ROM	006	005	For if we have become united with [him] by the likeness of his death, we shall be also [by the likeness] of his resurrection;
045	ROM	006	006	knowing this, that our old man was crucified with [him], that the body of sin might be done away, that so we should no longer be in bondage to sin;
045	ROM	006	007	for he that hath died is justified from sin.
045	ROM	006	008	But if we died with Christ, we believe that we shall also live with him;
045	ROM	006	009	knowing that Christ being raised from the dead dieth no more; death no more hath dominion over him.
045	ROM	006	010	For the death that he died, he died unto sin once: but the life that he liveth, he liveth unto God.
045	ROM	006	011	Even so reckon ye also yourselves to be dead unto sin, but alive unto God in Christ Jesus.
045	ROM	006	012	Let not sin therefore reign in your mortal body, that ye should obey the lusts thereof:
045	ROM	006	013	neither present your members unto sin [as] instruments of unrighteousness; but present yourselves unto God, as alive from the dead, and your members [as] instruments of righteousness unto God.
045	ROM	006	014	For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under law, but under grace.
045	ROM	006	015	What then? shall we sin, because we are not under law, but under grace? God forbid.
045	ROM	006	016	Know ye not, that to whom ye present yourselves [as] servants unto obedience, his servants ye are whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?
045	ROM	006	017	But thanks be to God, that, whereas ye were servants of sin, ye became obedient from the heart to that form of teaching whereunto ye were delivered;
045	ROM	006	018	and being made free from sin, ye became servants of righteousness.
045	ROM	006	019	I speak after the manner of men because of the infirmity of your flesh: for as ye presented your members [as] servants to uncleanness and to iniquity unto iniquity, even so now present your members [as] servants to righteousness unto sanctification.
045	ROM	006	020	For when ye were servants of sin, ye were free in regard of righteousness.
045	ROM	006	021	What fruit then had ye at that time in the things whereof ye are now ashamed? for the end of those things is death.
045	ROM	006	022	But now being made free from sin, and become servants to God, ye have your fruit unto sanctification, and the end eternal life.
045	ROM	006	023	For the wages of sin is death; but the free gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord.
045	ROM	007	001	Or are ye ignorant, brethren (for I speak to men that know the law), how that the law hath dominion over a man for so long time as he liveth?
045	ROM	007	002	For the woman that hath a husband is bound by law to the husband while he liveth; but if the husband die, she is discharged from the law of the husband.
045	ROM	007	003	So then if, while the husband liveth, she be joined to another man, she shall be called an adulteress: but if the husband die, she is free from the law, so that she is no adulteress, though she be joined to another man.
045	ROM	007	004	Wherefore, my brethren, ye also were made dead to the law through the body of Christ; that ye should be joined to another, [even] to him who was raised from the dead, that we might bring forth fruit unto God.
045	ROM	007	005	For when we were in the flesh, the sinful passions, which were through the law, wrought in our members to bring forth fruit unto death.
045	ROM	007	006	But now we have been discharged from the law, having died to that wherein we were holden; so that we serve in newness of the spirit, and not in oldness of the letter.
045	ROM	007	007	What shall we say then? Is the law sin? God forbid. Howbeit, I had not known sin, except through the law: for I had not known coveting, except the law had said, Thou shalt not covet:
045	ROM	007	008	but sin, finding occasion, wrought in me through the commandment all manner of coveting: for apart from the law sin [is] dead.
045	ROM	007	009	And I was alive apart from the law once: but when the commandment came, sin revived, and I died;
045	ROM	007	010	and the commandment, which [was] unto life, this I found [to be] unto death:
045	ROM	007	011	for sin, finding occasion, through the commandment beguiled me, and through it slew me.
045	ROM	007	012	So that the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and righteous, and good.
045	ROM	007	013	Did then that which is good become death unto me? God forbid. But sin, that it might be shewn to be sin, by working death to me through that which is good; —that through the commandment sin might become exceeding sinful.
045	ROM	007	014	For we know that the law is spiritual: but I am carnal, sold under sin.
045	ROM	007	015	For that which I do I know not: for not what I would, that do I practise; but what I hate, that I do.
045	ROM	007	016	But if what I would not, that I do, I consent unto the law that it is good.
045	ROM	007	017	So now it is no more I that do it, but sin which dwelleth in me.
045	ROM	007	018	For I know that in me, that is, in my flesh, dwelleth no good thing: for to will is present with me, but to do that which is good [is] not.
045	ROM	007	019	For the good which I would I do not: but the evil which I would not, that I practise.
045	ROM	007	020	But if what I would not, that I do, it is no more I that do it, but sin which dwelleth in me.
045	ROM	007	021	I find then the law, that, to me who would do good, evil is present.
045	ROM	007	022	For I delight in the law of God after the inward man:
045	ROM	007	023	but I see a different law in my members, warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity under the law of sin which is in my members.
045	ROM	007	024	O wretched man that I am! who shall deliver me out of the body of this death?
045	ROM	007	025	I thank God through Jesus Christ our Lord. So then I myself with the mind serve the law of God; but with the flesh the law of sin.
045	ROM	008	001	There is therefore now no condemnation to them that are in Christ Jesus.
045	ROM	008	002	For the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus made me free from the law of sin and of death.
045	ROM	008	003	For what the law could not do, in that it was weak through the flesh, God, sending his own Son in the likeness of sinful flesh and [as an offering] for sin, condemned sin in the flesh:
045	ROM	008	004	that the ordinance of the law might be fulfilled in us, who walk not after the flesh, but after the spirit.
045	ROM	008	005	For they that are after the flesh do mind the things of the flesh; but they that are after the spirit the things of the spirit.
045	ROM	008	006	For the mind of the flesh is death; but the mind of the spirit is life and peace:
045	ROM	008	007	because the mind of the flesh is enmity against God; for it is not subject to the law of God, neither indeed can it be:
045	ROM	008	008	and they that are in the flesh cannot please God.
045	ROM	008	009	But ye are not in the flesh, but in the spirit, if so be that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you. But if any man hath not the Spirit of Christ, he is none of his.
045	ROM	008	010	And if Christ is in you, the body is dead because of sin; but the spirit is life because of righteousness.
045	ROM	008	011	But if the Spirit of him that raised up Jesus from the dead dwelleth in you, he that raised up Christ Jesus from the dead shall quicken also your mortal bodies through his Spirit that dwelleth in you.
045	ROM	008	012	So then, brethren, we are debtors, not to the flesh, to live after the flesh:
045	ROM	008	013	for if ye live after the flesh, ye must die; but if by the spirit ye mortify the deeds of the body, ye shall live.
045	ROM	008	014	For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are sons of God.
045	ROM	008	015	For ye received not the spirit of bondage again unto fear; but ye received the spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father.
045	ROM	008	016	The Spirit himself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are children of God:
045	ROM	008	017	and if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ; if so be that we suffer with [him], that we may be also glorified with [him].
045	ROM	008	018	For I reckon that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed to us-ward.
045	ROM	008	019	For the earnest expectation of the creation waiteth for the revealing of the sons of God.
045	ROM	008	020	For the creation was subjected to vanity, not of its own will, but by reason of him who subjected it, in hope
045	ROM	008	021	that the creation itself also shall be delivered from the bondage of corruption into the liberty of the glory of the children of God.
045	ROM	008	022	For we know that the whole creation groaneth and travaileth in pain together until now.
045	ROM	008	023	And not only so, but ourselves also, which have the firstfruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, waiting for [our] adoption, [to wit], the redemption of our body.
045	ROM	008	024	For by hope were we saved: but hope that is seen is not hope: for who hopeth for that which he seeth?
045	ROM	008	025	But if we hope for that which we see not, [then] do we with patience wait for it.
045	ROM	008	026	And in like manner the Spirit also helpeth our infirmity: for we know not how to pray as we ought; but the Spirit himself maketh intercession for [us] with groanings which cannot be uttered;
045	ROM	008	027	and he that searcheth the hearts knoweth what is the mind of the Spirit, because he maketh intercession for the saints according to [the will of] God.
045	ROM	008	028	And we know that to them that love God all things work together for good, [even] to them that are called according to [his] purpose.
045	ROM	008	029	For whom he foreknew, he also foreordained [to be] conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren:
045	ROM	008	030	and whom he foreordained, them he also called: and whom he called, them he also justified: and whom he justified, them he also glorified.
045	ROM	008	031	What then shall we say to these things? If God [is] for us, who [is] against us?
045	ROM	008	032	He that spared not his own Son, but delivered him up for us all, how shall he not also with him freely give us all things?
045	ROM	008	033	Who shall lay anything to the charge of God’s elect? It is God that justifieth;
045	ROM	008	034	who is he that shall condemn? It is Christ Jesus that died, yea rather, that was raised from the dead, who is at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us.
045	ROM	008	035	Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? shall tribulation, or anguish, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword?
045	ROM	008	036	Even as it is written, For thy sake we are killed all the day long; We were accounted as sheep for the slaughter.
045	ROM	008	037	Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him that loved us.
045	ROM	008	038	For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor things present, nor things to come, nor powers,
045	ROM	008	039	nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.
045	ROM	009	001	I say the truth in Christ, I lie not, my conscience bearing witness with me in the Holy Ghost,
045	ROM	009	002	that I have great sorrow and unceasing pain in my heart.
045	ROM	009	003	For I could wish that I myself were anathema from Christ for my brethren’s sake, my kinsmen according to the flesh:
045	ROM	009	004	who are Israelites; whose is the adoption, and the glory, and the covenants, and the giving of the law, and the service [of God], and the promises;
045	ROM	009	005	whose are the fathers, and of whom is Christ as concerning the flesh, who is over all, God blessed for ever. Amen.
045	ROM	009	006	But [it is] not as though the word of God hath come to nought. For they are not all Israel, which are of Israel:
045	ROM	009	007	neither, because they are Abraham’s seed, are they all children: but, In Isaac shall thy seed be called.
045	ROM	009	008	That is, it is not the children of the flesh that are children of God; but the children of the promise are reckoned for a seed.
045	ROM	009	009	For this is a word of promise, According to this season will I come, and Sarah shall have a son.
045	ROM	009	010	And not only so; but Rebecca also having conceived by one, [even] by our father Isaac—
045	ROM	009	011	for [the children] being not yet born, neither having done anything good or bad, that the purpose of God according to election might stand, not of works, but of him that calleth,
045	ROM	009	012	it was said unto her, The elder shall serve the younger.
045	ROM	009	013	Even as it is written, Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.
045	ROM	009	014	What shall we say then? Is there unrighteousness with God? God forbid.
045	ROM	009	015	For he saith to Moses, I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.
045	ROM	009	016	So then it is not of him that willeth, nor of him that runneth, but of God that hath mercy.
045	ROM	009	017	For the scripture saith unto Pharaoh, For this very purpose did I raise thee up, that I might shew in thee my power, and that my name might be published abroad in all the earth.
045	ROM	009	018	So then he hath mercy on whom he will, and whom he will he hardeneth.
045	ROM	009	019	Thou wilt say then unto me, Why doth he still find fault? For who withstandeth his will?
045	ROM	009	020	Nay but, O man, who art thou that repliest against God? Shall the thing formed say to him that formed it, Why didst thou make me thus?
045	ROM	009	021	Or hath not the potter a right over the clay, from the same lump to make one part a vessel unto honour, and another unto dishonour?
045	ROM	009	022	What if God, willing to shew his wrath, and to make his power known, endured with much longsuffering vessels of wrath fitted unto destruction:
045	ROM	009	023	and that he might make known the riches of his glory upon vessels of mercy, which he afore prepared unto glory,
045	ROM	009	024	[even] us, whom he also called, not from the Jews only, but also from the Gentiles?
045	ROM	009	025	As he saith also in Hosea, I will call that my people, which was not my people; And her beloved, which was not beloved.
045	ROM	009	026	And it shall be, [that] in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people, There shall they be called sons of the living God.
045	ROM	009	027	And Isaiah crieth concerning Israel, If the number of the children of Israel be as the sand of the sea, it is the remnant that shall be saved:
045	ROM	009	028	for the Lord will execute [his] word upon the earth, finishing it and cutting it short.
045	ROM	009	029	And, as Isaiah hath said before, Except the Lord of Sabaoth had left us a seed, We had become as Sodom, and had been made like unto Gomorrah.
045	ROM	009	030	What shall we say then? That the Gentiles, which followed not after righteousness, attained to righteousness, even the righteousness which is of faith:
045	ROM	009	031	but Israel, following after a law of righteousness, did not arrive at [that] law.
045	ROM	009	032	Wherefore? Because [they sought it] not by faith, but as it were by works. They stumbled at the stone of stumbling;
045	ROM	009	033	even as it is written, Behold, I lay in Zion a stone of stumbling and a rock of offence: And he that believeth on him shall not be put to shame.
045	ROM	010	001	Brethren, my heart’s desire and my supplication to God is for them, that they may be saved.
045	ROM	010	002	For I bear them witness that they have a zeal for God, but not according to knowledge.
045	ROM	010	003	For being ignorant of God’s righteousness, and seeking to establish their own, they did not subject themselves to the righteousness of God.
045	ROM	010	004	For Christ is the end of the law unto righteousness to every one that believeth.
045	ROM	010	005	For Moses writeth that the man that doeth the righteousness which is of the law shall live thereby.
045	ROM	010	006	But the righteousness which is of faith saith thus, Say not in thy heart, Who shall ascend into heaven? (that is, to bring Christ down:)
045	ROM	010	007	or, Who shall descend into the abyss? (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead.)
045	ROM	010	008	But what saith it? The word is nigh thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart: that is, the word of faith, which we preach:
045	ROM	010	009	because if thou shalt confess with thy mouth Jesus [as] Lord, and shalt believe in thy heart that God raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved:
045	ROM	010	010	for with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation.
045	ROM	010	011	For the scripture saith, Whosoever believeth on him shall not be put to shame.
045	ROM	010	012	For there is no distinction between Jew and Greek: for the same [Lord] is Lord of all, and is rich unto all that call upon him:
045	ROM	010	013	for, Whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved.
045	ROM	010	014	How then shall they call on him in whom they have not believed? and how shall they believe in him whom they have not heard? and how shall they hear without a preacher?
045	ROM	010	015	and how shall they preach, except they be sent? even as it is written, How beautiful are the feet of them that bring glad tidings of good things!
045	ROM	010	016	But they did not all hearken to the glad tidings. For Isaiah saith, Lord, who hath believed our report?
045	ROM	010	017	So belief [cometh] of hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ.
045	ROM	010	018	But I say, Did they not hear? Yea, verily, Their sound went out into all the earth, And their words unto the ends of the world.
045	ROM	010	019	But I say, Did Israel not know? First Moses saith, I will provoke you to jealousy with that which is no nation, With a nation void of understanding will I anger you.
045	ROM	010	020	And Isaiah is very bold, and saith, I was found of them that sought me not; I became manifest unto them that asked not of me.
045	ROM	010	021	But as to Israel he saith, All the day long did I spread out my hands unto a disobedient and gainsaying people.
045	ROM	011	001	I say then, Did God cast off his people? God forbid. For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.
045	ROM	011	002	God did not cast off his people which he foreknew. Or wot ye not what the scripture saith of Elijah? how he pleadeth with God against Israel,
045	ROM	011	003	Lord, they have killed thy prophets, they have digged down thine altars: and I am left alone, and they seek my life.
045	ROM	011	004	But what saith the answer of God unto him? I have left for myself seven thousand men, who have not bowed the knee to Baal.
045	ROM	011	005	Even so then at this present time also there is a remnant according to the election of grace.
045	ROM	011	006	But if it is by grace, it is no more of works: otherwise grace is no more grace.
045	ROM	011	007	What then? That which Israel seeketh for, that he obtained not; but the election obtained it, and the rest were hardened:
045	ROM	011	008	according as it is written, God gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that they should not see, and ears that they should not hear, unto this very day.
045	ROM	011	009	And David saith, Let their table be made a snare, and a trap, And a stumblingblock, and a recompense unto them:
045	ROM	011	010	Let their eyes be darkened, that they may not see, And bow thou down their back alway.
045	ROM	011	011	I say then, Did they stumble that they might fall? God forbid: but by their fall salvation [is come] unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.
045	ROM	011	012	Now if their fall is the riches of the world, and their loss the riches of the Gentiles; how much more their fulness?
045	ROM	011	013	But I speak to you that are Gentiles. Inasmuch then as I am an apostle of Gentiles, I glorify my ministry:
045	ROM	011	014	if by any means I may provoke to jealousy [them that are] my flesh, and may save some of them.
045	ROM	011	015	For if the casting away of them [is] the reconciling of the world, what [shall] the receiving [of them be], but life from the dead?
045	ROM	011	016	And if the firstfruit is holy, so is the lump: and if the root is holy, so are the branches.
045	ROM	011	017	But if some of the branches were broken off, and thou, being a wild olive, wast grafted in among them, and didst become partaker with them of the root of the fatness of the olive tree;
045	ROM	011	018	glory not over the branches: but if thou gloriest, it is not thou that bearest the root, but the root thee.
045	ROM	011	019	Thou wilt say then, Branches were broken off, that I might be grafted in.
045	ROM	011	020	Well; by their unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by thy faith. Be not highminded, but fear:
045	ROM	011	021	for if God spared not the natural branches, neither will he spare thee.
045	ROM	011	022	Behold then the goodness and severity of God: toward them that fell, severity; but toward thee, God’s goodness, if thou continue in his goodness: otherwise thou also shalt be cut off.
045	ROM	011	023	And they also, if they continue not in their unbelief, shall be grafted in: for God is able to graft them in again.
045	ROM	011	024	For if thou wast cut out of that which is by nature a wild olive tree, and wast grafted contrary to nature into a good olive tree: how much more shall these, which are the natural [branches], be grafted into their own olive tree?
045	ROM	011	025	For I would not, brethren, have you ignorant of this mystery, lest ye be wise in your own conceits, that a hardening in part hath befallen Israel, until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in;
045	ROM	011	026	and so all Israel shall be saved: even as it is written, There shall come out of Zion the Deliverer; He shall turn away ungodliness from Jacob:
045	ROM	011	027	And this is my covenant unto them, When I shall take away their sins.
045	ROM	011	028	As touching the gospel, they are enemies for your sake: but as touching the election, they are beloved for the fathers’ sake.
045	ROM	011	029	For the gifts and the calling of God are without repentance.
045	ROM	011	030	For as ye in time past were disobedient to God, but now have obtained mercy by their disobedience,
045	ROM	011	031	even so have these also now been disobedient, that by the mercy shewn to you they also may now obtain mercy.
045	ROM	011	032	For God hath shut up all unto disobedience, that he might have mercy upon all.
045	ROM	011	033	O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and the knowledge of God! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past tracing out!
045	ROM	011	034	For who hath known the mind of the Lord? or who hath been his counsellor?
045	ROM	011	035	or who hath first given to him, and it shall be recompensed unto him again?
045	ROM	011	036	For of him, and through him, and unto him, are all things. To him [be] the glory for ever. Amen.
045	ROM	012	001	I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, to present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God, [which is] your reasonable service.
045	ROM	012	002	And be not fashioned according to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is the good and acceptable and perfect will of God.
045	ROM	012	003	For I say, through the grace that was given me, to every man that is among you, not to think of himself more highly than he ought to think; but so to think as to think soberly, according as God hath dealt to each man a measure of faith.
045	ROM	012	004	For even as we have many members in one body, and all the members have not the same office:
045	ROM	012	005	so we, who are many, are one body in Christ, and severally members one of another.
045	ROM	012	006	And having gifts differing according to the grace that was given to us, whether prophecy, [let us prophesy] according to the proportion of our faith;
045	ROM	012	007	or ministry, [let us give ourselves] to our ministry; or he that teacheth, to his teaching;
045	ROM	012	008	or he that exhorteth, to his exhorting: he that giveth, [let him do it] with liberality; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness.
045	ROM	012	009	Let love be without hypocrisy. Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good.
045	ROM	012	010	In love of the brethren be tenderly affectioned one to another; in honour preferring one another;
045	ROM	012	011	in diligence not slothful; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord;
045	ROM	012	012	rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing stedfastly in prayer;
045	ROM	012	013	communicating to the necessities of the saints; given to hospitality.
045	ROM	012	014	Bless them that persecute you; bless, and curse not.
045	ROM	012	015	Rejoice with them that rejoice; weep with them that weep.
045	ROM	012	016	Be of the same mind one toward another. Set not your mind on high things, but condescend to things that are lowly. Be not wise in your own conceits.
045	ROM	012	017	Render to no man evil for evil. Take thought for things honourable in the sight of all men.
045	ROM	012	018	If it be possible, as much as in you lieth, be at peace with all men.
045	ROM	012	019	Avenge not yourselves, beloved, but give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance belongeth unto me; I will recompense, saith the Lord.
045	ROM	012	020	But if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him to drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head.
045	ROM	012	021	Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.
045	ROM	013	001	Let every soul be in subjection to the higher powers: for there is no power but of God; and the [powers] that be are ordained of God.
045	ROM	013	002	Therefore he that resisteth the power, withstandeth the ordinance of God: and they that withstand shall receive to themselves judgment.
045	ROM	013	003	For rulers are not a terror to the good work, but to the evil. And wouldest thou have no fear of the power? do that which is good, and thou shalt have praise from the same:
045	ROM	013	004	for he is a minister of God to thee for good. But if thou do that which is evil, be afraid; for he beareth not the sword in vain: for he is a minister of God, an avenger for wrath to him that doeth evil.
045	ROM	013	005	Wherefore [ye] must needs be in subjection, not only because of the wrath, but also for conscience sake.
045	ROM	013	006	For for this cause ye pay tribute also; for they are ministers of God’s service, attending continually upon this very thing.
045	ROM	013	007	Render to all their dues: tribute to whom tribute [is due]; custom to whom custom; fear to whom fear; honour to whom honour.
045	ROM	013	008	Owe no man anything, save to love one another: for he that loveth his neighbour hath fulfilled the law.
045	ROM	013	009	For this, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not kill, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not covet, and if there be any other commandment, it is summed up in this word, namely, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.
045	ROM	013	010	Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: love therefore is the fulfillment of the law.
045	ROM	013	011	And this, knowing the season, that now it is high time for you to awake out of sleep: for now is salvation nearer to us than when we [first] believed.
045	ROM	013	012	The night is far spent, and the day is at hand: let us therefore cast off the works of darkness, and let us put on the armour of light.
045	ROM	013	013	Let us walk honestly, as in the day; not in revelling and drunkenness, not in chambering and wantonness, not in strife and jealousy.
045	ROM	013	014	But put ye on the Lord Jesus Christ, and make not provision for the flesh, to [fulfill] the lusts [thereof].
045	ROM	014	001	But him that is weak in faith receive ye, [yet] not to doubtful disputations.
045	ROM	014	002	One man hath faith to eat all things: but he that is weak eateth herbs.
045	ROM	014	003	Let not him that eateth set at nought him that eateth not; and let not him that eateth not judge him that eateth: for God hath received him.
045	ROM	014	004	Who art thou that judgest the servant of another? to his own lord he standeth or falleth. Yea, he shall be made to stand; for the Lord hath power to make him stand.
045	ROM	014	005	One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day [alike]. Let each man be fully assured in his own mind.
045	ROM	014	006	He that regardeth the day, regardeth it unto the Lord: and he that eateth, eateth unto the Lord, for he giveth God thanks; and he that eateth not, unto the Lord he eateth not, and giveth God thanks.
045	ROM	014	007	For none of us liveth to himself, and none dieth to himself.
045	ROM	014	008	For whether we live, we live unto the Lord; or whether we die, we die unto the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord’s.
045	ROM	014	009	For to this end Christ died, and lived [again], that he might be Lord of both the dead and the living.
045	ROM	014	010	But thou, why dost thou judge thy brother? or thou again, why dost thou set at nought thy brother? for we shall all stand before the judgment-seat of God.
045	ROM	014	011	For it is written, As I live, saith the Lord, to me every knee shall bow, And every tongue shall confess to God.
045	ROM	014	012	So then each one of us shall give account of himself to God.
045	ROM	014	013	Let us not therefore judge one another any more: but judge ye this rather, that no man put a stumblingblock in his brother’s way, or an occasion of falling.
045	ROM	014	014	I know, and am persuaded in the Lord Jesus, that nothing is unclean of itself: save that to him who accounteth anything to be unclean, to him it is unclean.
045	ROM	014	015	For if because of meat thy brother is grieved, thou walkest no longer in love. Destroy not with thy meat him for whom Christ died.
045	ROM	014	016	Let not then your good be evil spoken of:
045	ROM	014	017	for the kingdom of God is not eating and drinking, but righteousness and peace and joy in the Holy Ghost.
045	ROM	014	018	For he that herein serveth Christ is well-pleasing to God, and approved of men.
045	ROM	014	019	So then let us follow after things which make for peace, and things whereby we may edify one another.
045	ROM	014	020	Overthrow not for meat’s sake the work of God. All things indeed are clean; howbeit it is evil for that man who eateth with offence.
045	ROM	014	021	It is good not to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor [to do anything] whereby thy brother stumbleth.
045	ROM	014	022	The faith which thou hast, have thou to thyself before God. Happy is he that judgeth not himself in that which he approveth.
045	ROM	014	023	But he that doubteth is condemned if he eat, because [he eateth] not of faith; and whatsoever is not of faith is sin.
045	ROM	015	001	Now we that are strong ought to bear the infirmities of the weak, and not to please ourselves.
045	ROM	015	002	Let each one of us please his neighbour for that which is good, unto edifying.
045	ROM	015	003	For Christ also pleased not himself; but, as it is written, The reproaches of them that reproached thee fell upon me.
045	ROM	015	004	For whatsoever things were written aforetime were written for our learning, that through patience and through comfort of the scriptures we might have hope.
045	ROM	015	005	Now the God of patience and of comfort grant you to be of the same mind one with another according to Christ Jesus:
045	ROM	015	006	that with one accord ye may with one mouth glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	015	007	Wherefore receive ye one another, even as Christ also received you, to the glory of God.
045	ROM	015	008	For I say that Christ hath been made a minister of the circumcision for the truth of God, that he might confirm the promises [given] unto the fathers,
045	ROM	015	009	and that the Gentiles might glorify God for his mercy; as it is written, Therefore will I give praise unto thee among the Gentiles, And sing unto thy name.
045	ROM	015	010	And again he saith, Rejoice, ye Gentiles, with his people.
045	ROM	015	011	And again, Praise the Lord, all ye Gentiles; And let all the peoples praise him.
045	ROM	015	012	And again, Isaiah saith, There shall be the root of Jesse, And he that ariseth to rule over the Gentiles; On him shall the Gentiles hope.
045	ROM	015	013	Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, in the power of the Holy Ghost.
045	ROM	015	014	And I myself also am persuaded of you, my brethren, that ye yourselves are full of goodness, filled with all knowledge, able also to admonish one another.
045	ROM	015	015	But I write the more boldly unto you in some measure, as putting you again in remembrance, because of the grace that was given me of God,
045	ROM	015	016	that I should be a minister of Christ Jesus unto the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of God, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be made acceptable, being sanctified by the Holy Ghost.
045	ROM	015	017	I have therefore my glorying in Christ Jesus in things pertaining to God.
045	ROM	015	018	For I will not dare to speak of any things save those which Christ wrought through me, for the obedience of the Gentiles, by word and deed,
045	ROM	015	019	in the power of signs and wonders, in the power of the Holy Ghost; so that from Jerusalem, and round about even unto Illyricum, I have fully preached the gospel of Christ;
045	ROM	015	020	yea, making it my aim so to preach the gospel, not where Christ was [already] named, that I might not build upon another man’s foundation;
045	ROM	015	021	but, as it is written, They shall see, to whom no tidings of him came, And they who have not heard shall understand.
045	ROM	015	022	Wherefore also I was hindered these many times from coming to you:
045	ROM	015	023	but now, having no more any place in these regions, and having these many years a longing to come unto you,
045	ROM	015	024	whensoever I go unto Spain (for I hope to see you in my journey, and to be brought on my way thitherward by you, if first in some measure I shall have been satisfied with your company)—
045	ROM	015	025	but now, [I say], I go unto Jerusalem, ministering unto the saints.
045	ROM	015	026	For it hath been the good pleasure of Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor among the saints that are at Jerusalem.
045	ROM	015	027	Yea, it hath been their good pleasure; and their debtors they are. For if the Gentiles have been made partakers of their spiritual things, they owe it [to them] also to minister unto them in carnal things.
045	ROM	015	028	When therefore I have accomplished this, and have sealed to them this fruit, I will go on by you unto Spain.
045	ROM	015	029	And I know that, when I come unto you, I shall come in the fulness of the blessing of Christ.
045	ROM	015	030	Now I beseech you, brethren, by our Lord Jesus Christ, and by the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with me in your prayers to God for me;
045	ROM	015	031	that I may be delivered from them that are disobedient in Judaea, and [that] my ministration which [I have] for Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints;
045	ROM	015	032	that I may come unto you in joy through the will of God, and together with you find rest.
045	ROM	015	033	Now the God of peace be with you all. Amen.
045	ROM	016	001	I commend unto you Phoebe our sister, who is a servant of the church that is at Cenchreae:
045	ROM	016	002	that ye receive her in the Lord, worthily of the saints, and that ye assist her in whatsoever matter she may have need of you: for she herself also hath been a succourer of many, and of mine own self.
045	ROM	016	003	Salute Prisca and Aquila my fellow-workers in Christ Jesus,
045	ROM	016	004	who for my life laid down their own necks; unto whom not only I give thanks, but also all the churches of the Gentiles:
045	ROM	016	005	and [salute] the church that is in their house. Salute Epaenetus my beloved, who is the firstfruits of Asia unto Christ.
045	ROM	016	006	Salute Mary, who bestowed much labour on you.
045	ROM	016	007	Salute Andronicus and Junias, my kinsmen, and my fellow-prisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also have been in Christ before me.
045	ROM	016	008	Salute Ampliatus my beloved in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	009	Salute Urbanus our fellow-worker in Christ, and Stachys my beloved.
045	ROM	016	010	Salute Apelles the approved in Christ. Salute them which are of the [household] of Aristobulus.
045	ROM	016	011	Salute Herodion my kinsman. Salute them of the [household] of Narcissus, which are in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	012	Salute Tryphaena and Tryphosa, who labour in the Lord. Salute Persis the beloved, which laboured much in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	013	Salute Rufus the chosen in the Lord, and his mother and mine.
045	ROM	016	014	Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the brethren that are with them.
045	ROM	016	015	Salute Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints that are with them.
045	ROM	016	016	Salute one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ salute you.
045	ROM	016	017	Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which are causing the divisions and occasions of stumbling, contrary to the doctrine which ye learned: and turn away from them.
045	ROM	016	018	For they that are such serve not our Lord Christ, but their own belly; and by their smooth and fair speech they beguile the hearts of the innocent.
045	ROM	016	019	For your obedience is come abroad unto all men. I rejoice therefore over you: but I would have you wise unto that which is good, and simple unto that which is evil.
045	ROM	016	020	And the God of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
045	ROM	016	021	Timothy my fellow-worker saluteth you; and Lucius and Jason and Sosipater, my kinsmen.
045	ROM	016	022	I Tertius, who write the epistle, salute you in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	023	Gaius my host, and of the whole church, saluteth you. Erastus the treasurer of the city saluteth you, and Quartus the brother.
045	ROM	016	025	Now to him that is able to stablish you according to my gospel and the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery which hath been kept in silence through times eternal,
045	ROM	016	026	but now is manifested, and by the scriptures of the prophets, according to the commandment of the eternal God, is made known unto all the nations unto obedience of faith;
045	ROM	016	027	to the only wise God, through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory for ever. Amen.
