# BOOK	047	2CO	2 Corinthians	2 Corinthians
047	2CO	001	001	Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, and Timothy our brother, unto the church of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints which are in the whole of Achaia:
047	2CO	001	002	Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	001	003	Blessed [be] the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies and God of all comfort;
047	2CO	001	004	who comforteth us in all our affliction, that we may be able to comfort them that are in any affliction, through the comfort wherewith we ourselves are comforted of God.
047	2CO	001	005	For as the sufferings of Christ abound unto us, even so our comfort also aboundeth through Christ.
047	2CO	001	006	But whether we be afflicted, it is for your comfort and salvation; or whether we be comforted, it is for your comfort, which worketh in the patient enduring of the same sufferings which we also suffer:
047	2CO	001	007	and our hope for you is stedfast; knowing that, as ye are partakers of the sufferings, so also are ye of the comfort.
047	2CO	001	008	For we would not have you ignorant, brethren, concerning our affliction which befell [us] in Asia, that we were weighed down exceedingly, beyond our power, insomuch that we despaired even of life:
047	2CO	001	009	yea, we ourselves have had the answer of death within ourselves, that we should not trust in ourselves, but in God which raiseth the dead:
047	2CO	001	010	who delivered us out of so great a death, and will deliver: on whom we have set our hope that he will also still deliver us;
047	2CO	001	011	ye also helping together on our behalf by your supplication; that, for the gift bestowed upon us by means of many, thanks may be given by many persons on our behalf.
047	2CO	001	012	For our glorying is this, the testimony of our conscience, that in holiness and sincerity of God, not in fleshly wisdom but in the grace of God, we behaved ourselves in the world, and more abundantly to you-ward.
047	2CO	001	013	For we write none other things unto you, than what ye read or even acknowledge, and I hope ye will acknowledge unto the end:
047	2CO	001	014	as also ye did acknowledge us in part, that we are your glorying, even as ye also are ours, in the day of our Lord Jesus.
047	2CO	001	015	And in this confidence I was minded to come before unto you, that ye might have a second benefit;
047	2CO	001	016	and by you to pass into Macedonia, and again from Macedonia to come unto you, and of you to be set forward on my journey unto Judaea.
047	2CO	001	017	When I therefore was thus minded, did I shew fickleness? or the things that I purpose, do I purpose according to the flesh, that with me there should be the yea yea and the nay nay?
047	2CO	001	018	But as God is faithful, our word toward you is not yea and nay.
047	2CO	001	019	For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was preached among you by us, [even] by me and Silvanus and Timothy, was not yea and nay, but in him is yea.
047	2CO	001	020	For how many soever be the promises of God, in him is the yea: wherefore also through him is the Amen, unto the glory of God through us.
047	2CO	001	021	Now he that stablisheth us with you in Christ, and anointed us, is God;
047	2CO	001	022	who also sealed us, and gave [us] the earnest of the Spirit in our hearts.
047	2CO	001	023	But I call God for a witness upon my soul, that to spare you I forbare to come unto Corinth.
047	2CO	001	024	Not that we have lordship over your faith, but are helpers of your joy: for by faith ye stand.
047	2CO	002	001	But I determined this for myself, that I would not come again to you with sorrow.
047	2CO	002	002	For if I make you sorry, who then is he that maketh me glad, but he that is made sorry by me?
047	2CO	002	003	And I wrote this very thing, lest, when I came, I should have sorrow from them of whom I ought to rejoice; having confidence in you all, that my joy is [the joy] of you all.
047	2CO	002	004	For out of much affliction and anguish of heart I wrote unto you with many tears; not that ye should be made sorry, but that ye might know the love which I have more abundantly unto you.
047	2CO	002	005	But if any hath caused sorrow, he hath caused sorrow, not to me, but in part (that I press not too heavily) to you all.
047	2CO	002	006	Sufficient to such a one is this punishment which was [inflicted] by the many;
047	2CO	002	007	so that contrariwise ye should rather forgive him and comfort him, lest by any means such a one should be swallowed up with his overmuch sorrow.
047	2CO	002	008	Wherefore I beseech you to confirm [your] love toward him.
047	2CO	002	009	For to this end also did I write, that I might know the proof of you, whether ye are obedient in all things.
047	2CO	002	010	But to whom ye forgive anything, I [forgive] also: for what I also have forgiven, if I have forgiven anything, for your sakes [have I forgiven it] in the person of Christ;
047	2CO	002	011	that no advantage may be gained over us by Satan: for we are not ignorant of his devices.
047	2CO	002	012	Now when I came to Troas for the gospel of Christ, and when a door was opened unto me in the Lord,
047	2CO	002	013	I had no relief for my spirit, because I found not Titus my brother: but taking my leave of them, I went forth into Macedonia.
047	2CO	002	014	But thanks be unto God, which always leadeth us in triumph in Christ, and maketh manifest through us the savour of his knowledge in every place.
047	2CO	002	015	For we are a sweet savour of Christ unto God, in them that are being saved, and in them that are perishing;
047	2CO	002	016	to the one a savour from death unto death; to the other a savour from life unto life. And who is sufficient for these things?
047	2CO	002	017	For we are not as the many, corrupting the word of God: but as of sincerity, but as of God, in the sight of God, speak we in Christ.
047	2CO	003	001	Are we beginning again to commend ourselves? or need we, as do some, epistles of commendation to you or from you?
047	2CO	003	002	Ye are our epistle, written in our hearts, known and read of all men;
047	2CO	003	003	being made manifest that ye are an epistle of Christ, ministered by us, written not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tables of stone, but in tables [that are] hearts of flesh.
047	2CO	003	004	And such confidence have we through Christ to God-ward:
047	2CO	003	005	not that we are sufficient of ourselves, to account anything as from ourselves; but our sufficiency is from God;
047	2CO	003	006	who also made us sufficient as ministers of a new covenant; not of the letter, but of the spirit: for the letter killeth, but the spirit giveth life.
047	2CO	003	007	But if the ministration of death, written, [and] engraven on stones, came with glory, so that the children of Israel could not look stedfastly upon the face of Moses for the glory of his face; which [glory] was passing away:
047	2CO	003	008	how shall not rather the ministration of the spirit be with glory?
047	2CO	003	009	For if the ministration of condemnation is glory, much rather doth the ministration of righteousness exceed in glory.
047	2CO	003	010	For verily that which hath been made glorious hath not been made glorious in this respect, by reason of the glory that surpasseth.
047	2CO	003	011	For if that which passeth away [was] with glory, much more that which remaineth [is] in glory.
047	2CO	003	012	Having therefore such a hope, we use great boldness of speech,
047	2CO	003	013	and [are] not as Moses, [who] put a veil upon his face, that the children of Israel should not look stedfastly on the end of that which was passing away:
047	2CO	003	014	but their minds were hardened: for until this very day at the reading of the old covenant the same veil remaineth unlifted; which [veil] is done away in Christ.
047	2CO	003	015	But unto this day, whensoever Moses is read, a veil lieth upon their heart.
047	2CO	003	016	But whensoever it shall turn to the Lord, the veil is taken away.
047	2CO	003	017	Now the Lord is the Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, [there] is liberty.
047	2CO	003	018	But we all, with unveiled face reflecting as a mirror the glory of the Lord, are transformed into the same image from glory to glory, even as from the Lord the Spirit.
047	2CO	004	001	Therefore seeing we have this ministry, even as we obtained mercy, we faint not:
047	2CO	004	002	but we have renounced the hidden things of shame, not walking in craftiness, nor handling the word of God deceitfully; but by the manifestation of the truth commending ourselves to every man’s conscience in the sight of God.
047	2CO	004	003	But and if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled in them that are perishing:
047	2CO	004	004	in whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of the unbelieving, that the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God, should not dawn [upon them].
047	2CO	004	005	For we preach not ourselves, but Christ Jesus as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus’ sake.
047	2CO	004	006	Seeing it is God, that said, Light shall shine out of darkness, who shined in our hearts, to give the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	004	007	But we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the exceeding greatness of the power may be of God, and not from ourselves;
047	2CO	004	008	[we are] pressed on every side, yet not straitened; perplexed, yet not unto despair;
047	2CO	004	009	pursued, yet not forsaken; smitten down, yet not destroyed;
047	2CO	004	010	always bearing about in the body the dying of Jesus, that the life also of Jesus may be manifested in our body.
047	2CO	004	011	For we which live are alway delivered unto death for Jesus’ sake, that the life also of Jesus may be manifested in our mortal flesh.
047	2CO	004	012	So then death worketh in us, but life in you.
047	2CO	004	013	But having the same spirit of faith, according to that which is written, I believed, and therefore did I speak; we also believe, and therefore also we speak;
047	2CO	004	014	knowing that he which raised up the Lord Jesus shall raise up us also with Jesus, and shall present us with you.
047	2CO	004	015	For all things [are] for your sakes, that the grace, being multiplied through the many, may cause the thanksgiving to abound unto the glory of God.
047	2CO	004	016	Wherefore we faint not; but though our outward man is decaying, yet our inward man is renewed day by day.
047	2CO	004	017	For our light affliction, which is for the moment, worketh for us more and more exceedingly an eternal weight of glory;
047	2CO	004	018	while we look not at the things which are seen, but at the things which are not seen: for the things which are seen are temporal; but the things which are not seen are eternal.
047	2CO	005	001	For we know that if the earthly house of our tabernacle be dissolved, we have a building from God, a house not made with hands, eternal, in the heavens.
047	2CO	005	002	For verily in this we groan, longing to be clothed upon with our habitation which is from heaven:
047	2CO	005	003	if so be that being clothed we shall not be found naked.
047	2CO	005	004	For indeed we that are in this tabernacle do groan, being burdened; not for that we would be unclothed, but that we would be clothed upon, that what is mortal may be swallowed up of life.
047	2CO	005	005	Now he that wrought us for this very thing is God, who gave unto us the earnest of the Spirit.
047	2CO	005	006	Being therefore always of good courage, and knowing that, whilst we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord
047	2CO	005	007	(for we walk by faith, not by sight);
047	2CO	005	008	we are of good courage, I say, and are willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be at home with the Lord.
047	2CO	005	009	Wherefore also we make it our aim, whether at home or absent, to be well-pleasing unto him.
047	2CO	005	010	For we must all be made manifest before the judgment-seat of Christ; that each one may receive the things [done] in the body, according to what he hath done, whether [it be] good or bad.
047	2CO	005	011	Knowing therefore the fear of the Lord, we persuade men, but we are made manifest unto God; and I hope that we are made manifest also in your consciences.
047	2CO	005	012	We are not again commending ourselves unto you, but [speak] as giving you occasion of glorying on our behalf, that ye may have wherewith to answer them that glory in appearance, and not in heart.
047	2CO	005	013	For whether we are beside ourselves, it is unto God; or whether we are of sober mind, it is unto you.
047	2CO	005	014	For the love of Christ constraineth us; because we thus judge, that one died for all, therefore all died;
047	2CO	005	015	and he died for all, that they which live should no longer live unto themselves, but unto him who for their sakes died and rose again.
047	2CO	005	016	Wherefore we henceforth know no man after the flesh: even though we have known Christ after the flesh, yet now we know [him so] no more.
047	2CO	005	017	Wherefore if any man is in Christ, [he is] a new creature: the old things are passed away; behold, they are become new.
047	2CO	005	018	But all things are of God, who reconciled us to himself through Christ, and gave unto us the ministry of reconciliation;
047	2CO	005	019	to wit, that God was in Christ reconciling the world unto himself, not reckoning unto them their trespasses, and having committed unto us the word of reconciliation.
047	2CO	005	020	We are ambassadors therefore on behalf of Christ, as though God were entreating by us: we beseech [you] on behalf of Christ, be ye reconciled to God.
047	2CO	005	021	Him who knew no sin he made [to be] sin on our behalf; that we might become the righteousness of God in him.
047	2CO	006	001	And working together [with him] we entreat also that ye receive not the grace of God in vain
047	2CO	006	002	(for he saith, At an acceptable time I hearkened unto thee, And in a day of salvation did I succour thee: behold, now is the acceptable time; behold, now is the day of salvation):
047	2CO	006	003	giving no occasion of stumbling in anything, that our ministration be not blamed;
047	2CO	006	004	but in everything commending ourselves, as ministers of God, in much patience, in afflictions, in necessities, in distresses,
047	2CO	006	005	in stripes, in imprisonments, in tumults, in labours, in watchings, in fastings;
047	2CO	006	006	in pureness, in knowledge, in longsuffering, in kindness, in the Holy Ghost, in love unfeigned,
047	2CO	006	007	in the word of truth, in the power of God; by the armour of righteousness on the right hand and on the left,
047	2CO	006	008	by glory and dishonour, by evil report and good report; as deceivers, and [yet] true;
047	2CO	006	009	as unknown, and [yet] well known; as dying, and behold, we live; as chastened, and not killed;
047	2CO	006	010	as sorrowful, yet alway rejoicing; as poor, yet making many rich; as having nothing, and [yet] possessing all things.
047	2CO	006	011	Our mouth is open unto you, O Corinthians, our heart is enlarged.
047	2CO	006	012	Ye are not straitened in us, but ye are straitened in your own affections.
047	2CO	006	013	Now for a recompense in like kind (I speak as unto [my] children), be ye also enlarged.
047	2CO	006	014	Be not unequally yoked with unbelievers: for what fellowship have righteousness and iniquity? or what communion hath light with darkness?
047	2CO	006	015	And what concord hath Christ with Belial? or what portion hath a believer with an unbeliever?
047	2CO	006	016	And what agreement hath a temple of God with idols? for we are a temple of the living God; even as God said, I will dwell in them, and walk in them; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people.
047	2CO	006	017	Wherefore Come ye out from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord, And touch no unclean thing; And I will receive you,
047	2CO	006	018	And will be to you a Father, And ye shall be to me sons and daughters, saith the Lord Almighty.
047	2CO	007	001	Having therefore these promises, beloved, let us cleanse ourselves from all defilement of flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God.
047	2CO	007	002	Open your hearts to us: we wronged no man, we corrupted no man, we took advantage of no man.
047	2CO	007	003	I say it not to condemn [you]: for I have said before, that ye are in our hearts to die together and live together.
047	2CO	007	004	Great is my boldness of speech toward you, great is my glorying on your behalf: I am filled with comfort, I overflow with joy in all our affliction.
047	2CO	007	005	For even when we were come into Macedonia, our flesh had no relief, but [we were] afflicted on every side; without [were] fightings, within [were] fears.
047	2CO	007	006	Nevertheless he that comforteth the lowly, [even] God, comforted us by the coming of Titus;
047	2CO	007	007	and not by his coming only, but also by the comfort wherewith he was comforted in you, while he told us your longing, your mourning, your zeal for me; so that I rejoiced yet more.
047	2CO	007	008	For though I made you sorry with my epistle, I do not regret it, though I did regret; for I see that that epistle made you sorry, though but for a season.
047	2CO	007	009	Now I rejoice, not that ye were made sorry, but that ye were made sorry unto repentance: for ye were made sorry after a godly sort, that ye might suffer loss by us in nothing.
047	2CO	007	010	For godly sorrow worketh repentance unto salvation, [a repentance] which bringeth no regret: but the sorrow of the world worketh death.
047	2CO	007	011	For behold, this selfsame thing, that ye were made sorry after a godly sort, what earnest care it wrought in you, yea, what clearing of yourselves, yea, what indignation, yea, what fear, yea, what longing, yea, what zeal, yea, what avenging! In everything ye approved yourselves to be pure in the matter.
047	2CO	007	012	So although I wrote unto you, [I wrote] not for his cause that did the wrong, nor for his cause that suffered the wrong, but that your earnest care for us might be made manifest unto you in the sight of God.
047	2CO	007	013	Therefore we have been comforted: and in our comfort we joyed the more exceedingly for the joy of Titus, because his spirit hath been refreshed by you all.
047	2CO	007	014	For if in anything I have gloried to him on your behalf, I was not put to shame; but as we spake all things to you in truth, so our glorying also, which I made before Titus, was found to be truth.
047	2CO	007	015	And his inward affection is more abundantly toward you, whilst he remembereth the obedience of you all, how with fear and trembling ye received him.
047	2CO	007	016	I rejoice that in everything I am of good courage concerning you.
047	2CO	008	001	Moreover, brethren, we make known to you the grace of God which hath been given in the churches of Macedonia;
047	2CO	008	002	how that in much proof of affliction the abundance of their joy and their deep poverty abounded unto the riches of their liberality.
047	2CO	008	003	For according to their power, I bear witness, yea and beyond their power, [they gave] of their own accord,
047	2CO	008	004	beseeching us with much entreaty in regard of this grace and the fellowship in the ministering to the saints:
047	2CO	008	005	and [this], not as we had hoped, but first they gave their own selves to the Lord, and to us by the will of God.
047	2CO	008	006	Insomuch that we exhorted Titus, that as he had made a beginning before, so he would also complete in you this grace also.
047	2CO	008	007	But as ye abound in everything, [in] faith, and utterance, and knowledge, and [in] all earnestness, and [in] your love to us, [see] that ye abound in this grace also.
047	2CO	008	008	I speak not by way of commandment, but as proving through the earnestness of others the sincerity also of your love.
047	2CO	008	009	For ye know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that, though he was rich, yet for your sakes he became poor, that ye through his poverty might become rich.
047	2CO	008	010	And herein I give [my] judgment: for this is expedient for you, who were the first to make a beginning a year ago, not only to do, but also to will.
047	2CO	008	011	But now complete the doing also; that as [there was] the readiness to will, so [there may be] the completion also out of your ability.
047	2CO	008	012	For if the readiness is there, [it is] acceptable according as [a man] hath, not according as [he] hath not.
047	2CO	008	013	For [I say] not [this], that others may be eased, [and] ye distressed:
047	2CO	008	014	but by equality; your abundance [being a supply] at this present time for their want, that their abundance also may become [a supply] for your want; that there may be equality:
047	2CO	008	015	as it is written, He that [gathered] much had nothing over; and he that [gathered] little had no lack.
047	2CO	008	016	But thanks be to God, which putteth the same earnest care for you into the heart of Titus.
047	2CO	008	017	For indeed he accepted our exhortation; but being himself very earnest, he went forth unto you of his own accord.
047	2CO	008	018	And we have sent together with him the brother whose praise in the gospel [is spread] through all the churches;
047	2CO	008	019	and not only so, but who was also appointed by the churches to travel with us in [the matter of] this grace, which is ministered by us to the glory of the Lord, and [to shew] our readiness:
047	2CO	008	020	Avoiding this, that any man should blame us in [the matter of] this bounty which is ministered by us:
047	2CO	008	021	for we take thought for things honourable, not only in the sight of the Lord, but also in the sight of men.
047	2CO	008	022	And we have sent with them our brother, whom we have many times proved earnest in many things, but now much more earnest, by reason of the great confidence which [he hath] in you.
047	2CO	008	023	Whether [any inquire] about Titus, [he is] my partner and [my] fellow-worker to you-ward; or our brethren, [they are] the messengers of the churches, [they are] the glory of Christ.
047	2CO	008	024	Shew ye therefore unto them in the face of the churches the proof of your love, and of our glorying on your behalf.
047	2CO	009	001	For as touching the ministering to the saints, it is superfluous for me to write to you:
047	2CO	009	002	for I know your readiness, of which I glory on your behalf to them of Macedonia, that Achaia hath been prepared for a year past; and your zeal hath stirred up very many of them.
047	2CO	009	003	But I have sent the brethren, that our glorying on your behalf may not be made void in this respect; that, even as I said, ye may be prepared:
047	2CO	009	004	lest by any means, if there come with me any of Macedonia, and find you unprepared, we (that we say not, ye) should be put to shame in this confidence.
047	2CO	009	005	I thought it necessary therefore to entreat the brethren, that they would go before unto you, and make up beforehand your aforepromised bounty, that the same might be ready, as a matter of bounty, and not of extortion.
047	2CO	009	006	But this [I say], He that soweth sparingly shall reap also sparingly; and he that soweth bountifully shall reap also bountifully.
047	2CO	009	007	[Let] each man [do] according as he hath purposed in his heart; not grudgingly, or of necessity: for God loveth a cheerful giver.
047	2CO	009	008	And God is able to make all grace abound unto you; that ye, having always all sufficiency in everything, may abound unto every good work:
047	2CO	009	009	as it is written, He hath scattered abroad, he hath given to the poor; His righteousness abideth for ever.
047	2CO	009	010	And he that supplieth seed to the sower and bread for food, shall supply and multiply your seed for sowing, and increase the fruits of your righteousness:
047	2CO	009	011	ye being enriched in everything unto all liberality, which worketh through us thanksgiving to God.
047	2CO	009	012	For the ministration of this service not only filleth up the measure of the wants of the saints, but aboundeth also through many thanksgivings unto God;
047	2CO	009	013	seeing that through the proving [of you] by this ministration they glorify God for the obedience of your confession unto the gospel of Christ, and for the liberality of [your] contribution unto them and unto all;
047	2CO	009	014	while they themselves also, with supplication on your behalf, long after you by reason of the exceeding grace of God in you.
047	2CO	009	015	Thanks be to God for his unspeakable gift.
047	2CO	010	001	Now I Paul myself entreat you by the meekness and gentleness of Christ, I who in your presence am lowly among you, but being absent am of good courage toward you:
047	2CO	010	002	yea, I beseech you, that I may not when present shew courage with the confidence wherewith I count to be bold against some, which count of us as if we walked according to the flesh.
047	2CO	010	003	For though we walk in the flesh, we do not war according to the flesh
047	2CO	010	004	(for the weapons of our warfare are not of the flesh, but mighty before God to the casting down of strong holds);
047	2CO	010	005	casting down imaginations, and every high thing that is exalted against the knowledge of God, and bringing every thought into captivity to the obedience of Christ;
047	2CO	010	006	and being in readiness to avenge all disobedience, when your obedience shall be fulfilled.
047	2CO	010	007	Ye look at the things that are before your face. If any man trusteth in himself that he is Christ’s, let him consider this again with himself, that, even as he is Christ’s, so also are we.
047	2CO	010	008	For though I should glory somewhat abundantly concerning our authority (which the Lord gave for building you up, and not for casting you down), I shall not be put to shame:
047	2CO	010	009	that I may not seem as if I would terrify you by my letters.
047	2CO	010	010	For, His letters, they say, are weighty and strong; but his bodily presence is weak, and his speech of no account.
047	2CO	010	011	Let such a one reckon this, that, what we are in word by letters when we are absent, such [are we] also in deed when we are present.
047	2CO	010	012	For we are not bold to number or compare ourselves with certain of them that commend themselves: but they themselves, measuring themselves by themselves, and comparing themselves with themselves, are without understanding.
047	2CO	010	013	But we will not glory beyond [our] measure, but according to the measure of the province which God apportioned to us as a measure, to reach even unto you.
047	2CO	010	014	For we stretch not ourselves overmuch, as though we reached not unto you: for we came even as far as unto you in the gospel of Christ:
047	2CO	010	015	not glorying beyond [our] measure, [that is], in other men’s labours; but having hope that, as your faith groweth, we shall be magnified in you according to our province unto [further] abundance,
047	2CO	010	016	so as to preach the gospel even unto the parts beyond you, [and] not to glory in another’s province in regard of things ready to our hand.
047	2CO	010	017	But he that glorieth, let him glory in the Lord.
047	2CO	010	018	For not he that commendeth himself is approved, but whom the Lord commendeth.
047	2CO	011	001	Would that ye could bear with me in a little foolishness: nay indeed bear with me.
047	2CO	011	002	For I am jealous over you with a godly jealousy: for I espoused you to one husband, that I might present you [as] a pure virgin to Christ.
047	2CO	011	003	But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve in his craftiness, your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity and the purity that is toward Christ.
047	2CO	011	004	For if he that cometh preacheth another Jesus, whom we did not preach, or [if] ye receive a different spirit, which ye did not receive, or a different gospel, which ye did not accept, ye do well to bear with [him].
047	2CO	011	005	For I reckon that I am not a whit behind the very chiefest apostles.
047	2CO	011	006	But though [I be] rude in speech, yet [am I] not in knowledge; nay, in everything we have made [it] manifest among all men to you-ward.
047	2CO	011	007	Or did I commit a sin in abasing myself that ye might be exalted, because I preached to you the gospel of God for nought?
047	2CO	011	008	I robbed other churches, taking wages [of them] that I might minister unto you;
047	2CO	011	009	and when I was present with you and was in want, I was not a burden on any man; for the brethren, when they came from Macedonia, supplied the measure of my want; and in everything I kept myself from being burdensome unto you, and [so] will I keep [myself].
047	2CO	011	010	As the truth of Christ is in me, no man shall stop me of this glorying in the regions of Achaia.
047	2CO	011	011	Wherefore? because I love you not? God knoweth.
047	2CO	011	012	But what I do, that I will do, that I may cut off occasion from them which desire an occasion; that wherein they glory, they may be found even as we.
047	2CO	011	013	For such men are false apostles, deceitful workers, fashioning themselves into apostles of Christ.
047	2CO	011	014	And no marvel; for even Satan fashioneth himself into an angel of light.
047	2CO	011	015	It is no great thing therefore if his ministers also fashion themselves as ministers of righteousness; whose end shall be according to their works.
047	2CO	011	016	I say again, Let no man think me foolish; but if [ye do], yet as foolish receive me, that I also may glory a little.
047	2CO	011	017	That which I speak, I speak not after the Lord, but as in foolishness, in this confidence of glorying.
047	2CO	011	018	Seeing that many glory after the flesh, I will glory also.
047	2CO	011	019	For ye bear with the foolish gladly, being wise [yourselves].
047	2CO	011	020	For ye bear with a man, if he bringeth you into bondage, if he devoureth you, if he taketh you [captive], if he exalteth himself, if he smiteth you on the face.
047	2CO	011	021	I speak by way of disparagement, as though we had been weak. Yet whereinsoever any is bold (I speak in foolishness), I am bold also.
047	2CO	011	022	Are they Hebrews? so am I. Are they Israelites? so am I. Are they the seed of Abraham? so am I.
047	2CO	011	023	Are they ministers of Christ? (I speak as one beside himself) I more; in labours more abundantly, in prisons more abundantly, in stripes above measure, in deaths oft.
047	2CO	011	024	Of the Jews five times received I forty [stripes] save one.
047	2CO	011	025	Thrice was I beaten with rods, once was I stoned, thrice I suffered shipwreck, a night and a day have I been in the deep;
047	2CO	011	026	[in] journeyings often, [in] perils of rivers, [in] perils of robbers, [in] perils from [my] countrymen, [in] perils from the Gentiles, [in] perils in the city, [in] perils in the wilderness, [in] perils in the sea, [in] perils among false brethren;
047	2CO	011	027	[in] labour and travail, in watchings often, in hunger and thirst, in fastings often, in cold and nakedness.
047	2CO	011	028	Beside those things that are without, there is that which presseth upon me daily, anxiety for all the churches.
047	2CO	011	029	Who is weak, and I am not weak? who is made to stumble, and I burn not?
047	2CO	011	030	If I must needs glory, I will glory of the things that concern my weakness.
047	2CO	011	031	The God and Father of the Lord Jesus, he who is blessed for evermore, knoweth that I lie not.
047	2CO	011	032	In Damascus the governor under Aretas the king guarded the city of the Damascenes, in order to take me:
047	2CO	011	033	and through a window was I let down in a basket by the wall, and escaped his hands.
047	2CO	012	001	I must needs glory, though it is not expedient; but I will come to visions and revelations of the Lord.
047	2CO	012	002	I know a man in Christ, fourteen years ago (whether in the body, I know not; or whether out of the body, I know not; God knoweth), such a one caught up even to the third heaven.
047	2CO	012	003	And I know such a man (whether in the body, or apart from the body, I know not; God knoweth),
047	2CO	012	004	how that he was caught up into Paradise, and heard unspeakable words, which it is not lawful for a man to utter.
047	2CO	012	005	On behalf of such a one will I glory: but on mine own behalf I will not glory, save in [my] weaknesses.
047	2CO	012	006	For if I should desire to glory, I shall not be foolish; for I shall speak the truth: but I forbear, lest any man should account of me above that which he seeth me [to be], or heareth from me.
047	2CO	012	007	And by reason of the exceeding greatness of the revelations—wherefore, that I should not be exalted overmuch, there was given to me a thorn in the flesh, a messenger of Satan to buffet me, that I should not be exalted overmuch.
047	2CO	012	008	Concerning this thing I besought the Lord thrice, that it might depart from me.
047	2CO	012	009	And he hath said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for [my] power is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my weaknesses, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.
047	2CO	012	010	Wherefore I take pleasure in weaknesses, in injuries, in necessities, in persecutions, in distresses, for Christ’s sake: for when I am weak, then am I strong.
047	2CO	012	011	I am become foolish: ye compelled me; for I ought to have been commended of you: for in nothing was I behind the very chiefest apostles, though I am nothing.
047	2CO	012	012	Truly the signs of an apostle were wrought among you in all patience, by signs and wonders and mighty works.
047	2CO	012	013	For what is there wherein ye were made inferior to the rest of the churches, except [it be] that I myself was not a burden to you? forgive me this wrong.
047	2CO	012	014	Behold, this is the third time I am ready to come to you; and I will not be a burden to you: for I seek not yours, but you: for the children ought not to lay up for the parents, but the parents for the children.
047	2CO	012	015	And I will most gladly spend and be spent for your souls. If I love you more abundantly, am I loved the less?
047	2CO	012	016	But be it so, I did not myself burden you; but, being crafty, I caught you with guile.
047	2CO	012	017	Did I take advantage of you by any one of them whom I have sent unto you?
047	2CO	012	018	I exhorted Titus, and I sent the brother with him. Did Titus take any advantage of you? walked we not by the same Spirit? [walked we] not in the same steps?
047	2CO	012	019	Ye think all this time that we are excusing ourselves unto you. In the sight of God speak we in Christ. But all things, beloved, [are] for your edifying.
047	2CO	012	020	For I fear, lest by any means, when I come, I should find you not such as I would, and should myself be found of you such as ye would not; lest by any means [there should be] strife, jealousy, wraths, factions, backbitings, whisperings, swellings, tumults;
047	2CO	012	021	lest, when I come again, my God should humble me before you, and I should mourn for many of them that have sinned heretofore, and repented not of the uncleanness and fornication and lasciviousness which they committed.
047	2CO	013	001	This is the third time I am coming to you. At the mouth of two witnesses or three shall every word be established.
047	2CO	013	002	I have said beforehand, and I do say beforehand, as when I was present the second time, so now, being absent, to them that have sinned heretofore, and to all the rest, that, if I come again, I will not spare;
047	2CO	013	003	seeing that ye seek a proof of Christ that speaketh in me; who to you-ward is not weak, but is powerful in you:
047	2CO	013	004	for he was crucified through weakness, yet he liveth through the power of God. For we also are weak in him, but we shall live with him through the power of God toward you.
047	2CO	013	005	Try your own selves, whether ye be in the faith; prove your own selves. Or know ye not as to your own selves, that Jesus Christ is in you? unless indeed ye be reprobate.
047	2CO	013	006	But I hope that ye shall know that we are not reprobate.
047	2CO	013	007	Now we pray to God that ye do no evil; not that we may appear approved, but that ye may do that which is honourable, though we be as reprobate.
047	2CO	013	008	For we can do nothing against the truth, but for the truth.
047	2CO	013	009	For we rejoice, when we are weak, and ye are strong: this we also pray for, even your perfecting.
047	2CO	013	010	For this cause I write these things while absent, that I may not when present deal sharply, according to the authority which the Lord gave me for building up, and not for casting down.
047	2CO	013	011	Finally, brethren, farewell. Be perfected; be comforted; be of the same mind; live in peace: and the God of love and peace shall be with you.
047	2CO	013	012	Salute one another with a holy kiss.
047	2CO	013	013	All the saints salute you.
047	2CO	013	014	The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the communion of the Holy Ghost, be with you all.
#
# BOOK	048	GAL	Galatians	Galatians
048	GAL	001	001	Paul, an apostle (not from men, neither through man, but through Jesus Christ, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead),
048	GAL	001	002	and all the brethren which are with me, unto the churches of Galatia:
048	GAL	001	003	Grace to you and peace from God the Father, and our Lord Jesus Christ,
048	GAL	001	004	who gave himself for our sins, that he might deliver us out of this present evil world, according to the will of our God and Father:
048	GAL	001	005	to whom [be] the glory for ever and ever. Amen.
048	GAL	001	006	I marvel that ye are so quickly removing from him that called you in the grace of Christ unto a different gospel;
048	GAL	001	007	which is not another [gospel]: only there are some that trouble you, and would pervert the gospel of Christ.
048	GAL	001	008	But though we, or an angel from heaven, should preach unto you any gospel other than that which we preached unto you, let him be anathema.
048	GAL	001	009	As we have said before, so say I now again, If any man preacheth unto you any gospel other than that which ye received, let him be anathema.
048	GAL	001	010	For am I now persuading men, or God? or am I seeking to please men? if I were still pleasing men, I should not be a servant of Christ.
048	GAL	001	011	For I make known to you, brethren, as touching the gospel which was preached by me, that it is not after man.
048	GAL	001	012	For neither did I receive it from man, nor was I taught it, but [it came to me] through revelation of Jesus Christ.
048	GAL	001	013	For ye have heard of my manner of life in time past in the Jews’ religion, how that beyond measure I persecuted the church of God, and made havock of it:
048	GAL	001	014	and I advanced in the Jews’ religion beyond many of mine own age among my countrymen, being more exceedingly zealous for the traditions of my fathers.
048	GAL	001	015	But when it was the good pleasure of God, who separated me, [even] from my mother’s womb, and called me through his grace,
048	GAL	001	016	to reveal his Son in me, that I might preach him among the Gentiles; immediately I conferred not with flesh and blood:
048	GAL	001	017	neither went I up to Jerusalem to them which were apostles before me: but I went away into Arabia; and again I returned unto Damascus.
048	GAL	001	018	Then after three years I went up to Jerusalem to visit Cephas, and tarried with him fifteen days.
048	GAL	001	019	But other of the apostles saw I none, save James the Lord’s brother.
048	GAL	001	020	Now touching the things which I write unto you, behold, before God, I lie not.
048	GAL	001	021	Then I came into the regions of Syria and Cilicia.
048	GAL	001	022	And I was still unknown by face unto the churches of Judaea which were in Christ:
048	GAL	001	023	but they only heard say, He that once persecuted us now preacheth the faith of which he once made havock;
048	GAL	001	024	and they glorified God in me.
048	GAL	002	001	Then after the space of fourteen years I went up again to Jerusalem with Barnabas, taking Titus also with me.
048	GAL	002	002	And I went up by revelation; and I laid before them the gospel which I preach among the Gentiles, but privately before them who were of repute, lest by any means I should be running, or had run, in vain.
048	GAL	002	003	But not even Titus who was with me, being a Greek, was compelled to be circumcised:
048	GAL	002	004	and that because of the false brethren privily brought in, who came in privily to spy out our liberty which we have in Christ Jesus, that they might bring us into bondage:
048	GAL	002	005	to whom we gave place in the way of subjection, no, not for an hour; that the truth of the gospel might continue with you.
048	GAL	002	006	But from those who were reputed to be somewhat (whatsoever they were, it maketh no matter to me: God accepteth not man’s person)—they, I say, who were of repute imparted nothing to me:
048	GAL	002	007	but contrariwise, when they saw that I had been intrusted with the gospel of the uncircumcision, even as Peter with [the gospel] of the circumcision
048	GAL	002	008	(for he that wrought for Peter unto the apostleship of the circumcision wrought for me also unto the Gentiles);
048	GAL	002	009	and when they perceived the grace that was given unto me, James and Cephas and John, they who were reputed to be pillars, gave to me and Barnabas the right hands of fellowship, that we should go unto the Gentiles, and they unto the circumcision;
048	GAL	002	010	only [they would] that we should remember the poor; which very thing I was also zealous to do.
048	GAL	002	011	But when Cephas came to Antioch, I resisted him to the face, because he stood condemned.
048	GAL	002	012	For before that certain came from James, he did eat with the Gentiles: but when they came, he drew back and separated himself, fearing them that were of the circumcision.
048	GAL	002	013	And the rest of the Jews dissembled likewise with him; insomuch that even Barnabas was carried away with their dissimulation.
048	GAL	002	014	But when I saw that they walked not uprightly according to the truth of the gospel, I said unto Cephas before [them] all, If thou, being a Jew, livest as do the Gentiles, and not as do the Jews, how compellest thou the Gentiles to live as do the Jews?
048	GAL	002	015	We being Jews by nature, and not sinners of the Gentiles,
048	GAL	002	016	yet knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law, save through faith in Jesus Christ, even we believed on Christ Jesus, that we might be justified by faith in Christ, and not by the works of the law: because by the works of the law shall no flesh be justified.
048	GAL	002	017	But if, while we sought to be justified in Christ, we ourselves also were found sinners, is Christ a minister of sin? God forbid.
048	GAL	002	018	For if I build up again those things which I destroyed, I prove myself a transgressor.
048	GAL	002	019	For I through the law died unto the law, that I might live unto God.
048	GAL	002	020	I have been crucified with Christ; yet I live; [and yet] no longer I, but Christ liveth in me: and that [life] which I now live in the flesh I live in faith, [the faith] which is in the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself up for me.
048	GAL	002	021	I do not make void the grace of God: for if righteousness is through the law, then Christ died for nought.
048	GAL	003	001	O foolish Galatians, who did bewitch you, before whose eyes Jesus Christ was openly set forth crucified?
048	GAL	003	002	This only would I learn from you, Received ye the Spirit by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?
048	GAL	003	003	Are ye so foolish? having begun in the Spirit, are ye now perfected in the flesh?
048	GAL	003	004	Did ye suffer so many things in vain? if it be indeed in vain.
048	GAL	003	005	He therefore that supplieth to you the Spirit, and worketh miracles among you, [doeth he it] by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?
048	GAL	003	006	Even as Abraham believed God, and it was reckoned unto him for righteousness.
048	GAL	003	007	Know therefore that they which be of faith, the same are sons of Abraham.
048	GAL	003	008	And the scripture, foreseeing that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, preached the gospel beforehand unto Abraham, [saying], In thee shall all the nations be blessed.
048	GAL	003	009	So then they which be of faith are blessed with the faithful Abraham.
048	GAL	003	010	For as many as are of the works of the law are under a curse: for it is written, Cursed is every one which continueth not in all things that are written in the book of the law, to do them.
048	GAL	003	011	Now that no man is justified by the law in the sight of God, is evident: for, The righteous shall live by faith;
048	GAL	003	012	and the law is not of faith; but, He that doeth them shall live in them.
048	GAL	003	013	Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law, having become a curse for us: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree:
048	GAL	003	014	that upon the Gentiles might come the blessing of Abraham in Christ Jesus; that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith.
048	GAL	003	015	Brethren, I speak after the manner of men: Though it be but a man’s covenant, yet when it hath been confirmed, no one maketh it void, or addeth thereto.
048	GAL	003	016	Now to Abraham were the promises spoken, and to his seed. He saith not, And to seeds, as of many; but as of one, And to thy seed, which is Christ.
048	GAL	003	017	Now this I say; A covenant confirmed beforehand by God, the law, which came four hundred and thirty years after, doth not disannul, so as to make the promise of none effect.
048	GAL	003	018	For if the inheritance is of the law, it is no more of promise: but God hath granted it to Abraham by promise.
048	GAL	003	019	What then is the law? It was added because of transgressions, till the seed should come to whom the promise hath been made; [and it was] ordained through angels by the hand of a mediator.
048	GAL	003	020	Now a mediator is not [a mediator] of one; but God is one.
048	GAL	003	021	Is the law then against the promises of God? God forbid: for if there had been a law given which could make alive, verily righteousness would have been of the law.
048	GAL	003	022	Howbeit the scripture hath shut up all things under sin, that the promise by faith in Jesus Christ might be given to them that believe.
048	GAL	003	023	But before faith came, we were kept in ward under the law, shut up unto the faith which should afterwards be revealed.
048	GAL	003	024	So that the law hath been our tutor [to bring us] unto Christ, that we might be justified by faith.
048	GAL	003	025	But now that faith is come, we are no longer under a tutor.
048	GAL	003	026	For ye are all sons of God, through faith, in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	027	For as many of you as were baptized into Christ did put on Christ.
048	GAL	003	028	There can be neither Jew nor Greek, there can be neither bond nor free, there can be no male and female: for ye all are one [man] in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	029	And if ye are Christ’s, then are ye Abraham’s seed, heirs according to promise.
048	GAL	004	001	But I say that so long as the heir is a child, he differeth nothing from a bondservant, though he is lord of all;
048	GAL	004	002	but is under guardians and stewards until the term appointed of the father.
048	GAL	004	003	So we also, when we were children, were held in bondage under the rudiments of the world:
048	GAL	004	004	but when the fulness of the time came, God sent forth his Son, born of a woman, born under the law,
048	GAL	004	005	that he might redeem them which were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.
048	GAL	004	006	And because ye are sons, God sent forth the Spirit of his Son into our hearts, crying, Abba, Father.
048	GAL	004	007	So that thou art no longer a bondservant, but a son; and if a son, then an heir through God.
048	GAL	004	008	Howbeit at that time, not knowing God, ye were in bondage to them which by nature are no gods:
048	GAL	004	009	but now that ye have come to know God, or rather to be known of God, how turn ye back again to the weak and beggarly rudiments, whereunto ye desire to be in bondage over again?
048	GAL	004	010	Ye observe days, and months, and seasons, and years.
048	GAL	004	011	I am afraid of you, lest by any means I have bestowed labour upon you in vain.
048	GAL	004	012	I beseech you, brethren, be as I [am], for I [am] as ye [are]. Ye did me no wrong:
048	GAL	004	013	but ye know that because of an infirmity of the flesh I preached the gospel unto you the first time:
048	GAL	004	014	and that which was a temptation to you in my flesh ye despised not, nor rejected; but ye received me as an angel of God, [even] as Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	004	015	Where then is that gratulation of yourselves? for I bear you witness, that, if possible, ye would have plucked out your eyes and given them to me.
048	GAL	004	016	So then am I become your enemy, because I tell you the truth?
048	GAL	004	017	They zealously seek you in no good way; nay, they desire to shut you out, that ye may seek them.
048	GAL	004	018	But it is good to be zealously sought in a good matter at all times, and not only when I am present with you.
048	GAL	004	019	My little children, of whom I am again in travail until Christ be formed in you,
048	GAL	004	020	yea, I could wish to be present with you now, and to change my voice; for I am perplexed about you.
048	GAL	004	021	Tell me, ye that desire to be under the law, do ye not hear the law?
048	GAL	004	022	For it is written, that Abraham had two sons, one by the handmaid, and one by the freewoman.
048	GAL	004	023	Howbeit the [son] by the handmaid is born after the flesh; but the [son] by the freewoman [is born] through promise.
048	GAL	004	024	Which things contain an allegory: for these [women] are two covenants; one from mount Sinai, bearing children unto bondage, which is Hagar.
048	GAL	004	025	Now this Hagar is mount Sinai in Arabia, and answereth to the Jerusalem that now is: for she is in bondage with her children.
048	GAL	004	026	But the Jerusalem that is above is free, which is our mother.
048	GAL	004	027	For it is written, Rejoice, thou barren that bearest not; Break forth and cry, thou that travailest not: For more are the children of the desolate than of her which hath the husband.
048	GAL	004	028	Now we, brethren, as Isaac was, are children of promise.
048	GAL	004	029	But as then he that was born after the flesh persecuted him [that was born] after the Spirit, even so it is now.
048	GAL	004	030	Howbeit what saith the scripture? Cast out the handmaid and her son: for the son of the handmaid shall not inherit with the son of the freewoman.
048	GAL	004	031	Wherefore, brethren, we are not children of a handmaid, but of the freewoman.
048	GAL	005	001	With freedom did Christ set us free: stand fast therefore, and be not entangled again in a yoke of bondage.
048	GAL	005	002	Behold, I Paul say unto you, that, if ye receive circumcision, Christ will profit you nothing.
048	GAL	005	003	Yea, I testify again to every man that receiveth circumcision, that he is a debtor to do the whole law.
048	GAL	005	004	Ye are severed from Christ, ye who would be justified by the law; ye are fallen away from grace.
048	GAL	005	005	For we through the Spirit by faith wait for the hope of righteousness.
048	GAL	005	006	For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision availeth anything, nor uncircumcision; but faith working through love.
048	GAL	005	007	Ye were running well; who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth?
048	GAL	005	008	This persuasion [came] not of him that calleth you.
048	GAL	005	009	A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump.
048	GAL	005	010	I have confidence to you-ward in the Lord, that ye will be none otherwise minded: but he that troubleth you shall bear his judgment, whosoever he be.
048	GAL	005	011	But I, brethren, if I still preach circumcision, why am I still persecuted? then hath the stumblingblock of the cross been done away.
048	GAL	005	012	I would that they which unsettle you would even cut themselves off.
048	GAL	005	013	For ye, brethren, were called for freedom; only [use] not your freedom for an occasion to the flesh, but through love be servants one to another.
048	GAL	005	014	For the whole law is fulfilled in one word, [even] in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.
048	GAL	005	015	But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one of another.
048	GAL	005	016	But I say, Walk by the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfill the lust of the flesh.
048	GAL	005	017	For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh; for these are contrary the one to the other; that ye may not do the things that ye would.
048	GAL	005	018	But if ye are led by the Spirit, ye are not under the law.
048	GAL	005	019	Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are [these], fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness,
048	GAL	005	020	idolatry, sorcery, enmities, strife, jealousies, wraths, factions, divisions, heresies,
048	GAL	005	021	envyings, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which I forewarn you, even as I did forewarn you, that they which practise such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God.
048	GAL	005	022	But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,
048	GAL	005	023	meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.
048	GAL	005	024	And they that are of Christ Jesus have crucified the flesh with the passions and the lusts thereof.
048	GAL	005	025	If we live by the Spirit, by the Spirit let us also walk.
048	GAL	005	026	Let us not be vainglorious, provoking one another, envying one another.
048	GAL	006	001	Brethren, even if a man be overtaken in any trespass, ye which are spiritual, restore such a one in a spirit of meekness; looking to thyself, lest thou also be tempted.
048	GAL	006	002	Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfill the law of Christ.
048	GAL	006	003	For if a man thinketh himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.
048	GAL	006	004	But let each man prove his own work, and then shall he have his glorying in regard of himself alone, and not of his neighbour.
048	GAL	006	005	For each man shall bear his own burden.
048	GAL	006	006	But let him that is taught in the word communicate unto him that teacheth in all good things.
048	GAL	006	007	Be not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap.
048	GAL	006	008	For he that soweth unto his own flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption; but he that soweth unto the Spirit shall of the Spirit reap eternal life.
048	GAL	006	009	And let us not be weary in well-doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.
048	GAL	006	010	So then, as we have opportunity, let us work that which is good toward all men, and especially toward them that are of the household of the faith.
048	GAL	006	011	See with how large letters I have written unto you with mine own hand.
048	GAL	006	012	As many as desire to make a fair show in the flesh, they compel you to be circumcised; only that they may not be persecuted for the cross of Christ.
048	GAL	006	013	For not even they who receive circumcision do themselves keep the law; but they desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh.
048	GAL	006	014	But far be it from me to glory, save in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world hath been crucified unto me, and I unto the world.
048	GAL	006	015	For neither is circumcision anything, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature.
048	GAL	006	016	And as many as shall walk by this rule, peace [be] upon them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God.
048	GAL	006	017	From henceforth let no man trouble me: for I bear branded on my body the marks of Jesus.
048	GAL	006	018	The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brethren. Amen.
#
# BOOK	049	EPH	Ephesians	Ephesians
049	EPH	001	001	Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, to the saints which are at Ephesus, and the faithful in Christ Jesus:
049	EPH	001	002	Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	001	003	Blessed [be] the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who hath blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly [places] in Christ:
049	EPH	001	004	even as he chose us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blemish before him in love:
049	EPH	001	005	having foreordained us unto adoption as sons through Jesus Christ unto himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,
049	EPH	001	006	to the praise of the glory of his grace, which he freely bestowed on us in the Beloved:
049	EPH	001	007	in whom we have our redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of his grace,
049	EPH	001	008	which he made to abound toward us in all wisdom and prudence,
049	EPH	001	009	having made known unto us the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure which he purposed in him
049	EPH	001	010	unto a dispensation of the fulness of the times, to sum up all things in Christ, the things in the heavens, and the things upon the earth; in him, [I say],
049	EPH	001	011	in whom also we were made a heritage, having been foreordained according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his will;
049	EPH	001	012	to the end that we should be unto the praise of his glory, we who had before hoped in Christ:
049	EPH	001	013	in whom ye also, having heard the word of the truth, the gospel of your salvation, —in whom, having also believed, ye were sealed with the Holy Spirit of promise,
049	EPH	001	014	which is an earnest of our inheritance, unto the redemption of [God’s] own possession, unto the praise of his glory.
049	EPH	001	015	For this cause I also, having heard of the faith in the Lord Jesus which is among you, and which [ye shew] toward all the saints,
049	EPH	001	016	cease not to give thanks for you, making mention [of you] in my prayers;
049	EPH	001	017	that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give unto you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him;
049	EPH	001	018	having the eyes of your heart enlightened, that ye may know what is the hope of his calling, what the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints,
049	EPH	001	019	and what the exceeding greatness of his power to us-ward who believe, according to that working of the strength of his might
049	EPH	001	020	which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and made him to sit at his right hand in the heavenly [places],
049	EPH	001	021	far above all rule, and authority, and power, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come:
049	EPH	001	022	and he put all things in subjection under his feet, and gave him to be head over all things to the church,
049	EPH	001	023	which is his body, the fulness of him that filleth all in all.
049	EPH	002	001	And you [did he quicken], when ye were dead through your trespasses and sins,
049	EPH	002	002	wherein aforetime ye walked according to the course of this world, according to the prince of the power of the air, of the spirit that now worketh in the sons of disobedience;
049	EPH	002	003	among whom we also all once lived in the lusts of our flesh, doing the desires of the flesh and of the mind, and were by nature children of wrath, even as the rest: —
049	EPH	002	004	but God, being rich in mercy, for his great love wherewith he loved us,
049	EPH	002	005	even when we were dead through our trespasses, quickened us together with Christ (by grace have ye been saved),
049	EPH	002	006	and raised us up with him, and made us to sit with him in the heavenly [places], in Christ Jesus:
049	EPH	002	007	that in the ages to come he might shew the exceeding riches of his grace in kindness toward us in Christ Jesus:
049	EPH	002	008	for by grace have ye been saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: [it is] the gift of God:
049	EPH	002	009	not of works, that no man should glory.
049	EPH	002	010	For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God afore prepared that we should walk in them.
049	EPH	002	011	Wherefore remember, that aforetime ye, the Gentiles in the flesh, who are called Uncircumcision by that which is called Circumcision, in the flesh, made by hands;
049	EPH	002	012	that ye were at that time separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers from the covenants of the promise, having no hope and without God in the world.
049	EPH	002	013	But now in Christ Jesus ye that once were far off are made nigh in the blood of Christ.
049	EPH	002	014	For he is our peace, who made both one, and brake down the middle wall of partition,
049	EPH	002	015	having abolished in his flesh the enmity, [even] the law of commandments [contained] in ordinances; that he might create in himself of the twain one new man, [so] making peace;
049	EPH	002	016	and might reconcile them both in one body unto God through the cross, having slain the enmity thereby:
049	EPH	002	017	and he came and preached peace to you that were far off, and peace to them that were nigh:
049	EPH	002	018	for through him we both have our access in one Spirit unto the Father.
049	EPH	002	019	So then ye are no more strangers and sojourners, but ye are fellow-citizens with the saints, and of the household of God,
049	EPH	002	020	being built upon the foundation of the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus himself being the chief corner stone;
049	EPH	002	021	in whom each several building, fitly framed together, groweth into a holy temple in the Lord;
049	EPH	002	022	in whom ye also are builded together for a habitation of God in the Spirit.
049	EPH	003	001	For this cause I Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus in behalf of you Gentiles, —
049	EPH	003	002	if so be that ye have heard of the dispensation of that grace of God which was given me to you-ward;
049	EPH	003	003	how that by revelation was made known unto me the mystery, as I wrote afore in few words,
049	EPH	003	004	whereby, when ye read, ye can perceive my understanding in the mystery of Christ;
049	EPH	003	005	which in other generations was not made known unto the sons of men, as it hath now been revealed unto his holy apostles and prophets in the Spirit;
049	EPH	003	006	[to wit], that the Gentiles are fellow-heirs, and fellow-members of the body, and fellow-partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus through the gospel,
049	EPH	003	007	whereof I was made a minister, according to the gift of that grace of God which was given me according to the working of his power.
049	EPH	003	008	Unto me, who am less than the least of all saints, was this grace given, to preach unto the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ;
049	EPH	003	009	and to make all men see what is the dispensation of the mystery which from all ages hath been hid in God who created all things;
049	EPH	003	010	to the intent that now unto the principalities and the powers in the heavenly [places] might be made known through the church the manifold wisdom of God,
049	EPH	003	011	according to the eternal purpose which he purposed in Christ Jesus our Lord:
049	EPH	003	012	in whom we have boldness and access in confidence through our faith in him.
049	EPH	003	013	Wherefore I ask that ye faint not at my tribulations for you, which are your glory.
049	EPH	003	014	For this cause I bow my knees unto the Father,
049	EPH	003	015	from whom every family in heaven and on earth is named,
049	EPH	003	016	that he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, that ye may be strengthened with power through his Spirit in the inward man;
049	EPH	003	017	that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith; to the end that ye, being rooted and grounded in love,
049	EPH	003	018	may be strong to apprehend with all the saints what is the breadth and length and height and depth,
049	EPH	003	019	and to know the love of Christ which passeth knowledge, that ye may be filled unto all the fulness of God.
049	EPH	003	020	Now unto him that is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think, according to the power that worketh in us,
049	EPH	003	021	unto him [be] the glory in the church and in Christ Jesus unto all generations for ever and ever. Amen.
049	EPH	004	001	I therefore, the prisoner in the Lord, beseech you to walk worthily of the calling wherewith ye were called,
049	EPH	004	002	with all lowliness and meekness, with longsuffering, forbearing one another in love;
049	EPH	004	003	giving diligence to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace.
049	EPH	004	004	[There is] one body, and one Spirit, even as also ye were called in one hope of your calling;
049	EPH	004	005	one Lord, one faith, one baptism,
049	EPH	004	006	one God and Father of all, who is over all, and through all, and in all.
049	EPH	004	007	But unto each one of us was the grace given according to the measure of the gift of Christ.
049	EPH	004	008	Wherefore he saith, When he ascended on high, he led captivity captive, And gave gifts unto men.
049	EPH	004	009	(Now this, He ascended, what is it but that he also descended into the lower parts of the earth?
049	EPH	004	010	He that descended is the same also that ascended far above all the heavens, that he might fill all things.)
049	EPH	004	011	And he gave some [to be] apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, pastors and teachers;
049	EPH	004	012	for the perfecting of the saints, unto the work of ministering, unto the building up of the body of Christ:
049	EPH	004	013	till we all attain unto the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of the Son of God, unto a fullgrown man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of Christ:
049	EPH	004	014	that we may be no longer children, tossed to and fro and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the sleight of men, in craftiness, after the wiles of error;
049	EPH	004	015	but speaking truth in love, may grow up in all things into him, which is the head, [even] Christ;
049	EPH	004	016	from whom all the body fitly framed and knit together through that which every joint supplieth, according to the working in [due] measure of each several part, maketh the increase of the body unto the building up of itself in love.
049	EPH	004	017	This I say therefore, and testify in the Lord, that ye no longer walk as the Gentiles also walk, in the vanity of their mind,
049	EPH	004	018	being darkened in their understanding, alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them, because of the hardening of their heart;
049	EPH	004	019	who being past feeling gave themselves up to lasciviousness, to work all uncleanness with greediness.
049	EPH	004	020	But ye did not so learn Christ;
049	EPH	004	021	if so be that ye heard him, and were taught in him, even as truth is in Jesus:
049	EPH	004	022	that ye put away, as concerning your former manner of life, the old man, which waxeth corrupt after the lusts of deceit;
049	EPH	004	023	and that ye be renewed in the spirit of your mind,
049	EPH	004	024	and put on the new man, which after God hath been created in righteousness and holiness of truth.
049	EPH	004	025	Wherefore, putting away falsehood, speak ye truth each one with his neighbour: for we are members one of another.
049	EPH	004	026	Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:
049	EPH	004	027	neither give place to the devil.
049	EPH	004	028	Let him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his hands the thing that is good, that he may have whereof to give to him that hath need.
049	EPH	004	029	Let no corrupt speech proceed out of your mouth, but such as is good for edifying as the need may be, that it may give grace to them that hear.
049	EPH	004	030	And grieve not the Holy Spirit of God, in whom ye were sealed unto the day of redemption.
049	EPH	004	031	Let all bitterness, and wrath, and anger, and clamour, and railing, be put away from you, with all malice:
049	EPH	004	032	and be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving each other, even as God also in Christ forgave you.
049	EPH	005	001	Be ye therefore imitators of God, as beloved children;
049	EPH	005	002	and walk in love, even as Christ also loved you, and gave himself up for us, an offering and a sacrifice to God for an odour of a sweet smell.
049	EPH	005	003	But fornication, and all uncleanness, or covetousness, let it not even be named among you, as becometh saints;
049	EPH	005	004	nor filthiness, nor foolish talking, or jesting, which are not befitting: but rather giving of thanks.
049	EPH	005	005	For this ye know of a surety, that no fornicator, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, which is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and God.
049	EPH	005	006	Let no man deceive you with empty words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of God upon the sons of disobedience.
049	EPH	005	007	Be not ye therefore partakers with them;
049	EPH	005	008	For ye were once darkness, but are now light in the Lord: walk as children of light
049	EPH	005	009	(for the fruit of the light is in all goodness and righteousness and truth),
049	EPH	005	010	proving what is well-pleasing unto the Lord;
049	EPH	005	011	and have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather even reprove them;
049	EPH	005	012	for the things which are done by them in secret it is a shame even to speak of.
049	EPH	005	013	But all things when they are reproved are made manifest by the light: for everything that is made manifest is light.
049	EPH	005	014	Wherefore [he] saith, Awake, thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall shine upon thee.
049	EPH	005	015	Look therefore carefully how ye walk, not as unwise, but as wise;
049	EPH	005	016	redeeming the time, because the days are evil.
049	EPH	005	017	Wherefore be ye not foolish, but understand what the will of the Lord is.
049	EPH	005	018	And be not drunken with wine, wherein is riot, but be filled with the Spirit;
049	EPH	005	019	speaking one to another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody with your heart to the Lord;
049	EPH	005	020	giving thanks always for all things in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ to God, even the Father;
049	EPH	005	021	subjecting yourselves one to another in the fear of Christ.
049	EPH	005	022	Wives, [be in subjection] unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.
049	EPH	005	023	For the husband is the head of the wife, as Christ also is the head of the church, [being] himself the saviour of the body.
049	EPH	005	024	But as the church is subject to Christ, so [let] the wives also [be] to their husbands in everything.
049	EPH	005	025	Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself up for it;
049	EPH	005	026	that he might sanctify it, having cleansed it by the washing of water with the word,
049	EPH	005	027	that he might present the church to himself a glorious [church], not having spot or wrinkle or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.
049	EPH	005	028	Even so ought husbands also to love their own wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his own wife loveth himself:
049	EPH	005	029	for no man ever hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as Christ also the church;
049	EPH	005	030	because we are members of his body.
049	EPH	005	031	For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall cleave to his wife; and the twain shall become one flesh.
049	EPH	005	032	This mystery is great: but I speak in regard of Christ and of the church.
049	EPH	005	033	Nevertheless do ye also severally love each one his own wife even as himself; and [let] the wife [see] that she fear her husband.
049	EPH	006	001	Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.
049	EPH	006	002	Honour thy father and mother (which is the first commandment with promise),
049	EPH	006	003	that it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth.
049	EPH	006	004	And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but nurture them in the chastening and admonition of the Lord.
049	EPH	006	005	Servants, be obedient unto them that according to the flesh are your masters, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto Christ;
049	EPH	006	006	not in the way of eyeservice, as men-pleasers; but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart;
049	EPH	006	007	with good will doing service, as unto the Lord, and not unto men:
049	EPH	006	008	knowing that whatsoever good thing each one doeth, the same shall he receive again from the Lord, whether [he be] bond or free.
049	EPH	006	009	And, ye masters, do the same things unto them, and forbear threatening: knowing that both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no respect of persons with him.
049	EPH	006	010	Finally, be strong in the Lord, and in the strength of his might.
049	EPH	006	011	Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.
049	EPH	006	012	For our wrestling is not against flesh and blood, but against the principalities, against the powers, against the world-rulers of this darkness, against the spiritual [hosts] of wickedness in the heavenly [places].
049	EPH	006	013	Wherefore take up the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and, having done all, to stand.
049	EPH	006	014	Stand therefore, having girded your loins with truth, and having put on the breastplate of righteousness,
049	EPH	006	015	and having shod your feet with the preparation of the gospel of peace;
049	EPH	006	016	withal taking up the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the evil [one].
049	EPH	006	017	And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:
049	EPH	006	018	with all prayer and supplication praying at all seasons in the Spirit, and watching thereunto in all perseverance and supplication for all the saints,
049	EPH	006	019	And on my behalf, that utterance may be given unto me in opening my mouth, to make known with boldness the mystery of the gospel,
049	EPH	006	020	for which I am an ambassador in chains; that in it I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak.
049	EPH	006	021	But that ye also may know my affairs, how I do, Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, shall make known to you all things:
049	EPH	006	022	whom I have sent unto you for this very purpose, that ye may know our state, and that he may comfort your hearts.
049	EPH	006	023	Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	006	024	Grace be with all them that love our Lord Jesus Christ in uncorruptness.
#
# BOOK	050	PHI	Philippians	Philippians
050	PHI	001	001	Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus, to all the saints in Christ Jesus which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:
050	PHI	001	002	Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	001	003	I thank my God upon all my remembrance of you,
050	PHI	001	004	always in every supplication of mine on behalf of you all making my supplication with joy,
050	PHI	001	005	for your fellowship in furtherance of the gospel from the first day until now;
050	PHI	001	006	being confident of this very thing, that he which began a good work in you will perfect it until the day of Jesus Christ:
050	PHI	001	007	even as it is right for me to be thus minded on behalf of you all, because I have you in my heart, inasmuch as, both in my bonds and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers with me of grace.
050	PHI	001	008	For God is my witness, how I long after you all in the tender mercies of Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	001	009	And this I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and all discernment;
050	PHI	001	010	so that ye may approve the things that are excellent; that ye may be sincere and void of offence unto the day of Christ;
050	PHI	001	011	being filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are through Jesus Christ, unto the glory and praise of God.
050	PHI	001	012	Now I would have you know, brethren, that the things [which happened] unto me have fallen out rather unto the progress of the gospel;
050	PHI	001	013	so that my bonds became manifest in Christ throughout the whole praetorian guard, and to all the rest;
050	PHI	001	014	and that most of the brethren in the Lord, being confident through my bonds, are more abundantly bold to speak the word of God without fear.
050	PHI	001	015	Some indeed preach Christ even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:
050	PHI	001	016	the one [do it] of love, knowing that I am set for the defence of the gospel:
050	PHI	001	017	but the other proclaim Christ of faction, not sincerely, thinking to raise up affliction for me in my bonds.
050	PHI	001	018	What then? only that in every way, whether in pretence or in truth, Christ is proclaimed; and therein I rejoice, yea, and will rejoice.
050	PHI	001	019	For I know that this shall turn to my salvation, through your supplication and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,
050	PHI	001	020	according to my earnest expectation and hope, that in nothing shall I be put to shame, but [that] with all boldness, as always, [so] now also Christ shall be magnified in my body, whether by life, or by death.
050	PHI	001	021	For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.
050	PHI	001	022	But if to live in the flesh, —[if] this is the fruit of my work, then what I shall choose I wot not.
050	PHI	001	023	But I am in a strait betwixt the two, having the desire to depart and be with Christ; for it is very far better:
050	PHI	001	024	yet to abide in the flesh is more needful for your sake.
050	PHI	001	025	And having this confidence, I know that I shall abide, yea, and abide with you all, for your progress and joy in the faith;
050	PHI	001	026	that your glorying may abound in Christ Jesus in me through my presence with you again.
050	PHI	001	027	Only let your manner of life be worthy of the gospel of Christ: that, whether I come and see you or be absent, I may hear of your state, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one soul striving for the faith of the gospel;
050	PHI	001	028	and in nothing affrighted by the adversaries: which is for them an evident token of perdition, but of your salvation, and that from God;
050	PHI	001	029	because to you it hath been granted in the behalf of Christ, not only to believe on him, but also to suffer in his behalf:
050	PHI	001	030	having the same conflict which ye saw in me, and now hear to be in me.
050	PHI	002	001	If there is therefore any comfort in Christ, if any consolation of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any tender mercies and compassions,
050	PHI	002	002	fulfill ye my joy, that ye be of the same mind, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind;
050	PHI	002	003	[doing] nothing through faction or through vainglory, but in lowliness of mind each counting other better than himself;
050	PHI	002	004	not looking each of you to his own things, but each of you also to the things of others.
050	PHI	002	005	Have this mind in you, which was also in Christ Jesus:
050	PHI	002	006	who, being in the form of God, counted it not a prize to be on an equality with God,
050	PHI	002	007	but emptied himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in the likeness of men;
050	PHI	002	008	and being found in fashion as a man, he humbled himself, becoming obedient [even] unto death, yea, the death of the cross.
050	PHI	002	009	Wherefore also God highly exalted him, and gave unto him the name which is above every name;
050	PHI	002	010	that in the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of [things] in heaven and [things] on earth and [things] under the earth,
050	PHI	002	011	and that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.
050	PHI	002	012	So then, my beloved, even as ye have always obeyed, not as in my presence only, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling;
050	PHI	002	013	for it is God which worketh in you both to will and to work, for his good pleasure.
050	PHI	002	014	Do all things without murmurings and disputings;
050	PHI	002	015	that ye may be blameless and harmless, children of God without blemish in the midst of a crooked and perverse generation, among whom ye are seen as lights in the world,
050	PHI	002	016	holding forth the word of life; that I may have whereof to glory in the day of Christ, that I did not run in vain neither labour in vain.
050	PHI	002	017	Yea, and if I am offered upon the sacrifice and service of your faith, I joy, and rejoice with you all:
050	PHI	002	018	and in the same manner do ye also joy, and rejoice with me.
050	PHI	002	019	But I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy shortly unto you, that I also may be of good comfort, when I know your state.
050	PHI	002	020	For I have no man likeminded, who will care truly for your state.
050	PHI	002	021	For they all seek their own, not the things of Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	002	022	But ye know the proof of him, that, as a child [serveth] a father, [so] he served with me in furtherance of the gospel.
050	PHI	002	023	Him therefore I hope to send forthwith, so soon as I shall see how it will go with me:
050	PHI	002	024	but I trust in the Lord that I myself also shall come shortly.
050	PHI	002	025	But I counted it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, my brother and fellow-worker and fellow-soldier, and your messenger and minister to my need;
050	PHI	002	026	since he longed after you all, and was sore troubled, because ye had heard that he was sick:
050	PHI	002	027	for indeed he was sick nigh unto death: but God had mercy on him; and not on him only, but on me also, that I might not have sorrow upon sorrow.
050	PHI	002	028	I have sent him therefore the more diligently, that, when ye see him again, ye may rejoice, and that I may be the less sorrowful.
050	PHI	002	029	Receive him therefore in the Lord with all joy; and hold such in honour:
050	PHI	002	030	because for the work of Christ he came nigh unto death, hazarding his life to supply that which was lacking in your service toward me.
050	PHI	003	001	Finally, my brethren, rejoice in the Lord. To write the same things to you, to me indeed is not irksome, but for you it is safe.
050	PHI	003	002	Beware of the dogs, beware of the evil workers, beware of the concision:
050	PHI	003	003	for we are the circumcision, who worship by the Spirit of God, and glory in Christ Jesus, and have no confidence in the flesh:
050	PHI	003	004	though I myself might have confidence even in the flesh: if any other man thinketh to have confidence in the flesh, I yet more:
050	PHI	003	005	circumcised the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews; as touching the law, a Pharisee;
050	PHI	003	006	as touching zeal, persecuting the church; as touching the righteousness which is in the law, found blameless.
050	PHI	003	007	Howbeit what things were gain to me, these have I counted loss for Christ.
050	PHI	003	008	Yea verily, and I count all things to be loss for the excellency of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord: for whom I suffered the loss of all things, and do count them but dung, that I may gain Christ,
050	PHI	003	009	and be found in him, not having a righteousness of mine own, [even] that which is of the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness which is of God by faith:
050	PHI	003	010	that I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, becoming conformed unto his death;
050	PHI	003	011	if by any means I may attain unto the resurrection from the dead.
050	PHI	003	012	Not that I have already obtained, or am already made perfect: but I press on, if so be that I may apprehend that for which also I was apprehended by Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	013	Brethren, I count not myself yet to have apprehended: but one thing [I do], forgetting the things which are behind, and stretching forward to the things which are before,
050	PHI	003	014	I press on toward the goal unto the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	015	Let us therefore, as many as be perfect, be thus minded: and if in anything ye are otherwise minded, even this shall God reveal unto you:
050	PHI	003	016	only, whereunto we have already attained, by that same [rule] let us walk.
050	PHI	003	017	Brethren, be ye imitators together of me, and mark them which so walk even as ye have us for an ensample.
050	PHI	003	018	For many walk, of whom I told you often, and now tell you even weeping, [that they are] the enemies of the cross of Christ:
050	PHI	003	019	whose end is perdition, whose god is the belly, and [whose] glory is in their shame, who mind earthly things.
050	PHI	003	020	For our citizenship is in heaven; from whence also we wait for a Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ:
050	PHI	003	021	who shall fashion anew the body of our humiliation, [that it may be] conformed to the body of his glory, according to the working whereby he is able even to subject all things unto himself.
050	PHI	004	001	Wherefore, my brethren beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, so stand fast in the Lord, my beloved.
050	PHI	004	002	I exhort Euodia, and I exhort Syntyche, to be of the same mind in the Lord.
050	PHI	004	003	Yea, I beseech thee also, true yokefellow, help these women, for they laboured with me in the gospel, with Clement also, and the rest of my fellow-workers, whose names are in the book of life.
050	PHI	004	004	Rejoice in the Lord alway: again I will say, Rejoice.
050	PHI	004	005	Let your forbearance be known unto all men. The Lord is at hand.
050	PHI	004	006	In nothing be anxious; but in everything by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.
050	PHI	004	007	And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall guard your hearts and your thoughts in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	008	Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honourable, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.
050	PHI	004	009	The things which ye both learned and received and heard and saw in me, these things do: and the God of peace shall be with you.
050	PHI	004	010	But I rejoice in the Lord greatly, that now at length ye have revived your thought for me; wherein ye did indeed take thought, but ye lacked opportunity.
050	PHI	004	011	Not that I speak in respect of want: for I have learned, in whatsoever state I am, therein to be content.
050	PHI	004	012	I know how to be abased, and I know also how to abound: in everything and in all things have I learned the secret both to be filled and to be hungry, both to abound and to be in want.
050	PHI	004	013	I can do all things in him that strengtheneth me.
050	PHI	004	014	Howbeit ye did well, that ye had fellowship with my affliction.
050	PHI	004	015	And ye yourselves also know, ye Philippians, that in the beginning of the gospel, when I departed from Macedonia, no church had fellowship with me in the matter of giving and receiving, but ye only;
050	PHI	004	016	for even in Thessalonica ye sent once and again unto my need.
050	PHI	004	017	Not that I seek for the gift; but I seek for the fruit that increaseth to your account.
050	PHI	004	018	But I have all things, and abound: I am filled, having received from Epaphroditus the things [that came] from you, an odour of a sweet smell, a sacrifice acceptable, well-pleasing to God.
050	PHI	004	019	And my God shall fulfill every need of yours according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	020	Now unto our God and Father [be] the glory for ever and ever. Amen.
050	PHI	004	021	Salute every saint in Christ Jesus. The brethren which are with me salute you.
050	PHI	004	022	All the saints salute you, especially they that are of Caesar’s household.
050	PHI	004	023	The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.
#
# BOOK	051	COL	Colossians	Colossians
051	COL	001	001	Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, and Timothy our brother,
051	COL	001	002	To the saints and faithful brethren in Christ [which are] at Colossae: Grace to you and peace from God our Father.
051	COL	001	003	We give thanks to God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, praying always for you,
051	COL	001	004	having heard of your faith in Christ Jesus, and of the love which ye have toward all the saints,
051	COL	001	005	because of the hope which is laid up for you in the heavens, whereof ye heard before in the word of the truth of the gospel,
051	COL	001	006	which is come unto you; even as it is also in all the world bearing fruit and increasing, as [it doth] in you also, since the day ye heard and knew the grace of God in truth;
051	COL	001	007	even as ye learned of Epaphras our beloved fellow-servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our behalf,
051	COL	001	008	who also declared unto us your love in the Spirit.
051	COL	001	009	For this cause we also, since the day we heard [it], do not cease to pray and make request for you, that ye may be filled with the knowledge of his will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,
051	COL	001	010	to walk worthily of the Lord unto all pleasing, bearing fruit in every good work, and increasing in the knowledge of God;
051	COL	001	011	strengthened with all power, according to the might of his glory, unto all patience and longsuffering with joy;
051	COL	001	012	giving thanks unto the Father, who made us meet to be partakers of the inheritance of the saints in light;
051	COL	001	013	who delivered us out of the power of darkness, and translated us into the kingdom of the Son of his love;
051	COL	001	014	in whom we have our redemption, the forgiveness of our sins:
051	COL	001	015	who is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of all creation;
051	COL	001	016	for in him were all things created, in the heavens and upon the earth, things visible and things invisible, whether thrones or dominions or principalities or powers; all things have been created through him, and unto him;
051	COL	001	017	and he is before all things, and in him all things consist.
051	COL	001	018	And he is the head of the body, the church: who is the beginning, the firstborn from the dead; that in all things he might have the preeminence.
051	COL	001	019	For it was the good pleasure [of the Father] that in him should all the fulness dwell;
051	COL	001	020	and through him to reconcile all things unto himself, having made peace through the blood of his cross; through him, [I say], whether things upon the earth, or things in the heavens.
051	COL	001	021	And you, being in time past alienated and enemies in your mind in your evil works, yet now hath he reconciled
051	COL	001	022	in the body of his flesh through death, to present you holy and without blemish and unreproveable before him:
051	COL	001	023	if so be that ye continue in the faith, grounded and stedfast, and not moved away from the hope of the gospel which ye heard, which was preached in all creation under heaven; whereof I Paul was made a minister.
051	COL	001	024	Now I rejoice in my sufferings for your sake, and fill up on my part that which is lacking of the afflictions of Christ in my flesh for his body’s sake, which is the church;
051	COL	001	025	whereof I was made a minister, according to the dispensation of God which was given me to you-ward, to fulfill the word of God,
051	COL	001	026	[even] the mystery which hath been hid from all ages and generations: but now hath it been manifested to his saints,
051	COL	001	027	to whom God was pleased to make known what is the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory:
051	COL	001	028	whom we proclaim, admonishing every man and teaching every man in all wisdom, that we may present every man perfect in Christ;
051	COL	001	029	whereunto I labour also, striving according to his working, which worketh in me mightily.
051	COL	002	001	For I would have you know how greatly I strive for you, and for them at Laodicea, and for as many as have not seen my face in the flesh;
051	COL	002	002	that their hearts may be comforted, they being knit together in love, and unto all riches of the full assurance of understanding, that they may know the mystery of God, [even] Christ,
051	COL	002	003	in whom are all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge hidden.
051	COL	002	004	This I say, that no one may delude you with persuasiveness of speech.
051	COL	002	005	For though I am absent in the flesh, yet am I with you in the spirit, joying and beholding your order, and the stedfastness of your faith in Christ.
051	COL	002	006	As therefore ye received Christ Jesus the Lord, [so] walk in him,
051	COL	002	007	rooted and builded up in him, and stablished in your faith, even as ye were taught, abounding in thanksgiving.
051	COL	002	008	Take heed lest there shall be any one that maketh spoil of you through his philosophy and vain deceit, after the tradition of men, after the rudiments of the world, and not after Christ:
051	COL	002	009	for in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily,
051	COL	002	010	and in him ye are made full, who is the head of all principality and power:
051	COL	002	011	in whom ye were also circumcised with a circumcision not made with hands, in the putting off of the body of the flesh, in the circumcision of Christ;
051	COL	002	012	having been buried with him in baptism, wherein ye were also raised with him through faith in the working of God, who raised him from the dead.
051	COL	002	013	And you, being dead through your trespasses and the uncircumcision of your flesh, you, [I say], did he quicken together with him, having forgiven us all our trespasses;
051	COL	002	014	having blotted out the bond written in ordinances that was against us, which was contrary to us: and he hath taken it out of the way, nailing it to the cross;
051	COL	002	015	having put off from himself the principalities and the powers, he made a show of them openly, triumphing over them in it.
051	COL	002	016	Let no man therefore judge you in meat, or in drink, or in respect of a feast day or a new moon or a sabbath day:
051	COL	002	017	which are a shadow of the things to come; but the body is Christ’s.
051	COL	002	018	Let no man rob you of your prize by a voluntary humility and worshipping of the angels, dwelling in the things which he hath seen, vainly puffed up by his fleshly mind,
051	COL	002	019	and not holding fast the Head, from whom all the body, being supplied and knit together through the joints and bands, increaseth with the increase of God.
051	COL	002	020	If ye died with Christ from the rudiments of the world, why, as though living in the world, do ye subject yourselves to ordinances,
051	COL	002	021	Handle not, nor taste, nor touch
051	COL	002	022	(all which things are to perish with the using), after the precepts and doctrines of men?
051	COL	002	023	Which things have indeed a show of wisdom in will-worship, and humility, and severity to the body; [but are] not of any value against the indulgence of the flesh.
051	COL	003	001	If then ye were raised together with Christ, seek the things that are above, where Christ is, seated on the right hand of God.
051	COL	003	002	Set your mind on the things that are above, not on the things that are upon the earth.
051	COL	003	003	For ye died, and your life is hid with Christ in God.
051	COL	003	004	When Christ, [who is] our life, shall be manifested, then shall ye also with him be manifested in glory.
051	COL	003	005	Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, uncleanness, passion, evil desire, and covetousness, the which is idolatry;
051	COL	003	006	for which things’ sake cometh the wrath of God upon the sons of disobedience;
051	COL	003	007	in the which ye also walked aforetime, when ye lived in these things.
051	COL	003	008	But now put ye also away all these; anger, wrath, malice, railing, shameful speaking out of your mouth:
051	COL	003	009	lie not one to another; seeing that ye have put off the old man with his doings,
051	COL	003	010	and have put on the new man, which is being renewed unto knowledge after the image of him that created him:
051	COL	003	011	where there cannot be Greek and Jew, circumcision and uncircumcision, barbarian, Scythian, bondman, freeman: but Christ is all, and in all.
051	COL	003	012	Put on therefore, as God’s elect, holy and beloved, a heart of compassion, kindness, humility, meekness, longsuffering;
051	COL	003	013	forbearing one another, and forgiving each other, if any man have a complaint against any; even as the Lord forgave you, so also do ye:
051	COL	003	014	and above all these things [put on] love, which is the bond of perfectness.
051	COL	003	015	And let the peace of Christ rule in your hearts, to the which also ye were called in one body; and be ye thankful.
051	COL	003	016	Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another with psalms [and] hymns [and] spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts unto God.
051	COL	003	017	And whatsoever ye do, in word or in deed, [do] all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through him.
051	COL	003	018	Wives, be in subjection to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord.
051	COL	003	019	Husbands, love your wives, and be not bitter against them.
051	COL	003	020	Children, obey your parents in all things, for this is well-pleasing in the Lord.
051	COL	003	021	Fathers, provoke not your children, that they be not discouraged.
051	COL	003	022	Servants, obey in all things them that are your masters according to the flesh; not with eyeservice, as men-pleasers, but in singleness of heart, fearing the Lord:
051	COL	003	023	whatsoever ye do, work heartily, as unto the Lord, and not unto men;
051	COL	003	024	knowing that from the Lord ye shall receive the recompense of the inheritance: ye serve the Lord Christ.
051	COL	003	025	For he that doeth wrong shall receive again for the wrong that he hath done: and there is no respect of persons.
051	COL	004	001	Masters, render unto your servants that which is just and equal; knowing that ye also have a Master in heaven.
051	COL	004	002	Continue stedfastly in prayer, watching therein with thanksgiving;
051	COL	004	003	withal praying for us also, that God may open unto us a door for the word, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds;
051	COL	004	004	that I may make it manifest, as I ought to speak.
051	COL	004	005	Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time.
051	COL	004	006	Let your speech be always with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer each one.
051	COL	004	007	All my affairs shall Tychicus make known unto you, the beloved brother and faithful minister and fellow-servant in the Lord:
051	COL	004	008	whom I have sent unto you for this very purpose, that ye may know our estate, and that he may comfort your hearts;
051	COL	004	009	together with Onesimus, the faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They shall make known unto you all things that [are done] here.
051	COL	004	010	Aristarchus my fellow-prisoner saluteth you, and Mark, the cousin of Barnabas (touching whom ye received commandments; if he come unto you, receive him),
051	COL	004	011	and Jesus, which is called Justus, who are of the circumcision: these only [are my] fellow-workers unto the kingdom of God, men that have been a comfort unto me.
051	COL	004	012	Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of Christ Jesus, saluteth you, always striving for you in his prayers, that ye may stand perfect and fully assured in all the will of God.
051	COL	004	013	For I bear him witness, that he hath much labour for you, and for them in Laodicea, and for them in Hierapolis.
051	COL	004	014	Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas salute you.
051	COL	004	015	Salute the brethren that are in Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the church that is in their house.
051	COL	004	016	And when this epistle hath been read among you, cause that it be read also in the church of the Laodiceans; and that ye also read the epistle from Laodicea.
051	COL	004	017	And say to Archippus, Take heed to the ministry which thou hast received in the Lord, that thou fulfill it.
051	COL	004	018	The salutation of me Paul with mine own hand. Remember my bonds. Grace be with you.
#
# BOOK	052	1TH	1 Thessalonians	1 Thessalonians
052	1TH	001	001	Paul, and Silvanus, and Timothy, unto the church of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace to you and peace.
052	1TH	001	002	We give thanks to God always for you all, making mention [of you] in our prayers;
052	1TH	001	003	remembering without ceasing your work of faith and labour of love and patience of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, before our God and Father;
052	1TH	001	004	knowing, brethren beloved of God, your election,
052	1TH	001	005	how that our gospel came not unto you in word only, but also in power, and in the Holy Ghost, and [in] much assurance; even as ye know what manner of men we shewed ourselves toward you for your sake.
052	1TH	001	006	And ye became imitators of us, and of the Lord, having received the word in much affliction, with joy of the Holy Ghost;
052	1TH	001	007	so that ye became an ensample to all that believe in Macedonia and in Achaia.
052	1TH	001	008	For from you hath sounded forth the word of the Lord, not only in Macedonia and Achaia, but in every place your faith to God-ward is gone forth; so that we need not to speak anything.
052	1TH	001	009	For they themselves report concerning us what manner of entering in we had unto you; and how ye turned unto God from idols, to serve a living and true God,
052	1TH	001	010	and to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, [even] Jesus, which delivereth us from the wrath to come.
052	1TH	002	001	For yourselves, brethren, know our entering in unto you, that it hath not been found vain:
052	1TH	002	002	but having suffered before, and been shamefully entreated, as ye know, at Philippi, we waxed bold in our God to speak unto you the gospel of God in much conflict.
052	1TH	002	003	For our exhortation [is] not of error, nor of uncleanness, nor in guile:
052	1TH	002	004	but even as we have been approved of God to be intrusted with the gospel, so we speak; not as pleasing men, but God which proveth our hearts.
052	1TH	002	005	For neither at any time were we found using words of flattery, as ye know, nor a cloke of covetousness, God is witness;
052	1TH	002	006	nor seeking glory of men, neither from you, nor from others, when we might have been burdensome, as apostles of Christ.
052	1TH	002	007	But we were gentle in the midst of you, as when a nurse cherisheth her own children:
052	1TH	002	008	even so, being affectionately desirous of you, we were well pleased to impart unto you, not the gospel of God only, but also our own souls, because ye were become very dear to us.
052	1TH	002	009	For ye remember, brethren, our labour and travail: working night and day, that we might not burden any of you, we preached unto you the gospel of God.
052	1TH	002	010	Ye are witnesses, and God [also], how holily and righteously and unblameably we behaved ourselves toward you that believe:
052	1TH	002	011	as ye know how we [dealt with] each one of you, as a father with his own children, exhorting you, and encouraging [you], and testifying,
052	1TH	002	012	to the end that ye should walk worthily of God, who calleth you into his own kingdom and glory.
052	1TH	002	013	And for this cause we also thank God without ceasing, that, when ye received from us the word of the message, [even the word] of God, ye accepted [it] not [as] the word of men, but, as it is in truth, the word of God, which also worketh in you that believe.
052	1TH	002	014	For ye, brethren, became imitators of the churches of God which are in Judaea in Christ Jesus: for ye also suffered the same things of your own countrymen, even as they did of the Jews;
052	1TH	002	015	who both killed the Lord Jesus and the prophets, and drave out us, and please not God, and are contrary to all men;
052	1TH	002	016	forbidding us to speak to the Gentiles that they may be saved; to fill up their sins alway: but the wrath is come upon them to the uttermost.
052	1TH	002	017	But we, brethren, being bereaved of you for a short season, in presence, not in heart, endeavoured the more exceedingly to see your face with great desire:
052	1TH	002	018	because we would fain have come unto you, I Paul once and again; and Satan hindered us.
052	1TH	002	019	For what is our hope, or joy, or crown of glorying? Are not even ye, before our Lord Jesus at his coming?
052	1TH	002	020	For ye are our glory and our joy.
052	1TH	003	001	Wherefore when we could no longer forbear, we thought it good to be left behind at Athens alone;
052	1TH	003	002	and sent Timothy, our brother and God’s minister in the gospel of Christ, to establish you, and to comfort [you] concerning your faith;
052	1TH	003	003	that no man be moved by these afflictions; for yourselves know that hereunto we are appointed.
052	1TH	003	004	For verily, when we were with you, we told you beforehand that we are to suffer affliction; even as it came to pass, and ye know.
052	1TH	003	005	For this cause I also, when I could no longer forbear, sent that I might know your faith, lest by any means the tempter had tempted you, and our labour should be in vain.
052	1TH	003	006	But when Timothy came even now unto us from you, and brought us glad tidings of your faith and love, and that ye have good remembrance of us always, longing to see us, even as we also [to see] you;
052	1TH	003	007	for this cause, brethren, we were comforted over you in all our distress and affliction through your faith:
052	1TH	003	008	for now we live, if ye stand fast in the Lord.
052	1TH	003	009	For what thanksgiving can we render again unto God for you, for all the joy wherewith we joy for your sakes before our God;
052	1TH	003	010	night and day praying exceedingly that we may see your face, and may perfect that which is lacking in your faith?
052	1TH	003	011	Now may our God and Father himself, and our Lord Jesus, direct our way unto you:
052	1TH	003	012	and the Lord make you to increase and abound in love one toward another, and toward all men, even as we also [do] toward you;
052	1TH	003	013	to the end he may stablish your hearts unblameable in holiness before our God and Father, at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all his saints.
052	1TH	004	001	Finally then, brethren, we beseech and exhort you in the Lord Jesus, that, as ye received of us how ye ought to walk and to please God, even as ye do walk, —that ye abound more and more.
052	1TH	004	002	For ye know what charge we gave you through the Lord Jesus.
052	1TH	004	003	For this is the will of God, [even] your sanctification, that ye abstain from fornication;
052	1TH	004	004	that each one of you know how to possess himself of his own vessel in sanctification and honour,
052	1TH	004	005	not in the passion of lust, even as the Gentiles which know not God;
052	1TH	004	006	that no man transgress, and wrong his brother in the matter: because the Lord is an avenger in all these things, as also we forewarned you and testified.
052	1TH	004	007	For God called us not for uncleanness, but in sanctification.
052	1TH	004	008	Therefore he that rejecteth, rejecteth not man, but God, who giveth his Holy Spirit unto you.
052	1TH	004	009	But concerning love of the brethren ye have no need that one write unto you: for ye yourselves are taught of God to love one another;
052	1TH	004	010	for indeed ye do it toward all the brethren which are in all Macedonia. But we exhort you, brethren, that ye abound more and more;
052	1TH	004	011	and that ye study to be quiet, and to do your own business, and to work with your hands, even as we charged you;
052	1TH	004	012	that ye may walk honestly toward them that are without, and may have need of nothing.
052	1TH	004	013	But we would not have you ignorant, brethren, concerning them that fall asleep; that ye sorrow not, even as the rest, which have no hope.
052	1TH	004	014	For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so them also that are fallen asleep in Jesus will God bring with him.
052	1TH	004	015	For this we say unto you by the word of the Lord, that we that are alive, that are left unto the coming of the Lord, shall in no wise precede them that are fallen asleep.
052	1TH	004	016	For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven, with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first:
052	1TH	004	017	then we that are alive, that are left, shall together with them be caught up in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.
052	1TH	004	018	Wherefore comfort one another with these words.
052	1TH	005	001	But concerning the times and the seasons, brethren, ye have no need that aught be written unto you.
052	1TH	005	002	For yourselves know perfectly that the day of the Lord so cometh as a thief in the night.
052	1TH	005	003	When they are saying, Peace and safety, then sudden destruction cometh upon them, as travail upon a woman with child; and they shall in no wise escape.
052	1TH	005	004	But ye, brethren, are not in darkness, that that day should overtake you as a thief:
052	1TH	005	005	for ye are all sons of light, and sons of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness;
052	1TH	005	006	so then let us not sleep, as do the rest, but let us watch and be sober.
052	1TH	005	007	For they that sleep sleep in the night; and they that be drunken are drunken in the night.
052	1TH	005	008	But let us, since we are of the day, be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love; and for a helmet, the hope of salvation.
052	1TH	005	009	For God appointed us not unto wrath, but unto the obtaining of salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ,
052	1TH	005	010	who died for us, that, whether we wake or sleep, we should live together with him.
052	1TH	005	011	Wherefore exhort one another, and build each other up, even as also ye do.
052	1TH	005	012	But we beseech you, brethren, to know them that labour among you, and are over you in the Lord, and admonish you;
052	1TH	005	013	and to esteem them exceeding highly in love for their work’s sake. Be at peace among yourselves.
052	1TH	005	014	And we exhort you, brethren, admonish the disorderly, encourage the fainthearted, support the weak, be longsuffering toward all.
052	1TH	005	015	See that none render unto any one evil for evil; but alway follow after that which is good, one toward another, and toward all.
052	1TH	005	016	Rejoice alway;
052	1TH	005	017	pray without ceasing;
052	1TH	005	018	in everything give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus to you-ward.
052	1TH	005	019	Quench not the Spirit;
052	1TH	005	020	despise not prophesyings;
052	1TH	005	021	prove all things; hold fast that which is good;
052	1TH	005	022	abstain from every form of evil.
052	1TH	005	023	And the God of peace himself sanctify you wholly; and may your spirit and soul and body be preserved entire, without blame at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.
052	1TH	005	024	Faithful is he that calleth you, who will also do it.
052	1TH	005	025	Brethren, pray for us.
052	1TH	005	026	Salute all the brethren with a holy kiss.
052	1TH	005	027	I adjure you by the Lord that this epistle be read unto all the brethren.
052	1TH	005	028	The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
#
# BOOK	053	2TH	2 Thessalonians	2 Thessalonians
053	2TH	001	001	Paul, and Silvanus, and Timothy, unto the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ;
053	2TH	001	002	Grace to you and peace from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	003	We are bound to give thanks to God alway for you, brethren, even as it is meet, for that your faith groweth exceedingly, and the love of each one of you all toward one another aboundeth;
053	2TH	001	004	so that we ourselves glory in you in the churches of God for your patience and faith in all your persecutions and in the afflictions which ye endure;
053	2TH	001	005	[which is] a manifest token of the righteous judgment of God; to the end that ye may be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which ye also suffer:
053	2TH	001	006	if so be that it is a righteous thing with God to recompense affliction to them that afflict you,
053	2TH	001	007	and to you that are afflicted rest with us, at the revelation of the Lord Jesus from heaven with the angels of his power
053	2TH	001	008	in flaming fire, rendering vengeance to them that know not God, and to them that obey not the gospel of our Lord Jesus:
053	2TH	001	009	who shall suffer punishment, [even] eternal destruction from the face of the Lord and from the glory of his might,
053	2TH	001	010	when he shall come to be glorified in his saints, and to be marveled at in all them that believed (because our testimony unto you was believed) in that day.
053	2TH	001	011	To which end we also pray always for you, that our God may count you worthy of your calling, and fulfill every desire of goodness and [every] work of faith, with power;
053	2TH	001	012	that the name of our Lord Jesus may be glorified in you, and ye in him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	001	Now we beseech you, brethren, touching the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, and our gathering together unto him;
053	2TH	002	002	to the end that ye be not quickly shaken from your mind, nor yet be troubled, either by spirit, or by word, or by epistle as from us, as that the day of the Lord is [now] present;
053	2TH	002	003	let no man beguile you in any wise: for [it will not be], except the falling away come first, and the man of sin be revealed, the son of perdition,
053	2TH	002	004	he that opposeth and exalteth himself against all that is called God or that is worshipped; so that he sitteth in the temple of God, setting himself forth as God.
053	2TH	002	005	Remember ye not, that, when I was yet with you, I told you these things?
053	2TH	002	006	And now ye know that which restraineth, to the end that he may be revealed in his own season.
053	2TH	002	007	For the mystery of lawlessness doth already work: only [there is] one that restraineth now, until he be taken out of the way.
053	2TH	002	008	And then shall be revealed the lawless one, whom the Lord Jesus shall slay with the breath of his mouth, and bring to nought by the manifestation of his coming;
053	2TH	002	009	[even he], whose coming is according to the working of Satan with all power and signs and lying wonders,
053	2TH	002	010	and with all deceit of unrighteousness for them that are perishing; because they received not the love of the truth, that they might be saved.
053	2TH	002	011	And for this cause God sendeth them a working of error, that they should believe a lie:
053	2TH	002	012	that they all might be judged who believed not the truth, but had pleasure in unrighteousness.
053	2TH	002	013	But we are bound to give thanks to God alway for you, brethren beloved of the Lord, for that God chose you from the beginning unto salvation in sanctification of the Spirit and belief of the truth:
053	2TH	002	014	whereunto he called you through our gospel, to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	015	So then, brethren, stand fast, and hold the traditions which ye were taught, whether by word, or by epistle of ours.
053	2TH	002	016	Now our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God our Father which loved us and gave us eternal comfort and good hope through grace,
053	2TH	002	017	comfort your hearts and stablish them in every good work and word.
053	2TH	003	001	Finally, brethren, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may run and be glorified, even as also [it is] with you;
053	2TH	003	002	and that we may be delivered from unreasonable and evil men; for all have not faith.
053	2TH	003	003	But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and guard you from the evil [one].
053	2TH	003	004	And we have confidence in the Lord touching you, that ye both do and will do the things which we command.
053	2TH	003	005	And the Lord direct your hearts into the love of God, and into the patience of Christ.
053	2TH	003	006	Now we command you, brethren, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that ye withdraw yourselves from every brother that walketh disorderly, and not after the tradition which they received of us.
053	2TH	003	007	For yourselves know how ye ought to imitate us: for we behaved not ourselves disorderly among you;
053	2TH	003	008	neither did we eat bread for nought at any man’s hand, but in labour and travail, working night and day, that we might not burden any of you:
053	2TH	003	009	not because we have not the right, but to make ourselves an ensample unto you, that ye should imitate us.
053	2TH	003	010	For even when we were with you, this we commanded you, If any will not work, neither let him eat.
053	2TH	003	011	For we hear of some that walk among you disorderly, that work not at all, but are busybodies.
053	2TH	003	012	Now them that are such we command and exhort in the Lord Jesus Christ, that with quietness they work, and eat their own bread.
053	2TH	003	013	But ye, brethren, be not weary in well-doing.
053	2TH	003	014	And if any man obeyeth not our word by this epistle, note that man, that ye have no company with him, to the end that he may be ashamed.
053	2TH	003	015	And [yet] count him not as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother.
053	2TH	003	016	Now the Lord of peace himself give you peace at all times in all ways. The Lord be with you all.
053	2TH	003	017	The salutation of me Paul with mine own hand, which is the token in every epistle: so I write.
053	2TH	003	018	The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all.
#
# BOOK	054	1TI	1 Timothy	1 Timothy
054	1TI	001	001	Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus according to the commandment of God our Saviour, and Christ Jesus our hope;
054	1TI	001	002	unto Timothy, my true child in faith: Grace, mercy, peace, from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.
054	1TI	001	003	As I exhorted thee to tarry at Ephesus, when I was going into Macedonia, that thou mightest charge certain men not to teach a different doctrine,
054	1TI	001	004	neither to give heed to fables and endless genealogies, the which minister questionings, rather than a dispensation of God which is in faith; [so do I now].
054	1TI	001	005	But the end of the charge is love out of a pure heart and a good conscience and faith unfeigned:
054	1TI	001	006	from which things some having swerved have turned aside unto vain talking;
054	1TI	001	007	desiring to be teachers of the law, though they understand neither what they say, nor whereof they confidently affirm.
054	1TI	001	008	But we know that the law is good, if a man use it lawfully,
054	1TI	001	009	as knowing this, that law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and unruly, for the ungodly and sinners, for the unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers,
054	1TI	001	010	for fornicators, for abusers of themselves with men, for menstealers, for liars, for false swearers, and if there be any other thing contrary to the sound doctrine;
054	1TI	001	011	according to the gospel of the glory of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust.
054	1TI	001	012	I thank him that enabled me, [even] Christ Jesus our Lord, for that he counted me faithful, appointing me to [his] service;
054	1TI	001	013	though I was before a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and injurious: howbeit I obtained mercy, because I did it ignorantly in unbelief;
054	1TI	001	014	and the grace of our Lord abounded exceedingly with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	001	015	Faithful is the saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief:
054	1TI	001	016	howbeit for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me as chief might Jesus Christ shew forth all his longsuffering, for an ensample of them which should hereafter believe on him unto eternal life.
054	1TI	001	017	Now unto the King eternal, incorruptible, invisible, the only God, [be] honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.
054	1TI	001	018	This charge I commit unto thee, my child Timothy, according to the prophecies which went before on thee, that by them thou mayest war the good warfare;
054	1TI	001	019	holding faith and a good conscience; which some having thrust from them made shipwreck concerning the faith:
054	1TI	001	020	of whom is Hymenaeus and Alexander; whom I delivered unto Satan, that they might be taught not to blaspheme.
054	1TI	002	001	I exhort therefore, first of all, that supplications, prayers, intercessions, thanksgivings, be made for all men;
054	1TI	002	002	for kings and all that are in high place; that we may lead a tranquil and quiet life in all godliness and gravity.
054	1TI	002	003	This is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Saviour;
054	1TI	002	004	who willeth that all men should be saved, and come to the knowledge of the truth.
054	1TI	002	005	For there is one God, one mediator also between God and men, [himself] man, Christ Jesus,
054	1TI	002	006	who gave himself a ransom for all; the testimony [to be borne] in its own times;
054	1TI	002	007	whereunto I was appointed a preacher and an apostle (I speak the truth, I lie not), a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and truth.
054	1TI	002	008	I desire therefore that the men pray in every place, lifting up holy hands, without wrath and disputing.
054	1TI	002	009	In like manner, that women adorn themselves in modest apparel, with shamefastness and sobriety; not with braided hair, and gold or pearls or costly raiment;
054	1TI	002	010	but (which becometh women professing godliness) through good works.
054	1TI	002	011	Let a woman learn in quietness with all subjection.
054	1TI	002	012	But I permit not a woman to teach, nor to have dominion over a man, but to be in quietness.
054	1TI	002	013	For Adam was first formed, then Eve;
054	1TI	002	014	and Adam was not beguiled, but the woman being beguiled hath fallen into transgression:
054	1TI	002	015	but she shall be saved through the childbearing, if they continue in faith and love and sanctification with sobriety.
054	1TI	003	001	Faithful is the saying, If a man seeketh the office of a bishop, he desireth a good work.
054	1TI	003	002	The bishop therefore must be without reproach, the husband of one wife, temperate, soberminded, orderly, given to hospitality, apt to teach;
054	1TI	003	003	no brawler, no striker; but gentle, not contentious, no lover of money;
054	1TI	003	004	one that ruleth well his own house, having [his] children in subjection with all gravity;
054	1TI	003	005	(but if a man knoweth not how to rule his own house, how shall he take care of the church of God?)
054	1TI	003	006	not a novice, lest being puffed up he fall into the condemnation of the devil.
054	1TI	003	007	Moreover he must have good testimony from them that are without; lest he fall into reproach and the snare of the devil.
054	1TI	003	008	Deacons in like manner [must be] grave, not doubletongued, not given to much wine, not greedy of filthy lucre;
054	1TI	003	009	holding the mystery of the faith in a pure conscience.
054	1TI	003	010	And let these also first be proved; then let them serve as deacons, if they be blameless.
054	1TI	003	011	Women in like manner [must be] grave, not slanderers, temperate, faithful in all things.
054	1TI	003	012	Let deacons be husbands of one wife, ruling [their] children and their own houses well.
054	1TI	003	013	For they that have served well as deacons gain to themselves a good standing, and great boldness in the faith which is in Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	003	014	These things write I unto thee, hoping to come unto thee shortly;
054	1TI	003	015	but if I tarry long, that thou mayest know how men ought to behave themselves in the house of God, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and ground of the truth.
054	1TI	003	016	And without controversy great is the mystery of godliness; He who was manifested in the flesh, justified in the spirit, seen of angels, preached among the nations, believed on in the world, received up in glory.
054	1TI	004	001	But the Spirit saith expressly, that in later times some shall fall away from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits and doctrines of devils,
054	1TI	004	002	through the hypocrisy of men that speak lies, branded in their own conscience as with a hot iron;
054	1TI	004	003	forbidding to marry, [and commanding] to abstain from meats, which God created to be received with thanksgiving by them that believe and know the truth.
054	1TI	004	004	For every creature of God is good, and nothing is to be rejected, if it be received with thanksgiving:
054	1TI	004	005	for it is sanctified through the word of God and prayer.
054	1TI	004	006	If thou put the brethren in mind of these things, thou shalt be a good minister of Christ Jesus, nourished in the words of the faith, and of the good doctrine which thou hast followed [until now]:
054	1TI	004	007	but refuse profane and old wives’ fables. And exercise thyself unto godliness:
054	1TI	004	008	for bodily exercise is profitable for a little; but godliness is profitable for all things, having promise of the life which now is, and of that which is to come.
054	1TI	004	009	Faithful is the saying, and worthy of all acceptation.
054	1TI	004	010	For to this end we labour and strive, because we have our hope set on the living God, who is the Saviour of all men, specially of them that believe.
054	1TI	004	011	These things command and teach.
054	1TI	004	012	Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an ensample to them that believe, in word, in manner of life, in love, in faith, in purity.
054	1TI	004	013	Till I come, give heed to reading, to exhortation, to teaching.
054	1TI	004	014	Neglect not the gift that is in thee, which was given thee by prophecy, with the laying on of the hands of the presbytery.
054	1TI	004	015	Be diligent in these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy progress may be manifest unto all.
054	1TI	004	016	Take heed to thyself, and to thy teaching. Continue in these things; for in doing this thou shalt save both thyself and them that hear thee.
054	1TI	005	001	Rebuke not an elder, but exhort him as a father; the younger men as brethren:
054	1TI	005	002	the elder women as mothers; the younger as sisters, in all purity.
054	1TI	005	003	Honour widows that are widows indeed.
054	1TI	005	004	But if any widow hath children or grandchildren, let them learn first to shew piety towards their own family, and to requite their parents: for this is acceptable in the sight of God.
054	1TI	005	005	Now she that is a widow indeed, and desolate, hath her hope set on God, and continueth in supplications and prayers night and day.
054	1TI	005	006	But she that giveth herself to pleasure is dead while she liveth.
054	1TI	005	007	These things also command, that they may be without reproach.
054	1TI	005	008	But if any provideth not for his own, and specially his own household, he hath denied the faith, and is worse than an unbeliever.
054	1TI	005	009	Let none be enrolled as a widow under threescore years old, [having been] the wife of one man,
054	1TI	005	010	well reported of for good works; if she hath brought up children, if she hath used hospitality to strangers, if she hath washed the saints’ feet, if she hath relieved the afflicted, if she hath diligently followed every good work.
054	1TI	005	011	But younger widows refuse: for when they have waxed wanton against Christ, they desire to marry;
054	1TI	005	012	having condemnation, because they have rejected their first faith.
054	1TI	005	013	And withal they learn also [to be] idle, going about from house to house; and not only idle, but tattlers also and busybodies, speaking things which they ought not.
054	1TI	005	014	I desire therefore that the younger [widows] marry, bear children, rule the household, give none occasion to the adversary for reviling:
054	1TI	005	015	for already some are turned aside after Satan.
054	1TI	005	016	If any woman that believeth hath widows, let her relieve them, and let not the church be burdened; that it may relieve them that are widows indeed.
054	1TI	005	017	Let the elders that rule well be counted worthy of double honour, especially those who labour in the word and in teaching.
054	1TI	005	018	For the scripture saith, Thou shalt not muzzle the ox when he treadeth out the corn. And, The labourer is worthy of his hire.
054	1TI	005	019	Against an elder receive not an accusation, except at [the mouth of] two or three witnesses.
054	1TI	005	020	Them that sin reprove in the sight of all, that the rest also may be in fear.
054	1TI	005	021	I charge [thee] in the sight of God, and Christ Jesus, and the elect angels, that thou observe these things without prejudice, doing nothing by partiality.
054	1TI	005	022	Lay hands hastily on no man, neither be partaker of other men’s sins: keep thyself pure.
054	1TI	005	023	Be no longer a drinker of water, but use a little wine for thy stomach’s sake and thine often infirmities.
054	1TI	005	024	Some men’s sins are evident, going before unto judgment; and some men also they follow after.
054	1TI	005	025	In like manner also there are good works that are evident; and such as are otherwise cannot be hid.
054	1TI	006	001	Let as many as are servants under the yoke count their own masters worthy of all honour, that the name of God and the doctrine be not blasphemed.
054	1TI	006	002	And they that have believing masters, let them not despise them, because they are brethren; but let them serve them the rather, because they that partake of the benefit are believing and beloved. These things teach and exhort.
054	1TI	006	003	If any man teacheth a different doctrine, and consenteth not to sound words, [even] the words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and to the doctrine which is according to godliness;
054	1TI	006	004	he is puffed up, knowing nothing, but doting about questionings and disputes of words, whereof cometh envy, strife, railings, evil surmisings,
054	1TI	006	005	wranglings of men corrupted in mind and bereft of the truth, supposing that godliness is a way of gain.
054	1TI	006	006	But godliness with contentment is great gain:
054	1TI	006	007	for we brought nothing into the world, for neither can we carry anything out;
054	1TI	006	008	but having food and covering we shall be therewith content.
054	1TI	006	009	But they that desire to be rich fall into a temptation and a snare and many foolish and hurtful lusts, such as drown men in destruction and perdition.
054	1TI	006	010	For the love of money is a root of all kinds of evil: which some reaching after have been led astray from the faith, and have pierced themselves through with many sorrows.
054	1TI	006	011	But thou, O man of God, flee these things; and follow after righteousness, godliness, faith, love, patience, meekness.
054	1TI	006	012	Fight the good fight of the faith, lay hold on the life eternal, whereunto thou wast called, and didst confess the good confession in the sight of many witnesses.
054	1TI	006	013	I charge thee in the sight of God, who quickeneth all things, and of Christ Jesus, who before Pontius Pilate witnessed the good confession;
054	1TI	006	014	that thou keep the commandment, without spot, without reproach, until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ:
054	1TI	006	015	which in its own times he shall shew, who is the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords;
054	1TI	006	016	who only hath immortality, dwelling in light unapproachable; whom no man hath seen, nor can see: to whom [be] honour and power eternal. Amen.
054	1TI	006	017	Charge them that are rich in this present world, that they be not highminded, nor have their hope set on the uncertainty of riches, but on God, who giveth us richly all things to enjoy;
054	1TI	006	018	that they do good, that they be rich in good works, that they be ready to distribute, willing to communicate;
054	1TI	006	019	laying up in store for themselves a good foundation against the time to come, that they may lay hold on the life which is [life] indeed.
054	1TI	006	020	O Timothy, guard that which is committed unto [thee], turning away from the profane babblings and oppositions of the knowledge which is falsely so called;
054	1TI	006	021	which some professing have erred concerning the faith. Grace be with you.
#
# BOOK	055	2TI	2 Timothy	2 Timothy
055	2TI	001	001	Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, according to the promise of the life which is in Christ Jesus,
055	2TI	001	002	to Timothy, my beloved child: Grace, mercy, peace, from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.
055	2TI	001	003	I thank God, whom I serve from my forefathers in a pure conscience, how unceasing is my remembrance of thee in my supplications, night and day
055	2TI	001	004	longing to see thee, remembering thy tears, that I may be filled with joy;
055	2TI	001	005	having been reminded of the unfeigned faith that is in thee; which dwelt first in thy grandmother Lois, and thy mother Eunice; and, I am persuaded, in thee also.
055	2TI	001	006	For the which cause I put thee in remembrance that thou stir up the gift of God, which is in thee through the laying on of my hands.
055	2TI	001	007	For God gave us not a spirit of fearfulness; but of power and love and discipline.
055	2TI	001	008	Be not ashamed therefore of the testimony of our Lord, nor of me his prisoner: but suffer hardship with the gospel according to the power of God;
055	2TI	001	009	who saved us, and called us with a holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in Christ Jesus before times eternal,
055	2TI	001	010	but hath now been manifested by the appearing of our Saviour Christ Jesus, who abolished death, and brought life and incorruption to light through the gospel,
055	2TI	001	011	whereunto I was appointed a preacher, and an apostle, and a teacher.
055	2TI	001	012	For the which cause I suffer also these things: yet I am not ashamed; for I know him whom I have believed, and I am persuaded that he is able to guard that which I have committed unto him against that day.
055	2TI	001	013	Hold the pattern of sound words which thou hast heard from me, in faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.
055	2TI	001	014	That good thing which was committed unto [thee] guard through the Holy Ghost which dwelleth in us.
055	2TI	001	015	This thou knowest, that all that are in Asia turned away from me; of whom are Phygelus and Hermogenes.
055	2TI	001	016	The Lord grant mercy unto the house of Onesiphorus: for he oft refreshed me, and was not ashamed of my chain;
055	2TI	001	017	but, when he was in Rome, he sought me diligently, and found me
055	2TI	001	018	(the Lord grant unto him to find mercy of the Lord in that day); and in how many things he ministered at Ephesus, thou knowest very well.
055	2TI	002	001	Thou therefore, my child, be strengthened in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.
055	2TI	002	002	And the things which thou hast heard from me among many witnesses, the same commit thou to faithful men, who shall be able to teach others also.
055	2TI	002	003	Suffer hardship with [me], as a good soldier of Christ Jesus.
055	2TI	002	004	No soldier on service entangleth himself in the affairs of [this] life; that he may please him who enrolled him as a soldier.
055	2TI	002	005	And if also a man contend in the games, he is not crowned, except he have contended lawfully.
055	2TI	002	006	The husbandman that laboureth must be the first to partake of the fruits.
055	2TI	002	007	Consider what I say; for the Lord shall give thee understanding in all things.
055	2TI	002	008	Remember Jesus Christ, risen from the dead, of the seed of David, according to my gospel:
055	2TI	002	009	wherein I suffer hardship unto bonds, as a malefactor; but the word of God is not bound.
055	2TI	002	010	Therefore I endure all things for the elect’s sake, that they also may obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus with eternal glory.
055	2TI	002	011	Faithful is the saying: For if we died with him, we shall also live with him:
055	2TI	002	012	if we endure, we shall also reign with him: if we shall deny him, he also will deny us:
055	2TI	002	013	if we are faithless, he abideth faithful; for he cannot deny himself.
055	2TI	002	014	Of these things put them in remembrance, charging [them] in the sight of the Lord, that they strive not about words, to no profit, to the subverting of them that hear.
055	2TI	002	015	Give diligence to present thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, handling aright the word of truth.
055	2TI	002	016	But shun profane babblings: for they will proceed further in ungodliness,
055	2TI	002	017	and their word will eat as doth a gangrene: of whom is Hymenaeus and Philetus;
055	2TI	002	018	men who concerning the truth have erred, saying that the resurrection is past already, and overthrow the faith of some.
055	2TI	002	019	Howbeit the firm foundation of God standeth, having this seal, The Lord knoweth them that are his: and, Let every one that nameth the name of the Lord depart from unrighteousness.
055	2TI	002	020	Now in a great house there are not only vessels of gold and of silver, but also of wood and of earth; and some unto honour, and some unto dishonour.
055	2TI	002	021	If a man therefore purge himself from these, he shall be a vessel unto honour, sanctified, meet for the master’s use, prepared unto every good work.
055	2TI	002	022	But flee youthful lusts, and follow after righteousness, faith, love, peace, with them that call on the Lord out of a pure heart.
055	2TI	002	023	But foolish and ignorant questionings refuse, knowing that they gender strifes.
055	2TI	002	024	And the Lord’s servant must not strive, but be gentle towards all, apt to teach, forbearing,
055	2TI	002	025	in meekness correcting them that oppose themselves; if peradventure God may give them repentance unto the knowledge of the truth,
055	2TI	002	026	and they may recover themselves out of the snare of the devil, having been taken captive by the Lord’s servant unto the will of God.
055	2TI	003	001	But know this, that in the last days grievous times shall come.
055	2TI	003	002	For men shall be lovers of self, lovers of money, boastful, haughty, railers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,
055	2TI	003	003	without natural affection, implacable, slanderers, without self-control, fierce, no lovers of good,
055	2TI	003	004	traitors, headstrong, puffed up, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God;
055	2TI	003	005	holding a form of godliness, but having denied the power thereof: from these also turn away.
055	2TI	003	006	For of these are they that creep into houses, and take captive silly women laden with sins, led away by divers lusts,
055	2TI	003	007	ever learning, and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth.
055	2TI	003	008	And like as Jannes and Jambres withstood Moses, so do these also withstand the truth; men corrupted in mind, reprobate concerning the faith.
055	2TI	003	009	But they shall proceed no further: for their folly shall be evident unto all men, as theirs also came to be.
055	2TI	003	010	But thou didst follow my teaching, conduct, purpose, faith, longsuffering, love, patience,
055	2TI	003	011	persecutions, sufferings; what things befell me at Antioch, at Iconium, at Lystra; what persecutions I endured: and out of them all the Lord delivered me.
055	2TI	003	012	Yea, and all that would live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution.
055	2TI	003	013	But evil men and impostors shall wax worse and worse, deceiving and being deceived.
055	2TI	003	014	But abide thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them;
055	2TI	003	015	and that from a babe thou hast known the sacred writings which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus.
055	2TI	003	016	Every scripture inspired of God [is] also profitable for teaching, for reproof, for correction, for instruction which is in righteousness:
055	2TI	003	017	that the man of God may be complete, furnished completely unto every good work.
055	2TI	004	001	I charge [thee] in the sight of God, and of Christ Jesus, who shall judge the quick and the dead, and by his appearing and his kingdom;
055	2TI	004	002	preach the word; be instant in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort, with all longsuffering and teaching.
055	2TI	004	003	For the time will come when they will not endure the sound doctrine; but, having itching ears, will heap to themselves teachers after their own lusts;
055	2TI	004	004	and will turn away their ears from the truth, and turn aside unto fables.
055	2TI	004	005	But be thou sober in all things, suffer hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfill thy ministry.
055	2TI	004	006	For I am already being offered, and the time of my departure is come.
055	2TI	004	007	I have fought the good fight, I have finished the course, I have kept the faith:
055	2TI	004	008	henceforth there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous judge, shall give to me at that day: and not only to me, but also to all them that have loved his appearing.
055	2TI	004	009	Do thy diligence to come shortly unto me:
055	2TI	004	010	for Demas forsook me, having loved this present world, and went to Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus to Dalmatia.
055	2TI	004	011	Only Luke is with me. Take Mark, and bring him with thee: for he is useful to me for ministering.
055	2TI	004	012	But Tychicus I sent to Ephesus.
055	2TI	004	013	The cloke that I left at Troas with Carpus, bring when thou comest, and the books, especially the parchments.
055	2TI	004	014	Alexander the coppersmith did me much evil: the Lord will render to him according to his works:
055	2TI	004	015	of whom be thou ware also; for he greatly withstood our words.
055	2TI	004	016	At my first defence no one took my part, but all forsook me: may it not be laid to their account.
055	2TI	004	017	But the Lord stood by me, and strengthened me; that through me the message might be fully proclaimed, and that all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion.
055	2TI	004	018	The Lord will deliver me from every evil work, and will save me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom [be] the glory for ever and ever. Amen.
055	2TI	004	019	Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the house of Onesiphorus.
055	2TI	004	020	Erastus abode at Corinth: but Trophimus I left at Miletus sick.
055	2TI	004	021	Do thy diligence to come before winter. Eubulus saluteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren.
055	2TI	004	022	The Lord be with thy spirit. Grace be with you.
#
# BOOK	056	TIT	Titus	Titus
056	TIT	001	001	Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the knowledge of the truth which is according to godliness,
056	TIT	001	002	in hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before times eternal;
056	TIT	001	003	but in his own seasons manifested his word in the message, wherewith I was intrusted according to the commandment of God our Saviour;
056	TIT	001	004	to Titus, my true child after a common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Saviour.
056	TIT	001	005	For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that were wanting, and appoint elders in every city, as I gave thee charge;
056	TIT	001	006	if any man is blameless, the husband of one wife, having children that believe, who are not accused of riot or unruly.
056	TIT	001	007	For the bishop must be blameless, as God’s steward; not selfwilled, not soon angry, no brawler, no striker, not greedy of filthy lucre;
056	TIT	001	008	but given to hospitality, a lover of good, soberminded, just, holy, temperate;
056	TIT	001	009	holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching, that he may be able both to exhort in the sound doctrine, and to convict the gainsayers.
056	TIT	001	010	For there are many unruly men, vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision,
056	TIT	001	011	whose mouths must be stopped; men who overthrow whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake.
056	TIT	001	012	One of themselves, a prophet of their own, said, Cretans are alway liars, evil beasts, idle gluttons.
056	TIT	001	013	This testimony is true. For which cause reprove them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith,
056	TIT	001	014	not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men who turn away from the truth.
056	TIT	001	015	To the pure all things are pure: but to them that are defiled and unbelieving nothing is pure; but both their mind and their conscience are defiled.
056	TIT	001	016	They profess that they know God; but by their works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.
056	TIT	002	001	But speak thou the things which befit the sound doctrine:
056	TIT	002	002	that aged men be temperate, grave, soberminded, sound in faith, in love, in patience:
056	TIT	002	003	that aged women likewise be reverent in demeanour, not slanderers nor enslaved to much wine, teachers of that which is good;
056	TIT	002	004	that they may train the young women to love their husbands, to love their children,
056	TIT	002	005	[to be] soberminded, chaste, workers at home, kind, being in subjection to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed:
056	TIT	002	006	the younger men likewise exhort to be soberminded:
056	TIT	002	007	in all things shewing thyself an ensample of good works; in thy doctrine [shewing] uncorruptness, gravity,
056	TIT	002	008	sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of us.
056	TIT	002	009	[Exhort] servants to be in subjection to their own masters, [and] to be well-pleasing [to them] in all things; not gainsaying;
056	TIT	002	010	not purloining, but shewing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Saviour in all things.
056	TIT	002	011	For the grace of God hath appeared, bringing salvation to all men,
056	TIT	002	012	instructing us, to the intent that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly and righteously and godly in this present world;
056	TIT	002	013	looking for the blessed hope and appearing of the glory of our great God and Saviour Jesus Christ;
056	TIT	002	014	who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a people for his own possession, zealous of good works.
056	TIT	002	015	These things speak and exhort and reprove with all authority. Let no man despise thee.
056	TIT	003	001	Put them in mind to be in subjection to rulers, to authorities, to be obedient, to be ready unto every good work,
056	TIT	003	002	to speak evil of no man, not to be contentious, to be gentle, shewing all meekness toward all men.
056	TIT	003	003	For we also were aforetime foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, hating one another.
056	TIT	003	004	But when the kindness of God our Saviour, and his love toward man, appeared,
056	TIT	003	005	not by works [done] in righteousness, which we did ourselves, but according to his mercy he saved us, through the washing of regeneration and renewing of the Holy Ghost,
056	TIT	003	006	which he poured out upon us richly, through Jesus Christ our Saviour;
056	TIT	003	007	that, being justified by his grace, we might be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.
056	TIT	003	008	Faithful is the saying, and concerning these things I will that thou affirm confidently, to the end that they which have believed God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable unto men:
056	TIT	003	009	but shun foolish questionings, and genealogies, and strifes, and fightings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain.
056	TIT	003	010	A man that is heretical after a first and second admonition refuse;
056	TIT	003	011	knowing that such a one is perverted, and sinneth, being self-condemned.
056	TIT	003	012	When I shall send Artemas unto thee, or Tychicus, give diligence to come unto me to Nicopolis: for there I have determined to winter.
056	TIT	003	013	Set forward Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing be wanting unto them.
056	TIT	003	014	And let our [people] also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they be not unfruitful.
056	TIT	003	015	All that are with me salute thee. Salute them that love us in faith. Grace be with you all.
#
# BOOK	057	PHM	Philemon	Philemon
057	PHM	001	001	Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, to Philemon our beloved and fellow-worker,
057	PHM	001	002	and to Apphia our sister, and to Archippus our fellow-soldier, and to the church in thy house:
057	PHM	001	003	Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
057	PHM	001	004	I thank my God always, making mention of thee in my prayers,
057	PHM	001	005	hearing of thy love, and of the faith which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all the saints;
057	PHM	001	006	that the fellowship of thy faith may become effectual, in the knowledge of every good thing which is in you, unto Christ.
057	PHM	001	007	For I had much joy and comfort in thy love, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed through thee, brother.
057	PHM	001	008	Wherefore, though I have all boldness in Christ to enjoin thee that which is befitting,
057	PHM	001	009	yet for love’s sake I rather beseech, being such a one as Paul the aged, and now a prisoner also of Christ Jesus:
057	PHM	001	010	I beseech thee for my child, whom I have begotten in my bonds, Onesimus,
057	PHM	001	011	who was aforetime unprofitable to thee, but now is profitable to thee and to me:
057	PHM	001	012	whom I have sent back to thee in his own person, that is, my very heart:
057	PHM	001	013	whom I would fain have kept with me, that in thy behalf he might minister unto me in the bonds of the gospel:
057	PHM	001	014	but without thy mind I would do nothing; that thy goodness should not be as of necessity, but of free will.
057	PHM	001	015	For perhaps he was therefore parted [from thee] for a season, that thou shouldest have him for ever;
057	PHM	001	016	no longer as a servant, but more than a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much rather to thee, both in the flesh and in the Lord.
057	PHM	001	017	If then thou countest me a partner, receive him as myself.
057	PHM	001	018	But if he hath wronged thee at all, or oweth [thee] aught, put that to mine account;
057	PHM	001	019	I Paul write it with mine own hand, I will repay it: that I say not unto thee how that thou owest to me even thine own self besides.
057	PHM	001	020	Yea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my heart in Christ.
057	PHM	001	021	Having confidence in thine obedience I write unto thee, knowing that thou wilt do even beyond what I say.
057	PHM	001	022	But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I hope that through your prayers I shall be granted unto you.
057	PHM	001	023	Epaphras, my fellow-prisoner in Christ Jesus, saluteth thee;
057	PHM	001	024	[and so do] Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, Luke, my fellow-workers.
057	PHM	001	025	The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
#
# BOOK	058	HEB	Hebrews	Hebrews
058	HEB	001	001	God, having of old time spoken unto the fathers in the prophets by divers portions and in divers manners,
058	HEB	001	002	hath at the end of these days spoken unto us in [his] Son, whom he appointed heir of all things, through whom also he made the worlds;
058	HEB	001	003	who being the effulgence of his glory, and the very image of his substance, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had made purification of sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high;
058	HEB	001	004	having become by so much better than the angels, as he hath inherited a more excellent name than they.
058	HEB	001	005	For unto which of the angels said he at any time, Thou art my Son, This day have I begotten thee? and again, I will be to him a Father, And he shall be to me a Son?
058	HEB	001	006	And when he again bringeth in the firstborn into the world he saith, And let all the angels of God worship him.
058	HEB	001	007	And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels winds, And his ministers a flame of fire:
058	HEB	001	008	but of the Son [he saith], Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever; And the sceptre of uprightness is the sceptre of thy kingdom.
058	HEB	001	009	Thou hast loved righteousness, and hated iniquity; Therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee With the oil of gladness above thy fellows.
058	HEB	001	010	And, Thou, Lord, in the beginning hast laid the foundation of the earth, And the heavens are the works of thy hands:
058	HEB	001	011	They shall perish; but thou continuest: And they all shall wax old as doth a garment;
058	HEB	001	012	And as a mantle shalt thou roll them up, As a garment, and they shall be changed: But thou art the same, And thy years shall not fail.
058	HEB	001	013	But of which of the angels hath he said at any time, Sit thou on my right hand, Till I make thine enemies the footstool of thy feet?
058	HEB	001	014	Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to do service for the sake of them that shall inherit salvation?
058	HEB	002	001	Therefore we ought to give the more earnest heed to the things that were heard, lest haply we drift away [from them].
058	HEB	002	002	For if the word spoken through angels proved stedfast, and every transgression and disobedience received a just recompense of reward;
058	HEB	002	003	how shall we escape, if we neglect so great salvation? which having at the first been spoken through the Lord, was confirmed unto us by them that heard;
058	HEB	002	004	God also bearing witness with them, both by signs and wonders, and by manifold powers, and by gifts of the Holy Ghost, according to his own will.
058	HEB	002	005	For not unto angels did he subject the world to come, whereof we speak.
058	HEB	002	006	But one hath somewhere testified, saying, What is man, that thou art mindful of him? Or the son of man, that thou visitest him?
058	HEB	002	007	Thou madest him a little lower than the angels; Thou crownedst him with glory and honour, And didst set him over the works of thy hands:
058	HEB	002	008	Thou didst put all things in subjection under his feet. For in that he subjected all things unto him, he left nothing that is not subject to him. But now we see not yet all things subjected to him.
058	HEB	002	009	But we behold him who hath been made a little lower than the angels, [even] Jesus, because of the suffering of death crowned with glory and honour, that by the grace of God he should taste death for every [man].
058	HEB	002	010	For it became him, for whom are all things, and through whom are all things, in bringing many sons unto glory, to make the author of their salvation perfect through sufferings.
058	HEB	002	011	For both he that sanctifieth and they that are sanctified are all of one: for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren,
058	HEB	002	012	saying, I will declare thy name unto my brethren, In the midst of the congregation will I sing thy praise.
058	HEB	002	013	And again, I will put my trust in him. And again, Behold, I and the children which God hath given me.
058	HEB	002	014	Since then the children are sharers in flesh and blood, he also himself in like manner partook of the same; that through death he might bring to nought him that had the power of death, that is, the devil;
058	HEB	002	015	and might deliver all them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage.
058	HEB	002	016	For verily not of angels doth he take hold, but he taketh hold of the seed of Abraham.
058	HEB	002	017	Wherefore it behoved him in all things to be made like unto his brethren, that he might be a merciful and faithful high priest in things pertaining to God, to make propitiation for the sins of the people.
058	HEB	002	018	For in that he himself hath suffered being tempted, he is able to succour them that are tempted.
058	HEB	003	001	Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of a heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our confession, [even] Jesus;
058	HEB	003	002	who was faithful to him that appointed him, as also was Moses in all his house.
058	HEB	003	003	For he hath been counted worthy of more glory than Moses, by so much as he that built the house hath more honour than the house.
058	HEB	003	004	For every house is builded by some one; but he that built all things is God.
058	HEB	003	005	And Moses indeed was faithful in all his house as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were afterward to be spoken;
058	HEB	003	006	but Christ as a son, over his house; whose house are we, if we hold fast our boldness and the glorying of our hope firm unto the end.
058	HEB	003	007	Wherefore, even as the Holy Ghost saith, Today if ye shall hear his voice,
058	HEB	003	008	Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, Like as in the day of the temptation in the wilderness,
058	HEB	003	009	Wherewith your fathers tempted [me] by proving [me], And saw my works forty years.
058	HEB	003	010	Wherefore I was displeased with this generation, And said, They do alway err in their heart: But they did not know my ways;
058	HEB	003	011	As I sware in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.
058	HEB	003	012	Take heed, brethren, lest haply there shall be in any one of you an evil heart of unbelief, in falling away from the living God:
058	HEB	003	013	but exhort one another day by day, so long as it is called Today; lest any one of you be hardened by the deceitfulness of sin:
058	HEB	003	014	for we are become partakers of Christ, if we hold fast the beginning of our confidence firm unto the end:
058	HEB	003	015	while it is said, Today if ye shall hear his voice, Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation.
058	HEB	003	016	For who, when they heard, did provoke? nay, did not all they that came out of Egypt by Moses?
058	HEB	003	017	And with whom was he displeased forty years? was it not with them that sinned, whose carcases fell in the wilderness?
058	HEB	003	018	And to whom sware he that they should not enter into his rest, but to them that were disobedient?
058	HEB	003	019	And we see that they were not able to enter in because of unbelief.
058	HEB	004	001	Let us fear therefore, lest haply, a promise being left of entering into his rest, any one of you should seem to have come short of it.
058	HEB	004	002	For indeed we have had good tidings preached unto us, even as also they: but the word of hearing did not profit them, because they were not united by faith with them that heard.
058	HEB	004	003	For we which have believed do enter into that rest; even as he hath said, As I sware in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest: although the works were finished from the foundation of the world.
058	HEB	004	004	For he hath said somewhere of the seventh [day] on this wise, And God rested on the seventh day from all his works;
058	HEB	004	005	and in this [place] again, They shall not enter into my rest.
058	HEB	004	006	Seeing therefore it remaineth that some should enter thereinto, and they to whom the good tidings were before preached failed to enter in because of disobedience,
058	HEB	004	007	he again defineth a certain day, saying in David, after so long a time, Today, as it hath been before said, Today if ye shall hear his voice, Harden not your hearts.
058	HEB	004	008	For if Joshua had given them rest, he would not have spoken afterward of another day.
058	HEB	004	009	There remaineth therefore a sabbath rest for the people of God.
058	HEB	004	010	For he that is entered into his rest hath himself also rested from his works, as God did from his.
058	HEB	004	011	Let us therefore give diligence to enter into that rest, that no man fall after the same example of disobedience.
058	HEB	004	012	For the word of God is living, and active, and sharper than any two-edged sword, and piercing even to the dividing of soul and spirit, of both joints and marrow, and quick to discern the thoughts and intents of the heart.
058	HEB	004	013	And there is no creature that is not manifest in his sight: but all things are naked and laid open before the eyes of him with whom we have to do.
058	HEB	004	014	Having then a great high priest, who hath passed through the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold fast our confession.
058	HEB	004	015	For we have not a high priest that cannot be touched with the feeling of our infirmities; but one that hath been in all points tempted like as [we are, yet] without sin.
058	HEB	004	016	Let us therefore draw near with boldness unto the throne of grace, that we may receive mercy, and may find grace to help [us] in time of need.
058	HEB	005	001	For every high priest, being taken from among men, is appointed for men in things pertaining to God, that he may offer both gifts and sacrifices for sins:
058	HEB	005	002	who can bear gently with the ignorant and erring, for that he himself also is compassed with infirmity;
058	HEB	005	003	and by reason thereof is bound, as for the people, so also for himself, to offer for sins.
058	HEB	005	004	And no man taketh the honour unto himself, but when he is called of God, even as was Aaron.
058	HEB	005	005	So Christ also glorified not himself to be made a high priest, but he that spake unto him, Thou art my Son, This day have I begotten thee:
058	HEB	005	006	as he saith also in another [place], Thou art a priest for ever After the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	005	007	Who in the days of his flesh, having offered up prayers and supplications with strong crying and tears unto him that was able to save him from death, and having been heard for his godly fear,
058	HEB	005	008	though he was a Son, yet learned obedience by the things which he suffered;
058	HEB	005	009	and having been made perfect, he became unto all them that obey him the author of eternal salvation;
058	HEB	005	010	named of God a high priest after the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	005	011	Of whom we have many things to say, and hard of interpretation, seeing ye are become dull of hearing.
058	HEB	005	012	For when by reason of the time ye ought to be teachers, ye have need again that some one teach you the rudiments of the first principles of the oracles of God; and are become such as have need of milk, and not of solid food.
058	HEB	005	013	For every one that partaketh of milk is without experience of the word of righteousness; for he is a babe.
058	HEB	005	014	But solid food is for fullgrown men, [even] those who by reason of use have their senses exercised to discern good and evil.
058	HEB	006	001	Wherefore let us cease to speak of the first principles of Christ, and press on unto perfection; not laying again a foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith toward God,
058	HEB	006	002	of the teaching of baptisms, and of laying on of hands, and of resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment.
058	HEB	006	003	And this will we do, if God permit.
058	HEB	006	004	For as touching those who were once enlightened and tasted of the heavenly gift, and were made partakers of the Holy Ghost,
058	HEB	006	005	and tasted the good word of God, and the powers of the age to come,
058	HEB	006	006	and [then] fell away, it is impossible to renew them again unto repentance; seeing they crucify to themselves the Son of God afresh, and put him to an open shame.
058	HEB	006	007	For the land which hath drunk the rain that cometh oft upon it, and bringeth forth herbs meet for them for whose sake it is also tilled, receiveth blessing from God:
058	HEB	006	008	but if it beareth thorns and thistles, it is rejected and nigh unto a curse; whose end is to be burned.
058	HEB	006	009	But, beloved, we are persuaded better things of you, and things that accompany salvation, though we thus speak:
058	HEB	006	010	for God is not unrighteous to forget your work and the love which ye shewed toward his name, in that ye ministered unto the saints, and still do minister.
058	HEB	006	011	And we desire that each one of you may shew the same diligence unto the fulness of hope even to the end:
058	HEB	006	012	that ye be not sluggish, but imitators of them who through faith and patience inherit the promises.
058	HEB	006	013	For when God made promise to Abraham, since he could swear by none greater, he sware by himself,
058	HEB	006	014	saying, Surely blessing I will bless thee, and multiplying I will multiply thee.
058	HEB	006	015	And thus, having patiently endured, he obtained the promise.
058	HEB	006	016	For men swear by the greater: and in every dispute of theirs the oath is final for confirmation.
058	HEB	006	017	Wherein God, being minded to shew more abundantly unto the heirs of the promise the immutability of his counsel, interposed with an oath:
058	HEB	006	018	that by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we may have a strong encouragement, who have fled for refuge to lay hold of the hope set before us;
058	HEB	006	019	which we have as an anchor of the soul, [a hope] both sure and stedfast and entering into that which is within the veil;
058	HEB	006	020	whither as a forerunner Jesus entered for us, having become a high priest for ever after the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	007	001	For this Melchizedek, king of Salem, priest of God Most High, who met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings, and blessed him,
058	HEB	007	002	to whom also Abraham divided a tenth part of all (being first, by interpretation, King of righteousness, and then also King of Salem, which is, King of peace;
058	HEB	007	003	without father, without mother, without genealogy, having neither beginning of days nor end of life, but made like unto the Son of God), abideth a priest continually.
058	HEB	007	004	Now consider how great this man was, unto whom Abraham, the patriarch, gave a tenth out of the chief spoils.
058	HEB	007	005	And they indeed of the sons of Levi that receive the priest’s office have commandment to take tithes of the people according to the law, that is, of their brethren, though these have come out of the loins of Abraham:
058	HEB	007	006	but he whose genealogy is not counted from them hath taken tithes of Abraham, and hath blessed him that hath the promises.
058	HEB	007	007	But without any dispute the less is blessed of the better.
058	HEB	007	008	And here men that die receive tithes; but there one, of whom it is witnessed that he liveth.
058	HEB	007	009	And, so to say, through Abraham even Levi, who receiveth tithes, hath paid tithes;
058	HEB	007	010	for he was yet in the loins of his father, when Melchizedek met him.
058	HEB	007	011	Now if there was perfection through the Levitical priesthood (for under it hath the people received the law), what further need [was there] that another priest should arise after the order of Melchizedek, and not be reckoned after the order of Aaron?
058	HEB	007	012	For the priesthood being changed, there is made of necessity a change also of the law.
058	HEB	007	013	For he of whom these things are said belongeth to another tribe, from which no man hath given attendance at the altar.
058	HEB	007	014	For it is evident that our Lord hath sprung out of Judah; as to which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priests.
058	HEB	007	015	And [what we say] is yet more abundantly evident, if after the likeness of Melchizedek there ariseth another priest,
058	HEB	007	016	who hath been made, not after the law of a carnal commandment, but after the power of an endless life:
058	HEB	007	017	for it is witnessed [of him], Thou art a priest for ever After the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	007	018	For there is a disannulling of a foregoing commandment because of its weakness and unprofitableness
058	HEB	007	019	(for the law made nothing perfect), and a bringing in thereupon of a better hope, through which we draw nigh unto God.
058	HEB	007	020	And inasmuch as [it is] not without the taking of an oath
058	HEB	007	021	(for they indeed have been made priests without an oath; but he with an oath by him that saith of him, The Lord sware and will not repent himself, Thou art a priest for ever);
058	HEB	007	022	by so much also hath Jesus become the surety of a better covenant.
058	HEB	007	023	And they indeed have been made priests many in number, because that by death they are hindered from continuing:
058	HEB	007	024	but he, because he abideth for ever, hath his priesthood unchangeable.
058	HEB	007	025	Wherefore also he is able to save to the uttermost them that draw near unto God through him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.
058	HEB	007	026	For such a high priest became us, holy, guileless, undefiled, separated from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;
058	HEB	007	027	who needeth not daily, like those high priests, to offer up sacrifices, first for his own sins, and then for the [sins] of the people: for this he did once for all, when he offered up himself.
058	HEB	007	028	For the law appointeth men high priests, having infirmity; but the word of the oath, which was after the law, [appointeth] a Son, perfected for evermore.
058	HEB	008	001	Now in the things which we are saying the chief point [is this]: We have such a high priest, who sat down on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens,
058	HEB	008	002	a minister of the sanctuary, and of the true tabernacle, which the Lord pitched, not man.
058	HEB	008	003	For every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices: wherefore it is necessary that this [high priest] also have somewhat to offer.
058	HEB	008	004	Now if he were on earth, he would not be a priest at all, seeing there are those who offer the gifts according to the law;
058	HEB	008	005	who serve [that which is] a copy and shadow of the heavenly things, even as Moses is warned [of God] when he is about to make the tabernacle: for, See, saith he, that thou make all things according to the pattern that was shewed thee in the mount.
058	HEB	008	006	But now hath he obtained a ministry the more excellent, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which hath been enacted upon better promises.
058	HEB	008	007	For if that first [covenant] had been faultless, then would no place have been sought for a second.
058	HEB	008	008	For finding fault with them, he saith, Behold, the days come, saith the Lord, That I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah;
058	HEB	008	009	Not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers In the day that I took them by the hand to lead them forth out of the land of Egypt; For they continued not in my covenant, And I regarded them not, saith the Lord.
058	HEB	008	010	For this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel After those days, saith the Lord; I will put my laws into their mind, And on their heart also will I write them: And I will be to them a God, And they shall be to me a people:
058	HEB	008	011	And they shall not teach every man his fellow-citizen, And every man his brother, saying, Know the Lord: For all shall know me, From the least to the greatest of them.
058	HEB	008	012	For I will be merciful to their iniquities, And their sins will I remember no more.
058	HEB	008	013	In that he saith, A new [covenant], he hath made the first old. But that which is becoming old and waxeth aged is nigh unto vanishing away.
058	HEB	009	001	Now even the first [covenant] had ordinances of divine service, and its sanctuary, [a sanctuary] of this world.
058	HEB	009	002	For there was a tabernacle prepared, the first, wherein [were] the candlestick, and the table, and the shewbread; which is called the Holy place.
058	HEB	009	003	And after the second veil, the tabernacle which is called the Holy of holies;
058	HEB	009	004	having a golden censer, and the ark of the covenant overlaid round about with gold, wherein [was] a golden pot holding the manna, and Aaron’s rod that budded, and the tables of the covenant;
058	HEB	009	005	and above it cherubim of glory overshadowing the mercy-seat; of which things we cannot now speak severally.
058	HEB	009	006	Now these things having been thus prepared, the priests go in continually into the first tabernacle, accomplishing the services;
058	HEB	009	007	but into the second the high priest alone, once in the year, not without blood, which he offereth for himself, and for the errors of the people:
058	HEB	009	008	the Holy Ghost this signifying, that the way into the holy place hath not yet been made manifest, while as the first tabernacle is yet standing;
058	HEB	009	009	which [is] a parable for the time [now] present; according to which are offered both gifts and sacrifices that cannot, as touching the conscience, make the worshipper perfect,
058	HEB	009	010	[being] only (with meats and drinks and divers washings) carnal ordinances, imposed until a time of reformation.
058	HEB	009	011	But Christ having come a high priest of the good things to come, through the greater and more perfect tabernacle, not made with hands, that is to say, not of this creation,
058	HEB	009	012	nor yet through the blood of goats and calves, but through his own blood, entered in once for all into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption.
058	HEB	009	013	For if the blood of goats and bulls, and the ashes of a heifer sprinkling them that have been defiled, sanctify unto the cleanness of the flesh:
058	HEB	009	014	how much more shall the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without blemish unto God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?
058	HEB	009	015	And for this cause he is the mediator of a new covenant, that a death having taken place for the redemption of the transgressions that were under the first covenant, they that have been called may receive the promise of the eternal inheritance.
058	HEB	009	016	For where a testament is, there must of necessity be the death of him that made it.
058	HEB	009	017	For a testament is of force where there hath been death: for doth it ever avail while he that made it liveth?
058	HEB	009	018	Wherefore even the first [covenant] hath not been dedicated without blood.
058	HEB	009	019	For when every commandment had been spoken by Moses unto all the people according to the law, he took the blood of the calves and the goats, with water and scarlet wool and hyssop, and sprinkled both the book itself, and all the people,
058	HEB	009	020	saying, This is the blood of the covenant which God commanded to you-ward.
058	HEB	009	021	Moreover the tabernacle and all the vessels of the ministry he sprinkled in like manner with the blood.
058	HEB	009	022	And according to the law, I may almost say, all things are cleansed with blood, and apart from shedding of blood there is no remission.
058	HEB	009	023	It was necessary therefore that the copies of the things in the heavens should be cleansed with these; but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these.
058	HEB	009	024	For Christ entered not into a holy place made with hands, like in pattern to the true; but into heaven itself, now to appear before the face of God for us:
058	HEB	009	025	nor yet that he should offer himself often; as the high priest entereth into the holy place year by year with blood not his own;
058	HEB	009	026	else must he often have suffered since the foundation of the world: but now once at the end of the ages hath he been manifested to put away sin by the sacrifice of himself.
058	HEB	009	027	And inasmuch as it is appointed unto men once to die, and after this [cometh] judgment;
058	HEB	009	028	so Christ also, having been once offered to bear the sins of many, shall appear a second time, apart from sin, to them that wait for him, unto salvation.
058	HEB	010	001	For the law having a shadow of the good [things] to come, not the very image of the things, they can never with the same sacrifices year by year, which they offer continually, make perfect them that draw nigh.
058	HEB	010	002	Else would they not have ceased to be offered, because the worshippers, having been once cleansed, would have had no more conscience of sins?
058	HEB	010	003	But in those [sacrifices] there is a remembrance made of sins year by year.
058	HEB	010	004	For it is impossible that the blood of bulls and goats should take away sins.
058	HEB	010	005	Wherefore when he cometh into the world, he saith, Sacrifice and offering thou wouldest not, But a body didst thou prepare for me;
058	HEB	010	006	In whole burnt offerings and [sacrifices] for sin thou hadst no pleasure:
058	HEB	010	007	Then said I, Lo, I am come (In the roll of the book it is written of me) To do thy will, O God.
058	HEB	010	008	Saying above, Sacrifices and offerings and whole burnt offerings and [sacrifices] for sin thou wouldest not, neither hadst pleasure therein (the which are offered according to the law),
058	HEB	010	009	then hath he said, Lo, I am come to do thy will. He taketh away the first, that he may establish the second.
058	HEB	010	010	By which will we have been sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.
058	HEB	010	011	And every priest indeed standeth day by day ministering and offering oftentimes the same sacrifices, the which can never take away sins:
058	HEB	010	012	but he, when he had offered one sacrifice for sins for ever, sat down on the right hand of God;
058	HEB	010	013	from henceforth expecting till his enemies be made the footstool of his feet.
058	HEB	010	014	For by one offering he hath perfected for ever them that are sanctified.
058	HEB	010	015	And the Holy Ghost also beareth witness to us: for after he hath said,
058	HEB	010	016	This is the covenant that I will make with them After those days, saith the Lord; I will put my laws on their heart, And upon their mind also will I write them; [then saith he],
058	HEB	010	017	And their sins and their iniquities will I remember no more.
058	HEB	010	018	Now where remission of these is, there is no more offering for sin.
058	HEB	010	019	Having therefore, brethren, boldness to enter into the holy place by the blood of Jesus,
058	HEB	010	020	by the way which he dedicated for us, a new and living way, through the veil, that is to say, his flesh;
058	HEB	010	021	and [having] a great priest over the house of God;
058	HEB	010	022	let us draw near with a true heart in fulness of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience, and our body washed with pure water:
058	HEB	010	023	let us hold fast the confession of our hope that it waver not; for he is faithful that promised:
058	HEB	010	024	and let us consider one another to provoke unto love and good works;
058	HEB	010	025	not forsaking the assembling of ourselves together, as the custom of some is, but exhorting [one another]; and so much the more, as ye see the day drawing nigh.
058	HEB	010	026	For if we sin wilfully after that we have received the knowledge of the truth, there remaineth no more a sacrifice for sins,
058	HEB	010	027	but a certain fearful expectation of judgment, and a fierceness of fire which shall devour the adversaries.
058	HEB	010	028	A man that hath set at nought Moses’ law dieth without compassion on [the word of] two or three witnesses:
058	HEB	010	029	of how much sorer punishment, think ye, shall he be judged worthy, who hath trodden under foot the Son of God, and hath counted the blood of the covenant, wherewith he was sanctified, an unholy thing, and hath done despite unto the Spirit of grace?
058	HEB	010	030	For we know him that said, Vengeance belongeth unto me, I will recompense. And again, The Lord shall judge his people.
058	HEB	010	031	It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.
058	HEB	010	032	But call to remembrance the former days, in which, after ye were enlightened, ye endured a great conflict of sufferings;
058	HEB	010	033	partly, being made a gazingstock both by reproaches and afflictions; and partly, becoming partakers with them that were so used.
058	HEB	010	034	For ye both had compassion on them that were in bonds, and took joyfully the spoiling of your possessions, knowing that ye yourselves have a better possession and an abiding one.
058	HEB	010	035	Cast not away therefore your boldness, which hath great recompense of reward.
058	HEB	010	036	For ye have need of patience, that, having done the will of God, ye may receive the promise.
058	HEB	010	037	For yet a very little while, He that cometh shall come, and shall not tarry.
058	HEB	010	038	But my righteous one shall live by faith: And if he shrink back, my soul hath no pleasure in him.
058	HEB	010	039	But we are not of them that shrink back unto perdition; but of them that have faith unto the saving of the soul.
058	HEB	011	001	Now faith is the assurance of [things] hoped for, the proving of things not seen.
058	HEB	011	002	For therein the elders had witness borne to them.
058	HEB	011	003	By faith we understand that the worlds have been framed by the word of God, so that what is seen hath not been made out of things which do appear.
058	HEB	011	004	By faith Abel offered unto God a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, through which he had witness borne to him that he was righteous, God bearing witness in respect of his gifts: and through it he being dead yet speaketh.
058	HEB	011	005	By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and he was not found, because God translated him: for before his translation he hath had witness borne to him that he had been well-pleasing unto God:
058	HEB	011	006	And without faith it is impossible to be well-pleasing [unto him]: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and [that] he is a rewarder of them that seek after him.
058	HEB	011	007	By faith Noah, being warned [of God] concerning things not seen as yet, moved with godly fear, prepared an ark to the saving of his house; through which he condemned the world, and became heir of the righteousness which is according to faith.
058	HEB	011	008	By faith Abraham, when he was called, obeyed to go out unto a place which he was to receive for an inheritance; and he went out, not knowing whither he went.
058	HEB	011	009	By faith he became a sojourner in the land of promise, as in a [land] not his own, dwelling in tents, with Isaac and Jacob, the heirs with him of the same promise:
058	HEB	011	010	for he looked for the city which hath the foundations, whose builder and maker is God.
058	HEB	011	011	By faith even Sarah herself received power to conceive seed when she was past age, since she counted him faithful who had promised:
058	HEB	011	012	wherefore also there sprang of one, and him as good as dead, [so many] as the stars of heaven in multitude, and as the sand, which is by the sea shore, innumerable.
058	HEB	011	013	These all died in faith, not having received the promises, but having seen them and greeted them from afar, and having confessed that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth.
058	HEB	011	014	For they that say such things make it manifest that they are seeking after a country of their own.
058	HEB	011	015	And if indeed they had been mindful of that [country] from which they went out, they would have had opportunity to return.
058	HEB	011	016	But now they desire a better [country], that is, a heavenly: wherefore God is not ashamed of them, to be called their God: for he hath prepared for them a city.
058	HEB	011	017	By faith Abraham, being tried, offered up Isaac: yea, he that had gladly received the promises was offering up his only begotten [son];
058	HEB	011	018	[even he] to whom it was said, In Isaac shall thy seed be called:
058	HEB	011	019	accounting that God [is] able to raise up, even from the dead; from whence he did also in a parable receive him back.
058	HEB	011	020	By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau, even concerning things to come.
058	HEB	011	021	By faith Jacob, when he was a dying, blessed each of the sons of Joseph; and worshipped, [leaning] upon the top of his staff.
058	HEB	011	022	By faith Joseph, when his end was nigh, made mention of the departure of the children of Israel; and gave commandment concerning his bones.
058	HEB	011	023	By faith Moses, when he was born, was hid three months by his parents, because they saw he was a goodly child; and they were not afraid of the king’s commandment.
058	HEB	011	024	By faith Moses, when he was grown up, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh’s daughter;
058	HEB	011	025	choosing rather to be evil entreated with the people of God, than to enjoy the pleasures of sin for a season;
058	HEB	011	026	accounting the reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures of Egypt: for he looked unto the recompense of reward.
058	HEB	011	027	By faith he forsook Egypt, not fearing the wrath of the king: for he endured, as seeing him who is invisible.
058	HEB	011	028	By faith he kept the passover, and the sprinkling of the blood, that the destroyer of the firstborn should not touch them.
058	HEB	011	029	By faith they passed through the Red sea as by dry land: which the Egyptians assaying to do were swallowed up.
058	HEB	011	030	By faith the walls of Jericho fell down, after they had been compassed about for seven days.
058	HEB	011	031	By faith Rahab the harlot perished not with them that were disobedient, having received the spies with peace.
058	HEB	011	032	And what shall I more say? for the time will fail me if I tell of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah; of David and Samuel and the prophets:
058	HEB	011	033	who through faith subdued kingdoms, wrought righteousness, obtained promises, stopped the mouths of lions,
058	HEB	011	034	quenched the power of fire, escaped the edge of the sword, from weakness were made strong, waxed mighty in war, turned to flight armies of aliens.
058	HEB	011	035	Women received their dead by a resurrection: and others were tortured, not accepting their deliverance; that they might obtain a better resurrection:
058	HEB	011	036	and others had trial of mockings and scourgings, yea, moreover of bonds and imprisonment:
058	HEB	011	037	they were stoned, they were sawn asunder, they were tempted, they were slain with the sword: they went about in sheepskins, in goatskins; being destitute, afflicted, evil entreated
058	HEB	011	038	(of whom the world was not worthy), wandering in deserts and mountains and caves, and the holes of the earth.
058	HEB	011	039	And these all, having had witness borne to them through their faith, received not the promise,
058	HEB	011	040	God having provided some better thing concerning us, that apart from us they should not be made perfect.
058	HEB	012	001	Therefore let us also, seeing we are compassed about with so great a cloud of witnesses, lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily beset us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us,
058	HEB	012	002	looking unto Jesus the author and perfecter of [our] faith, who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising shame, and hath sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.
058	HEB	012	003	For consider him that hath endured such gainsaying of sinners against themselves, that ye wax not weary, fainting in your souls.
058	HEB	012	004	Ye have not yet resisted unto blood, striving against sin:
058	HEB	012	005	and ye have forgotten the exhortation, which reasoneth with you as with sons, My son, regard not lightly the chastening of the Lord, Nor faint when thou art reproved of him;
058	HEB	012	006	For whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth, And scourgeth every son whom he receiveth.
058	HEB	012	007	It is for chastening that ye endure; God dealeth with you as with sons; for what son is there whom [his] father chasteneth not?
058	HEB	012	008	But if ye are without chastening, whereof all have been made partakers, then are ye bastards, and not sons.
058	HEB	012	009	Furthermore, we had the fathers of our flesh to chasten us, and we gave them reverence: shall we not much rather be in subjection unto the Father of spirits, and live?
058	HEB	012	010	For they verily for a few days chastened [us] as seemed good to them; but he for [our] profit, that [we] may be partakers of his holiness.
058	HEB	012	011	All chastening seemeth for the present to be not joyous, but grievous: yet afterward it yieldeth peaceable fruit unto them that have been exercised thereby, [even the fruit] of righteousness.
058	HEB	012	012	Wherefore lift up the hands that hang down, and the palsied knees;
058	HEB	012	013	and make straight paths for your feet, that that which is lame be not turned out of the way, but rather be healed.
058	HEB	012	014	Follow after peace with all men, and the sanctification without which no man shall see the Lord:
058	HEB	012	015	looking carefully lest [there be] any man that falleth short of the grace of God; lest any root of bitterness springing up trouble [you], and thereby the many be defiled;
058	HEB	012	016	lest [there be] any fornicator, or profane person, as Esau, who for one mess of meat sold his own birthright.
058	HEB	012	017	For ye know that even when he afterward desired to inherit the blessing, he was rejected (for he found no place of repentance), though he sought it diligently with tears.
058	HEB	012	018	For ye are not come unto [a mount] that might be touched, and that burned with fire, and unto blackness, and darkness, and tempest,
058	HEB	012	019	and the sound of a trumpet, and the voice of words; which [voice] they that heard entreated that no word more should be spoken unto them:
058	HEB	012	020	for they could not endure that which was enjoined, If even a beast touch the mountain, it shall be stoned;
058	HEB	012	021	and so fearful was the appearance, [that] Moses said, I exceedingly fear and quake:
058	HEB	012	022	but ye are come unto mount Zion, and unto the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to innumerable hosts of angels,
058	HEB	012	023	to the general assembly and church of the firstborn who are enrolled in heaven, and to God the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect,
058	HEB	012	024	and to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling that speaketh better than [that of] Abel.
058	HEB	012	025	See that ye refuse not him that speaketh. For if they escaped not, when they refused him that warned [them] on earth, much more [shall not] we [escape], who turn away from him that [warneth] from heaven:
058	HEB	012	026	whose voice then shook the earth: but now he hath promised, saying, Yet once more will I make to tremble not the earth only, but also the heaven.
058	HEB	012	027	And this [word], Yet once more, signifieth the removing of those things that are shaken, as of things that have been made, that those things which are not shaken may remain.
058	HEB	012	028	Wherefore, receiving a kingdom that cannot be shaken, let us have grace, whereby we may offer service well-pleasing to God with reverence and awe:
058	HEB	012	029	for our God is a consuming fire.
058	HEB	013	001	Let love of the brethren continue.
058	HEB	013	002	Forget not to shew love unto strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares.
058	HEB	013	003	Remember them that are in bonds, as bound with them; them that are evil entreated, as being yourselves also in the body.
058	HEB	013	004	[Let] marriage [be] had in honour among all, and [let] the bed [be] undefiled: for fornicators and adulterers God will judge.
058	HEB	013	005	Be ye free from the love of money; content with such things as ye have: for himself hath said, I will in no wise fail thee, neither will I in any wise forsake thee.
058	HEB	013	006	So that with good courage we say, The Lord is my helper; I will not fear: What shall man do unto me?
058	HEB	013	007	Remember them that had the rule over you, which spake unto you the word of God; and considering the issue of their life, imitate their faith.
058	HEB	013	008	Jesus Christ [is] the same yesterday and today, [yea] and for ever.
058	HEB	013	009	Be not carried away by divers and strange teachings: for it is good that the heart be stablished by grace; not by meats, wherein they that occupied themselves were not profited.
058	HEB	013	010	We have an altar, whereof they have no right to eat which serve the tabernacle.
058	HEB	013	011	For the bodies of those beasts, whose blood is brought into the holy place by the high priest [as an offering] for sin, are burned without the camp.
058	HEB	013	012	Wherefore Jesus also, that he might sanctify the people through his own blood, suffered without the gate.
058	HEB	013	013	Let us therefore go forth unto him without the camp, bearing his reproach.
058	HEB	013	014	For we have not here an abiding city, but we seek after [the city] which is to come.
058	HEB	013	015	Through him then let us offer up a sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of lips which make confession to his name.
058	HEB	013	016	But to do good and to communicate forget not: for with such sacrifices God is well pleased.
058	HEB	013	017	Obey them that have the rule over you, and submit [to them]: for they watch in behalf of your souls, as they that shall give account; that they may do this with joy, and not with grief: for this [were] unprofitable for you.
058	HEB	013	018	Pray for us: for we are persuaded that we have a good conscience, desiring to live honestly in all things.
058	HEB	013	019	And I exhort [you] the more exceedingly to do this, that I may be restored to you the sooner.
058	HEB	013	020	Now the God of peace, who brought again from the dead the great shepherd of the sheep with the blood of the eternal covenant, [even] our Lord Jesus,
058	HEB	013	021	make you perfect in every good thing to do his will, working in us that which is well-pleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ; to whom [be] the glory for ever and ever. Amen.
058	HEB	013	022	But I exhort you, brethren, bear with the word of exhortation: for I have written unto you in few words.
058	HEB	013	023	Know ye that our brother Timothy hath been set at liberty; with whom, if he come shortly, I will see you.
058	HEB	013	024	Salute all them that have the rule over you, and all the saints. They of Italy salute you.
058	HEB	013	025	Grace be with you all. Amen.
