# BOOK	059	JAM	James	James
059	JAM	001	001	James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are of the Dispersion, greeting.
059	JAM	001	002	Count it all joy, my brethren, when ye fall into manifold temptations;
059	JAM	001	003	Knowing that the proof of your faith worketh patience.
059	JAM	001	004	And let patience have [its] perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, lacking in nothing.
059	JAM	001	005	But if any of you lacketh wisdom, let him ask of God, who giveth to all liberally and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.
059	JAM	001	006	But let him ask in faith, nothing doubting: for he that doubteth is like the surge of the sea driven by the wind and tossed.
059	JAM	001	007	For let not that man think that he shall receive anything of the Lord;
059	JAM	001	008	a doubleminded man, unstable in all his ways.
059	JAM	001	009	But let the brother of low degree glory in his high estate:
059	JAM	001	010	and the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away.
059	JAM	001	011	For the sun ariseth with the scorching wind, and withereth the grass; and the flower thereof falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his goings.
059	JAM	001	012	Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he hath been approved, he shall receive the crown of life, which [the Lord] promised to them that love him.
059	JAM	001	013	Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, and he himself tempteth no man:
059	JAM	001	014	but each man is tempted, when he is drawn away by his own lust, and enticed.
059	JAM	001	015	Then the lust, when it hath conceived, beareth sin: and the sin, when it is fullgrown, bringeth forth death.
059	JAM	001	016	Be not deceived, my beloved brethren.
059	JAM	001	017	Every good gift and every perfect boon is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, with whom can be no variation, neither shadow that is cast by turning.
059	JAM	001	018	Of his own will he brought us forth by the word of truth, that we should be a kind of firstfruits of his creatures.
059	JAM	001	019	Ye know [this], my beloved brethren. But let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:
059	JAM	001	020	for the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God.
059	JAM	001	021	Wherefore putting away all filthiness and overflowing of wickedness, receive with meekness the implanted word, which is able to save your souls.
059	JAM	001	022	But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deluding your own selves.
059	JAM	001	023	For if any one is a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a mirror:
059	JAM	001	024	for he beholdeth himself, and goeth away, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was.
059	JAM	001	025	But he that looketh into the perfect law, the [law] of liberty, and [so] continueth, being not a hearer that forgetteth, but a doer that worketh, this man shall be blessed in his doing.
059	JAM	001	026	If any man thinketh himself to be religious, while he bridleth not his tongue but deceiveth his heart, this man’s religion is vain.
059	JAM	001	027	Pure religion and undefiled before our God and Father is this, to visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, [and] to keep himself unspotted from the world.
059	JAM	002	001	My brethren, hold not the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, [the Lord] of glory, with respect of persons.
059	JAM	002	002	For if there come into your synagogue a man with a gold ring, in fine clothing, and there come in also a poor man in vile clothing;
059	JAM	002	003	and ye have regard to him that weareth the fine clothing, and say, Sit thou here in a good place; and ye say to the poor man, Stand thou there, or sit under my footstool;
059	JAM	002	004	are ye not divided in your own mind, and become judges with evil thoughts?
059	JAM	002	005	Hearken, my beloved brethren; did not God choose them that are poor as to the world [to be] rich in faith, and heirs of the kingdom which he promised to them that love him?
059	JAM	002	006	But ye have dishonoured the poor man. Do not the rich oppress you, and themselves drag you before the judgment-seats?
059	JAM	002	007	Do not they blaspheme the honourable name by the which ye are called?
059	JAM	002	008	Howbeit if ye fulfill the royal law, according to the scripture, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself, ye do well:
059	JAM	002	009	but if ye have respect of persons, ye commit sin, being convicted by the law as transgressors.
059	JAM	002	010	For whosoever shall keep the whole law, and yet stumble in one [point], he is become guilty of all.
059	JAM	002	011	For he that said, Do not commit adultery, said also, Do not kill. Now if thou dost not commit adultery, but killest, thou art become a transgressor of the law.
059	JAM	002	012	So speak ye, and so do, as men that are to be judged by a law of liberty.
059	JAM	002	013	For judgment [is] without mercy to him that hath shewed no mercy: mercy glorieth against judgment.
059	JAM	002	014	What doth it profit, my brethren, if a man say he hath faith, but have not works? can that faith save him?
059	JAM	002	015	If a brother or sister be naked, and in lack of daily food,
059	JAM	002	016	and one of you say unto them, Go in peace, be ye warmed and filled; and yet ye give them not the things needful to the body; what doth it profit?
059	JAM	002	017	Even so faith, if it have not works, is dead in itself.
059	JAM	002	018	Yea, a man will say, Thou hast faith, and I have works: shew me thy faith apart from [thy] works, and I by my works will shew thee [my] faith.
059	JAM	002	019	Thou believest that God is one; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and shudder.
059	JAM	002	020	But wilt thou know, O vain man, that faith apart from works is barren?
059	JAM	002	021	Was not Abraham our father justified by works, in that he offered up Isaac his son upon the altar?
059	JAM	002	022	Thou seest that faith wrought with his works, and by works was faith made perfect;
059	JAM	002	023	and the scripture was fulfilled which saith, And Abraham believed God, and it was reckoned unto him for righteousness; and he was called the friend of God.
059	JAM	002	024	Ye see that by works a man is justified, and not only by faith.
059	JAM	002	025	And in like manner was not also Rahab the harlot justified by works, in that she received the messengers, and sent them out another way?
059	JAM	002	026	For as the body apart from the spirit is dead, even so faith apart from works is dead.
059	JAM	003	001	Be not many teachers, my brethren, knowing that we shall receive heavier judgment.
059	JAM	003	002	For in many things we all stumble. If any stumbleth not in word, the same is a perfect man, able to bridle the whole body also.
059	JAM	003	003	Now if we put the horses’ bridles into their mouths, that they may obey us, we turn about their whole body also.
059	JAM	003	004	Behold, the ships also, though they are so great, and are driven by rough winds, are yet turned about by a very small rudder, whither the impulse of the steersman willeth.
059	JAM	003	005	So the tongue also is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how much wood is kindled by how small a fire!
059	JAM	003	006	And the tongue is a fire: the world of iniquity among our members is the tongue, which defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the wheel of nature, and is set on fire by hell.
059	JAM	003	007	For every kind of beasts and birds, of creeping things and things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed by mankind:
059	JAM	003	008	but the tongue can no man tame; [it is] a restless evil, [it is] full of deadly poison.
059	JAM	003	009	Therewith bless we the Lord and Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the likeness of God:
059	JAM	003	010	out of the same mouth cometh forth blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not so to be.
059	JAM	003	011	Doth the fountain send forth from the same opening sweet [water] and bitter?
059	JAM	003	012	Can a fig tree, my brethren, yield olives, or a vine figs? neither [can] salt water yield sweet.
059	JAM	003	013	Who is wise and understanding among you? let him shew by his good life his works in meekness of wisdom.
059	JAM	003	014	But if ye have bitter jealousy and faction in your heart, glory not and lie not against the truth.
059	JAM	003	015	This wisdom is not [a wisdom] that cometh down from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish.
059	JAM	003	016	For where jealousy and faction are, there is confusion and every vile deed.
059	JAM	003	017	But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, easy to be entreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without variance, without hypocrisy.
059	JAM	003	018	And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace for them that make peace.
059	JAM	004	001	Whence [come] wars and whence [come] fightings among you? [come they] not hence, [even] of your pleasures that war in your members?
059	JAM	004	002	Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and covet, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war; ye have not, because ye ask not.
059	JAM	004	003	Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may spend [it] in your pleasures.
059	JAM	004	004	Ye adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? Whosoever therefore would be a friend of the world maketh himself an enemy of God.
059	JAM	004	005	Or think ye that the scripture speaketh in vain? Doth the spirit which he made to dwell in us long unto envying?
059	JAM	004	006	But he giveth more grace. Wherefore [the scripture] saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace to the humble.
059	JAM	004	007	Be subject therefore unto God; but resist the devil, and he will flee from you.
059	JAM	004	008	Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye doubleminded.
059	JAM	004	009	Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness.
059	JAM	004	010	Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall exalt you.
059	JAM	004	011	Speak not one against another, brethren. He that speaketh against a brother, or judgeth his brother, speaketh against the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judgest the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.
059	JAM	004	012	One [only] is the lawgiver and judge, [even] he who is able to save and to destroy: but who art thou that judgest thy neighbour?
059	JAM	004	013	Go to now, ye that say, Today or tomorrow we will go into this city, and spend a year there, and trade, and get gain:
059	JAM	004	014	whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow. What is your life? For ye are a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.
059	JAM	004	015	For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall both live, and do this or that.
059	JAM	004	016	But now ye glory in your vauntings: all such glorying is evil.
059	JAM	004	017	To him therefore that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.
059	JAM	005	001	Go to now, ye rich, weep and howl for your miseries that are coming upon you.
059	JAM	005	002	Your riches are corrupted, and your garments are moth-eaten.
059	JAM	005	003	Your gold and your silver are rusted; and their rust shall be for a testimony against you, and shall eat your flesh as fire. Ye have laid up your treasure in the last days.
059	JAM	005	004	Behold, the hire of the labourers who mowed your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth out: and the cries of them that reaped have entered into the ears of the Lord of Sabaoth.
059	JAM	005	005	Ye have lived delicately on the earth, and taken your pleasure; ye have nourished your hearts in a day of slaughter.
059	JAM	005	006	Ye have condemned, ye have killed the righteous [one]; he doth not resist you.
059	JAM	005	007	Be patient therefore, brethren, until the coming of the Lord. Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, being patient over it, until it receive the early and latter rain.
059	JAM	005	008	Be ye also patient; stablish your hearts: for the coming of the Lord is at hand.
059	JAM	005	009	Murmur not, brethren, one against another, that ye be not judged: behold, the judge standeth before the doors.
059	JAM	005	010	Take, brethren, for an example of suffering and of patience, the prophets who spake in the name of the Lord.
059	JAM	005	011	Behold, we call them blessed which endured: ye have heard of the patience of Job, and have seen the end of the Lord, how that the Lord is full of pity, and merciful.
059	JAM	005	012	But above all things, my brethren, swear not, neither by the heaven, nor by the earth, nor by any other oath: but let your yea be yea, and your nay, nay; that ye fall not under judgment.
059	JAM	005	013	Is any among you suffering? let him pray. Is any cheerful? let him sing praise.
059	JAM	005	014	Is any among you sick? let him call for the elders of the church; and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord:
059	JAM	005	015	and the prayer of faith shall save him that is sick, and the Lord shall raise him up; and if he have committed sins, it shall be forgiven him.
059	JAM	005	016	Confess therefore your sins one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed. The supplication of a righteous man availeth much in its working.
059	JAM	005	017	Elijah was a man of like passions with us, and he prayed fervently that it might not rain; and it rained not on the earth for three years and six months.
059	JAM	005	018	And he prayed again; and the heaven gave rain, and the earth brought forth her fruit.
059	JAM	005	019	My brethren, if any among you do err from the truth, and one convert him;
059	JAM	005	020	let him know, that he which converteth a sinner from the error of his way shall save a soul from death, and shall cover a multitude of sins.
