# BOOK	062	1JO	1 John	1 John
062	1JO	001	001	That which was from the beginning, that which we have heard, that which we have seen with our eyes, that which we beheld, and our hands handled, concerning the Word of life
062	1JO	001	002	(and the life was manifested, and we have seen, and bear witness, and declare unto you the life, the eternal [life], which was with the Father, and was manifested unto us);
062	1JO	001	003	that which we have seen and heard declare we unto you also, that ye also may have fellowship with us: yea, and our fellowship is with the Father, and with his Son Jesus Christ:
062	1JO	001	004	and these things we write, that our joy may be fulfilled.
062	1JO	001	005	And this is the message which we have heard from him, and announce unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.
062	1JO	001	006	If we say that we have fellowship with him, and walk in the darkness, we lie, and do not the truth:
062	1JO	001	007	but if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus his Son cleanseth us from all sin.
062	1JO	001	008	If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.
062	1JO	001	009	If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.
062	1JO	001	010	If we say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us.
062	1JO	002	001	My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye may not sin. And if any man sin, we have an Advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous:
062	1JO	002	002	and he is the propitiation for our sins; and not for ours only, but also for the whole world.
062	1JO	002	003	And hereby know we that we know him, if we keep his commandments.
062	1JO	002	004	He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him:
062	1JO	002	005	but whoso keepeth his word, in him verily hath the love of God been perfected. Hereby know we that we are in him:
062	1JO	002	006	he that saith he abideth in him ought himself also to walk even as he walked.
062	1JO	002	007	Beloved, no new commandment write I unto you, but an old commandment which ye had from the beginning: the old commandment is the word which ye heard.
062	1JO	002	008	Again, a new commandment write I unto you, which thing is true in him and in you; because the darkness is passing away, and the true light already shineth.
062	1JO	002	009	He that saith he is in the light, and hateth his brother, is in the darkness even until now.
062	1JO	002	010	He that loveth his brother abideth in the light, and there is none occasion of stumbling in him.
062	1JO	002	011	But he that hateth his brother is in the darkness, and walketh in the darkness, and knoweth not whither he goeth, because the darkness hath blinded his eyes.
062	1JO	002	012	I write unto you, [my] little children, because your sins are forgiven you for his name’s sake.
062	1JO	002	013	I write unto you, fathers, because ye know him which is from the beginning. I write unto you, young men, because ye have overcome the evil one. I have written unto you, little children, because ye know the Father.
062	1JO	002	014	I have written unto you, fathers, because ye know him which is from the beginning. I have written unto you, young men, because ye are strong, and the word of God abideth in you, and ye have overcome the evil one.
062	1JO	002	015	Love not the world, neither the things that are in the world. If any man love the world, the love of the Father is not in him.
062	1JO	002	016	For all that is in the world, the lust of the flesh, and the lust of the eyes, and the vainglory of life, is not of the Father, but is of the world.
062	1JO	002	017	And the world passeth away, and the lust thereof: but he that doeth the will of God abideth for ever.
062	1JO	002	018	Little children, it is the last hour: and as ye heard that antichrist cometh, even now have there arisen many antichrists; whereby we know that it is the last hour.
062	1JO	002	019	They went out from us, but they were not of us; for if they had been of us, they would have continued with us: but [they went out], that they might be made manifest how that they all are not of us.
062	1JO	002	020	And ye have an anointing from the Holy One, and ye know all things.
062	1JO	002	021	I have not written unto you because ye know not the truth, but because ye know it, and because no lie is of the truth.
062	1JO	002	022	Who is the liar but he that denieth that Jesus is the Christ? This is the antichrist, [even] he that denieth the Father and the Son.
062	1JO	002	023	Whosoever denieth the Son, the same hath not the Father: he that confesseth the Son hath the Father also.
062	1JO	002	024	As for you, let that abide in you which ye heard from the beginning. If that which ye heard from the beginning abide in you, ye also shall abide in the Son, and in the Father.
062	1JO	002	025	And this is the promise which he promised us, [even] the life eternal.
062	1JO	002	026	These things have I written unto you concerning them that would lead you astray.
062	1JO	002	027	And as for you, the anointing which ye received of him abideth in you, and ye need not that any one teach you; but as his anointing teacheth you concerning all things, and is true, and is no lie, and even as it taught you, ye abide in him.
062	1JO	002	028	And now, [my] little children, abide in him; that, if he shall be manifested, we may have boldness, and not be ashamed before him at his coming.
062	1JO	002	029	If ye know that he is righteous, ye know that every one also that doeth righteousness is begotten of him.
062	1JO	003	001	Behold what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called children of God: and [such] we are. For this cause the world knoweth us not, because it knew him not.
062	1JO	003	002	Beloved, now are we children of God, and it is not yet made manifest what we shall be. We know that, if he shall be manifested, we shall be like him; for we shall see him even as he is.
062	1JO	003	003	And every one that hath this hope [set] on him purifieth himself, even as he is pure.
062	1JO	003	004	Every one that doeth sin doeth also lawlessness: and sin is lawlessness.
062	1JO	003	005	And ye know that he was manifested to take away sins; and in him is no sin.
062	1JO	003	006	Whosoever abideth in him sinneth not: whosoever sinneth hath not seen him, neither knoweth him.
062	1JO	003	007	[My] little children, let no man lead you astray: he that doeth righteousness is righteous, even as he is righteous:
062	1JO	003	008	he that doeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. To this end was the Son of God manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.
062	1JO	003	009	Whosoever is begotten of God doeth no sin, because his seed abideth in him: and he cannot sin, because he is begotten of God.
062	1JO	003	010	In this the children of God are manifest, and the children of the devil: whosoever doeth not righteousness is not of God, neither he that loveth not his brother.
062	1JO	003	011	For this is the message which ye heard from the beginning, that we should love one another:
062	1JO	003	012	not as Cain was of the evil one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his works were evil, and his brother’s righteous.
062	1JO	003	013	Marvel not, brethren, if the world hateth you.
062	1JO	003	014	We know that we have passed out of death into life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not abideth in death.
062	1JO	003	015	Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.
062	1JO	003	016	Hereby know we love, because he laid down his life for us: and we ought to lay down our lives for the brethren.
062	1JO	003	017	But whoso hath the world’s goods, and beholdeth his brother in need, and shutteth up his compassion from him, how doth the love of God abide in him?
062	1JO	003	018	[My] little children, let us not love in word, neither with the tongue; but in deed and truth.
062	1JO	003	019	Hereby shall we know that we are of the truth, and shall assure our heart before him,
062	1JO	003	020	whereinsoever our heart condemn us; because God is greater than our heart, and knoweth all things.
062	1JO	003	021	Beloved, if our heart condemn us not, we have boldness toward God;
062	1JO	003	022	and whatsoever we ask, we receive of him, because we keep his commandments, and do the things that are pleasing in his sight.
062	1JO	003	023	And this is his commandment, that we should believe in the name of his Son Jesus Christ, and love one another, even as he gave us commandment.
062	1JO	003	024	And he that keepeth his commandments abideth in him, and he in him. And hereby we know that he abideth in us, by the Spirit which he gave us.
062	1JO	004	001	Beloved, believe not every spirit, but prove the spirits, whether they are of God: because many false prophets are gone out into the world.
062	1JO	004	002	Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: every spirit which confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God:
062	1JO	004	003	and every spirit which confesseth not Jesus is not of God: and this is the [spirit] of the antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it cometh; and now it is in the world already.
062	1JO	004	004	Ye are of God, [my] little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you than he that is in the world.
062	1JO	004	005	They are of the world: therefore speak they [as] of the world, and the world heareth them.
062	1JO	004	006	We are of God: he that knoweth God heareth us; he who is not of God heareth us not. By this we know the spirit of truth, and the spirit of error.
062	1JO	004	007	Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is begotten of God, and knoweth God.
062	1JO	004	008	He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love.
062	1JO	004	009	Herein was the love of God manifested in us, that God hath sent his only begotten Son into the world, that we might live through him.
062	1JO	004	010	Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son [to be] the propitiation for our sins.
062	1JO	004	011	Beloved, if God so loved us, we also ought to love one another.
062	1JO	004	012	No man hath beheld God at any time: if we love one another, God abideth in us, and his love is perfected in us:
062	1JO	004	013	hereby know we that we abide in him, and he in us, because he hath given us of his Spirit.
062	1JO	004	014	And we have beheld and bear witness that the Father hath sent the Son [to be] the Saviour of the world.
062	1JO	004	015	Whosoever shall confess that Jesus is the Son of God, God abideth in him, and he in God.
062	1JO	004	016	And we know and have believed the love which God hath in us. God is love; and he that abideth in love abideth in God, and God abideth in him.
062	1JO	004	017	Herein is love made perfect with us, that we may have boldness in the day of judgment; because as he is, even so are we in this world.
062	1JO	004	018	There is no fear in love: but perfect love casteth out fear, because fear hath punishment; and he that feareth is not made perfect in love.
062	1JO	004	019	We love, because he first loved us.
062	1JO	004	020	If a man say, I love God, and hateth his brother, he is a liar: for he that loveth not his brother whom he hath seen, cannot love God whom he hath not seen.
062	1JO	004	021	And this commandment have we from him, that he who loveth God love his brother also.
062	1JO	005	001	Whosoever believeth that Jesus is the Christ is begotten of God: and whosoever loveth him that begat loveth him also that is begotten of him.
062	1JO	005	002	Hereby we know that we love the children of God, when we love God, and do his commandments.
062	1JO	005	003	For this is the love of God, that we keep his commandments: and his commandments are not grievous.
062	1JO	005	004	For whatsoever is begotten of God overcometh the world: and this is the victory that hath overcome the world, [even] our faith.
062	1JO	005	005	And who is he that overcometh the world, but he that believeth that Jesus is the Son of God?
062	1JO	005	006	This is he that came by water and blood, [even] Jesus Christ; not with the water only, but with the water and with the blood.
062	1JO	005	007	And it is the Spirit that beareth witness, because the Spirit is the truth.
062	1JO	005	008	For there are three who bear witness, the Spirit, and the water, and the blood: and the three agree in one.
062	1JO	005	009	If we receive the witness of men, the witness of God is greater: for the witness of God is this, that he hath borne witness concerning his Son.
062	1JO	005	010	He that believeth on the Son of God hath the witness in him: he that believeth not God hath made him a liar; because he hath not believed in the witness that God hath borne concerning his Son.
062	1JO	005	011	And the witness is this, that God gave unto us eternal life, and this life is in his Son.
062	1JO	005	012	He that hath the Son hath the life; he that hath not the Son of God hath not the life.
062	1JO	005	013	These things have I written unto you, that ye may know that ye have eternal life, [even] unto you that believe on the name of the Son of God.
062	1JO	005	014	And this is the boldness which we have toward him, that, if we ask anything according to his will, he heareth us:
062	1JO	005	015	and if we know that he heareth us whatsoever we ask, we know that we have the petitions which we have asked of him.
062	1JO	005	016	If any man see his brother sinning a sin not unto death, he shall ask, and [God] will give him life for them that sin not unto death. There is a sin unto death: not concerning this do I say that he should make request.
062	1JO	005	017	All unrighteousness is sin: and there is a sin not unto death.
062	1JO	005	018	We know that whosoever is begotten of God sinneth not; but he that was begotten of God keepeth him, and the evil one toucheth him not.
062	1JO	005	019	We know that we are of God, and the whole world lieth in the evil one.
062	1JO	005	020	And we know that the Son of God is come, and hath given us an understanding, that we know him that is true, and we are in him that is true, [even] in his Son Jesus Christ. This is the true God, and eternal life.
062	1JO	005	021	[My] little children, guard yourselves from idols.
#
# BOOK	063	2JO	2 John	2 John
063	2JO	001	001	The elder unto the elect lady and her children, whom I love in truth; and not I only, but also all they that know the truth;
063	2JO	001	002	for the truth’s sake which abideth in us, and it shall be with us for ever:
063	2JO	001	003	Grace, mercy, peace shall be with us, from God the Father, and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.
063	2JO	001	004	I rejoice greatly that I have found [certain] of thy children walking in truth, even as we received commandment from the Father.
063	2JO	001	005	And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though I wrote to thee a new commandment, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another.
063	2JO	001	006	And this is love, that we should walk after his commandments. This is the commandment, even as ye heard from the beginning, that ye should walk in it.
063	2JO	001	007	For many deceivers are gone forth into the world, [even] they that confess not that Jesus Christ cometh in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist.
063	2JO	001	008	Look to yourselves, that ye lose not the things which we have wrought, but that ye receive a full reward.
063	2JO	001	009	Whosoever goeth onward and abideth not in the teaching of Christ, hath not God: he that abideth in the teaching, the same hath both the Father and the Son.
063	2JO	001	010	If any one cometh unto you, and bringeth not this teaching, receive him not into [your] house, and give him no greeting:
063	2JO	001	011	for he that giveth him greeting partaketh in his evil works.
063	2JO	001	012	Having many things to write unto you, I would not [write them] with paper and ink: but I hope to come unto you, and to speak face to face, that your joy may be fulfilled.
063	2JO	001	013	The children of thine elect sister salute thee.
#
# BOOK	064	3JO	3 John	3 John
064	3JO	001	001	The elder unto Gaius the beloved, whom I love in truth.
064	3JO	001	002	Beloved, I pray that in all things thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.
064	3JO	001	003	For I rejoiced greatly, when brethren came and bare witness unto thy truth, even as thou walkest in truth.
064	3JO	001	004	Greater joy have I none than this, to hear of my children walking in the truth.
064	3JO	001	005	Beloved, thou doest a faithful work in whatsoever thou doest toward them that are brethren and strangers withal;
064	3JO	001	006	who bare witness to thy love before the church: whom thou wilt do well to set forward on their journey worthily of God:
064	3JO	001	007	because that for the sake of the Name they went forth, taking nothing of the Gentiles.
064	3JO	001	008	We therefore ought to welcome such, that we may be fellow-workers with the truth.
064	3JO	001	009	I wrote somewhat unto the church: but Diotrephes, who loveth to have the preeminence among them, receiveth us not.
064	3JO	001	010	Therefore, if I come, I will bring to remembrance his works which he doeth, prating against us with wicked words: and not content therewith, neither doth he himself receive the brethren, and them that would he forbiddeth, and casteth [them] out of the church.
064	3JO	001	011	Beloved, imitate not that which is evil, but that which is good. He that doeth good is of God: he that doeth evil hath not seen God.
064	3JO	001	012	Demetrius hath the witness of all [men], and of the truth itself: yea, we also bear witness; and thou knowest that our witness is true.
064	3JO	001	013	I had many things to write unto thee, but I am unwilling to write [them] to thee with ink and pen:
064	3JO	001	014	but I hope shortly to see thee, and we shall speak face to face. Peace [be] unto thee. The friends salute thee. Salute the friends by name.
#
# BOOK	065	JUD	Jude	Jude
065	JUD	001	001	Judas, a servant of Jesus Christ, and brother of James, to them that are called, beloved in God the Father, and kept for Jesus Christ:
065	JUD	001	002	Mercy unto you and peace and love be multiplied.
065	JUD	001	003	Beloved, while I was giving all diligence to write unto you of our common salvation, I was constrained to write unto you exhorting you to contend earnestly for the faith which was once for all delivered unto the saints.
065	JUD	001	004	For there are certain men crept in privily, [even] they who were of old set forth unto this condemnation, ungodly men, turning the grace of our God into lasciviousness, and denying our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.
065	JUD	001	005	Now I desire to put you in remembrance, though ye know all things once for all, how that the Lord, having saved a people out of the land of Egypt, afterward destroyed them that believed not.
065	JUD	001	006	And angels which kept not their own principality, but left their proper habitation, he hath kept in everlasting bonds under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.
065	JUD	001	007	Even as Sodom and Gomorrah, and the cities about them, having in like manner with these given themselves over to fornication, and gone after strange flesh, are set forth as an example, suffering the punishment of eternal fire.
065	JUD	001	008	Yet in like manner these also in their dreamings defile the flesh, and set at nought dominion, and rail at dignities.
065	JUD	001	009	But Michael the archangel, when contending with the devil he disputed about the body of Moses, durst not bring against him a railing judgment, but said, The Lord rebuke thee.
065	JUD	001	010	But these rail at whatsoever things they know not: and what they understand naturally, like the creatures without reason, in these things are they destroyed.
065	JUD	001	011	Woe unto them! for they went in the way of Cain, and ran riotously in the error of Balaam for hire, and perished in the gainsaying of Korah.
065	JUD	001	012	These are they who are hidden rocks in your love-feasts when they feast with you, shepherds that without fear feed themselves; clouds without water, carried along by winds; autumn trees without fruit, twice dead, plucked up by the roots;
065	JUD	001	013	Wild waves of the sea, foaming out their own shame; wandering stars, for whom the blackness of darkness hath been reserved for ever.
065	JUD	001	014	And to these also Enoch, the seventh from Adam, prophesied, saying, Behold, the Lord came with ten thousands of his holy ones,
065	JUD	001	015	to execute judgment upon all, and to convict all the ungodly of all their works of ungodliness which they have ungodly wrought, and of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against him.
065	JUD	001	016	These are murmurers, complainers, walking after their lusts (and their mouth speaketh great swelling [words]), shewing respect of persons for the sake of advantage.
065	JUD	001	017	But ye, beloved, remember ye the words which have been spoken before by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ;
065	JUD	001	018	how that they said to you, In the last time there shall be mockers, walking after their own ungodly lusts.
065	JUD	001	019	These are they who make separations, sensual, having not the Spirit.
065	JUD	001	020	But ye, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Spirit,
065	JUD	001	021	keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.
065	JUD	001	022	And on some have mercy, who are in doubt;
065	JUD	001	023	and some save, snatching them out of the fire; and on some have mercy with fear; hating even the garment spotted by the flesh.
065	JUD	001	024	Now unto him that is able to guard you from stumbling, and to set you before the presence of his glory without blemish in exceeding joy,
065	JUD	001	025	to the only God our Saviour, through Jesus Christ our Lord, [be] glory, majesty, dominion and power, before all time, and now, and for evermore. Amen.
